20:13:18.702 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/1/1/4
20:13:18.702 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":4,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Here I find myself once more in my native place after misfortune unlooked for &amp; unmeritted &amp; two years of anxiety and in settling our affairs, the disgraceful conduct of our attorney (Baily) &amp; his clients, proceeding from ignorance &amp; stupidity, I believe caused the delay, but which however has ended by the various amendments &amp; and alterations in the deeds suggested by William &amp; myself, much more to the advantage of ourselves &amp; all parties, than could possibly have been anticipated at the commencement. I now trust this is the beginning of a new life, where in its course will be attended with prosperity &amp; happiness both to my brother &amp; myself &amp; that he may soon have it in his power as I'm sure it is his wish &amp; intention to &quot;render unto every man his due&quot; he may have committed errors but this I know, they have been errors of the head not of the heart. If he had a fault, it was too great a desire to serve others without perhaps prudently asking himself whether he could do so, without committing an act of injustice to himself his family or those who were next to those connected to him by the nearest &amp; dearest ties, however &quot;Expereentia docet&quot;. Here's oblivion to the past &amp; may prosperity attend the future. As for myself, I feel as every ...</p>","pageId":685,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1,"lock":null}
20:13:18.703 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.703 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/1/1/4
20:13:18.703 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":4,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Here I find myself once more in my native place after misfortune unlooked for &amp; unmeritted &amp; two years of anxiety and in settling our affairs, the disgraceful conduct of our attorney (Baily) &amp; his clients, proceeding from ignorance &amp; stupidity, I believe caused the delay, but which however has ended by the various amendments &amp; and alterations in the deeds suggested by William &amp; myself, much more to the advantage of ourselves &amp; all parties, than could possibly have been anticipated at the commencement. I now trust this is the beginning of a new life, where in its course will be attended with prosperity &amp; happiness both to my brother &amp; myself &amp; that he may soon have it in his power as I'm sure it is his wish &amp; intention to &quot;render unto every man his due&quot; he may have committed errors but this I know, they have been errors of the head not of the heart. If he had a fault, it was too great a desire to serve others without perhaps prudently asking himself whether he could do so, without committing an act of injustice to himself his family or those who were next to those connected to him by the nearest &amp; dearest ties, however &quot;Expereentia docet&quot;. Here's oblivion to the past &amp; may prosperity attend the future. As for myself, I feel as every ...</p>","pageId":685,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1,"lock":null}
20:13:18.703 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/1/1/5
20:13:18.703 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":5,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":1,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... as every man must do, who keeps there grand maxim in view &quot;Do onto others as you would they should do unto you&quot;, he who attends to this well , never get far wrong &amp; thank god so far I feel I can apply the quotation &quot;mens conscia recti&quot; to myself indeed . I am made to feel it by the kind &amp; friendly manner in which every person receive me I hope I deserve it, I do not know that I ever did an injury to anyone certain never intentionally.</p>\r\n<p>However there is one person whose conduct has indeed been that of a friend &amp; such a friend as seldom is met with &amp; I cannot omit recording it here &amp; were I ever to forget it should indeed be ungrateful &amp; unworthy of every kind feeling. John Tinley is the man who could feel for the misfortunes of another. He it was who paved the way for our emancipation from all difficulties. Where is the friend that would have acted as he did? I fear not to be found. He came forward not a friend in words but in deeds. He made not promises, nor exacted hopes &amp; expectations, to disappoint &amp; blast them when called upon. He saw our situation, he volunteered his services as security, without which we could have effected nothing &amp; thus has the primary cause of our accomplishing all that has been done. He thought he knew us &amp; I hope has not been deceived. This is what I call friendship, true &amp; sincere, not according to the worldly acceptation &amp; profanation of the word, but friendship in the true spirit &amp; meaning of the word.</p>\r\n<p>I yesterday, the last day of the old year, dined with this my excellent friend &amp; accompanied him Miss Barton A party to the ball &amp; spent a very pleasant evening &amp; thus ended the old &amp; began the new year merrily. I hope it is a good omen. Today I again dined with J Tinley to meet Mr Waldie to a very agreeable party.</p>","pageId":686,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2,"lock":null}
20:13:18.703 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.704 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/1/1/5
20:13:18.704 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":5,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":1,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... as every man must do, who keeps there grand maxim in view &quot;Do onto others as you would they should do unto you&quot;, he who attends to this well , never get far wrong &amp; thank god so far I feel I can apply the quotation &quot;mens conscia recti&quot; to myself indeed . I am made to feel it by the kind &amp; friendly manner in which every person receive me I hope I deserve it, I do not know that I ever did an injury to anyone certain never intentionally.</p>\r\n<p>However there is one person whose conduct has indeed been that of a friend &amp; such a friend as seldom is met with &amp; I cannot omit recording it here &amp; were I ever to forget it should indeed be ungrateful &amp; unworthy of every kind feeling. John Tinley is the man who could feel for the misfortunes of another. He it was who paved the way for our emancipation from all difficulties. Where is the friend that would have acted as he did? I fear not to be found. He came forward not a friend in words but in deeds. He made not promises, nor exacted hopes &amp; expectations, to disappoint &amp; blast them when called upon. He saw our situation, he volunteered his services as security, without which we could have effected nothing &amp; thus has the primary cause of our accomplishing all that has been done. He thought he knew us &amp; I hope has not been deceived. This is what I call friendship, true &amp; sincere, not according to the worldly acceptation &amp; profanation of the word, but friendship in the true spirit &amp; meaning of the word.</p>\r\n<p>I yesterday, the last day of the old year, dined with this my excellent friend &amp; accompanied him Miss Barton A party to the ball &amp; spent a very pleasant evening &amp; thus ended the old &amp; began the new year merrily. I hope it is a good omen. Today I again dined with J Tinley to meet Mr Waldie to a very agreeable party.</p>","pageId":686,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2,"lock":null}
20:13:18.704 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/1/10/14
20:13:18.704 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":14,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Dined with Mrs Scott. Spent the evening with the Whist club. Lost 4/-. Wind SE with frost. Wrote to Sir D Smith</p>","pageId":687,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":11,"lock":null}
20:13:18.704 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.705 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/1/10/14
20:13:18.705 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":14,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Dined with Mrs Scott. Spent the evening with the Whist club. Lost 4/-. Wind SE with frost. Wrote to Sir D Smith</p>","pageId":687,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":11,"lock":null}
20:13:18.705 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/1/11/15
20:13:18.705 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":15,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Dined with Mrs Scott Went to the theatre in the evening. The bespeak of the Bachelors of North Shields for the benefit of Miss C Scsuton. A good house &pound;59.16/-. Play The Haunted Tower with Registers Officer &amp; High life below stairs, a very good company. Wind SSE. A heavy fall of snow, the latter part of the evening it thawed. Sea fallen</p>","pageId":687,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":12,"lock":null}
20:13:18.705 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.705 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/1/11/15
20:13:18.705 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":15,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Dined with Mrs Scott Went to the theatre in the evening. The bespeak of the Bachelors of North Shields for the benefit of Miss C Scsuton. A good house &pound;59.16/-. Play The Haunted Tower with Registers Officer &amp; High life below stairs, a very good company. Wind SSE. A heavy fall of snow, the latter part of the evening it thawed. Sea fallen</p>","pageId":687,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":12,"lock":null}
20:13:18.706 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/1/12/16
20:13:18.706 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":16,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A foggy unpleasant day &amp; the thaw continuing, excessively wet and sloppy Received a letter from Dixon stating the impossibility of his assisting me (Promises much easier made than kept). Wind W&amp;SW. Sea fallen &amp; ship &amp; sailed</p>","pageId":687,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":13,"lock":null}
20:13:18.706 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.706 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/1/12/16
20:13:18.706 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":16,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A foggy unpleasant day &amp; the thaw continuing, excessively wet and sloppy Received a letter from Dixon stating the impossibility of his assisting me (Promises much easier made than kept). Wind W&amp;SW. Sea fallen &amp; ship &amp; sailed</p>","pageId":687,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":13,"lock":null}
20:13:18.706 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/1/13/17
20:13:18.706 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":17,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>After a blowy and rainy night, on rising this morning, found the snow nearly dissolved. Wind E to ESE &amp; very heavy sea upon the bar, a few ships arrived. Another disappointment! Received a letter from Sir D Smith stating the Dukes inability to comply with my request for a loan. Every person poor when you want assistance! Adversities the time for trying friendship, in prosperity you have professions enough. I've oft been told, but I have now ascertained it's a d-d selfish world we live in; every one for himself. &lsquo;tis almost a crime to be liberal &amp; kind hearted</p>","pageId":687,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":14,"lock":null}
20:13:18.706 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.707 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/1/13/17
20:13:18.707 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":17,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>After a blowy and rainy night, on rising this morning, found the snow nearly dissolved. Wind E to ESE &amp; very heavy sea upon the bar, a few ships arrived. Another disappointment! Received a letter from Sir D Smith stating the Dukes inability to comply with my request for a loan. Every person poor when you want assistance! Adversities the time for trying friendship, in prosperity you have professions enough. I've oft been told, but I have now ascertained it's a d-d selfish world we live in; every one for himself. &lsquo;tis almost a crime to be liberal &amp; kind hearted</p>","pageId":687,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":14,"lock":null}
20:13:18.707 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/1/14/18
20:13:18.707 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":18,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A wet unpleasant day &amp; a gale from the east, with a heavy sea on the bar, snow at heights. Dined with the associated clubs at the George Tavern. A very handsome dinner &amp; nearly two hundred sat down. Looked into the theatre in the evening</p>","pageId":687,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":15,"lock":null}
20:13:18.707 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
