20:13:18.731 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":310,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<figure>\r\n  <img src=\"images/img2860-image-map-alnwick-tyneside.jpg\" width=\"600px\" />\r\n  <figcaption>Map Alnwick and Tyneside</figcaption>\r\n</figure>","pageId":null,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":null,"lock":null}
20:13:18.731 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/17/311
20:13:18.731 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":311,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":17,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind NNW. Left Shields at 8 o'clock am after breakfast &amp; got to Newcastle at &frac12; past 9 o'clock. Received a letter from William before I left Shields of the arrival of the Hope, but not sold. Wrote to J Fenwick of Preston Villa from Newcastle what William says about freights for <span class=highlight_yellow>Elgin coals</span> &amp; also sent J Tinley the part of the letter relative to <span class=highlight_yellow>N Birds</span> debts to W &amp; JS. Then left Newcastle at 10 o'clock by the Alnwick coach &amp; got to Felton about 2 o'clock. The day much changed, being very cloudy &amp; beginning to rain at &frac12; past 2 o'clock. After having some lunch, started for Togston to walk in the rain &amp; arrived there at 4 o'clock. Found only Mrs Smith &amp; Emma Galbraith at home. The rest of the family in Alnwick to attend the Jessions Ball. 2<sup>nd</sup> &amp; 3<sup>rd</sup> voyages received for manure &pound;3.17.6</p>","pageId":712,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":294,"lock":null}
20:13:18.731 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.732 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/17/311
20:13:18.732 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":311,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":17,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind NNW. Left Shields at 8 o'clock am after breakfast &amp; got to Newcastle at &frac12; past 9 o'clock. Received a letter from William before I left Shields of the arrival of the Hope, but not sold. Wrote to J Fenwick of Preston Villa from Newcastle what William says about freights for <span class=highlight_yellow>Elgin coals</span> &amp; also sent J Tinley the part of the letter relative to <span class=highlight_yellow>N Birds</span> debts to W &amp; JS. Then left Newcastle at 10 o'clock by the Alnwick coach &amp; got to Felton about 2 o'clock. The day much changed, being very cloudy &amp; beginning to rain at &frac12; past 2 o'clock. After having some lunch, started for Togston to walk in the rain &amp; arrived there at 4 o'clock. Found only Mrs Smith &amp; Emma Galbraith at home. The rest of the family in Alnwick to attend the Jessions Ball. 2<sup>nd</sup> &amp; 3<sup>rd</sup> voyages received for manure &pound;3.17.6</p>","pageId":712,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":294,"lock":null}
20:13:18.732 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/18/312
20:13:18.732 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":312,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild morning. Wind WNW. After breakfast, Emma &amp; I walked to see the new colliery sunk by Tom Smith &amp; others &amp; afterwards went down to Amble &amp; the sands &amp; returned about 2 o'clock after a most pleasurable walk. Tom, Fanny, Anna &amp; Bell returned from Alnwick to dinner at 5 o'clock</p>","pageId":712,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":295,"lock":null}
20:13:18.732 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.732 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/18/312
20:13:18.732 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":312,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild morning. Wind WNW. After breakfast, Emma &amp; I walked to see the new colliery sunk by Tom Smith &amp; others &amp; afterwards went down to Amble &amp; the sands &amp; returned about 2 o'clock after a most pleasurable walk. Tom, Fanny, Anna &amp; Bell returned from Alnwick to dinner at 5 o'clock</p>","pageId":712,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":295,"lock":null}
20:13:18.732 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/19/313
20:13:18.732 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":313,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful autumnal day. Wind WSW. Drove Fanny, Bell &amp; Emma Galbraith down to Warkworth church. Called upon the <span class=highlight_yellow>Miss</span> Watsons. Saw the Chatterbucks etc. In the afternoon took a walk with Tom to the colliery. <span class=highlight_yellow>res</span> Matt Culley came to dinner at 5 o'clock</p>","pageId":712,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":296,"lock":null}
20:13:18.732 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.733 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/19/313
20:13:18.733 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":313,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful autumnal day. Wind WSW. Drove Fanny, Bell &amp; Emma Galbraith down to Warkworth church. Called upon the <span class=highlight_yellow>Miss</span> Watsons. Saw the Chatterbucks etc. In the afternoon took a walk with Tom to the colliery. <span class=highlight_yellow>res</span> Matt Culley came to dinner at 5 o'clock</p>","pageId":712,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":296,"lock":null}
20:13:18.733 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/2/294
20:13:18.733 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":294,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still fine weather. Wind SW &amp; SSW. Went down to the Hope, only to do 10 &frac12; cha today. Dined on board. Walked up &amp; went to Drury Lane Theatre to the pit at full price &amp; saw &quot;A cure for the heartache&quot; &amp; XYZ. Very much entertained.</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":278,"lock":null}
