20:13:18.741 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":325,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Continuance of fine weather &amp; wind NNW. Out shooting &amp; killed 1 &frac12; braces of birds. Wrote to Mr Vernon &amp; R Snowdon</p>","pageId":713,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":308,"lock":null}
20:13:18.741 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.742 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/31/325
20:13:18.742 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":325,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Continuance of fine weather &amp; wind NNW. Out shooting &amp; killed 1 &frac12; braces of birds. Wrote to Mr Vernon &amp; R Snowdon</p>","pageId":713,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":308,"lock":null}
20:13:18.742 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/4/296
20:13:18.742 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":296,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet morning. Wind WSW. Cleared up towards the middle of the day &amp; turned out a fine afternoon. Went down to the ship about 1 o'clock pm. Found her nearly out. Watt came on board. Sailed about 3 o'clock &amp; got below Woolwich &amp; brought up, where Watt left us. A breeze springing up got underway again about 9 o'clock against the flood but obliged again to let go our anchor about 11 o'clock for want of wind! For the night William slept on board. Brought today a life preserver for 18/- Some white &amp; coloured neckcloths for &pound;2</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":280,"lock":null}
20:13:18.742 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.742 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/4/296
20:13:18.742 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":296,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet morning. Wind WSW. Cleared up towards the middle of the day &amp; turned out a fine afternoon. Went down to the ship about 1 o'clock pm. Found her nearly out. Watt came on board. Sailed about 3 o'clock &amp; got below Woolwich &amp; brought up, where Watt left us. A breeze springing up got underway again about 9 o'clock against the flood but obliged again to let go our anchor about 11 o'clock for want of wind! For the night William slept on board. Brought today a life preserver for 18/- Some white &amp; coloured neckcloths for &pound;2</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":280,"lock":null}
20:13:18.742 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/5/297
20:13:18.742 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":297,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind South. Got underway from off _____ at 11 o'clock am with a fresh breeze, landed William at Gravesend. At 1 o'clock pm. At 4 o'clock passed through Shoe Hole 8 o'clock abreast of Harwich &amp; 10 o'clock off the Lowestoft Light &amp; turned in for the night. Blowing fresh.</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":281,"lock":null}
20:13:18.742 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.743 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/5/297
20:13:18.743 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":297,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind South. Got underway from off _____ at 11 o'clock am with a fresh breeze, landed William at Gravesend. At 1 o'clock pm. At 4 o'clock passed through Shoe Hole 8 o'clock abreast of Harwich &amp; 10 o'clock off the Lowestoft Light &amp; turned in for the night. Blowing fresh.</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":281,"lock":null}
20:13:18.743 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/6/298
20:13:18.743 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":298,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Blowing hard all night with rain towards morning. Got up at 8 o'clock am. Wind just changed to WNW, rather squally. Ship off Cromer. At 11 o'clock abreast of the floating light. Blowing hard from West. Ship under foresail &amp; reefed topsail, mainsail &amp; double reefed main topsail &amp; reefed trysail. At 2 o'clock pm double reefed fore-top-sail. At 3 o'clock made the Spurn <font color=#BFBFBF>[Point]</font><font color=#BFBFBF> </font> being off the floating light. Still blowing strong from the West</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":282,"lock":null}
20:13:18.743 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.743 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/6/298
20:13:18.744 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":298,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Blowing hard all night with rain towards morning. Got up at 8 o'clock am. Wind just changed to WNW, rather squally. Ship off Cromer. At 11 o'clock abreast of the floating light. Blowing hard from West. Ship under foresail &amp; reefed topsail, mainsail &amp; double reefed main topsail &amp; reefed trysail. At 2 o'clock pm double reefed fore-top-sail. At 3 o'clock made the Spurn <font color=#BFBFBF>[Point]</font><font color=#BFBFBF> </font> being off the floating light. Still blowing strong from the West</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":282,"lock":null}
20:13:18.744 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/6/299
20:13:18.744 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":299,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":6,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>About 7 o'clock got bound. Flamborough Head at 10 o'clock. Off Robin Hoods bay blowing hard with squalls at 11 o'clock between the bay &amp; Whitby met a fleet of London vessels. Blowing hard. Nearly run down one vessel owing to his own obstinacy or keeping a bad lookout. Stowed trysail &amp; main sail &amp; took in jib. Very dark ahead. At 12 o'clock or little after it, clear weather but continued to blow off Hunt Cliff Foot. Turned in for the night.</p>","pageId":711,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":283,"lock":null}
20:13:18.744 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.744 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/6/299
20:13:18.744 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":299,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":6,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>About 7 o'clock got bound. Flamborough Head at 10 o'clock. Off Robin Hoods bay blowing hard with squalls at 11 o'clock between the bay &amp; Whitby met a fleet of London vessels. Blowing hard. Nearly run down one vessel owing to his own obstinacy or keeping a bad lookout. Stowed trysail &amp; main sail &amp; took in jib. Very dark ahead. At 12 o'clock or little after it, clear weather but continued to blow off Hunt Cliff Foot. Turned in for the night.</p>","pageId":711,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":283,"lock":null}
20:13:18.744 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/7/300
20:13:18.744 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":300,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At 5 o'clock am off Sunderland with fine weather. Wind about WSW. Got a pilot on board. At 6 o'clock brought up off Shields Bar, turned out dressed &amp; landed in Tynemouth Haven. Breakfasted in Dockwray Square. Mrs Scott not up being rather unwell. Went up to Newcastle but the Carrs busy from a fortnight to three weeks, returned to Shields by steam &amp; fixed the Hope to take Burdon main to be load up under the spout on Friday. The ship towed safe into the harbour by a steam boat. Blowing a gale of wind from about WSW. Dined with Mrs Scott. Wrote to William</p>","pageId":711,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":284,"lock":null}
20:13:18.744 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.745 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/7/300
20:13:18.745 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":300,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At 5 o'clock am off Sunderland with fine weather. Wind about WSW. Got a pilot on board. At 6 o'clock brought up off Shields Bar, turned out dressed &amp; landed in Tynemouth Haven. Breakfasted in Dockwray Square. Mrs Scott not up being rather unwell. Went up to Newcastle but the Carrs busy from a fortnight to three weeks, returned to Shields by steam &amp; fixed the Hope to take Burdon main to be load up under the spout on Friday. The ship towed safe into the harbour by a steam boat. Blowing a gale of wind from about WSW. Dined with Mrs Scott. Wrote to William</p>","pageId":711,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":284,"lock":null}
20:13:18.745 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/8/301
20:13:18.745 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":301,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind NW. Received a letter from William with the Hope's Balance Note for &pound;63.18/-  Engaged all the morning on board ship. Got the ballast out. Dined at home. Mrs Scott not well. Spent the evening at J Tinleys. W Temple there. Won 10/- at whist. Several ships got to sea.</p>","pageId":711,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":285,"lock":null}
20:13:18.745 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.745 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/8/301
20:13:18.745 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":301,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind NW. Received a letter from William with the Hope's Balance Note for &pound;63.18/-  Engaged all the morning on board ship. Got the ballast out. Dined at home. Mrs Scott not well. Spent the evening at J Tinleys. W Temple there. Won 10/- at whist. Several ships got to sea.</p>","pageId":711,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":285,"lock":null}
20:13:18.745 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/9/302
20:13:18.745 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":302,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind NW. Made the Hope's book up. On board the ship under the spout. Got some keels in. Set the new for-topmast backstays. The Lady Jane arrived from Greenland with 15 fish, a full ship. Gave Stephenson &pound;30. Made an agreement with the washerwoman for the quarter at 1 &frac12; guinea. Dined with J Tindley. Won at whist 4/-</p>","pageId":711,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":286,"lock":null}
20:13:18.745 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.746 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/9/302
20:13:18.746 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":302,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind NW. Made the Hope's book up. On board the ship under the spout. Got some keels in. Set the new for-topmast backstays. The Lady Jane arrived from Greenland with 15 fish, a full ship. Gave Stephenson &pound;30. Made an agreement with the washerwoman for the quarter at 1 &frac12; guinea. Dined with J Tindley. Won at whist 4/-</p>","pageId":711,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":286,"lock":null}
20:13:18.746 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/1/326
20:13:18.746 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":326,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather. Wind NW. Out shooting, no sport, the dog being tired by having been at Warkworth &amp; the birds wild. Dined at Mr A Moises. <span class=highlight_yellow>Amble</span> &amp; spent a very pleasant day. The party consisting of Major Mr &amp; Miss Clatterburn, Mr &amp; Mrs Moises, Mr Elliott, Tom &amp; Fanny Smith, self &amp; Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>I Ord</span>. Received a letter from master of the Hope being to sail on Thursday from London</p>","pageId":713,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":309,"lock":null}
20:13:18.746 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.746 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/1/326
20:13:18.746 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":326,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather. Wind NW. Out shooting, no sport, the dog being tired by having been at Warkworth &amp; the birds wild. Dined at Mr A Moises. <span class=highlight_yellow>Amble</span> &amp; spent a very pleasant day. The party consisting of Major Mr &amp; Miss Clatterburn, Mr &amp; Mrs Moises, Mr Elliott, Tom &amp; Fanny Smith, self &amp; Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>I Ord</span>. Received a letter from master of the Hope being to sail on Thursday from London</p>","pageId":713,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":309,"lock":null}
20:13:18.746 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/10/335
20:13:18.746 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":335,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A winters day. Very stormy with sleet &amp; hail. Wind in the morning NE &amp; changed to SE. On board the Hope. Tom &amp; Fanny Smith &amp; Emma Galbraith arrived from Togston.</p>","pageId":714,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":318,"lock":null}
20:13:18.746 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.747 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/10/335
20:13:18.747 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":335,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A winters day. Very stormy with sleet &amp; hail. Wind in the morning NE &amp; changed to SE. On board the Hope. Tom &amp; Fanny Smith &amp; Emma Galbraith arrived from Togston.</p>","pageId":714,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":318,"lock":null}
20:13:18.747 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/11/336
20:13:18.747 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":336,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very frosty cold day. Wind WSW. The Hope got 4 keels down today. Dined at home. Robert made a bad collection of rents.</p>","pageId":714,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":319,"lock":null}
20:13:18.747 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.747 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/11/336
20:13:18.747 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":336,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very frosty cold day. Wind WSW. The Hope got 4 keels down today. Dined at home. Robert made a bad collection of rents.</p>","pageId":714,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":319,"lock":null}
20:13:18.747 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/12/337
20:13:18.747 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":337,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very unpleasant &amp; raw cold day. Wind SSW. The Hope got all her coals today, but being thick weather and poor prospect, did not go to sea. Mrs Matthews &amp; Miss Liddell drank tea with us. Gave Stephenson &pound;8. To my astonishment a writ of arrest was opened against me by Bland, Dunn the tailor partners . Very unhandsome conduct as William had called upon him to settle the account before I left town.</p>","pageId":714,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":320,"lock":null}
20:13:18.747 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.748 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/12/337
20:13:18.748 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":337,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very unpleasant &amp; raw cold day. Wind SSW. The Hope got all her coals today, but being thick weather and poor prospect, did not go to sea. Mrs Matthews &amp; Miss Liddell drank tea with us. Gave Stephenson &pound;8. To my astonishment a writ of arrest was opened against me by Bland, Dunn the tailor partners . Very unhandsome conduct as William had called upon him to settle the account before I left town.</p>","pageId":714,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":320,"lock":null}
20:13:18.748 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/13/338
20:13:18.748 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":338,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An exceedingly cold damp unpleasant day. Thick weather &amp; wind SE &amp; SSE. The Smiths left us for Togston. Wrote to William. Dined with Mrs Scott. In the evening at the card club. Won 4/-. The Hope not got out. Wrote to William</p>","pageId":714,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":321,"lock":null}
20:13:18.748 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.749 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/13/338
20:13:18.749 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":338,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An exceedingly cold damp unpleasant day. Thick weather &amp; wind SE &amp; SSE. The Smiths left us for Togston. Wrote to William. Dined with Mrs Scott. In the evening at the card club. Won 4/-. The Hope not got out. Wrote to William</p>","pageId":714,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":321,"lock":null}
20:13:18.749 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/14/339
20:13:18.749 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":339,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A raw damp day. A few loaded ships got out [in] the morning tide with a poor prospect. Wind SE blowing fresh all day. Several light ships got down. The Hope still in the harbour. <span class=highlight_yellow>Wellington</span> coals 45/- at Wednesdays market. Only 7 ships there</p>","pageId":714,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":322,"lock":null}
20:13:18.749 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.749 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/14/339
20:13:18.749 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":339,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A raw damp day. A few loaded ships got out [in] the morning tide with a poor prospect. Wind SE blowing fresh all day. Several light ships got down. The Hope still in the harbour. <span class=highlight_yellow>Wellington</span> coals 45/- at Wednesdays market. Only 7 ships there</p>","pageId":714,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":322,"lock":null}
20:13:18.749 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/15/340
20:13:18.749 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":340,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of cold weather with rain. Wind SE. Mr Mark dined with me on board the Hope. No ships got to sea this day</p>","pageId":714,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":323,"lock":null}
20:13:18.749 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.750 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/15/340
20:13:18.750 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":340,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of cold weather with rain. Wind SE. Mr Mark dined with me on board the Hope. No ships got to sea this day</p>","pageId":714,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":323,"lock":null}
20:13:18.750 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/16/341
20:13:18.750 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":341,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A heavy fall of rain with wind at ESE in the afternoon. It got to E &amp; NE with a deluge of rain. Dined at home. No ships sailed. Received a letter from William of his having paid Bland, the tailor my bill with costs &pound;35.9.10</p>","pageId":714,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":324,"lock":null}
20:13:18.750 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.751 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/16/341
20:13:18.751 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":341,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A heavy fall of rain with wind at ESE in the afternoon. It got to E &amp; NE with a deluge of rain. Dined at home. No ships sailed. Received a letter from William of his having paid Bland, the tailor my bill with costs &pound;35.9.10</p>","pageId":714,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":324,"lock":null}
20:13:18.751 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/17/342
20:13:18.751 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":342,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet day. Wind NNW. A large fleet of small ships got to sea. The pilot refused to take charge of the Hope there being a heavy sea upon the bar. Dined at J Tinley with a small party.</p>","pageId":714,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":325,"lock":null}
20:13:18.751 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.751 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/17/342
20:13:18.751 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":342,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet day. Wind NNW. A large fleet of small ships got to sea. The pilot refused to take charge of the Hope there being a heavy sea upon the bar. Dined at J Tinley with a small party.</p>","pageId":714,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":325,"lock":null}
20:13:18.751 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/18/343
20:13:18.751 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":343,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp day with a little rain &amp; wind in the morning. NE afterwards changed to SE &amp; heavy sea upon the bar. The Hope still not able to get to sea. Dined at home. Attended the new whist club for the first time at J Tinleys. Won 20/-</p>","pageId":714,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":326,"lock":null}
20:13:18.751 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.752 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/18/343
20:13:18.752 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":343,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp day with a little rain &amp; wind in the morning. NE afterwards changed to SE &amp; heavy sea upon the bar. The Hope still not able to get to sea. Dined at home. Attended the new whist club for the first time at J Tinleys. Won 20/-</p>","pageId":714,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":326,"lock":null}
20:13:18.752 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/19/344
20:13:18.752 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":344,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine day. Wind NW &amp; sea down. A very large fleet with the Hope sailed with a fine prospect. Walked to Tynemouth &amp; called upon Mr Marks of the 5<sup>th</sup> Regiment. Dined at Mr Mayne. Met Captain Bunbury of the 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment. Mr Hopkins, Mr Mayne &amp; Mr Ferguson.</p>","pageId":714,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":327,"lock":null}
20:13:18.752 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.752 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/19/344
20:13:18.752 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":344,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine day. Wind NW &amp; sea down. A very large fleet with the Hope sailed with a fine prospect. Walked to Tynemouth &amp; called upon Mr Marks of the 5<sup>th</sup> Regiment. Dined at Mr Mayne. Met Captain Bunbury of the 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment. Mr Hopkins, Mr Mayne &amp; Mr Ferguson.</p>","pageId":714,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":327,"lock":null}
20:13:18.752 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/2/327
20:13:18.752 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":327,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful day. Wind NNW. Went to Warkworth Church in the morning. Called upon Mr &amp; Miss Watons. Drove Fanny &amp; Bell Smith &amp; Emma Galbraith in the afternoon. Robert Brown walked down from Brinkburn, dined &amp; stayed all night. Spent a jolly evening.</p>","pageId":713,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":310,"lock":null}
20:13:18.752 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
