20:13:18.753 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":327,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful day. Wind NNW. Went to Warkworth Church in the morning. Called upon Mr &amp; Miss Watons. Drove Fanny &amp; Bell Smith &amp; Emma Galbraith in the afternoon. Robert Brown walked down from Brinkburn, dined &amp; stayed all night. Spent a jolly evening.</p>","pageId":713,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":310,"lock":null}
20:13:18.753 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/20/345
20:13:18.753 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":345,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind WNW. A few ships went to sea. Engaged all the morning in the office. Wrote to William. Paid Barthewan an advance of &pound;5.5.4. At the whist club in the evening. Paid into Chapman &pound;50 rents on acct of ex<font color=#BFBFBF>ecut</font>ors</p>","pageId":714,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":328,"lock":null}
20:13:18.753 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
