20:13:18.763 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":334,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very cold day. Wind NE. At church in the morning. In the afternoon walked to Tynemouth. Dined with Mrs Scott,</p>","pageId":713,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":317,"lock":null}
20:13:18.763 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/1/356
20:13:18.763 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":356,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Early this morning it blew a very heavy gale of wind from the NE &amp; ENE with showers of rain &amp; heavy sea. Towards afternoon the wind abated but continued from the east. Engaged in the office the principal part of the morning. Wrote to William. Dined at home. Mr Wheatley buried a son &amp; daughter Mr Gun today. They died of consumption.</p>","pageId":716,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":339,"lock":null}
20:13:18.763 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.764 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/1/356
20:13:18.764 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":356,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Early this morning it blew a very heavy gale of wind from the NE &amp; ENE with showers of rain &amp; heavy sea. Towards afternoon the wind abated but continued from the east. Engaged in the office the principal part of the morning. Wrote to William. Dined at home. Mr Wheatley buried a son &amp; daughter Mr Gun today. They died of consumption.</p>","pageId":716,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":339,"lock":null}
20:13:18.764 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/10/365
20:13:18.764 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":365,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine but cold frosty day. Wind WNW. Went to Benton by the coach in the morning. Walked there from the turnpike &amp; afterwards onto Newcastle where I wrote to William to sell the Hope. Missed Dixons, walked out to Benton again to dinner. Mr Colonel Dixon staying there. Mr Allinson dined with us</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":348,"lock":null}
20:13:18.764 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.764 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/10/365
20:13:18.764 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":365,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine but cold frosty day. Wind WNW. Went to Benton by the coach in the morning. Walked there from the turnpike &amp; afterwards onto Newcastle where I wrote to William to sell the Hope. Missed Dixons, walked out to Benton again to dinner. Mr Colonel Dixon staying there. Mr Allinson dined with us</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":348,"lock":null}
20:13:18.764 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/11/366
20:13:18.764 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":366,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Rather a stormy day &amp; cold. Wind WNW. Walked into Newcastle with Dixon. A great day at Gosforth guns firing etc etc. Mr Char<font color=#BFBFBF>les</font> Bell married one the Miss Brandlengs. Returned to Benton to Dinner.</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":349,"lock":null}
20:13:18.764 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.765 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/11/366
20:13:18.765 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":366,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Rather a stormy day &amp; cold. Wind WNW. Walked into Newcastle with Dixon. A great day at Gosforth guns firing etc etc. Mr Char<font color=#BFBFBF>les</font> Bell married one the Miss Brandlengs. Returned to Benton to Dinner.</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":349,"lock":null}
20:13:18.765 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/12/367
20:13:18.765 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":367,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful mild day. Wind WNN. Out greyhound coursing. Ran 8 or 9 hares &amp; killed none. The dogs out of wind not having had any exercise lately. But had some pretty running.</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":350,"lock":null}
20:13:18.765 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.766 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/12/367
20:13:18.766 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":367,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful mild day. Wind WNN. Out greyhound coursing. Ran 8 or 9 hares &amp; killed none. The dogs out of wind not having had any exercise lately. But had some pretty running.</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":350,"lock":null}
20:13:18.766 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/13/368
20:13:18.766 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":368,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Exceedingly fine mild. More like summer than December. Walked with Dixon to Newcastle. Spent the morning there, took the steamer boat &amp; got to Shields at 3 o'clock. Dined with J Tinley in the evening at Mr Harry's. Then whist club. At night the wind got round to the east.</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":351,"lock":null}
20:13:18.766 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.767 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/13/368
20:13:18.767 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":368,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Exceedingly fine mild. More like summer than December. Walked with Dixon to Newcastle. Spent the morning there, took the steamer boat &amp; got to Shields at 3 o'clock. Dined with J Tinley in the evening at Mr Harry's. Then whist club. At night the wind got round to the east.</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":351,"lock":null}
20:13:18.767 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/14/369
20:13:18.767 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":369,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very foggy day &amp; unpleasant day. Wind about S by E. At church in the morning. Tinley, Mr Brereton of Liverpool &amp; I walked to Tynemouth in the afternoon. Dined at Tinley's. Met Mr Brereton &amp; a Mr Smith of Oporto.</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":352,"lock":null}
20:13:18.767 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.767 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/14/369
20:13:18.767 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":369,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very foggy day &amp; unpleasant day. Wind about S by E. At church in the morning. Tinley, Mr Brereton of Liverpool &amp; I walked to Tynemouth in the afternoon. Dined at Tinley's. Met Mr Brereton &amp; a Mr Smith of Oporto.</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":352,"lock":null}
20:13:18.767 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/15/370
20:13:18.767 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":370,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull day but dry. Wind about S. Received a letter from William of the sale of the Hope at 34/6, a miserable price = 8/6 freight. After laying a fortnight at London. Dined at home. Wind changed to about SW in the evening.</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":353,"lock":null}
20:13:18.767 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.768 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/15/370
20:13:18.768 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":370,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull day but dry. Wind about S. Received a letter from William of the sale of the Hope at 34/6, a miserable price = 8/6 freight. After laying a fortnight at London. Dined at home. Wind changed to about SW in the evening.</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":353,"lock":null}
20:13:18.768 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/16/371
20:13:18.768 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":371,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind S &amp; SW. Went at Williams request to look for Baxter Arthur of the amety, but he had gone to sea. Called upon J<font color=#BFBFBF>u</font>n<font color=#BFBFBF>io</font><sup>r</sup> Carr &amp; gave him William's letter to pay me the balance of the Hope's freight account. Dinned at home. Wrote to William. Payed into Chapmans &pound;15 rents on account of ex<font color=#BFBFBF>ecut</font>ors</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":354,"lock":null}
20:13:18.768 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.768 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/16/371
20:13:18.768 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":371,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind S &amp; SW. Went at Williams request to look for Baxter Arthur of the amety, but he had gone to sea. Called upon J<font color=#BFBFBF>u</font>n<font color=#BFBFBF>io</font><sup>r</sup> Carr &amp; gave him William's letter to pay me the balance of the Hope's freight account. Dinned at home. Wrote to William. Payed into Chapmans &pound;15 rents on account of ex<font color=#BFBFBF>ecut</font>ors</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":354,"lock":null}
20:13:18.768 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/17/372
20:13:18.768 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":372,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A little rain in the morning. Wind W &amp; SW. A pleasant afternoon. Dined on board the Combatant, Captain Barnes. A ship of the Tinleys, an agreeable party consisting of J Tinley, A Harry, Mr Boswell, Captain Webb, W Barnes, Mr Richardson &amp; self, went to the play at &frac12; price to pass an hour but returned home at 10 o'clock at which hour Mrs Scott had made up her mind I should be in. Her conduct towards me so pointed &amp; bad that I have determined to go to lodgings as I neither have nor do I wish to give her any annoyance at the same time. I don't choose to submit to it myself, for it seems her temper &amp; disposition neither to be happy &amp; comfortable herself or to let others be so.</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":355,"lock":null}
20:13:18.768 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.769 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/17/372
20:13:18.769 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":372,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A little rain in the morning. Wind W &amp; SW. A pleasant afternoon. Dined on board the Combatant, Captain Barnes. A ship of the Tinleys, an agreeable party consisting of J Tinley, A Harry, Mr Boswell, Captain Webb, W Barnes, Mr Richardson &amp; self, went to the play at &frac12; price to pass an hour but returned home at 10 o'clock at which hour Mrs Scott had made up her mind I should be in. Her conduct towards me so pointed &amp; bad that I have determined to go to lodgings as I neither have nor do I wish to give her any annoyance at the same time. I don't choose to submit to it myself, for it seems her temper &amp; disposition neither to be happy &amp; comfortable herself or to let others be so.</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":355,"lock":null}
20:13:18.769 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/18/373
20:13:18.769 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":373,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine day. Wind WNW. Took a walk to Tynemouth. Dined at home. At the whist club in the evening</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":356,"lock":null}
20:13:18.769 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.769 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/18/373
20:13:18.769 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":373,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine day. Wind WNW. Took a walk to Tynemouth. Dined at home. At the whist club in the evening</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":356,"lock":null}
20:13:18.769 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/19/374
20:13:18.769 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":374,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Blowing a gale of wind from NW with a little rain. Captain Bunbury, Mr Mark &amp; I went over to Sunderland &amp; dined at the mess of the 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment &amp; spent a very agreeable day, the dinner given to colonel Cookson who was for many years commanding officer of the regiment in India. Slept at <span class=highlight_yellow>Joyscys</span> Inn</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":357,"lock":null}
20:13:18.769 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.770 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/19/374
20:13:18.770 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":374,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Blowing a gale of wind from NW with a little rain. Captain Bunbury, Mr Mark &amp; I went over to Sunderland &amp; dined at the mess of the 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment &amp; spent a very agreeable day, the dinner given to colonel Cookson who was for many years commanding officer of the regiment in India. Slept at <span class=highlight_yellow>Joyscys</span> Inn</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":357,"lock":null}
20:13:18.770 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/2/357
20:13:18.770 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":357,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind N by S towards evening the wind got up &amp; increased to a perfect gale from the S by W &amp; excessively cold. Understand that several ships, all on shore, some near Sunderland. Walked with Mr Mark &amp; called upon Captain Bunbury &amp; Mr Hopkins. Dined at home. In the evening went to the Commercial to see Mr Ildeston who was waiting there for Mr Tibbs. Received an invitation &amp; suppered with the committee of Association for prosecuting felons. Sat rather late.</p>","pageId":716,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":340,"lock":null}
20:13:18.770 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.770 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/2/357
20:13:18.770 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":357,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind N by S towards evening the wind got up &amp; increased to a perfect gale from the S by W &amp; excessively cold. Understand that several ships, all on shore, some near Sunderland. Walked with Mr Mark &amp; called upon Captain Bunbury &amp; Mr Hopkins. Dined at home. In the evening went to the Commercial to see Mr Ildeston who was waiting there for Mr Tibbs. Received an invitation &amp; suppered with the committee of Association for prosecuting felons. Sat rather late.</p>","pageId":716,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":340,"lock":null}
20:13:18.770 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/20/375
20:13:18.770 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":375,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild morning. Wind about W by N. Blowing strong. After breakfast, called at the Barrack &amp; afterwards returned to Shields. Dined with Mrs Scott &amp; in the evening at the whist club at R Pearts</p>","pageId":718,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":358,"lock":null}
20:13:18.770 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
