20:13:18.776 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":384,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine weather day. Excessively cold. Wind SW. Engaged in the morning drawing &amp; on board ship. Dined at home. Took wine with Mark Cunningham &amp; Boswick at the Albion</p>","pageId":718,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":367,"lock":null}
20:13:18.776 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/3/358
20:13:18.776 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":358,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild day and wind about W by N. Walked to Tynemouth called at Tibbs upon Mr Ildeston who returned to Shields with me. Dined at home &amp; in the evening met Mr Ildeston at Mr Baskers to take wine. Mr Mark there.</p>","pageId":716,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":341,"lock":null}
20:13:18.776 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.776 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/3/358
20:13:18.776 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":358,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild day and wind about W by N. Walked to Tynemouth called at Tibbs upon Mr Ildeston who returned to Shields with me. Dined at home &amp; in the evening met Mr Ildeston at Mr Baskers to take wine. Mr Mark there.</p>","pageId":716,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":341,"lock":null}
20:13:18.776 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/30/385
20:13:18.776 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":385,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Rather thick. Wind SW. Dined at home. Paid into Chapmans on my own account &pound;10.11.2</p>","pageId":719,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":368,"lock":null}
20:13:18.776 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.777 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/30/385
20:13:18.777 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":385,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Rather thick. Wind SW. Dined at home. Paid into Chapmans on my own account &pound;10.11.2</p>","pageId":719,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":368,"lock":null}
20:13:18.777 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/31/386
20:13:18.777 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":386,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant day. Wind WNW. Engaged in the morning drawing &amp; on board of ship. Sails all on shore at Mr Hearns. Ordered the running rigging to be taken to Mr Sharps, as there's nothing safe on board from the nightly visits the thieves pay. Thus ends the year, a very poor one for ship &amp; owners. I for one can safely say that I have not made one farthing. I only hope the next year will be productive of more good or I know not what will be the consequence. Dined at home &amp; in the evening attended the theatre. The <span class=highlight_yellow>bespeak</span> of the Subscriber to the Assemblies. A very fair house, as things <span class=highlight_yellow>are</span>.</p>","pageId":719,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":369,"lock":null}
20:13:18.777 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.777 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/31/386
20:13:18.777 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":386,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant day. Wind WNW. Engaged in the morning drawing &amp; on board of ship. Sails all on shore at Mr Hearns. Ordered the running rigging to be taken to Mr Sharps, as there's nothing safe on board from the nightly visits the thieves pay. Thus ends the year, a very poor one for ship &amp; owners. I for one can safely say that I have not made one farthing. I only hope the next year will be productive of more good or I know not what will be the consequence. Dined at home &amp; in the evening attended the theatre. The <span class=highlight_yellow>bespeak</span> of the Subscriber to the Assemblies. A very fair house, as things <span class=highlight_yellow>are</span>.</p>","pageId":719,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":369,"lock":null}
20:13:18.777 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/4/359
20:13:18.777 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":359,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind WSW. During the morning at home reading. Dined at home &amp; in the evening at the whist club. Bad accounts of losses in the Monday morning gale upon the Yorkshire coast.</p>","pageId":716,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":342,"lock":null}
20:13:18.777 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.778 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/4/359
20:13:18.778 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":359,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind WSW. During the morning at home reading. Dined at home &amp; in the evening at the whist club. Bad accounts of losses in the Monday morning gale upon the Yorkshire coast.</p>","pageId":716,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":342,"lock":null}
20:13:18.778 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/5/360
20:13:18.778 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":360,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant day, but rather cool &amp; wind SW. Dined at Mr Tibbs at Tynemouth. Mr &amp; Mrs Tinley, Miss Hewson, Mr &amp; Mrs L Fenwick, Mr &amp; Mrs I Fenwick, Misses Drury, Captain Bunbury &amp; self the party</p>","pageId":716,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":343,"lock":null}
20:13:18.778 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.778 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/5/360
20:13:18.778 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":360,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant day, but rather cool &amp; wind SW. Dined at Mr Tibbs at Tynemouth. Mr &amp; Mrs Tinley, Miss Hewson, Mr &amp; Mrs L Fenwick, Mr &amp; Mrs I Fenwick, Misses Drury, Captain Bunbury &amp; self the party</p>","pageId":716,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":343,"lock":null}
20:13:18.778 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/6/361
20:13:18.778 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":361,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful day. Fresh breeze from SW. The two Mrs Dixons came down from Benton, lunched &amp; took Emma back with them. Dined at home. In the evening attended the whist club at <span class=highlight_yellow>Greenhows</span>. Towards night it began to blow very hard. Mr Harry, H French, Mr Mark &amp; I took wind at the George. Ps Sub<font color=#BFBFBF>scription</font> 1G to newsroom</p>","pageId":716,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":344,"lock":null}
20:13:18.778 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.779 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/6/361
20:13:18.779 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":361,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful day. Fresh breeze from SW. The two Mrs Dixons came down from Benton, lunched &amp; took Emma back with them. Dined at home. In the evening attended the whist club at <span class=highlight_yellow>Greenhows</span>. Towards night it began to blow very hard. Mr Harry, H French, Mr Mark &amp; I took wind at the George. Ps Sub<font color=#BFBFBF>scription</font> 1G to newsroom</p>","pageId":716,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":344,"lock":null}
20:13:18.779 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/7/362
20:13:18.779 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":362,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Blowing a heavy gale of wind all night from S by E. This morning SSW &amp; towards afternoon got to W by S. Received a letter from William informing  me of <span class=highlight_yellow>Jon</span> Young demanding payment of their claims. Attended morning service. Dined at home. In the evening took wine with <span class=highlight_yellow>Mr</span> Harry at the Albion.</p>","pageId":716,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":345,"lock":null}
20:13:18.779 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.779 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/7/362
20:13:18.779 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":362,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Blowing a heavy gale of wind all night from S by E. This morning SSW &amp; towards afternoon got to W by S. Received a letter from William informing  me of <span class=highlight_yellow>Jon</span> Young demanding payment of their claims. Attended morning service. Dined at home. In the evening took wine with <span class=highlight_yellow>Mr</span> Harry at the Albion.</p>","pageId":716,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":345,"lock":null}
20:13:18.779 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/8/363
20:13:18.779 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":363,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant winters morning. Wind NNW which changed in the afternoon to about WSW. Got &pound;5 from the bank for own use. Dined with J Tinley. Went to the theatre at <span class=highlight_yellow>the Prince</span>. Mrs Metcalf of Tynemouth buried today</p>","pageId":716,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":346,"lock":null}
