20:13:18.811 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":107,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An exceedingly fine day &amp; mild wind W by S. Dined at the George Tavern. The dinner given by a party of married men consisting of J Dale president: Mr Clark   vise: A Dale, J Tindley, W C Wright. R Peach, A Metcalf     Bachelors: I Craig, Mr Horner, E Drurg, J Keilyside, A Harry</p>","pageId":694,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":102,"lock":null}
20:13:18.811 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/11/108
20:13:18.811 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":108,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful mild day. Wind WSW. Master R Jldesters and I dined on board the Hope &amp; spent the afternoon</p>","pageId":694,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":103,"lock":null}
20:13:18.811 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.812 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/11/108
20:13:18.812 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":108,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful mild day. Wind WSW. Master R Jldesters and I dined on board the Hope &amp; spent the afternoon</p>","pageId":694,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":103,"lock":null}
20:13:18.812 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/12/109
20:13:18.812 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":109,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind WSW. Received a most distressing letter from Mr Vernon Rector of Carlow of the poor Bafer being very ill of a typhous fever. I therefore have determined to set off for carlow in the morning from South Shields at 5 o'clock by Pelot Leeds coach</p>","pageId":694,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":104,"lock":null}
20:13:18.812 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.812 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/12/109
20:13:18.812 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":109,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind WSW. Received a most distressing letter from Mr Vernon Rector of Carlow of the poor Bafer being very ill of a typhous fever. I therefore have determined to set off for carlow in the morning from South Shields at 5 o'clock by Pelot Leeds coach</p>","pageId":694,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":104,"lock":null}
20:13:18.812 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/13/110
20:13:18.812 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":110,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A heavy fall of rain last night during the day showers &amp; in the evening it came down in torrents. Wind variable from SS to NW. Not able to leave for Carlow, this morning being  Sunday, coach doesn't run, but shall start in the morning. Dined at home. At church in the morning.</p>","pageId":694,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":105,"lock":null}
20:13:18.812 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.812 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/13/110
20:13:18.813 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":110,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A heavy fall of rain last night during the day showers &amp; in the evening it came down in torrents. Wind variable from SS to NW. Not able to leave for Carlow, this morning being  Sunday, coach doesn't run, but shall start in the morning. Dined at home. At church in the morning.</p>","pageId":694,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":105,"lock":null}
20:13:18.813 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/14/111
20:13:18.813 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":111,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up this morning at 3 o'clock &amp; left South Shields at &frac12; past 4 o'clock coach for Carlow. A fine day, arrived at Leeds at 6 o'clock where I stay all night</p>","pageId":694,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":106,"lock":null}
20:13:18.813 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.813 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/14/111
20:13:18.813 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":111,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up this morning at 3 o'clock &amp; left South Shields at &frac12; past 4 o'clock coach for Carlow. A fine day, arrived at Leeds at 6 o'clock where I stay all night</p>","pageId":694,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":106,"lock":null}
20:13:18.813 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/15/112
20:13:18.813 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":112,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Much annoyed at finding I should not get to Liverpool in time to catch the Post Office packit for Dublin. Deceived by the people at the coach office. Left Leeds by coach at &frac12; past 5 o'clock. Outside a cloudy morning, soon began to rain &amp; continued very heavy all day. Reached Huddersfield at 10 o'clock. I think where I had to wait an hour &amp; change coach. Got to Manchester at 1 o'clock &amp; found to my surprise &amp; vexation the coach would not proceed until 5 o'clock. Kicked up a row at the office, got part of any money returned &amp; fortunately caught a coach about to start for Liverpool where I arrived at 6 o'clock &amp; immediately embarked on board the &quot;Bereuenyham&quot;  steam boat which as luck would have it, was that evening going to start for Dublin. Wind WSW</p>","pageId":694,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":107,"lock":null}
20:13:18.813 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.814 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/15/112
20:13:18.814 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":112,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Much annoyed at finding I should not get to Liverpool in time to catch the Post Office packit for Dublin. Deceived by the people at the coach office. Left Leeds by coach at &frac12; past 5 o'clock. Outside a cloudy morning, soon began to rain &amp; continued very heavy all day. Reached Huddersfield at 10 o'clock. I think where I had to wait an hour &amp; change coach. Got to Manchester at 1 o'clock &amp; found to my surprise &amp; vexation the coach would not proceed until 5 o'clock. Kicked up a row at the office, got part of any money returned &amp; fortunately caught a coach about to start for Liverpool where I arrived at 6 o'clock &amp; immediately embarked on board the &quot;Bereuenyham&quot;  steam boat which as luck would have it, was that evening going to start for Dublin. Wind WSW</p>","pageId":694,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":107,"lock":null}
20:13:18.814 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/16/113
20:13:18.814 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":113,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>During the whole of last night we had a heavy sea &amp; foul wind blowing WSW very hard, to contend with but fortunately a fine boat under us. As it was low water when we started, we overtook to steam Office packit at anchor, at the Rock not able to proceed for want of water, having left 2 &frac12;  hours before us so that after all, I lost no time, no thanks to the rascally clerks at the coach office. We kept company all night &amp; after a tedious passage arrived at the custom House quay, Dublin at 3 o'clock PM. Took my luggage to Mackens Hotel, Dawson Street where I stayed all night</p>","pageId":694,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":108,"lock":null}
20:13:18.814 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.814 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/16/113
20:13:18.814 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":113,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>During the whole of last night we had a heavy sea &amp; foul wind blowing WSW very hard, to contend with but fortunately a fine boat under us. As it was low water when we started, we overtook to steam Office packit at anchor, at the Rock not able to proceed for want of water, having left 2 &frac12;  hours before us so that after all, I lost no time, no thanks to the rascally clerks at the coach office. We kept company all night &amp; after a tedious passage arrived at the custom House quay, Dublin at 3 o'clock PM. Took my luggage to Mackens Hotel, Dawson Street where I stayed all night</p>","pageId":694,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":108,"lock":null}
