20:13:18.817 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":118,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":17,"sequence":5.0000,"text":"<figure>\r\n  <img src=\"images/img2842-image-map-tynemouth-to-carlow.jpg\" width=\"600px\" />\"\r\n  <figcaption>Map of journey from Tynemouth to Carlow</figcaption>\r\n</figure>","pageId":null,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":null,"lock":null}
20:13:18.817 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/17/119
20:13:18.817 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":119,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":17,"sequence":6.0000,"text":"<p>Left Dublin outside the Carlow coach at 9 o'clock AM. When I arrived at 4 o'clock in a state of anxiety impossible for me to describe, misery was in store for me &amp; on enquiring of the servant &quot;how my sister was?&quot; to my insufferable horror I learned she was dead. The fever was so malignant nature could not struggle with it &amp; and on Sunday last at 10 o'clock I lost one of the kindest &amp; most affectionate of sisters &amp; the town one of the best &amp; most benevolent of human beings. I was doomed not even one last parting look at her cold remains for such was the rapidity with which decomposition took place that her remains were obliged to be deposited in the select tomb next to her dear husband yesterday. However upon ...</p>","pageId":694,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":109,"lock":null}
20:13:18.817 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.817 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/17/119
20:13:18.817 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":119,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":17,"sequence":6.0000,"text":"<p>Left Dublin outside the Carlow coach at 9 o'clock AM. When I arrived at 4 o'clock in a state of anxiety impossible for me to describe, misery was in store for me &amp; on enquiring of the servant &quot;how my sister was?&quot; to my insufferable horror I learned she was dead. The fever was so malignant nature could not struggle with it &amp; and on Sunday last at 10 o'clock I lost one of the kindest &amp; most affectionate of sisters &amp; the town one of the best &amp; most benevolent of human beings. I was doomed not even one last parting look at her cold remains for such was the rapidity with which decomposition took place that her remains were obliged to be deposited in the select tomb next to her dear husband yesterday. However upon ...</p>","pageId":694,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":109,"lock":null}
20:13:18.817 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/17/120
20:13:18.817 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":120,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":17,"sequence":7.0000,"text":"<p>... upon reflection, I am resigned and convinced that I have been spared a great deal of painful feeling distress &amp; misery by not having witnessed her suffering &amp; tis a consolation to find that she has had so many kind &amp; attentive friends about her, particularly one Mr Vernon, whose conduct both to my poor sister &amp; myself I shall I trust never forget or be ungrateful for. He insists upon my staying at his house &amp; his great anxiety id to console &amp; make me comfortable. Poor little Emma has fortunately been at Captain Butlins at Broomville &amp; the boys at school. Poor children, they are too young to be sensible of the irreparable loss they have sustained. But I trust that god the father of all will spare &amp; enable me to supply the place of their dear parents they have lost. John J Baker came up to see me in the evening</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":110,"lock":null}
20:13:18.817 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.817 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/17/120
20:13:18.817 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":120,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":17,"sequence":7.0000,"text":"<p>... upon reflection, I am resigned and convinced that I have been spared a great deal of painful feeling distress &amp; misery by not having witnessed her suffering &amp; tis a consolation to find that she has had so many kind &amp; attentive friends about her, particularly one Mr Vernon, whose conduct both to my poor sister &amp; myself I shall I trust never forget or be ungrateful for. He insists upon my staying at his house &amp; his great anxiety id to console &amp; make me comfortable. Poor little Emma has fortunately been at Captain Butlins at Broomville &amp; the boys at school. Poor children, they are too young to be sensible of the irreparable loss they have sustained. But I trust that god the father of all will spare &amp; enable me to supply the place of their dear parents they have lost. John J Baker came up to see me in the evening</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":110,"lock":null}
20:13:18.817 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/18/121
20:13:18.817 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":121,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind about North. Much refreshed by a good night's rest. Received a letter from William. Wrote to Mrs Scott. F Falknes &amp; Mr J Fitzmaurice called upon me. Took a long &amp; retired walk upon the banks of the river Barrow with Mr Vernon, returned to dine. John J Baker dined with us</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":111,"lock":null}
20:13:18.817 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.817 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/18/121
20:13:18.819 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":121,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind about North. Much refreshed by a good night's rest. Received a letter from William. Wrote to Mrs Scott. F Falknes &amp; Mr J Fitzmaurice called upon me. Took a long &amp; retired walk upon the banks of the river Barrow with Mr Vernon, returned to dine. John J Baker dined with us</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":111,"lock":null}
20:13:18.819 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/19/122
20:13:18.819 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":122,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather cloudy. Wind N. Wrote to William. J Harry &amp; Mr Jamison called upon Mr I Called upon &amp; saw poor old Miss Falkman who seemed much affected &amp; grieved at dear Bopy's death. Took a walk to Clogrennane, coll Rockforts seat with Mr Vernon &amp; the boys. Caught in heavy shower of rain on our way home got wet through. The boys dined with us</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":112,"lock":null}
20:13:18.819 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.819 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/19/122
20:13:18.819 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":122,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather cloudy. Wind N. Wrote to William. J Harry &amp; Mr Jamison called upon Mr I Called upon &amp; saw poor old Miss Falkman who seemed much affected &amp; grieved at dear Bopy's death. Took a walk to Clogrennane, coll Rockforts seat with Mr Vernon &amp; the boys. Caught in heavy shower of rain on our way home got wet through. The boys dined with us</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":112,"lock":null}
20:13:18.819 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/2/99
20:13:18.819 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":99,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very cold day with a little rain. Wind NNE. Dined on board the Hope. Had a very pleasant party.  J Tinley, H Harry &amp; Mr Marks. Received a letter from William</p>","pageId":693,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":94,"lock":null}
20:13:18.819 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.820 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/2/99
20:13:18.820 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":99,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very cold day with a little rain. Wind NNE. Dined on board the Hope. Had a very pleasant party.  J Tinley, H Harry &amp; Mr Marks. Received a letter from William</p>","pageId":693,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":94,"lock":null}
20:13:18.820 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/20/123
20:13:18.820 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":123,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant day. Wind still from the North. Did not go to church. Read the service at home. Received a letter from William remitting a &pound;50 Bank Post bill. Took a long walk with Mr Vernon along the Athy road &amp; returned to dinner at &frac12; past 5 o'clock. The boys again with us. W W Fishbrown called upon me</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":113,"lock":null}
20:13:18.820 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.820 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/20/123
20:13:18.820 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":123,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant day. Wind still from the North. Did not go to church. Read the service at home. Received a letter from William remitting a &pound;50 Bank Post bill. Took a long walk with Mr Vernon along the Athy road &amp; returned to dinner at &frac12; past 5 o'clock. The boys again with us. W W Fishbrown called upon me</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":113,"lock":null}
20:13:18.820 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/21/124
20:13:18.820 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":124,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind still from the North. Engaged all the morning in examining Dear Betsy's books &amp; papers. In the afternoon Mr Vernon, the boys &amp; I walked out to Crossleigh to see the Herrings &amp; also called upon F Falkener, went round by Old derrgy &amp; home to dinner</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":114,"lock":null}
20:13:18.820 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.821 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/21/124
20:13:18.821 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":124,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind still from the North. Engaged all the morning in examining Dear Betsy's books &amp; papers. In the afternoon Mr Vernon, the boys &amp; I walked out to Crossleigh to see the Herrings &amp; also called upon F Falkener, went round by Old derrgy &amp; home to dinner</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":114,"lock":null}
20:13:18.821 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/22/125
20:13:18.821 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":125,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of the same sort of weather with the cool wind. Engaged all the morning with Mr Turner in examining &amp; entering rents. In the afternoon Mr Vernon &amp; I took a walk along the Kilkenny Road, returned home to drefs &amp; took a family dinner with Mr W<sup>en</sup> Fishburn who was exceedingly kind, but yet I should have preferred dining quietly at Mr Vernon's. Received a letter from William</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":115,"lock":null}
20:13:18.821 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.822 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/22/125
20:13:18.822 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":125,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of the same sort of weather with the cool wind. Engaged all the morning with Mr Turner in examining &amp; entering rents. In the afternoon Mr Vernon &amp; I took a walk along the Kilkenny Road, returned home to drefs &amp; took a family dinner with Mr W<sup>en</sup> Fishburn who was exceedingly kind, but yet I should have preferred dining quietly at Mr Vernon's. Received a letter from William</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":115,"lock":null}
20:13:18.822 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/23/126
20:13:18.822 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":126,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A change of wind and weather. Wind WSW with heavy rain which warmed the air. Engaged all the morning in taking inventory of furniture &amp; packing up the linin that I intended to go to England. Dined at Coopers Hill. Spent a very quiet &amp; pleasant day</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":116,"lock":null}
20:13:18.822 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.823 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/23/126
20:13:18.823 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":126,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A change of wind and weather. Wind WSW with heavy rain which warmed the air. Engaged all the morning in taking inventory of furniture &amp; packing up the linin that I intended to go to England. Dined at Coopers Hill. Spent a very quiet &amp; pleasant day</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":116,"lock":null}
20:13:18.823 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/24/127
20:13:18.823 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":127,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild day. Wind WSW. Engaged all day in finishing inventory he. Dined at Mr Vernon's with the boys.</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":117,"lock":null}
20:13:18.823 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.823 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/24/127
20:13:18.823 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":127,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild day. Wind WSW. Engaged all day in finishing inventory he. Dined at Mr Vernon's with the boys.</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":117,"lock":null}
20:13:18.823 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/25/128
20:13:18.823 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":128,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>This day rather cooler. Wind NW with showers of rain. Engaged again all the morning in packing up &amp; separating the books that I take to England from those for sale. Called upon Dr Reed &amp; Dr Home. Dined at Mr Vernon's with the boys Received letter from fanny Smith</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":118,"lock":null}
20:13:18.823 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.824 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/25/128
20:13:18.824 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":128,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>This day rather cooler. Wind NW with showers of rain. Engaged again all the morning in packing up &amp; separating the books that I take to England from those for sale. Called upon Dr Reed &amp; Dr Home. Dined at Mr Vernon's with the boys Received letter from fanny Smith</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":118,"lock":null}
20:13:18.824 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/26/129
20:13:18.824 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":129,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A little rain in the morning. Wind WSW but afterwards turned out a beautiful day. Wrote to William. Called upon Mr Jameson. Had a very delightful drive in the afternoon to Broomfield.  Found the Butlers &amp; Emma quite well, a very affecting meeting, my feelings quite overpowered un &amp; I blubbered like a child, but I could not help it.</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":119,"lock":null}
20:13:18.824 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.825 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/26/129
20:13:18.825 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":129,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A little rain in the morning. Wind WSW but afterwards turned out a beautiful day. Wrote to William. Called upon Mr Jameson. Had a very delightful drive in the afternoon to Broomfield.  Found the Butlers &amp; Emma quite well, a very affecting meeting, my feelings quite overpowered un &amp; I blubbered like a child, but I could not help it.</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":119,"lock":null}
20:13:18.825 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/27/130
20:13:18.825 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":130,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet day. Wind WSW. Captain Butler read the morning service. We afterwards took a drive between showers &amp; returned to dinner</p>","pageId":696,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":120,"lock":null}
20:13:18.825 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.826 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/27/130
20:13:18.826 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":130,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet day. Wind WSW. Captain Butler read the morning service. We afterwards took a drive between showers &amp; returned to dinner</p>","pageId":696,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":120,"lock":null}
20:13:18.826 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/28/131
20:13:18.826 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":131,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull and damp morning. Wind the same. Left Broomville &amp; reached Carlow without rain. Received a letter from William. Dined with Mr Vernon</p>","pageId":696,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":121,"lock":null}
20:13:18.826 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.826 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/28/131
20:13:18.826 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":131,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull and damp morning. Wind the same. Left Broomville &amp; reached Carlow without rain. Received a letter from William. Dined with Mr Vernon</p>","pageId":696,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":121,"lock":null}
20:13:18.826 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/29/132
20:13:18.826 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":132,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another dull day with showers of rain. Wind WSW. Engaged in the morning writing and walked out with Mr Vernon, returned to dinner.  Mr Jameson &amp; Reverend O'Connor dined with us. Spent a very pleasant day</p>","pageId":696,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":122,"lock":null}
20:13:18.826 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.827 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/29/132
