20:13:18.868 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/22/186
20:13:18.868 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":186,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Left Carlow for Dublin to attend an appointment before Mr Townsend, a master in chancery tomorrow Arrived in Dublin &frac12; past 4 o'clock &ndash; after a pleasant journey. Dined at Mackens</p>","pageId":700,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":176,"lock":null}
20:13:18.868 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/23/187
20:13:18.868 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":187,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Called the first thing upon Mr Carmichael. Attended the master at 11 o'clock at the Four Courts. Damm the law say I. My patience is exhausted, got nothing done this day, for want of an affidavit that there were no other next of kin having but Mr Falkener &amp; ourselves. Dined at Mackens. Suppered at the Steades with Ian Gale</p>","pageId":700,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":177,"lock":null}
20:13:18.868 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.868 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/23/187
20:13:18.868 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":187,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Called the first thing upon Mr Carmichael. Attended the master at 11 o'clock at the Four Courts. Damm the law say I. My patience is exhausted, got nothing done this day, for want of an affidavit that there were no other next of kin having but Mr Falkener &amp; ourselves. Dined at Mackens. Suppered at the Steades with Ian Gale</p>","pageId":700,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":177,"lock":null}
20:13:18.868 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/24/188
20:13:18.868 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":188,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. This being a holy day at the Court of Chancery, we could do nothing. I therefor went in the steam boat to Kingstown &amp; dined with J Thompson on board the Royal Charlotte. The Mayor of Anglesey came down &amp; took a sail in his yacht the Pearl. Lieutenant M  Paget came on too and the Royal Charlotte to whom I was introduced. No great honor as it is not likely he will know me again.</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":178,"lock":null}
20:13:18.868 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.869 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/24/188
20:13:18.869 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":188,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. This being a holy day at the Court of Chancery, we could do nothing. I therefor went in the steam boat to Kingstown &amp; dined with J Thompson on board the Royal Charlotte. The Mayor of Anglesey came down &amp; took a sail in his yacht the Pearl. Lieutenant M  Paget came on too and the Royal Charlotte to whom I was introduced. No great honor as it is not likely he will know me again.</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":178,"lock":null}
20:13:18.869 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/25/189
20:13:18.869 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":189,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Attended the Master Townsend, who appointed us guardians. Dined at Mackens Before dinner had a hot &amp; dusty walk to Phoenix Park</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":179,"lock":null}
20:13:18.869 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.869 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/25/189
20:13:18.869 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":189,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Attended the Master Townsend, who appointed us guardians. Dined at Mackens Before dinner had a hot &amp; dusty walk to Phoenix Park</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":179,"lock":null}
20:13:18.869 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/26/190
20:13:18.869 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":190,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An exceptionally hot day. Attended the Master again for him to look over draft of report, when he thought it would be better to appoint me sole guardian. I cannot make up mind to take in so much trouble difficulties &amp; anxiety that I feel very unhappy. Cannot stand it much longer. Dined at Mackens</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":180,"lock":null}
20:13:18.869 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.870 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/26/190
20:13:18.870 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":190,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An exceptionally hot day. Attended the Master again for him to look over draft of report, when he thought it would be better to appoint me sole guardian. I cannot make up mind to take in so much trouble difficulties &amp; anxiety that I feel very unhappy. Cannot stand it much longer. Dined at Mackens</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":180,"lock":null}
20:13:18.870 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/27/191
20:13:18.870 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":191,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another hot summers day. Called at Mr Carmichael's &amp; from the difficult situation in which I am placed, determined upon asking my brother to come to Ireland &amp; going to Carlow tomorrow there to remain until I either see him or have a letter from him in answer to one I wrote this day. Wrote also to Mrs Scott. Dined at Mackens &amp; went to the Lying In Hospital Gardens where there was an immense assembly of company</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":181,"lock":null}
20:13:18.870 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.870 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/27/191
20:13:18.870 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":191,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another hot summers day. Called at Mr Carmichael's &amp; from the difficult situation in which I am placed, determined upon asking my brother to come to Ireland &amp; going to Carlow tomorrow there to remain until I either see him or have a letter from him in answer to one I wrote this day. Wrote also to Mrs Scott. Dined at Mackens &amp; went to the Lying In Hospital Gardens where there was an immense assembly of company</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":181,"lock":null}
20:13:18.870 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/28/192
20:13:18.870 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":192,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very hot day. Left Dublin for Carlow The Heat most oppressive &amp; clouds of dust. We did not reach Carlow until 7 o'clock. The coach wheel taking fire Dined at Mr Jamesons. Letter from William</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":182,"lock":null}
20:13:18.870 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.871 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/28/192
20:13:18.871 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":192,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very hot day. Left Dublin for Carlow The Heat most oppressive &amp; clouds of dust. We did not reach Carlow until 7 o'clock. The coach wheel taking fire Dined at Mr Jamesons. Letter from William</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":182,"lock":null}
20:13:18.871 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/29/193
20:13:18.871 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":193,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another very hot day. Attended morning service at Graigh Church to hear a sermon preached by Mr Vernon. For the education of poor children, a collection was made Dined at Mr Jameson. Bathed in the Barrow A letter from William</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":183,"lock":null}
20:13:18.871 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.871 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/29/193
20:13:18.871 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":193,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another very hot day. Attended morning service at Graigh Church to hear a sermon preached by Mr Vernon. For the education of poor children, a collection was made Dined at Mr Jameson. Bathed in the Barrow A letter from William</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":183,"lock":null}
20:13:18.871 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/3/167
20:13:18.871 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":167,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Left Carlos at &frac12; past 7 o'clock in a car &amp; went to Athy to breakfast in 1 &frac12; hours being 11 &frac12; miles. Saw Captain Pope respecting the property there, but could learn nothing satisfactory. He said it was a divided property. His father having 2/3 one of which he sold &amp; the other 1/3 was the Galbraeths &amp; to prove it was a divided property he said the Galbraiths had granted a lease of their part consisting of an old house now in ruins &amp; a tanyard in the rear. He further said that the original lease had somehow or other got out of his hands, but that I could see it at Mr Warrens, Jarvis Street Dublin. That he would be glad to give me every information &amp; assistance &amp; allow me to see all papers that are in his possession. Returned to Carlow in the afternoon. Dined alone. Mr Vernon having gone to Coopers Hill &amp; went to a pleasant quadrille party at Mrs Whilliam Fishbourn. We kept it up until 3 o'clock</p>","pageId":699,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":157,"lock":null}
20:13:18.871 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.872 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/3/167
20:13:18.872 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":167,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Left Carlos at &frac12; past 7 o'clock in a car &amp; went to Athy to breakfast in 1 &frac12; hours being 11 &frac12; miles. Saw Captain Pope respecting the property there, but could learn nothing satisfactory. He said it was a divided property. His father having 2/3 one of which he sold &amp; the other 1/3 was the Galbraeths &amp; to prove it was a divided property he said the Galbraiths had granted a lease of their part consisting of an old house now in ruins &amp; a tanyard in the rear. He further said that the original lease had somehow or other got out of his hands, but that I could see it at Mr Warrens, Jarvis Street Dublin. That he would be glad to give me every information &amp; assistance &amp; allow me to see all papers that are in his possession. Returned to Carlow in the afternoon. Dined alone. Mr Vernon having gone to Coopers Hill &amp; went to a pleasant quadrille party at Mrs Whilliam Fishbourn. We kept it up until 3 o'clock</p>","pageId":699,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":157,"lock":null}
20:13:18.872 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/30/194
20:13:18.872 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":194,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Very little to do Received a letter from William. Saw Mr Turner who thought he would be able to give security Paid Carroll for spirits 19/- &amp; Haughton for funeral expenses &pound;8.18/-. Dined at Mr Vernon's &amp; took a long walk in the evening. Bathed in the morning</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":184,"lock":null}
20:13:18.872 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.872 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/30/194
20:13:18.872 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":194,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Very little to do Received a letter from William. Saw Mr Turner who thought he would be able to give security Paid Carroll for spirits 19/- &amp; Haughton for funeral expenses &pound;8.18/-. Dined at Mr Vernon's &amp; took a long walk in the evening. Bathed in the morning</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":184,"lock":null}
20:13:18.872 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/4/168
20:13:18.872 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":168,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet day. Quite a deluge of rain. Confined to the house all the morning by the wet. Engaged in covrtey for wrote a letter to Mr Buther of Athy. Asking to whom he pays rent for the tanyard. Dined at home with Mr Vernon</p>","pageId":699,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":158,"lock":null}
20:13:18.872 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.873 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/4/168
20:13:18.873 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":168,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet day. Quite a deluge of rain. Confined to the house all the morning by the wet. Engaged in covrtey for wrote a letter to Mr Buther of Athy. Asking to whom he pays rent for the tanyard. Dined at home with Mr Vernon</p>","pageId":699,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":158,"lock":null}
20:13:18.873 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/5/169
20:13:18.873 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":169,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A wet day. Heavy showers Dined with Mr Vernon, the two Careys dined with us &amp; Mr Moor. Spent a pleasant day. Agreed to let the house to Mr Dugan at &pound;35 a year when appointed guard<font color=#BFBFBF>ian</font></p>","pageId":699,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":159,"lock":null}
20:13:18.873 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.873 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/5/169
20:13:18.873 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":169,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A wet day. Heavy showers Dined with Mr Vernon, the two Careys dined with us &amp; Mr Moor. Spent a pleasant day. Agreed to let the house to Mr Dugan at &pound;35 a year when appointed guard<font color=#BFBFBF>ian</font></p>","pageId":699,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":159,"lock":null}
20:13:18.873 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/6/170
20:13:18.873 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":170,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Left Carlow for Dublin to take over letters of guardianship. A showery day. Got to Dublin at 5 o'clock</p>","pageId":699,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":160,"lock":null}
20:13:18.873 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.874 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/6/170
20:13:18.874 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":170,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Left Carlow for Dublin to take over letters of guardianship. A showery day. Got to Dublin at 5 o'clock</p>","pageId":699,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":160,"lock":null}
20:13:18.874 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/7/171
20:13:18.874 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":171,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>The first thing in the morning called upon Mr Carmichael but being engaged made an appointment with for 1 o'clock. Walked down to see the guard returned at the castle. Much to my surprise, met captain <span class=highlight_yellow>flu </span><span class=highlight_yellow>ie</span> Butler. At 1 o'clock saw Mr C<font color=#BFBFBF>armichael</font> &amp; then went to Mr Stocks the Proctor who filled up a form for the children to sign that they are willing. I should administer (in my opinion very inconsistent), sent it off by post to Mr Vernon. Dined at Mackens</p>","pageId":699,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":161,"lock":null}
20:13:18.874 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.874 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/7/171
20:13:18.874 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":171,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>The first thing in the morning called upon Mr Carmichael but being engaged made an appointment with for 1 o'clock. Walked down to see the guard returned at the castle. Much to my surprise, met captain <span class=highlight_yellow>flu </span><span class=highlight_yellow>ie</span> Butler. At 1 o'clock saw Mr C<font color=#BFBFBF>armichael</font> &amp; then went to Mr Stocks the Proctor who filled up a form for the children to sign that they are willing. I should administer (in my opinion very inconsistent), sent it off by post to Mr Vernon. Dined at Mackens</p>","pageId":699,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":161,"lock":null}
20:13:18.874 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/8/172
20:13:18.874 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":172,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Went to see the guard relieved &amp; afterwards attended morning service at the castle chapel. The interior very beautiful &amp; chaunting good. Called upon Char<font color=#BFBFBF>les</font> Hurry</span>. Walked out &amp; afterwards dined with Him</p>","pageId":699,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":162,"lock":null}
20:13:18.874 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.875 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/8/172
20:13:18.875 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":172,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Went to see the guard relieved &amp; afterwards attended morning service at the castle chapel. The interior very beautiful &amp; chaunting good. Called upon Char<font color=#BFBFBF>les</font> Hurry</span>. Walked out &amp; afterwards dined with Him</p>","pageId":699,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":162,"lock":null}
20:13:18.875 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/9/173
20:13:18.875 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":173,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day &amp; very warm. Engaged with Mr Carmichael &amp; wrote to Mr Vernon for leases etc. Received the documents which I sent by post on Saturday for the children to sign. Dined at Mackens. Much fatigued with my days work. Received a letter from William</p>","pageId":699,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":163,"lock":null}
20:13:18.875 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.875 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/9/173
20:13:18.875 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":173,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day &amp; very warm. Engaged with Mr Carmichael &amp; wrote to Mr Vernon for leases etc. Received the documents which I sent by post on Saturday for the children to sign. Dined at Mackens. Much fatigued with my days work. Received a letter from William</p>","pageId":699,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":163,"lock":null}
20:13:18.875 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/7/1/195
20:13:18.875 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":195,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":7,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine day after a fall of rain during the night. Bathed in the Barrow. Attended the examination of the boys at Mr Jameson's &amp; dined there Took a long walk with Mr Vernon in the evening Paid Montgomery Chemist &pound;1.2.4</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":185,"lock":null}
20:13:18.875 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.876 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/7/1/195
20:13:18.876 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":195,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":7,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine day after a fall of rain during the night. Bathed in the Barrow. Attended the examination of the boys at Mr Jameson's &amp; dined there Took a long walk with Mr Vernon in the evening Paid Montgomery Chemist &pound;1.2.4</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":185,"lock":null}
20:13:18.876 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/7/10/204
20:13:18.876 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":204,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":7,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine day. Left Carlow at 9 o'clock for Dublin with Emma who bore the fatigues of the journey well. Took her to Mrs Balskams in Grafton Street to sleep. Dined by myself at Mackens</p>","pageId":702,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":194,"lock":null}
20:13:18.876 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.877 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/7/10/204
20:13:18.877 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":204,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":7,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine day. Left Carlow at 9 o'clock for Dublin with Emma who bore the fatigues of the journey well. Took her to Mrs Balskams in Grafton Street to sleep. Dined by myself at Mackens</p>","pageId":702,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":194,"lock":null}
20:13:18.877 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/7/11/205
20:13:18.877 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":205,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":7,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. After breakfast, called &amp; saw Emma &amp; took her to see her friends, the Bagots in Peter Street who requested she should spend the day with them. Called upon Mr Carmichael &amp; got the leases. Dined with Char<font color=#BFBFBF>les</font> Hurry &amp; brought Emma home in the evening. Sent the leases by Mr Gale to Mr Vernon</p>","pageId":702,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":195,"lock":null}
20:13:18.877 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.877 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/7/11/205
20:13:18.877 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":205,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":7,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. After breakfast, called &amp; saw Emma &amp; took her to see her friends, the Bagots in Peter Street who requested she should spend the day with them. Called upon Mr Carmichael &amp; got the leases. Dined with Char<font color=#BFBFBF>les</font> Hurry &amp; brought Emma home in the evening. Sent the leases by Mr Gale to Mr Vernon</p>","pageId":702,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":195,"lock":null}
20:13:18.877 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/7/12/206
20:13:18.877 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":206,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":7,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Breakfast with Char<font color=#BFBFBF>les</font> Hurry. Hired a car &amp; took Emma to Kingstown. Left Luggage on board the St George steam boat &amp; afterwards dined at Greshams Hotel Left Kingstown at 7 o'clock with a great many passengers on board</p>","pageId":702,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":196,"lock":null}
20:13:18.877 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.878 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/7/12/206
20:13:18.878 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":206,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":7,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Breakfast with Char<font color=#BFBFBF>les</font> Hurry. Hired a car &amp; took Emma to Kingstown. Left Luggage on board the St George steam boat &amp; afterwards dined at Greshams Hotel Left Kingstown at 7 o'clock with a great many passengers on board</p>","pageId":702,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":196,"lock":null}
20:13:18.878 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/7/13/207
20:13:18.878 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":207,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":7,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>It began very early in the morning to rain &amp; blow hard &amp; it increased to a heavy gale. Nearly all on board sick. Obliged about 12 o'clock to lay to not being able to see land or make the floating light. The weather so thick. Between 1 &amp; 2 o'clock made the light &amp; got into Liverpool at 3 o'clock after a very stormy passage across of 20 hours and landed very wet. Got Emma to bed, much exhausted from the fatigues &amp; sickness. We stopped at the Angel Inn</p>","pageId":702,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":197,"lock":null}
20:13:18.878 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.878 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/7/13/207
20:13:18.878 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":207,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":7,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>It began very early in the morning to rain &amp; blow hard &amp; it increased to a heavy gale. Nearly all on board sick. Obliged about 12 o'clock to lay to not being able to see land or make the floating light. The weather so thick. Between 1 &amp; 2 o'clock made the light &amp; got into Liverpool at 3 o'clock after a very stormy passage across of 20 hours and landed very wet. Got Emma to bed, much exhausted from the fatigues &amp; sickness. We stopped at the Angel Inn</p>","pageId":702,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":197,"lock":null}
20:13:18.878 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/7/14/208
20:13:18.878 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":208,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":7,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A deluge of rain which continued all day. Left Liverpool for Leeds at 5 o'clock where we arrived about 6 o'clock. Poor Emma much annoyed by an eruption on the skin with great heat &amp; itching like the nettle rash from the heat &amp; sickness on board the steam boat. Took tea &amp; slept at Greaves</p>","pageId":702,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":198,"lock":null}
20:13:18.878 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.879 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/7/14/208
20:13:18.879 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":208,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":7,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A deluge of rain which continued all day. Left Liverpool for Leeds at 5 o'clock where we arrived about 6 o'clock. Poor Emma much annoyed by an eruption on the skin with great heat &amp; itching like the nettle rash from the heat &amp; sickness on board the steam boat. Took tea &amp; slept at Greaves</p>","pageId":702,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":198,"lock":null}
20:13:18.879 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/7/15/209
20:13:18.879 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":209,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":7,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Rather  cloudy in the morning, but turned out a fine day. Left Leeds at 6 o'clock for Shields where we arrived at 8 o'clock &amp; got home at 9 o'clock. Poor Emma tormented by the eruption. Dr Grunhow saw her &amp; sent some physic. Mrs Scott from home at Togston. Got some tea &amp; went to bed early</p>","pageId":702,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":199,"lock":null}
20:13:18.879 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.879 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/7/15/209
20:13:18.879 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":209,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":7,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Rather  cloudy in the morning, but turned out a fine day. Left Leeds at 6 o'clock for Shields where we arrived at 8 o'clock &amp; got home at 9 o'clock. Poor Emma tormented by the eruption. Dr Grunhow saw her &amp; sent some physic. Mrs Scott from home at Togston. Got some tea &amp; went to bed early</p>","pageId":702,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":199,"lock":null}
20:13:18.879 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/7/16/210
20:13:18.879 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":210,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":7,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Emma a great deal better. Engaged all morning writing to Mrs Falkener, Mr Verrnon &amp; Miss Scott. Dined with I Tindley</p>","pageId":703,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":200,"lock":null}
20:13:18.879 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
