20:13:18.881 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":213,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":7,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy day. Emma not very well. Stayed and dined at home. I dined with I Tindley</p>","pageId":703,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":203,"lock":null}
20:13:18.881 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/7/2/196
20:13:18.881 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":196,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":7,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Showers of rain in the morning, but towards noon cleared up &amp; turned into a beautiful day. Attended the examination John &amp; I walked out to Crossleigh &amp; I returned to dine with Mr Vernon. In the evening took a long walk</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":186,"lock":null}
20:13:18.881 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.882 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/7/2/196
20:13:18.882 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":196,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":7,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Showers of rain in the morning, but towards noon cleared up &amp; turned into a beautiful day. Attended the examination John &amp; I walked out to Crossleigh &amp; I returned to dine with Mr Vernon. In the evening took a long walk</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":186,"lock":null}
20:13:18.882 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/7/20/214
20:13:18.882 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":214,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":7,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Received a letter from Fanny Smith to take Emma to Togstow which I'm not able to do expecting the Hope. Went to church in the morning. I dined with H Harry, walked to Tynemouth in the evening &amp; on our return found Geo &amp; his wife had arrived. Wrote to Fanny Smith</p>","pageId":703,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":204,"lock":null}
20:13:18.882 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.882 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/7/20/214
20:13:18.882 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":214,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":7,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Received a letter from Fanny Smith to take Emma to Togstow which I'm not able to do expecting the Hope. Went to church in the morning. I dined with H Harry, walked to Tynemouth in the evening &amp; on our return found Geo &amp; his wife had arrived. Wrote to Fanny Smith</p>","pageId":703,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":204,"lock":null}
20:13:18.882 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/7/21/215
20:13:18.882 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":215,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":7,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A tremendous fall of rain all the morning, fear it will do much injury to the crops. Dined with I Tindley. Emma spent the day with Mrs Greenhow</p>","pageId":703,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":205,"lock":null}
20:13:18.882 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
