20:13:18.891 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":199,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":7,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Amused myself with John, fishing. The Cary's dined with Mr Vernon &amp; spent a very pleasant evening at Major Wolsleys, quadrilles etc</p>","pageId":702,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":189,"lock":null}
20:13:18.891 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/7/6/200
20:13:18.891 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":200,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":7,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day, Received a letter from William from Shields. Refusing to come over &amp; assist me out of my difficulties. Much disappointed, determined upon leaving Carlow on Thursday &amp; wrote to Captain Butler to send Emma to me.</p>","pageId":702,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":190,"lock":null}
20:13:18.891 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.892 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/7/6/200
20:13:18.892 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":200,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":7,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day, Received a letter from William from Shields. Refusing to come over &amp; assist me out of my difficulties. Much disappointed, determined upon leaving Carlow on Thursday &amp; wrote to Captain Butler to send Emma to me.</p>","pageId":702,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":190,"lock":null}
20:13:18.892 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/7/7/201
20:13:18.892 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":201,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":7,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy morning. Bathed before breakfast with the boys. Saw Mr Justin to inform him of my intention to endeavor to manage the property etc. without interference of chancery. Wrote to William of my determination to return to England. Turned out a very wet day Dined with Mr Vernon</p>","pageId":702,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":191,"lock":null}
20:13:18.892 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.892 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/7/7/201
20:13:18.892 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":201,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":7,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy morning. Bathed before breakfast with the boys. Saw Mr Justin to inform him of my intention to endeavor to manage the property etc. without interference of chancery. Wrote to William of my determination to return to England. Turned out a very wet day Dined with Mr Vernon</p>","pageId":702,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":191,"lock":null}
20:13:18.892 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/7/8/202
20:13:18.892 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":202,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":7,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day after a little rain in the morning. Emma arrived from Broomville &amp; much better than I could have expected. Engaged with Mr Turner settling his accounts. Paid Haughton &pound;9.12.6 Byrm Chymist &pound;9.18. Mrs Connolly &pound;7.4.6 Dined with Mr Vernon. Drank tea with Mrs Falkener</p>","pageId":702,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":192,"lock":null}
20:13:18.892 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.893 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/7/8/202
20:13:18.893 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":202,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":7,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day after a little rain in the morning. Emma arrived from Broomville &amp; much better than I could have expected. Engaged with Mr Turner settling his accounts. Paid Haughton &pound;9.12.6 Byrm Chymist &pound;9.18. Mrs Connolly &pound;7.4.6 Dined with Mr Vernon. Drank tea with Mrs Falkener</p>","pageId":702,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":192,"lock":null}
20:13:18.893 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/7/9/203
20:13:18.893 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":203,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":7,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Engaged during the morning in paying bills etc. paid Davies &pound;14.5 Sally bal wages &pound;13.17.7 &amp; left with Mr Vernon a bill at 1 mo<font color=#BFBFBF>nth</font>: WBS for the balance of his account &pound;56.9/-. Wrote to Mrs Scott of my intention to leave Carlow tomorrow. Dined with Mr Vernon &amp; took tea with Mrs Falkiner</p>","pageId":702,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":193,"lock":null}
20:13:18.893 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.893 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/7/9/203
20:13:18.893 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":203,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":7,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Engaged during the morning in paying bills etc. paid Davies &pound;14.5 Sally bal wages &pound;13.17.7 &amp; left with Mr Vernon a bill at 1 mo<font color=#BFBFBF>nth</font>: WBS for the balance of his account &pound;56.9/-. Wrote to Mrs Scott of my intention to leave Carlow tomorrow. Dined with Mr Vernon &amp; took tea with Mrs Falkiner</p>","pageId":702,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":193,"lock":null}
20:13:18.893 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/1/226
20:13:18.893 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":226,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<figure>\r\n  <img src=\"images/img2852-image-black-middens.jpg\" width=\"600px\" />\r\n  <figcaption>The Black Middens</figcaption>\r\n</figure>","pageId":null,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":null,"lock":null}
20:13:18.893 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.894 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/1/226
20:13:18.894 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":226,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<figure>\r\n  <img src=\"images/img2852-image-black-middens.jpg\" width=\"600px\" />\r\n  <figcaption>The Black Middens</figcaption>\r\n</figure>","pageId":null,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":null,"lock":null}
20:13:18.894 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/1/227
20:13:18.894 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":227,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":1,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Cloudy with wind SW Several ships got to sea in the morning. In the afternoon a few light ships got down after a 12 days passage amongst them the Hope, went on board at &frac12; past 4 o'clock, when off the Black Middens &amp; got her papers. Went to Newcastle &amp; fixed her for Carr's Walls before 6 o'clock either on my own account or 10/- freight, optimal to give an answer tomorrow.</p>","pageId":704,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":216,"lock":null}
20:13:18.894 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.895 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/1/227
20:13:18.895 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":227,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":1,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Cloudy with wind SW Several ships got to sea in the morning. In the afternoon a few light ships got down after a 12 days passage amongst them the Hope, went on board at &frac12; past 4 o'clock, when off the Black Middens &amp; got her papers. Went to Newcastle &amp; fixed her for Carr's Walls before 6 o'clock either on my own account or 10/- freight, optimal to give an answer tomorrow.</p>","pageId":704,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":216,"lock":null}
20:13:18.895 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/10/237
20:13:18.895 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":237,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At 6 o'clock am rose. Ship a little to the north of Flamborough Head &amp; stood in on the eastbound tack. Wind about W &amp; W by N. Made Robin Hood's bay at 11 o'clock am tacked &amp; stood to the southward again wind &amp; weather now moderate, set main staysail. At 12 o'clock let a reef out of top sails at 1 o'clock set main sail. Turned out a beautiful summers afternoon with a fine breeze, about 6 o'clock lay too under Flamborough head, unbent &amp; repaired foresail at 8 o'clock, again got underway with a fine westerly breeze to cross the Dups. Drank a glass of porter, smoked a pipe &amp; turned in between 9 &amp; 10 o'clock</p>","pageId":704,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":225,"lock":null}
20:13:18.895 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.895 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/10/237
20:13:18.895 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":237,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At 6 o'clock am rose. Ship a little to the north of Flamborough Head &amp; stood in on the eastbound tack. Wind about W &amp; W by N. Made Robin Hood's bay at 11 o'clock am tacked &amp; stood to the southward again wind &amp; weather now moderate, set main staysail. At 12 o'clock let a reef out of top sails at 1 o'clock set main sail. Turned out a beautiful summers afternoon with a fine breeze, about 6 o'clock lay too under Flamborough head, unbent &amp; repaired foresail at 8 o'clock, again got underway with a fine westerly breeze to cross the Dups. Drank a glass of porter, smoked a pipe &amp; turned in between 9 &amp; 10 o'clock</p>","pageId":704,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":225,"lock":null}
20:13:18.895 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/11/238
20:13:18.895 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":238,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up at 8 o'clock. Found the ship off Dunlengton Church with a fine leading wind from W by S about two points worse than last night. A fine morning, towards evening began to blow fresh. Found the fore topmast backstay spring, secured it with a tackle &amp; took in a reef being rather squally Turned in about &frac12; past 9 o'clock</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":226,"lock":null}
20:13:18.895 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.895 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/11/238
20:13:18.895 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":238,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up at 8 o'clock. Found the ship off Dunlengton Church with a fine leading wind from W by S about two points worse than last night. A fine morning, towards evening began to blow fresh. Found the fore topmast backstay spring, secured it with a tackle &amp; took in a reef being rather squally Turned in about &frac12; past 9 o'clock</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":226,"lock":null}
20:13:18.896 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/12/239
20:13:18.896 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":239,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Looked out a little after 4 o'clock am. Found we had got a change of wind about 2 o'clock from about WNW. An agreeable change for us, making all sail. The ship passed the floating light at 3 o'clock, reached Cromer at ____. Passed through Yarmouth Roads at 11 o'clock &amp; brought up being high water, at &frac12; past. Off Golaton, the <span class=highlight_yellow>Dalryaple</span> &amp; Nancy in company. Wind about W &amp; by S. The latter ship from Archangel Captain Stormont came on board to dinner. At 5 pm being low-water got underway with a light breeze from the W by S &amp; sailed out of St Nicholas Gateway &amp; beat to the southern water highwater between 12 &amp; 1 o'clock, when we brought up for the tide between the reefs points about 4 miles to the south of Southwold, between 1 &amp; 2 o'clock am. After supper, turned in for the night.</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":227,"lock":null}
20:13:18.896 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.896 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/12/239
20:13:18.896 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":239,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Looked out a little after 4 o'clock am. Found we had got a change of wind about 2 o'clock from about WNW. An agreeable change for us, making all sail. The ship passed the floating light at 3 o'clock, reached Cromer at ____. Passed through Yarmouth Roads at 11 o'clock &amp; brought up being high water, at &frac12; past. Off Golaton, the <span class=highlight_yellow>Dalryaple</span> &amp; Nancy in company. Wind about W &amp; by S. The latter ship from Archangel Captain Stormont came on board to dinner. At 5 pm being low-water got underway with a light breeze from the W by S &amp; sailed out of St Nicholas Gateway &amp; beat to the southern water highwater between 12 &amp; 1 o'clock, when we brought up for the tide between the reefs points about 4 miles to the south of Southwold, between 1 &amp; 2 o'clock am. After supper, turned in for the night.</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":227,"lock":null}
20:13:18.896 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/13/240
20:13:18.896 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":240,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up between 9 &amp; 10 o'clock having a slight cold &amp; a little rheumatism upon me. A fine warm summers day we have had for the last five weeks. Wind about south, but little of it, between 10 &amp; 11 o'clock. The United Kingdom steam ship passed us bound to London at &frac12; past 11 o'clock. When off Orford the [wind] changed to the east, a fair wind, but we want a little more of it. I hope it will continue. The breeze continued &amp; we got down to the south end of the Middle Sand where we brought up for the night, not being able to run through the Shoe Hole in the dark. After we got to bed, the wind increased &amp; blew hard with a heavy swell, a great many ships around, which gave us a foul berth extremely dangerous in that part should a gale come on from the ESE. &amp; cause of the loss of so many ships and lives we had in the March gale about five years ago.</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":228,"lock":null}
20:13:18.896 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.896 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/13/240
20:13:18.896 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":240,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up between 9 &amp; 10 o'clock having a slight cold &amp; a little rheumatism upon me. A fine warm summers day we have had for the last five weeks. Wind about south, but little of it, between 10 &amp; 11 o'clock. The United Kingdom steam ship passed us bound to London at &frac12; past 11 o'clock. When off Orford the [wind] changed to the east, a fair wind, but we want a little more of it. I hope it will continue. The breeze continued &amp; we got down to the south end of the Middle Sand where we brought up for the night, not being able to run through the Shoe Hole in the dark. After we got to bed, the wind increased &amp; blew hard with a heavy swell, a great many ships around, which gave us a foul berth extremely dangerous in that part should a gale come on from the ESE. &amp; cause of the loss of so many ships and lives we had in the March gale about five years ago.</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":228,"lock":null}
20:13:18.897 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/14/2299
20:13:18.897 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":2299,"version":14,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at 3 o'clock. A dismal &amp; wet morning, blowing hard from the east. Had not light enough to get us underway until about 4 o'clock, when the whole fleet were in motion, fortunately, at last with a fair wind. Being excessively wet &amp; unpleasant I got into bed again &amp; lay till &frac12; past 10 o'clock &amp; then found the ship off Leigh above Southend &amp; still raining hard. Brought up off Greenwich at &frac12; past 3 &amp; o'clock landed with ...</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2239,"lock":null}
20:13:18.897 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.897 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/14/2299
20:13:18.897 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":2299,"version":14,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at 3 o'clock. A dismal &amp; wet morning, blowing hard from the east. Had not light enough to get us underway until about 4 o'clock, when the whole fleet were in motion, fortunately, at last with a fair wind. Being excessively wet &amp; unpleasant I got into bed again &amp; lay till &frac12; past 10 o'clock &amp; then found the ship off Leigh above Southend &amp; still raining hard. Brought up off Greenwich at &frac12; past 3 &amp; o'clock landed with ...</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2239,"lock":null}
20:13:18.897 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/14/241
20:13:18.897 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":241,"version":8,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":14,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... the ship papers, entered her &amp; went up to Richmond's, a very unpleasant walk. Richmond was going out to dinner. Got my boots etc. dried &amp; then went to Millers coffee house, Red Lyon Square, where I found William and Bob Marsh &amp; had my dinner. They not a little surprised to see me. Slept at Nottingham Place</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":229,"lock":null}
20:13:18.897 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.898 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/14/241
20:13:18.898 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":241,"version":8,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":14,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... the ship papers, entered her &amp; went up to Richmond's, a very unpleasant walk. Richmond was going out to dinner. Got my boots etc. dried &amp; then went to Millers coffee house, Red Lyon Square, where I found William and Bob Marsh &amp; had my dinner. They not a little surprised to see me. Slept at Nottingham Place</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":229,"lock":null}
20:13:18.898 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/15/242
20:13:18.898 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":242,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind WNW Took the Greenwich passage boat at the tower &amp; went down to the Hope off Greenwich &amp; found her just getting underway for the pool, on my return pesance conveyances much surprised at meeting Watt. Carr's Walls such a bad coal than none of the Hope was sold today. Wrote to Mrs Scott. Dined with Richmond &amp; met Tom Griffeth. Played a few rubbers in the evening &amp; lost &pound;3.15/- Got home  to Nottingham Place at 2 o'clock am Saturday</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":230,"lock":null}
20:13:18.898 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.898 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/15/242
20:13:18.898 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":242,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind WNW Took the Greenwich passage boat at the tower &amp; went down to the Hope off Greenwich &amp; found her just getting underway for the pool, on my return pesance conveyances much surprised at meeting Watt. Carr's Walls such a bad coal than none of the Hope was sold today. Wrote to Mrs Scott. Dined with Richmond &amp; met Tom Griffeth. Played a few rubbers in the evening &amp; lost &pound;3.15/- Got home  to Nottingham Place at 2 o'clock am Saturday</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":230,"lock":null}
20:13:18.898 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/16/243
20:13:18.898 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":243,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine day. Wind SW Went to the city as yesterday on the Paddington coach. Engaged during the morning with Captain Dawson of the Dalryaple swearing affidavit respecting timbers etc. walked out of the city. Called upon Bob Marsh. We went with Mr Vincent, hired a boat &amp; rowed up to Putney, where we had tea, mutton chops etc. &amp; returned to town at 9 o'clock after a very pleasant evening</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":231,"lock":null}
20:13:18.898 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.899 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/16/243
20:13:18.899 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":243,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine day. Wind SW Went to the city as yesterday on the Paddington coach. Engaged during the morning with Captain Dawson of the Dalryaple swearing affidavit respecting timbers etc. walked out of the city. Called upon Bob Marsh. We went with Mr Vincent, hired a boat &amp; rowed up to Putney, where we had tea, mutton chops etc. &amp; returned to town at 9 o'clock after a very pleasant evening</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":231,"lock":null}
20:13:18.899 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/17/244
20:13:18.899 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":244,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind SW with rain during the day. Bob March breakfasted with us. Went to the chapel in Vere Street. I afterwards walked round by Gower Street &amp; called upon the Lumleys, they [had] gone down to Stanmore for the day. Continued upon and saw the Linskills in York terrace, Regants Park. Walked round by Hyde park, very little to be seen. Town exceedingly dull. Took a beef steak at the Blue Posts in Cork Street &amp; drank wine in Nottingham place</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":232,"lock":null}
20:13:18.899 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.899 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/17/244
20:13:18.899 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":244,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind SW with rain during the day. Bob March breakfasted with us. Went to the chapel in Vere Street. I afterwards walked round by Gower Street &amp; called upon the Lumleys, they [had] gone down to Stanmore for the day. Continued upon and saw the Linskills in York terrace, Regants Park. Walked round by Hyde park, very little to be seen. Town exceedingly dull. Took a beef steak at the Blue Posts in Cork Street &amp; drank wine in Nottingham place</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":232,"lock":null}
20:13:18.899 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/18/245
20:13:18.899 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":245,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A Beautiful day. Wind SW Went into the city this morning by the Paddington stage about 80 fresh ships got up to market, 2 or 3 of Carr's Walls? The coals bear such a bad character on the market that we could not sell any of the Hope's cargo. Walked out of the city, called upon Bob March, dined at the Blue Ports &amp; took wine in Nottingham Place</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":233,"lock":null}
20:13:18.899 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.900 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/18/245
20:13:18.900 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":245,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A Beautiful day. Wind SW Went into the city this morning by the Paddington stage about 80 fresh ships got up to market, 2 or 3 of Carr's Walls? The coals bear such a bad character on the market that we could not sell any of the Hope's cargo. Walked out of the city, called upon Bob March, dined at the Blue Ports &amp; took wine in Nottingham Place</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":233,"lock":null}
20:13:18.900 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/19/246
20:13:18.900 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":246,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A glorious day. Such a change. Quite cheering after the stormy weather we had. Wind WSW Did not go into the city. At 12 o'clock walked down to Hartley the dentists in mags Building &amp; had my teeth examined &amp; cleaned. Called at fosby's &amp; Bob March's &amp; afterwards walked home with William to drufs. Dined at 7 o'clock with Mr Linskill, met Mrs &amp; Miss Payin Mr Ro Bill &amp; spent a pleasant day. Lady Campbell came in to tea</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":234,"lock":null}
20:13:18.900 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.900 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/19/246
20:13:18.900 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":246,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A glorious day. Such a change. Quite cheering after the stormy weather we had. Wind WSW Did not go into the city. At 12 o'clock walked down to Hartley the dentists in mags Building &amp; had my teeth examined &amp; cleaned. Called at fosby's &amp; Bob March's &amp; afterwards walked home with William to drufs. Dined at 7 o'clock with Mr Linskill, met Mrs &amp; Miss Payin Mr Ro Bill &amp; spent a pleasant day. Lady Campbell came in to tea</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":234,"lock":null}
20:13:18.900 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/2/228
20:13:18.900 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":228,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold cloudy morning. Wind about NNW. Went to Newcastle &amp; agreed to take 10/- freight. It turned out a very wet day. Dined with J Tinley. Ship went to the spout. Gave Stephenson &pound;40</p>","pageId":704,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":217,"lock":null}
20:13:18.900 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.900 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/2/228
20:13:18.900 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":228,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold cloudy morning. Wind about NNW. Went to Newcastle &amp; agreed to take 10/- freight. It turned out a very wet day. Dined with J Tinley. Ship went to the spout. Gave Stephenson &pound;40</p>","pageId":704,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":217,"lock":null}
20:13:18.900 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/20/247
20:13:18.900 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":247,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind SSW Went into the city by a Paddington stage. A few fresh ships up. Could not sell the Hope. Bob March, Mr Vincent, William &amp; I went down by water &amp; dined on board.  In the evening at English Opera House</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":235,"lock":null}
20:13:18.900 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.901 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/20/247
20:13:18.901 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":247,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind SSW Went into the city by a Paddington stage. A few fresh ships up. Could not sell the Hope. Bob March, Mr Vincent, William &amp; I went down by water &amp; dined on board.  In the evening at English Opera House</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":235,"lock":null}
20:13:18.901 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/21/248
20:13:18.901 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":248,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet &amp; disagreeable day. Wind SW. Took the Paddington coach into the city. Called at Lees &amp; left the policy of the Hope Club. Dined at I Loblengs, a large party</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":236,"lock":null}
20:13:18.901 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.901 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/21/248
20:13:18.901 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":248,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet &amp; disagreeable day. Wind SW. Took the Paddington coach into the city. Called at Lees &amp; left the policy of the Hope Club. Dined at I Loblengs, a large party</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":236,"lock":null}
20:13:18.901 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/22/249
20:13:18.901 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":249,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A showery day. Wind from NW to N Went into the city at &frac12; past 11 o'clock by the Paddington stage. With some difficulty got the Hope sold at 30/s Walked out of the city with William &amp; dined with Richmond, met Rob Jobling Played at whist &amp; won 4/-</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":237,"lock":null}
20:13:18.901 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.902 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/22/249
20:13:18.902 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":249,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A showery day. Wind from NW to N Went into the city at &frac12; past 11 o'clock by the Paddington stage. With some difficulty got the Hope sold at 30/s Walked out of the city with William &amp; dined with Richmond, met Rob Jobling Played at whist &amp; won 4/-</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":237,"lock":null}
20:13:18.902 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/23/250
20:13:18.902 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":250,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine day. Wind West Walked round the Regents park. Took an early dinner with Richmond who afterwards drove me down to Stanmore to stay the night. Left town at &frac12; past 5 o'clock. A beautiful evening. Took tea and went to bed in good time.</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":238,"lock":null}
20:13:18.902 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.902 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/23/250
20:13:18.902 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":250,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine day. Wind West Walked round the Regents park. Took an early dinner with Richmond who afterwards drove me down to Stanmore to stay the night. Left town at &frac12; past 5 o'clock. A beautiful evening. Took tea and went to bed in good time.</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":238,"lock":null}
20:13:18.902 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/24/251
20:13:18.902 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":251,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An exceedingly fine Day. Hot summer weather. Richmond &amp; I after breakfast took a long walk. Upon our return found Mr &amp; Mrs Lumly had arrived. Mr &amp; Mrs Griffiths also came down before dinner &amp; Jobling came after we had sat down. We spend a very aggregable &amp; pleasant  day &amp; returned to town  in the evening.</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":239,"lock":null}
20:13:18.902 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.902 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/24/251
20:13:18.902 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":251,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An exceedingly fine Day. Hot summer weather. Richmond &amp; I after breakfast took a long walk. Upon our return found Mr &amp; Mrs Lumly had arrived. Mr &amp; Mrs Griffiths also came down before dinner &amp; Jobling came after we had sat down. We spend a very aggregable &amp; pleasant  day &amp; returned to town  in the evening.</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":239,"lock":null}
20:13:18.902 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/25/252
20:13:18.902 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":252,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A hot day, wind west. Went into the city by a Paddington stage. On the market,  coal lower. Walked out of the city. Dined at 6 o'clock with Mrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Whenbury</span> in Gower Street; a quiet party only Richmond there. He &amp; I went in the evening to Vauxhall Gardens to meet Bob Marsh, Vincent &amp; William. A great many people there, but of the inferior classes. Got home between 1 &amp; 2 o'clock.</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":240,"lock":null}
20:13:18.902 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.903 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/25/252
20:13:18.903 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":252,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A hot day, wind west. Went into the city by a Paddington stage. On the market,  coal lower. Walked out of the city. Dined at 6 o'clock with Mrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Whenbury</span> in Gower Street; a quiet party only Richmond there. He &amp; I went in the evening to Vauxhall Gardens to meet Bob Marsh, Vincent &amp; William. A great many people there, but of the inferior classes. Got home between 1 &amp; 2 o'clock.</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":240,"lock":null}
20:13:18.903 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/26/253
20:13:18.903 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":253,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day, but exceedingly hot. Wind SE. Breakfasted with Richmond who afterwards drove me into the city &amp; then to Stone Stairs &amp; we went on board the Hope. Took a Paddington stage home. Dressed &amp; dined at Joblings. A large party.</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":241,"lock":null}
20:13:18.903 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.903 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/26/253
20:13:18.903 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":253,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day, but exceedingly hot. Wind SE. Breakfasted with Richmond who afterwards drove me into the city &amp; then to Stone Stairs &amp; we went on board the Hope. Took a Paddington stage home. Dressed &amp; dined at Joblings. A large party.</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":241,"lock":null}
20:13:18.903 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/27/254
20:13:18.903 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":254,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful day. Wind SE. left town at 9 o'clock am. By the Portsmouth coach with Bob Marsh, where we arrived at &frac12; past 5 o'clock, crossed over by the steam boat to Ryde to stay with Mr Lee. Dined between 7 &amp; 8 o'clock. Mr Lee living at Navarino House, beautifully. Situated about &frac12; a mile west of the town, upon the side of the hill which descended to the sea of which it commands a most beautiful view, with the mainland, Portsmouth</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":242,"lock":null}
20:13:18.903 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.904 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/27/254
20:13:18.904 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":254,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful day. Wind SE. left town at 9 o'clock am. By the Portsmouth coach with Bob Marsh, where we arrived at &frac12; past 5 o'clock, crossed over by the steam boat to Ryde to stay with Mr Lee. Dined between 7 &amp; 8 o'clock. Mr Lee living at Navarino House, beautifully. Situated about &frac12; a mile west of the town, upon the side of the hill which descended to the sea of which it commands a most beautiful view, with the mainland, Portsmouth</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":242,"lock":null}
20:13:18.904 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/28/255
20:13:18.904 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":255,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A glorious day. Wind east. Got up before 7 o'clock &amp; bathed. Breakfasted at Mr Lees at Navarino House. At 11 o'clock went on the pier to see the Regatta, but dull work, being small boats. Dined with Mr Lee &amp; afterwards attended the Ball at the Library, a very poor one &amp; company bad. Not a pretty girl in the room.</p>","pageId":707,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":243,"lock":null}
20:13:18.904 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.904 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/28/255
20:13:18.904 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":255,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A glorious day. Wind east. Got up before 7 o'clock &amp; bathed. Breakfasted at Mr Lees at Navarino House. At 11 o'clock went on the pier to see the Regatta, but dull work, being small boats. Dined with Mr Lee &amp; afterwards attended the Ball at the Library, a very poor one &amp; company bad. Not a pretty girl in the room.</p>","pageId":707,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":243,"lock":null}
20:13:18.904 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/29/256
20:13:18.904 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":256,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very foggy morning, wind NE. Cleared up towards 12 o'clock &amp; turned out a delightful day. Rebecca Captain &amp; Mr Lewis, F Barclay, Bob Marsh, William &amp; I went in a sailing boat to Portsmouth to see the Victory &amp; much pleased with our trip. The wind being  against us, we were obliged to land &amp; walk about two miles to Gosport. Returned to Navarino at &frac12; past 7 o'clock to dinner</p>","pageId":707,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":244,"lock":null}
20:13:18.904 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
