20:13:18.911 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/7/234
20:13:18.911 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":234,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":7,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. The Hope got safe down from the spout having taken in 13 keels &amp; 6 char. The remainder followed her down &amp; we got to sea about &frac12; past 1 o'clock PM wind about NE but very little of it so that we did not get much beyond Sunderland before dark. Gave Richardson &amp; Davidson notice of appeal against the land tax for the property in Shields &amp; Preston. Wrote to William</p>","pageId":704,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":222,"lock":null}
20:13:18.911 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.911 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/7/234
20:13:18.911 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":234,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":7,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. The Hope got safe down from the spout having taken in 13 keels &amp; 6 char. The remainder followed her down &amp; we got to sea about &frac12; past 1 o'clock PM wind about NE but very little of it so that we did not get much beyond Sunderland before dark. Gave Richardson &amp; Davidson notice of appeal against the land tax for the property in Shields &amp; Preston. Wrote to William</p>","pageId":704,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":222,"lock":null}
20:13:18.911 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/8/235
20:13:18.911 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":235,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Quite calm during the whole of the night Got up at 8 o'clock &amp; found we were only off Hartlepool A heavy rain early in the morning &amp; a change of wind to about S. A large steam boat passed us for Leith at 9 o'clock. The weather fine but still little wind &amp; continued moderate all night</p>","pageId":704,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":223,"lock":null}
20:13:18.911 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.912 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/8/235
20:13:18.912 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":235,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Quite calm during the whole of the night Got up at 8 o'clock &amp; found we were only off Hartlepool A heavy rain early in the morning &amp; a change of wind to about S. A large steam boat passed us for Leith at 9 o'clock. The weather fine but still little wind &amp; continued moderate all night</p>","pageId":704,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":223,"lock":null}
20:13:18.912 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/9/236
20:13:18.912 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":236,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At 6 o'clock am off Whitby. Wind about SE by S &amp; SSE during the day heavy squalls with rain &amp; a little thunder &amp; lightning. Obliged to take in sail until at last we only carried two close reefed topsails, reefed trysail &amp; fore topmast staysail before dark the wind got to W by S &amp; WSW when off Robin Hood's bay &amp; increased to a heavy gale &amp; tremendous sea which lasted all night, continued on the starboard tack until 6 o'clock Sunday morning. Still blowing a gale with heavy sea. Up all night</p>","pageId":704,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":224,"lock":null}
20:13:18.912 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.912 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/9/236
20:13:18.912 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":236,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At 6 o'clock am off Whitby. Wind about SE by S &amp; SSE during the day heavy squalls with rain &amp; a little thunder &amp; lightning. Obliged to take in sail until at last we only carried two close reefed topsails, reefed trysail &amp; fore topmast staysail before dark the wind got to W by S &amp; WSW when off Robin Hood's bay &amp; increased to a heavy gale &amp; tremendous sea which lasted all night, continued on the starboard tack until 6 o'clock Sunday morning. Still blowing a gale with heavy sea. Up all night</p>","pageId":704,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":224,"lock":null}
20:13:18.912 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/1/263
20:13:18.912 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":263,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind still from the NE. F Barclay, WBS &amp; I bathed &amp; after breakfast started for Newport where after passing through a pretty country, we arrived about 2 o'clock, stopping to see Carisbrooke Castle on the way. After lunch continued our journey to East Cows, where we dined. <del>For</del> Previously crossing the water to see West Cowes &amp; in the evening, after a most delightful tour &amp; favored with most beautiful weather. We all returned safe to Navarino House much pleased &amp; satisfied. Expenses of the tour &pound;3.10.</p>","pageId":707,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":247,"lock":null}
20:13:18.913 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.913 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/1/263
