20:13:18.914 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":273,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Wind still blowing hard from the SW but finer weather. Received a letter from William &amp; wrote to Turner at London about the packages. Took a walk with Rebecca &amp; Laura &amp; Bob Marsh over the <span class=highlight_yellow>Daffers</span></p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":257,"lock":null}
20:13:18.914 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/12/274
20:13:18.914 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":274,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A showery morning &amp; blowing hard from the SE. Walked into town after breakfast &amp; played at billiards in the afternoon. Turned out fine. Attended the theatre. Mrs Hugh Barclays bespeak, a fair house.</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":258,"lock":null}
20:13:18.914 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
