20:13:18.917 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":280,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Extraordinary fine weather . Wind about east. Finished &amp; set the kite up. Lounged about the town in the afternoon.</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":264,"lock":null}
20:13:18.917 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/19/281
20:13:18.917 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":281,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather. Wind about SE. Passed the day much in the usual way.</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":265,"lock":null}
20:13:18.917 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.918 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/19/281
20:13:18.918 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":281,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather. Wind about SE. Passed the day much in the usual way.</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":265,"lock":null}
20:13:18.918 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/2/264
20:13:18.918 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":264,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather. Wind fresh from the NE. After taking an early breakfast F Barclay, Bob Marsh &amp; I embarked in the Geo<font color=#BFBFBF>rge</font> IV steam boat &amp; went to see Southampton, stopping &frac12; home at Cowes on the way, &amp; after spending a very pleasant day returned to Ryde to dinner. William left for Town</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":248,"lock":null}
20:13:18.918 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.918 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/2/264
20:13:18.918 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":264,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather. Wind fresh from the NE. After taking an early breakfast F Barclay, Bob Marsh &amp; I embarked in the Geo<font color=#BFBFBF>rge</font> IV steam boat &amp; went to see Southampton, stopping &frac12; home at Cowes on the way, &amp; after spending a very pleasant day returned to Ryde to dinner. William left for Town</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":248,"lock":null}
20:13:18.918 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/20/282
20:13:18.918 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":282,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind SE. After breakfast Rebecca, Mrs Lewis, Lee and the girls &amp; I went in the Isis to Portsmouth on board the Melville man-of-war. Captain Hill &amp; much gratified &amp; pleased with the beautiful order she was in &amp; after lunching with Mrs Hill, returned to Ryde, delighted with our sail. The 1<sup>st</sup> Lieutenant got his promotion this day after 21 years hard service.</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":266,"lock":null}
20:13:18.918 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.918 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/20/282
20:13:18.919 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":282,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind SE. After breakfast Rebecca, Mrs Lewis, Lee and the girls &amp; I went in the Isis to Portsmouth on board the Melville man-of-war. Captain Hill &amp; much gratified &amp; pleased with the beautiful order she was in &amp; after lunching with Mrs Hill, returned to Ryde, delighted with our sail. The 1<sup>st</sup> Lieutenant got his promotion this day after 21 years hard service.</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":266,"lock":null}
20:13:18.919 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/21/283
20:13:18.919 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":283,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful day. Wind SW. Went to church in the morning &amp; heard a very poor commonplace sermon from a Mr Moors. Walked upon the pier in the afternoon. Mr &amp; Mrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Gve</span> Lee &amp; Miss Jane Lee dined at Navarinos. Wind changed with <span class=highlight_yellow>a</span> some rain at night</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":267,"lock":null}
