20:13:18.920 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":285,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Beautiful weather. Wind SW. Remained in the house until after lunch. In the afternoon strolled about the town. Went to a Quadrille party at the library in the evening. Very well attended &amp; good company. Wrote to William</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":269,"lock":null}
20:13:18.920 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/24/286
20:13:18.920 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":286,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of most extraordinary fine weather, with wind SW. Strolled about the pier &amp; town</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":270,"lock":null}
20:13:18.920 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.920 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/24/286
20:13:18.920 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":286,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of most extraordinary fine weather, with wind SW. Strolled about the pier &amp; town</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":270,"lock":null}
20:13:18.920 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/25/287
20:13:18.920 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":287,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A glorious day. Not a cloud to be seen. Wind SW. After breakfast Lewis, Fanny, Bob Marsh took a boat &amp; sailed round to Brading Harbour. Much pleased with the views of the country &amp; coast &amp; delighted with our sail. Got back at &frac12; past 3 pm. Received a letter from William of the arrival of the Hope but too late for yesterdays market.</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":271,"lock":null}
20:13:18.920 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.921 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/25/287
20:13:18.921 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":287,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A glorious day. Not a cloud to be seen. Wind SW. After breakfast Lewis, Fanny, Bob Marsh took a boat &amp; sailed round to Brading Harbour. Much pleased with the views of the country &amp; coast &amp; delighted with our sail. Got back at &frac12; past 3 pm. Received a letter from William of the arrival of the Hope but too late for yesterdays market.</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":271,"lock":null}
20:13:18.921 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/26/288
20:13:18.921 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":288,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind SW to W. After breakfast walked to Binstead parsonage, about 1 mile, from Naravinos. In my opinion the prettiest &amp; most picturesque place in the island. The grounds laid out with great taste &amp; kept in the highest order. The views from them very fine. Wrote to William of my intention to be in town on Sunday.</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":272,"lock":null}
20:13:18.921 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.922 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/26/288
20:13:18.922 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":288,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind SW to W. After breakfast walked to Binstead parsonage, about 1 mile, from Naravinos. In my opinion the prettiest &amp; most picturesque place in the island. The grounds laid out with great taste &amp; kept in the highest order. The views from them very fine. Wrote to William of my intention to be in town on Sunday.</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":272,"lock":null}
20:13:18.922 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/27/289
20:13:18.922 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":289,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A wet morning. Wind NW to SW. Cleared up before 12 o'clock &amp; turned out a pleasant day. Booked outside place by the Rocket coach from tomorrow morning. Received a letter from William of the sale of the Hope at 32/3</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":273,"lock":null}
20:13:18.922 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.922 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/27/289
20:13:18.922 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":289,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A wet morning. Wind NW to SW. Cleared up before 12 o'clock &amp; turned out a pleasant day. Booked outside place by the Rocket coach from tomorrow morning. Received a letter from William of the sale of the Hope at 32/3</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":273,"lock":null}
20:13:18.922 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/28/290
20:13:18.922 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":290,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A good deal of rain in the night. Wind SW. Left Ryde at 9 o'clock am. Steam for Portsmouth. Took an outside place in the Rocket coach &amp; arrived in London at &frac12; past 7 o'clock pm having had a few showers of rain on the road. Got a bed in Nottingham Place. William out of town at his friend <span class=highlight_yellow>Oliphants</span>. Found a note from him that Stephenson had been obliged to leave the Hope &amp; return to the North in consequence of the illness of his uncle. Spent a very pleasant month with my friends, the Lees at Ryde&amp; sorry to leave there.</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":274,"lock":null}
20:13:18.922 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.923 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/28/290
20:13:18.923 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":290,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A good deal of rain in the night. Wind SW. Left Ryde at 9 o'clock am. Steam for Portsmouth. Took an outside place in the Rocket coach &amp; arrived in London at &frac12; past 7 o'clock pm having had a few showers of rain on the road. Got a bed in Nottingham Place. William out of town at his friend <span class=highlight_yellow>Oliphants</span>. Found a note from him that Stephenson had been obliged to leave the Hope &amp; return to the North in consequence of the illness of his uncle. Spent a very pleasant month with my friends, the Lees at Ryde&amp; sorry to leave there.</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":274,"lock":null}
20:13:18.923 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/29/291
20:13:18.923 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":291,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind SW. Went into the city by a Paddington Stage. Saw William. Attended the market &amp; afterwards went down the river and dined on board the Hope. Walked home in the evening on our way drinking tea with <span class=highlight_yellow>Oliphant</span> at Cockspur Street.</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":275,"lock":null}
20:13:18.923 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.923 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/29/291
20:13:18.923 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":291,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind SW. Went into the city by a Paddington Stage. Saw William. Attended the market &amp; afterwards went down the river and dined on board the Hope. Walked home in the evening on our way drinking tea with <span class=highlight_yellow>Oliphant</span> at Cockspur Street.</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":275,"lock":null}
20:13:18.923 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/3/265
20:13:18.923 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":265,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still delightful weather. Wind variable between NE &amp; NW but returned to the old quarter NE in the afternoon again. Strolled about the town &amp; pier all day. Dined at Navarino</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":249,"lock":null}
20:13:18.923 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.924 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/3/265
20:13:18.924 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":265,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still delightful weather. Wind variable between NE &amp; NW but returned to the old quarter NE in the afternoon again. Strolled about the town &amp; pier all day. Dined at Navarino</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":249,"lock":null}
20:13:18.924 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/30/292
20:13:18.924 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":292,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning during the day showers of rain. Wind SW. Walked into the city. Brought a new hat of <span class=highlight_yellow>Oliphant</span>. Paid &pound;3 for the Hopes ballast &amp; took a Greenwich boat into the pool to her. Gave the mate charge for the passage to Shields. Returned to the city &amp; had a basin of turtle soup at Bleadens. Afterwards took a Paddington Stage &amp; went with William to see the Zoological Society garden in the Regent park. Well worth the walk. In the evening went to the Argyle rooms &amp; was much amused with <span class=highlight_yellow>Fumtas</span> chin</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":276,"lock":null}
20:13:18.924 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.925 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/30/292
20:13:18.925 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":292,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning during the day showers of rain. Wind SW. Walked into the city. Brought a new hat of <span class=highlight_yellow>Oliphant</span>. Paid &pound;3 for the Hopes ballast &amp; took a Greenwich boat into the pool to her. Gave the mate charge for the passage to Shields. Returned to the city &amp; had a basin of turtle soup at Bleadens. Afterwards took a Paddington Stage &amp; went with William to see the Zoological Society garden in the Regent park. Well worth the walk. In the evening went to the Argyle rooms &amp; was much amused with <span class=highlight_yellow>Fumtas</span> chin</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":276,"lock":null}
20:13:18.925 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/4/266
20:13:18.925 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":266,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind NE. Changed to NW &amp; N with thunder &amp; lightning &amp; apparently heavy rain in Hampshire, but returned to the old quarter at night. F Barclay left us this morning for London. Sorry to loose him, a pleasant fellow. Mr Lee &amp; Laura in the chaise &amp; the rest walked to Binstead to see the abbey of which there is little remaining, after lunching on the grass with difficulty &amp; getting our feet covered with mud. We returned home by the beach.</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":250,"lock":null}
20:13:18.925 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.925 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/4/266
20:13:18.925 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":266,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind NE. Changed to NW &amp; N with thunder &amp; lightning &amp; apparently heavy rain in Hampshire, but returned to the old quarter at night. F Barclay left us this morning for London. Sorry to loose him, a pleasant fellow. Mr Lee &amp; Laura in the chaise &amp; the rest walked to Binstead to see the abbey of which there is little remaining, after lunching on the grass with difficulty &amp; getting our feet covered with mud. We returned home by the beach.</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":250,"lock":null}
20:13:18.925 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/5/267
20:13:18.925 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":267,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Delightful weather. Wind SE. Sea quite calm. Captain &amp; Mrs Lewis, Bob Marsh &amp; I took a boat &amp; amused ourselves four hours fishing. Great success having caught 89 what they call whiting <span class=highlight_yellow>pacets</span>, a small fish. Took a walk on the pier after dressing &amp; dined at Navarino. The two young Wainwrights dined with us</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":251,"lock":null}
20:13:18.925 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.926 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/5/267
20:13:18.926 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":267,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Delightful weather. Wind SE. Sea quite calm. Captain &amp; Mrs Lewis, Bob Marsh &amp; I took a boat &amp; amused ourselves four hours fishing. Great success having caught 89 what they call whiting <span class=highlight_yellow>pacets</span>, a small fish. Took a walk on the pier after dressing &amp; dined at Navarino. The two young Wainwrights dined with us</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":251,"lock":null}
20:13:18.926 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/6/268
20:13:18.926 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":268,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still fine weather. Wind variable between SE &amp; N. Spent the morning Lewis Marsh &amp; I in taking a walk to St John's towards St Helens &amp; home in the afternoon. On the pier blowing very fresh. The Samarary frigate sailed &amp; an Indiaman brought up off Ryde</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":252,"lock":null}
20:13:18.926 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.926 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/6/268
20:13:18.926 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":268,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still fine weather. Wind variable between SE &amp; N. Spent the morning Lewis Marsh &amp; I in taking a walk to St John's towards St Helens &amp; home in the afternoon. On the pier blowing very fresh. The Samarary frigate sailed &amp; an Indiaman brought up off Ryde</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":252,"lock":null}
20:13:18.926 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/7/269
20:13:18.926 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":269,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather. Wind ESE. Attended divine services in the morning. The afternoon walked on the pier. Never was at such a dull place on a Sunday. Scarcely a soul to be seen.</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":253,"lock":null}
20:13:18.926 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.927 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/7/269
20:13:18.927 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":269,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather. Wind ESE. Attended divine services in the morning. The afternoon walked on the pier. Never was at such a dull place on a Sunday. Scarcely a soul to be seen.</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":253,"lock":null}
20:13:18.927 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/8/270
20:13:18.927 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":270,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind ESE blowing fresh. Took a walk after breakfast with Captain Lewis &amp; Marsh across the <span class=highlight_yellow>Daffers</span> to the wood from which is a very beautiful  view. Played a few games at billiards with the Captain. Spent the evening as usual at Navarinos</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":254,"lock":null}
20:13:18.927 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.927 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/8/270
20:13:18.927 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":270,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind ESE blowing fresh. Took a walk after breakfast with Captain Lewis &amp; Marsh across the <span class=highlight_yellow>Daffers</span> to the wood from which is a very beautiful  view. Played a few games at billiards with the Captain. Spent the evening as usual at Navarinos</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":254,"lock":null}
20:13:18.927 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/9/271
20:13:18.927 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":271,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning, after heavy showers in the night. With a change of wind to SW a slight shower or two during the morning. The Valorous frigate arrived from the West Indies at Spithead after four years absence. Twice on the pier the only walk today. At Navarinos.</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":255,"lock":null}
