20:13:18.956 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.957 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/10/27/742
20:13:18.957 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":742,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":27,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>Went to the theatre &amp; saw Madam Vestris again. She &amp; her sister Miss Bartolozzi performed for the benefit. About ___ in the house</p>","pageId":781,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":696,"lock":null}
20:13:18.957 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/10/28/743
20:13:18.957 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":743,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. After a rainy night &amp; wind NE, changed now to NNW. During the day variable between W by N &amp; NNE and cold. A sea upon the bar. Amused myself drawing all the morning. Dined at home. Received from Robert &pound;7 on WBS account for newspapers sent Commercial Rooms &amp; &pound;1.18.6 on account of Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>albraith</font>'s.</p>\r\n<p>The Grenville Bay &amp; Love arrived from Greenland well <span class=highlight_yellow>fisked</span>. H Harry &amp; I had a bottle of port together at the George. With Ann Stokes in the evening</p>","pageId":781,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":697,"lock":null}
20:13:18.957 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.957 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/10/28/743
20:13:18.957 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":743,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. After a rainy night &amp; wind NE, changed now to NNW. During the day variable between W by N &amp; NNE and cold. A sea upon the bar. Amused myself drawing all the morning. Dined at home. Received from Robert &pound;7 on WBS account for newspapers sent Commercial Rooms &amp; &pound;1.18.6 on account of Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>albraith</font>'s.</p>\r\n<p>The Grenville Bay &amp; Love arrived from Greenland well <span class=highlight_yellow>fisked</span>. H Harry &amp; I had a bottle of port together at the George. With Ann Stokes in the evening</p>","pageId":781,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":697,"lock":null}
20:13:18.957 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/10/29/744
20:13:18.957 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":744,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; milder weather. Wind WNW. Engaged the principle part of the morning in drawing. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. In the evening eat some oysters at <span class=highlight_yellow>Marks</span> &amp; afterwards attended  the whist club.</p>","pageId":781,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":698,"lock":null}
20:13:18.957 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.957 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/10/29/744
20:13:18.957 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":744,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; milder weather. Wind WNW. Engaged the principle part of the morning in drawing. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. In the evening eat some oysters at <span class=highlight_yellow>Marks</span> &amp; afterwards attended  the whist club.</p>","pageId":781,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":698,"lock":null}
20:13:18.957 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/10/3/713
20:13:18.958 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":713,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning after a rainy night. Wind NW. Wrote a letter to Stephenson to meet him at Elsineur which I gave to H French to put on board some vessel at Hull bound to the Baltic. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. J Tinley returned from Liverpool, called in the evening &amp; took a cup of coffee with him. Met Ann at &frac12; past 7 o'clock</p>","pageId":777,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":671,"lock":null}
20:13:18.958 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.958 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/10/3/713
20:13:18.958 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":713,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning after a rainy night. Wind NW. Wrote a letter to Stephenson to meet him at Elsineur which I gave to H French to put on board some vessel at Hull bound to the Baltic. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. J Tinley returned from Liverpool, called in the evening &amp; took a cup of coffee with him. Met Ann at &frac12; past 7 o'clock</p>","pageId":777,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":671,"lock":null}
20:13:18.958 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/10/30/745
20:13:18.958 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":745,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning. Wind WNW. Again engaged the morning in drawing. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. H Harry &amp; I went to the Commercial &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>punished</span> two bottles of port. His treat having heard of the safe arrival of the Choice at Hull from <span class=highlight_yellow>Wybarz</span> making the voyage in two months. In the evening at Mrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Lays</span> at Tynemouth. Drank tea &amp; played a rubber.</p>","pageId":781,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":699,"lock":null}
20:13:18.958 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.958 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/10/30/745
20:13:18.958 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":745,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning. Wind WNW. Again engaged the morning in drawing. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. H Harry &amp; I went to the Commercial &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>punished</span> two bottles of port. His treat having heard of the safe arrival of the Choice at Hull from <span class=highlight_yellow>Wybarz</span> making the voyage in two months. In the evening at Mrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Lays</span> at Tynemouth. Drank tea &amp; played a rubber.</p>","pageId":781,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":699,"lock":null}
20:13:18.958 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/10/31/746
20:13:18.958 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":746,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather cool. Wind changeable between NNW &amp; NNE. Sea high, having blown very hard early this morning from NE. Emma Galbraith came to spend the day with Mrs Scott. Took a walk with her round by Preston Lane etc. Dined at 5 o'clock with Allen, J Craig, J Wright, W Harrison &amp; Robinson of the 80<sup>th</sup> there. Spent a pleasant day &amp; won of W Harrison &pound;6</p>","pageId":781,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":700,"lock":null}
20:13:18.958 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.959 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/10/31/746
20:13:18.959 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":746,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather cool. Wind changeable between NNW &amp; NNE. Sea high, having blown very hard early this morning from NE. Emma Galbraith came to spend the day with Mrs Scott. Took a walk with her round by Preston Lane etc. Dined at 5 o'clock with Allen, J Craig, J Wright, W Harrison &amp; Robinson of the 80<sup>th</sup> there. Spent a pleasant day &amp; won of W Harrison &pound;6</p>","pageId":781,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":700,"lock":null}
20:13:18.959 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/10/4/714
20:13:18.959 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":714,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>The early part of the morning very fine but afterwards turned dull &amp; like rain. Wind WNW blowing hard in the afternoon at W. Went to church in the morning. Mrs Dixon Fanny &amp; Bell Smith came down to see Mrs Scott. In the afternoon walked down to Tynemouth &amp; dined at 5 o'clock. <span class=highlight_yellow>Note from William</span>. Metcalf, Henry &amp; his wife there &amp; Mr &amp; Mrs J Dale in the evening</p>","pageId":777,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":672,"lock":null}
20:13:18.959 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.959 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/10/4/714
20:13:18.959 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":714,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>The early part of the morning very fine but afterwards turned dull &amp; like rain. Wind WNW blowing hard in the afternoon at W. Went to church in the morning. Mrs Dixon Fanny &amp; Bell Smith came down to see Mrs Scott. In the afternoon walked down to Tynemouth &amp; dined at 5 o'clock. <span class=highlight_yellow>Note from William</span>. Metcalf, Henry &amp; his wife there &amp; Mr &amp; Mrs J Dale in the evening</p>","pageId":777,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":672,"lock":null}
20:13:18.959 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/10/5/715
20:13:18.959 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":715,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning having had rain during the night. Wind W by N <span class=highlight_yellow>&amp; cots</span>. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. In the evening with Ann. Took supper &amp; a glass of punch with Allen</p>","pageId":778,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":673,"lock":null}
20:13:18.959 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.960 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/10/5/715
20:13:18.960 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":715,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning having had rain during the night. Wind W by N <span class=highlight_yellow>&amp; cots</span>. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. In the evening with Ann. Took supper &amp; a glass of punch with Allen</p>","pageId":778,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":673,"lock":null}
20:13:18.960 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/10/6/716
20:13:18.960 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":716,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but cold. Wind NW by N. Walked with Mark to the New Quay &amp; afterwards with Mrs Tinley up Preston Lane. Dined at J Tinley. He treated us with turtle soup, spent a pleasant day. Present the vicar, William &amp; H Metcalf, J Fenwick, J Dale &amp; myself</p>","pageId":778,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":674,"lock":null}
20:13:18.960 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.961 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/10/6/716
20:13:18.961 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":716,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but cold. Wind NW by N. Walked with Mark to the New Quay &amp; afterwards with Mrs Tinley up Preston Lane. Dined at J Tinley. He treated us with turtle soup, spent a pleasant day. Present the vicar, William &amp; H Metcalf, J Fenwick, J Dale &amp; myself</p>","pageId":778,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":674,"lock":null}
20:13:18.961 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/10/7/717
20:13:18.961 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":717,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, cool. Wind NW. Dined at home. Walked with captain Webb to Tynemouth in the evening. Called at Miss Marr's &amp; saw Emma G. At night blew hard with heavy rain &amp; sleet. Wrote to William</p>","pageId":778,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":675,"lock":null}
20:13:18.961 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.961 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/10/7/717
20:13:18.961 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":717,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, cool. Wind NW. Dined at home. Walked with captain Webb to Tynemouth in the evening. Called at Miss Marr's &amp; saw Emma G. At night blew hard with heavy rain &amp; sleet. Wrote to William</p>","pageId":778,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":675,"lock":null}
20:13:18.961 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/10/8/718
20:13:18.961 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":718,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very stormy morning. Exceptional wet &amp; heavy sleet showers. Wind about N. Got breakfast early &amp; took the steam boat to Newcastle &amp; at 10 o'clock got into the Express coach &amp; went to Durham. When we arrived a little after 12 o'clock Richmond had sent his man and gig for me but by some mistake the man supposing I had not come, returned to <span class=highlight_yellow>Burn</span><span class=highlight_yellow>hopeside</span> without me at &frac12; past 12 o'clock. I therefor started &amp; walked out to dinner.</p>","pageId":778,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":676,"lock":null}
20:13:18.961 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.962 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/10/8/718
20:13:18.962 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":718,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very stormy morning. Exceptional wet &amp; heavy sleet showers. Wind about N. Got breakfast early &amp; took the steam boat to Newcastle &amp; at 10 o'clock got into the Express coach &amp; went to Durham. When we arrived a little after 12 o'clock Richmond had sent his man and gig for me but by some mistake the man supposing I had not come, returned to <span class=highlight_yellow>Burn</span><span class=highlight_yellow>hopeside</span> without me at &frac12; past 12 o'clock. I therefor started &amp; walked out to dinner.</p>","pageId":778,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":676,"lock":null}
20:13:18.962 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/10/9/719
20:13:18.962 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":719,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine day &amp; frosty. Richardson &amp; I out shooting all the morning. The birds very wild &amp; we only got two braces. <span class=highlight_yellow>Kit</span> rode a pony, not being able to walk much. <span class=highlight_yellow>Jo</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span> out this morning exercising the hounds, preparing to begin the season tomorrow.</p>","pageId":778,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":677,"lock":null}
20:13:18.962 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.963 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/10/9/719
20:13:18.963 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":719,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine day &amp; frosty. Richardson &amp; I out shooting all the morning. The birds very wild &amp; we only got two braces. <span class=highlight_yellow>Kit</span> rode a pony, not being able to walk much. <span class=highlight_yellow>Jo</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span> out this morning exercising the hounds, preparing to begin the season tomorrow.</p>","pageId":778,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":677,"lock":null}
20:13:18.963 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/11/1/747
20:13:18.963 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":747,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Rather frosty. Wind NNW. The sea still continues heavy upon the bar. Attended morning services.</p>\r\n<p>Received a letter from WBS &amp; another from Captain Stephenson dated <span class=highlight_yellow>aneruel</span> 17<sup>th</sup> Oct &amp; expecting to sail next day. London on the 15<sup>th</sup> drawn upon Chapmans for expenses &pound;93.4/- which I consider heavy.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home at 2 o'clock &amp; afterwards took a walk to Tynemouth with H Harry. Mrs Scott not so well. Indeed the Dr considering her getting considerably worse. The disease having extended to the armpits.</p>\r\n<p>At the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":781,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":701,"lock":null}
20:13:18.963 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.963 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/11/1/747
20:13:18.963 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":747,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Rather frosty. Wind NNW. The sea still continues heavy upon the bar. Attended morning services.</p>\r\n<p>Received a letter from WBS &amp; another from Captain Stephenson dated <span class=highlight_yellow>aneruel</span> 17<sup>th</sup> Oct &amp; expecting to sail next day. London on the 15<sup>th</sup> drawn upon Chapmans for expenses &pound;93.4/- which I consider heavy.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home at 2 o'clock &amp; afterwards took a walk to Tynemouth with H Harry. Mrs Scott not so well. Indeed the Dr considering her getting considerably worse. The disease having extended to the armpits.</p>\r\n<p>At the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":781,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":701,"lock":null}
20:13:18.963 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/11/10/755
20:13:18.963 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":755,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp morning. Wind SW &amp; blowing fresh. Walked out. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. Emma came from school for a few days. Spent the evening at home</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":709,"lock":null}
20:13:18.963 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
