20:13:18.973 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":771,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Thick weather. Wind NW. Drew &pound;5 out of Chapmans. Dined at home. H Harry, Boswell, Nicholson &amp; I took grog together at the Commercial &amp; afterwards went to the theatre</p>","pageId":784,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":725,"lock":null}
20:13:18.973 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.973 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/11/27/771
20:13:18.973 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":771,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Thick weather. Wind NW. Drew &pound;5 out of Chapmans. Dined at home. H Harry, Boswell, Nicholson &amp; I took grog together at the Commercial &amp; afterwards went to the theatre</p>","pageId":784,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":725,"lock":null}
20:13:18.973 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/11/28/772
20:13:18.973 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":772,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A thick dull morning with a little rain. Wind about north. Allen &amp; I took a walk to Tynemouth. Government having given up the burial ground to the parish again, excepting 40 feet round the sides of the yard. Dined at home.</p>\r\n<p>Spent the evening with Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Lewison</span>, H Harry, and A Nicholson at the Duke of York.</p>","pageId":784,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":726,"lock":null}
20:13:18.973 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.974 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/11/28/772
20:13:18.974 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":772,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A thick dull morning with a little rain. Wind about north. Allen &amp; I took a walk to Tynemouth. Government having given up the burial ground to the parish again, excepting 40 feet round the sides of the yard. Dined at home.</p>\r\n<p>Spent the evening with Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Lewison</span>, H Harry, and A Nicholson at the Duke of York.</p>","pageId":784,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":726,"lock":null}
20:13:18.974 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/11/29/773
20:13:18.974 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":773,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A foggy and damp morning. Wind SW. Received a letter from Stephenson of the Hope being out on Saturday having delivered 279 loads 49 feet of timber equal to 320 loads with deals of broken stowage.</p>\r\n<p>Took Emma to church with me. Dined at home &amp; afterwards took wine with Boswell. H Harry &amp; Allen there.</p>\r\n<p>In the evening at mother Maxwell's</p>","pageId":784,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":727,"lock":null}
20:13:18.974 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.974 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/11/29/773
20:13:18.974 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":773,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A foggy and damp morning. Wind SW. Received a letter from Stephenson of the Hope being out on Saturday having delivered 279 loads 49 feet of timber equal to 320 loads with deals of broken stowage.</p>\r\n<p>Took Emma to church with me. Dined at home &amp; afterwards took wine with Boswell. H Harry &amp; Allen there.</p>\r\n<p>In the evening at mother Maxwell's</p>","pageId":784,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":727,"lock":null}
20:13:18.974 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/11/3/749
20:13:18.974 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":749,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another mild morning. Wind WSW. A number of light ships arrived this morning.  N Boswell arrived the morning in his ship the <span class=highlight_yellow>William</span> Shand, a fine vessel, about 280 tons <span class=highlight_yellow>coppond</span><span class=highlight_yellow> called</span> on board. Dined at home. H Harry &amp; I took wine together at the Commercial with Bill Jervis <font color=#BFBFBF>in the </font>afternoon.</p>","pageId":781,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":703,"lock":null}
20:13:18.974 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.974 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/11/3/749
20:13:18.974 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":749,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another mild morning. Wind WSW. A number of light ships arrived this morning.  N Boswell arrived the morning in his ship the <span class=highlight_yellow>William</span> Shand, a fine vessel, about 280 tons <span class=highlight_yellow>coppond</span><span class=highlight_yellow> called</span> on board. Dined at home. H Harry &amp; I took wine together at the Commercial with Bill Jervis <font color=#BFBFBF>in the </font>afternoon.</p>","pageId":781,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":703,"lock":null}
20:13:18.974 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/11/30/774
20:13:18.974 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":774,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather. Wind SW. Received a letter from William. Dined with H Harry on board the Choice. A pleasant party.</p>","pageId":784,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":728,"lock":null}
20:13:18.974 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.976 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/11/30/774
20:13:18.976 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":774,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather. Wind SW. Received a letter from William. Dined with H Harry on board the Choice. A pleasant party.</p>","pageId":784,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":728,"lock":null}
20:13:18.976 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/11/5/750
20:13:18.976 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":750,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind NW. Captain Webb &amp; I took a walk round by the sands to Cullercoats &amp; returned by the fields. Dined at the house at 2 o'clock. Mark came in after dinner &amp; took a bottle of port with me. With Bill Jervis. In the evening at the whist club</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":704,"lock":null}
20:13:18.976 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.977 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/11/5/750
20:13:18.977 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":750,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind NW. Captain Webb &amp; I took a walk round by the sands to Cullercoats &amp; returned by the fields. Dined at the house at 2 o'clock. Mark came in after dinner &amp; took a bottle of port with me. With Bill Jervis. In the evening at the whist club</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":704,"lock":null}
20:13:18.977 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/11/6/751
20:13:18.977 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":751,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild morning with the appearance of rain. Wind WSW. Dined at the George Tavern with William Harrison who had last a <span class=highlight_yellow>diciseen</span> upon the death of Major <span class=highlight_yellow>Wergs</span>. He (WH) saying that the major was killed at Corunna when it was at S<sup>t</sup> Sabastian's. Had an exceedingly pleasant day &amp; excellent dinner &amp; wine. Present J Tinley, Captain French, Mr West &amp; Mr Robinson of the 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment, Mr Allen, William, Tom &amp; Benj Wright, I Craig, Mr Christie of London, Mr Harrison &amp; myself</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":705,"lock":null}
20:13:18.977 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.977 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/11/6/751
20:13:18.977 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":751,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild morning with the appearance of rain. Wind WSW. Dined at the George Tavern with William Harrison who had last a <span class=highlight_yellow>diciseen</span> upon the death of Major <span class=highlight_yellow>Wergs</span>. He (WH) saying that the major was killed at Corunna when it was at S<sup>t</sup> Sabastian's. Had an exceedingly pleasant day &amp; excellent dinner &amp; wine. Present J Tinley, Captain French, Mr West &amp; Mr Robinson of the 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment, Mr Allen, William, Tom &amp; Benj Wright, I Craig, Mr Christie of London, Mr Harrison &amp; myself</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":705,"lock":null}
20:13:18.977 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/11/7/752
20:13:18.977 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":752,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind NW. The air rather frosty. Intended going to Newcastle with H Harry but prevented by a most disturbing letter from captain Stephenson of the Hope dated <i>Elsinore</i><i> </i>the 24<sup>th</sup> Oct informing me of the loss of poor J Galbraith. He having fallen overboard from the maintop sail yard when reefing pitching upon the top in his fall, poor fellow, his career has been short but &lsquo;tis all for the best. I hope he has left a world of misery &amp; is now I trust happy with his dear parents. Remained in the house all day in consequence of this sad news. Wrote to WBS, Mr Vernon &amp; D Dixon</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":706,"lock":null}
20:13:18.977 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.978 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/11/7/752
20:13:18.978 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":752,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind NW. The air rather frosty. Intended going to Newcastle with H Harry but prevented by a most disturbing letter from captain Stephenson of the Hope dated <i>Elsinore</i><i> </i>the 24<sup>th</sup> Oct informing me of the loss of poor J Galbraith. He having fallen overboard from the maintop sail yard when reefing pitching upon the top in his fall, poor fellow, his career has been short but &lsquo;tis all for the best. I hope he has left a world of misery &amp; is now I trust happy with his dear parents. Remained in the house all day in consequence of this sad news. Wrote to WBS, Mr Vernon &amp; D Dixon</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":706,"lock":null}
20:13:18.978 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/11/8/753
20:13:18.978 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":753,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather cool. Wind NW. In consequence of the account of J Galbraith's death, did not go to church. Dined at home. In the evening went &amp; drank tea with J Tinley. Turned out a boisterous night.</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":707,"lock":null}
20:13:18.978 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.978 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/11/8/753
20:13:18.978 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":753,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather cool. Wind NW. In consequence of the account of J Galbraith's death, did not go to church. Dined at home. In the evening went &amp; drank tea with J Tinley. Turned out a boisterous night.</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":707,"lock":null}
20:13:18.978 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/11/9/754
20:13:18.978 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":754,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine autumnal morning. Wind NW by W. Sea high upon the bar. Took a walk with mark &amp; captain Webb round by Cullercoats. Held the annual meeting at newsrooms. Old Crofs discharged in consequence of his continued disgraceful &amp; insolent conduct. Temple,  Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Lins</span><span class=highlight_yellow> </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Rell's</span> late butler appointed in his place. Dined at home at 2 o'clock.</p>\r\n<p>Fanny Smith arrived from Togston for a few days.</p>\r\n<p>Paid <span class=highlight_yellow>Sab</span><sup><span class=highlight_yellow>n</span></sup><sup> </sup>to newsroom 30/.</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":708,"lock":null}
20:13:18.978 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.979 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/11/9/754
20:13:18.979 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":754,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine autumnal morning. Wind NW by W. Sea high upon the bar. Took a walk with mark &amp; captain Webb round by Cullercoats. Held the annual meeting at newsrooms. Old Crofs discharged in consequence of his continued disgraceful &amp; insolent conduct. Temple,  Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Lins</span><span class=highlight_yellow> </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Rell's</span> late butler appointed in his place. Dined at home at 2 o'clock.</p>\r\n<p>Fanny Smith arrived from Togston for a few days.</p>\r\n<p>Paid <span class=highlight_yellow>Sab</span><sup><span class=highlight_yellow>n</span></sup><sup> </sup>to newsroom 30/.</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":708,"lock":null}
20:13:18.979 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/1/775
20:13:18.979 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":775,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull &amp; damp morning. Wind S. Afterwards got to SE blowing very hard towards night with heavy rain. Mrs Scott so unwell obliged to keep her bed &amp; not able to see any person. Dined at home. Drank tea &amp; spent the evening at J Tinley's</p>","pageId":785,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":729,"lock":null}
20:13:18.979 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.979 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/1/775
20:13:18.979 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":775,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull &amp; damp morning. Wind S. Afterwards got to SE blowing very hard towards night with heavy rain. Mrs Scott so unwell obliged to keep her bed &amp; not able to see any person. Dined at home. Drank tea &amp; spent the evening at J Tinley's</p>","pageId":785,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":729,"lock":null}
20:13:18.979 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/10/784
20:13:18.979 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":784,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold frosty morning. Wind WSW. On board the Hope. One man at work replacing the after <span class=highlight_yellow>raft</span><span class=highlight_yellow>p</span><span class=highlight_yellow>o</span><span class=highlight_yellow>rts</span>. Paid Walker block maker &pound;8.13/- for making new mainmast in 1828 outfit. H harry &amp; I walked up to Tynemouth &amp; had some whiskey toddy with J Cunningham &amp; afterwards attended the whist club.</p>","pageId":786,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":738,"lock":null}
20:13:18.979 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.980 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/10/784
20:13:18.980 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":784,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold frosty morning. Wind WSW. On board the Hope. One man at work replacing the after <span class=highlight_yellow>raft</span><span class=highlight_yellow>p</span><span class=highlight_yellow>o</span><span class=highlight_yellow>rts</span>. Paid Walker block maker &pound;8.13/- for making new mainmast in 1828 outfit. H harry &amp; I walked up to Tynemouth &amp; had some whiskey toddy with J Cunningham &amp; afterwards attended the whist club.</p>","pageId":786,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":738,"lock":null}
20:13:18.980 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/11/785
20:13:18.980 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":785,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning &amp; hard frost. Wind SW. On board the Hope. The carpenter still employed at the <span class=highlight_yellow>raftport</span>. Dined at home. Mrs Dixon down to see Mrs Scott.</p>","pageId":786,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":739,"lock":null}
20:13:18.980 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
