20:13:18.985 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":794,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp raw morning. Wind SE by E. received a letter from WBS with Hope's freight account. Stayed in the house all day, having a swelled face</p>","pageId":786,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":748,"lock":null}
20:13:18.985 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/21/795
20:13:18.985 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":795,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A thick frost morning. Wind SW by W. Paid the washerwoman for a quarter washing &pound;1.11.6. On board the Hope. The carpenter busy fixing the new hook at the stern. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon. In the evening at home.</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":749,"lock":null}
20:13:18.985 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.986 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/21/795
20:13:18.986 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":795,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A thick frost morning. Wind SW by W. Paid the washerwoman for a quarter washing &pound;1.11.6. On board the Hope. The carpenter busy fixing the new hook at the stern. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon. In the evening at home.</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":749,"lock":null}
20:13:18.986 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/22/796
20:13:18.986 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":796,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A foggy damp and very unpleasant morning. Some snow on the ground, having fallen during the night. Wind, the little there is NNW. Dined at 4 o'clock at Mr Metcalf's in Saville Street. A party there. Spent a pleasant day. Wrote to William. Called at the Bank. Spencer promised to under me what accommodation I <span class=highlight_yellow>may</span> want this Xmas. Paid Linskill &amp; etc &pound;24.11.6 for <span class=highlight_yellow>cordage</span> &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Lane</span> &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Spence</span> &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Foster</span> &pound;8.10/- for canvas</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":750,"lock":null}
20:13:18.986 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.986 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/22/796
20:13:18.986 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":796,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A foggy damp and very unpleasant morning. Some snow on the ground, having fallen during the night. Wind, the little there is NNW. Dined at 4 o'clock at Mr Metcalf's in Saville Street. A party there. Spent a pleasant day. Wrote to William. Called at the Bank. Spencer promised to under me what accommodation I <span class=highlight_yellow>may</span> want this Xmas. Paid Linskill &amp; etc &pound;24.11.6 for <span class=highlight_yellow>cordage</span> &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Lane</span> &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Spence</span> &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Foster</span> &pound;8.10/- for canvas</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":750,"lock":null}
20:13:18.986 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/23/797
20:13:18.986 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":797,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A frosty morning. Wind East. H Harry went with me on board the Hope to give me his advice with regard to the repairs. Found they had taken the broken hold beam out &amp; preparing a new one. Ordered several new <span class=highlight_yellow>kne</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span><span class=highlight_yellow>s</span> to be put in. Dined at home &amp; spent the evening</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":751,"lock":null}
20:13:18.986 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.987 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/23/797
20:13:18.987 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":797,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A frosty morning. Wind East. H Harry went with me on board the Hope to give me his advice with regard to the repairs. Found they had taken the broken hold beam out &amp; preparing a new one. Ordered several new <span class=highlight_yellow>kne</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span><span class=highlight_yellow>s</span> to be put in. Dined at home &amp; spent the evening</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":751,"lock":null}
20:13:18.987 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/24/798
20:13:18.987 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":798,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold frosty morning. Wind E by N. Been blowing a gale all night. A heavy sea upon the bar. On board the Hope. The master &amp; carpenter absent looking for some knees for the hold beans. Dined at home. H Harry came in &amp; took wine with me. Mrs Dixon down &amp; took Emma to Benton with her. Attended the whist club in the evening. Saw Ann Maxwell</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":752,"lock":null}
20:13:18.987 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.987 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/24/798
20:13:18.987 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":798,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold frosty morning. Wind E by N. Been blowing a gale all night. A heavy sea upon the bar. On board the Hope. The master &amp; carpenter absent looking for some knees for the hold beans. Dined at home. H Harry came in &amp; took wine with me. Mrs Dixon down &amp; took Emma to Benton with her. Attended the whist club in the evening. Saw Ann Maxwell</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":752,"lock":null}
20:13:18.987 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/25/799
20:13:18.987 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":799,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Xmas day. Seasonal weather. Very cold with a little snow. Wind East &amp; blowing hard. Walked up to Benton. Dined &amp; remained all night.</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":753,"lock":null}
20:13:18.987 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.988 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/25/799
20:13:18.988 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":799,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Xmas day. Seasonal weather. Very cold with a little snow. Wind East &amp; blowing hard. Walked up to Benton. Dined &amp; remained all night.</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":753,"lock":null}
20:13:18.988 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/26/800
20:13:18.988 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":800,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty morning. Wind ESE. A slight fall of snow during the day. Walked into Newcastle with Dixon. Nothing doing on the Quay side in the way of freights, at least none to suite me. Returned to Shields in a gig. Dined at home. In the evening attended the whist club at H Dales. Received a letter from Boswell from Rye informing me he had got 90 passengers for New York</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":754,"lock":null}
20:13:18.988 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.988 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/26/800
20:13:18.988 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":800,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty morning. Wind ESE. A slight fall of snow during the day. Walked into Newcastle with Dixon. Nothing doing on the Quay side in the way of freights, at least none to suite me. Returned to Shields in a gig. Dined at home. In the evening attended the whist club at H Dales. Received a letter from Boswell from Rye informing me he had got 90 passengers for New York</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":754,"lock":null}
20:13:18.988 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/27/801
20:13:18.988 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":801,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine seasonal morning. Wind NW &amp; snowing heavy. Did not go to church. Made up the Hope's <span class=highlight_yellow>final</span> voyage in the ships <span class=highlight_yellow>log</span>. She clears nothing much to my unsurprised &amp; disappointment. Dined with H Harry. In the evening with Bell Jarvis &amp; Jane Dryden.</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":755,"lock":null}
20:13:18.988 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.989 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/27/801
20:13:18.989 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":801,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine seasonal morning. Wind NW &amp; snowing heavy. Did not go to church. Made up the Hope's <span class=highlight_yellow>final</span> voyage in the ships <span class=highlight_yellow>log</span>. She clears nothing much to my unsurprised &amp; disappointment. Dined with H Harry. In the evening with Bell Jarvis &amp; Jane Dryden.</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":755,"lock":null}
20:13:18.989 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/28/802
20:13:18.989 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":802,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of frost, but not yet much snow has fallen. Wind NW. On board the Hope. The carpenter nearly finished. Intend hauling her off the shore at high water. Dined at home.</p>\r\n<p>Mary <span class=highlight_yellow>Carss</span> called upon me.</p>\r\n<p>H Harry, Mark &amp; I had a glass of grog together. Spent the evening at home.</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":756,"lock":null}
20:13:18.989 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.989 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/28/802
20:13:18.990 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":802,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of frost, but not yet much snow has fallen. Wind NW. On board the Hope. The carpenter nearly finished. Intend hauling her off the shore at high water. Dined at home.</p>\r\n<p>Mary <span class=highlight_yellow>Carss</span> called upon me.</p>\r\n<p>H Harry, Mark &amp; I had a glass of grog together. Spent the evening at home.</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":756,"lock":null}
20:13:18.990 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/29/803
20:13:18.990 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":803,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull winters morning. Frost gone, having been rain during the night. Wind E by S but still cold.</p>\r\n<p>Attended a meeting at the church to take into consideration the offer of the board of ordinance either to purchase the burial ground at Tynemouth or give a piece of ground in lieu of it. The meeting determined not to do either, but to let the Board apply to Parliament for an act to take it from us, which they had threatened to do. Dined at home. In the evening H Harry, H Nicolson &amp; I had a glass of grog at the George together</p>","pageId":788,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":757,"lock":null}
20:13:18.990 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.990 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/29/803
20:13:18.990 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":803,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull winters morning. Frost gone, having been rain during the night. Wind E by S but still cold.</p>\r\n<p>Attended a meeting at the church to take into consideration the offer of the board of ordinance either to purchase the burial ground at Tynemouth or give a piece of ground in lieu of it. The meeting determined not to do either, but to let the Board apply to Parliament for an act to take it from us, which they had threatened to do. Dined at home. In the evening H Harry, H Nicolson &amp; I had a glass of grog at the George together</p>","pageId":788,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":757,"lock":null}
20:13:18.990 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/3/777
20:13:18.990 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":777,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very unpleasant damp morning. Wind about south with a heavy sea upon the bar. Two ships have got upon the rock in entering the harbour. Dined at home. Mr Allen came &amp; took wine with me. In the evening attended the whist club.</p>","pageId":785,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":731,"lock":null}
20:13:18.990 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.990 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/3/777
20:13:18.991 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":777,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very unpleasant damp morning. Wind about south with a heavy sea upon the bar. Two ships have got upon the rock in entering the harbour. Dined at home. Mr Allen came &amp; took wine with me. In the evening attended the whist club.</p>","pageId":785,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":731,"lock":null}
20:13:18.991 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/30/804
20:13:18.991 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":804,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Rather a dull morning. Inclined to freeze. Wind E by S. Drew &pound;5 out of Chapmans. On board the Hope. Carpenter nearly finished laying the half deck. H Harry &amp; Nicolson lunched on board. Dined at home. Received a letter from WBS &amp; answered it In the evening H Nicholson &amp; I called to see jane Mills. With Jane Dryden</p>","pageId":788,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":758,"lock":null}
20:13:18.991 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.992 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/30/804
20:13:18.992 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":804,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Rather a dull morning. Inclined to freeze. Wind E by S. Drew &pound;5 out of Chapmans. On board the Hope. Carpenter nearly finished laying the half deck. H Harry &amp; Nicolson lunched on board. Dined at home. Received a letter from WBS &amp; answered it In the evening H Nicholson &amp; I called to see jane Mills. With Jane Dryden</p>","pageId":788,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":758,"lock":null}
20:13:18.992 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/31/805
20:13:18.992 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":805,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>The wind continuing from the SE makes it appear as if there was not much if any frost. Though some snow has fallen during the night.</p>\r\n<p>The last day of the year, which has been to me anything but a prosperous one. I trust I may be more fortunate the next one. I know not what will become of me. It appears to me my destiny is fixed &amp; that I'm never to rise in the world again.</p>\r\n<p>Walked to Cullercoats &amp; saw the fishing boats come in having been successful. The fish very <span class=highlight_yellow>firm</span>, particularly the haddock. There were 16 boats. Dined at home. Attended the whist club &amp; sat the new year in.</p>","pageId":788,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":759,"lock":null}
20:13:18.992 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.992 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/31/805
20:13:18.992 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":805,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>The wind continuing from the SE makes it appear as if there was not much if any frost. Though some snow has fallen during the night.</p>\r\n<p>The last day of the year, which has been to me anything but a prosperous one. I trust I may be more fortunate the next one. I know not what will become of me. It appears to me my destiny is fixed &amp; that I'm never to rise in the world again.</p>\r\n<p>Walked to Cullercoats &amp; saw the fishing boats come in having been successful. The fish very <span class=highlight_yellow>firm</span>, particularly the haddock. There were 16 boats. Dined at home. Attended the whist club &amp; sat the new year in.</p>","pageId":788,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":759,"lock":null}
20:13:18.992 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/4/778
20:13:18.992 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":778,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather but still rather foggy &amp; dull. Wind S &amp; S by E. The <span class=highlight_yellow>Qurnoury</span> belonging to <font color=#222222>Messrs</font><font color=#222222> </font>Young son got upon the rocks last night. Allen &amp; I walked round by Tynemouth &amp; the rocks to see them. Dined at home. Boswell treated H Nicholson &amp; me to some punch at the Mulstrum, it being his last night at Shields</p>","pageId":785,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":732,"lock":null}
20:13:18.992 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.993 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/4/778
20:13:18.993 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":778,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather but still rather foggy &amp; dull. Wind S &amp; S by E. The <span class=highlight_yellow>Qurnoury</span> belonging to <font color=#222222>Messrs</font><font color=#222222> </font>Young son got upon the rocks last night. Allen &amp; I walked round by Tynemouth &amp; the rocks to see them. Dined at home. Boswell treated H Nicholson &amp; me to some punch at the Mulstrum, it being his last night at Shields</p>","pageId":785,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":732,"lock":null}
20:13:18.993 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/5/779
20:13:18.993 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":779,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather. Wind SW. Sea fallen. Received a letter from WBS enclosing &pound;50 BK post bill. Wrote to WBS paid the &pound;50 bill into Chapmans. Dined at home. With Ann Stokes in the evening.</p>","pageId":785,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":733,"lock":null}
20:13:18.993 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.994 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/5/779
20:13:18.994 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":779,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather. Wind SW. Sea fallen. Received a letter from WBS enclosing &pound;50 BK post bill. Wrote to WBS paid the &pound;50 bill into Chapmans. Dined at home. With Ann Stokes in the evening.</p>","pageId":785,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":733,"lock":null}
20:13:18.994 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/6/780
20:13:18.994 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":780,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind SSW. Attended morning service at the Church. Walked in the afternoon with J Tinley &amp; his boys to Tynemouth &amp; afterwards dined with him.</p>","pageId":785,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":734,"lock":null}
20:13:18.994 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.994 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/6/780
20:13:18.994 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":780,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind SSW. Attended morning service at the Church. Walked in the afternoon with J Tinley &amp; his boys to Tynemouth &amp; afterwards dined with him.</p>","pageId":785,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":734,"lock":null}
20:13:18.994 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/7/781
20:13:18.994 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":781,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather, rather frosty. Wind SW &amp; SSW. The Hope arrived safe last night at 11 o'clock. Determined upon laying her up &amp; therefore took her off risk in the Premium &amp; Hope Clubs. Gave Stephenson &pound;20 to pay wages. The William Shand, Mr Boswell sailed today for <span class=highlight_yellow>Ryes</span> to take on passengers for New York. A great many colliers also got to sea. Dined with the Committee of the ____ &amp; in the evening went to the theatre, it being the bespeak of the Bachelors of North Shields.</p>","pageId":785,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":735,"lock":null}
20:13:18.994 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.995 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/7/781
20:13:18.995 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":781,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather, rather frosty. Wind SW &amp; SSW. The Hope arrived safe last night at 11 o'clock. Determined upon laying her up &amp; therefore took her off risk in the Premium &amp; Hope Clubs. Gave Stephenson &pound;20 to pay wages. The William Shand, Mr Boswell sailed today for <span class=highlight_yellow>Ryes</span> to take on passengers for New York. A great many colliers also got to sea. Dined with the Committee of the ____ &amp; in the evening went to the theatre, it being the bespeak of the Bachelors of North Shields.</p>","pageId":785,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":735,"lock":null}
20:13:18.995 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/8/782
20:13:18.995 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":782,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine day &amp; frosty. Wind WNW. On board the Hope all the morning. The people busy unrigging. Mr Allen &amp; I dined on board. Took wine and spent the evening at J Tinley's. Mr Temple there.</p>","pageId":785,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":736,"lock":null}
20:13:18.995 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.995 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/8/782
20:13:18.995 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":782,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine day &amp; frosty. Wind WNW. On board the Hope all the morning. The people busy unrigging. Mr Allen &amp; I dined on board. Took wine and spent the evening at J Tinley's. Mr Temple there.</p>","pageId":785,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":736,"lock":null}
20:13:18.995 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/9/783
20:13:18.995 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":783,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine seasonable morning &amp; a hard frost. Wind SW. On board the Hope all the morning, where I dined. Hauled her upon Platty ways to get upained in the safe port etc. Drank tea with H Harry &amp; went to the theatre at half price, it being the Officers <span class=highlight_yellow>bespeak</span>.</p>","pageId":785,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":737,"lock":null}
20:13:18.995 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.996 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/9/783
20:13:18.996 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":783,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine seasonable morning &amp; a hard frost. Wind SW. On board the Hope all the morning, where I dined. Hauled her upon Platty ways to get upained in the safe port etc. Drank tea with H Harry &amp; went to the theatre at half price, it being the Officers <span class=highlight_yellow>bespeak</span>.</p>","pageId":785,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":737,"lock":null}
20:13:18.996 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/1/419
20:13:18.996 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":419,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty day. Wind W by N. A large fleet of colliers went to sea. Attended church in the morning. Dined at home. In the evening at the Mulstrum. A French, Boswell &amp; Nicolson. <span class=highlight_yellow>Jane</span> Muston</p>","pageId":722,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":401,"lock":null}
20:13:18.996 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.997 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/1/419
20:13:18.997 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":419,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty day. Wind W by N. A large fleet of colliers went to sea. Attended church in the morning. Dined at home. In the evening at the Mulstrum. A French, Boswell &amp; Nicolson. <span class=highlight_yellow>Jane</span> Muston</p>","pageId":722,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":401,"lock":null}
20:13:18.997 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/10/428
20:13:18.997 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":428,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning &amp; wind NW. Mrs Scott in great pain last night. Got &pound;5 from Chapmans for private use. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined in the Commercial, the <span class=highlight_yellow>Limited</span> &amp; Eligible Clubs. Sat very late.</p>","pageId":723,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":410,"lock":null}
20:13:18.997 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.998 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/10/428
20:13:18.998 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":428,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning &amp; wind NW. Mrs Scott in great pain last night. Got &pound;5 from Chapmans for private use. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined in the Commercial, the <span class=highlight_yellow>Limited</span> &amp; Eligible Clubs. Sat very late.</p>","pageId":723,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":410,"lock":null}
20:13:18.998 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/11/429
20:13:18.998 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":429,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind NW. Attended the meeting of the Master Mariners, when the rules were read over &amp; adopted. Walked up to Milburn's Place to see the ship. Dined at home. In the evening at the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":723,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":411,"lock":null}
20:13:18.998 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.998 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/11/429
20:13:18.998 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":429,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind NW. Attended the meeting of the Master Mariners, when the rules were read over &amp; adopted. Walked up to Milburn's Place to see the ship. Dined at home. In the evening at the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":723,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":411,"lock":null}
20:13:18.998 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/12/430
20:13:18.998 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":430,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A mild morning, but damp having been a great deal of rain in the night. Wind NW. A meeting held of the committees of clubs to demand an explanation of Joe Elder for fixing his ship below the rates of freight determined upon by shipowners. <span class=highlight_yellow>It is</span> not the first time he has been guilty of such dishonest practices. He could not <span class=highlight_yellow>explain</span> himself &amp; unless Mr Bell cancels the charter, which will be known tomorrow, Eldess ships will be turned out of the clubs, the proper way of treating such fellows. Dined at home. In the evening attended the whist club &amp; afterwards went to a large bridal party at Tom Wrights</p>","pageId":723,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":412,"lock":null}
20:13:18.998 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:18.999 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/12/430
20:13:18.999 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":430,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A mild morning, but damp having been a great deal of rain in the night. Wind NW. A meeting held of the committees of clubs to demand an explanation of Joe Elder for fixing his ship below the rates of freight determined upon by shipowners. <span class=highlight_yellow>It is</span> not the first time he has been guilty of such dishonest practices. He could not <span class=highlight_yellow>explain</span> himself &amp; unless Mr Bell cancels the charter, which will be known tomorrow, Eldess ships will be turned out of the clubs, the proper way of treating such fellows. Dined at home. In the evening attended the whist club &amp; afterwards went to a large bridal party at Tom Wrights</p>","pageId":723,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":412,"lock":null}
20:13:18.999 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/13/431
20:13:18.999 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":431,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Quite mild &amp; spring weather. Wind WNW. Took a walk to Tynemouth. Dined with the Friendly club at the George Tavern where we had a handsome dinner &amp; spent a pleasant evening. Saw Ann <span class=highlight_yellow>Mallot</span></p>","pageId":724,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":413,"lock":null}
20:13:18.999 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
