20:13:19.000 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":431,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Quite mild &amp; spring weather. Wind WNW. Took a walk to Tynemouth. Dined with the Friendly club at the George Tavern where we had a handsome dinner &amp; spent a pleasant evening. Saw Ann <span class=highlight_yellow>Mallot</span></p>","pageId":724,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":413,"lock":null}
20:13:19.000 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/14/432
20:13:19.000 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":432,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW. Went by coach to Newcastle. Called at D Dixons. Found Mrs Dixon about to set off for Shields to see Mrs Scott. Called at G Dunn &amp; Sons &amp; refused to load their coals without being upheld. Afterwards walked down to Shields. Dined at Mrs Reeds with a large party. The bridal party Mr &amp; Mrs Tom Wright there. Attended the whist club at A Metcalf. Paid R Brown the account &pound;4.10/-</p>","pageId":724,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":414,"lock":null}
20:13:19.000 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.000 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/14/432
20:13:19.000 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":432,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW. Went by coach to Newcastle. Called at D Dixons. Found Mrs Dixon about to set off for Shields to see Mrs Scott. Called at G Dunn &amp; Sons &amp; refused to load their coals without being upheld. Afterwards walked down to Shields. Dined at Mrs Reeds with a large party. The bridal party Mr &amp; Mrs Tom Wright there. Attended the whist club at A Metcalf. Paid R Brown the account &pound;4.10/-</p>","pageId":724,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":414,"lock":null}
20:13:19.000 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/15/433
20:13:19.000 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":433,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A mild morning with the appearance of rain &amp; blowing fresh at WNW. Mrs Scott in a devil of a humour blowing every person up right &amp; left. I think her mind must be affected. Went to church. Took a family dinner with A Harry. In the evening at the Mulstrum. Met Bell Jervis for the first time.</p>","pageId":724,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":415,"lock":null}
20:13:19.000 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.001 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/15/433
20:13:19.001 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":433,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A mild morning with the appearance of rain &amp; blowing fresh at WNW. Mrs Scott in a devil of a humour blowing every person up right &amp; left. I think her mind must be affected. Went to church. Took a family dinner with A Harry. In the evening at the Mulstrum. Met Bell Jervis for the first time.</p>","pageId":724,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":415,"lock":null}
20:13:19.001 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/16/434
20:13:19.001 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":434,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; calm wind about West. Walked to the ship &amp; ordered the sails &amp; small stones on board. About noon it turned very thick weather &amp; the wind suddenly changed to NE with heavy rain that lasted all night</p>","pageId":724,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":416,"lock":null}
20:13:19.001 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.002 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/16/434
20:13:19.002 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":434,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; calm wind about West. Walked to the ship &amp; ordered the sails &amp; small stones on board. About noon it turned very thick weather &amp; the wind suddenly changed to NE with heavy rain that lasted all night</p>","pageId":724,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":416,"lock":null}
20:13:19.002 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/17/435
20:13:19.002 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":435,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp morning it having been a great deal of rain &amp; sleet during the night. Wind NNW changeable during the day to ENE &amp; NE. Went down to the ship. The committee on board surveying stores for the Hope club. Dined at J Tinleys with a party of gentlemen. We all afterwards went to the ball. Only 52 there, but a pleasant dancing ball. Ordered a new mainstaysail for the Hope.</p>","pageId":724,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":417,"lock":null}
20:13:19.002 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.002 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/17/435
20:13:19.002 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":435,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp morning it having been a great deal of rain &amp; sleet during the night. Wind NNW changeable during the day to ENE &amp; NE. Went down to the ship. The committee on board surveying stores for the Hope club. Dined at J Tinleys with a party of gentlemen. We all afterwards went to the ball. Only 52 there, but a pleasant dancing ball. Ordered a new mainstaysail for the Hope.</p>","pageId":724,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":417,"lock":null}
20:13:19.002 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/18/436
20:13:19.002 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":436,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Rather a dull morning. Wind WNN &amp; looks like more rain. Turned very cold towards afternoon &amp; wind changed to SE &amp; S by E. Went to Newcastle but everything very dull &amp; could do nothing for the Hope. Returned home to dinner.</p>","pageId":724,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":418,"lock":null}
20:13:19.002 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.003 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/18/436
20:13:19.003 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":436,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Rather a dull morning. Wind WNN &amp; looks like more rain. Turned very cold towards afternoon &amp; wind changed to SE &amp; S by E. Went to Newcastle but everything very dull &amp; could do nothing for the Hope. Returned home to dinner.</p>","pageId":724,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":418,"lock":null}
20:13:19.003 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/19/437
20:13:19.003 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":437,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold morning. Wind SW. Has been some rain in the night. Received a letter from the committee of the Hope Club ordering us to get a new <span class=highlight_yellow>lamp</span> &amp; next winter a new foresail. Also now four new ballast shovels. Engaged all the morning writing to William &amp; the Galbraiths. Found Mrs Craig in a chaise &amp; went to <span class=highlight_yellow>Walls</span> to dine with Mr J Wright, a large party of 18. Spent a pleasant day &amp; had the best port wine I ever tasted in my life. Got home at 12 o'clock.</p>","pageId":724,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":419,"lock":null}
20:13:19.003 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.003 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/19/437
20:13:19.003 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":437,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold morning. Wind SW. Has been some rain in the night. Received a letter from the committee of the Hope Club ordering us to get a new <span class=highlight_yellow>lamp</span> &amp; next winter a new foresail. Also now four new ballast shovels. Engaged all the morning writing to William &amp; the Galbraiths. Found Mrs Craig in a chaise &amp; went to <span class=highlight_yellow>Walls</span> to dine with Mr J Wright, a large party of 18. Spent a pleasant day &amp; had the best port wine I ever tasted in my life. Got home at 12 o'clock.</p>","pageId":724,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":419,"lock":null}
20:13:19.003 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/2/420
20:13:19.003 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":420,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty day &amp; sharp frost. Wind W by S. Engaged part of the morning drawing. Took a walk round by the ship. Found all <span class=highlight_yellow>right</span>, Stephenson on board waiting for Mr Cleths to survey her for the Premium Club. Dinned with Mr Chapman of <span class=highlight_yellow>Elseneur</span> at the Commercial. A French &amp; W Boswell came and took wine. Went to the theatre, Crooks benefit, a fair house&amp; the last night of performance for the season. Got &pound;5 of Chapman for self.</p>","pageId":722,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":402,"lock":null}
20:13:19.003 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.004 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/2/420
20:13:19.004 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":420,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty day &amp; sharp frost. Wind W by S. Engaged part of the morning drawing. Took a walk round by the ship. Found all <span class=highlight_yellow>right</span>, Stephenson on board waiting for Mr Cleths to survey her for the Premium Club. Dinned with Mr Chapman of <span class=highlight_yellow>Elseneur</span> at the Commercial. A French &amp; W Boswell came and took wine. Went to the theatre, Crooks benefit, a fair house&amp; the last night of performance for the season. Got &pound;5 of Chapman for self.</p>","pageId":722,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":402,"lock":null}
20:13:19.004 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/20/438
20:13:19.004 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":438,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind SW. Mr mark &amp; I took a walk along the Herd sand. Dined at home. Suppered at Mr Bradshower</p>","pageId":724,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":420,"lock":null}
20:13:19.004 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.005 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/20/438
20:13:19.005 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":438,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind SW. Mr mark &amp; I took a walk along the Herd sand. Dined at home. Suppered at Mr Bradshower</p>","pageId":724,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":420,"lock":null}
20:13:19.005 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/21/439
20:13:19.005 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":439,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind SW At 10 o'clock am wind suddenly changed to SE with thick fog &amp; very raw and cold. Went to Newcastle by coach but could not get anything for the Hope. Called at Mrs Dixon's. Dined at home. In the evening at the whist club at A Dales. Received a letter from J Young demanding payment of their claims upon W &amp; J Scott which we shall most certainly not accede to, he having agreed to take the <span class=highlight_yellow>comporation</span> with the other creditors.</p>","pageId":725,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":421,"lock":null}
20:13:19.005 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.005 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/21/439
20:13:19.005 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":439,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind SW At 10 o'clock am wind suddenly changed to SE with thick fog &amp; very raw and cold. Went to Newcastle by coach but could not get anything for the Hope. Called at Mrs Dixon's. Dined at home. In the evening at the whist club at A Dales. Received a letter from J Young demanding payment of their claims upon W &amp; J Scott which we shall most certainly not accede to, he having agreed to take the <span class=highlight_yellow>comporation</span> with the other creditors.</p>","pageId":725,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":421,"lock":null}
20:13:19.005 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/22/440
20:13:19.005 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":440,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind E by N. About 10 o'clock am it began to rain very heavy &amp; continued all the morning. Went to church. Dined with J Tinley</p>","pageId":725,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":422,"lock":null}
20:13:19.005 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.006 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/22/440
20:13:19.006 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":440,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind E by N. About 10 o'clock am it began to rain very heavy &amp; continued all the morning. Went to church. Dined with J Tinley</p>","pageId":725,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":422,"lock":null}
20:13:19.006 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/23/441
20:13:19.006 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":441,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Blowing fresh from the WNW &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>lo</span>. Wrote to J Young requesting a few days to communicate with my brother. Walked up to the ship with J Tinley in the morning, who wrote to <span class=highlight_yellow>Netern</span> to send down the deed of release. All letters <span class=highlight_yellow>be</span> relative to our composition. Dined at home. In the evening had an <span class=highlight_yellow>ryotes</span> supper at the Northumberland. <span class=highlight_yellow>Won</span> a bet lost by <span class=highlight_yellow>Locklder</span> &amp; Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Holroryd</span>. Sat down 13 &amp; spent a pleasant evening</p>","pageId":725,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":423,"lock":null}
20:13:19.006 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.006 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/23/441
20:13:19.006 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":441,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Blowing fresh from the WNW &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>lo</span>. Wrote to J Young requesting a few days to communicate with my brother. Walked up to the ship with J Tinley in the morning, who wrote to <span class=highlight_yellow>Netern</span> to send down the deed of release. All letters <span class=highlight_yellow>be</span> relative to our composition. Dined at home. In the evening had an <span class=highlight_yellow>ryotes</span> supper at the Northumberland. <span class=highlight_yellow>Won</span> a bet lost by <span class=highlight_yellow>Locklder</span> &amp; Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Holroryd</span>. Sat down 13 &amp; spent a pleasant evening</p>","pageId":725,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":423,"lock":null}
20:13:19.006 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/24/442
20:13:19.006 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":442,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW &amp; afterwards changed to East with snow. Walked to Tynemouth. Attended a sale of old furniture at Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Lenskerths</span>. Mrs Dixon came down to see Mrs Scott. Dined at J Tinleys. A large party.</p>","pageId":725,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":424,"lock":null}
20:13:19.006 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.007 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/24/442
20:13:19.007 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":442,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW &amp; afterwards changed to East with snow. Walked to Tynemouth. Attended a sale of old furniture at Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Lenskerths</span>. Mrs Dixon came down to see Mrs Scott. Dined at J Tinleys. A large party.</p>","pageId":725,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":424,"lock":null}
20:13:19.007 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/25/443
20:13:19.007 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":443,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. A hard frost. Wind E by S. Has been a little snow in the night. Last night the <span class=highlight_yellow>mews</span> room was on fire but was discovered in time to get put out before much damage was done. In a short time it would broken out &amp; spread that the whole building would have been destroyed. The floor rafters and ceiling of <span class=highlight_yellow>mews</span> room partly burnt. Walked with Boswell to Tynemouth. Dined at J Dales. Met a large party &amp; spent a pleasant day.</p>","pageId":725,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":425,"lock":null}
20:13:19.007 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.007 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/25/443
20:13:19.007 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":443,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. A hard frost. Wind E by S. Has been a little snow in the night. Last night the <span class=highlight_yellow>mews</span> room was on fire but was discovered in time to get put out before much damage was done. In a short time it would broken out &amp; spread that the whole building would have been destroyed. The floor rafters and ceiling of <span class=highlight_yellow>mews</span> room partly burnt. Walked with Boswell to Tynemouth. Dined at J Dales. Met a large party &amp; spent a pleasant day.</p>","pageId":725,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":425,"lock":null}
20:13:19.007 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/26/444
20:13:19.007 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":444,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; blowing fresh from E. Received a letter from William with a copy of his answer to J Young. Paid Morton &amp; Thompson for the Hope's bowsprit pump for &pound;25.7/-. Dined with H Dale, Mr Mark &amp; Mr Jackson of the 80<sup>th</sup> regiment. Spent a pleasant evening. Walked to the ship in the morning. Turned out a very wet night. Sleet</p>","pageId":725,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":426,"lock":null}
20:13:19.007 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
