20:13:19.008 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":444,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; blowing fresh from E. Received a letter from William with a copy of his answer to J Young. Paid Morton &amp; Thompson for the Hope's bowsprit pump for &pound;25.7/-. Dined with H Dale, Mr Mark &amp; Mr Jackson of the 80<sup>th</sup> regiment. Spent a pleasant evening. Walked to the ship in the morning. Turned out a very wet night. Sleet</p>","pageId":725,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":426,"lock":null}
20:13:19.008 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/27/445
20:13:19.008 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":445,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull wet morning. Wind SSW. Dined at home. In the evening attended a large party at Mr J Fenwicks, Preston Villa, about 120 there, a dinner.</p>","pageId":725,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":427,"lock":null}
20:13:19.008 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
