20:13:19.008 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":445,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull wet morning. Wind SSW. Dined at home. In the evening attended a large party at Mr J Fenwicks, Preston Villa, about 120 there, a dinner.</p>","pageId":725,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":427,"lock":null}
20:13:19.008 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/28/446
20:13:19.008 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":446,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A raw cold foggy morning. Wind SW. Drove up to Newcastle with Mr Tinley, called upon Mrs Dixon, went to the Quay side, but could not do anything for the Hope. Returned to Shields by steam boat. Dined with J Tinley &amp; went to the whist club at Mr Richmonds in the evening.</p>","pageId":725,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":428,"lock":null}
20:13:19.008 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.009 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/28/446
20:13:19.009 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":446,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A raw cold foggy morning. Wind SW. Drove up to Newcastle with Mr Tinley, called upon Mrs Dixon, went to the Quay side, but could not do anything for the Hope. Returned to Shields by steam boat. Dined with J Tinley &amp; went to the whist club at Mr Richmonds in the evening.</p>","pageId":725,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":428,"lock":null}
20:13:19.009 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/3/421
20:13:19.009 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":421,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning &amp; hard frost. Wind W &amp; W by S. A French &amp; I walked round the town with Mr Chapman of <span class=highlight_yellow>Elseneur</span> to call upon his friends. Dined at 2 o'clock with A Harry. On board the Choise, A French, A Nicholson, <span class=highlight_yellow>Drewing</span>, Cunningham, Mark ____, self &amp; Captain ____ Mr Bradshaw came on board. After dinner we spent a very pleasant day.</p>","pageId":722,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":403,"lock":null}
20:13:19.009 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.009 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/3/421
20:13:19.009 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":421,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning &amp; hard frost. Wind W &amp; W by S. A French &amp; I walked round the town with Mr Chapman of <span class=highlight_yellow>Elseneur</span> to call upon his friends. Dined at 2 o'clock with A Harry. On board the Choise, A French, A Nicholson, <span class=highlight_yellow>Drewing</span>, Cunningham, Mark ____, self &amp; Captain ____ Mr Bradshaw came on board. After dinner we spent a very pleasant day.</p>","pageId":722,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":403,"lock":null}
20:13:19.010 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/4/422
20:13:19.010 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":422,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp morning. Wind West. Passed part of the morning in drawing &amp; writing to William with Robert's account of <span class=highlight_yellow>seats</span>. Attended a meeting of shipowners &amp; masters for the purpose of establishing a asylum for aged &amp; infirm master mariners, an excellent institution &amp; long wasted the meeting most respectfully &amp; numerous attended &amp; then business well conducted &amp; a most liberal feeling persuading every person as the donation &amp; subscriptions best testified. Read a letter from Geo Dunn to know if I intended loading the Hope. Answered in the negative unless <span class=highlight_yellow>fieghted</span> or upheld. Dined at home. Mrs Scott  very unwell, but downstairs. Saw <span class=highlight_yellow>arr</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>&gamma;&alpha;</span><span class=highlight_yellow>&lambda;&lambda;&omicron;</span><span class=highlight_yellow>&pi;</span></p>","pageId":723,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":404,"lock":null}
20:13:19.010 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.010 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/4/422
20:13:19.010 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":422,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp morning. Wind West. Passed part of the morning in drawing &amp; writing to William with Robert's account of <span class=highlight_yellow>seats</span>. Attended a meeting of shipowners &amp; masters for the purpose of establishing a asylum for aged &amp; infirm master mariners, an excellent institution &amp; long wasted the meeting most respectfully &amp; numerous attended &amp; then business well conducted &amp; a most liberal feeling persuading every person as the donation &amp; subscriptions best testified. Read a letter from Geo Dunn to know if I intended loading the Hope. Answered in the negative unless <span class=highlight_yellow>fieghted</span> or upheld. Dined at home. Mrs Scott  very unwell, but downstairs. Saw <span class=highlight_yellow>arr</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>&gamma;&alpha;</span><span class=highlight_yellow>&lambda;&lambda;&omicron;</span><span class=highlight_yellow>&pi;</span></p>","pageId":723,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":404,"lock":null}
20:13:19.010 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/5/423
20:13:19.010 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":423,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Weather rather damp &amp; foggy. Wind from W to N by S. Passed the first of the morning in drawing. Dined at home. Saw <span class=highlight_yellow>a</span><span class=highlight_yellow>nn</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>&gamma;&alpha;</span><span class=highlight_yellow>&lambda;&lambda;&omicron;</span><span class=highlight_yellow>&pi;</span>. At the whist club</p>","pageId":723,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":405,"lock":null}
20:13:19.010 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
