20:13:19.019 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/16/462
20:13:19.019 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":462,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but cold &amp; Wind SW. A great number of light ships coming in. On board the Hope. Moved her from the Quay (Smiths) &amp; laid her upon the shore to have her keel surveyed for the Liberal Premium Club. Dined at home. Mrs Dixon down to see Mrs Scott. With Bell Jarvis at her sister Mary's</p>","pageId":727,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":444,"lock":null}
20:13:19.019 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.020 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/16/462
20:13:19.020 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":462,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but cold &amp; Wind SW. A great number of light ships coming in. On board the Hope. Moved her from the Quay (Smiths) &amp; laid her upon the shore to have her keel surveyed for the Liberal Premium Club. Dined at home. Mrs Dixon down to see Mrs Scott. With Bell Jarvis at her sister Mary's</p>","pageId":727,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":444,"lock":null}
20:13:19.020 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/17/463
20:13:19.020 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":463,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; blowing fresh from the SW &amp; cold. Another large fleet coming in. Borrowed off Robert &pound;5. On board the Hope. Two keels alongside. People engaged <span class=highlight_yellow>lending</span> sails. Walked up to the spout/<span class=highlight_yellow>huroonaschs</span> &amp; took lunch on board the 3 Brothers with A French, H Harry, Allen, W Harrison, J Wright there. Dined with J Tinley a party &amp; in the evening went to the ball which was thinly attended but a very pleasant one.</p>","pageId":727,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":445,"lock":null}
20:13:19.020 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.020 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/17/463
20:13:19.021 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":463,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; blowing fresh from the SW &amp; cold. Another large fleet coming in. Borrowed off Robert &pound;5. On board the Hope. Two keels alongside. People engaged <span class=highlight_yellow>lending</span> sails. Walked up to the spout/<span class=highlight_yellow>huroonaschs</span> &amp; took lunch on board the 3 Brothers with A French, H Harry, Allen, W Harrison, J Wright there. Dined with J Tinley a party &amp; in the evening went to the ball which was thinly attended but a very pleasant one.</p>","pageId":727,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":445,"lock":null}
20:13:19.021 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/18/464
20:13:19.021 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":464,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant day. Wind SW. Paid E Reed's mother &pound;1.8.9 being &frac14; years wages. On board the Hope. Got 9 keels in. paid Fenwick for making main stagsail &amp; foretopmast <span class=highlight_yellow>sturing</span><span class=highlight_yellow>s</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ail</span> &pound;2.9/-. Dined at home. Spent the evening at J Tinley's</p>","pageId":727,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":446,"lock":null}
20:13:19.021 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.021 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/18/464
20:13:19.021 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":464,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant day. Wind SW. Paid E Reed's mother &pound;1.8.9 being &frac14; years wages. On board the Hope. Got 9 keels in. paid Fenwick for making main stagsail &amp; foretopmast <span class=highlight_yellow>sturing</span><span class=highlight_yellow>s</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ail</span> &pound;2.9/-. Dined at home. Spent the evening at J Tinley's</p>","pageId":727,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":446,"lock":null}
20:13:19.021 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/19/465
20:13:19.021 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":465,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp morning. Showers of rain &amp; blowing fresh from SSW. Attended a meeting of the parishioners at the church respecting the burial ground at Tynemouth. The board of ordinance having given orders that no more interments shall take place. A most arbitrary &amp; unjust proceeding &amp; which the parish considers they have no right to do, it having been the parish church &amp; ground for time immemorial. Dined with Mr Allen &amp; afterward went on board the Hope. Got six more keels on board today. In the evening at the whist club. Paid Geo Slops &pound;1.13/- the balance of years wages account.</p>","pageId":727,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":447,"lock":null}
20:13:19.021 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.023 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/19/465
20:13:19.023 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":465,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp morning. Showers of rain &amp; blowing fresh from SSW. Attended a meeting of the parishioners at the church respecting the burial ground at Tynemouth. The board of ordinance having given orders that no more interments shall take place. A most arbitrary &amp; unjust proceeding &amp; which the parish considers they have no right to do, it having been the parish church &amp; ground for time immemorial. Dined with Mr Allen &amp; afterward went on board the Hope. Got six more keels on board today. In the evening at the whist club. Paid Geo Slops &pound;1.13/- the balance of years wages account.</p>","pageId":727,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":447,"lock":null}
20:13:19.023 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/2/448
20:13:19.023 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":448,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty morning. Wind SE &amp; E by S. Went to Newcastle by steam. Could do nothing for the Hope. Walked up to Westgate Street &amp; the billiard rooms. Returned to Shields to dinner. Spent the latter part of the evening at J Tinleys</p>","pageId":726,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":430,"lock":null}
20:13:19.023 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.023 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/2/448
20:13:19.023 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":448,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty morning. Wind SE &amp; E by S. Went to Newcastle by steam. Could do nothing for the Hope. Walked up to Westgate Street &amp; the billiard rooms. Returned to Shields to dinner. Spent the latter part of the evening at J Tinleys</p>","pageId":726,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":430,"lock":null}
20:13:19.023 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/20/466
20:13:19.023 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":466,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; blowing fresh from the SW. Mr Mark &amp; Ferguson dined with me on board the Hope at 1 o'clock. Got the last keel down in the morning at 3 o'clock pm <span class=highlight_yellow>move</span> ship out but having a foul anchor could not get to sea. Much damage done but on the middle sand &amp; much <span class=highlight_yellow>stove</span>. With Bell Jarvis in the evening.</p>","pageId":728,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":448,"lock":null}
20:13:19.023 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.024 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/20/466
20:13:19.024 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":466,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; blowing fresh from the SW. Mr Mark &amp; Ferguson dined with me on board the Hope at 1 o'clock. Got the last keel down in the morning at 3 o'clock pm <span class=highlight_yellow>move</span> ship out but having a foul anchor could not get to sea. Much damage done but on the middle sand &amp; much <span class=highlight_yellow>stove</span>. With Bell Jarvis in the evening.</p>","pageId":728,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":448,"lock":null}
20:13:19.024 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/21/467
20:13:19.024 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":467,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful spring morning. The Hope got to sea early. Wind NW. Paid Foy boat 13/- Went with Mr &amp; Mrs Tinley to Newcastle. Signed the Hope's cargo bill &pound;176.7.7 The <span class=highlight_yellow>Dmans</span> refused to change less than 21/- to upheld &amp; have I <span class=highlight_yellow>conceded</span> treated me <span class=highlight_yellow>exceptional</span> ill. Dined &amp; stayed all night with D Dixon. Wrote to William.</p>","pageId":728,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":449,"lock":null}
20:13:19.024 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.025 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/21/467
20:13:19.025 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":467,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful spring morning. The Hope got to sea early. Wind NW. Paid Foy boat 13/- Went with Mr &amp; Mrs Tinley to Newcastle. Signed the Hope's cargo bill &pound;176.7.7 The <span class=highlight_yellow>Dmans</span> refused to change less than 21/- to upheld &amp; have I <span class=highlight_yellow>conceded</span> treated me <span class=highlight_yellow>exceptional</span> ill. Dined &amp; stayed all night with D Dixon. Wrote to William.</p>","pageId":728,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":449,"lock":null}
20:13:19.025 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/22/468
20:13:19.025 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":468,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Most beautiful weather. Rather frosty &amp; wind SSE &amp; SE. Came down to Shields by steamer &amp; changed my cloths. Received a letter from William with one to J Tinley. Returned by steam to Newcastle &amp; again dined and stayed all night with D Dixon. Mrs Coll Dixon dined with us</p>","pageId":728,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":450,"lock":null}
20:13:19.025 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.026 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/22/468
20:13:19.026 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":468,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Most beautiful weather. Rather frosty &amp; wind SSE &amp; SE. Came down to Shields by steamer &amp; changed my cloths. Received a letter from William with one to J Tinley. Returned by steam to Newcastle &amp; again dined and stayed all night with D Dixon. Mrs Coll Dixon dined with us</p>","pageId":728,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":450,"lock":null}
20:13:19.026 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/23/469
20:13:19.026 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":469,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp &amp; unpleasant cold morning, blowing fresh  from the SE. Some loaded ships put back. Gave J Tinley, William's letter. My cold so much worse today &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>allofother</span> so unwell that I was obliged to lay up &amp; take physic.</p>","pageId":728,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":451,"lock":null}
20:13:19.026 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.026 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/23/469
20:13:19.026 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":469,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp &amp; unpleasant cold morning, blowing fresh  from the SE. Some loaded ships put back. Gave J Tinley, William's letter. My cold so much worse today &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>allofother</span> so unwell that I was obliged to lay up &amp; take physic.</p>","pageId":728,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":451,"lock":null}
20:13:19.026 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/24/470
20:13:19.026 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":470,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather but the wind still from the SE. Confined myself entirely to the house in consequence of my cold.</p>","pageId":728,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":452,"lock":null}
20:13:19.026 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.027 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/24/470
20:13:19.028 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":470,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather but the wind still from the SE. Confined myself entirely to the house in consequence of my cold.</p>","pageId":728,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":452,"lock":null}
20:13:19.028 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/25/471
20:13:19.028 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":471,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Frosty weather. Wind changed to NW. Walked to the newsroom about 2 o'clock &amp; read the papers. Wind in the afternoon changed to about N by E &amp; NNE. The Lady Jane sailed for the <span class=highlight_yellow>fishery</span>. Gave Mrs Scott her &frac14; year annuity &pound;75</p>","pageId":728,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":453,"lock":null}
20:13:19.028 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
