20:13:19.031 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":449,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind NW. Went by steam to Newcastle. Nothing to be done for the Hope. Dined with Dixon Dixon. In the evening went to the theatre. Met the  <span class=highlight_yellow>Ildestons</span> there. A very thin house. The high sheriffs benefit. The Dixons &amp; Tom &amp; Bell Smith went to a ball given by the offices of the dragoon quarter at Newcastle.</p>","pageId":726,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":431,"lock":null}
20:13:19.031 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/30/476
20:13:19.031 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":476,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp morning having been a little rain. Wind E. Went over to Sunderland with Captain Bunbury &amp; Jackson of the 80<sup>th</sup>. Allen Davies of the artillery to dine at the Mulstrum &amp; spent a pleasant day. The Hope got to London on Friday afternoon.</p>","pageId":729,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":458,"lock":null}
20:13:19.031 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
