20:13:19.032 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":477,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A wet morning &amp; cool. Wind NE with showers of snow towards the middle of the day. Jackson &amp; I returned from Sunderland. Dined at Mr Matthews, a party.</p>","pageId":729,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":459,"lock":null}
20:13:19.032 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/4/450
20:13:19.032 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":450,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A raw cold morning. Wind NE. Tom &amp; Bell Smith started for Togston. I returned to Shields by steam to dinner. Went to a small party in the evening at Mr Marks</p>","pageId":726,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":432,"lock":null}
20:13:19.032 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.033 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/4/450
20:13:19.033 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":450,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A raw cold morning. Wind NE. Tom &amp; Bell Smith started for Togston. I returned to Shields by steam to dinner. Went to a small party in the evening at Mr Marks</p>","pageId":726,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":432,"lock":null}
20:13:19.033 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/5/451
20:13:19.033 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":451,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather. Wind NE. Wrote to J Young that we were made to pay him &amp; his father's lie <span class=highlight_yellow>leaedind</span> but no more. Added a postscript to J Tindley's letter to William. Dined at home. Attended the whist club in the evening.</p>","pageId":726,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":433,"lock":null}
20:13:19.033 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.033 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/5/451
20:13:19.033 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":451,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather. Wind NE. Wrote to J Young that we were made to pay him &amp; his father's lie <span class=highlight_yellow>leaedind</span> but no more. Added a postscript to J Tindley's letter to William. Dined at home. Attended the whist club in the evening.</p>","pageId":726,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":433,"lock":null}
20:13:19.033 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/6/452
20:13:19.033 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":452,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather cold. Wind NNE. Walked up to the ship. George <span class=highlight_yellow>Slofs</span> employed rigging her with only the <span class=highlight_yellow>apprentice</span> of the little boy Ned Reed. <span class=highlight_yellow>For</span> a very fine young man, only been seven coal voyages &amp; is as good as any man. Dined at home. Saw poor Richard Brown who I much fear has not long to live.</p>","pageId":726,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":434,"lock":null}
20:13:19.033 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.034 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/6/452
20:13:19.034 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":452,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather cold. Wind NNE. Walked up to the ship. George <span class=highlight_yellow>Slofs</span> employed rigging her with only the <span class=highlight_yellow>apprentice</span> of the little boy Ned Reed. <span class=highlight_yellow>For</span> a very fine young man, only been seven coal voyages &amp; is as good as any man. Dined at home. Saw poor Richard Brown who I much fear has not long to live.</p>","pageId":726,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":434,"lock":null}
20:13:19.034 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/7/453
20:13:19.034 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":453,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning. Wind NW. Went by coach to Newcastle but evening continues very dull &amp; could do nothing for the Hope. An immense number of people at Newcastle, having been to see the unfortunate woman <span class=highlight_silver>Jane </span><span class=highlight_silver>Jameson</span> hanged for the murder of her mother. Returned home by steam to dinner. Attended the whist club at J Dale's. Met Jane Thompson for the first time at Jenny Maxwells</p>","pageId":726,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":435,"lock":null}
20:13:19.034 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.034 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/7/453
20:13:19.034 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":453,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning. Wind NW. Went by coach to Newcastle but evening continues very dull &amp; could do nothing for the Hope. An immense number of people at Newcastle, having been to see the unfortunate woman <span class=highlight_silver>Jane </span><span class=highlight_silver>Jameson</span> hanged for the murder of her mother. Returned home by steam to dinner. Attended the whist club at J Dale's. Met Jane Thompson for the first time at Jenny Maxwells</p>","pageId":726,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":435,"lock":null}
20:13:19.034 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/8/454
20:13:19.034 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":454,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, but rather dull. Wind NW. Took physic &amp; could not go to church. Wrote to Mr P Lacing respecting C Harry's claim. At the <span class=highlight_yellow>grange man</span> Sunderland. Dined at home. The newspapers today filled with <span class=highlight_yellow>Mr </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Puls</span> expositions of the measures of <span class=highlight_yellow>ministise</span> for the relief of the Catholics. Took wine in the evening with H Harry &amp; J Lunning have at the Albion. Afterwards called at the Mulstrum &amp; saw Bell Jarvis !!!!</p>","pageId":726,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":436,"lock":null}
20:13:19.034 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.035 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/8/454
20:13:19.035 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":454,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, but rather dull. Wind NW. Took physic &amp; could not go to church. Wrote to Mr P Lacing respecting C Harry's claim. At the <span class=highlight_yellow>grange man</span> Sunderland. Dined at home. The newspapers today filled with <span class=highlight_yellow>Mr </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Puls</span> expositions of the measures of <span class=highlight_yellow>ministise</span> for the relief of the Catholics. Took wine in the evening with H Harry &amp; J Lunning have at the Albion. Afterwards called at the Mulstrum &amp; saw Bell Jarvis !!!!</p>","pageId":726,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":436,"lock":null}
20:13:19.035 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/9/455
20:13:19.035 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":455,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW. On board the Hope. Brought some beef <span class=highlight_yellow>6.0.6 at 4 o'clock</span>. Dined at Mr Allen's &amp; suppered in the evening at the George with a party. An Oyster supper. Kept it up very late. Paid &pound;1.4/- entrance for Friday C Club. Got &pound;5 of Chapmans</p>","pageId":726,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":437,"lock":null}
20:13:19.035 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.035 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/9/455
20:13:19.035 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":455,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW. On board the Hope. Brought some beef <span class=highlight_yellow>6.0.6 at 4 o'clock</span>. Dined at Mr Allen's &amp; suppered in the evening at the George with a party. An Oyster supper. Kept it up very late. Paid &pound;1.4/- entrance for Friday C Club. Got &pound;5 of Chapmans</p>","pageId":726,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":437,"lock":null}
20:13:19.035 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/1/478
20:13:19.035 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":478,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold winter's morning. Wind NE having been a good deal of snow during the night. Wind changed to NW with heavy showers of hail &amp; snow during the day&amp; night. Dined at home. In the evening at a party at Mr Mathews</p>","pageId":729,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":460,"lock":null}
20:13:19.035 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.036 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/1/478
20:13:19.036 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":478,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold winter's morning. Wind NE having been a good deal of snow during the night. Wind changed to NW with heavy showers of hail &amp; snow during the day&amp; night. Dined at home. In the evening at a party at Mr Mathews</p>","pageId":729,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":460,"lock":null}
20:13:19.036 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/10/487
20:13:19.036 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":487,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Weather moderating and fair having been very strong all night. Wind about E by S. Several ships arrived this morning. Among them the Hope having left London on Tuesday. A schooner loaded with grain got upon the hard Sand, the sea higher than has been this winter. Went to Newcastle &amp; fixed the Hope to load <span class=highlight_yellow>Townty</span><span class=highlight_yellow> main</span> again the price <span class=highlight_yellow>20/ chat</span> &amp; to be applied 8/6 freight. Returned by steam to dinner. Wind changed to SW &amp; then to SE.</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":469,"lock":null}
20:13:19.036 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.036 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/10/487
20:13:19.036 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":487,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Weather moderating and fair having been very strong all night. Wind about E by S. Several ships arrived this morning. Among them the Hope having left London on Tuesday. A schooner loaded with grain got upon the hard Sand, the sea higher than has been this winter. Went to Newcastle &amp; fixed the Hope to load <span class=highlight_yellow>Townty</span><span class=highlight_yellow> main</span> again the price <span class=highlight_yellow>20/ chat</span> &amp; to be applied 8/6 freight. Returned by steam to dinner. Wind changed to SW &amp; then to SE.</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":469,"lock":null}
20:13:19.036 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/11/488
20:13:19.036 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":488,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fair morning. Wind WNW. About 11 o'clock began to rain. Drew &pound;40 out of Chapmans to pay wages &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>hadesmens</span> bells for the Hope. Mr Mark <span class=highlight_yellow>sit </span>took our dinner on board. Wind got to ESE again. Attended the whist club at R Pearts. Wrote to William.</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":470,"lock":null}
20:13:19.036 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.037 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/11/488
20:13:19.037 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":488,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fair morning. Wind WNW. About 11 o'clock began to rain. Drew &pound;40 out of Chapmans to pay wages &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>hadesmens</span> bells for the Hope. Mr Mark <span class=highlight_yellow>sit </span>took our dinner on board. Wind got to ESE again. Attended the whist club at R Pearts. Wrote to William.</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":470,"lock":null}
20:13:19.037 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/12/489
20:13:19.037 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":489,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet morning. Wind SSE. Received a letter from William <span class=highlight_yellow>weth</span> the Hope. Balance note $40.11/- &amp; &pound;50 lent = &pound;90.11. Went to church. Dined with J Tinley. Mr &amp; Mrs Carr &amp; Jane Kelsoe there.</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":471,"lock":null}
20:13:19.037 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.038 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/12/489
20:13:19.038 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":489,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet morning. Wind SSE. Received a letter from William <span class=highlight_yellow>weth</span> the Hope. Balance note $40.11/- &amp; &pound;50 lent = &pound;90.11. Went to church. Dined with J Tinley. Mr &amp; Mrs Carr &amp; Jane Kelsoe there.</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":471,"lock":null}
20:13:19.038 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/13/490
20:13:19.038 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":490,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Rather a dull morning. Wind blowing fresh from SW &amp; W. Several ships sailed for America but no loaded vessels got out. A heavy sea being upon the bar. Moved the Hope from the crane to a tees in South Shields. The river on the north side being so crowded Dined at home. Joined a party on board the Harmony. <span class=highlight_yellow>Mr</span> Peark in the evening. With Bell Jarvis. Paid into Chapmans. The bill for &pound;90.10/-</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":472,"lock":null}
20:13:19.038 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.038 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/13/490
20:13:19.038 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":490,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Rather a dull morning. Wind blowing fresh from SW &amp; W. Several ships sailed for America but no loaded vessels got out. A heavy sea being upon the bar. Moved the Hope from the crane to a tees in South Shields. The river on the north side being so crowded Dined at home. Joined a party on board the Harmony. <span class=highlight_yellow>Mr</span> Peark in the evening. With Bell Jarvis. Paid into Chapmans. The bill for &pound;90.10/-</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":472,"lock":null}
20:13:19.038 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/14/491
20:13:19.038 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":491,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning &amp; blowing fresh from the SW. On board of ship Mr Allen &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Mary</span> &amp; Bell Jarvis. Danced on board with me. Drew a draft for self for &pound;15 &amp; paid into the account of Exors &pound;20. Paid Mr Lough an <span class=highlight_yellow>average</span> for Hope Club &pound;19.2.1. In the evening the wind changed to SSE blowing hard all night with rain.</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":473,"lock":null}
20:13:19.038 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.039 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/14/491
20:13:19.039 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":491,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning &amp; blowing fresh from the SW. On board of ship Mr Allen &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Mary</span> &amp; Bell Jarvis. Danced on board with me. Drew a draft for self for &pound;15 &amp; paid into the account of Exors &pound;20. Paid Mr Lough an <span class=highlight_yellow>average</span> for Hope Club &pound;19.2.1. In the evening the wind changed to SSE blowing hard all night with rain.</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":473,"lock":null}
20:13:19.039 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/15/492
20:13:19.039 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":492,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>This morning dry weather but <span class=highlight_yellow>still</span> blowing hard all night &amp; still continuing from SSE &amp; S by E. The Hope moved down to a tier below the library to load up. Dined at home. Wrote the secretary of the Hope Club to reduce the value of the Hope to &pound;1600.</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":474,"lock":null}
20:13:19.039 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.040 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/15/492
20:13:19.040 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":492,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>This morning dry weather but <span class=highlight_yellow>still</span> blowing hard all night &amp; still continuing from SSE &amp; S by E. The Hope moved down to a tier below the library to load up. Dined at home. Wrote the secretary of the Hope Club to reduce the value of the Hope to &pound;1600.</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":474,"lock":null}
20:13:19.040 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/16/2301
20:13:19.040 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":2301,"version":4,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":16,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>Could not attend the oyster supplier at the George in consequence. Gave Goe Slops 20/- on account of his wages.</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2241,"lock":null}
20:13:19.040 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.040 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/16/2301
20:13:19.040 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":2301,"version":4,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":16,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>Could not attend the oyster supplier at the George in consequence. Gave Goe Slops 20/- on account of his wages.</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2241,"lock":null}
20:13:19.040 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/16/493
20:13:19.040 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":493,"version":1,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A&nbsp;very&nbsp;wet&nbsp;morning.&nbsp;Wind&nbsp;SW.&nbsp;On&nbsp;board&nbsp;the&nbsp;Hope.&nbsp;She&nbsp;got&nbsp;two&nbsp;keels&nbsp;down&nbsp;today&nbsp;making&nbsp;15.&nbsp;Dined&nbsp;on&nbsp;board.&nbsp;Dr&nbsp;Drewery&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;W&nbsp;Peart&nbsp;with&nbsp;me.&nbsp;A&nbsp;great&nbsp;many&nbsp;ships&nbsp;got&nbsp;to&nbsp;sea&nbsp;this&nbsp;afternoon.&nbsp;The&nbsp;wind&nbsp;changed&nbsp;to&nbsp;S&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;S&nbsp;by&nbsp;E.&nbsp;Poor&nbsp;R&nbsp;Brown&nbsp;died&nbsp;today.&nbsp;A&nbsp;serious&nbsp;loss&nbsp;to&nbsp;his&nbsp;family.&nbsp;</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":475,"lock":null}
20:13:19.040 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
