20:13:19.041 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":493,"version":1,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A&nbsp;very&nbsp;wet&nbsp;morning.&nbsp;Wind&nbsp;SW.&nbsp;On&nbsp;board&nbsp;the&nbsp;Hope.&nbsp;She&nbsp;got&nbsp;two&nbsp;keels&nbsp;down&nbsp;today&nbsp;making&nbsp;15.&nbsp;Dined&nbsp;on&nbsp;board.&nbsp;Dr&nbsp;Drewery&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;W&nbsp;Peart&nbsp;with&nbsp;me.&nbsp;A&nbsp;great&nbsp;many&nbsp;ships&nbsp;got&nbsp;to&nbsp;sea&nbsp;this&nbsp;afternoon.&nbsp;The&nbsp;wind&nbsp;changed&nbsp;to&nbsp;S&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;S&nbsp;by&nbsp;E.&nbsp;Poor&nbsp;R&nbsp;Brown&nbsp;died&nbsp;today.&nbsp;A&nbsp;serious&nbsp;loss&nbsp;to&nbsp;his&nbsp;family.&nbsp;</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":475,"lock":null}
20:13:19.041 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/17/494
20:13:19.041 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":494,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Good Friday. A most beautiful morning. Wind NW. Did not go to church in consequence of poor Robert Brown's death. On board the Hope. She got the remainder of her coals down &amp; sailed this afternoon. Towed out by a steam boat, the wind being from the SSE. Dined at home &amp; afterwards went with H Harry to Mr Sadlers at Whittle Point to take wine in the evening at <span class=highlight_yellow>Nancy</span> Jervis</p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":476,"lock":null}
20:13:19.041 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.041 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/17/494
20:13:19.041 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":494,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Good Friday. A most beautiful morning. Wind NW. Did not go to church in consequence of poor Robert Brown's death. On board the Hope. She got the remainder of her coals down &amp; sailed this afternoon. Towed out by a steam boat, the wind being from the SSE. Dined at home &amp; afterwards went with H Harry to Mr Sadlers at Whittle Point to take wine in the evening at <span class=highlight_yellow>Nancy</span> Jervis</p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":476,"lock":null}
20:13:19.041 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/18/495
20:13:19.041 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":495,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, but has been rain early. Wind WNW. Paid the pilot of the Hope &pound;1.15/. Paid <span class=highlight_yellow>Twi</span><span class=highlight_yellow>g</span><span class=highlight_yellow>el</span><span class=highlight_yellow> </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Bragier</span> for the Hope &pound;12.13/-. Call upon &amp; saw about Richard's funeral. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home. In the evening suppered at the Albion upon some oysters, given by A Cunningham. <span class=highlight_lime>With Ann!!!!!!</span></p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":477,"lock":null}
20:13:19.041 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.042 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/18/495
20:13:19.042 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":495,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, but has been rain early. Wind WNW. Paid the pilot of the Hope &pound;1.15/. Paid <span class=highlight_yellow>Twi</span><span class=highlight_yellow>g</span><span class=highlight_yellow>el</span><span class=highlight_yellow> </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Bragier</span> for the Hope &pound;12.13/-. Call upon &amp; saw about Richard's funeral. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home. In the evening suppered at the Albion upon some oysters, given by A Cunningham. <span class=highlight_lime>With Ann!!!!!!</span></p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":477,"lock":null}
20:13:19.042 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/19/496
20:13:19.042 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":496,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A wet morning. Wind NW. Signed the Hope's cargo bill &pound;166.5.1 &amp; returned it to Geo Dunn&amp; Sons. Continued raining heavily until 4 o'clock when it cleared up. Dined at home. With Bell Jervis in the evening. Turned out a very rainy night.</p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":478,"lock":null}
20:13:19.042 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.042 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/19/496
20:13:19.042 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":496,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A wet morning. Wind NW. Signed the Hope's cargo bill &pound;166.5.1 &amp; returned it to Geo Dunn&amp; Sons. Continued raining heavily until 4 o'clock when it cleared up. Dined at home. With Bell Jervis in the evening. Turned out a very rainy night.</p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":478,"lock":null}
20:13:19.042 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/2/479
20:13:19.042 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":479,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of cold weather with showers of snow &amp; wind NNW. Although a heavy swell upon the bar &amp; occasionally breaking, several ships got to sea. Dined at home. In the evening at the Jarvis's with Bell.</p>","pageId":729,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":461,"lock":null}
20:13:19.042 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.043 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/2/479
20:13:19.043 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":479,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of cold weather with showers of snow &amp; wind NNW. Although a heavy swell upon the bar &amp; occasionally breaking, several ships got to sea. Dined at home. In the evening at the Jarvis's with Bell.</p>","pageId":729,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":461,"lock":null}
20:13:19.043 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/20/497
20:13:19.043 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":497,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather. Wind about N by E. Turned out a most beautiful &amp; warm day &amp; favourable for Tynemouth Races. Immense number of people out. Dined at home</p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":479,"lock":null}
20:13:19.043 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.043 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/20/497
20:13:19.043 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":497,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather. Wind about N by E. Turned out a most beautiful &amp; warm day &amp; favourable for Tynemouth Races. Immense number of people out. Dined at home</p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":479,"lock":null}
20:13:19.043 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/21/498
20:13:19.043 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":498,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Rather a dull morning. Wind SSE. Dixon &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Befry</span> came down from Beaton &amp; the foreman &amp; I attended the remains of poor Rich Brown to the grave with his three youngest boys. I returned with them to dine &amp; stay all night at Benton.</p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":480,"lock":null}
20:13:19.044 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.045 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/21/498
20:13:19.045 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":498,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Rather a dull morning. Wind SSE. Dixon &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Befry</span> came down from Beaton &amp; the foreman &amp; I attended the remains of poor Rich Brown to the grave with his three youngest boys. I returned with them to dine &amp; stay all night at Benton.</p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":480,"lock":null}
20:13:19.045 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/22/499
20:13:19.045 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":499,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold morning with a dry easterly wind. Walked down to Shields. Dined at homer &amp; afterwards went to Tynemouth races, very few people there &amp; not worth going to. Drank tea with Mr Tibbs. With Bell Jarvis in the evening</p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":481,"lock":null}
20:13:19.045 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.045 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/22/499
20:13:19.045 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":499,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold morning with a dry easterly wind. Walked down to Shields. Dined at homer &amp; afterwards went to Tynemouth races, very few people there &amp; not worth going to. Drank tea with Mr Tibbs. With Bell Jarvis in the evening</p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":481,"lock":null}
20:13:19.045 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/23/500
20:13:19.045 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":500,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another cold morning. Wind easterly. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined with J Tinley. In the evening called upon Mr J Young &amp; had a long conversation both with him about taking our dividend without surveying. Also he did not seem so determined in his opposition. He desired me to see H Dale &amp; talk to him.</p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":482,"lock":null}
20:13:19.045 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.046 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/23/500
20:13:19.046 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":500,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another cold morning. Wind easterly. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined with J Tinley. In the evening called upon Mr J Young &amp; had a long conversation both with him about taking our dividend without surveying. Also he did not seem so determined in his opposition. He desired me to see H Dale &amp; talk to him.</p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":482,"lock":null}
20:13:19.046 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/24/501
20:13:19.046 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":501,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of cold weather &amp; ENE wind. Dined at home &amp; afterwards went with H Harry &amp; R Peart &amp; drank whisky on board the Ardineaple  steamer Captain Cunningham. On our return when the boat reached the shore, Cunningham stumbled &amp; falling upon me, we both rolled overboard. Got a good dunking. Wrote to Mrs Scott of my determination not to make her an allowance.</p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":483,"lock":null}
20:13:19.046 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.046 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/24/501
20:13:19.046 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":501,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of cold weather &amp; ENE wind. Dined at home &amp; afterwards went with H Harry &amp; R Peart &amp; drank whisky on board the Ardineaple  steamer Captain Cunningham. On our return when the boat reached the shore, Cunningham stumbled &amp; falling upon me, we both rolled overboard. Got a good dunking. Wrote to Mrs Scott of my determination not to make her an allowance.</p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":483,"lock":null}
20:13:19.046 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/25/502
20:13:19.046 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":502,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning but still cool &amp; wind NE &amp; ENE. Walked with H Harry to Tynemouth. Dined at home. Received a letter from William of the arrival &amp; sale of the Hope on Wednesday at 27/- = to 6/6 freight. This well I'm <span class=highlight_yellow>upheld</span> 8/6. Answered the letter desiring him to tender the Hope to the Gafs Co. to carry coal at &pound;9 a keel or 21/6 freight Newcastle <span class=highlight_yellow>cha</span>. Attended the whist club at Tibbs. Got &pound;5 of Chapman. <span class=highlight_yellow>Paid</span> steam boat for Hope 30/- <span class=highlight_yellow>aformenbec</span> 20/- washing 31/6</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":484,"lock":null}
20:13:19.046 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.047 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/25/502
20:13:19.047 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":502,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning but still cool &amp; wind NE &amp; ENE. Walked with H Harry to Tynemouth. Dined at home. Received a letter from William of the arrival &amp; sale of the Hope on Wednesday at 27/- = to 6/6 freight. This well I'm <span class=highlight_yellow>upheld</span> 8/6. Answered the letter desiring him to tender the Hope to the Gafs Co. to carry coal at &pound;9 a keel or 21/6 freight Newcastle <span class=highlight_yellow>cha</span>. Attended the whist club at Tibbs. Got &pound;5 of Chapman. <span class=highlight_yellow>Paid</span> steam boat for Hope 30/- <span class=highlight_yellow>aformenbec</span> 20/- washing 31/6</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":484,"lock":null}
20:13:19.047 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/26/503
20:13:19.047 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":503,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Quite summer weather. Wind S &amp; changed before 12 o'clock to SE. Attended morning service. Dined at home at 2 o'clock &amp; afterwards walked to Tynemouth with H Harry. On our return had a bottle of port at the George. With Bell Jarvis in the evening.</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":485,"lock":null}
20:13:19.047 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.047 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/26/503
20:13:19.047 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":503,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Quite summer weather. Wind S &amp; changed before 12 o'clock to SE. Attended morning service. Dined at home at 2 o'clock &amp; afterwards walked to Tynemouth with H Harry. On our return had a bottle of port at the George. With Bell Jarvis in the evening.</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":485,"lock":null}
20:13:19.047 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/27/504
20:13:19.047 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":504,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A showery morning. Wind N by W. In the house all the morning. Mrs Dixon brought Emma down again. Dined at house. In the evening went up to the castle &amp; played a rubber at Dacres rooms.  With rum I think!!!</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":486,"lock":null}
20:13:19.047 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.048 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/27/504
20:13:19.048 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":504,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A showery morning. Wind N by W. In the house all the morning. Mrs Dixon brought Emma down again. Dined at house. In the evening went up to the castle &amp; played a rubber at Dacres rooms.  With rum I think!!!</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":486,"lock":null}
20:13:19.048 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/28/505
20:13:19.048 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":505,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A showery morning &amp; blowing fresh from the N &amp; W by N and increased to a very heavy gale of wind varying between NNW and NNE which brought on a tremendous sea, a small sloop in coming in got upon the Heard Sand. Dined at home.</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":487,"lock":null}
20:13:19.048 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.048 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/28/505
20:13:19.048 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":505,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A showery morning &amp; blowing fresh from the N &amp; W by N and increased to a very heavy gale of wind varying between NNW and NNE which brought on a tremendous sea, a small sloop in coming in got upon the Heard Sand. Dined at home.</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":487,"lock":null}
20:13:19.048 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/29/506
20:13:19.048 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":506,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>The gale has continued all night with showers of snow with a tremendous sea. Wind continues the same as yesterday. The gales abated towards evening. Dined at home. In the evening with Bell Jarvis</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":488,"lock":null}
20:13:19.048 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.049 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/29/506
20:13:19.049 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":506,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>The gale has continued all night with showers of snow with a tremendous sea. Wind continues the same as yesterday. The gales abated towards evening. Dined at home. In the evening with Bell Jarvis</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":488,"lock":null}
20:13:19.049 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/3/480
20:13:19.049 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":480,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A clear frosty morning. Wind NW. received a letter from William of the sale of the Hope at 38/6  8/3 for <span class=highlight_yellow>Town by</span> = to <span class=highlight_yellow>7</span> freight <span class=highlight_yellow>eneserable</span> work. Dined at home. Slept all night with Bell Jervis at her sisters.</p>","pageId":729,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":462,"lock":null}
20:13:19.049 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.049 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/3/480
20:13:19.049 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":480,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A clear frosty morning. Wind NW. received a letter from William of the sale of the Hope at 38/6  8/3 for <span class=highlight_yellow>Town by</span> = to <span class=highlight_yellow>7</span> freight <span class=highlight_yellow>eneserable</span> work. Dined at home. Slept all night with Bell Jervis at her sisters.</p>","pageId":729,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":462,"lock":null}
20:13:19.049 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/30/507
20:13:19.049 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":507,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; again calm Weather. Wind NW by N. Went to Newcastle by steamer to dine with Mr R <span class=highlight_yellow>Arsey</span> in Eldon Square. Spent a very pleasant day &amp; returned to Shields. In the evening took Mr Dacres <font color=#BFBFBF>&amp;</font><font color=#BFBFBF> </font><span class=highlight_yellow>RA</span> with me. Tom Smith &amp; his mother arrived at Dockwray Square today.</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":489,"lock":null}
20:13:19.049 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.050 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/30/507
20:13:19.050 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":507,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; again calm Weather. Wind NW by N. Went to Newcastle by steamer to dine with Mr R <span class=highlight_yellow>Arsey</span> in Eldon Square. Spent a very pleasant day &amp; returned to Shields. In the evening took Mr Dacres <font color=#BFBFBF>&amp;</font><font color=#BFBFBF> </font><span class=highlight_yellow>RA</span> with me. Tom Smith &amp; his mother arrived at Dockwray Square today.</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":489,"lock":null}
20:13:19.050 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/4/481
20:13:19.050 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":481,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful mild morning. Wind WNW. Got home to breakfast after sleeping with Bell Jarvis. The wind in the afternoon changed to SE. Several ships sailed for America &amp; the Baltic. The XYZ <span class=highlight_yellow>Ld</span><span class=highlight_yellow> the soles run</span>.  Dined with J Tinley, Ian Carr married to Sam Barton &amp; got home this morning attended the whist club at H Dales.</p>","pageId":729,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":463,"lock":null}
20:13:19.050 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.050 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/4/481
20:13:19.050 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":481,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful mild morning. Wind WNW. Got home to breakfast after sleeping with Bell Jarvis. The wind in the afternoon changed to SE. Several ships sailed for America &amp; the Baltic. The XYZ <span class=highlight_yellow>Ld</span><span class=highlight_yellow> the soles run</span>.  Dined with J Tinley, Ian Carr married to Sam Barton &amp; got home this morning attended the whist club at H Dales.</p>","pageId":729,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":463,"lock":null}
20:13:19.050 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/5/482
20:13:19.050 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":482,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp morning wind SSE. Turned out very wet. Wrote to William. Wind changed in the afternoon to SE. Found myself very queer this morning in consequence of late hours &amp; last night at the Dales. Stayed in the house all day. In the evening at the newsroom &amp; called at the Mulstrum &amp; gave Bennett a <span class=highlight_yellow>turn</span>.</p>","pageId":729,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":464,"lock":null}
20:13:19.050 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
