20:13:19.052 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":484,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet morning. Wind East &amp; been much rain during the night. Dined with ben Wright &amp; a party <span class=highlight_yellow>ra</span><span class=highlight_yellow> bard</span>. Then Stephen &amp; spent a very pleasant evening.</p>","pageId":729,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":466,"lock":null}
20:13:19.052 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/8/485
20:13:19.052 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":485,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull thick morning &amp; turned out wet. Wind NW. Heard from Mr Stephenson the Hope was out on Monday &amp; going to take in dung. Dined at home.</p>","pageId":729,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":467,"lock":null}
20:13:19.052 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.052 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/8/485
20:13:19.052 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":485,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull thick morning &amp; turned out wet. Wind NW. Heard from Mr Stephenson the Hope was out on Monday &amp; going to take in dung. Dined at home.</p>","pageId":729,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":467,"lock":null}
20:13:19.052 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/9/486
20:13:19.052 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":486,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind S by E &amp; heavy sea upon the bar. Bowies Brittania arrived in the harbour this morning without the Captain Mr W Bowie on board. Supposed to have jumped out of the cabin window when off the bar. Dined at home. Mrs Dixon joined me &amp; returned home in the evening.</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":468,"lock":null}
20:13:19.052 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.053 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/9/486
20:13:19.053 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":486,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind S by E &amp; heavy sea upon the bar. Bowies Brittania arrived in the harbour this morning without the Captain Mr W Bowie on board. Supposed to have jumped out of the cabin window when off the bar. Dined at home. Mrs Dixon joined me &amp; returned home in the evening.</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":468,"lock":null}
20:13:19.053 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/1/508
20:13:19.053 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":508,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW walked about the town with Tom Smith the principle part of the morning. Dined at home &amp; took a walk to Tynemouth after dinner. Accepted <span class=highlight_yellow>In</span> Hearn's bill for &pound;34.7/- at 3 <span class=highlight_yellow>mo</span><span class=highlight_yellow>nth</span><span class=highlight_yellow>s</span> dated 27 April, due 30 July, for repairing Hope's sails. A most extraordinary bill.</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":490,"lock":null}
20:13:19.053 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.054 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/1/508
20:13:19.054 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":508,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW walked about the town with Tom Smith the principle part of the morning. Dined at home &amp; took a walk to Tynemouth after dinner. Accepted <span class=highlight_yellow>In</span> Hearn's bill for &pound;34.7/- at 3 <span class=highlight_yellow>mo</span><span class=highlight_yellow>nth</span><span class=highlight_yellow>s</span> dated 27 April, due 30 July, for repairing Hope's sails. A most extraordinary bill.</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":490,"lock":null}
20:13:19.054 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/10/517
20:13:19.054 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":517,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning &amp; summers weather SE. Went with Emma to church. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. Took wine with H Harry. Walked to Tynemouth in the  evening.</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":499,"lock":null}
20:13:19.054 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
