20:13:19.056 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":520,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind SE. The Hope gone up to the spout this tide. Walked with Captain Webb up to the Hope &amp; dined on board</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":502,"lock":null}
20:13:19.056 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/14/521
20:13:19.056 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":521,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine day. Wind W by N. Changed to SW. Went by steam to Newcastle. Gave the fitter the Hope's monthly bill. Called upon J Hodgson &amp; returned to dinner. In the evening a little rain.</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":503,"lock":null}
20:13:19.056 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.056 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/14/521
20:13:19.056 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":521,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine day. Wind W by N. Changed to SW. Went by steam to Newcastle. Gave the fitter the Hope's monthly bill. Called upon J Hodgson &amp; returned to dinner. In the evening a little rain.</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":503,"lock":null}
20:13:19.056 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/15/522
20:13:19.056 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":522,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning but fine spring weather. Wind NE. Mr Mark, Mr Sadler &amp; I walked up to Cramlington Spout. Found the Hope hauling off &amp; she shortly after proceeded down the river having only taken in 14 keels. Dined with Mr Sadler. With Bell Jarvis in the evening.</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":504,"lock":null}
20:13:19.056 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.056 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/15/522
20:13:19.056 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":522,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning but fine spring weather. Wind NE. Mr Mark, Mr Sadler &amp; I walked up to Cramlington Spout. Found the Hope hauling off &amp; she shortly after proceeded down the river having only taken in 14 keels. Dined with Mr Sadler. With Bell Jarvis in the evening.</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":504,"lock":null}
20:13:19.057 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/16/523
20:13:19.057 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":523,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful summers morning. Wind ENE. Received a letter from William agreeing to offer Younger 10/- in the &pound;. Drew &pound;20 out of Chapman. &pound;15 for Stephenson &amp; &pound;5 for self. Drew &pound;5 more in the afternoon. Stephenson wanting &pound;20. Dined at home. In the evening called upon A Dale to propose to join Younger's 10/- in full. Dale <span class=highlight_yellow>sacfe</span> for Younger, who I afterwards found much to my relief of mind had agreed to our proposal. Spent the evening with Mr Allen. With Bell Jervis.</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":505,"lock":null}
20:13:19.057 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.057 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/16/523
20:13:19.057 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":523,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful summers morning. Wind ENE. Received a letter from William agreeing to offer Younger 10/- in the &pound;. Drew &pound;20 out of Chapman. &pound;15 for Stephenson &amp; &pound;5 for self. Drew &pound;5 more in the afternoon. Stephenson wanting &pound;20. Dined at home. In the evening called upon A Dale to propose to join Younger's 10/- in full. Dale <span class=highlight_yellow>sacfe</span> for Younger, who I afterwards found much to my relief of mind had agreed to our proposal. Spent the evening with Mr Allen. With Bell Jervis.</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":505,"lock":null}
20:13:19.057 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/17/2302
20:13:19.057 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":2302,"version":2,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":17,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... in the morning. Packed my cloths up. H Harry &amp; I walked to Tynemouth in the evening &amp; took some gin punch with <span class=highlight_yellow>Daises</span>. Took leave of Mrs Scott &amp; slept on board the Hope. Our <span class=highlight_yellow>from</span><span class=highlight_yellow> all</span> passengers. Anne Stoke also on board.</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2242,"lock":null}
20:13:19.057 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
