20:13:19.057 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":2302,"version":2,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":17,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... in the morning. Packed my cloths up. H Harry &amp; I walked to Tynemouth in the evening &amp; took some gin punch with <span class=highlight_yellow>Daises</span>. Took leave of Mrs Scott &amp; slept on board the Hope. Our <span class=highlight_yellow>from</span><span class=highlight_yellow> all</span> passengers. Anne Stoke also on board.</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2242,"lock":null}
20:13:19.057 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/17/524
20:13:19.057 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":524,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind SE. The Hope was loaded on Friday but we could not go to sea in consequence of Young business. Determined not to sail until the morning tide. Walked to Tynemouth with H Harry. Took a warm bath. Dined at home. H Harry &amp; Mr Dadler took wine with me. Wrote to William of my intention to sail ...</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":506,"lock":null}
20:13:19.057 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
