20:13:19.058 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":524,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind SE. The Hope was loaded on Friday but we could not go to sea in consequence of Young business. Determined not to sail until the morning tide. Walked to Tynemouth with H Harry. Took a warm bath. Dined at home. H Harry &amp; Mr Dadler took wine with me. Wrote to William of my intention to sail ...</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":506,"lock":null}
20:13:19.058 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/18/525
20:13:19.058 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":525,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At 3 o'clock am got under way &amp; sailed from Shields with a westerly breeze &amp; fine weather. At 10 o'clock am becalmed off Sunderland, the wind having got round to SE. Between 1 &amp; 2 o'clock the breeze freshened a little but we made little way, being ebb tide. At 10 o'clock <span class=highlight_yellow>we</span> went to bed, the ship being abreast of the Tees</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":507,"lock":null}
20:13:19.058 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.058 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/18/525
20:13:19.058 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":525,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At 3 o'clock am got under way &amp; sailed from Shields with a westerly breeze &amp; fine weather. At 10 o'clock am becalmed off Sunderland, the wind having got round to SE. Between 1 &amp; 2 o'clock the breeze freshened a little but we made little way, being ebb tide. At 10 o'clock <span class=highlight_yellow>we</span> went to bed, the ship being abreast of the Tees</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":507,"lock":null}
20:13:19.058 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/19/526
20:13:19.058 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":526,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>has been blowing pretty fresh all night from the SE &amp; SSE. Got up at 8 o'clock am. The ship abreast of <span class=highlight_yellow>Hunt</span><span class=highlight_yellow>c</span><span class=highlight_yellow>li</span><span class=highlight_yellow>f</span><span class=highlight_yellow>f</span> Foot. The wind the same but moderate &amp; fine weather. Anne very unwell, but more frightened not having been at sea before. Towards evening wind very calm again. Turned in at 10 o'clock.  The ship in <span class=highlight_yellow>a very</span> little wind.</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":508,"lock":null}
