20:13:19.095 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/7/11/606
20:13:19.095 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":606,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<figure>\r\n  <img src=\"images/img2903-image-st-isaac-church.png\" width=\"600px\" />\r\n  <figcaption>St Isaac church</figcaption>\r\n</figure>","pageId":null,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":null,"lock":null}
20:13:19.095 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/7/11/607
20:13:19.095 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":607,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":11,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, but windy &amp; dusty. This being the <font color=#BFBFBF>[day] </font>of St Peter &amp; St Paul, is a general holiday here &amp; services in all the churches. Mr Lindsey his friend Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Miggete</span>, Bob &amp; I walked out at 12 o'clock for a stroll. Looked into the Catholic Church where they were just concluding the service, their singing seemed to be good. Returned to my lodgings about 3 o'clock, leaving Bob to prolong his walk &amp; had a snooze being tired. Dined at the German Club at &frac12; past 5 o'clock. In the evening Bob &amp; I ...</p>","pageId":755,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":574,"lock":null}
20:13:19.095 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.096 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/7/11/607
20:13:19.096 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":607,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":11,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, but windy &amp; dusty. This being the <font color=#BFBFBF>[day] </font>of St Peter &amp; St Paul, is a general holiday here &amp; services in all the churches. Mr Lindsey his friend Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Miggete</span>, Bob &amp; I walked out at 12 o'clock for a stroll. Looked into the Catholic Church where they were just concluding the service, their singing seemed to be good. Returned to my lodgings about 3 o'clock, leaving Bob to prolong his walk &amp; had a snooze being tired. Dined at the German Club at &frac12; past 5 o'clock. In the evening Bob &amp; I ...</p>","pageId":755,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":574,"lock":null}
20:13:19.096 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/7/12/608
20:13:19.096 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":608,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>After breakfast walked to the Roman Catholic Chapel to hear the singing which was very fair. A great many people there. Bob &amp; I perfectly disgusted at the superstition of both the Catholic Religion, their bowings, protestation &amp; kissing the feet * <span class=highlight_yellow>gassment</span> of the different saints. In the ceremonies &amp; forms they do not appear to differ much.</p>\r\n<p>Dined today with Mr Wishaw at his house on the <span class=highlight_yellow>Wybury</span> Island. We were nearly an hour after our time, Mr Wishaw very stupidly not having given us proper directions to enable us to find his house out. After dinner accompanied the ladies in a boat to the opposite side of the river. Unfortunately we were late &amp; could not use the hothouse. They seem to be expensive. Here was a military band &amp; a good deal of company.</p>","pageId":755,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":575,"lock":null}
20:13:19.096 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.096 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/7/12/608
20:13:19.096 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":608,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>After breakfast walked to the Roman Catholic Chapel to hear the singing which was very fair. A great many people there. Bob &amp; I perfectly disgusted at the superstition of both the Catholic Religion, their bowings, protestation &amp; kissing the feet * <span class=highlight_yellow>gassment</span> of the different saints. In the ceremonies &amp; forms they do not appear to differ much.</p>\r\n<p>Dined today with Mr Wishaw at his house on the <span class=highlight_yellow>Wybury</span> Island. We were nearly an hour after our time, Mr Wishaw very stupidly not having given us proper directions to enable us to find his house out. After dinner accompanied the ladies in a boat to the opposite side of the river. Unfortunately we were late &amp; could not use the hothouse. They seem to be expensive. Here was a military band &amp; a good deal of company.</p>","pageId":755,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":575,"lock":null}
20:13:19.096 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/7/13/609
20:13:19.096 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":609,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>After breakfast Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Bartleuace</span> of the David just arrived from Grangemouth &amp; I took a donkey &amp; drove over to Mr Dryers whose partner Mr Gray had chartered the David &amp; introduced him. Then drove to the <span class=highlight_yellow>news key</span> ...</p>","pageId":755,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":576,"lock":null}
