20:13:19.108 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":2318,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":23,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... humour to go on shore. Obliged to go to bed. The pain &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>opium</span> making me exceptionally drowsy. Bought some flannel &amp; hartshorn in the evening which I put upon my face when I went to bed</p>","pageId":760,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2258,"lock":null}
20:13:19.108 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/7/23/625
20:13:19.108 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":625,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still wind bound, blowing fresh from the SW. Suffered a great deal of pain during the night from my tooth &amp; my face swollen to a giant size. Could with difficulty eat. In no ...</p>","pageId":760,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":589,"lock":null}
20:13:19.108 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.108 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/7/23/625
20:13:19.108 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":625,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still wind bound, blowing fresh from the SW. Suffered a great deal of pain during the night from my tooth &amp; my face swollen to a giant size. Could with difficulty eat. In no ...</p>","pageId":760,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":589,"lock":null}
20:13:19.108 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/7/24/626
20:13:19.108 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":626,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather but still a fresh westerly breeze, which detains us. Relieved from pain by the flannel &amp; hartshorn, but my face still much swollen. Remained on board &amp; upon the mole head all the morning.</p>\r\n<p>Mr Bookers clerk called to demand 15 rubbles brokerage for the copper. Went on shore at 5 o'clock to see him upon the subject. It appears I treated with a broker &amp; nob the merchant or I supposed, the brokerage therefore due. Desired Mr Booker to request Mr Hubbardth to pay it &amp; I should settle it in London, having no Russian money left. Amused ourselves on the mole head all evening</p>","pageId":760,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":590,"lock":null}
20:13:19.108 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.109 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/7/24/626
20:13:19.109 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":626,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather but still a fresh westerly breeze, which detains us. Relieved from pain by the flannel &amp; hartshorn, but my face still much swollen. Remained on board &amp; upon the mole head all the morning.</p>\r\n<p>Mr Bookers clerk called to demand 15 rubbles brokerage for the copper. Went on shore at 5 o'clock to see him upon the subject. It appears I treated with a broker &amp; nob the merchant or I supposed, the brokerage therefore due. Desired Mr Booker to request Mr Hubbardth to pay it &amp; I should settle it in London, having no Russian money left. Amused ourselves on the mole head all evening</p>","pageId":760,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":590,"lock":null}
20:13:19.109 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/7/25/627
20:13:19.109 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":627,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Blowing very hard during the whole of the day from the westward. Several ships arrived having had fine passages of 13 days from London. Amongst them the Sceptre, <span class=highlight_yellow>Coui</span> Greenhod. Several laden ships having hauled out made the <span class=highlight_yellow>roadshad</span> very <span class=highlight_yellow>throng</span>. On the mole head all the morning. Mr Lendaley came down in the steam boat &amp; brought <span class=highlight_yellow>me </span><span class=highlight_yellow>ec</span> ...</p>","pageId":760,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":591,"lock":null}
20:13:19.109 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.109 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/7/25/627
20:13:19.109 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":627,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Blowing very hard during the whole of the day from the westward. Several ships arrived having had fine passages of 13 days from London. Amongst them the Sceptre, <span class=highlight_yellow>Coui</span> Greenhod. Several laden ships having hauled out made the <span class=highlight_yellow>roadshad</span> very <span class=highlight_yellow>throng</span>. On the mole head all the morning. Mr Lendaley came down in the steam boat &amp; brought <span class=highlight_yellow>me </span><span class=highlight_yellow>ec</span> ...</p>","pageId":760,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":591,"lock":null}
20:13:19.109 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/7/25/628
20:13:19.109 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":628,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":25,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... packet from Mr Dye, a present for Emma Galbraith. Mr L took a glass of grog with us &amp; we afterwards accompanied him on board. The Chase, captain Thompson arrived today in 13 days from Hull, and had supper.</p>","pageId":761,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":592,"lock":null}
20:13:19.109 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.109 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/7/25/628
20:13:19.109 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":628,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":25,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... packet from Mr Dye, a present for Emma Galbraith. Mr L took a glass of grog with us &amp; we afterwards accompanied him on board. The Chase, captain Thompson arrived today in 13 days from Hull, and had supper.</p>","pageId":761,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":592,"lock":null}
20:13:19.109 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/7/26/629
20:13:19.109 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":629,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning, but exceptionally hot. The wind having got round to the north &amp; an appearance of changing. We after breakfast hauled out of the mole but being quite calm were obliged to get a boat ahead &amp; toe the ship down to the guard ship. Cleared at the guard ship about 12 o'clock &amp; proceeded with a leading wind, but little of it.</p>","pageId":761,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":593,"lock":null}
20:13:19.110 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.110 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/7/26/629
20:13:19.110 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":629,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning, but exceptionally hot. The wind having got round to the north &amp; an appearance of changing. We after breakfast hauled out of the mole but being quite calm were obliged to get a boat ahead &amp; toe the ship down to the guard ship. Cleared at the guard ship about 12 o'clock &amp; proceeded with a leading wind, but little of it.</p>","pageId":761,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":593,"lock":null}
20:13:19.110 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/7/27/630
20:13:19.110 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":630,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, rather dull. The ship working windward, the wind having unfortunately changed during the night direct against us being west. Continued <span class=highlight_yellow>binting</span> about all day without making any way. For little to the eastward of Seascar Island. In the evening we again got a leading wind &amp; before bed time, getting more to the northward, we were enabled to set lower fore &amp; topmast &amp; studding sails with a fine fresh breeze</p>","pageId":761,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":594,"lock":null}
20:13:19.110 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.110 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/7/27/630
20:13:19.110 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":630,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, rather dull. The ship working windward, the wind having unfortunately changed during the night direct against us being west. Continued <span class=highlight_yellow>binting</span> about all day without making any way. For little to the eastward of Seascar Island. In the evening we again got a leading wind &amp; before bed time, getting more to the northward, we were enabled to set lower fore &amp; topmast &amp; studding sails with a fine fresh breeze</p>","pageId":761,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":594,"lock":null}
20:13:19.110 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/7/28/631
20:13:19.110 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":631,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very thick wet disagreeable morning, been raining nearly all night, but thank God, with a fine fresh breeze from the eastward. The ship making good way passed the north end of Hogsland this morning at 6 o'clock. Continued raining all day from 5 &frac12; to 6 &frac12; knots. When we went to bed at a little before 10 o'clock we were abreast of Revel, still blowing fresh from the East. </p>","pageId":761,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":595,"lock":null}
20:13:19.110 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.111 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/7/28/631
20:13:19.111 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":631,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very thick wet disagreeable morning, been raining nearly all night, but thank God, with a fine fresh breeze from the eastward. The ship making good way passed the north end of Hogsland this morning at 6 o'clock. Continued raining all day from 5 &frac12; to 6 &frac12; knots. When we went to bed at a little before 10 o'clock we were abreast of Revel, still blowing fresh from the East. </p>","pageId":761,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":595,"lock":null}
