20:13:19.140 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":2324,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":28,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... were compelled to give the ship the whole chain. Wind WNW &amp; cloudy. Dismal weather with rain. A light ship close by us drove &amp; another broke his chain &amp; sun down the river. Continued blowing hard all day with heavy showers of rain &amp; squalls &amp; towards evening the wind got to about N by W but the tide not answering. <span class=highlight_yellow>Till</span> near dark, we lay still, indeed it blew too hard to think of getting under way &amp; one or two vessels that weighed were soon obliged to bring up again</p>","pageId":770,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2264,"lock":null}
