20:13:19.140 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":670,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out before 8 o'clock. The gale increased &amp; blowing so hard that we cannot get underway. In the middle of the night it was tremendous &amp; we ...</p>","pageId":770,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":632,"lock":null}
20:13:19.140 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/29/671
20:13:19.140 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":671,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at &frac12; past 6 o'clock. When I got upon the deck found the ship under way. Weather much moderated with a fine stiff breeze from the northward which carried us up to Gravesend in about a couple of hours, where we took on board a <span class=highlight_yellow>ca</span><span class=highlight_yellow>r</span><span class=highlight_yellow>bonhouse</span> officer &amp; proceeded. At about 12 o'clock we came to an anchor at Blackwall after a fine run, having made only one tack the whole of the day. Our watersman, whose boat Bob &amp; I got into soon after we anchored with all our luggage on board, who allowed us to take it out of the ships, which few would have done &amp; rowed up to the Tower Stairs, took a coach &amp; drove up to <font color=#BFBFBF>the </font>New Inn calling in Philpot Lane on our way, where I found there letters from William</p>\r\n<p>Glad once more to get under a comfortable roof. When I had written a letter to William &amp; we had ...</p>","pageId":770,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":633,"lock":null}
20:13:19.140 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.141 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/29/671
20:13:19.141 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":671,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at &frac12; past 6 o'clock. When I got upon the deck found the ship under way. Weather much moderated with a fine stiff breeze from the northward which carried us up to Gravesend in about a couple of hours, where we took on board a <span class=highlight_yellow>ca</span><span class=highlight_yellow>r</span><span class=highlight_yellow>bonhouse</span> officer &amp; proceeded. At about 12 o'clock we came to an anchor at Blackwall after a fine run, having made only one tack the whole of the day. Our watersman, whose boat Bob &amp; I got into soon after we anchored with all our luggage on board, who allowed us to take it out of the ships, which few would have done &amp; rowed up to the Tower Stairs, took a coach &amp; drove up to <font color=#BFBFBF>the </font>New Inn calling in Philpot Lane on our way, where I found there letters from William</p>\r\n<p>Glad once more to get under a comfortable roof. When I had written a letter to William &amp; we had ...</p>","pageId":770,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":633,"lock":null}
20:13:19.141 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/29/672
20:13:19.141 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":672,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":29,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... made ourselves decent &amp; comfortable Bob &amp; I walked up to George in the Red Lion Square where we made &amp; enjoyed a hearty dinner of pigeon &amp; veal pies &amp; cold <span class=highlight_yellow>mullion</span>, discharged a good glass of punch &amp; returned to Chambers. With the <span class=highlight_yellow>appearance</span> of Mrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Furmedye</span>, Bob's <span class=highlight_yellow>laudress</span>, I made myself a good perch for the night with Bob's <span class=highlight_yellow>mallrafs</span> in the corner of his room, turned in &amp; enjoyed an excellent nights rest, although the bed was rather a hard one.</p>\r\n<p>Thus ends our Petersburg voyage which upon the whole we have enjoyed, but we could have dispensed with the tumultuous bad weather we experienced. Thank God we have got back safe &amp; without any accident worth mentioning to the ship.</p>","pageId":771,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":634,"lock":null}
20:13:19.141 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.141 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/29/672
20:13:19.141 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":672,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":29,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... made ourselves decent &amp; comfortable Bob &amp; I walked up to George in the Red Lion Square where we made &amp; enjoyed a hearty dinner of pigeon &amp; veal pies &amp; cold <span class=highlight_yellow>mullion</span>, discharged a good glass of punch &amp; returned to Chambers. With the <span class=highlight_yellow>appearance</span> of Mrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Furmedye</span>, Bob's <span class=highlight_yellow>laudress</span>, I made myself a good perch for the night with Bob's <span class=highlight_yellow>mallrafs</span> in the corner of his room, turned in &amp; enjoyed an excellent nights rest, although the bed was rather a hard one.</p>\r\n<p>Thus ends our Petersburg voyage which upon the whole we have enjoyed, but we could have dispensed with the tumultuous bad weather we experienced. Thank God we have got back safe &amp; without any accident worth mentioning to the ship.</p>","pageId":771,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":634,"lock":null}
20:13:19.141 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/3/640
20:13:19.141 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":640,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning &amp; clear weather, still blowing fresh from the NW which has continued the whole day, with a heavy sea which has prevented us making more than 3 knots. Amused myself the whole of the day reading Peregrine Pickle. At 4 o'clock pm wind got to W by N. At 5 o'clock pm tacked ship &amp; stood across towards Gothland again. By observation at 12 o'clock lat:55.52 Reefed topsail at 2 o'clock pm</p>","pageId":762,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":602,"lock":null}
20:13:19.141 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.142 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/3/640
20:13:19.142 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":640,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning &amp; clear weather, still blowing fresh from the NW which has continued the whole day, with a heavy sea which has prevented us making more than 3 knots. Amused myself the whole of the day reading Peregrine Pickle. At 4 o'clock pm wind got to W by N. At 5 o'clock pm tacked ship &amp; stood across towards Gothland again. By observation at 12 o'clock lat:55.52 Reefed topsail at 2 o'clock pm</p>","pageId":762,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":602,"lock":null}
20:13:19.142 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/30/673
20:13:19.142 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":673,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up much refreshed. More moderate weather. Wind NE rather cloudy. We fully intended to have gone to church, but Bob &amp; I took up so much linin in the washing &amp; cleaning ourselves that it was past the hour before we were aware of it. Turned out a very fine day. We called upon Mr Ward who had gone to Paris will William. Walked through St James park up to Hyde Park where we strolled till 6 o'clock. Very few people or carriages there. Town exceedingly thin from thence came we went to Mr Piazza Covent garden &amp; enjoyed a comfortable dinner &amp; a good bottle of old port. Returned to Chambers between 10 &amp; 11 o'clock &amp; went to bed.</p>","pageId":771,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":635,"lock":null}
20:13:19.142 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.142 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/30/673
20:13:19.142 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":673,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up much refreshed. More moderate weather. Wind NE rather cloudy. We fully intended to have gone to church, but Bob &amp; I took up so much linin in the washing &amp; cleaning ourselves that it was past the hour before we were aware of it. Turned out a very fine day. We called upon Mr Ward who had gone to Paris will William. Walked through St James park up to Hyde Park where we strolled till 6 o'clock. Very few people or carriages there. Town exceedingly thin from thence came we went to Mr Piazza Covent garden &amp; enjoyed a comfortable dinner &amp; a good bottle of old port. Returned to Chambers between 10 &amp; 11 o'clock &amp; went to bed.</p>","pageId":771,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":635,"lock":null}
20:13:19.142 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/31/674
20:13:19.142 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":674,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy morning, rather cool. Wind NE. Walked into the city. Called at the office, nothing there. Proceeded after being at Chapmans to St Catherine's docks. The ship got safe in yesterday. Stephenson noted a protest this morning, the ship having been so leaky. Found Mrs Stephenson on board, eat some dinner with them. Attended <span class=highlight_yellow>cha</span><span class=highlight_yellow>mb</span><span class=highlight_yellow>er</span><span class=highlight_yellow>s</span>. Walked westward &amp; called upon Jobling.</p>","pageId":771,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":636,"lock":null}
20:13:19.142 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.143 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/31/674
20:13:19.143 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":674,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy morning, rather cool. Wind NE. Walked into the city. Called at the office, nothing there. Proceeded after being at Chapmans to St Catherine's docks. The ship got safe in yesterday. Stephenson noted a protest this morning, the ship having been so leaky. Found Mrs Stephenson on board, eat some dinner with them. Attended <span class=highlight_yellow>cha</span><span class=highlight_yellow>mb</span><span class=highlight_yellow>er</span><span class=highlight_yellow>s</span>. Walked westward &amp; called upon Jobling.</p>","pageId":771,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":636,"lock":null}
20:13:19.143 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/4/641
20:13:19.143 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":641,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A delightful change. Now beautiful weather. Wind NW &amp; W. Light breeze &amp; sea very much fallen, only going about 2 knots. At 12 o'clock by observation at lat:55.47N. Employed myself all the morning in preparing the wood for a dog kennel. At 2 o'clock pm the wind got to the WSW course NW. At 5 pm set studding sails, top masts &amp; main top gallant. Sea quite fallen &amp; a fine fresh breeze at 6 o'clock wind S course W by S going 5 knots at 10 o'clock <span class=highlight_yellow>discharged</span> our grog &amp; turned in for the night, ship going 5 &frac12; knots</p>","pageId":763,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":603,"lock":null}
20:13:19.143 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.143 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/4/641
20:13:19.143 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":641,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A delightful change. Now beautiful weather. Wind NW &amp; W. Light breeze &amp; sea very much fallen, only going about 2 knots. At 12 o'clock by observation at lat:55.47N. Employed myself all the morning in preparing the wood for a dog kennel. At 2 o'clock pm the wind got to the WSW course NW. At 5 pm set studding sails, top masts &amp; main top gallant. Sea quite fallen &amp; a fine fresh breeze at 6 o'clock wind S course W by S going 5 knots at 10 o'clock <span class=highlight_yellow>discharged</span> our grog &amp; turned in for the night, ship going 5 &frac12; knots</p>","pageId":763,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":603,"lock":null}
20:13:19.143 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/5/2319
20:13:19.143 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":2319,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":5,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... not inhabited. They are all within a stone's throw of each other. After passing Ertholmene, we had a most delightful sail under the Island of Bornholm &amp; a good view of it. This is one of the richest and most beautiful islands that can be imagined. It is in fact a perfect garden &amp; to us had all the appearance of a gentleman's park. The soil is good &amp; exceedingly productive yielding as much in one season as would keep the inhabitants several years. A boat came out to us from the shore &amp; we purchased of them four ducks &frac34; score of eggs &amp; 2 pounds of butter for which we gave only 6/6</p>\r\n<p>When we reached the west end of the island then wind took us all at a <span class=highlight_yellow>lk</span>, but soon favoured us again. In the evening it became quite calm. At &frac12; past 8 o'clock the captain, Bob &amp; I as usual had our grog &amp; being in the humour, <span class=highlight_yellow>had</span> some supper &amp; had a regular jollification, blew a cloud &amp; got to roost between 12 &amp; 1 o'clock</p>","pageId":763,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2259,"lock":null}
20:13:19.143 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.144 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/5/2319
20:13:19.144 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":2319,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":5,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... not inhabited. They are all within a stone's throw of each other. After passing Ertholmene, we had a most delightful sail under the Island of Bornholm &amp; a good view of it. This is one of the richest and most beautiful islands that can be imagined. It is in fact a perfect garden &amp; to us had all the appearance of a gentleman's park. The soil is good &amp; exceedingly productive yielding as much in one season as would keep the inhabitants several years. A boat came out to us from the shore &amp; we purchased of them four ducks &frac34; score of eggs &amp; 2 pounds of butter for which we gave only 6/6</p>\r\n<p>When we reached the west end of the island then wind took us all at a <span class=highlight_yellow>lk</span>, but soon favoured us again. In the evening it became quite calm. At &frac12; past 8 o'clock the captain, Bob &amp; I as usual had our grog &amp; being in the humour, <span class=highlight_yellow>had</span> some supper &amp; had a regular jollification, blew a cloud &amp; got to roost between 12 &amp; 1 o'clock</p>","pageId":763,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2259,"lock":null}
20:13:19.144 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/5/642
20:13:19.144 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":642,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful day. The ship making good way about 4 &frac12; knots with a fine breeze at SSE going free. We can perceive the Islands of <span class=highlight_yellow>E</span><span class=highlight_yellow>r</span><span class=highlight_yellow>tholm</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ene</span> &amp; Bornholm with the glass. The ship much to my annoyance very leaky. Obliged to pump every hour. At 1 o'clock pm passed close to <span class=highlight_yellow>Erth</span><span class=highlight_yellow>o</span><span class=highlight_yellow>lm</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ene</span>. With a fine breeze at S by E. Studding sails set. These are small rocky islands belonging to Denmark about 11 miles from Bornholm. Upon the largest is a lighthouse, a few small batteries &amp; houses. On the south side a very good harbour I understand. The other two islands are mostly rocks &amp; ...</p>","pageId":763,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":604,"lock":null}
20:13:19.144 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.144 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/5/642
20:13:19.144 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":642,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful day. The ship making good way about 4 &frac12; knots with a fine breeze at SSE going free. We can perceive the Islands of <span class=highlight_yellow>E</span><span class=highlight_yellow>r</span><span class=highlight_yellow>tholm</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ene</span> &amp; Bornholm with the glass. The ship much to my annoyance very leaky. Obliged to pump every hour. At 1 o'clock pm passed close to <span class=highlight_yellow>Erth</span><span class=highlight_yellow>o</span><span class=highlight_yellow>lm</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ene</span>. With a fine breeze at S by E. Studding sails set. These are small rocky islands belonging to Denmark about 11 miles from Bornholm. Upon the largest is a lighthouse, a few small batteries &amp; houses. On the south side a very good harbour I understand. The other two islands are mostly rocks &amp; ...</p>","pageId":763,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":604,"lock":null}
20:13:19.144 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/6/643
20:13:19.144 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":643,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out this morning at the usual hour. Coppers hot &amp; rather feverish, took a <span class=highlight_yellow>seidletz</span>, very pleasant answering a double purpose. A beautiful morning. Summer returned. A light breeze at SE. At noon by observation in lat 55.10N. Kept our reach the whole of the day. Wind NW. At 8 o'clock tacked ship. <span class=highlight_yellow>Reigen</span> Island bearing S by W distant 10 or 12 miles.</p>","pageId":763,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":605,"lock":null}
20:13:19.144 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.145 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/6/643
20:13:19.145 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":643,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out this morning at the usual hour. Coppers hot &amp; rather feverish, took a <span class=highlight_yellow>seidletz</span>, very pleasant answering a double purpose. A beautiful morning. Summer returned. A light breeze at SE. At noon by observation in lat 55.10N. Kept our reach the whole of the day. Wind NW. At 8 o'clock tacked ship. <span class=highlight_yellow>Reigen</span> Island bearing S by W distant 10 or 12 miles.</p>","pageId":763,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":605,"lock":null}
20:13:19.145 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/7/644
20:13:19.145 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":644,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy morning &amp; fresh breeze at NNW &amp; N. Employed myself all the morning in drawing. At noon clear weather but still a fresh breeze. <span class=highlight_yellow>Falsterbo</span> light bearing WNW distant 8 miles. A large fleet of ships passed us upward bound. At 5 o'clock tacked ship a little to the southward of <span class=highlight_yellow>Moea</span> Island after which it became quite calm until 9 o'clock when we got a light air from the NNW. Afterwards most favourable. At 10 o'clock after our grog we turned in, the ship proceeding quickly towards Drags in the island <span class=highlight_yellow>Verf</span><span class=highlight_yellow> </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Amag</span></p>","pageId":764,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":606,"lock":null}
20:13:19.145 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
