20:13:19.145 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":644,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy morning &amp; fresh breeze at NNW &amp; N. Employed myself all the morning in drawing. At noon clear weather but still a fresh breeze. <span class=highlight_yellow>Falsterbo</span> light bearing WNW distant 8 miles. A large fleet of ships passed us upward bound. At 5 o'clock tacked ship a little to the southward of <span class=highlight_yellow>Moea</span> Island after which it became quite calm until 9 o'clock when we got a light air from the NNW. Afterwards most favourable. At 10 o'clock after our grog we turned in, the ship proceeding quickly towards Drags in the island <span class=highlight_yellow>Verf</span><span class=highlight_yellow> </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Amag</span></p>","pageId":764,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":606,"lock":null}
20:13:19.145 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/8/2320
20:13:19.145 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":2320,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":8,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>.. glass of wine with him &amp; I don't know how to account for it, excepting it was drinking upon an empty stomach but I really got muzzy of which I was sensible enough to feel heartily ashamed when I had to appear in the presence of Mr ships Chapmans. Got on board a little after 12 o'clock after one or two adventured before we left the town H French's ship, the 3 Brothers &amp; several other vessels passed us upward bound between Copenhagen &amp; Elsinore</p>","pageId":764,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2260,"lock":null}
