20:13:19.146 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":645,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Hearing the master speaking a ship, I turned out before 7 o'clock. It was Hutchenson's Ajax bound to <span class=highlight_yellow>Wybury</span>, several other ships passing us. Hazy weather &amp; light rain, wind WNW. At &frac12; past 7 o'clock got a piolet onboard &amp; at 8 o'clock passed Drago. At 10 o'clock got there through the Grounds when the piolet left us off Copenhagen proceeding with a fine breeze for <span class=highlight_yellow>Elsinore</span>. The weather cleared up &amp; turned out a fine warm day, giving us a beautiful view of the coast. Brought up at <span class=highlight_yellow>Elsinore</span> at 3 o'clock &amp; went on shore. Received a letter from William informing me of Mrs Scott's illness, not expected to live long &amp; his intention of going to Shields on the 11 th August in the steam boat with C Richmond. Took some wine with <span class=highlight_yellow>warm </span><span class=highlight_yellow>chapurars</span> &amp; afterwards walked out to his fathers house who kindly sent to ask us when he heard of our arrival to go &amp; drink a ...</p>","pageId":764,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":607,"lock":null}
20:13:19.146 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/9/646
20:13:19.146 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":646,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at the usual hour &amp; found the ship off the Koll having got underway at 9 am with a fresh breeze at W by S, proceeding at the rate of 6 or 6 &frac12; knots during the whole of the day. Passed Anholt at about 6 o'clock in the evening</p>","pageId":764,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":608,"lock":null}
20:13:19.146 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.147 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/9/646
20:13:19.147 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":646,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at the usual hour &amp; found the ship off the Koll having got underway at 9 am with a fresh breeze at W by S, proceeding at the rate of 6 or 6 &frac12; knots during the whole of the day. Passed Anholt at about 6 o'clock in the evening</p>","pageId":764,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":608,"lock":null}
20:13:19.147 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/1/675
20:13:19.147 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":675,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull day &amp; showery. Walked into the city &amp; down to the docks. Found them employed in moving the ship to a birth &amp; then began to deliver her cargo before I left. Went to <span class=highlight_yellow>cha</span><span class=highlight_yellow>mbers</span> &amp; afterwards walked westward. Dined with Jobling in the Adelphi, only ourselves. Spent a pleasant day. Got rather too much wine. Slept all night in Villiers Street</p>","pageId":771,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":637,"lock":null}
20:13:19.147 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.147 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/1/675
20:13:19.147 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":675,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull day &amp; showery. Walked into the city &amp; down to the docks. Found them employed in moving the ship to a birth &amp; then began to deliver her cargo before I left. Went to <span class=highlight_yellow>cha</span><span class=highlight_yellow>mbers</span> &amp; afterwards walked westward. Dined with Jobling in the Adelphi, only ourselves. Spent a pleasant day. Got rather too much wine. Slept all night in Villiers Street</p>","pageId":771,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":637,"lock":null}
20:13:19.147 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/10/689
20:13:19.147 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":689,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Showery weather. Wind S W. Took a cab into the city and afterwards walked to the docks. Found the people employed hauling the ship out, intending to take her down to Dukes shore. Received from Stephenson &pound;89.7.6 for the lathwood. <span class=underline_double>With Maryann</span>.  Attended chambers. H Harry never made his appearance. Did nothing. Went by a Paddington stage to Nottingham Place where Bob Marsh &amp; I dined with William &amp; enjoyed ourselves much.</p>","pageId":773,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":647,"lock":null}
20:13:19.147 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.148 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/10/689
20:13:19.148 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":689,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Showery weather. Wind S W. Took a cab into the city and afterwards walked to the docks. Found the people employed hauling the ship out, intending to take her down to Dukes shore. Received from Stephenson &pound;89.7.6 for the lathwood. <span class=underline_double>With Maryann</span>.  Attended chambers. H Harry never made his appearance. Did nothing. Went by a Paddington stage to Nottingham Place where Bob Marsh &amp; I dined with William &amp; enjoyed ourselves much.</p>","pageId":773,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":647,"lock":null}
20:13:19.148 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/11/2325
20:13:19.148 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":2325,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":11,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... since I had the pleasure of seeing him. We afterwards took a Greenwich boat &amp; went down to the Hope upon Dowslands way where we dined off cold mutton. At low water looked at her bottom &amp; gave orders for her to go into the dock to be caulked. Turned out an exceptionally wet evening. Had our tea on board &amp; afterwards took a <span class=highlight_yellow>Mackware</span> stage to Leadenhall Street &amp; then walked to New Inn. Bob Marsh at the theatre.</p>","pageId":773,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2265,"lock":null}
20:13:19.148 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.148 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/11/2325
20:13:19.148 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":2325,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":11,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... since I had the pleasure of seeing him. We afterwards took a Greenwich boat &amp; went down to the Hope upon Dowslands way where we dined off cold mutton. At low water looked at her bottom &amp; gave orders for her to go into the dock to be caulked. Turned out an exceptionally wet evening. Had our tea on board &amp; afterwards took a <span class=highlight_yellow>Mackware</span> stage to Leadenhall Street &amp; then walked to New Inn. Bob Marsh at the theatre.</p>","pageId":773,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2265,"lock":null}
20:13:19.148 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/11/690
20:13:19.148 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":690,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind SW. Walked into the city early. Called at Chapmans at 10 o'clock &amp; fixed the Hope for <span class=highlight_yellow>memel</span> at 21/- <span class=highlight_yellow>&amp;</span> load for a full cargo of timber. Found Mr Mewburn at the office, tis a long time ...</p>","pageId":773,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":648,"lock":null}
20:13:19.149 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.149 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/11/690
20:13:19.149 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":690,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind SW. Walked into the city early. Called at Chapmans at 10 o'clock &amp; fixed the Hope for <span class=highlight_yellow>memel</span> at 21/- <span class=highlight_yellow>&amp;</span> load for a full cargo of timber. Found Mr Mewburn at the office, tis a long time ...</p>","pageId":773,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":648,"lock":null}
20:13:19.149 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/12/691
20:13:19.149 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":691,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW William, J Galbraith called at the New Inn &amp; I walked into the city with them.</p>\r\n<p>In the afternoon we got upon a Paddington stage &amp; went up to Nottingham Place &amp; thence to the Zoological gardens, which are much improved. Dined at 6 o'clock with Mr R Chapman in <span class=highlight_yellow>John Street</span>, Bedford Row. Mr Hancock, Mr Graham &amp; another gentleman there. Spent a very pleasant day.</p>\r\n<p>On my return to chambers found Bob marsh reading. Asked him to allow me to remain in his chambers for the few days I stopped in town, but much to my surprise he refused, which hurt me not a little. After living nearly three months with me on board the Hope. It was doing me but a trifling favour &amp; without either inconveniencing or expense to himself, I could not have expected &amp; I know not how he could possibly make his mind up to treat me with so much unkindness. However I shall not forget it in a hurry. I pronounce him to be a mean and shabby fellow</p>","pageId":773,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":649,"lock":null}
20:13:19.149 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.150 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/12/691
20:13:19.150 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":691,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW William, J Galbraith called at the New Inn &amp; I walked into the city with them.</p>\r\n<p>In the afternoon we got upon a Paddington stage &amp; went up to Nottingham Place &amp; thence to the Zoological gardens, which are much improved. Dined at 6 o'clock with Mr R Chapman in <span class=highlight_yellow>John Street</span>, Bedford Row. Mr Hancock, Mr Graham &amp; another gentleman there. Spent a very pleasant day.</p>\r\n<p>On my return to chambers found Bob marsh reading. Asked him to allow me to remain in his chambers for the few days I stopped in town, but much to my surprise he refused, which hurt me not a little. After living nearly three months with me on board the Hope. It was doing me but a trifling favour &amp; without either inconveniencing or expense to himself, I could not have expected &amp; I know not how he could possibly make his mind up to treat me with so much unkindness. However I shall not forget it in a hurry. I pronounce him to be a mean and shabby fellow</p>","pageId":773,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":649,"lock":null}
20:13:19.150 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/13/692
20:13:19.150 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":692,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning wind. Feeling exceptionally annoyed &amp; hurt by Bob Marsh's conduct, I got up early &amp; left his chambers. Indeed had it not been so late I should have done so last night. Breakfasted with William in Nottingham Place. We afterwards went to <span class=highlight_yellow>vere</span> St Chapel. In the afternoon we walked to Sloan Street &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>we</span> called at Mrs Locks to see Mary &amp; Emma. On our way home had a <span class=highlight_yellow>stroll</span> in Hyde Park. Very few people there. Vincent <span class=highlight_yellow>Fitz</span><span class=highlight_yellow>manian</span> &amp; Bob Marsh dined with us. We intended to have given the latter a hint that his company could be dispensed with, but did not, as it might have caused much unpleasantness. I determined however to tell him what I thought of his conduct, but had not an opportunity. He shall yet hear more about it. A very wet night</p>","pageId":774,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":650,"lock":null}
20:13:19.150 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.150 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/13/692
20:13:19.150 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":692,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning wind. Feeling exceptionally annoyed &amp; hurt by Bob Marsh's conduct, I got up early &amp; left his chambers. Indeed had it not been so late I should have done so last night. Breakfasted with William in Nottingham Place. We afterwards went to <span class=highlight_yellow>vere</span> St Chapel. In the afternoon we walked to Sloan Street &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>we</span> called at Mrs Locks to see Mary &amp; Emma. On our way home had a <span class=highlight_yellow>stroll</span> in Hyde Park. Very few people there. Vincent <span class=highlight_yellow>Fitz</span><span class=highlight_yellow>manian</span> &amp; Bob Marsh dined with us. We intended to have given the latter a hint that his company could be dispensed with, but did not, as it might have caused much unpleasantness. I determined however to tell him what I thought of his conduct, but had not an opportunity. He shall yet hear more about it. A very wet night</p>","pageId":774,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":650,"lock":null}
20:13:19.150 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/14/2326
20:13:19.150 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":2326,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":14,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>Rather showery. Called at the New Inn. Put my <font color=#222222>portmanteau</font>  &amp; bag into a cab &amp; drove up to Nottingham Place. Spent the evening quietly at home.</p>","pageId":774,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2266,"lock":null}
20:13:19.150 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.151 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/14/2326
20:13:19.151 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":2326,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":14,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>Rather showery. Called at the New Inn. Put my <font color=#222222>portmanteau</font>  &amp; bag into a cab &amp; drove up to Nottingham Place. Spent the evening quietly at home.</p>","pageId":774,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2266,"lock":null}
20:13:19.151 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/14/693
20:13:19.151 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":693,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy morning. Wind WSW. Went into the city upon a Paddington stage coach rather early, to pack a hamper of <span class=highlight_yellow>special madeira</span> up for Mr Chapman of Elseineur. J Galbraith &amp; I thence walked down to Dowson's dock to the Hope, where we dined. The people busy caulking &amp; repairing some soft places where she has been leaking. Left the ship between 4 &amp; 5 o'clock. Brought new <span class=highlight_yellow>umbrella</span></p>","pageId":774,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":651,"lock":null}
20:13:19.151 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.151 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/14/693
20:13:19.151 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":693,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy morning. Wind WSW. Went into the city upon a Paddington stage coach rather early, to pack a hamper of <span class=highlight_yellow>special madeira</span> up for Mr Chapman of Elseineur. J Galbraith &amp; I thence walked down to Dowson's dock to the Hope, where we dined. The people busy caulking &amp; repairing some soft places where she has been leaking. Left the ship between 4 &amp; 5 o'clock. Brought new <span class=highlight_yellow>umbrella</span></p>","pageId":774,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":651,"lock":null}
20:13:19.151 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/15/694
20:13:19.151 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":694,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull showery day. Wind W by N. Went by a Paddington dray into the city. Stephenson called at the office having got his dispatches. Surprised to find that Chapmans had given him a copy of a charter which did not agree with that I signed, having <span class=highlight_yellow>Stavers</span> introduced. Called at <span class=highlight_yellow>Color's</span> office &amp; saw the original charter &amp; found it <span class=highlight_yellow>outlined</span>. Exceedingly surprised &amp; angry that such a thing should be done without my knowledge or sanction &amp; the more surprised that Chapmans should permit it. A most unjustifiable act, nay worse. Walked down to the ship, the people getting on very well or it seem to be giving her a good caulking. Dined on board. J Galbraith &amp; I walked home by Fleet Street, Regent Street etc...</p>","pageId":774,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":652,"lock":null}
20:13:19.151 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.152 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/15/694
20:13:19.152 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":694,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull showery day. Wind W by N. Went by a Paddington dray into the city. Stephenson called at the office having got his dispatches. Surprised to find that Chapmans had given him a copy of a charter which did not agree with that I signed, having <span class=highlight_yellow>Stavers</span> introduced. Called at <span class=highlight_yellow>Color's</span> office &amp; saw the original charter &amp; found it <span class=highlight_yellow>outlined</span>. Exceedingly surprised &amp; angry that such a thing should be done without my knowledge or sanction &amp; the more surprised that Chapmans should permit it. A most unjustifiable act, nay worse. Walked down to the ship, the people getting on very well or it seem to be giving her a good caulking. Dined on board. J Galbraith &amp; I walked home by Fleet Street, Regent Street etc...</p>","pageId":774,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":652,"lock":null}
20:13:19.152 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/16/695
20:13:19.152 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":695,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet day &amp; been raining heavy all night. Wind NE. Took a Paddington dray to the city. Called at Chapmans &amp; agreed to take 500 staves and not more unless the master wished. The agent giving me a letter pledging himself to that effect. On the Coal Exchange nothing particular there. Did not find a ship to take me to Shields. Took a coach &amp; carried all J G's cloths down to the ship. Found her just hauled out of dock. Had some <span class=highlight_yellow>beef</span>.</p>","pageId":774,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":653,"lock":null}
20:13:19.152 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.152 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/16/695
20:13:19.152 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":695,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet day &amp; been raining heavy all night. Wind NE. Took a Paddington dray to the city. Called at Chapmans &amp; agreed to take 500 staves and not more unless the master wished. The agent giving me a letter pledging himself to that effect. On the Coal Exchange nothing particular there. Did not find a ship to take me to Shields. Took a coach &amp; carried all J G's cloths down to the ship. Found her just hauled out of dock. Had some <span class=highlight_yellow>beef</span>.</p>","pageId":774,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":653,"lock":null}
20:13:19.152 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/16/696
20:13:19.152 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":696,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":16,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>Packed my clothes up ready to tranship. William, J.G. &amp; I walked up home calling at Mrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Carfs</span> &amp; at the Cock in the Fleet Street where we had some oysters &amp; brandy &amp; water. Stephenson gave me his accounts.</p>","pageId":775,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":654,"lock":null}
20:13:19.152 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.153 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/16/696
20:13:19.153 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":696,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":16,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>Packed my clothes up ready to tranship. William, J.G. &amp; I walked up home calling at Mrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Carfs</span> &amp; at the Cock in the Fleet Street where we had some oysters &amp; brandy &amp; water. Stephenson gave me his accounts.</p>","pageId":775,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":654,"lock":null}
20:13:19.153 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/17/697
20:13:19.153 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":697,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind NE. Took a Paddington stage into the city. Stephenson up, but not cleared for want of papers relative to the sum, from the West India docks. J Galbraith &amp; I walked down to the ship. Dined on board. Got our ballast alongside. Put all my cloths etc. on board the Peggy, captain Hunter, intending to take my passage to Shields in her. She hauled out of the Regents Canal &amp; proceeded down the river to Purfleet to ballast. William &amp; I walked up to the city, calling at Chapmans respecting the clearing papers.</p>","pageId":775,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":655,"lock":null}
20:13:19.153 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.154 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/17/697
20:13:19.154 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":697,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind NE. Took a Paddington stage into the city. Stephenson up, but not cleared for want of papers relative to the sum, from the West India docks. J Galbraith &amp; I walked down to the ship. Dined on board. Got our ballast alongside. Put all my cloths etc. on board the Peggy, captain Hunter, intending to take my passage to Shields in her. She hauled out of the Regents Canal &amp; proceeded down the river to Purfleet to ballast. William &amp; I walked up to the city, calling at Chapmans respecting the clearing papers.</p>","pageId":775,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":655,"lock":null}
20:13:19.154 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/18/2327
20:13:19.154 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":2327,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":18,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... Peggy laying at the wharf at Purfleet. Young White of Wordland near Durham, a 4<sup>th</sup> mate in the company's service also joined us. Blew a cloud or two &amp; turned in.</p>","pageId":775,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2267,"lock":null}
20:13:19.154 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.154 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/18/2327
20:13:19.154 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":2327,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":18,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... Peggy laying at the wharf at Purfleet. Young White of Wordland near Durham, a 4<sup>th</sup> mate in the company's service also joined us. Blew a cloud or two &amp; turned in.</p>","pageId":775,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2267,"lock":null}
20:13:19.154 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/18/698
20:13:19.154 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":698,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Been raining very heavy all night. Weather thick. Wind NE. Packed my cloths up. Took a packing coach &amp; went down to the office. Paid &pound;4.12. for 23 gallons of rum at 4/ per gallon. William paid it out of &pound;30 I gave him to place to my <span class=highlight_yellow>Chapmans account</span>. William &amp; I got on board the Pearl Gravesend boat. He accompanied me as far as Woolwich where he landed &amp; I proceeded to the ...</p>","pageId":775,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":656,"lock":null}
20:13:19.154 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.154 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/18/698
20:13:19.154 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":698,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Been raining very heavy all night. Weather thick. Wind NE. Packed my cloths up. Took a packing coach &amp; went down to the office. Paid &pound;4.12. for 23 gallons of rum at 4/ per gallon. William paid it out of &pound;30 I gave him to place to my <span class=highlight_yellow>Chapmans account</span>. William &amp; I got on board the Pearl Gravesend boat. He accompanied me as far as Woolwich where he landed &amp; I proceeded to the ...</p>","pageId":775,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":656,"lock":null}
20:13:19.154 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/19/699
20:13:19.154 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":699,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Been blowing a gale of wind from the NNE all night &amp; continued with rain all day. Amused ourselves during the morning strolling about Purfleet &amp; playing at billiards. Got our ballast on board &amp; hauled from the wharf about 5 o'clock. Weighed anchor &amp; sailed down to the Tower. Hope when we brought up for the night. Blowing a gale of wind. Finished a couple of glasses of whiskey punch, smoked a pipe &amp; turned in at 9 o'clock</p>","pageId":775,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":657,"lock":null}
20:13:19.154 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.155 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/19/699
20:13:19.155 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":699,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Been blowing a gale of wind from the NNE all night &amp; continued with rain all day. Amused ourselves during the morning strolling about Purfleet &amp; playing at billiards. Got our ballast on board &amp; hauled from the wharf about 5 o'clock. Weighed anchor &amp; sailed down to the Tower. Hope when we brought up for the night. Blowing a gale of wind. Finished a couple of glasses of whiskey punch, smoked a pipe &amp; turned in at 9 o'clock</p>","pageId":775,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":657,"lock":null}
20:13:19.155 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/2/676
20:13:19.155 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":676,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind NW. Called upon Jobling. He drove me down to Woolwich to see the Lumley's. Eat some cold meat with them &amp; returned to the ship at Greenwich to dinner, where Tom Jobling joined us. Left the ship about 7 o'clock &amp; drove to town. Had a glass of brandy &amp; wine with Jobling &amp; got to bed at &frac12; past 10 o'clock</p>","pageId":771,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":638,"lock":null}
20:13:19.155 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.156 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/2/676
20:13:19.156 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":676,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind NW. Called upon Jobling. He drove me down to Woolwich to see the Lumley's. Eat some cold meat with them &amp; returned to the ship at Greenwich to dinner, where Tom Jobling joined us. Left the ship about 7 o'clock &amp; drove to town. Had a glass of brandy &amp; wine with Jobling &amp; got to bed at &frac12; past 10 o'clock</p>","pageId":771,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":638,"lock":null}
20:13:19.156 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/20/700
20:13:19.156 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":700,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind about NNE. Got under way about 6 o'clock &amp; ran down to the <span class=highlight_yellow>Warp</span> where we brought up about &frac12; past 9 o'clock am.  Turned out an uncommonly fine day &amp; warm. About 12 o'clock the wind got to the NNW then NW &amp; after dinner to W by S &amp; WSW. When we got our anchor up, but being little wind, did not make much way. At about 8 o'clock being dark &amp; not able to see the buoy of the middle, we brought up for the night. Several ships in company.</p>\r\n<p>At 9 o'clock smoked a pipe, wet both eyes &amp; turned in. A good deal annoyed at not being able to proceed, there being a fine breeze.</p>","pageId":775,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":658,"lock":null}
20:13:19.156 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.156 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/20/700
20:13:19.156 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":700,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind about NNE. Got under way about 6 o'clock &amp; ran down to the <span class=highlight_yellow>Warp</span> where we brought up about &frac12; past 9 o'clock am.  Turned out an uncommonly fine day &amp; warm. About 12 o'clock the wind got to the NNW then NW &amp; after dinner to W by S &amp; WSW. When we got our anchor up, but being little wind, did not make much way. At about 8 o'clock being dark &amp; not able to see the buoy of the middle, we brought up for the night. Several ships in company.</p>\r\n<p>At 9 o'clock smoked a pipe, wet both eyes &amp; turned in. A good deal annoyed at not being able to proceed, there being a fine breeze.</p>","pageId":775,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":658,"lock":null}
20:13:19.156 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/21/701
20:13:19.156 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":701,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Been blowing fresh all night &amp; still continues at SE with small rain. The ship remaining down river with a strong ebb tide at the rate of about 10 knots, having got underway at day light between 5 &amp; 6 o'clock. At 10 o'clock am abreast of <span class=highlight_yellow>Ald</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span><span class=highlight_yellow>b</span><span class=highlight_yellow>urgh</span>. Clearer weather. Top mast &amp; lower studding sails set. Passed through the <span class=highlight_yellow>Br</span><span class=highlight_yellow>oads</span> about 1 o'clock with a fine breeze. At about 8 o'clock pm abreast of <span class=highlight_yellow>H</span><span class=highlight_yellow>appisburg</span><span class=highlight_yellow>h</span>. Took our pipe &amp; nip &amp; turned in at 9 o'clock. A beautiful star light night. Wind about W by S</p>","pageId":776,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":659,"lock":null}
20:13:19.156 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.157 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/21/701
20:13:19.157 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":701,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Been blowing fresh all night &amp; still continues at SE with small rain. The ship remaining down river with a strong ebb tide at the rate of about 10 knots, having got underway at day light between 5 &amp; 6 o'clock. At 10 o'clock am abreast of <span class=highlight_yellow>Ald</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span><span class=highlight_yellow>b</span><span class=highlight_yellow>urgh</span>. Clearer weather. Top mast &amp; lower studding sails set. Passed through the <span class=highlight_yellow>Br</span><span class=highlight_yellow>oads</span> about 1 o'clock with a fine breeze. At about 8 o'clock pm abreast of <span class=highlight_yellow>H</span><span class=highlight_yellow>appisburg</span><span class=highlight_yellow>h</span>. Took our pipe &amp; nip &amp; turned in at 9 o'clock. A beautiful star light night. Wind about W by S</p>","pageId":776,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":659,"lock":null}
20:13:19.157 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/22/702
20:13:19.157 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":702,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at &frac12; past 7 o'clock ship abreast of Darlington, having had a fine run all night. Wind W by S &amp; W SW &amp; beautiful weather at noon got round Flamborough Head close in shore. A delightful sail. Passed Scarborough about 2 o'clock &amp; at 3 o'clock where off the south cheek of Robin Hoods Bay, had a small shower of rain, but soon cleared up &amp; we had fine weather again &amp; being close in shore enjoyed a most beautiful view of the coast &amp; country. Passed Huntcliff Foot before dusk with a continuance of the breeze at about W. At 11 o'clock brought up off Tynemouth Bar, being past high water, we could only attempt to go in.</p>","pageId":776,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":660,"lock":null}
20:13:19.157 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.157 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/22/702
20:13:19.157 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":702,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at &frac12; past 7 o'clock ship abreast of Darlington, having had a fine run all night. Wind W by S &amp; W SW &amp; beautiful weather at noon got round Flamborough Head close in shore. A delightful sail. Passed Scarborough about 2 o'clock &amp; at 3 o'clock where off the south cheek of Robin Hoods Bay, had a small shower of rain, but soon cleared up &amp; we had fine weather again &amp; being close in shore enjoyed a most beautiful view of the coast &amp; country. Passed Huntcliff Foot before dusk with a continuance of the breeze at about W. At 11 o'clock brought up off Tynemouth Bar, being past high water, we could only attempt to go in.</p>","pageId":776,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":660,"lock":null}
20:13:19.157 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/23/703
20:13:19.157 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":703,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind about W by N. At 7 o'clock a steam boat came alongside &amp; afterwards towed us into the harbour, where Mr White &amp; I landed &amp; went up to Dockwray Square to breakfast. Found Mrs Scott much better than I expected &amp; able to get into the drawing room. Took an early dinner with Mr Tinley. Sat with <span class=highlight_yellow>neuf</span> for some time in the evening &amp; took tea with Mr Tinley.</p>\r\n<p>Much mortified and unhappy at being informed by <font color=#0000FF>Ann</font><font color=#0070C0> </font><font color=#BFBFBF>Maxwell </font>of her being with child to me. What the end of it be, I cannot divine, but it makes me miserable that I should have been such a fool &amp; madman to have committed such an act. Such a break of hospitality, such shaming &amp; disgraceful conduct. I am ashamed of myself.</p>","pageId":776,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":661,"lock":null}
20:13:19.157 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.158 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/23/703
20:13:19.158 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":703,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind about W by N. At 7 o'clock a steam boat came alongside &amp; afterwards towed us into the harbour, where Mr White &amp; I landed &amp; went up to Dockwray Square to breakfast. Found Mrs Scott much better than I expected &amp; able to get into the drawing room. Took an early dinner with Mr Tinley. Sat with <span class=highlight_yellow>neuf</span> for some time in the evening &amp; took tea with Mr Tinley.</p>\r\n<p>Much mortified and unhappy at being informed by <font color=#0000FF>Ann</font><font color=#0070C0> </font><font color=#BFBFBF>Maxwell </font>of her being with child to me. What the end of it be, I cannot divine, but it makes me miserable that I should have been such a fool &amp; madman to have committed such an act. Such a break of hospitality, such shaming &amp; disgraceful conduct. I am ashamed of myself.</p>","pageId":776,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":661,"lock":null}
20:13:19.158 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/24/704
20:13:19.158 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":704,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind North. Engaged writing nearly all the morning. Mrs Dixon unexpectedly came down, dined &amp; left us in the evening. Much confusion in the house.</p>\r\n<p>Poor <font color=#0000FF>Ann </font><font color=#BFBFBF>Maxwell </font>being obliged to acknowledge herself in a family way. Consequently Mrs Scott discharged her &amp; she left the house. A strong suspicion I believe, but not known that I am the father. This day passed over without any further discovery &amp; I hope I shall be able to keep it a secret in all events from Mrs Scott. In a devil of a stew.</p>\r\n<p>Settled with Robert for payment of <span class=highlight_yellow>mo</span><sup><span class=highlight_yellow>ly</span></sup><span class=highlight_yellow> recovery</span>. Wrote to William at Windsor. <font color=#0000FE>Mr French died suddenly</font></p>","pageId":776,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":662,"lock":null}
20:13:19.158 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.158 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/24/704
20:13:19.158 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":704,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind North. Engaged writing nearly all the morning. Mrs Dixon unexpectedly came down, dined &amp; left us in the evening. Much confusion in the house.</p>\r\n<p>Poor <font color=#0000FF>Ann </font><font color=#BFBFBF>Maxwell </font>being obliged to acknowledge herself in a family way. Consequently Mrs Scott discharged her &amp; she left the house. A strong suspicion I believe, but not known that I am the father. This day passed over without any further discovery &amp; I hope I shall be able to keep it a secret in all events from Mrs Scott. In a devil of a stew.</p>\r\n<p>Settled with Robert for payment of <span class=highlight_yellow>mo</span><sup><span class=highlight_yellow>ly</span></sup><span class=highlight_yellow> recovery</span>. Wrote to William at Windsor. <font color=#0000FE>Mr French died suddenly</font></p>","pageId":776,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":662,"lock":null}
20:13:19.158 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/25/705
20:13:19.158 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":705,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful day. Wind ESE &amp; SE. Nothing further transpired respecting this unfortunate business with <font color=#0000FF>Ann</font> <font color=#BFBFBF>Maxwell</font>. Mrs Scott has not spoken to me about, though I believe &lsquo;tis her intention. I gave her every opportunity by dining at home &amp; sitting with her, for I'm anxious it was over, for this suspense is unpleasant.</p>\r\n<p>Saw <font color=#0000FF>Ann</font> <font color=#BFBFBF>Maxwell </font>in the evening &amp; gave her a sovereign</p>","pageId":776,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":663,"lock":null}
20:13:19.158 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.159 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/25/705
20:13:19.159 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":705,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful day. Wind ESE &amp; SE. Nothing further transpired respecting this unfortunate business with <font color=#0000FF>Ann</font> <font color=#BFBFBF>Maxwell</font>. Mrs Scott has not spoken to me about, though I believe &lsquo;tis her intention. I gave her every opportunity by dining at home &amp; sitting with her, for I'm anxious it was over, for this suspense is unpleasant.</p>\r\n<p>Saw <font color=#0000FF>Ann</font> <font color=#BFBFBF>Maxwell </font>in the evening &amp; gave her a sovereign</p>","pageId":776,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":663,"lock":null}
20:13:19.159 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/26/706
20:13:19.159 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":706,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Afterwards turned to rain. Wind SW &amp; WSW blowing strong. Engaged all the morning in the office making up the Hope's Petersburg voyage. Dined at home. Mrs S<font color=#BFBFBF>cott</font> put the question to me whether I was the cause of <font color=#0000FF>Ann</font> <font color=#BFBFBF>Maxwell </font>being with child, which on her (Mrs Scott's ) account being in so precarious a state of health, I denied.  Therefor if she hears of it through some kind officious friend &amp; anything happens, be the blame upon their shoulders. I shall not be the cause.</p>\r\n<p>With Ann Stokes this evening</p>\r\n<p>The Childers, Captain <span class=highlight_yellow>Moriay</span> came into harbour</p>","pageId":777,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":664,"lock":null}
20:13:19.159 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.159 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/26/706
20:13:19.159 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":706,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Afterwards turned to rain. Wind SW &amp; WSW blowing strong. Engaged all the morning in the office making up the Hope's Petersburg voyage. Dined at home. Mrs S<font color=#BFBFBF>cott</font> put the question to me whether I was the cause of <font color=#0000FF>Ann</font> <font color=#BFBFBF>Maxwell </font>being with child, which on her (Mrs Scott's ) account being in so precarious a state of health, I denied.  Therefor if she hears of it through some kind officious friend &amp; anything happens, be the blame upon their shoulders. I shall not be the cause.</p>\r\n<p>With Ann Stokes this evening</p>\r\n<p>The Childers, Captain <span class=highlight_yellow>Moriay</span> came into harbour</p>","pageId":777,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":664,"lock":null}
20:13:19.159 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/27/707
20:13:19.159 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":707,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind SW blowing fresh during the day. Sent a letter by Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>J </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Haker's</span>  ship, the Ajax, to Elsineus, directed to Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>In</span> Brown, Copenhagen, that I forgot to deliver when there. Attended church in the morning. Walked with Mr Allen to Tynemouth in the afternoon &amp; afterward dined with him</p>","pageId":777,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":665,"lock":null}
20:13:19.159 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
