20:13:19.160 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":707,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind SW blowing fresh during the day. Sent a letter by Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>J </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Haker's</span>  ship, the Ajax, to Elsineus, directed to Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>In</span> Brown, Copenhagen, that I forgot to deliver when there. Attended church in the morning. Walked with Mr Allen to Tynemouth in the afternoon &amp; afterward dined with him</p>","pageId":777,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":665,"lock":null}
20:13:19.160 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/28/708
20:13:19.160 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":708,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind N by W &amp; cold. Received a letter from C Richmond asking me to go to <span class=highlight_yellow>Bur</span><span class=highlight_yellow>nhopeside</span> tomorrow. Answered it &amp; fixed Sunday to be there. Dined at home &amp; in the afternoon took a walk with Mark Webb &amp; Mr Robinson, the latter with his <span class=highlight_yellow>guardian</span></p>","pageId":777,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":666,"lock":null}
