20:13:19.165 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/7/685
20:13:19.165 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":685,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":7,"sequence":3.0000,"text":"<p>A showery day, at intervals, at intervals very fine. Wind about SE. Got into a Greenwich boat at &frac12; past 10 o'clock &amp; landed at Catherine dock. Found them busy with the <span class=highlight_yellow>lathwood</span> which was sold on Thursday to Mr Martin at &pound;16.5/- a fathom. Had not been long on board when Bob Marsh came. We had our dinner &amp; afterwards walked up to Philpot lane where I found a letter from William of his intention to be in town by the Highflyer in the evening.</p>\r\n<p>Called at J Chapmans &amp; from the state of the coal trades, the coal owners having again restricted the <span class=highlight_yellow>vends</span>, raised their price 5/- &amp; refusing either to freight or uphold, I almost determined to send the Hope to <span class=highlight_yellow>memel</span> at 21/- &amp; load for timber. Shall settle tomorrow.</p>\r\n<p>Bob &amp; I called upon J Hodgsons &amp; afterwards took a walk up Regent Street. Brought a new Hat at Oliphants &amp; a pair of trousers at Laffins. At &frac12; past 8 o'clock went to the Cock in Fleet Street &amp; eat some oysters &amp; at 10 o'clock met William &amp; Lea at the White Horse in Fetter Lane having just arrived from Shields by the Highflyer. A very wet night</p>","pageId":772,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":643,"lock":null}
20:13:19.165 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.166 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/7/685
20:13:19.166 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":685,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":7,"sequence":3.0000,"text":"<p>A showery day, at intervals, at intervals very fine. Wind about SE. Got into a Greenwich boat at &frac12; past 10 o'clock &amp; landed at Catherine dock. Found them busy with the <span class=highlight_yellow>lathwood</span> which was sold on Thursday to Mr Martin at &pound;16.5/- a fathom. Had not been long on board when Bob Marsh came. We had our dinner &amp; afterwards walked up to Philpot lane where I found a letter from William of his intention to be in town by the Highflyer in the evening.</p>\r\n<p>Called at J Chapmans &amp; from the state of the coal trades, the coal owners having again restricted the <span class=highlight_yellow>vends</span>, raised their price 5/- &amp; refusing either to freight or uphold, I almost determined to send the Hope to <span class=highlight_yellow>memel</span> at 21/- &amp; load for timber. Shall settle tomorrow.</p>\r\n<p>Bob &amp; I called upon J Hodgsons &amp; afterwards took a walk up Regent Street. Brought a new Hat at Oliphants &amp; a pair of trousers at Laffins. At &frac12; past 8 o'clock went to the Cock in Fleet Street &amp; eat some oysters &amp; at 10 o'clock met William &amp; Lea at the White Horse in Fetter Lane having just arrived from Shields by the Highflyer. A very wet night</p>","pageId":772,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":643,"lock":null}
20:13:19.166 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/8/686
20:13:19.166 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":686,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Showery. Wind SW. William &amp; Lea called at new Inn &amp; we went into the city together in a coach. Called at Chapmans but did not freight the Hope, thinking to send her to Shields. Walked down to the ship. William took J Galbraith to Nottingham Place with him. I &amp; J Hodgson ...</p>","pageId":772,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":644,"lock":null}
20:13:19.166 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.166 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/8/686
20:13:19.166 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":686,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Showery. Wind SW. William &amp; Lea called at new Inn &amp; we went into the city together in a coach. Called at Chapmans but did not freight the Hope, thinking to send her to Shields. Walked down to the ship. William took J Galbraith to Nottingham Place with him. I &amp; J Hodgson ...</p>","pageId":772,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":644,"lock":null}
20:13:19.166 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/8/687
20:13:19.166 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":687,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":8,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>.. got into a stage at 6 o'clock &amp; went down to Greenwich &amp; dined with G Watt, it being his wife's birthday. Returned to town in the evening.</p>","pageId":773,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":645,"lock":null}
20:13:19.166 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.167 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/8/687
20:13:19.167 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":687,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":8,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>.. got into a stage at 6 o'clock &amp; went down to Greenwich &amp; dined with G Watt, it being his wife's birthday. Returned to town in the evening.</p>","pageId":773,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":645,"lock":null}
20:13:19.167 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/9/688
20:13:19.167 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":688,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather. Wind about SW. Nothing particular occurred today. Attended chambers. Sam Harry offered me 21/- <span class=highlight_yellow>pload</span> for Hull, having had a letter from Henry, that such freights could be obtained. Agreed to wait till tomorrow when Henry would be in town. Walked to the Blue Ports in Cork Square where we all met &amp; dined.</p>","pageId":773,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":646,"lock":null}
20:13:19.167 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.167 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/9/688
20:13:19.167 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":688,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather. Wind about SW. Nothing particular occurred today. Attended chambers. Sam Harry offered me 21/- <span class=highlight_yellow>pload</span> for Hull, having had a letter from Henry, that such freights could be obtained. Agreed to wait till tomorrow when Henry would be in town. Walked to the Blue Ports in Cork Square where we all met &amp; dined.</p>","pageId":773,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":646,"lock":null}
20:13:19.167 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/1/1/806
20:13:19.167 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":806,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":1,"day":1,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<div class=\"highlights-section\" >\r\n<section>\r\n\r\n\t<h2>Highlights</h2>\r\n\r\n\t<a href=\"/diaries/1830.html#1830-01-24\">\r\n\t<p>1830-01-24 Mrs Scott falls out of bed and breaks her leg</p>\r\n\t</a>\r\n\r\n\t<a href=\"/diaries/1830.html#1830-07-13\">\r\n\t<p>1830-07-13 JSR witnessed an accident which killed a girl sitting under cliffs</p>\r\n\t</a>\r\n\r\n</section>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"page-break-after: always;\">\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n</div>","pageId":null,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":null,"lock":null}
