20:13:19.168 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":807,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":1,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Seasonal weather but not very severe. Wind WNW. Walked again to Cullercoats &amp; saw them land their fish which were remarkably fine. Dined at home. In the evening Cunningham, Nicolson, &amp; I went to the Duke of York &amp; drank a jug of punch. In the evening at the Mulstrum &amp; with Bell Jervis</p>","pageId":788,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":760,"lock":null}
20:13:19.168 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/1/10/817
20:13:19.168 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":817,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":1,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>It has been a hard frost &amp; blowing a gale at north all night &amp; still continues with a very high sea. Went to church in the morning. Dined at 2 o'clock with H Harry. Mr Sadler there. In the evening at the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":789,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":769,"lock":null}
20:13:19.168 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.169 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/1/10/817
20:13:19.169 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":817,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":1,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>It has been a hard frost &amp; blowing a gale at north all night &amp; still continues with a very high sea. Went to church in the morning. Dined at 2 o'clock with H Harry. Mr Sadler there. In the evening at the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":789,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":769,"lock":null}
20:13:19.169 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/1/11/818
20:13:19.169 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":818,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":1,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Been a slight frost in the night with a little snow. Wind NNW. Mrs Dixon brought Emma home. Dined at home. Spent the evening at J Tinleys</p>","pageId":789,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":770,"lock":null}
20:13:19.169 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.169 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/1/11/818
20:13:19.169 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":818,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":1,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Been a slight frost in the night with a little snow. Wind NNW. Mrs Dixon brought Emma home. Dined at home. Spent the evening at J Tinleys</p>","pageId":789,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":770,"lock":null}
20:13:19.169 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/1/12/819
20:13:19.169 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":819,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":1,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Last night very stormy. A gale from the NE with heavy showers of sleet &amp; hail.</p>\r\n<p>Received a letter in the name of the Bank, but evidently written by that little puppy F Chapman without consulting his partners, desiring me to pay the balance of my account with them of some &pound;106. Called &amp; saw Spence who seemed ignorant of such a letter having been written. Told him what I thought of such conduct. I having ample security in their hands.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home. At the Duke of York with Mr Hewson, Nicholson, Cunningham &amp; Wheatley. Received of newsroom &pound;3.10/- for WBD</p>","pageId":789,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":771,"lock":null}
20:13:19.169 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.170 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/1/12/819
20:13:19.170 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":819,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":1,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Last night very stormy. A gale from the NE with heavy showers of sleet &amp; hail.</p>\r\n<p>Received a letter in the name of the Bank, but evidently written by that little puppy F Chapman without consulting his partners, desiring me to pay the balance of my account with them of some &pound;106. Called &amp; saw Spence who seemed ignorant of such a letter having been written. Told him what I thought of such conduct. I having ample security in their hands.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home. At the Duke of York with Mr Hewson, Nicholson, Cunningham &amp; Wheatley. Received of newsroom &pound;3.10/- for WBD</p>","pageId":789,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":771,"lock":null}
20:13:19.170 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/1/13/820
20:13:19.170 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":820,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":1,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine dry winters morning. Rather frosty &amp; blowing fresh at NE. Dined at home. H Harry, Mr Hewson, Nicholson &amp; I had a glass of grog together at the Duke of York. A stormy night, a hurricane with snow.</p>","pageId":789,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":772,"lock":null}
20:13:19.170 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
