20:13:19.186 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1097,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":10,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind SSE. Walked with Allen round by Whitley. Called upon Mr Wright &amp; returned by Callercoat. Dined with H Metcalfe. At the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":854,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1045,"lock":null}
20:13:19.186 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/10/15/1098
20:13:19.186 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1098,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":10,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but foggy which is clearing away Wind SW. Walked to Tynemouth Could not see the Hope. Dined at home At Dr Drury's garden in the afternoon &amp; in the evening at the Albion &amp; Mulstrum. Paid Mrs Brown &pound;3.5.6 for making mainsail</p>","pageId":855,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1046,"lock":null}
