20:13:19.193 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1110,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":10,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold morning. Wind NW Saw the Northhumberland fox hounds from Benton show off at Gosforth. Dixon &amp; I walked upto Newcastle. Saw Tom Smith, walked to see the horses being fair team. Sold an old silver spoon cracked &amp; gave five shillings in addition for a new one for Emma. Took the steam boat at 2 o'clock. Came home to dinner. Wrote to WBS expecting Miss Gauntley &amp; Mary Carfs. Wrote unto C Richmond that I could not meet him at Dersham on Saturday. Albion</p>","pageId":857,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1058,"lock":null}
20:13:19.193 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/10/28/1111
20:13:19.193 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1111,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":10,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning after a good deal of rain in the night &amp; blowing fresh from W  by N Dined on board the Ruby with Mr Lewry &amp; at the whist club in the evening</p>","pageId":858,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1059,"lock":null}
20:13:19.193 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
