20:13:19.202 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1131,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":11,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning, rather frosty. Wind west Walked up to the ship Took an early dinner on board the Crises. In the evening at the Albion &amp; Duke of York.</p>\r\n<p>Received a letter from Mrs Bagot Wishing Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>albraith</font> to be placed under their mothers care</p>","pageId":861,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1079,"lock":null}
20:13:19.202 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/11/18/1132
20:13:19.202 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1132,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":11,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A showery morning Wind NE. Been a great deal of rain in the night. Sea high. Paid Gibson butcher bill &frac14; of year &pound;4.9/- also executors of Scott <span class=highlight_yellow>painer</span> &pound;3.8- for the home &amp; &pound;12.19/- property. Walked to Tynemouth &amp; called upon two officers of the 15<sup>th</sup> regiment Hind &amp; <font color=#A6A6A6>[         ]</font> afterwards. Walked up &amp; dined at the Point with Sadby. Attended the whist club in the evening &amp; the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":861,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1080,"lock":null}
20:13:19.202 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
