20:13:19.215 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1155,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Weather completely changed. A little sunshine at last. Wind W by N &amp; WNN. A large fleet of ships got to sea but too much swell on the bar to allow the Hope to sail, although some nearly her draught of water <span class=highlight_yellow>veateered</span> , but <span class=highlight_yellow>do</span><span class=highlight_yellow>w</span><span class=highlight_yellow>t</span> down struck. Dined at home at the whist club at Rev<font color=#BFBFBF>erand</font> Richmonds in evening</p>","pageId":865,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1103,"lock":null}
20:13:19.215 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/12/12/1156
20:13:19.215 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1156,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Although it was a most beautiful night at the home I left Rev<font color=#BFBFBF>erand</font> Richmonds &amp; frosty <span class=highlight_yellow>buk</span> soon after 12 o'clock the wind got to NE &amp; increased before daylight to a perfect gale, with heavy showers of sleet &amp; a very high sea on the bar/over</p>","pageId":865,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1104,"lock":null}
20:13:19.215 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.216 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/12/12/1156
20:13:19.216 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1156,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Although it was a most beautiful night at the home I left Rev<font color=#BFBFBF>erand</font> Richmonds &amp; frosty <span class=highlight_yellow>buk</span> soon after 12 o'clock the wind got to NE &amp; increased before daylight to a perfect gale, with heavy showers of sleet &amp; a very high sea on the bar/over</p>","pageId":865,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1104,"lock":null}
20:13:19.216 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/12/12/1157
20:13:19.216 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1157,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":12,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>Stayed in the home all morning. Dined at home. Went to the newsroom in the afternoon. Very strong with heavy showers of snow, hail &amp; sleet. <span class=highlight_yellow>Guefal</span> got upon the Herd. Spent the evening at home. Turned out a fine clear night &amp; hard frost.</p>","pageId":866,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1105,"lock":null}
20:13:19.216 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.217 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/12/12/1157
20:13:19.217 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1157,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":12,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>Stayed in the home all morning. Dined at home. Went to the newsroom in the afternoon. Very strong with heavy showers of snow, hail &amp; sleet. <span class=highlight_yellow>Guefal</span> got upon the Herd. Spent the evening at home. Turned out a fine clear night &amp; hard frost.</p>","pageId":866,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1105,"lock":null}
20:13:19.217 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/12/13/1158
20:13:19.217 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1158,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; hard frost with a little snow on the ground. Wind NW. On board the Hope &amp; the Lightning Government Steamer came down here with 150 marines for the garrison at Tynemouth. A beautiful <span class=highlight_yellow>copal</span> of elegantly fit up.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home &amp; in the evening attended the theatre  with Hargraves beautiful &amp; bespeake of the Bachelors of <span class=highlight_yellow>Nosh</span><span class=highlight_yellow>u</span><span class=highlight_yellow>l</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span><span class=highlight_yellow>s</span>. Finished off at the Albion. Sleet and rain at night.</p>","pageId":866,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1106,"lock":null}
20:13:19.217 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.217 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/12/13/1158
20:13:19.217 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1158,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; hard frost with a little snow on the ground. Wind NW. On board the Hope &amp; the Lightning Government Steamer came down here with 150 marines for the garrison at Tynemouth. A beautiful <span class=highlight_yellow>copal</span> of elegantly fit up.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home &amp; in the evening attended the theatre  with Hargraves beautiful &amp; bespeake of the Bachelors of <span class=highlight_yellow>Nosh</span><span class=highlight_yellow>u</span><span class=highlight_yellow>l</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span><span class=highlight_yellow>s</span>. Finished off at the Albion. Sleet and rain at night.</p>","pageId":866,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1106,"lock":null}
20:13:19.217 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/12/14/1159
20:13:19.217 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1159,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet raw unpleasant morning. Wind W by N. The Hope got to sea in the afternoon without touching the bar, there being a great deal of sea on. Some had accounts of the ships that sailed on Saturday many struck very heavily on the bar &amp; some in consequence the crew not being able to <span class=highlight_yellow>Kup</span> them, foundered &amp; all the people drowned. At least we had an account of one &amp; another having run on shore. Dined at the Albion, a bed dance &amp; a very good one, spent a pleasant day. In visiting Bradshaw &amp; H Harry, chain &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>vi</span><span class=highlight_yellow>n</span><span class=highlight_yellow>c</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span>. 12 percent</p>","pageId":866,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1107,"lock":null}
20:13:19.217 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.218 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/12/14/1159
20:13:19.218 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1159,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet raw unpleasant morning. Wind W by N. The Hope got to sea in the afternoon without touching the bar, there being a great deal of sea on. Some had accounts of the ships that sailed on Saturday many struck very heavily on the bar &amp; some in consequence the crew not being able to <span class=highlight_yellow>Kup</span> them, foundered &amp; all the people drowned. At least we had an account of one &amp; another having run on shore. Dined at the Albion, a bed dance &amp; a very good one, spent a pleasant day. In visiting Bradshaw &amp; H Harry, chain &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>vi</span><span class=highlight_yellow>n</span><span class=highlight_yellow>c</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span>. 12 percent</p>","pageId":866,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1107,"lock":null}
20:13:19.218 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/12/15/1160
20:13:19.218 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1160,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very dull thick &amp; raining morning. Wind SW but little of it. Received  a letter from WBS answered it informing him of the sailing of the Hope &amp; Dined at home.</p>\r\n<p>At the Albion in the evening, for the benefit of Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>P</span><span class=highlight_yellow>er</span><span class=highlight_yellow>rs</span>, the <span class=highlight_yellow>vishrak</span> as the bells started of the gents of the commercial newsroom but not more than three or four there. Called at the Mulstrum</p>\r\n<p>HMS Childers came</p>\r\n<p>Answered WBS's letter informing him also that chapman had agreed to service the note of &pound;300 for four months. They carried &pound;50 to my account remitted by WBS</p>","pageId":867,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1108,"lock":null}
20:13:19.218 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.219 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/12/15/1160
20:13:19.219 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1160,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very dull thick &amp; raining morning. Wind SW but little of it. Received  a letter from WBS answered it informing him of the sailing of the Hope &amp; Dined at home.</p>\r\n<p>At the Albion in the evening, for the benefit of Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>P</span><span class=highlight_yellow>er</span><span class=highlight_yellow>rs</span>, the <span class=highlight_yellow>vishrak</span> as the bells started of the gents of the commercial newsroom but not more than three or four there. Called at the Mulstrum</p>\r\n<p>HMS Childers came</p>\r\n<p>Answered WBS's letter informing him also that chapman had agreed to service the note of &pound;300 for four months. They carried &pound;50 to my account remitted by WBS</p>","pageId":867,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1108,"lock":null}
20:13:19.219 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/12/16/1161
20:13:19.219 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1161,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind SW Dined at home. HMS <span class=highlight_yellow>Jacasacy</span> came into harbour to lay as a guard ship. At the billiard room &amp; whist club in the evening</p>","pageId":867,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1109,"lock":null}
20:13:19.219 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.219 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/12/16/1161
20:13:19.219 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1161,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind SW Dined at home. HMS <span class=highlight_yellow>Jacasacy</span> came into harbour to lay as a guard ship. At the billiard room &amp; whist club in the evening</p>","pageId":867,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1109,"lock":null}
20:13:19.219 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/12/17/1162
20:13:19.219 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1162,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>In the night it began to blow very hard from the NNE. &amp; continued pretty near a gale the whole of the day from that to NE with heavy showers of hail &amp; snow &amp; high sea. Another <span class=highlight_yellow>catic</span> put in making two, live government steamers, a Green Boy, 28 gun frigate in the harbour. Attended a public meeting for the purpose of entering this resolution with regard to the Rail road. Dined at home. At the billiard &amp; news rooms &amp; finished at the Duke of York. Got &pound;5 of chapman</p>","pageId":867,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1110,"lock":null}
20:13:19.219 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.220 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/12/17/1162
20:13:19.220 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1162,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>In the night it began to blow very hard from the NNE. &amp; continued pretty near a gale the whole of the day from that to NE with heavy showers of hail &amp; snow &amp; high sea. Another <span class=highlight_yellow>catic</span> put in making two, live government steamers, a Green Boy, 28 gun frigate in the harbour. Attended a public meeting for the purpose of entering this resolution with regard to the Rail road. Dined at home. At the billiard &amp; news rooms &amp; finished at the Duke of York. Got &pound;5 of chapman</p>","pageId":867,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1110,"lock":null}
20:13:19.220 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/12/18/1163
20:13:19.220 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1163,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>it blew very hard last night from the NE with showers of hail &amp; snow, but towards morning relented &amp; at breakfast time wind NW. But at sea still apparently <span class=highlight_yellow>Easta</span> of north. Paid Ed: Keids <span class=highlight_yellow>moshvo</span> &pound;1.13.9 &frac14; years wages. Dined at home. Attended the whist club at Craigs in the evening. Frosty</p>","pageId":868,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1111,"lock":null}
20:13:19.220 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.220 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/12/18/1163
20:13:19.220 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1163,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>it blew very hard last night from the NE with showers of hail &amp; snow, but towards morning relented &amp; at breakfast time wind NW. But at sea still apparently <span class=highlight_yellow>Easta</span> of north. Paid Ed: Keids <span class=highlight_yellow>moshvo</span> &pound;1.13.9 &frac14; years wages. Dined at home. Attended the whist club at Craigs in the evening. Frosty</p>","pageId":868,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1111,"lock":null}
20:13:19.220 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/12/19/1164
20:13:19.220 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1164,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>More moderate &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>rainy</span> weather. Wind W by S. A frost during the night. Did not go to church. Read the service at home. In the afternoon it came on to blow a heavy gale of wind at NW. Many ships got to sea.</p>\r\n<p>HMS Chelders running to go to sea but at blowing hard with a heavy fresh in the river, the ships were quite unmanageable. The first officer on board the cutter &amp; threw to the opposite side of the river &amp; letting go her anchor prevented her going to shore. Some <span class=highlight_yellow>coll</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span><span class=highlight_yellow>cse</span> there got foul of her &amp; finally she was prevented going to sea &amp; obliged next tide to move again in her old birth. Dined with J Tenley where the officer was expected but prevented coming.</p>\r\n<p>10 o'clock pm calmer weather again</p>","pageId":868,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1112,"lock":null}
20:13:19.220 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.221 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/12/19/1164
20:13:19.221 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1164,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>More moderate &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>rainy</span> weather. Wind W by S. A frost during the night. Did not go to church. Read the service at home. In the afternoon it came on to blow a heavy gale of wind at NW. Many ships got to sea.</p>\r\n<p>HMS Chelders running to go to sea but at blowing hard with a heavy fresh in the river, the ships were quite unmanageable. The first officer on board the cutter &amp; threw to the opposite side of the river &amp; letting go her anchor prevented her going to shore. Some <span class=highlight_yellow>coll</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span><span class=highlight_yellow>cse</span> there got foul of her &amp; finally she was prevented going to sea &amp; obliged next tide to move again in her old birth. Dined with J Tenley where the officer was expected but prevented coming.</p>\r\n<p>10 o'clock pm calmer weather again</p>","pageId":868,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1112,"lock":null}
20:13:19.221 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/12/2/1146
20:13:19.221 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1146,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Amore moderate weather. Wind S by W &amp; very damp. On board the Hope. The men still busy with the windlass. Dined at home Attended the whist club in the evening</p>","pageId":864,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1094,"lock":null}
20:13:19.221 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.221 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/12/2/1146
20:13:19.221 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1146,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Amore moderate weather. Wind S by W &amp; very damp. On board the Hope. The men still busy with the windlass. Dined at home Attended the whist club in the evening</p>","pageId":864,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1094,"lock":null}
20:13:19.221 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/12/20/1165
20:13:19.221 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1165,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>During the night the wind veered round to the NE. Blowing half a gale and a heavy sea came on. The <font color=#BFBFBF>HMS </font>Childers moored into Peggy's hole again. Cunningham dined with me. At the billiard room in the afternoon. J Agusley got his discharge today from hews &amp; billiard room having given himself up to drunkenness. At the theatre in the evening. The bespeak of the officers of the garrison.</p>\r\n<p>P J Hutchison &pound;2.16.3 averages</p>","pageId":869,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1113,"lock":null}
20:13:19.221 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.222 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/12/20/1165
20:13:19.222 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1165,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>During the night the wind veered round to the NE. Blowing half a gale and a heavy sea came on. The <font color=#BFBFBF>HMS </font>Childers moored into Peggy's hole again. Cunningham dined with me. At the billiard room in the afternoon. J Agusley got his discharge today from hews &amp; billiard room having given himself up to drunkenness. At the theatre in the evening. The bespeak of the officers of the garrison.</p>\r\n<p>P J Hutchison &pound;2.16.3 averages</p>","pageId":869,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1113,"lock":null}
20:13:19.222 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/12/21/1166
20:13:19.222 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1166,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, rather Cold. Wind W by N.  Sea fallen. Walked up to the Point to dine with Sadler. Spent a pleasant day</p>","pageId":869,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1114,"lock":null}
20:13:19.222 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
