20:13:19.224 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1169,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful winter's morning. Most intense frost &amp; NW wind, sea high. Received a letter from WBS of the arrival &amp; sale of 126 chars of the Hope cargo at Wednesday day mackerel  at 34/-. Mr C Wright &amp; Mr L Loyd a <span class=highlight_yellow>dined</span> on board the Lamaracy came &amp; took dinner today. Attended the whist club in the evening at Fenwicks. A most intense frost</p>","pageId":870,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1117,"lock":null}
20:13:19.224 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/12/25/1170
20:13:19.224 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1170,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><u>Xmas day</u> After a most intense frost during the night, we have a heavy fall of snow. Wind NW. At the newsroom. Paris in a fearful state of excitement. The most fearing the decision of the peers well be in favour of the later. Herewith to WBS giving him an account of the weather here. Walked to Tynemouth &amp; dined with J Cunningham, family party. Spent a very pleasant day</p>","pageId":870,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1118,"lock":null}
