20:13:19.234 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":851,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind about SW. On board the Hopes &amp; engaged looking for a Kedger getting but the beef at 4 o'clock. Dined with I Tiney &amp; at the Whist Club in the evening at Mr Richmounds The Hope got these Rich</p>","pageId":798,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":803,"lock":null}
20:13:19.234 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/14/852
20:13:19.234 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":852,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful spring morning. Wind SW. Went to church Mr Mark &amp;  the vicar dest the duty. Dined at home at 1 o'Clock. H Harry, H French Nicholson &amp; I walked to Tynemouth round the castle &amp; took wine at the Star &amp; Garter In the evening at the <span class=highlight_yellow>M</span><span class=highlight_yellow>u</span><span class=highlight_yellow>l</span><span class=highlight_yellow>st</span><span class=highlight_yellow>rum</span></p>","pageId":798,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":804,"lock":null}
20:13:19.234 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.234 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/14/852
20:13:19.234 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":852,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful spring morning. Wind SW. Went to church Mr Mark &amp;  the vicar dest the duty. Dined at home at 1 o'Clock. H Harry, H French Nicholson &amp; I walked to Tynemouth round the castle &amp; took wine at the Star &amp; Garter In the evening at the <span class=highlight_yellow>M</span><span class=highlight_yellow>u</span><span class=highlight_yellow>l</span><span class=highlight_yellow>st</span><span class=highlight_yellow>rum</span></p>","pageId":798,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":804,"lock":null}
20:13:19.234 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/15/853
20:13:19.234 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":853,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful morning &amp; quite mild wind about north. On board the Hope only got J Kuls down Today. Dined at home. Mrs Dixon down to See Mrs Scott. Drank tea at home &amp; in The evening at the George with H Harry &amp; Wrote to WBS</p>","pageId":798,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":805,"lock":null}
20:13:19.234 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.235 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/15/853
20:13:19.235 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":853,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful morning &amp; quite mild wind about north. On board the Hope only got J Kuls down Today. Dined at home. Mrs Dixon down to See Mrs Scott. Drank tea at home &amp; in The evening at the George with H Harry &amp; Wrote to WBS</p>","pageId":798,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":805,"lock":null}
20:13:19.235 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/16/854
20:13:19.235 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":854,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A delightful morning &amp; frosty. Wind mild. On board the Hope When she finished her loading leffering in 16 Kule &amp; 5 Char. Attended the annual meeting of the eligible &amp; afterwards and dined with Placaad &amp; spend a pleasant day. In the evening with Bell Jervis</p>","pageId":798,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":806,"lock":null}
20:13:19.235 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.235 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/16/854
20:13:19.235 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":854,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A delightful morning &amp; frosty. Wind mild. On board the Hope When she finished her loading leffering in 16 Kule &amp; 5 Char. Attended the annual meeting of the eligible &amp; afterwards and dined with Placaad &amp; spend a pleasant day. In the evening with Bell Jervis</p>","pageId":798,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":806,"lock":null}
20:13:19.235 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/17/855
20:13:19.235 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":855,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning Rather frosty wind fresh at NW. Got up at 7 o'clock and went on board the Hope. The pilot on board but decided to not venture to take her out, it being in bad tide &amp; threw feet sea upon the bar. Received a letter from WBS &amp; one from Tom Lee. Answered Tom Lees. Dined at home &amp; spent the afternoon at the billiard table. In the evening, heavy rain &amp; wind to NNE. At the Duke of York with H Harry &amp; Nicholson</p>","pageId":799,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":807,"lock":null}
20:13:19.235 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.236 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/17/855
20:13:19.236 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":855,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning Rather frosty wind fresh at NW. Got up at 7 o'clock and went on board the Hope. The pilot on board but decided to not venture to take her out, it being in bad tide &amp; threw feet sea upon the bar. Received a letter from WBS &amp; one from Tom Lee. Answered Tom Lees. Dined at home &amp; spent the afternoon at the billiard table. In the evening, heavy rain &amp; wind to NNE. At the Duke of York with H Harry &amp; Nicholson</p>","pageId":799,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":807,"lock":null}
20:13:19.236 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/18/856
20:13:19.236 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":856,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A frosty morning wind NW. A sea upon the bar which will prevent the Hope getting out. Dined at home In the evening at the Whist Club.</p>","pageId":799,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":808,"lock":null}
20:13:19.236 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.237 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/18/856
20:13:19.237 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":856,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A frosty morning wind NW. A sea upon the bar which will prevent the Hope getting out. Dined at home In the evening at the Whist Club.</p>","pageId":799,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":808,"lock":null}
20:13:19.237 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/19/857
20:13:19.237 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":857,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A course frost. Wind NNW &amp; blowing fresh &amp; although the sea was breaking upon the bar, several small ships ventured out &amp; some were literally smothered in the surf, but all got out safe. Dined with I Readhead on board the Nautalus At the billiard room in the afternoon. Drank tea at home &amp; in the evening With Bode Jerois &amp; afterwards at the Duke Of York</p>","pageId":799,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":809,"lock":null}
20:13:19.237 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.237 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/19/857
20:13:19.237 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":857,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A course frost. Wind NNW &amp; blowing fresh &amp; although the sea was breaking upon the bar, several small ships ventured out &amp; some were literally smothered in the surf, but all got out safe. Dined with I Readhead on board the Nautalus At the billiard room in the afternoon. Drank tea at home &amp; in the evening With Bode Jerois &amp; afterwards at the Duke Of York</p>","pageId":799,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":809,"lock":null}
20:13:19.237 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/2/840
20:13:19.237 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":840,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A countenance of winter weather, very cold. Been blowing a gale all night with snow showers A heavy sea upon the bar. Wind E.S.E Dined at home. At 3 o'clock at the billiard room in the afternoon. In the evening called and sat an hour or two with Mark, he having had a severe loin attack</p>","pageId":795,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":792,"lock":null}
20:13:19.237 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.238 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/2/840
20:13:19.238 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":840,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A countenance of winter weather, very cold. Been blowing a gale all night with snow showers A heavy sea upon the bar. Wind E.S.E Dined at home. At 3 o'clock at the billiard room in the afternoon. In the evening called and sat an hour or two with Mark, he having had a severe loin attack</p>","pageId":795,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":792,"lock":null}
20:13:19.238 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/20/858
20:13:19.238 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":858,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of frost Wind NW. Got up early &amp; went by stream to Newcastle; had a heavy snow storm Returned to dinner at 1 o'clock. Emma G with us. Mrs Dixon came to see Mrs Scott Not water sufficient for the Hope to get to sea. Attended the Whist Club at Allans in the evening</p>\r\n<p>xx</p>","pageId":799,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":810,"lock":null}
20:13:19.238 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.239 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/20/858
20:13:19.239 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":858,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of frost Wind NW. Got up early &amp; went by stream to Newcastle; had a heavy snow storm Returned to dinner at 1 o'clock. Emma G with us. Mrs Dixon came to see Mrs Scott Not water sufficient for the Hope to get to sea. Attended the Whist Club at Allans in the evening</p>\r\n<p>xx</p>","pageId":799,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":810,"lock":null}
20:13:19.239 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/21/859
20:13:19.239 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":859,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty morning Been a delightful fall of snow in the night. Blowing fresh at NWW. Attended morning Service; a collection was made for the singers &pound;9.6 received. Dined at home. Being a fine sea tide a great many ships got to sea among them the Hope. Dined at home &amp; went to afternoon service. Afternoon walked to Tynemouth In the evening at the Duke of York</p>","pageId":800,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":811,"lock":null}
20:13:19.239 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.239 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/21/859
20:13:19.239 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":859,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty morning Been a delightful fall of snow in the night. Blowing fresh at NWW. Attended morning Service; a collection was made for the singers &pound;9.6 received. Dined at home. Being a fine sea tide a great many ships got to sea among them the Hope. Dined at home &amp; went to afternoon service. Afternoon walked to Tynemouth In the evening at the Duke of York</p>","pageId":800,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":811,"lock":null}
20:13:19.239 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/22/860
20:13:19.239 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":860,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A countenance of severe frost. &amp; NW wind. Payed 5/- for the Hope's foy boat. Having a cold &amp; Pain in my side, took physician &amp; remained in the house. Dined at home At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; spent the evening at home.</p>","pageId":800,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":812,"lock":null}
20:13:19.239 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.240 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/22/860
20:13:19.240 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":860,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A countenance of severe frost. &amp; NW wind. Payed 5/- for the Hope's foy boat. Having a cold &amp; Pain in my side, took physician &amp; remained in the house. Dined at home At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; spent the evening at home.</p>","pageId":800,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":812,"lock":null}
20:13:19.240 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/23/861
20:13:19.240 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":861,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull weather morning Having been a great deal of snow during the night but now a thaw Wind SE. Several light vessels off the harbour. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; spent the evening at home.</p>","pageId":800,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":813,"lock":null}
20:13:19.240 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.240 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/23/861
20:13:19.240 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":861,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull weather morning Having been a great deal of snow during the night but now a thaw Wind SE. Several light vessels off the harbour. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; spent the evening at home.</p>","pageId":800,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":813,"lock":null}
20:13:19.240 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/24/862
20:13:19.240 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":862,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind W by N Went to South Shields &amp; saw Salmon who was not persuaded to give in the money, but promised to send it over tomorrow. Dined at home. In the afternoon at the billiard room &amp; spent the evening at home</p>","pageId":800,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":814,"lock":null}
