20:13:19.243 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":866,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A mild morning Rather dull; been a great deal of rain in the night. Wind NW. Went to church in the morning. A rainy afternoon. Dined with I Judy At the Mulstream</p>","pageId":801,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":818,"lock":null}
20:13:19.243 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/3/841
20:13:19.243 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":841,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still very cold and frosty and A good deal of snow on the ground Wind about East blowing fresh. Received from Robert and paid into Chapmans &pound;86 rents. Gave Mrs Scott a draft for her quarter annuity &pound;75. Mrs Dixon down I returned with her in the carriage to Barton. Dined &amp; stayed all night.</p>","pageId":795,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":793,"lock":null}
20:13:19.243 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.243 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/3/841
20:13:19.243 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":841,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still very cold and frosty and A good deal of snow on the ground Wind about East blowing fresh. Received from Robert and paid into Chapmans &pound;86 rents. Gave Mrs Scott a draft for her quarter annuity &pound;75. Mrs Dixon down I returned with her in the carriage to Barton. Dined &amp; stayed all night.</p>","pageId":795,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":793,"lock":null}
20:13:19.243 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/4/842
20:13:19.243 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":842,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning (wind NW), Frosty with a show of showers. After Breakfast Dixon &amp; I had the beagles out &amp; started above base which We left them running &amp; walked Into Newcastle &amp; not being able to get anything for the Hope, I got into a gig &amp; came down to Shields Dined with the whist club at the Commercial, spent a pleasant day In the evening at the Card club and Afterwards at the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":796,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":794,"lock":null}
20:13:19.243 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.244 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/4/842
20:13:19.244 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":842,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning (wind NW), Frosty with a show of showers. After Breakfast Dixon &amp; I had the beagles out &amp; started above base which We left them running &amp; walked Into Newcastle &amp; not being able to get anything for the Hope, I got into a gig &amp; came down to Shields Dined with the whist club at the Commercial, spent a pleasant day In the evening at the Card club and Afterwards at the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":796,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":794,"lock":null}
20:13:19.244 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/5/843
20:13:19.244 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":843,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuum of Winter weather with snow showers Wind East S E blowing fresh. Stayed at home at 2 o'clock at the billiard room after dinner. After tea walked upto Tynemouth &amp; spent the evening with Capt French at the Castle. Played a few rubbers at whist &amp; lost</p>","pageId":796,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":795,"lock":null}
