20:13:19.250 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/3/15/881
20:13:19.250 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":881,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet morning, wind SE Afterwards changed to SW &amp; blowing fresh with fine weather. Brought a large fleet down amongst them the Hope. Dixon &amp; his aid Tom Smith Mrs Yellowley &amp; Emma came down to attend the funeral which took place between 12 &amp; 1 o'clock. Captain Caudisson of the 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment kindly allowing the hearse and carriages to enter the castle ...</p>","pageId":804,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":833,"lock":null}
20:13:19.250 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
