20:13:19.253 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":886,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another boisterous day blowing a hurricane at about W by N Walked up to the Hope. Dined at home. After dinner went to the George to settle the damage done to the Commerce of Whitby referred it to A French &amp; H Walker who awarded the owner of the Commerce (Mr Wood) &pound;4 which I paid him. After which we had A few bottles of port. At the Mulstrum house in the Evening</p>","pageId":806,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":838,"lock":null}
20:13:19.253 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/3/2/868
20:13:19.253 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":868,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A delightful spring day, quite warm weather. Went up to Newcastle by stream. The Courts so crowded could not get in. Dined &amp; stayed all night with D Dixon Tom Smith &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Hnoises</span> there</p>","pageId":802,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":820,"lock":null}
