20:13:19.254 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":887,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but blowing fresh at WNW. Norman &amp; I went by steam to Newcastle. Called at Dixons, Mr Loathinby's for the Dined &amp; stayed all night at Dixons</p>","pageId":806,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":839,"lock":null}
20:13:19.254 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/3/21/888
20:13:19.254 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":888,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning Wind WNW. After breakfast &amp; having some conversation with Dixon respecting the will Fanny Smith consort to be embarked on board a steamer &amp; got to <span class=highlight_yellow>DSguases</span> about of &frac12; past 1 o'clock &amp; had our dinner; found Mary Cary there, having got down the night before</p>","pageId":807,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":840,"lock":null}
