20:13:19.261 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":897,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Rather a dull morning. Wind ENE. Dined with a party at H Harrys invitation at Roddany &amp; spent a pleasant day</p>","pageId":808,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":849,"lock":null}
20:13:19.261 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/3/31/898
20:13:19.261 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":898,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind WNW bun a great day of dunny this night. Wind and off to the NE &amp; very cold. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined with the vicar a pleasant day.</p>","pageId":808,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":850,"lock":null}
20:13:19.261 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.261 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/3/31/898
20:13:19.261 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":898,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind WNW bun a great day of dunny this night. Wind and off to the NE &amp; very cold. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined with the vicar a pleasant day.</p>","pageId":808,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":850,"lock":null}
20:13:19.261 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/3/4/870
20:13:19.261 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":870,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Most extraordinary Fine weather. Wind about South. Took a walk with A Nicholson round by Preston &amp; Tynmouth. Dined with A Harry on board the Choice &amp; in the Evening at the Whist Club</p>","pageId":802,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":822,"lock":null}
20:13:19.261 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.262 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/3/4/870
20:13:19.262 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":870,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Most extraordinary Fine weather. Wind about South. Took a walk with A Nicholson round by Preston &amp; Tynmouth. Dined with A Harry on board the Choice &amp; in the Evening at the Whist Club</p>","pageId":802,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":822,"lock":null}
20:13:19.262 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/3/5/871
20:13:19.262 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":871,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine morning, rather Frosty. Wind SW. Sent an answer to Mr Anderson's letter. Hope Club stating the Hope being laid up between 20 Dec &amp; 20 Feb Went with H Harry &amp; the H Pemberton of Quebec to Sunderland. Called upon Capt Bunbury of the 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment &amp; returned to dine with H Harry at 5 o'clock A small party to <span class=highlight_yellow>mubt</span> Mrs Pemberton. attended Mrs Heddill's evening party. Received a letter from WBS confirming the of the sale of the Hope's cargo at 29/6 A miserable price, about 6/6 <span class=highlight_yellow>pecght</span> Shall lose I dare say between &pound;30 &amp; &pound;40</p>","pageId":802,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":823,"lock":null}
20:13:19.262 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.262 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/3/5/871
20:13:19.262 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":871,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine morning, rather Frosty. Wind SW. Sent an answer to Mr Anderson's letter. Hope Club stating the Hope being laid up between 20 Dec &amp; 20 Feb Went with H Harry &amp; the H Pemberton of Quebec to Sunderland. Called upon Capt Bunbury of the 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment &amp; returned to dine with H Harry at 5 o'clock A small party to <span class=highlight_yellow>mubt</span> Mrs Pemberton. attended Mrs Heddill's evening party. Received a letter from WBS confirming the of the sale of the Hope's cargo at 29/6 A miserable price, about 6/6 <span class=highlight_yellow>pecght</span> Shall lose I dare say between &pound;30 &amp; &pound;40</p>","pageId":802,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":823,"lock":null}
20:13:19.262 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/3/6/872
20:13:19.262 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":872,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A duller foggy morning. Wind SW.  <del>Afterwards got to the L&amp;E</del> <del>Cold accompanied</del> Took a walk with Captain Webb to Tynemouth. Dined with Nicholson a party spent a very Pleasant day &amp; in the evening Attended the Whist Club at I Dales</p>","pageId":802,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":824,"lock":null}
20:13:19.262 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.263 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/3/6/872
20:13:19.263 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":872,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A duller foggy morning. Wind SW.  <del>Afterwards got to the L&amp;E</del> <del>Cold accompanied</del> Took a walk with Captain Webb to Tynemouth. Dined with Nicholson a party spent a very Pleasant day &amp; in the evening Attended the Whist Club at I Dales</p>","pageId":802,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":824,"lock":null}
20:13:19.263 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/3/7/873
20:13:19.263 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":873,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A foggy morning. Wind NE. Afterwards changed to SE &amp; fine clear weather. Went to Church in the morning. Mr Pemberton accompanied me. I was engaged to dine with I Tealey today but on my return from Church. I found that Mrs Scott was so much poorer &amp; her death expected every moment. I sent an apology. She expired precisely at 9 o'clock without a struggle</p>","pageId":802,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":825,"lock":null}
20:13:19.263 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.263 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/3/7/873
20:13:19.263 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":873,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A foggy morning. Wind NE. Afterwards changed to SE &amp; fine clear weather. Went to Church in the morning. Mr Pemberton accompanied me. I was engaged to dine with I Tealey today but on my return from Church. I found that Mrs Scott was so much poorer &amp; her death expected every moment. I sent an apology. She expired precisely at 9 o'clock without a struggle</p>","pageId":802,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":825,"lock":null}
20:13:19.263 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/3/8/874
20:13:19.263 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":874,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather Frosty. Wind  SSW. Emma G came From school. Mrs Dixon down &amp; Took Emma to N Coatts with her. Wrote to WBS: BBG: &amp; A <span class=highlight_yellow>Deighera</span> of Mrs Scotts death. Kept the house all day.</p>","pageId":803,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":826,"lock":null}
