20:13:19.266 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":908,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A thick damp morning. Wind WNW Walk with J Tinley to Newcastle. WBS &amp; Mary Carf went up in Dunn's coach Torrents of rain the whole day after our arrival. Dined &amp; stayed all night at A Dixon</p>","pageId":811,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":860,"lock":null}
20:13:19.266 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/4/11/909
20:13:19.266 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":909,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind SW. Embarked on board a steam boat at 10 o'clock and returned to Shields. Dined at home. After dinner walked with A Harry to Cullercoat Sands. About a dozen tents erected &amp; a great many people there. Met W E Wrights &amp; adjourned with him to Spencer's where we had some wine. At the Mulstrum in the evening.</p>","pageId":811,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":861,"lock":null}
20:13:19.266 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
