20:13:19.268 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":911,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind changed about during the day. Dined early, the Decghtow called  &amp; dined with us &amp; in the afternoon Harry &amp; I walked to the races, a great many people there being so beautiful a day. The rest of the party went to hear the choral society at the church. In the evening A H &amp; I went to the Ball . Very few people there, Mr Craig behind very ill. He took offence at something &amp; having a strong ...</p>","pageId":811,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":863,"lock":null}
20:13:19.268 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/4/13/912
20:13:19.268 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":912,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":13,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... party consisting of the <span class=highlight_yellow>Joblary</span> &amp; he took them all away, which prevented the remainder of the company, being too few, having any dancing. Craig it appears took the party with much of the gentlemen to his own house &amp; prevailing upon the musicians to accompany him. May these had a dance. But that would be expected from a fellow brought up behind a counter ! the filles ! place for him.</p>","pageId":812,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":864,"lock":null}
20:13:19.268 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
