20:13:19.275 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":917,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning Wind WNW. Went to church Rev Mark did duty &amp; gave us an excellent sermon I Tenby &amp; I walked to Tynemouth &amp; I afterwards dined with him, Mr Mark with us</p>","pageId":813,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":869,"lock":null}
20:13:19.275 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/4/19/918
20:13:19.275 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":918,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning blowing fresh from SW. A letter came for Captain Jameson of the London which I sent by one of the Hopes boys to the ship at Bewick <span class=highlight_yellow>oCrasters</span> spout. Dined at home, H Harry came in &amp; took wine with him &amp; in the evening he Captain Webb &amp; Peash Frantook of a cockle supper with us.</p>","pageId":813,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":870,"lock":null}
