20:13:19.284 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":928,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A countenance of beautiful weather. Wind ESE. Took a walk to Tynemouth with <span class=highlight_yellow>Lt H</span><span class=highlight_yellow>arry</span>. Dined at home. Onboard the John Dunn in the evening with I <span class=highlight_yellow>Wesglot</span> &amp; afterwards at the Duke of York.</p>","pageId":815,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":880,"lock":null}
20:13:19.284 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/4/3/901
20:13:19.284 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":901,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A stormy morning with heavy showers of snow. A great deal having fallen during the night. Wind ENE. Dined at home. Emma G: came from school to us. In the evening attended the whist club at Mrs Creigs. And asked the club to come to me on Thursday</p>","pageId":809,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":853,"lock":null}
20:13:19.284 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.285 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/4/3/901
20:13:19.285 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":901,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A stormy morning with heavy showers of snow. A great deal having fallen during the night. Wind ENE. Dined at home. Emma G: came from school to us. In the evening attended the whist club at Mrs Creigs. And asked the club to come to me on Thursday</p>","pageId":809,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":853,"lock":null}
20:13:19.285 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/4/30/929
20:13:19.285 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":929,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Most beautiful weather. Wind ESE. Went by Steamer to Newcastle could get nothing for the Hope. Dined with D Dixon, a party Tom Smith, Mr Busqter; they all went to the theater to see Liston, I looked in but did not remain long, the house very full for his benefit. Got into a gig &amp; returned to Shields</p>","pageId":815,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":881,"lock":null}
20:13:19.285 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.285 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/4/30/929
20:13:19.285 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":929,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Most beautiful weather. Wind ESE. Went by Steamer to Newcastle could get nothing for the Hope. Dined with D Dixon, a party Tom Smith, Mr Busqter; they all went to the theater to see Liston, I looked in but did not remain long, the house very full for his benefit. Got into a gig &amp; returned to Shields</p>","pageId":815,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":881,"lock":null}
20:13:19.285 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/4/4/902
20:13:19.285 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":902,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty morning wind NW. Emma Mary Carfs &amp; went to church. Heard a funeral sermon from Mr Mark who held the service. The Vicars father being dead &amp; also young Mrs Read he died in London of the gout in the head &amp; after two days illness. Dined at home &amp; afternoon walked with H Henry to Tynemouth. In the evening at <span class=highlight_yellow>n</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ews</span><span class=highlight_yellow> r</span><span class=highlight_yellow>oo</span><span class=highlight_yellow>m</span> &amp; H Harry's</p>","pageId":809,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":854,"lock":null}
20:13:19.285 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.286 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/4/4/902
20:13:19.286 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":902,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty morning wind NW. Emma Mary Carfs &amp; went to church. Heard a funeral sermon from Mr Mark who held the service. The Vicars father being dead &amp; also young Mrs Read he died in London of the gout in the head &amp; after two days illness. Dined at home &amp; afternoon walked with H Henry to Tynemouth. In the evening at <span class=highlight_yellow>n</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ews</span><span class=highlight_yellow> r</span><span class=highlight_yellow>oo</span><span class=highlight_yellow>m</span> &amp; H Harry's</p>","pageId":809,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":854,"lock":null}
20:13:19.286 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/4/5/903
20:13:19.286 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":903,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another frosty morning blowing fresh at NW Dined at home</p>","pageId":809,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":855,"lock":null}
20:13:19.286 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.286 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/4/5/903
20:13:19.286 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":903,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another frosty morning blowing fresh at NW Dined at home</p>","pageId":809,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":855,"lock":null}
20:13:19.286 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/4/6/904
20:13:19.286 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":904,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Mild weather &amp; blowing fresh from the WNW. Saw Brown about his continuancy in the George. He is to give us an address by Thursday Took the steam boat &amp; went to Newcastle Could not get anything for the Hope Lunched with A Weyhtos &amp; at 3 o'clock called in Westgate Street. I found Mrs Dixon just arrived from Brenbuch &amp; Joys Cow Dined &amp; stayed all night with them</p>","pageId":810,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":856,"lock":null}
20:13:19.286 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.287 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/4/6/904
20:13:19.287 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":904,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Mild weather &amp; blowing fresh from the WNW. Saw Brown about his continuancy in the George. He is to give us an address by Thursday Took the steam boat &amp; went to Newcastle Could not get anything for the Hope Lunched with A Weyhtos &amp; at 3 o'clock called in Westgate Street. I found Mrs Dixon just arrived from Brenbuch &amp; Joys Cow Dined &amp; stayed all night with them</p>","pageId":810,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":856,"lock":null}
20:13:19.287 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/4/7/905
20:13:19.287 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":905,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Milder weather. Wind SW. WBS came up to Newcastle. We lunched in Westgate Street &amp; afterward returned to Shields by steam. Dined at home. In the evening A Harry &amp; I at the Duke</p>","pageId":810,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":857,"lock":null}
20:13:19.287 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.287 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/4/7/905
20:13:19.287 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":905,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Milder weather. Wind SW. WBS came up to Newcastle. We lunched in Westgate Street &amp; afterward returned to Shields by steam. Dined at home. In the evening A Harry &amp; I at the Duke</p>","pageId":810,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":857,"lock":null}
20:13:19.287 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/4/8/906
20:13:19.287 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":906,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather. Wind SW. A dull morning, the glass down &amp; evening appearance of rain Saw Brown who declined taking the George again excepting at a very great reduction of rent he offered &pound;50 a year. Dined at home. The Saturdays nights whist club spent the evening with me. Heavy showers during the day &amp; much thunder &amp; lightening in the evening. A number of light ships arrived</p>","pageId":810,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":858,"lock":null}
20:13:19.287 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.288 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/4/8/906
20:13:19.288 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":906,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather. Wind SW. A dull morning, the glass down &amp; evening appearance of rain Saw Brown who declined taking the George again excepting at a very great reduction of rent he offered &pound;50 a year. Dined at home. The Saturdays nights whist club spent the evening with me. Heavy showers during the day &amp; much thunder &amp; lightening in the evening. A number of light ships arrived</p>","pageId":810,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":858,"lock":null}
20:13:19.288 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/4/9/907
20:13:19.288 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":907,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning after a great deal of rain. Wind SE. Walked with A Henry to Tynemouth. Dined at home. Took another walk in the afternoon with A Harry down by Dr Drury's garden. In the evening at the Duke of York</p>","pageId":810,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":859,"lock":null}
20:13:19.289 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
