20:13:19.290 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":938,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather. Wind East blowing fresh &amp; heavy sea. Lower ladder off its put back left Shields </p>","pageId":817,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":890,"lock":null}
20:13:19.290 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/10/939
20:13:19.290 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":939,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":10,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>at &frac12; past 8 o'clock. Got the Alnwick coach at Newcastle at 10 o'clock and reached Alnwick at 3. Mr &amp; Mrs Ilderstow there in the carriage &amp; took me out to Leamington to dinner</p>","pageId":818,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":891,"lock":null}
20:13:19.290 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.291 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/10/939
20:13:19.291 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":939,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":10,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>at &frac12; past 8 o'clock. Got the Alnwick coach at Newcastle at 10 o'clock and reached Alnwick at 3. Mr &amp; Mrs Ilderstow there in the carriage &amp; took me out to Leamington to dinner</p>","pageId":818,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":891,"lock":null}
20:13:19.291 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/11/940
20:13:19.291 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":940,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still blowing fresh from the NE &amp; cold. Robert &amp; Tom I Ldestow &amp; I started after breakfast to fish in the Alm, but had bad sport &amp; river busy sheet &amp; cold weather</p>","pageId":818,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":892,"lock":null}
20:13:19.291 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.291 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/11/940
20:13:19.291 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":940,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still blowing fresh from the NE &amp; cold. Robert &amp; Tom I Ldestow &amp; I started after breakfast to fish in the Alm, but had bad sport &amp; river busy sheet &amp; cold weather</p>","pageId":818,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":892,"lock":null}
20:13:19.291 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/12/941
20:13:19.291 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":941,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fairer and warmer weather. Robert Ilderstow &amp; I had an early breakfast &amp; rode over the river till below Hedghey, where we fished until it began to rain when we took shelter at a mill &amp; then walked up to Rosea an estate of the Ildestonn's.  Had tea &amp; eggs &amp; rode home in the evening, when we found Mrs Crosby &amp; Mrs Strothard had arrived from Newcastle on a visit. Had better sport today, brought home a few good trout</p>","pageId":818,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":893,"lock":null}
20:13:19.291 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.292 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/12/941
20:13:19.292 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":941,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fairer and warmer weather. Robert Ilderstow &amp; I had an early breakfast &amp; rode over the river till below Hedghey, where we fished until it began to rain when we took shelter at a mill &amp; then walked up to Rosea an estate of the Ildestonn's.  Had tea &amp; eggs &amp; rode home in the evening, when we found Mrs Crosby &amp; Mrs Strothard had arrived from Newcastle on a visit. Had better sport today, brought home a few good trout</p>","pageId":818,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":893,"lock":null}
20:13:19.292 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/13/942
20:13:19.292 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":942,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather again. Wind about SW. After breakfast we went to fish in the Ala Had fair sport &amp; got home to dinner. Spent a quiet evening</p>","pageId":819,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":894,"lock":null}
20:13:19.292 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.292 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/13/942
20:13:19.292 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":942,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather again. Wind about SW. After breakfast we went to fish in the Ala Had fair sport &amp; got home to dinner. Spent a quiet evening</p>","pageId":819,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":894,"lock":null}
20:13:19.292 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/14/943
20:13:19.292 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":943,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine day. Wind much the same. Again went &amp; fished in the Alm. Not such good sport. Returned to dinner found Mrs Forston of Alnwick there, who fed  with us. Got a letter from WBS.</p>","pageId":819,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":895,"lock":null}
20:13:19.292 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.293 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/14/943
20:13:19.293 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":943,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine day. Wind much the same. Again went &amp; fished in the Alm. Not such good sport. Returned to dinner found Mrs Forston of Alnwick there, who fed  with us. Got a letter from WBS.</p>","pageId":819,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":895,"lock":null}
20:13:19.293 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/15/944
20:13:19.293 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":944,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up in the morning at 5 o'clock &amp; after having some bread &amp; milk, started on horseback to fish in Breamish, starting from the Powburn &amp; leaving off at Ingram, caught a dog trout but very small. Got home to dinner before 5 o'clock very tired</p>","pageId":819,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":896,"lock":null}
20:13:19.293 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
