20:13:19.295 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":948,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine day. Amused ourselves this morning in shooting rooks. Rode over to Broom Park to call upon Mr Burrell, not at home.</p>","pageId":820,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":900,"lock":null}
20:13:19.295 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/2/931
20:13:19.296 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":931,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind West. Tom Smith &amp; I went to Church. Afterwards called at Mrs Marr's who would not let Emma go up to Newcastle to see Bell Smith. The King by Lodges paper a little better back still in a very precarious start. Dined at home. Pscous to which I Smith left. Walk to Tynemouth in the afternoon &amp; took wine &amp; tea with Libbs</p>","pageId":816,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":883,"lock":null}
