20:13:19.303 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":959,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":29,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... &amp; continued showering all day. Got upon Dunns coach at 4 o'clock &amp; arrived at home a little after 5 o'clock to dinner. Received a letter from <span class=highlight_yellow>l</span><span class=highlight_yellow>o</span><span class=highlight_yellow>r</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ss</span>. That my friend A Harry &amp; A Nicholson the latter the first time since his parried <span class=highlight_yellow>extect</span><span class=highlight_yellow> </span><span class=highlight_yellow>es</span> captain his ship the Tenacity having foundered in the North Sea &amp; he &amp; the crew taken aboard on <span class=highlight_yellow>gallcot</span> that <span class=highlight_yellow>Cuekerly</span> hove in sights before dark. Spent the evening together with Mr Com <span class=highlight_yellow>Hewesion</span> at the Duke of York</p>","pageId":822,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":911,"lock":null}
20:13:19.303 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/3/932
20:13:19.303 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":932,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine morning. Wind about West. By Steam to Newcastle but did not find the Hope to load coal for Dublin as intended as they could not load her before they did of much works. Returned to Dinner on board the Choice in the afternoon. Drank tea with H Harry &amp; In the evening at the Duke of York</p>","pageId":816,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":884,"lock":null}
20:13:19.303 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.304 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/3/932
20:13:19.304 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":932,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine morning. Wind about West. By Steam to Newcastle but did not find the Hope to load coal for Dublin as intended as they could not load her before they did of much works. Returned to Dinner on board the Choice in the afternoon. Drank tea with H Harry &amp; In the evening at the Duke of York</p>","pageId":816,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":884,"lock":null}
20:13:19.304 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/30/960
20:13:19.304 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":960,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather. Wind about West. Icy cold having flown to the locns suffering some pain. Got Robert to sub the park with <span class=highlight_yellow>opadildoc</span>, took a <span class=highlight_yellow>scidlily</span> &amp; did not go to church. Wrote a long letter to ABP Emma G: came over to see us. Dined at home &amp; in the afternoon A Harry &amp; I walked up to North Sheilds to take wine</p>","pageId":822,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":912,"lock":null}
20:13:19.304 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.304 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/30/960
20:13:19.304 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":960,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather. Wind about West. Icy cold having flown to the locns suffering some pain. Got Robert to sub the park with <span class=highlight_yellow>opadildoc</span>, took a <span class=highlight_yellow>scidlily</span> &amp; did not go to church. Wrote a long letter to ABP Emma G: came over to see us. Dined at home &amp; in the afternoon A Harry &amp; I walked up to North Sheilds to take wine</p>","pageId":822,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":912,"lock":null}
20:13:19.304 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/31/961
20:13:19.304 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":961,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind NSW Blowing hard. Sent my letter off to WBS. Gave a draft on estate then 4 on after  for &pound;50 for ABS. Crew also from &pound;10.10s + &pound;16.3.8 = 27.3.8 for av wages ...</p>","pageId":822,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":913,"lock":null}
20:13:19.304 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.305 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/31/961
20:13:19.305 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":961,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind NSW Blowing hard. Sent my letter off to WBS. Gave a draft on estate then 4 on after  for &pound;50 for ABS. Crew also from &pound;10.10s + &pound;16.3.8 = 27.3.8 for av wages ...</p>","pageId":822,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":913,"lock":null}
20:13:19.305 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/31/962
20:13:19.305 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":962,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":31,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... Hope &amp; Liberal club. A Harry, A Nicholson &amp; Richardson NP took 1 o'clock dinner with me &amp; we afterwards crossed the water to South Shields Races, but it came on such a stormy afternoon we could not do the sport</p>","pageId":823,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":914,"lock":null}
20:13:19.305 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.306 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/31/962
20:13:19.306 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":962,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":31,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... Hope &amp; Liberal club. A Harry, A Nicholson &amp; Richardson NP took 1 o'clock dinner with me &amp; we afterwards crossed the water to South Shields Races, but it came on such a stormy afternoon we could not do the sport</p>","pageId":823,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":914,"lock":null}
20:13:19.306 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/4/933
20:13:19.306 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":933,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of most beautiful weather with a West wind. Turned out at 6 o'clock &amp; took a long walk round by Cullercoat Sands &amp; before breakfast. And afterwards Webb, Mark &amp; I took a walk along the hard sand where I made a sketch of Tynmouth Castle be. Returned home to dinner. In the evening at the Duke of York</p>","pageId":817,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":885,"lock":null}
20:13:19.306 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.306 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/4/933
20:13:19.306 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":933,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of most beautiful weather with a West wind. Turned out at 6 o'clock &amp; took a long walk round by Cullercoat Sands &amp; before breakfast. And afterwards Webb, Mark &amp; I took a walk along the hard sand where I made a sketch of Tynmouth Castle be. Returned home to dinner. In the evening at the Duke of York</p>","pageId":817,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":885,"lock":null}
20:13:19.306 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/5/934
20:13:19.306 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":934,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Glorious weather. Wind very variable between SE &amp; W. Went to Newcastle by steam. Gave up the Dublin charter &amp; returned home to dinner. A Harry took a bottle of port with us &amp; I gave him an order to fix the Hope for anchorage &amp; Hull dealers at &pound;4.7.6 At the Duke of York in the evening</p>","pageId":817,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":886,"lock":null}
20:13:19.306 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.307 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/5/934
20:13:19.307 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":934,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Glorious weather. Wind very variable between SE &amp; W. Went to Newcastle by steam. Gave up the Dublin charter &amp; returned home to dinner. A Harry took a bottle of port with us &amp; I gave him an order to fix the Hope for anchorage &amp; Hull dealers at &pound;4.7.6 At the Duke of York in the evening</p>","pageId":817,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":886,"lock":null}
20:13:19.307 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/7/935
20:13:19.307 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":935,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Delightful weather. Wind East &amp; SE. Walked beyond Marsden Rocks with Webb, Gosling RNW To see <span class=highlight_yellow>exfrenements</span> laid for saving shipwrecked men, my means of a rope ladder &amp; air jacket. Returned home to dinner. Webb &amp; Gosling dinned with us. Afterwards walked to Tynemouth &amp; spent the evening at Webb </p>","pageId":817,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":887,"lock":null}
20:13:19.307 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.307 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/7/935
20:13:19.307 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":935,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Delightful weather. Wind East &amp; SE. Walked beyond Marsden Rocks with Webb, Gosling RNW To see <span class=highlight_yellow>exfrenements</span> laid for saving shipwrecked men, my means of a rope ladder &amp; air jacket. Returned home to dinner. Webb &amp; Gosling dinned with us. Afterwards walked to Tynemouth &amp; spent the evening at Webb </p>","pageId":817,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":887,"lock":null}
20:13:19.307 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/8/936
20:13:19.307 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":936,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull think morning with wind SE blowing fresh. Dined with I Finely, met char Nicholas &amp; in the evening went to the whist club at I Newghts. A very stormy night, a gale of wind at ESE with torrents of rain. Gabe Stephenson a debt on Chapmans for &pound;30 &amp; got &pound;5 for self. Gave G Stafs &pound;1 on account of wages</p>","pageId":817,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":888,"lock":null}
20:13:19.307 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.308 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/8/936
20:13:19.308 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":936,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull think morning with wind SE blowing fresh. Dined with I Finely, met char Nicholas &amp; in the evening went to the whist club at I Newghts. A very stormy night, a gale of wind at ESE with torrents of rain. Gabe Stephenson a debt on Chapmans for &pound;30 &amp; got &pound;5 for self. Gave G Stafs &pound;1 on account of wages</p>","pageId":817,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":888,"lock":null}
20:13:19.308 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/9/937
20:13:19.308 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":937,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>All last night marsh dismal &amp; stormy blowing a gale of wind at ESE with a deluge of rain &amp; still continuous Did not go to church. Employed myself in writing to WBS &amp; G Farell. Gave Stephenson a draft upon Chapmans exors at &pound;14.11.7 ( &pound;5 cook + &pound;9.11.7 Balance of after) Dined with a Harry. Called on Webb in the evening who had gout a which prevents him going to Mr Aldertons At the Duke of York in evening. Weather <span class=highlight_yellow>inade</span><span class=highlight_yellow>s</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ater</span></p>","pageId":817,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":889,"lock":null}
20:13:19.308 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.308 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/9/937
20:13:19.308 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":937,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>All last night marsh dismal &amp; stormy blowing a gale of wind at ESE with a deluge of rain &amp; still continuous Did not go to church. Employed myself in writing to WBS &amp; G Farell. Gave Stephenson a draft upon Chapmans exors at &pound;14.11.7 ( &pound;5 cook + &pound;9.11.7 Balance of after) Dined with a Harry. Called on Webb in the evening who had gout a which prevents him going to Mr Aldertons At the Duke of York in evening. Weather <span class=highlight_yellow>inade</span><span class=highlight_yellow>s</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ater</span></p>","pageId":817,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":889,"lock":null}
20:13:19.308 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/6/1/963
20:13:19.308 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":963,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind blowing fresh at SW. A Harry, Nicholson took a walk around Tynmouth &amp; at 2 o'clock dined with I Richardson MP at 4 o'clock. We crossed the water to attend the races which were all won easy by chamber horses. Got home at 10 o'clock</p>","pageId":823,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":915,"lock":null}
20:13:19.308 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.308 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/6/1/963
20:13:19.308 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":963,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind blowing fresh at SW. A Harry, Nicholson took a walk around Tynmouth &amp; at 2 o'clock dined with I Richardson MP at 4 o'clock. We crossed the water to attend the races which were all won easy by chamber horses. Got home at 10 o'clock</p>","pageId":823,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":915,"lock":null}
20:13:19.308 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/6/15/972
20:13:19.308 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":972,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull unpleasant morning Blowing fresh from the north with rain Which continued in torrents &amp; without ceasing the whole day &amp; a gale of wind. Dined at home &amp; in the evening at the Duke of York</p>","pageId":826,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":924,"lock":null}
20:13:19.308 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.308 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/6/15/972
20:13:19.308 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":972,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull unpleasant morning Blowing fresh from the north with rain Which continued in torrents &amp; without ceasing the whole day &amp; a gale of wind. Dined at home &amp; in the evening at the Duke of York</p>","pageId":826,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":924,"lock":null}
20:13:19.308 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/6/16/973
20:13:19.308 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":973,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A stormy morning blowing a gale at about N by E It has never ceased raining since yesterday morning. Still coming down in torrents. I fear it will do great harm to the country. Turned out fair about the middle of the day, but still very cold &amp; stormy Dined at home. At the Duke of York in the evening</p>","pageId":826,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":925,"lock":null}
20:13:19.308 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.310 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/6/16/973
20:13:19.310 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":973,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A stormy morning blowing a gale at about N by E It has never ceased raining since yesterday morning. Still coming down in torrents. I fear it will do great harm to the country. Turned out fair about the middle of the day, but still very cold &amp; stormy Dined at home. At the Duke of York in the evening</p>","pageId":826,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":925,"lock":null}
20:13:19.310 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/6/17/974
20:13:19.310 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":974,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fair weather after a great deal of rain in the night but still blowing hard at NE &amp; cold Received a letter &amp; notes from ABS. Took a walk around by Cullercoat Fields &amp; Tynemouth. Found Mrs Dixon at the house on my return. Dined at home &amp; in the evening again walked to Tynemouth. Finished at the Duke of York</p>","pageId":826,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":926,"lock":null}
20:13:19.310 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.310 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/6/17/974
20:13:19.310 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":974,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fair weather after a great deal of rain in the night but still blowing hard at NE &amp; cold Received a letter &amp; notes from ABS. Took a walk around by Cullercoat Fields &amp; Tynemouth. Found Mrs Dixon at the house on my return. Dined at home &amp; in the evening again walked to Tynemouth. Finished at the Duke of York</p>","pageId":826,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":926,"lock":null}
20:13:19.310 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/6/18/975
20:13:19.310 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":975,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another wet morning Wind West. Walked to Tynemouth after breakfast &amp; saw the soldiers parading. Returned by the fields. Dined at home. Wrote to Fanny Smith that Emma would meet his at Morpeth on Thursday next. Paid monthly money for the Hope to do which I drew on Chapmans for &pound;20. Turned out a wet evening &amp; at bed time it was a deluge</p>","pageId":826,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":927,"lock":null}
20:13:19.310 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.311 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/6/18/975
20:13:19.311 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":975,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another wet morning Wind West. Walked to Tynemouth after breakfast &amp; saw the soldiers parading. Returned by the fields. Dined at home. Wrote to Fanny Smith that Emma would meet his at Morpeth on Thursday next. Paid monthly money for the Hope to do which I drew on Chapmans for &pound;20. Turned out a wet evening &amp; at bed time it was a deluge</p>","pageId":826,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":927,"lock":null}
20:13:19.311 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/6/19/976
20:13:19.311 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":976,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather but still showering. Wind NW. Paid Ned's mother yesterday a quarter wages &pound;1.13.9 &amp; lent Mary Carfs &pound;2. Dined at home. Wrote to WBS &amp; sent him the last search account. Joined a party at Roddames &amp; spent the evening</p>","pageId":827,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":928,"lock":null}
20:13:19.311 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.311 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/6/19/976
20:13:19.312 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":976,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather but still showering. Wind NW. Paid Ned's mother yesterday a quarter wages &pound;1.13.9 &amp; lent Mary Carfs &pound;2. Dined at home. Wrote to WBS &amp; sent him the last search account. Joined a party at Roddames &amp; spent the evening</p>","pageId":827,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":928,"lock":null}
20:13:19.312 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/6/2/964
20:13:19.312 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":964,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful day, particularly the afternoon. Wind west, Took a walk with Captain Webb to Tynemouth. Met Smiths, Hannah, I Weston. Webb took her &amp; the <span class=highlight_yellow>Blenkensops</span> on board the <span class=highlight_yellow>Mers</span><span class=highlight_yellow>er</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ard</span> Tatter, laying too off the Castle &amp; gave them a few hours sail to the Sunderland. Dined at home &amp; the afternoon being so fine tempted H Harry, for the sake of the walk to go to the tents on the sands but there was no racing. One match</p>","pageId":823,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":916,"lock":null}
20:13:19.312 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.312 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/6/2/964
20:13:19.312 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":964,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful day, particularly the afternoon. Wind west, Took a walk with Captain Webb to Tynemouth. Met Smiths, Hannah, I Weston. Webb took her &amp; the <span class=highlight_yellow>Blenkensops</span> on board the <span class=highlight_yellow>Mers</span><span class=highlight_yellow>er</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ard</span> Tatter, laying too off the Castle &amp; gave them a few hours sail to the Sunderland. Dined at home &amp; the afternoon being so fine tempted H Harry, for the sake of the walk to go to the tents on the sands but there was no racing. One match</p>","pageId":823,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":916,"lock":null}
20:13:19.312 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/6/20/977
20:13:19.312 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":977,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but still cloudy with the appearance of showers wind NNW.  Walked  to Tynemouth. Dined at home. Went to church in the afternoon. Drank tea with A Harry, again walked to Tynemouth to hear the band. A great many people there. Returned &amp; had a glass of whisky toddy with A Harry</p>","pageId":827,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":929,"lock":null}
20:13:19.312 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.313 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/6/20/977
20:13:19.313 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":977,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but still cloudy with the appearance of showers wind NNW.  Walked  to Tynemouth. Dined at home. Went to church in the afternoon. Drank tea with A Harry, again walked to Tynemouth to hear the band. A great many people there. Returned &amp; had a glass of whisky toddy with A Harry</p>","pageId":827,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":929,"lock":null}
20:13:19.313 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/6/21/978
20:13:19.313 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":978,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy morning with a cold NE wind. Went over to South Shields to see Salmon. He was not at home. Dined at home &amp; afterwards A harry Ltd French &amp; I went up to the Point &amp; took wine with Sadler</p>","pageId":827,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":930,"lock":null}
20:13:19.313 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.313 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/6/21/978
20:13:19.313 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":978,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy morning with a cold NE wind. Went over to South Shields to see Salmon. He was not at home. Dined at home &amp; afterwards A harry Ltd French &amp; I went up to the Point &amp; took wine with Sadler</p>","pageId":827,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":930,"lock":null}
20:13:19.313 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/6/22/979
20:13:19.313 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":979,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning wind NE  with showers. H Harry, French &amp; I went up to Newcastle in a steam boat. Walked out to the race course. Very little company there. The running very good. Dined at the Stand &amp;  got to Shields again in a gig by the country road at 9 o'clock</p>","pageId":827,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":931,"lock":null}
20:13:19.313 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.313 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/6/22/979
20:13:19.313 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":979,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning wind NE  with showers. H Harry, French &amp; I went up to Newcastle in a steam boat. Walked out to the race course. Very little company there. The running very good. Dined at the Stand &amp;  got to Shields again in a gig by the country road at 9 o'clock</p>","pageId":827,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":931,"lock":null}
