20:13:19.335 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":991,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":7,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind SE. Walked to Tynemouth. Much to my surprise met with Mrs Lumley and Mrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Bcagdon</span> who had arrived by sea. The long <span class=highlight_yellow>gifore</span>. Dined at home &amp; in the afternoon Webb Hopkins the boy &amp; I went in a boat to fish but had no sport, weather unpleasant &amp; thick.</p>","pageId":830,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":942,"lock":null}
20:13:19.335 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/7/30/1018
20:13:19.335 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1018,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":7,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning, rather thick, wind East. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home. Cleaned up and turned out excessively hot. A little rain in the evening which brought the wind round to NW. Some lightning</p>","pageId":838,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":969,"lock":null}
