20:13:19.353 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1048,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":8,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy morning. Been rain in the night. Wind N to NE &amp; WNW. Turned out a very fine day. Received a letter from J Chapman. William and I went out with our guns &amp; walked to Marsden Rock by the sands. Got to the top of the rock, a man having made steps up. Got a lunch there &amp; on our way home took a few glasses of punch with the sea breeze &amp; Phasine Society who has <span class=highlight_yellow>this tent</span> pitched on the cliffs.</p>","pageId":844,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":996,"lock":null}
20:13:19.353 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/8/27/1049
20:13:19.353 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1049,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":8,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. A little wind at SE with showers. Mr Mark, William &amp; I went in a chaise to Whitby Park &amp; dined with Mr J Wright. Turned out very wet night</p>","pageId":845,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":997,"lock":null}
20:13:19.353 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.353 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/8/27/1049
20:13:19.353 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1049,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":8,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. A little wind at SE with showers. Mr Mark, William &amp; I went in a chaise to Whitby Park &amp; dined with Mr J Wright. Turned out very wet night</p>","pageId":845,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":997,"lock":null}
20:13:19.353 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/8/28/1050
20:13:19.353 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1050,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":8,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A wet morning having been a deluge of rain in the night &amp; blowing hard from NE. Wind changed to NW &amp; nearly calm. After breakfast turned out a very fair day. Emma came from school. WBS went to Newcastle to see D Dixon. Moor &amp; his brother called, after a great deal of conversation, agreed to let him continue on the farm should he exert himself to pay off the arrears. His brother promised his <span class=highlight_yellow>abstinence</span> &amp; to continue his security. Emma &amp; I walked round by the wells to Tynemouth. Dined at home at 5 o'clock. At the Duke in the evening.</p>","pageId":845,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":998,"lock":null}
20:13:19.353 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
