20:13:19.361 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/9/11/1064
20:13:19.361 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1064,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind WNW. HMS Cordelia sailed. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home</p>","pageId":848,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1012,"lock":null}
20:13:19.361 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.362 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/9/11/1064
20:13:19.362 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1064,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind WNW. HMS Cordelia sailed. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home</p>","pageId":848,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1012,"lock":null}
20:13:19.362 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/9/12/1065
20:13:19.362 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1065,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull rainy morning. Very heavy rain during the night &amp; blowing hard from the SSE. At church in the morning. Dined at home. H Harry &amp; I walked to Tynemouth in the afternoon. Saw the Hope off <span class=highlight_yellow>Sonter</span>. She soon got into the harbour. Went on board &amp; saw Stephenson. At the Duke &amp; Malstrum in the evening</p>","pageId":848,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1013,"lock":null}
20:13:19.362 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.362 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/9/12/1065
20:13:19.362 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1065,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull rainy morning. Very heavy rain during the night &amp; blowing hard from the SSE. At church in the morning. Dined at home. H Harry &amp; I walked to Tynemouth in the afternoon. Saw the Hope off <span class=highlight_yellow>Sonter</span>. She soon got into the harbour. Went on board &amp; saw Stephenson. At the Duke &amp; Malstrum in the evening</p>","pageId":848,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1013,"lock":null}
20:13:19.362 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/9/13/1066
20:13:19.362 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1066,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind N by E. Got up early &amp; went by steam to Newcastle. Fixed the Hope with <span class=highlight_yellow>Hindhaegh</span> at 10/3 freight. Got home to dinner. Took wine at the George with French &amp; Harry. Drank tea at H Harry's &amp; in the evening at the Duke.</p>","pageId":848,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1014,"lock":null}
20:13:19.362 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.363 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/9/13/1066
20:13:19.363 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1066,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind N by E. Got up early &amp; went by steam to Newcastle. Fixed the Hope with <span class=highlight_yellow>Hindhaegh</span> at 10/3 freight. Got home to dinner. Took wine at the George with French &amp; Harry. Drank tea at H Harry's &amp; in the evening at the Duke.</p>","pageId":848,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1014,"lock":null}
20:13:19.363 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/9/14/1067
20:13:19.363 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1067,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Been rain in the night &amp; has the appearance of more wind SW. Went up to the ship. Walked to Tynemouth. Ordered a new square mainsail. Got the canvas of Bradshaw &amp; to be made by Mrs Brown Polly of Wallsend. J Carr, H Harry &amp; French dined with me. Spent a very pleasant day. At the Mulstrum in the evening</p>","pageId":848,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1015,"lock":null}
20:13:19.363 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.364 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/9/14/1067
20:13:19.364 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1067,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Been rain in the night &amp; has the appearance of more wind SW. Went up to the ship. Walked to Tynemouth. Ordered a new square mainsail. Got the canvas of Bradshaw &amp; to be made by Mrs Brown Polly of Wallsend. J Carr, H Harry &amp; French dined with me. Spent a very pleasant day. At the Mulstrum in the evening</p>","pageId":848,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1015,"lock":null}
20:13:19.364 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/9/15/1068
20:13:19.364 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1068,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind SW. Walked up to the Hope alongside <span class=highlight_yellow>gran</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span> getting ballast out. Got her down up the shore at Metcalf dock to sink her to find out the peak. Walked to Tynemouth, saw Potts, who returned with me to Shields. He, Harry, French &amp; I  went to the Albion &amp; Mulstrum</p>","pageId":849,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1016,"lock":null}
20:13:19.364 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.364 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/9/15/1068
20:13:19.364 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1068,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind SW. Walked up to the Hope alongside <span class=highlight_yellow>gran</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span> getting ballast out. Got her down up the shore at Metcalf dock to sink her to find out the peak. Walked to Tynemouth, saw Potts, who returned with me to Shields. He, Harry, French &amp; I  went to the Albion &amp; Mulstrum</p>","pageId":849,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1016,"lock":null}
20:13:19.364 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/9/16/1069
20:13:19.364 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1069,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. A fresh breeze from the West. The Hope upon the shore having been sank did not find any bad places of consequence. The buts ends bolts been in a great many places corroded &amp; heavily worn was the principal cause of her making so much water. Employed getting new bolts put in &amp; the buts ends caulked. Dined at Home. Spent the afternoon at Dr Drury's garden playing at quoits &amp; the evening at the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":849,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1017,"lock":null}
20:13:19.364 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.365 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/9/16/1069
20:13:19.365 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1069,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. A fresh breeze from the West. The Hope upon the shore having been sank did not find any bad places of consequence. The buts ends bolts been in a great many places corroded &amp; heavily worn was the principal cause of her making so much water. Employed getting new bolts put in &amp; the buts ends caulked. Dined at Home. Spent the afternoon at Dr Drury's garden playing at quoits &amp; the evening at the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":849,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1017,"lock":null}
20:13:19.365 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/9/17/1070
20:13:19.365 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1070,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning Wind WSW. Went down to the Hope. The starboard side as bad as the other. A number of the bolts bad. Walked to Tynemouth. Saw Potts hounds run a trail. Dined on board the Hope. I Dale, Harry French &amp; I took wine at the George &amp; spent a pleasant afternoon at the Mulstrum in the evening</p>","pageId":849,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1018,"lock":null}
20:13:19.365 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.365 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/9/17/1070
20:13:19.365 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1070,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning Wind WSW. Went down to the Hope. The starboard side as bad as the other. A number of the bolts bad. Walked to Tynemouth. Saw Potts hounds run a trail. Dined on board the Hope. I Dale, Harry French &amp; I took wine at the George &amp; spent a pleasant afternoon at the Mulstrum in the evening</p>","pageId":849,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1018,"lock":null}
20:13:19.365 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/9/18/1071
20:13:19.365 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1071,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful morning. Wind NW. Onboard the Hope. Got two keels of <span class=highlight_yellow>wqlaure</span> down. Pain G Slop &pound;3.11.3 wages up to today. Dined at home. H Henry &amp; I on board the Hope to taste some brandy. In the evening at the Albion</p>","pageId":849,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1019,"lock":null}
20:13:19.365 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.366 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/9/18/1071
20:13:19.366 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1071,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful morning. Wind NW. Onboard the Hope. Got two keels of <span class=highlight_yellow>wqlaure</span> down. Pain G Slop &pound;3.11.3 wages up to today. Dined at home. H Henry &amp; I on board the Hope to taste some brandy. In the evening at the Albion</p>","pageId":849,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1019,"lock":null}
20:13:19.366 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/9/19/1072
20:13:19.366 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1072,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning with a little rain. Wind SW, increased in the afternoon to a gale. Attended morning service. The vicar did duty &amp; preached. Dined at home. Took wine with H Harry &amp; tea in the evening at the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":849,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1020,"lock":null}
20:13:19.366 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.366 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/9/19/1072
20:13:19.366 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1072,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning with a little rain. Wind SW, increased in the afternoon to a gale. Attended morning service. The vicar did duty &amp; preached. Dined at home. Took wine with H Harry &amp; tea in the evening at the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":849,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1020,"lock":null}
20:13:19.366 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/9/2/1055
20:13:19.366 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1055,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Been a great deal of rain in the night &amp; still continuous heavy wind SW. Borrowed &pound;300 of Chapman's upon WBS &amp; I are named executors to pay bills &amp; for Mrs Scott's executors, funeral etc. Dined at home. In the evening there was a total eclipse of the moon</p>","pageId":846,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1003,"lock":null}
20:13:19.366 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.367 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/9/2/1055
20:13:19.367 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1055,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Been a great deal of rain in the night &amp; still continuous heavy wind SW. Borrowed &pound;300 of Chapman's upon WBS &amp; I are named executors to pay bills &amp; for Mrs Scott's executors, funeral etc. Dined at home. In the evening there was a total eclipse of the moon</p>","pageId":846,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1003,"lock":null}
20:13:19.367 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/9/20/1073
20:13:19.367 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1073,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>It has blown a gale of wind all night at SW &amp; continuing. The Suffolk Hull steamer was driven upon the rock in coming in last night. Walked to the rock to see the Suffolk. No chance of getting her off. Afterwards walked up to Sadlers at the Point to dinner &amp; spent a pleasant day at the Malstrum in the evening. Got our <span class=highlight_yellow>buf</span> for the ship this morning</p>","pageId":849,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1021,"lock":null}
20:13:19.367 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.367 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/9/20/1073
20:13:19.367 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1073,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>It has blown a gale of wind all night at SW &amp; continuing. The Suffolk Hull steamer was driven upon the rock in coming in last night. Walked to the rock to see the Suffolk. No chance of getting her off. Afterwards walked up to Sadlers at the Point to dinner &amp; spent a pleasant day at the Malstrum in the evening. Got our <span class=highlight_yellow>buf</span> for the ship this morning</p>","pageId":849,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1021,"lock":null}
20:13:19.367 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/9/21/1074
20:13:19.367 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1074,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A rainy morning but calmer weather. Wind SW. J Drury &amp; Allen dined with me on board the Hope. Got five keels down</p>","pageId":849,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1022,"lock":null}
20:13:19.367 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
