20:13:19.377 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1062,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A wet morning. Wind SSW. A great many ships got to sea. Dreadful weather for the farmers, being heavy all day. Harry Cunningham &amp; I after dinner went to the George &amp; enjoyed ourselves over a jug or two of punch &amp; oysters. Called in at the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":847,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1010,"lock":null}
