20:13:19.382 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/16/1194
20:13:19.382 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1194,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of foggy weather. Wind SW. Did not go to church as Mr Burdan was to sit in our pew to try how he liked it before he would determine upon taking it. Dined at home. Dr Drury &amp; friends came in &amp; took a glass of wine with me. In the evening at the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":877,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1140,"lock":null}
20:13:19.382 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/17/1195
20:13:19.382 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1195,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still very unpleasant foggy weather. Wind SSW. Received a letter from WBS. Sent him a copy of Chapmans book for the last quarter, also gave him authority to apply to the Duke for a commission in the Northumbria Militia. Dined at home. Wind freshened at SE &amp; every appearance of bad weather.</p>","pageId":877,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1141,"lock":null}
20:13:19.382 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.383 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/17/1195
20:13:19.383 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1195,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still very unpleasant foggy weather. Wind SSW. Received a letter from WBS. Sent him a copy of Chapmans book for the last quarter, also gave him authority to apply to the Duke for a commission in the Northumbria Militia. Dined at home. Wind freshened at SE &amp; every appearance of bad weather.</p>","pageId":877,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1141,"lock":null}
20:13:19.383 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/18/1196
20:13:19.383 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1196,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very damp foggy morning. Wind fresh at SE &amp; a good deal of sea. Dined at 5 o'clock with the Gastling RA Tynemouth Place. A very pleasant party. Got home before1 o'clock in the morning. Gave notes to the Premium &amp; Hope clubs of the Hope being loaded. Leadbetter went to Newcastle</p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1142,"lock":null}
20:13:19.383 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.383 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/18/1196
20:13:19.383 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1196,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very damp foggy morning. Wind fresh at SE &amp; a good deal of sea. Dined at 5 o'clock with the Gastling RA Tynemouth Place. A very pleasant party. Got home before1 o'clock in the morning. Gave notes to the Premium &amp; Hope clubs of the Hope being loaded. Leadbetter went to Newcastle</p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1142,"lock":null}
20:13:19.383 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/19/1197
20:13:19.383 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1197,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp &amp; foggy weather. Still continuing with a SE wind. <span class=highlight_yellow>Signed</span> the <span class=highlight_yellow>book</span> for the Hope's <span class=highlight_yellow>cassign</span> of <span class=highlight_yellow>oxd</span>. <span class=highlight_yellow>Redheangh</span> for &pound;153.18.8 date 14<sup>th</sup> Jan at 60 days on WBS. Leadbetter not having returned from Newcastle. Robert &amp; I dined on board the Hope. At the Albion in the evening. Leadbetter got home in the evening.</p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1143,"lock":null}
20:13:19.383 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.384 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/19/1197
20:13:19.384 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1197,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp &amp; foggy weather. Still continuing with a SE wind. <span class=highlight_yellow>Signed</span> the <span class=highlight_yellow>book</span> for the Hope's <span class=highlight_yellow>cassign</span> of <span class=highlight_yellow>oxd</span>. <span class=highlight_yellow>Redheangh</span> for &pound;153.18.8 date 14<sup>th</sup> Jan at 60 days on WBS. Leadbetter not having returned from Newcastle. Robert &amp; I dined on board the Hope. At the Albion in the evening. Leadbetter got home in the evening.</p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1143,"lock":null}
20:13:19.384 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/2/1179
20:13:19.384 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1179,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull and unpleasant damp morning.  Wind SW.  Walked down to Shields.  Dined with H Harry in the evening. At the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":873,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1126,"lock":null}
20:13:19.384 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.384 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/2/1179
20:13:19.384 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1179,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull and unpleasant damp morning.  Wind SW.  Walked down to Shields.  Dined with H Harry in the evening. At the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":873,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1126,"lock":null}
20:13:19.384 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/20/1198
20:13:19.384 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1198,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very rainy &amp; foggy day &amp; blowing strong from SE &amp; high sea. Sent the bill for the Hope's cargo by Dunn the <span class=highlight_yellow>coach</span><span class=highlight_yellow>man</span> to Mr Heindhaigh. Received a letter from Margaret Scott of Crathorn, I having forgot to send her 20/- her quarters allowance. Sent it by return of post. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; the whist club in the evening. Drew upon Chapman for &pound;5</p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1144,"lock":null}
20:13:19.384 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.385 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/20/1198
20:13:19.385 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1198,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very rainy &amp; foggy day &amp; blowing strong from SE &amp; high sea. Sent the bill for the Hope's cargo by Dunn the <span class=highlight_yellow>coach</span><span class=highlight_yellow>man</span> to Mr Heindhaigh. Received a letter from Margaret Scott of Crathorn, I having forgot to send her 20/- her quarters allowance. Sent it by return of post. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; the whist club in the evening. Drew upon Chapman for &pound;5</p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1144,"lock":null}
20:13:19.385 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/21/1199
20:13:19.385 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1199,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning blowing hard &amp; has been all night from the E by S &amp; ESE with a heavy sea. On board the Hope. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; the Albion &amp; Mulstrum in the evening. Gave Bess a turn, <u>first time</u><span class=underline_double> since</span></p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1145,"lock":null}
20:13:19.385 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.385 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/21/1199
20:13:19.385 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1199,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning blowing hard &amp; has been all night from the E by S &amp; ESE with a heavy sea. On board the Hope. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; the Albion &amp; Mulstrum in the evening. Gave Bess a turn, <u>first time</u><span class=underline_double> since</span></p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1145,"lock":null}
20:13:19.385 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/22/1200
20:13:19.385 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1200,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A deluge of rain this morning. Wind about East with a heavy sea. Went by Dunn's coach to Newcastle. Dined &amp; stayed all night at D Dixons. Mentioned to him my having applied to the Duke for a commission in the North<font color=#BFBFBF>umbria</font> militia of which he approved</p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1146,"lock":null}
20:13:19.385 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.385 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/22/1200
20:13:19.385 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1200,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A deluge of rain this morning. Wind about East with a heavy sea. Went by Dunn's coach to Newcastle. Dined &amp; stayed all night at D Dixons. Mentioned to him my having applied to the Duke for a commission in the North<font color=#BFBFBF>umbria</font> militia of which he approved</p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1146,"lock":null}
20:13:19.385 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/23/1201
20:13:19.385 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1201,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather. For the first time for many days we have seen the sun. Wind ENE &amp; cold with showers. Left Dixon's after breakfast took the steam boat &amp; returned to Shields to dinner. Emma Galbraith looking much better. No letter from WBS, disappointed. At the Mulstrum in the evening.</p>","pageId":879,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1147,"lock":null}
20:13:19.385 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.386 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/23/1201
20:13:19.386 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1201,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather. For the first time for many days we have seen the sun. Wind ENE &amp; cold with showers. Left Dixon's after breakfast took the steam boat &amp; returned to Shields to dinner. Emma Galbraith looking much better. No letter from WBS, disappointed. At the Mulstrum in the evening.</p>","pageId":879,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1147,"lock":null}
20:13:19.386 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/24/1202
20:13:19.386 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1202,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Been a slight frost with a little snow during the night. Wind NW. Sea much fallen, so that I think many ships will get to sea.</p>\r\n<p>Received a letter from WBS with copies of letters written to the Duke &amp; Lord Beverley applying for a commission for me in the North<font color=#BFBFBF>umbria</font> Militia. Answered his letter.</p>\r\n<p>Wrote to <span class=highlight_yellow>Bevor's</span> brother to come down to Shields to make some arrangements with regard to the <span class=highlight_yellow>fasern</span> after seeing J Tinley upon the subject.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home. Spent the evening &amp; suppered with H Harry.</p>","pageId":879,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1148,"lock":null}
20:13:19.386 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.386 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/24/1202
20:13:19.387 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1202,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Been a slight frost with a little snow during the night. Wind NW. Sea much fallen, so that I think many ships will get to sea.</p>\r\n<p>Received a letter from WBS with copies of letters written to the Duke &amp; Lord Beverley applying for a commission for me in the North<font color=#BFBFBF>umbria</font> Militia. Answered his letter.</p>\r\n<p>Wrote to <span class=highlight_yellow>Bevor's</span> brother to come down to Shields to make some arrangements with regard to the <span class=highlight_yellow>fasern</span> after seeing J Tinley upon the subject.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home. Spent the evening &amp; suppered with H Harry.</p>","pageId":879,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1148,"lock":null}
20:13:19.387 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/25/1203
20:13:19.387 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1203,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine wintery morning having been a very heavy fall of snow during the night. Wind WNW.</p>\r\n<p>Received a letter from B B Galbraith. A bill for &pound;6.0.10 drawn by <span class=highlight_yellow>Stodter</span> of the Eligible club presented for payment, but I did not take it up having no notice. Dined at 5 o'clock with J Dale &amp; in the evening attended the ball at the George which was the best we have had for a long time. Got home at &frac14; past 3 o'clock</p>","pageId":879,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1149,"lock":null}
20:13:19.387 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.387 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/25/1203
20:13:19.387 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1203,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine wintery morning having been a very heavy fall of snow during the night. Wind WNW.</p>\r\n<p>Received a letter from B B Galbraith. A bill for &pound;6.0.10 drawn by <span class=highlight_yellow>Stodter</span> of the Eligible club presented for payment, but I did not take it up having no notice. Dined at 5 o'clock with J Dale &amp; in the evening attended the ball at the George which was the best we have had for a long time. Got home at &frac14; past 3 o'clock</p>","pageId":879,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1149,"lock":null}
20:13:19.387 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/26/1204
20:13:19.387 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1204,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of sharp frost. Wind NNW. Very little additional snow fallen in the night. Went by Dunn's coach to Newcastle, there being a meeting of the <span class=highlight_yellow>leiabenantcy</span> &amp; saw Dixon who promised to speak to Captain <span class=highlight_yellow>Carlson</span> respecting a commission for me in the military. <span class=highlight_yellow>Had</span> some dinner with Emma Galbraith &amp; returned by Duna in the afternoon.</p>\r\n<p>Eat a couple of mutton chops at 6 o'clock &amp; finished in the evening at the Albion</p>","pageId":880,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1150,"lock":null}
20:13:19.387 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.387 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/26/1204
20:13:19.387 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1204,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of sharp frost. Wind NNW. Very little additional snow fallen in the night. Went by Dunn's coach to Newcastle, there being a meeting of the <span class=highlight_yellow>leiabenantcy</span> &amp; saw Dixon who promised to speak to Captain <span class=highlight_yellow>Carlson</span> respecting a commission for me in the military. <span class=highlight_yellow>Had</span> some dinner with Emma Galbraith &amp; returned by Duna in the afternoon.</p>\r\n<p>Eat a couple of mutton chops at 6 o'clock &amp; finished in the evening at the Albion</p>","pageId":880,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1150,"lock":null}
20:13:19.387 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/27/1205
20:13:19.387 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1205,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning &amp; every appearance of snow or sleet &amp; looking as if it would thaw. Wind about west. The ship preparing for sea. Received a note from D Dixon stating he had seen Colonel Coulson &amp; that there are several commissions vacant &amp; I must apply through Colonel Coulson.</p>\r\n<p>Accepted a bill for &pound;8.17 the <span class=highlight_yellow>prccuccia</span> for the present voyage: due 27<sup>th</sup> April dated 18 Jan at 9 months.</p>\r\n<p>Gave Mr Brown of the George Tavern a <span class=highlight_yellow>signature</span> written notice to quit on the 1<sup>st</sup> Aug next.</p>\r\n<p>On board the Hope. Got a steam boat which towed her to sea with fine NW wind.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; the whist club I the evening. The wind got round &amp; blew hard from the NE &amp; brought on a heavy sea &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>remained</span> thaw during the whole of the day.</p>","pageId":880,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1151,"lock":null}
20:13:19.387 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.388 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/27/1205
20:13:19.388 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1205,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning &amp; every appearance of snow or sleet &amp; looking as if it would thaw. Wind about west. The ship preparing for sea. Received a note from D Dixon stating he had seen Colonel Coulson &amp; that there are several commissions vacant &amp; I must apply through Colonel Coulson.</p>\r\n<p>Accepted a bill for &pound;8.17 the <span class=highlight_yellow>prccuccia</span> for the present voyage: due 27<sup>th</sup> April dated 18 Jan at 9 months.</p>\r\n<p>Gave Mr Brown of the George Tavern a <span class=highlight_yellow>signature</span> written notice to quit on the 1<sup>st</sup> Aug next.</p>\r\n<p>On board the Hope. Got a steam boat which towed her to sea with fine NW wind.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; the whist club I the evening. The wind got round &amp; blew hard from the NE &amp; brought on a heavy sea &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>remained</span> thaw during the whole of the day.</p>","pageId":880,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1151,"lock":null}
20:13:19.388 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/28/1206
20:13:19.388 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1206,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A very fine frosty morning. Wind NW. Wrote to Colonel Coalson applying for a commission. Took a walk round by Tynemouth. Dined at home. At billiard room latter in the afternoon &amp; abbey in the evening</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":881,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1152,"lock":null}
20:13:19.388 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.389 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/28/1206
20:13:19.389 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1206,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A very fine frosty morning. Wind NW. Wrote to Colonel Coalson applying for a commission. Took a walk round by Tynemouth. Dined at home. At billiard room latter in the afternoon &amp; abbey in the evening</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":881,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1152,"lock":null}
20:13:19.389 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/29/1207
20:13:19.389 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1207,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine winter's morning. Slight frost &amp; been a great deal of snow during the night &amp; appearance of more. Wind NW.</p> <p></p> <p>Went by Durrer's coach to Newcastle &amp; took Robert with me. Tom, Ann &amp; Bell Smith at D Dixons. Tom Dixon &amp; I called at Leadbetters The attorneys &amp; I settled with them as Mrs Scott's executor giving them a draft on Chapmans on WBS &amp; JRS executors account for &pound;108.19.5 which with other payments we have made, leaves only &pound;702 due from us, of the &pound;1000 left under Mrs Scott's will. Robert &amp; Leadbetters received their legacies. Called twice on Colonel Coulson, not at home. Met him afterwards in the street &amp; had some conversation with him as to my application for a commission.</p> <p></p> <p>Dined with Mrs Dixon. The whole party excepting myself went to a concert. I called &amp; saw Mr Weatherly &amp; by his advice afterwards called upon Mr Turnbull, deputy clerk of the Peace, but he was not at home.</p> <p></p> <p>Suppered at Dixons &amp; slept at the <span class=highlight_yellow>Jessop</span> Hotel</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":881,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1153,"lock":null}
20:13:19.389 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.390 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/29/1207
20:13:19.390 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1207,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine winter's morning. Slight frost &amp; been a great deal of snow during the night &amp; appearance of more. Wind NW.</p> <p></p> <p>Went by Durrer's coach to Newcastle &amp; took Robert with me. Tom, Ann &amp; Bell Smith at D Dixons. Tom Dixon &amp; I called at Leadbetters The attorneys &amp; I settled with them as Mrs Scott's executor giving them a draft on Chapmans on WBS &amp; JRS executors account for &pound;108.19.5 which with other payments we have made, leaves only &pound;702 due from us, of the &pound;1000 left under Mrs Scott's will. Robert &amp; Leadbetters received their legacies. Called twice on Colonel Coulson, not at home. Met him afterwards in the street &amp; had some conversation with him as to my application for a commission.</p> <p></p> <p>Dined with Mrs Dixon. The whole party excepting myself went to a concert. I called &amp; saw Mr Weatherly &amp; by his advice afterwards called upon Mr Turnbull, deputy clerk of the Peace, but he was not at home.</p> <p></p> <p>Suppered at Dixons &amp; slept at the <span class=highlight_yellow>Jessop</span> Hotel</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":881,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1153,"lock":null}
20:13:19.390 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/3/1180
20:13:19.390 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1180,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Most unpleasant weather, damp &amp; uncomfortable. Wind SW. Received a letter yesterday from Stephenson of the ship being out on Thursday delivering 282 char &amp; expecting to get his ballast on Saturday. Received the Hope's <span class=highlight_yellow>afsales</span> with a balance note for &pound;93.7. which I paid into Chapmans &amp; drew for &pound;50 with which I paid the bells for the Archangel voyage viz: swan &pound;___ sharp &pound;___ &amp; spares &pound;___. At the theatre in the evening, Michaels benefit. A good house.</p>","pageId":873,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1127,"lock":null}
20:13:19.390 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.390 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/3/1180
20:13:19.390 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1180,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Most unpleasant weather, damp &amp; uncomfortable. Wind SW. Received a letter yesterday from Stephenson of the ship being out on Thursday delivering 282 char &amp; expecting to get his ballast on Saturday. Received the Hope's <span class=highlight_yellow>afsales</span> with a balance note for &pound;93.7. which I paid into Chapmans &amp; drew for &pound;50 with which I paid the bells for the Archangel voyage viz: swan &pound;___ sharp &pound;___ &amp; spares &pound;___. At the theatre in the evening, Michaels benefit. A good house.</p>","pageId":873,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1127,"lock":null}
20:13:19.390 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/30/1208
20:13:19.390 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1208,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine morning &amp; hard frost. Wind NW. Breakfasted at Dixons.</p> <p></p> <p>Afterwards called &amp; saw Mr Turnball who wrote out my declaration of qualifications which I signed &amp; which he will deliver to Mr Thorp the clerk of the Peace tomorrow.</p> <p></p> <p>Called upon &amp; saw Colonel Coulson who was with Captain Bigg &amp; told him what I had done &amp; had some conversation with them. He of course will immediately apply for a captain's course for me which will most likely come down in the course of the work, as the military is to go into training immediately.</p> <p></p> <p>Returned to Shields by steam &amp; dined at home at 2 o'clock. H Harry &amp; Nicholson took wine with me in the afternoon &amp; in the evening I walked to the Mulstrum. Received a letter from WBS</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":882,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1154,"lock":null}
20:13:19.390 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.391 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/30/1208
20:13:19.391 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1208,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine morning &amp; hard frost. Wind NW. Breakfasted at Dixons.</p> <p></p> <p>Afterwards called &amp; saw Mr Turnball who wrote out my declaration of qualifications which I signed &amp; which he will deliver to Mr Thorp the clerk of the Peace tomorrow.</p> <p></p> <p>Called upon &amp; saw Colonel Coulson who was with Captain Bigg &amp; told him what I had done &amp; had some conversation with them. He of course will immediately apply for a captain's course for me which will most likely come down in the course of the work, as the military is to go into training immediately.</p> <p></p> <p>Returned to Shields by steam &amp; dined at home at 2 o'clock. H Harry &amp; Nicholson took wine with me in the afternoon &amp; in the evening I walked to the Mulstrum. Received a letter from WBS</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":882,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1154,"lock":null}
20:13:19.391 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/31/1209
20:13:19.391 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1209,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A frosty morning. Rather <span class=highlight_yellow>damp</span> with a fall of snow. Wind NW. Dined at home. Received a letter from B B Galbraith &amp; answered it &amp; also WBS's. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; Albion in the evening.</p> <p></p> <p>During the afternoon the wind got round to SW, S by W. At night blew fresh at S by E &amp; still frosty.</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":882,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1155,"lock":null}
20:13:19.391 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.392 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/31/1209
20:13:19.392 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1209,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A frosty morning. Rather <span class=highlight_yellow>damp</span> with a fall of snow. Wind NW. Dined at home. Received a letter from B B Galbraith &amp; answered it &amp; also WBS's. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; Albion in the evening.</p> <p></p> <p>During the afternoon the wind got round to SW, S by W. At night blew fresh at S by E &amp; still frosty.</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":882,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1155,"lock":null}
20:13:19.392 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/4/1181
20:13:19.392 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1181,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp day. Wind ___. Dined at home. The Saturday night whist club with me in the evening. Kept it up till &frac12; past 2 o'clock in the morning</p>","pageId":874,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1128,"lock":null}
20:13:19.392 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
