20:13:19.410 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1498,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind SW. A great many ships sailed. The Hope came down below to load. Got some damage done by the painter. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined with Tom Jobling at Mrs Atkinson.</p>\r\n<p>Quarrelled with Bess</p>","pageId":957,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1444,"lock":null}
20:13:19.410 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/29/1499
20:13:19.410 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1499,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful morning. Wind SW. Took a long walk with Mark to Tynemouth, Cullercoat Sands &amp; dined with Joblings at the George at 4 o'clock</p>","pageId":957,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1445,"lock":null}
20:13:19.410 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.411 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/29/1499
20:13:19.411 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1499,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful morning. Wind SW. Took a long walk with Mark to Tynemouth, Cullercoat Sands &amp; dined with Joblings at the George at 4 o'clock</p>","pageId":957,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1445,"lock":null}
20:13:19.411 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/3/1473
20:13:19.411 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1473,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned the hands up about 5 o'clock being low water &amp; the wind at SSW I got up before 6 o'clock. The people busy getting the anchor &amp; setting sails. Had a fine run during the day down <span class=highlight_yellow>swin</span>, studding sails set but not much wind which varied between <span class=highlight_yellow>SE</span> &amp; S by W. At &frac12; past 8 o'clock at night off Aldeburgh &amp; beautiful clear weather but a strong flood tide against us. Turned in about 9 o'clock</p>","pageId":949,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1419,"lock":null}
20:13:19.411 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.411 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/3/1473
20:13:19.411 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1473,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned the hands up about 5 o'clock being low water &amp; the wind at SSW I got up before 6 o'clock. The people busy getting the anchor &amp; setting sails. Had a fine run during the day down <span class=highlight_yellow>swin</span>, studding sails set but not much wind which varied between <span class=highlight_yellow>SE</span> &amp; S by W. At &frac12; past 8 o'clock at night off Aldeburgh &amp; beautiful clear weather but a strong flood tide against us. Turned in about 9 o'clock</p>","pageId":949,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1419,"lock":null}
20:13:19.411 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/30/1500
20:13:19.411 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1500,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of mild weather. Wind SW.</p>\r\n<p>After breakfast took a walk to Tynemouth &amp; went to church in the afternoon, again walked to Tynemouth. Jobling dined with me at 5 o'clock. Reconciled with <font color=#BFBFBF>Bess</font></p>","pageId":957,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1446,"lock":null}
20:13:19.411 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.412 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/30/1500
20:13:19.412 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1500,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of mild weather. Wind SW.</p>\r\n<p>After breakfast took a walk to Tynemouth &amp; went to church in the afternoon, again walked to Tynemouth. Jobling dined with me at 5 o'clock. Reconciled with <font color=#BFBFBF>Bess</font></p>","pageId":957,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1446,"lock":null}
20:13:19.412 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/31/1501
20:13:19.412 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1501,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind West. After breakfast walked to Tynemouth &amp; with others. Amused ourselves on Cullercoat Sands practicing ball firing. Dined at home at 5 o'clock.</p>\r\n<p>Wrote to Mr Archer last night the owner of the planter to meet me at 11 o'clock on Tuesday morning to survey the damage.</p>\r\n<p>With Bess at night.</p>","pageId":957,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1447,"lock":null}
20:13:19.412 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.412 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/31/1501
20:13:19.412 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1501,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind West. After breakfast walked to Tynemouth &amp; with others. Amused ourselves on Cullercoat Sands practicing ball firing. Dined at home at 5 o'clock.</p>\r\n<p>Wrote to Mr Archer last night the owner of the planter to meet me at 11 o'clock on Tuesday morning to survey the damage.</p>\r\n<p>With Bess at night.</p>","pageId":957,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1447,"lock":null}
20:13:19.412 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/4/1474
20:13:19.412 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1474,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at 12 o'clock am. The ship then running with a fresh breeze at SW for the <span class=highlight_yellow>Newrope</span> light which we passed about 1 o'clock &amp; ran through Hasbrough Gateway. Turned into my crib again before 2 o'clock I awoke or rather disturbed at 5 o'clock by a tremendous squall at SW a little to the south w of Cromer with heavy rise. It took us suddenly &amp; without any warning &amp; therefore with all sails standing that they had great difficulty in taking them in. However they succeeded at last in taking them without losing anything, which considering the violence of the squall was fortunate. When they had double reefed the topsails &amp; made all snug I again went to bed. Got up at 8 o'clock still blowing hard from the WSW. We were then abreast of the Dadgrow floating light. It continued to blow fresh all the morning varying between WSW &amp; W by N. After dinner Nicholson &amp; I turned in &amp; had a good snooze until &frac12; past 4 o'clock where we found Flamborough in sight distant probably about 15 miles. Wind &amp; sea very much fallen, but still a fine light breeze from about WSW. All reefs out, top gallant <del>sails set</del> &amp; fore topmast studding sails set. Passed Flamborough Head at 8 o'clock, a most beautiful night. At 9 o'clock we had a glass of grog &amp; I afterwards walked the deck with Nicholson till 12 o'clock when we turned in.</p>","pageId":950,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1420,"lock":null}
20:13:19.412 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.413 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/4/1474
20:13:19.413 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1474,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at 12 o'clock am. The ship then running with a fresh breeze at SW for the <span class=highlight_yellow>Newrope</span> light which we passed about 1 o'clock &amp; ran through Hasbrough Gateway. Turned into my crib again before 2 o'clock I awoke or rather disturbed at 5 o'clock by a tremendous squall at SW a little to the south w of Cromer with heavy rise. It took us suddenly &amp; without any warning &amp; therefore with all sails standing that they had great difficulty in taking them in. However they succeeded at last in taking them without losing anything, which considering the violence of the squall was fortunate. When they had double reefed the topsails &amp; made all snug I again went to bed. Got up at 8 o'clock still blowing hard from the WSW. We were then abreast of the Dadgrow floating light. It continued to blow fresh all the morning varying between WSW &amp; W by N. After dinner Nicholson &amp; I turned in &amp; had a good snooze until &frac12; past 4 o'clock where we found Flamborough in sight distant probably about 15 miles. Wind &amp; sea very much fallen, but still a fine light breeze from about WSW. All reefs out, top gallant <del>sails set</del> &amp; fore topmast studding sails set. Passed Flamborough Head at 8 o'clock, a most beautiful night. At 9 o'clock we had a glass of grog &amp; I afterwards walked the deck with Nicholson till 12 o'clock when we turned in.</p>","pageId":950,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1420,"lock":null}
20:13:19.413 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/5/1475
20:13:19.413 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1475,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>We were disturbed again this morning at about 3 o'clock by a heavy squall with rain from the SSW which increased. I &amp; Nicholson immediately turned out, the ship being off the Tees by the time we got upon deck, they had got the top sail &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>missen</span> stowed &amp; top sail reefed,  <span class=highlight_yellow>lay</span> the ship too soon afterwards left with the head to the land, between Seaham &amp; Hartlepool, the squall gradually subsided &amp; at day light 5 o'clock fine weather again. Ran the ship in for the land &amp; between 7 &amp; 8 o'clock got a piolet on board. Lay off the harbour until the tide flowed sufficiently for us to run the bar, which we did at 11 o'clock, working up to the narrows &amp; then dropping up to the <span class=highlight_yellow>Lenickeln</span> shore where I landed &amp; came home. Robert got my things on shore.</p>\r\n<p>I dined with J Tinley &amp; in the evening called &amp; saw Bess, got home before 11 o'clock</p>","pageId":951,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1421,"lock":null}
20:13:19.413 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.413 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/5/1475
20:13:19.413 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1475,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>We were disturbed again this morning at about 3 o'clock by a heavy squall with rain from the SSW which increased. I &amp; Nicholson immediately turned out, the ship being off the Tees by the time we got upon deck, they had got the top sail &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>missen</span> stowed &amp; top sail reefed,  <span class=highlight_yellow>lay</span> the ship too soon afterwards left with the head to the land, between Seaham &amp; Hartlepool, the squall gradually subsided &amp; at day light 5 o'clock fine weather again. Ran the ship in for the land &amp; between 7 &amp; 8 o'clock got a piolet on board. Lay off the harbour until the tide flowed sufficiently for us to run the bar, which we did at 11 o'clock, working up to the narrows &amp; then dropping up to the <span class=highlight_yellow>Lenickeln</span> shore where I landed &amp; came home. Robert got my things on shore.</p>\r\n<p>I dined with J Tinley &amp; in the evening called &amp; saw Bess, got home before 11 o'clock</p>","pageId":951,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1421,"lock":null}
20:13:19.413 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/6/1476
20:13:19.413 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1476,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp morning having been a great deal of rain at an early hour, blowing fresh at SSW. Paid Robert. Borrowed of him &pound;3 for child 8 weeks &pound;1.16 &amp; settled his book in passages etc. &pound;3.5.3</p>\r\n<p>Dined at the Northumberland Alms being the Dukes court day, the <span class=highlight_yellow>cooks on recorder</span> of Newcastle <span class=highlight_yellow>proceeded</span> there for the first time. At the <span class=highlight_yellow>nefs</span> room ...</p>","pageId":951,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1422,"lock":null}
20:13:19.413 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.414 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/6/1476
20:13:19.414 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1476,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp morning having been a great deal of rain at an early hour, blowing fresh at SSW. Paid Robert. Borrowed of him &pound;3 for child 8 weeks &pound;1.16 &amp; settled his book in passages etc. &pound;3.5.3</p>\r\n<p>Dined at the Northumberland Alms being the Dukes court day, the <span class=highlight_yellow>cooks on recorder</span> of Newcastle <span class=highlight_yellow>proceeded</span> there for the first time. At the <span class=highlight_yellow>nefs</span> room ...</p>","pageId":951,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1422,"lock":null}
20:13:19.414 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/7/1477
20:13:19.414 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1477,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but still blowing hard from the SSW. Several light ships got down &amp; must have had a good run. Lockwood &amp; I walked round by Tynemouth. H Nicholson &amp; Mark dined with me at 3 o'clock. In the evening attended <span class=highlight_yellow>Aldertons</span> Committee room &amp; afterwards with Bess</p>","pageId":952,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1423,"lock":null}
20:13:19.414 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.414 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/7/1477
20:13:19.414 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1477,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but still blowing hard from the SSW. Several light ships got down &amp; must have had a good run. Lockwood &amp; I walked round by Tynemouth. H Nicholson &amp; Mark dined with me at 3 o'clock. In the evening attended <span class=highlight_yellow>Aldertons</span> Committee room &amp; afterwards with Bess</p>","pageId":952,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1423,"lock":null}
20:13:19.414 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/8/1478
20:13:19.414 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1478,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind SW &amp; still looks like more rain. Walked to Preston to see Moor's brother who had not come down. Dined on board the Crisis with A Nicholson. In the evening we walked to Tynemouth at night with Bess</p>","pageId":952,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1424,"lock":null}
20:13:19.414 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.415 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/8/1478
20:13:19.415 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1478,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind SW &amp; still looks like more rain. Walked to Preston to see Moor's brother who had not come down. Dined on board the Crisis with A Nicholson. In the evening we walked to Tynemouth at night with Bess</p>","pageId":952,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1424,"lock":null}
20:13:19.415 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/9/1479
20:13:19.415 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1479,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather. Wind during the day varying between SE &amp; SE. At church in the morning. Saw Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Spencer</span> yesterday who agreed to renew our bill upon our rubbing off &pound;100 or &pound;150. Wrote to WBS. Dined at home. Walked to Tynemouth in the afternoon. Called at Cunningham's Dr Drury there &amp; had some excellent glenlivet with them. Called afterwards at the castle, sat with the Marines &amp; at night again with Bess</p>","pageId":952,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1425,"lock":null}
20:13:19.415 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.415 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/9/1479
20:13:19.415 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1479,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather. Wind during the day varying between SE &amp; SE. At church in the morning. Saw Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Spencer</span> yesterday who agreed to renew our bill upon our rubbing off &pound;100 or &pound;150. Wrote to WBS. Dined at home. Walked to Tynemouth in the afternoon. Called at Cunningham's Dr Drury there &amp; had some excellent glenlivet with them. Called afterwards at the castle, sat with the Marines &amp; at night again with Bess</p>","pageId":952,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1425,"lock":null}
20:13:19.415 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/1/1502
20:13:19.415 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1502,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning blowing &amp; has been all night hard from the SW. Ob board the Hope. Mr Archer did not come to survey the damage but sent a letter with an estimate, offering me &pound;1.10 &amp; the old boom etc. Walked up &amp; saw him but did not agree, however afterwards determined to take it with an 18 inch plank.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home.</p>","pageId":957,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1448,"lock":null}
20:13:19.415 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.416 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/1/1502
20:13:19.416 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1502,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning blowing &amp; has been all night hard from the SW. Ob board the Hope. Mr Archer did not come to survey the damage but sent a letter with an estimate, offering me &pound;1.10 &amp; the old boom etc. Walked up &amp; saw him but did not agree, however afterwards determined to take it with an 18 inch plank.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home.</p>","pageId":957,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1448,"lock":null}
20:13:19.416 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/10/1511
20:13:19.416 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1511,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A raw damp &amp; cold morning. Wind WSW. Two ships got upon the herd in coming into the harbour. Received a letter from Harry &amp;  G of Yarmouth informing me that the Hope had sprung a leak on Sunday night off Orford &amp; got a boat with 14 men to assist in pumping &amp; could scarcely keep her with both pumps going. They however had got her to Yarmouth close to the bar where they were lightening her to get her into the harbour. Laid the letter before the club who sent instructions to Messrs Hurry. I wrote to Stephenson &amp; WBS &amp; also sent a copy of the letter to the Hope Club at Newcastle.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at 2 o'clock. At the whist club in the evening &amp; suppered with Bess. Jobling with me</p>","pageId":960,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1457,"lock":null}
20:13:19.416 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.417 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/10/1511
20:13:19.417 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1511,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A raw damp &amp; cold morning. Wind WSW. Two ships got upon the herd in coming into the harbour. Received a letter from Harry &amp;  G of Yarmouth informing me that the Hope had sprung a leak on Sunday night off Orford &amp; got a boat with 14 men to assist in pumping &amp; could scarcely keep her with both pumps going. They however had got her to Yarmouth close to the bar where they were lightening her to get her into the harbour. Laid the letter before the club who sent instructions to Messrs Hurry. I wrote to Stephenson &amp; WBS &amp; also sent a copy of the letter to the Hope Club at Newcastle.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at 2 o'clock. At the whist club in the evening &amp; suppered with Bess. Jobling with me</p>","pageId":960,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1457,"lock":null}
20:13:19.417 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/11/1512
20:13:19.417 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1512,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW.</p>\r\n<p>The two ships got off the herd.</p>\r\n<p>Received a letter from WBS with our note to Chapman for &pound;200 dated the 9<sup>th</sup> Nov. Jobling left for Seghill. Tom Smith arrived from Togston. Dined at home.</p>","pageId":960,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1458,"lock":null}
20:13:19.417 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.418 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/11/1512
20:13:19.418 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1512,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW.</p>\r\n<p>The two ships got off the herd.</p>\r\n<p>Received a letter from WBS with our note to Chapman for &pound;200 dated the 9<sup>th</sup> Nov. Jobling left for Seghill. Tom Smith arrived from Togston. Dined at home.</p>","pageId":960,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1458,"lock":null}
20:13:19.418 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/12/1513
20:13:19.418 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1513,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW. Received a letter from Messrs Hurry &amp; Co &amp; Stephenson of the ship having struck upon the bar in going into Yarmouth. Wrote to them to deliver &amp; sell the coals, get the leak stopped &amp; return to Shields. Wrote also to WBS. Went across the water &amp; saw Mr Potts who is to send me a copy of the <span class=highlight_yellow>Harmongs</span> protest on Monday. Tom Smith &amp; I dined at home at 5 o'clock &amp; had the whist club in the evening. A pleasant party. Jobling returned late</p>","pageId":960,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1459,"lock":null}
20:13:19.418 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.418 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/12/1513
20:13:19.418 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1513,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW. Received a letter from Messrs Hurry &amp; Co &amp; Stephenson of the ship having struck upon the bar in going into Yarmouth. Wrote to them to deliver &amp; sell the coals, get the leak stopped &amp; return to Shields. Wrote also to WBS. Went across the water &amp; saw Mr Potts who is to send me a copy of the <span class=highlight_yellow>Harmongs</span> protest on Monday. Tom Smith &amp; I dined at home at 5 o'clock &amp; had the whist club in the evening. A pleasant party. Jobling returned late</p>","pageId":960,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1459,"lock":null}
20:13:19.418 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/13/1514
20:13:19.418 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1514,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine but cold morning blowing hard from the NW &amp; NNW.</p>\r\n<p>Tom Smith &amp; I walked to Tynemouth &amp; he afterwards drove up to Benton. Jobling &amp; I dined at home at 4 o'clock.</p>\r\n<p>At night with Bess</p>","pageId":961,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1460,"lock":null}
20:13:19.418 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.419 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/13/1514
20:13:19.419 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1514,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine but cold morning blowing hard from the NW &amp; NNW.</p>\r\n<p>Tom Smith &amp; I walked to Tynemouth &amp; he afterwards drove up to Benton. Jobling &amp; I dined at home at 4 o'clock.</p>\r\n<p>At night with Bess</p>","pageId":961,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1460,"lock":null}
20:13:19.419 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/14/1515
20:13:19.419 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1515,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold raw damp morning. Frosty during the night. Wind W &amp; W by S.</p>\r\n<p>Gave Spencer our note for &pound;200 at 6 months dated 9<sup>th</sup> Nov to be placed to the credit of the executors &amp; paid &pound;85 rents to their credit also Jobling &amp; I dined at home at 2 o'clock. I refused an invitation to dinner at Mr Reeds. At the billiard</p>","pageId":961,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1461,"lock":null}
20:13:19.419 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.420 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/14/1515
20:13:19.420 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1515,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold raw damp morning. Frosty during the night. Wind W &amp; W by S.</p>\r\n<p>Gave Spencer our note for &pound;200 at 6 months dated 9<sup>th</sup> Nov to be placed to the credit of the executors &amp; paid &pound;85 rents to their credit also Jobling &amp; I dined at home at 2 o'clock. I refused an invitation to dinner at Mr Reeds. At the billiard</p>","pageId":961,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1461,"lock":null}
20:13:19.420 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/15/1516
20:13:19.420 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1516,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty morning. Wind W by N. Received two letters, one from Hurry &amp; Co, the other from Stephenson stating the ship to be still very leaky requiring 6 extra men to pumps. They had got her about &frac14; of a mile up the way up to the quay. Laid the letters before the club. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; with Bess at night.</p>","pageId":961,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1462,"lock":null}
20:13:19.420 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.420 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/15/1516
20:13:19.421 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1516,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty morning. Wind W by N. Received two letters, one from Hurry &amp; Co, the other from Stephenson stating the ship to be still very leaky requiring 6 extra men to pumps. They had got her about &frac14; of a mile up the way up to the quay. Laid the letters before the club. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; with Bess at night.</p>","pageId":961,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1462,"lock":null}
20:13:19.421 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/16/1517
20:13:19.421 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1517,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Received a letter from WBS</p>\r\n<p>A comfortable winter's morning. Been a heavy fall of snow during the night. The country covered. Wind NNW. Thawing.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home. With Bess at night.</p>\r\n<p>Sent Robert over the water to Mr Potts who let me have the Harmony Protest in the evening for which I paid &pound;1.11-6</p>","pageId":961,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1463,"lock":null}
20:13:19.421 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.421 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/16/1517
20:13:19.421 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1517,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Received a letter from WBS</p>\r\n<p>A comfortable winter's morning. Been a heavy fall of snow during the night. The country covered. Wind NNW. Thawing.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home. With Bess at night.</p>\r\n<p>Sent Robert over the water to Mr Potts who let me have the Harmony Protest in the evening for which I paid &pound;1.11-6</p>","pageId":961,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1463,"lock":null}
20:13:19.421 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/17/1518
20:13:19.421 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1518,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A sharp frost in the night having been a thaw yesterday. The streets this morning a sheet of ice &amp; dangerous walking. Wind WNW. The clubs received a letter from Messrs Hurry's stating they had sold the remainder of the coals to be taken out of the ship in two days. Wrote to WBS &amp; sent the Hairmongers protest with a copy of Chapman's book &amp; an account of rents. Attended the whist club. Boswell came home with us in the evening to join us in a glass of toddy. Took physic</p>","pageId":962,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1464,"lock":null}
20:13:19.421 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.422 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/17/1518
20:13:19.422 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1518,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A sharp frost in the night having been a thaw yesterday. The streets this morning a sheet of ice &amp; dangerous walking. Wind WNW. The clubs received a letter from Messrs Hurry's stating they had sold the remainder of the coals to be taken out of the ship in two days. Wrote to WBS &amp; sent the Hairmongers protest with a copy of Chapman's book &amp; an account of rents. Attended the whist club. Boswell came home with us in the evening to join us in a glass of toddy. Took physic</p>","pageId":962,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1464,"lock":null}
20:13:19.422 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/18/1519
20:13:19.422 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1519,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty morning. Wind WNW. Having from cold I suppose, the back of my neck &amp; head much affected &amp; sore. I this morning took a black draught &amp; lay in bed till 1 o'clock. Charles Redley called from Hartley. Dined &amp; spent the afternoon with us. He left us at &frac14; past 9 o'clock to walk back being a fine moonlight night. I went along &amp; slept with Bess. Robert yesterday paid Philipson Mason his bill &pound;37 &amp; today paid into Chapman's &pound;15 more rents</p>","pageId":962,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1465,"lock":null}
20:13:19.422 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.423 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/18/1519
20:13:19.423 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1519,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty morning. Wind WNW. Having from cold I suppose, the back of my neck &amp; head much affected &amp; sore. I this morning took a black draught &amp; lay in bed till 1 o'clock. Charles Redley called from Hartley. Dined &amp; spent the afternoon with us. He left us at &frac14; past 9 o'clock to walk back being a fine moonlight night. I went along &amp; slept with Bess. Robert yesterday paid Philipson Mason his bill &pound;37 &amp; today paid into Chapman's &pound;15 more rents</p>","pageId":962,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1465,"lock":null}
20:13:19.423 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/19/1520
20:13:19.423 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1520,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A heavy fall of snow last night again. A complete thaw with sleet. Wind E by N. Paid average Eligible Club &pound;12. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; at night with Bess</p>","pageId":962,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1466,"lock":null}
20:13:19.423 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.424 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/19/1520
20:13:19.424 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1520,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A heavy fall of snow last night again. A complete thaw with sleet. Wind E by N. Paid average Eligible Club &pound;12. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; at night with Bess</p>","pageId":962,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1466,"lock":null}
20:13:19.424 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/2/1503
20:13:19.424 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1503,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Rather a dull morning. Wind fresh from SW &amp; little rain.</p>\r\n<p>Sent Stephenson up to &amp; he settled with Mr Archer. Received 30/0 &amp; a deal plank. The ship got her beef on board. Sent WBS a round up. Walked up to Tynemouth. Saw Rifles march for Manchester. Dined at home at 5 o'clock. Lockerwood came in &amp; took a glass of toddy with me.</p>\r\n<p>With Bess in the evening</p>","pageId":958,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1449,"lock":null}
20:13:19.424 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.425 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/2/1503
20:13:19.425 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1503,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Rather a dull morning. Wind fresh from SW &amp; little rain.</p>\r\n<p>Sent Stephenson up to &amp; he settled with Mr Archer. Received 30/0 &amp; a deal plank. The ship got her beef on board. Sent WBS a round up. Walked up to Tynemouth. Saw Rifles march for Manchester. Dined at home at 5 o'clock. Lockerwood came in &amp; took a glass of toddy with me.</p>\r\n<p>With Bess in the evening</p>","pageId":958,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1449,"lock":null}
20:13:19.425 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/20/1521
20:13:19.425 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1521,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful winter's morning. Hard frost &amp; wind NW. At the newsroom in the morning. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. Spent the evening with Bess. Jobling there.</p>","pageId":962,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1467,"lock":null}
20:13:19.425 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
