20:13:19.426 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1522,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A thick damp morning having been rain with a SSE wind during the night. Wind now SW. Received a letter from WBS. Transferred from executors account at <span class=highlight_yellow>G's </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Ho</span> to mine &pound;150. Dined with Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Th</span><span class=highlight_yellow>o</span> Wright, Whitley Park, a pleasant day.</p>","pageId":962,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1468,"lock":null}
20:13:19.426 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/22/1523
20:13:19.426 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1523,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A mild day. Wind about west. Walked to Tynemouth with Boswell. Received a letter from Messrs Hurry &amp; co. The coals being all out on Saturday &amp; that they had found the leak to be in an open trennail hole between the timber under the starboard for chain about two feet below <font color=#BFBFBF>the </font>light water mark. Had plugged it up &amp; after heaving down &amp; driving a new trennail, expected she would be able to return to Shields without the necessity of being docked at Yarmouth.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; with Bess at night.</p>","pageId":963,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1469,"lock":null}
20:13:19.426 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.427 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/22/1523
20:13:19.427 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1523,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A mild day. Wind about west. Walked to Tynemouth with Boswell. Received a letter from Messrs Hurry &amp; co. The coals being all out on Saturday &amp; that they had found the leak to be in an open trennail hole between the timber under the starboard for chain about two feet below <font color=#BFBFBF>the </font>light water mark. Had plugged it up &amp; after heaving down &amp; driving a new trennail, expected she would be able to return to Shields without the necessity of being docked at Yarmouth.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; with Bess at night.</p>","pageId":963,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1469,"lock":null}
20:13:19.427 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/23/1524
20:13:19.427 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1524,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Mild weather &amp; fresh breezes from WNW. Wrote to WBS with a list of ships that sailed before &amp; after the Hope. Dined at home. At the billiard room &amp; at night at Bess's. Jobling, H Hurry &amp; Boswell <font color=#BFBFBF>there</font>.</p>","pageId":963,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1470,"lock":null}
20:13:19.427 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.427 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/23/1524
20:13:19.427 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1524,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Mild weather &amp; fresh breezes from WNW. Wrote to WBS with a list of ships that sailed before &amp; after the Hope. Dined at home. At the billiard room &amp; at night at Bess's. Jobling, H Hurry &amp; Boswell <font color=#BFBFBF>there</font>.</p>","pageId":963,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1470,"lock":null}
20:13:19.427 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/24/1525
20:13:19.427 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1525,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuation of mild weather. Wind WSW. Received a letter from Stephenson of his having got the leak stopped. The ballast alongside &amp; expecting to get away the next day. Gave a draft on Ch<font color=#BFBFBF>apmans</font> for &pound;5 <span class=highlight_yellow>account</span> for self. Dined with Mr Harrison the brewer at 3 o'clock. At the whist club &amp; at night with Bess. Jobling went to South Shields</p>","pageId":963,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1471,"lock":null}
20:13:19.427 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.428 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/24/1525
20:13:19.428 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1525,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuation of mild weather. Wind WSW. Received a letter from Stephenson of his having got the leak stopped. The ballast alongside &amp; expecting to get away the next day. Gave a draft on Ch<font color=#BFBFBF>apmans</font> for &pound;5 <span class=highlight_yellow>account</span> for self. Dined with Mr Harrison the brewer at 3 o'clock. At the whist club &amp; at night with Bess. Jobling went to South Shields</p>","pageId":963,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1471,"lock":null}
20:13:19.428 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/25/1526
20:13:19.428 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1526,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet morning. Wind SW. gave a draft on Ch<font color=#BFBFBF>apmans</font> for &pound;9.10 average Hope Club. Wind changed to SE. A great many ships got down. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon. With Bess at night. Lockwood there</p>","pageId":963,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1472,"lock":null}
20:13:19.428 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.428 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/25/1526
20:13:19.428 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1526,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet morning. Wind SW. gave a draft on Ch<font color=#BFBFBF>apmans</font> for &pound;9.10 average Hope Club. Wind changed to SE. A great many ships got down. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon. With Bess at night. Lockwood there</p>","pageId":963,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1472,"lock":null}
20:13:19.428 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/26/1527
20:13:19.428 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1527,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather but cold and wind SE. A great many light ships arrived <span class=highlight_yellow>ravenjot</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>this</span>. The Hope from Yarmouth quite light. Went to Newcastle &amp; fixed her to load Bell&amp; Brown again to be loaded in 3 weeks,. Returned home to dinner. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; attended the club. At night at <span class=highlight_yellow>Garthays</span></p>","pageId":964,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1473,"lock":null}
20:13:19.428 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.429 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/26/1527
20:13:19.429 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1527,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather but cold and wind SE. A great many light ships arrived <span class=highlight_yellow>ravenjot</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>this</span>. The Hope from Yarmouth quite light. Went to Newcastle &amp; fixed her to load Bell&amp; Brown again to be loaded in 3 weeks,. Returned home to dinner. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; attended the club. At night at <span class=highlight_yellow>Garthays</span></p>","pageId":964,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1473,"lock":null}
20:13:19.429 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/27/1528
20:13:19.429 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1528,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather cold &amp; frosty. Wind SW. My head still being bad from cold, T this morning breakfasted in bed &amp; got up at 12 o'clock. Went to church in the afternoon. Afterwards walked round by Tynemouth. Dined with Tinley at 5 o'clock, Jobley &amp; Captain Cuthbert 15<sup>th</sup> there</p>","pageId":964,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1474,"lock":null}
20:13:19.429 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
