20:13:19.432 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1530,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Cold weather, rather frosty. Wind WNW.</p>\r\n<p>Paid Beall app<font color=#BFBFBF>renti</font><sup>ce</sup><sup> </sup> in advance &pound;1. Received a letter from Hurry &amp; Co Yarmouth with their accounts &amp; a bill for balance at 2 months for &pound;59.9.</p>\r\n<p>Walked with H Hurry &amp; Richardson up to Sadlers &amp; dined with him</p>","pageId":964,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1476,"lock":null}
20:13:19.432 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/3/1504
20:13:19.432 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1504,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp morning having been showers in the night. Wind WNW.</p>\r\n<p>On board the Hope. Her loading not completed by two keels, thereby prevented getting to sea. Walked to Tynemouth. The two keels came down in the afternoon. Lockerwood came &amp; dined with me. At the whist club in the evening &amp; with Bess at night</p>","pageId":958,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1450,"lock":null}
20:13:19.432 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
