20:13:19.462 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1223,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A delightful morning. Quite spring, mild weather. A light air from about W.  Walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home. Attended the whist club at H Harry's in the evening</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":887,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1169,"lock":null}
20:13:19.462 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/13/1224
20:13:19.462 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1224,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A continuance of mild weather. Wind SSW. At church in the morning. Dined with H Harry. Received a letter from WBS. In the evening at the Mulstrum.</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":887,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1170,"lock":null}
20:13:19.462 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.462 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/13/1224
20:13:19.462 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1224,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A continuance of mild weather. Wind SSW. At church in the morning. Dined with H Harry. Received a letter from WBS. In the evening at the Mulstrum.</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":887,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1170,"lock":null}
20:13:19.462 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/14/1225
20:13:19.462 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1225,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A beautiful morning. Wind SW. Strolled about the town until dinner at 2 o'clock at home. At the billiard room all the afternoon &amp; at the Albion in the evening</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":887,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1171,"lock":null}
20:13:19.462 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.463 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/14/1225
20:13:19.463 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1225,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A beautiful morning. Wind SW. Strolled about the town until dinner at 2 o'clock at home. At the billiard room all the afternoon &amp; at the Albion in the evening</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":887,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1171,"lock":null}
20:13:19.463 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/15/1226
20:13:19.463 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1226,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild morning. Wind SW. Dined at 1 o'clock with J Ridhard on board the Nautilus &amp; in the evening went to a party at J Cunningham's. Wrote a note yesterday to D Dixon requesting him to ask Colonel Coulston if he could give me any positive information about my commission.</p>","pageId":887,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1172,"lock":null}
20:13:19.463 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.463 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/15/1226
20:13:19.463 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1226,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild morning. Wind SW. Dined at 1 o'clock with J Ridhard on board the Nautilus &amp; in the evening went to a party at J Cunningham's. Wrote a note yesterday to D Dixon requesting him to ask Colonel Coulston if he could give me any positive information about my commission.</p>","pageId":887,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1172,"lock":null}
20:13:19.463 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/16/1227
20:13:19.463 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1227,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A damp morning having been rain in the night. Wind WNW. Received a note from D Dixon, having seen Colonel Coulston who says I shall be in the regiment in a few days for a captaincy. Dined again on board the Nautilus &amp; at the Albion in the evening.</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":887,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1173,"lock":null}
20:13:19.463 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.464 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/16/1227
20:13:19.464 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1227,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A damp morning having been rain in the night. Wind WNW. Received a note from D Dixon, having seen Colonel Coulston who says I shall be in the regiment in a few days for a captaincy. Dined again on board the Nautilus &amp; at the Albion in the evening.</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":887,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1173,"lock":null}
20:13:19.464 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/17/1228
20:13:19.464 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1228,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine morning blowing fresh at WNW. Went by the coach to Newcastle. Called at the club house to see Colonel Coulson who had left town in the morning. At D Dixons, saw Dixon &amp; the ladies. Called on young Bigger who gave me the names of the trader men in London who have the regulation patterns. Walked down from Newcastle. Met Dr Drury &amp; Mr Harrison near Mr Robson who were on their way to dine with Saddler at the Point &amp; prevailed on me to accompany them. At the whist club &amp; Mulstrum in the evening.</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":888,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1174,"lock":null}
20:13:19.464 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.466 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/17/1228
20:13:19.466 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1228,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine morning blowing fresh at WNW. Went by the coach to Newcastle. Called at the club house to see Colonel Coulson who had left town in the morning. At D Dixons, saw Dixon &amp; the ladies. Called on young Bigger who gave me the names of the trader men in London who have the regulation patterns. Walked down from Newcastle. Met Dr Drury &amp; Mr Harrison near Mr Robson who were on their way to dine with Saddler at the Point &amp; prevailed on me to accompany them. At the whist club &amp; Mulstrum in the evening.</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":888,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1174,"lock":null}
20:13:19.466 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/18/1229
20:13:19.466 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1229,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A continuance of fine weather. Wind WNW.</p> <p></p> <p>Received a letter from WBS &amp; after breakfast went on board the Jane at his request to see Mr Brown to desire him not to clear the Harmony or of cleared to order the master to stop below Gravesend until after the 1 March when the coal duties are to be taken off.</p> <p></p> <p>Attended a meeting at the Commercial &amp; entered into resolutions to be followed up by petitions against the proposed <span class=highlight_yellow>carecase</span> of duty upon north American timber.</p> <p></p> <p>Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon. Suppered with H harry</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":888,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1175,"lock":null}
20:13:19.466 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.466 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/18/1229
20:13:19.466 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1229,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A continuance of fine weather. Wind WNW.</p> <p></p> <p>Received a letter from WBS &amp; after breakfast went on board the Jane at his request to see Mr Brown to desire him not to clear the Harmony or of cleared to order the master to stop below Gravesend until after the 1 March when the coal duties are to be taken off.</p> <p></p> <p>Attended a meeting at the Commercial &amp; entered into resolutions to be followed up by petitions against the proposed <span class=highlight_yellow>carecase</span> of duty upon north American timber.</p> <p></p> <p>Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon. Suppered with H harry</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":888,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1175,"lock":null}
20:13:19.466 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/19/1230
20:13:19.466 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1230,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A beautiful morning. Wind NW. Wrote to WBS to order all my clothes etc. for the North<font color=#BFBFBF>humbria</font> Regiment immediately, should I be in the <span class=highlight_yellow>Gagelle</span> which is expected. Took wine at the Albion with W C Wright etc. &amp; attended the club at Dr Drury's in the evening.</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":888,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1176,"lock":null}
20:13:19.466 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.467 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/19/1230
20:13:19.467 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1230,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A beautiful morning. Wind NW. Wrote to WBS to order all my clothes etc. for the North<font color=#BFBFBF>humbria</font> Regiment immediately, should I be in the <span class=highlight_yellow>Gagelle</span> which is expected. Took wine at the Albion with W C Wright etc. &amp; attended the club at Dr Drury's in the evening.</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":888,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1176,"lock":null}
20:13:19.467 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/19/1231
20:13:19.467 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1231,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":19,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p><p>Withdrew the &pound;500 insurance on the Hope from the Great Premium Club &amp; put it into the Eligible making &pound;1000 in that club. Left a written notice with Bulmers clerk to that effect.</p> <p></p> <p>A good deal of rain this evening.</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":889,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1177,"lock":null}
20:13:19.467 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.467 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/19/1231
20:13:19.467 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1231,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":19,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p><p>Withdrew the &pound;500 insurance on the Hope from the Great Premium Club &amp; put it into the Eligible making &pound;1000 in that club. Left a written notice with Bulmers clerk to that effect.</p> <p></p> <p>A good deal of rain this evening.</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":889,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1177,"lock":null}
20:13:19.467 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/2/1211
20:13:19.467 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1211,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>Storm abated &amp; finer weather. Wind SE and a rapid thaw.</p> <p></p> <p>Many ships on shore. Two on the Herd Sand &amp; one a wreck, two on the rocks <span class=highlight_yellow>and</span> broken to pieces, three under the castle light house <span class=highlight_yellow>too</span> scattered to pieces <span class=highlight_yellow>mesher</span> &amp; boy of one drowned a smack at Cullercoats, all hands drowned. Three or four near Whitley, two broke to pieces immediately on coming on shore at night &amp; crews drowned. Walked round by the rock &amp; Tynemouth. Dreadful destruction.</p> <p></p> <p>Dined at home. At the billiard room all the afternoon &amp; <font color=#BFBFBF>in the </font>evening Mr Lockword came home with me &amp; drank a glass of punch. Paid an average bill Eligible Club by draft for &pound;6.0.10. Came on to blow almost as hard as ever. Many ships got in today.</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":883,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1157,"lock":null}
20:13:19.467 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.468 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/2/1211
20:13:19.468 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1211,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>Storm abated &amp; finer weather. Wind SE and a rapid thaw.</p> <p></p> <p>Many ships on shore. Two on the Herd Sand &amp; one a wreck, two on the rocks <span class=highlight_yellow>and</span> broken to pieces, three under the castle light house <span class=highlight_yellow>too</span> scattered to pieces <span class=highlight_yellow>mesher</span> &amp; boy of one drowned a smack at Cullercoats, all hands drowned. Three or four near Whitley, two broke to pieces immediately on coming on shore at night &amp; crews drowned. Walked round by the rock &amp; Tynemouth. Dreadful destruction.</p> <p></p> <p>Dined at home. At the billiard room all the afternoon &amp; <font color=#BFBFBF>in the </font>evening Mr Lockword came home with me &amp; drank a glass of punch. Paid an average bill Eligible Club by draft for &pound;6.0.10. Came on to blow almost as hard as ever. Many ships got in today.</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":883,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1157,"lock":null}
20:13:19.468 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/20/1232
20:13:19.468 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1232,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine day. Wind NNW. Must have been in the night NNE there being a deal of sea on the bar. Went to church in the morning. Sadler dined with me &amp; H Harry came in &amp; took wine with us. At the Multrum in the evening</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":889,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1178,"lock":null}
20:13:19.468 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.469 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/20/1232
20:13:19.469 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1232,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine day. Wind NNW. Must have been in the night NNE there being a deal of sea on the bar. Went to church in the morning. Sadler dined with me &amp; H Harry came in &amp; took wine with us. At the Multrum in the evening</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":889,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1178,"lock":null}
20:13:19.469 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/21/1233
20:13:19.469 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1233,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A beautiful morning. Wind NW. Much disappointed at not finding my name in the Gazette. Took a long walk with Cunningham round by Preston, Whitley, Cullercoats &amp; Tynemouth. Wrote to WBS with an account of <span class=highlight_yellow>units</span>. Dined at Jebbs at 5 o'clock, a gentleman's party &amp; spent a very pleasant day</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":889,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1179,"lock":null}
20:13:19.469 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.469 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/21/1233
20:13:19.470 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1233,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A beautiful morning. Wind NW. Much disappointed at not finding my name in the Gazette. Took a long walk with Cunningham round by Preston, Whitley, Cullercoats &amp; Tynemouth. Wrote to WBS with an account of <span class=highlight_yellow>units</span>. Dined at Jebbs at 5 o'clock, a gentleman's party &amp; spent a very pleasant day</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":889,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1179,"lock":null}
20:13:19.470 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/22/1234
20:13:19.470 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1234,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>Blowing hard half a gale from NNE &amp; has been rain or snow during the night. Called upon the <span class=highlight_yellow>messrs</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>Hdestorns</span>  at Mr Reeds. Dined at home &amp; in the evening went to the assembly which was a very good one. About 68 there. Got home at 4 o'clock. Paid Brown 16/ my subscription</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":889,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1180,"lock":null}
20:13:19.470 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.470 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/22/1234
20:13:19.470 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1234,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>Blowing hard half a gale from NNE &amp; has been rain or snow during the night. Called upon the <span class=highlight_yellow>messrs</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>Hdestorns</span>  at Mr Reeds. Dined at home &amp; in the evening went to the assembly which was a very good one. About 68 there. Got home at 4 o'clock. Paid Brown 16/ my subscription</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":889,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1180,"lock":null}
20:13:19.470 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/23/1235
20:13:19.470 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1235,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine frosty morning. Wind WNW. Received a letter from WBS. Walked to Tynemouth. Called upon &amp; had lunch with Jibbs. Dined at 5 o'clock with H Dale &amp; spent a very pleasant day</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":889,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1181,"lock":null}
20:13:19.470 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.471 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/23/1235
20:13:19.471 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1235,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine frosty morning. Wind WNW. Received a letter from WBS. Walked to Tynemouth. Called upon &amp; had lunch with Jibbs. Dined at 5 o'clock with H Dale &amp; spent a very pleasant day</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":889,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1181,"lock":null}
20:13:19.471 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/24/1236
20:13:19.471 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1236,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful morning. Wind NW. Received a letter from WBS with his note for &pound;95.10 enclosed. Dined at home. Mr Lockwood to his dinner with me. In the evening at the club. The Samarang frigate got orders to go to <span class=highlight_yellow>Chathace</span> &amp; take all the mariners</p>","pageId":890,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1182,"lock":null}
20:13:19.471 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.472 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/24/1236
20:13:19.472 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1236,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful morning. Wind NW. Received a letter from WBS with his note for &pound;95.10 enclosed. Dined at home. Mr Lockwood to his dinner with me. In the evening at the club. The Samarang frigate got orders to go to <span class=highlight_yellow>Chathace</span> &amp; take all the mariners</p>","pageId":890,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1182,"lock":null}
20:13:19.472 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/25/1237
20:13:19.472 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1237,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Blowing hard at WNW. The Samarang frigate sailed at 1 o'clock. Dined at home. Paid <span class=highlight_yellow>Twigell</span> &pound;2.14. <span class=highlight_yellow>tharp</span> 15/ <span class=highlight_yellow>coates</span> &pound;1.15/ <span class=highlight_yellow>Tygack</span> &pound;1.8. all for the Hope. At the Duke of York &amp; Mulstrum in the evening.</p>","pageId":890,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1183,"lock":null}
20:13:19.472 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.473 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/25/1237
20:13:19.473 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1237,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Blowing hard at WNW. The Samarang frigate sailed at 1 o'clock. Dined at home. Paid <span class=highlight_yellow>Twigell</span> &pound;2.14. <span class=highlight_yellow>tharp</span> 15/ <span class=highlight_yellow>coates</span> &pound;1.15/ <span class=highlight_yellow>Tygack</span> &pound;1.8. all for the Hope. At the Duke of York &amp; Mulstrum in the evening.</p>","pageId":890,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1183,"lock":null}
20:13:19.473 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/26/1238
20:13:19.473 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1238,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A dull rainy morning. Wind NE. Received the Hope's <span class=highlight_yellow>assales</span> from WBS. Took the 11 o'clock steam boat &amp; went to Newcastle. Called to see Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>albraith</font>. Could learn nothing further with regard to our conversation. All as much in the dark &amp; suspense as myself. Saw Dixon &amp; the ladies in Westgate Street where I lunched. Received of the <span class=highlight_yellow>Hind</span><span class=highlight_yellow>h</span><span class=highlight_yellow>augh</span> &pound;36.0.9 being the difference between what the Hope made &amp; 11/- freight applied. Returned by steam by the 4 o'clock boat &amp; came home to dinner. Attended the club at Tibb's in the evening</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":890,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1184,"lock":null}
20:13:19.473 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.473 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/26/1238
20:13:19.473 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1238,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A dull rainy morning. Wind NE. Received the Hope's <span class=highlight_yellow>assales</span> from WBS. Took the 11 o'clock steam boat &amp; went to Newcastle. Called to see Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>albraith</font>. Could learn nothing further with regard to our conversation. All as much in the dark &amp; suspense as myself. Saw Dixon &amp; the ladies in Westgate Street where I lunched. Received of the <span class=highlight_yellow>Hind</span><span class=highlight_yellow>h</span><span class=highlight_yellow>augh</span> &pound;36.0.9 being the difference between what the Hope made &amp; 11/- freight applied. Returned by steam by the 4 o'clock boat &amp; came home to dinner. Attended the club at Tibb's in the evening</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":890,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1184,"lock":null}
20:13:19.473 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/27/1239
20:13:19.473 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1239,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A thick damp morning. Wind SW. Did not go to church. Dined at home. In the evening at the Abbey &amp; Mulstrums</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":890,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1185,"lock":null}
20:13:19.473 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.474 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/27/1239
20:13:19.474 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1239,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A thick damp morning. Wind SW. Did not go to church. Dined at home. In the evening at the Abbey &amp; Mulstrums</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":890,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1185,"lock":null}
20:13:19.474 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/28/1240
20:13:19.474 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1240,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine but cold morning having been a frost in the night. Wind NW. My name not in the Gazette. Received a letter from WBS stating the season that Lord Melbourn had not made up his mind as to filling up the vacancies. Gave Robert a draft for &pound;5 executor's account for the house. Drew also for &pound;6.9 to pay Mrs Dixon for sundries got for Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>albraith</font>. Paid into Chapman on my own account WBS's note for &pound;95.10 &amp; &pound;36.0.9 received of Hindhaugh = 131.16.9. Called upon Dr Drury &amp; gave him a draft on C&amp;C for his bills &pound;11.4/- afterwards walked up to Craigs &amp; took wine at the Mulstrum in the evening.</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":891,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1186,"lock":null}
20:13:19.474 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.475 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/28/1240
20:13:19.475 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1240,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine but cold morning having been a frost in the night. Wind NW. My name not in the Gazette. Received a letter from WBS stating the season that Lord Melbourn had not made up his mind as to filling up the vacancies. Gave Robert a draft for &pound;5 executor's account for the house. Drew also for &pound;6.9 to pay Mrs Dixon for sundries got for Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>albraith</font>. Paid into Chapman on my own account WBS's note for &pound;95.10 &amp; &pound;36.0.9 received of Hindhaugh = 131.16.9. Called upon Dr Drury &amp; gave him a draft on C&amp;C for his bills &pound;11.4/- afterwards walked up to Craigs &amp; took wine at the Mulstrum in the evening.</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":891,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1186,"lock":null}
20:13:19.475 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/3/1212
20:13:19.475 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1212,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A calm morning. Very foggy. Wind S by W &amp; a frost.</p> <p></p> <p>Attended a meeting of the Eligible Club &amp; the members agreed to resist Mr Kings of South Shields claim as being unjust.</p> <p></p> <p>Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; whist club in the evening.</p> <p></p> <p>Received a letter from WBS of the safe arrival of the Hope &amp; a copy of a letter received from the Duke of Northumbria in answer to his application for a commission in the military for me; very polite.</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":884,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1158,"lock":null}
20:13:19.475 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.475 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/3/1212
20:13:19.475 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1212,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A calm morning. Very foggy. Wind S by W &amp; a frost.</p> <p></p> <p>Attended a meeting of the Eligible Club &amp; the members agreed to resist Mr Kings of South Shields claim as being unjust.</p> <p></p> <p>Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; whist club in the evening.</p> <p></p> <p>Received a letter from WBS of the safe arrival of the Hope &amp; a copy of a letter received from the Duke of Northumbria in answer to his application for a commission in the military for me; very polite.</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":884,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1158,"lock":null}
20:13:19.475 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/4/1213
20:13:19.475 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1213,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A very stormy morning. Blew a gale of wind all night from ENE with heavy sleet &amp; rain.</p> <p></p> <p>Two ships have got upon the Herd <span class=highlight_yellow>Sand</span>. One from America, the other from ____</p> <p></p> <p>Settled with Robert &amp; paid into Chapmans on executors account &pound;65 of rents &amp; drew for &pound;18.11.6 to pay Mrs Noakes, late Miss Robinson for Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>ilbraith</font> boards etc.</p> <p></p> <p>Another small light vessel got upon the Herd.</p> <p></p> <p>At the news &amp; billiard rooms all the morning. No moving out such stormy weather. Dined at 5 o'clock with J Tinley, a party. Attended an evening party at the Messes Frenches'</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":884,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1159,"lock":null}
20:13:19.475 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.476 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/4/1213
20:13:19.476 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1213,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A very stormy morning. Blew a gale of wind all night from ENE with heavy sleet &amp; rain.</p> <p></p> <p>Two ships have got upon the Herd <span class=highlight_yellow>Sand</span>. One from America, the other from ____</p> <p></p> <p>Settled with Robert &amp; paid into Chapmans on executors account &pound;65 of rents &amp; drew for &pound;18.11.6 to pay Mrs Noakes, late Miss Robinson for Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>ilbraith</font> boards etc.</p> <p></p> <p>Another small light vessel got upon the Herd.</p> <p></p> <p>At the news &amp; billiard rooms all the morning. No moving out such stormy weather. Dined at 5 o'clock with J Tinley, a party. Attended an evening party at the Messes Frenches'</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":884,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1159,"lock":null}
20:13:19.476 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/5/1214
20:13:19.476 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1214,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>It has been very stormy all night with showers of sleet &amp; snow. Wind this morning got round to NW. Sea very high. One of the ships that got upon the Herd Sand ...</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":884,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1160,"lock":null}
20:13:19.476 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.476 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/5/1214
20:13:19.476 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1214,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>It has been very stormy all night with showers of sleet &amp; snow. Wind this morning got round to NW. Sea very high. One of the ships that got upon the Herd Sand ...</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":884,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1160,"lock":null}
20:13:19.476 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/5/1215
20:13:19.476 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1215,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":5,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p><p>... yesterday gone to pieces.</p> <p></p> <p>The Magpie cutter being embayed was obliged yesterday to run for the harbour &amp; providentially got in safe, losing before she took the bar, one of her boats &amp; being obliged to cut away her square-sail, a sea having filled it and they could not take it in.</p> <p></p> <p>Sent Mr Leadbetter by Dunn this morning <span class=highlight_yellow>Rawling's</span> valuation of wines etc &amp; also Leadbitter the cook's receipt for her legacy. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; attended the whist club at H Dales in the evening. Turned rather frosty. Received a letter from WBS &amp; answered it.</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":885,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1161,"lock":null}
20:13:19.476 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.477 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/5/1215
20:13:19.477 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1215,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":5,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p><p>... yesterday gone to pieces.</p> <p></p> <p>The Magpie cutter being embayed was obliged yesterday to run for the harbour &amp; providentially got in safe, losing before she took the bar, one of her boats &amp; being obliged to cut away her square-sail, a sea having filled it and they could not take it in.</p> <p></p> <p>Sent Mr Leadbetter by Dunn this morning <span class=highlight_yellow>Rawling's</span> valuation of wines etc &amp; also Leadbitter the cook's receipt for her legacy. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; attended the whist club at H Dales in the evening. Turned rather frosty. Received a letter from WBS &amp; answered it.</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":885,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1161,"lock":null}
20:13:19.477 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/6/1216
20:13:19.477 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1216,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine morning &amp; hard frost. Wind NW. Did not go to church. Took a walk to Tynemouth after seeing the newspapers. Some light ships got in today from Leith Roads &amp; also some laden ones passed for London.</p> <p></p> <p>Dined at home. At the Mulstrum in the evening. A heavy gale of snow &amp; blowing hard, 12 pm</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":885,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1162,"lock":null}
20:13:19.477 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.478 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/6/1216
20:13:19.478 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1216,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine morning &amp; hard frost. Wind NW. Did not go to church. Took a walk to Tynemouth after seeing the newspapers. Some light ships got in today from Leith Roads &amp; also some laden ones passed for London.</p> <p></p> <p>Dined at home. At the Mulstrum in the evening. A heavy gale of snow &amp; blowing hard, 12 pm</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":885,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1162,"lock":null}
20:13:19.478 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/7/1217
20:13:19.478 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1217,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A dull rainy morning. Wind S by W &amp; SSW. Such unpleasant weather prevented going to Newcastle as I intended. The same course kept me at home on Saturday. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon. Suppered &amp; spent the evening with a party at Dr Drury's</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":885,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1163,"lock":null}
20:13:19.478 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.478 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/7/1217
20:13:19.478 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1217,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A dull rainy morning. Wind S by W &amp; SSW. Such unpleasant weather prevented going to Newcastle as I intended. The same course kept me at home on Saturday. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon. Suppered &amp; spent the evening with a party at Dr Drury's</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":885,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1163,"lock":null}
20:13:19.478 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/8/1218
20:13:19.478 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1218,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A mild morning but rather dull; Wind SW. Afterwards turning out a fine day. J Cunningham breakfasted with me &amp; we went up to Newcastle together by steam. Mr Gorthing RA ...</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":885,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1164,"lock":null}
20:13:19.478 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.479 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/8/1218
20:13:19.479 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1218,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A mild morning but rather dull; Wind SW. Afterwards turning out a fine day. J Cunningham breakfasted with me &amp; we went up to Newcastle together by steam. Mr Gorthing RA ...</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":885,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1164,"lock":null}
20:13:19.479 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/8/1219
20:13:19.479 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1219,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":8,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p><p>... accompanied us. J Cunningham left me to see captain Maun of the north, wishing to obtain a commission. I called at D Dixon &amp; then went to Mrs Noaks &amp; paid her &pound;18.11.6 for Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>ailbraith</font>'s &frac14; year board etc. and also &pound;2.2 entrance for training dancing &amp; drawing. Gostling &amp; I lunched at D Dixons afterwards played at billiards at the rooms &amp; at 5 o'clock returned in a gig to Shields. The ice above <font color=#BFBFBF>the </font>bridge having come away in immense quantities with the ebb tide prevented the steam boats plying.</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":886,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1165,"lock":null}
20:13:19.479 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.479 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/8/1219
20:13:19.479 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1219,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":8,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p><p>... accompanied us. J Cunningham left me to see captain Maun of the north, wishing to obtain a commission. I called at D Dixon &amp; then went to Mrs Noaks &amp; paid her &pound;18.11.6 for Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>ailbraith</font>'s &frac14; year board etc. and also &pound;2.2 entrance for training dancing &amp; drawing. Gostling &amp; I lunched at D Dixons afterwards played at billiards at the rooms &amp; at 5 o'clock returned in a gig to Shields. The ice above <font color=#BFBFBF>the </font>bridge having come away in immense quantities with the ebb tide prevented the steam boats plying.</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":886,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1165,"lock":null}
20:13:19.479 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/9/1220
20:13:19.479 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1220,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A very fine mild morning. Wind WSW. Several light ships got down. Went to Milburn Place to see Mr Stephenson respecting <span class=highlight_yellow>remitting</span> &pound;13.10 to London. Afterwards walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home. At a party in the evening at Mr W Hewson's</p> <p></p> <p>Great confusion &amp; I fear damage in the harbour tonight, the heavy fresh <font color=#BFBFBF>wind </font>having driven the ships adrift.</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":886,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1166,"lock":null}
20:13:19.479 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.480 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/2/9/1220
20:13:19.480 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1220,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A very fine mild morning. Wind WSW. Several light ships got down. Went to Milburn Place to see Mr Stephenson respecting <span class=highlight_yellow>remitting</span> &pound;13.10 to London. Afterwards walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home. At a party in the evening at Mr W Hewson's</p> <p></p> <p>Great confusion &amp; I fear damage in the harbour tonight, the heavy fresh <font color=#BFBFBF>wind </font>having driven the ships adrift.</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":886,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1166,"lock":null}
20:13:19.480 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/3/1/1241
20:13:19.480 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1241,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Frosty &amp; wind at NW blowing fresh. Called upon Captain Webb. He &amp; I walked round by the high end of the town, Plett's Yard &amp; Chesterton, home to dinner. In the afternoon at the billiard room &amp; at the Duke of York in the evening.</p>","pageId":891,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1187,"lock":null}
20:13:19.480 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.481 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/3/1/1241
20:13:19.481 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1241,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Frosty &amp; wind at NW blowing fresh. Called upon Captain Webb. He &amp; I walked round by the high end of the town, Plett's Yard &amp; Chesterton, home to dinner. In the afternoon at the billiard room &amp; at the Duke of York in the evening.</p>","pageId":891,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1187,"lock":null}
20:13:19.481 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/3/10/1247
20:13:19.481 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1247,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful day. Wind SW. Went to Newcastle by steam &amp; ordered coals down on Monday. Enrolled <span class=highlight_yellow>H A </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Bealls</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>interviews</span> at the Custom House. Returned home to dinner. Dr Drewry &amp; Chartson dined with me. At the club in the evening.</p>","pageId":893,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1193,"lock":null}
20:13:19.481 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.481 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/3/10/1247
20:13:19.481 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1247,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful day. Wind SW. Went to Newcastle by steam &amp; ordered coals down on Monday. Enrolled <span class=highlight_yellow>H A </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Bealls</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>interviews</span> at the Custom House. Returned home to dinner. Dr Drewry &amp; Chartson dined with me. At the club in the evening.</p>","pageId":893,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1193,"lock":null}
20:13:19.481 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/3/11/1248
20:13:19.481 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1248,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet unpleasant day. Wind between SW &amp; WNW. Could not get to the ship. Received a letter from WBS informing me of my name being in the Gazette, which I see in this days papers. Dined at home. H harry, Cunningham &amp; and I took wine at the Albion &amp; in the evening finished at the Duke <font color=#BFBFBF>of York</font><font color=#BFBFBF> </font></p>","pageId":893,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1194,"lock":null}
20:13:19.481 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.482 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/3/11/1248
20:13:19.482 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1248,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet unpleasant day. Wind between SW &amp; WNW. Could not get to the ship. Received a letter from WBS informing me of my name being in the Gazette, which I see in this days papers. Dined at home. H harry, Cunningham &amp; and I took wine at the Albion &amp; in the evening finished at the Duke <font color=#BFBFBF>of York</font><font color=#BFBFBF> </font></p>","pageId":893,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1194,"lock":null}
20:13:19.482 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/3/12/1249
20:13:19.482 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1249,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning and wind SW. Received a letter from Alnwick from the adj<font color=#BFBFBF>utant</font> Crisp ordering me to join the Regiment. Walked to Tynemouth with the intention of taking a warm bath, but they are not yet open for the season. Returned &amp; went up to the Hope. <span class=highlight_yellow>Repairs</span> nearly finished. At high water they hauled her off the shore &amp; dropped her down to Custom House Quay. Toward the afternoon it began to blow very hard varying between SSW &amp; SSE &amp; increased to a gale which continued all night. Spent the evening at home writing etc.</p>","pageId":893,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1195,"lock":null}
20:13:19.482 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.483 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/3/12/1249
20:13:19.483 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1249,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning and wind SW. Received a letter from Alnwick from the adj<font color=#BFBFBF>utant</font> Crisp ordering me to join the Regiment. Walked to Tynemouth with the intention of taking a warm bath, but they are not yet open for the season. Returned &amp; went up to the Hope. <span class=highlight_yellow>Repairs</span> nearly finished. At high water they hauled her off the shore &amp; dropped her down to Custom House Quay. Toward the afternoon it began to blow very hard varying between SSW &amp; SSE &amp; increased to a gale which continued all night. Spent the evening at home writing etc.</p>","pageId":893,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1195,"lock":null}
20:13:19.483 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/3/13/1250
20:13:19.483 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1250,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning blowing fresh from WSW. Engaged at home all the morning packing up. Dined at home. Took wine with H Harry. A very rainy afternoon &amp; blowing hard from SSW. At the Abbey &amp; Mulstrum in the evening. Received a letter from WBS</p>","pageId":893,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1196,"lock":null}
20:13:19.483 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.483 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/3/13/1250
20:13:19.483 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1250,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning blowing fresh from WSW. Engaged at home all the morning packing up. Dined at home. Took wine with H Harry. A very rainy afternoon &amp; blowing hard from SSW. At the Abbey &amp; Mulstrum in the evening. Received a letter from WBS</p>","pageId":893,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1196,"lock":null}
20:13:19.483 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/3/14/1251
