20:13:19.532 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1336,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cold &amp; unpleasant day. Wind NE. Took a walk round by Tynemouth. Dined at home &amp; in the afternoon walked up to Billy Mill &amp; drank wine with Charlton. Bess came up in the car<font color=#BFBFBF>riage</font> &amp; a pretty finish we made of it.</p>","pageId":912,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1282,"lock":null}
20:13:19.532 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/5/27/1337
20:13:19.532 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1337,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning &amp; cool wind NE. Went by Dunn's coach to Newcastle with R Reed. Dined with him at the Half Moon House. He left by coach at 4 o'clock for Mr Ridley's near Chester-le-Street &amp; I returned to Shields by steam. Had some whisky toddy at the Albion &amp; afterwards called to see Bess whom I found very <span class=highlight_yellow>uncoale</span> from the <span class=highlight_yellow>brecisex</span> she <span class=highlight_yellow>accd</span> the night before.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Paid Hope's <span class=highlight_yellow>mo</span><span class=highlight_yellow> </span><span class=highlight_yellow>mo</span> &pound;16.10</p>","pageId":912,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1283,"lock":null}
20:13:19.532 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.533 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/5/27/1337
20:13:19.533 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1337,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning &amp; cool wind NE. Went by Dunn's coach to Newcastle with R Reed. Dined with him at the Half Moon House. He left by coach at 4 o'clock for Mr Ridley's near Chester-le-Street &amp; I returned to Shields by steam. Had some whisky toddy at the Albion &amp; afterwards called to see Bess whom I found very <span class=highlight_yellow>uncoale</span> from the <span class=highlight_yellow>brecisex</span> she <span class=highlight_yellow>accd</span> the night before.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Paid Hope's <span class=highlight_yellow>mo</span><span class=highlight_yellow> </span><span class=highlight_yellow>mo</span> &pound;16.10</p>","pageId":912,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1283,"lock":null}
20:13:19.533 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/5/28/1338
20:13:19.533 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1338,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another dull morning. The wind still from the old quarter NE. Walked to Tynemouth &amp; saw the troops fire a salute at 12 o'clock in honour of the King's birthday. Returned &amp; also saw the <font color=#BFBFBF>HMS </font>Orestes gun brig do the same &amp; man her yards. Dined at 4 o'clock with Mr Bradshaw in celebration of his wife's birthday, a very pleasant party &amp; most splendid dinner &amp; wines.</p>","pageId":913,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1284,"lock":null}
20:13:19.533 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.533 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/5/28/1338
20:13:19.533 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1338,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another dull morning. The wind still from the old quarter NE. Walked to Tynemouth &amp; saw the troops fire a salute at 12 o'clock in honour of the King's birthday. Returned &amp; also saw the <font color=#BFBFBF>HMS </font>Orestes gun brig do the same &amp; man her yards. Dined at 4 o'clock with Mr Bradshaw in celebration of his wife's birthday, a very pleasant party &amp; most splendid dinner &amp; wines.</p>","pageId":913,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1284,"lock":null}
20:13:19.533 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/5/29/1339
20:13:19.533 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1339,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning rather dull wind S by E. Attended morning service. Dined at home. Lockwood took dinner with me. Walked to Tynemouth in the afternoon. Took wine with Tibbs &amp; spent the evening in the castle yard &amp; Lockwood</p>","pageId":913,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1285,"lock":null}
20:13:19.533 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.533 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/5/29/1339
20:13:19.534 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1339,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning rather dull wind S by E. Attended morning service. Dined at home. Lockwood took dinner with me. Walked to Tynemouth in the afternoon. Took wine with Tibbs &amp; spent the evening in the castle yard &amp; Lockwood</p>","pageId":913,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1285,"lock":null}
20:13:19.534 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/5/3/1311
20:13:19.534 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1311,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull orning &amp; damp heavy been a good deal of rain in the night. Wind SE. Lord Howielt &amp; Mr Beaumont came into the town conducted by an immense crowd of people with bands &amp; colours, whom they addressed from a hustings erected in front on the Commercial. Turned out a very rainy afternoon. H Harry dined with us at the Mulstrum. In the evening gave Jonny Smith &pound;28.1.6 <span class=highlight_yellow>Int</span> for his mother.</p>","pageId":906,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1257,"lock":null}
20:13:19.534 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.534 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/5/3/1311
20:13:19.534 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1311,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull orning &amp; damp heavy been a good deal of rain in the night. Wind SE. Lord Howielt &amp; Mr Beaumont came into the town conducted by an immense crowd of people with bands &amp; colours, whom they addressed from a hustings erected in front on the Commercial. Turned out a very rainy afternoon. H Harry dined with us at the Mulstrum. In the evening gave Jonny Smith &pound;28.1.6 <span class=highlight_yellow>Int</span> for his mother.</p>","pageId":906,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1257,"lock":null}
20:13:19.534 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/5/30/1340
20:13:19.534 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1340,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind ESE. Received a letter from WBS. At Tynemouth all the morning. Dined with Griffiths, RM &amp; Dick RA at the castle. At the Mulstrum in the evening.</p>","pageId":913,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1286,"lock":null}
20:13:19.534 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
