20:13:19.535 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1341,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of delightful weather. Wind E by S. Took a walk to Tynemouth &amp; the Sands with Bess. Dined at 6 o'clock. At the Star &amp; Garter. With <span class=highlight_yellow>Mit</span>. Redhead who <span class=highlight_yellow>cosh</span> the dinner by <span class=highlight_yellow>locking</span> his pony to go to Eldon Square in &frac12; an hour. He did it in 33 minutes.</p>","pageId":913,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1287,"lock":null}
20:13:19.535 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/5/4/1312
20:13:19.535 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1312,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine sprint morning. A light breeze at NE. Tom Smith left for Newcastle after breakfast. Took a walk to Cullercoat Sands &amp; dined with Lockwood &amp; in the evening attended the theatre to <span class=highlight_yellow>se</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span><span class=highlight_yellow> beam</span>. At the Mustrum.</p>","pageId":906,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1258,"lock":null}
20:13:19.535 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.535 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/5/4/1312
20:13:19.535 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1312,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine sprint morning. A light breeze at NE. Tom Smith left for Newcastle after breakfast. Took a walk to Cullercoat Sands &amp; dined with Lockwood &amp; in the evening attended the theatre to <span class=highlight_yellow>se</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span><span class=highlight_yellow> beam</span>. At the Mustrum.</p>","pageId":906,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1258,"lock":null}
20:13:19.535 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/5/5/1313
20:13:19.535 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1313,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning &amp; at last a change of wind having got from the NW. Walked to Tynemouth &amp; from thence by the sands to Whitley Park and called upon Mr J Weight. Wind changes to NNE with heavy showers of hail &amp; rain in one of which I was caught &amp; got nearly wet through.  Returned home to dinner. Spent the evening at home.</p>","pageId":907,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1259,"lock":null}
20:13:19.535 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.536 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/5/5/1313
20:13:19.536 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1313,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning &amp; at last a change of wind having got from the NW. Walked to Tynemouth &amp; from thence by the sands to Whitley Park and called upon Mr J Weight. Wind changes to NNE with heavy showers of hail &amp; rain in one of which I was caught &amp; got nearly wet through.  Returned home to dinner. Spent the evening at home.</p>","pageId":907,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1259,"lock":null}
20:13:19.536 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/5/6/1314
20:13:19.536 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1314,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but cold. Wind NW. heavy changed from NE from which <span class=highlight_yellow>ash</span> it has been blowing fresh all night with a heavy sea. Dined at home. At Dr Drury's in the afternoon &amp; in the evening went to the theatre, but the house was so badly attended that <span class=highlight_yellow>Kean</span> would not perform. Finished at the Albion</p>","pageId":907,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1260,"lock":null}
