20:13:19.564 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/7/23/1398
20:13:19.564 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1398,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":23,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<figure>\r\n  <a href=\"https://www.google.co.uk/maps/@55.3478179,-1.6119057,3a,75y,8.95h,91.34t/data=!3m6!1e1!3m4!1s95CsW_l0SmZLJy3kVYXurQ!2e0!7i13312!8i6656?hl=en\" >\r\n    <img src=\"images/img2788-hermitage-inn-warkworth.png\" width=\"600px\" />\r\n    <figcaption>The Hermitage Inn, Warkworth</figcaption>\r\n  </a>\r\n</figure>","pageId":928,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":1344,"lock":null}
20:13:19.564 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/7/23/1399
20:13:19.564 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1399,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":23,"sequence":3.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful day. Ben Galbraith, Rob Snowdon &amp; I after breakfast, set off to fish at the Hermitage. I however turned off to begin at the Granary but the tide had risen too high. Walked up to the mill streams &amp; fished there all the morning. Fanny &amp; Bell Smith &amp; Emma Galbraith came down &amp; joined us &amp; we all dined together at the Hermitage <font color=#BFBFBF>Inn</font>. Fished up the <span class=highlight_yellow>w</span><span class=highlight_yellow>aterside</span> &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Morick</span> streams in the evening but had very poor sport. Got home to supper after spending a most delightful day.</p>","pageId":928,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1345,"lock":null}
20:13:19.564 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.564 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/7/23/1399
20:13:19.564 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1399,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":23,"sequence":3.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful day. Ben Galbraith, Rob Snowdon &amp; I after breakfast, set off to fish at the Hermitage. I however turned off to begin at the Granary but the tide had risen too high. Walked up to the mill streams &amp; fished there all the morning. Fanny &amp; Bell Smith &amp; Emma Galbraith came down &amp; joined us &amp; we all dined together at the Hermitage <font color=#BFBFBF>Inn</font>. Fished up the <span class=highlight_yellow>w</span><span class=highlight_yellow>aterside</span> &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Morick</span> streams in the evening but had very poor sport. Got home to supper after spending a most delightful day.</p>","pageId":928,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1345,"lock":null}
20:13:19.564 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/7/24/1400
20:13:19.564 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1400,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather. Tom Smith taken suddenly ill. Tom, Bea &amp; I drove down to church, returned home after calling upon Mr Clutterbuck by Amble. Dined at 3 o'clock &amp; took a walk with Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>albraith</font> &amp; Tom round the farm in the evening</p>","pageId":928,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1346,"lock":null}
20:13:19.564 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.565 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/7/24/1400
20:13:19.565 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1400,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather. Tom Smith taken suddenly ill. Tom, Bea &amp; I drove down to church, returned home after calling upon Mr Clutterbuck by Amble. Dined at 3 o'clock &amp; took a walk with Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>albraith</font> &amp; Tom round the farm in the evening</p>","pageId":928,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1346,"lock":null}
20:13:19.565 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/7/25/1401
20:13:19.565 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1401,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Beautiful weather. After breakfast, Tom drove Ben &amp; I into Alnwick being fair day. Called upon Ian W Smith who with others of the family being very unwell, we did not go in. Called upon Captain <span class=highlight_yellow>Wund</span> Forster &amp; got home to dinner at 5 o'clock.</p>","pageId":928,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1347,"lock":null}
20:13:19.565 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.565 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/7/25/1401
20:13:19.565 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1401,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Beautiful weather. After breakfast, Tom drove Ben &amp; I into Alnwick being fair day. Called upon Ian W Smith who with others of the family being very unwell, we did not go in. Called upon Captain <span class=highlight_yellow>Wund</span> Forster &amp; got home to dinner at 5 o'clock.</p>","pageId":928,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1347,"lock":null}
20:13:19.565 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/7/26/1402
20:13:19.565 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1402,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Most beautiful weather. Wind SW. Walked down after breakfast to Amble &amp; fish the Granary Stream but without success. Ben G<font color=#BFBFBF>albraith</font> &amp; Rob S<font color=#BFBFBF>mith</font> with me afterwards. Ben &amp; I bathed &amp; then joined Tom at Amble. Looked over his fields there. Turnips in a very bad state. Got home to dinner at 3 o'clock. Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Ellenth</span> dined with us. Mrs Scott much better.</p>","pageId":929,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1348,"lock":null}
20:13:19.565 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.566 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/7/26/1402
20:13:19.566 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1402,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Most beautiful weather. Wind SW. Walked down after breakfast to Amble &amp; fish the Granary Stream but without success. Ben G<font color=#BFBFBF>albraith</font> &amp; Rob S<font color=#BFBFBF>mith</font> with me afterwards. Ben &amp; I bathed &amp; then joined Tom at Amble. Looked over his fields there. Turnips in a very bad state. Got home to dinner at 3 o'clock. Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Ellenth</span> dined with us. Mrs Scott much better.</p>","pageId":929,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1348,"lock":null}
20:13:19.566 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/7/27/1403
20:13:19.566 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1403,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still delightful weather. After breakfast Tom &amp; I set off for Newcastle in his <span class=highlight_yellow>jones </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Auisn</span>. Stopped at Morpeth for two hours. Saw <span class=highlight_yellow>Shapton</span> &amp; got to Newcastle at 5 o'clock to dinner. Saw the High Sherriff, Mr <font color=#202122>Silvertop</font><font color=#202122> </font><font color=#202122>go out accompanied by a very numerous train of friends &amp; carriages to meet the judges. The High Sheriff turned out very handsome. Took a gig in the evening &amp; got home a little before 10 o'clock</font></p>","pageId":929,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1349,"lock":null}
20:13:19.566 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.566 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/7/27/1403
20:13:19.566 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1403,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still delightful weather. After breakfast Tom &amp; I set off for Newcastle in his <span class=highlight_yellow>jones </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Auisn</span>. Stopped at Morpeth for two hours. Saw <span class=highlight_yellow>Shapton</span> &amp; got to Newcastle at 5 o'clock to dinner. Saw the High Sherriff, Mr <font color=#202122>Silvertop</font><font color=#202122> </font><font color=#202122>go out accompanied by a very numerous train of friends &amp; carriages to meet the judges. The High Sheriff turned out very handsome. Took a gig in the evening &amp; got home a little before 10 o'clock</font></p>","pageId":929,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1349,"lock":null}
20:13:19.566 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/7/28/1404
20:13:19.566 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1404,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A glorious day. Wind SW. Went up to Newcastle by Dunn's Gig in the morning. Saw &amp; had some conversation about Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Haig</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>regagatted</span> &amp; placed below <span class=highlight_yellow>Lorain</span> &amp; Cleaning could make nothing of him. He <span class=highlight_yellow>evidently</span> the friend of the other <span class=highlight_yellow>Party</span>. <span class=highlight_yellow>went</span> go up ...</p>","pageId":929,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1350,"lock":null}
20:13:19.566 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.566 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/7/28/1404
20:13:19.567 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1404,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A glorious day. Wind SW. Went up to Newcastle by Dunn's Gig in the morning. Saw &amp; had some conversation about Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Haig</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>regagatted</span> &amp; placed below <span class=highlight_yellow>Lorain</span> &amp; Cleaning could make nothing of him. He <span class=highlight_yellow>evidently</span> the friend of the other <span class=highlight_yellow>Party</span>. <span class=highlight_yellow>went</span> go up ...</p>","pageId":929,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1350,"lock":null}
20:13:19.567 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/7/28/1405
20:13:19.567 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1405,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":28,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... to London &amp;see the Duke told Colonel Coulson it was my intention. Went to the courts, excessively hot, glad to get out again after strolling about with T<font color=#BFBFBF>om</font> Smith &amp; Dixon. Returned to Shields to dinner at 5 o'clock. Attended Mr Alderton's Committee room in the evening. At the Albion &amp; Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":930,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1351,"lock":null}
20:13:19.567 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.567 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/7/28/1405
20:13:19.567 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1405,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":28,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... to London &amp;see the Duke told Colonel Coulson it was my intention. Went to the courts, excessively hot, glad to get out again after strolling about with T<font color=#BFBFBF>om</font> Smith &amp; Dixon. Returned to Shields to dinner at 5 o'clock. Attended Mr Alderton's Committee room in the evening. At the Albion &amp; Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":930,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1351,"lock":null}
20:13:19.567 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/7/29/1406
20:13:19.567 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1406,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but very hot weather. Gave a draft on <span class=highlight_yellow>Cols</span> for balance of Premium and Hope clubs &pound;4.7.1 also a draft for &pound;6.15 <span class=highlight_yellow>momo</span> to be paid tomorrow. Attended Mr Ilderton's Committee room and came <span class=highlight_yellow>after</span> Lenskill Street. Dined at home. At the Committee Room again in the afternoon. A fine shower of rain in the afterwards. At the theatre &amp; Mulstrum in the evening</p>","pageId":930,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1352,"lock":null}
20:13:19.567 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
