20:13:19.579 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1420,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":19,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<figure>\r\n  <a href=\"https://southamptonlocalhistorycentre.files.wordpress.com/2014/11/lhf-journal-19-spring-2012.pdf\" >\r\n    <img src=\"images/img2792-baths-southampton.jpg\" width=\"600px\" />\r\n    <figcaption>Baths at Southampton</figcaption>\r\n  </a>\r\n</figure>","pageId":932,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":1366,"lock":null}
20:13:19.579 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/19/1421
20:13:19.579 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1421,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":19,"sequence":3.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning having been rain in the night. Wind fresh at WNW. In endeavouring to throw my portmanteau upon my shoulder, it being very heavy, I strained the muscles of my back very severely &amp; I fear I shall not soon recover from it. Pain very acute. Got on the coach at the White Horse <span class=highlight_yellow>ally</span> at 8 o'clock with WBS &amp; BBG &amp; started for Southampton where we arrived at &frac12; past 4 o'clock having had very fine weather &amp; a pleasant journey, the dust being laid by the rain. My back very painful &amp; with some difficulty got down to my lodgings &amp; to bed. We got Mrs Sands lodgings, the same as when at Southampton before.</p>","pageId":932,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1367,"lock":null}
20:13:19.579 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.580 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/19/1421
20:13:19.580 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1421,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":19,"sequence":3.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning having been rain in the night. Wind fresh at WNW. In endeavouring to throw my portmanteau upon my shoulder, it being very heavy, I strained the muscles of my back very severely &amp; I fear I shall not soon recover from it. Pain very acute. Got on the coach at the White Horse <span class=highlight_yellow>ally</span> at 8 o'clock with WBS &amp; BBG &amp; started for Southampton where we arrived at &frac12; past 4 o'clock having had very fine weather &amp; a pleasant journey, the dust being laid by the rain. My back very painful &amp; with some difficulty got down to my lodgings &amp; to bed. We got Mrs Sands lodgings, the same as when at Southampton before.</p>","pageId":932,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1367,"lock":null}
20:13:19.580 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/20/1422
20:13:19.580 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1422,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day &amp; blowing fresh from the WNW. I made an attempt to get out of bed this morning but my back was so bad I was obliged to lay down again. Breakfasted in bed. About 1 o'clock determined to make another attempt to get up &amp; dress myself &amp; with much difficulty &amp; pain &amp; the assistance of Ben I succeeded. After being up &amp; walking a short time, found myself much easier. Walked down to the Pier &amp; baths. Had a warm bath &amp; Mr Lee afterwards drove me home in his gig. The remainder of the afternoon &amp; evening found myself much relieved. About dinner time we had a very heavy squall with rain.</p>","pageId":932,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1368,"lock":null}
20:13:19.580 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.580 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/20/1422
20:13:19.580 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1422,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day &amp; blowing fresh from the WNW. I made an attempt to get out of bed this morning but my back was so bad I was obliged to lay down again. Breakfasted in bed. About 1 o'clock determined to make another attempt to get up &amp; dress myself &amp; with much difficulty &amp; pain &amp; the assistance of Ben I succeeded. After being up &amp; walking a short time, found myself much easier. Walked down to the Pier &amp; baths. Had a warm bath &amp; Mr Lee afterwards drove me home in his gig. The remainder of the afternoon &amp; evening found myself much relieved. About dinner time we had a very heavy squall with rain.</p>","pageId":932,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1368,"lock":null}
20:13:19.580 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/21/1423
20:13:19.580 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1423,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but blowing hard from the N by E. got up &amp; walked to Mr Lee's to breakfast. Walked down to the post office &amp; pier. Mr Lee drove me down to Shirley to call upon the Lewis. Dined at Mr Lees</p>","pageId":933,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1369,"lock":null}
20:13:19.580 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
