20:13:19.581 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1424,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning . Wind fresh from N by E. Played at billiards. The Lewis's came in &amp; dined at Mr Lees. Messrs Horsford &amp; Hawksley came in the evening. My back much better.</p>","pageId":933,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1370,"lock":null}
20:13:19.581 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/23/1425
20:13:19.581 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1425,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An exceedingly fine morning. Wind SW. Wrote to Garbull &amp; son of Hull to inform him when the Hope arrived etc. Dined at 2 o'clock at Mr lee's. The Lewis there &amp; embarked at &frac12; past 5 o'clock on board the Ariadne steam boat at 6 o'clock. Sailed for Guernsey with a good many passengers on board. A most beautiful evening. Moon light &amp; not a cloud to be seen. I walked the deck until we had passed the Needles &amp; went to bed at 12 o'clock. R Marsh with us</p>","pageId":933,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1371,"lock":null}
20:13:19.581 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.582 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/23/1425
20:13:19.582 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1425,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An exceedingly fine morning. Wind SW. Wrote to Garbull &amp; son of Hull to inform him when the Hope arrived etc. Dined at 2 o'clock at Mr lee's. The Lewis there &amp; embarked at &frac12; past 5 o'clock on board the Ariadne steam boat at 6 o'clock. Sailed for Guernsey with a good many passengers on board. A most beautiful evening. Moon light &amp; not a cloud to be seen. I walked the deck until we had passed the Needles &amp; went to bed at 12 o'clock. R Marsh with us</p>","pageId":933,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1371,"lock":null}
20:13:19.582 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/24/1426
20:13:19.582 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1426,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather cloudy. Wind SW. Got up at 6 o'clock at which time we were abreast of the ____ with Alderney, Sark &amp; Guernsey or S<sup>t</sup> Peters <font color=#BFBFBF>Port </font>in sight. Came to an anchor in Guernsey Sands about 8 o'clock &amp; landed after a most delightful passage. The town of St Peter port is beautifully situated above the bay upon a rising hill &amp; consists of a great many very excellent houses. It is of considerable extent but the streets are narrow. It however is rapidly improving and contains a great many beautiful private houses as well as public institutions, the collage the most striking ...</p>","pageId":933,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1372,"lock":null}
20:13:19.582 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.583 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/24/1426
20:13:19.583 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1426,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather cloudy. Wind SW. Got up at 6 o'clock at which time we were abreast of the ____ with Alderney, Sark &amp; Guernsey or S<sup>t</sup> Peters <font color=#BFBFBF>Port </font>in sight. Came to an anchor in Guernsey Sands about 8 o'clock &amp; landed after a most delightful passage. The town of St Peter port is beautifully situated above the bay upon a rising hill &amp; consists of a great many very excellent houses. It is of considerable extent but the streets are narrow. It however is rapidly improving and contains a great many beautiful private houses as well as public institutions, the collage the most striking ...</p>","pageId":933,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1372,"lock":null}
20:13:19.583 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/24/1427
20:13:19.583 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1427,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":24,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>We put up at Mousehole Hotel which is near the harbour &amp; the back bed room window commanded an exceedingly fine view of the sea adjacent islands. This hotel I recommend to all travellers both for the activity &amp; attention of the landlady &amp; her daughter Mrs ____ &amp; their reasonable charges. There is a small harbour formed by piers which is dry at low water. The rise and fall is very considerable being I should think thirty feet.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Having changed our cloths &amp; made ourselves comfortable we had breakfast. Much to our surprise met James Basher in the coffee room who agreed to join our party at dinner. After breakfast strolled out to see the town. Much pleased with the new market. Fish &amp; butchers etc. It is the best &amp; most perfect thing of the kind I ever saw or heard of.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Afterwards called upon Dr Proctor who was not at home. Went over &amp; saw the interior of the collage, a very fine institution &amp; apparently well placed &amp; of it were not for the low heavy square towers in the centre would be a handsome building.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>During the afternoon saw the <span class=highlight_yellow>presence</span> feast of the town &amp; walked up to the garrison which stands very high upon the south point of the bay which <span class=highlight_yellow>with</span> the town, it &amp; fort completely commands. In our rambles we met with old Charlton late of the firm of Scott &amp; Charlton, who came &amp; dined with us at 6 o'clock. He has lived about a year here. Saw Dr Proctor this afternoon. Much pleased with him.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p></p>","pageId":934,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1373,"lock":null}
20:13:19.583 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.583 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/24/1427
20:13:19.583 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1427,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":24,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>We put up at Mousehole Hotel which is near the harbour &amp; the back bed room window commanded an exceedingly fine view of the sea adjacent islands. This hotel I recommend to all travellers both for the activity &amp; attention of the landlady &amp; her daughter Mrs ____ &amp; their reasonable charges. There is a small harbour formed by piers which is dry at low water. The rise and fall is very considerable being I should think thirty feet.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Having changed our cloths &amp; made ourselves comfortable we had breakfast. Much to our surprise met James Basher in the coffee room who agreed to join our party at dinner. After breakfast strolled out to see the town. Much pleased with the new market. Fish &amp; butchers etc. It is the best &amp; most perfect thing of the kind I ever saw or heard of.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Afterwards called upon Dr Proctor who was not at home. Went over &amp; saw the interior of the collage, a very fine institution &amp; apparently well placed &amp; of it were not for the low heavy square towers in the centre would be a handsome building.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>During the afternoon saw the <span class=highlight_yellow>presence</span> feast of the town &amp; walked up to the garrison which stands very high upon the south point of the bay which <span class=highlight_yellow>with</span> the town, it &amp; fort completely commands. In our rambles we met with old Charlton late of the firm of Scott &amp; Charlton, who came &amp; dined with us at 6 o'clock. He has lived about a year here. Saw Dr Proctor this afternoon. Much pleased with him.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p></p>","pageId":934,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1373,"lock":null}
20:13:19.583 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/25/1428
20:13:19.583 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1428,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Most delightful weather. Wind SW. Had a warm bath this morning. At 12 o'clock we all got into a four wheeled vehicle. Drove round the greater part of the island, excepting the north angles, but there is nothing very picturesque or beautiful to be seen. Got home to dinner at 6 o'clock. Ian Basnes dines out</p>","pageId":935,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1374,"lock":null}
20:13:19.583 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.584 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/25/1428
20:13:19.584 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1428,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Most delightful weather. Wind SW. Had a warm bath this morning. At 12 o'clock we all got into a four wheeled vehicle. Drove round the greater part of the island, excepting the north angles, but there is nothing very picturesque or beautiful to be seen. Got home to dinner at 6 o'clock. Ian Basnes dines out</p>","pageId":935,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1374,"lock":null}
20:13:19.584 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/26/1429
20:13:19.584 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1429,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather. Amused ourselves by strolling about the markets etc. William went &amp; saw Dr Proctor again, but I being tired did not go. Having settled our bill, at 2 o'clock we again embarked on board the <font color=#000000>Ariadne</font><font size=3.4pt color=#000000>&nbsp;</font>&amp; sailed about 9 o'clock. The vessel most uncomfortably crowded, being about 155 passengers on board. We could not get berths. Passed close by the Island of Alderney. A fine sight.</p>","pageId":935,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1375,"lock":null}
20:13:19.584 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.584 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/26/1429
20:13:19.584 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1429,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather. Amused ourselves by strolling about the markets etc. William went &amp; saw Dr Proctor again, but I being tired did not go. Having settled our bill, at 2 o'clock we again embarked on board the <font color=#000000>Ariadne</font><font size=3.4pt color=#000000>&nbsp;</font>&amp; sailed about 9 o'clock. The vessel most uncomfortably crowded, being about 155 passengers on board. We could not get berths. Passed close by the Island of Alderney. A fine sight.</p>","pageId":935,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1375,"lock":null}
20:13:19.584 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/27/1430
20:13:19.584 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1430,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind SW. We arrived at Southampton at &frac12; past 5 o'clock, very much fatigued having been waiting to sleep or lay on deck all night. After waiting two hours &amp; a half at the custom house, we were obliged to go home to breakfast without our luggage. Dined at the Lewises at Shirley. Colonel Ogilvie &amp; Captain Cobb there.</p>","pageId":935,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1376,"lock":null}
20:13:19.584 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.585 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/27/1430
20:13:19.585 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1430,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind SW. We arrived at Southampton at &frac12; past 5 o'clock, very much fatigued having been waiting to sleep or lay on deck all night. After waiting two hours &amp; a half at the custom house, we were obliged to go home to breakfast without our luggage. Dined at the Lewises at Shirley. Colonel Ogilvie &amp; Captain Cobb there.</p>","pageId":935,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1376,"lock":null}
20:13:19.585 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/28/1431
20:13:19.585 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1431,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful day. Wind NW. Did not go to church. After lunch took a walk round by the Pier, the baths to the Itchen &amp; crossed the ferry to see PearTree Green. Returned to dinner</p>","pageId":936,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1377,"lock":null}
20:13:19.585 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.585 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/28/1431
20:13:19.585 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1431,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful day. Wind NW. Did not go to church. After lunch took a walk round by the Pier, the baths to the Itchen &amp; crossed the ferry to see PearTree Green. Returned to dinner</p>","pageId":936,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1377,"lock":null}
20:13:19.585 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/29/1432
20:13:19.585 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1432,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of delightful weather. Wind SW. Passed the morning in walking about, playing at billiards etc. Wrote to the Duke of Northumberland at court requesting him to grant me an interview &amp; complaining of my having been a second time passed for the purpose of Captains Loraiac &amp;  being placed over my head. Dined at Mr Lees</p>","pageId":936,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1378,"lock":null}
20:13:19.585 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.586 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/29/1432
20:13:19.586 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1432,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of delightful weather. Wind SW. Passed the morning in walking about, playing at billiards etc. Wrote to the Duke of Northumberland at court requesting him to grant me an interview &amp; complaining of my having been a second time passed for the purpose of Captains Loraiac &amp;  being placed over my head. Dined at Mr Lees</p>","pageId":936,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1378,"lock":null}
20:13:19.586 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/30/1433
20:13:19.586 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1433,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine day. Wind SW. Again engaged much the same as yesterday. Received a letter from Stephenson as which both Roads dated the 24<sup>th</sup> all well. The Lewis' &amp; Mr Carry dined with us. Major Falls of the 93<sup>rd</sup> &amp; Colonel Ogilvie came in the evening.</p>","pageId":936,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1379,"lock":null}
20:13:19.586 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.586 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/30/1433
20:13:19.586 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1433,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine day. Wind SW. Again engaged much the same as yesterday. Received a letter from Stephenson as which both Roads dated the 24<sup>th</sup> all well. The Lewis' &amp; Mr Carry dined with us. Major Falls of the 93<sup>rd</sup> &amp; Colonel Ogilvie came in the evening.</p>","pageId":936,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1379,"lock":null}
20:13:19.586 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/31/1434
20:13:19.586 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1434,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind SW. Bob Marsh left for London. Received an answer from the Duke referring me to Colonel Coulson. The Duke tied up with the gout &amp; not able to see me. Wrote to Stephenson, Major Falls, Colonel Ogilvie, William &amp; I went to Shirley to dine. Amused ourselves in rifle shooting</p>","pageId":936,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1380,"lock":null}
20:13:19.586 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.587 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/31/1434
20:13:19.587 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1434,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind SW. Bob Marsh left for London. Received an answer from the Duke referring me to Colonel Coulson. The Duke tied up with the gout &amp; not able to see me. Wrote to Stephenson, Major Falls, Colonel Ogilvie, William &amp; I went to Shirley to dine. Amused ourselves in rifle shooting</p>","pageId":936,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1380,"lock":null}
20:13:19.587 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/1/1435
20:13:19.587 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1435,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A miserable cold morning. Wind NE. rained continuously all day. After breakfast packed up my cloths &amp; spent the remainder of the day till dinner playing at billiards until Colonel Ogilvie, captain Lewis &amp; Harry RM. The former of whom with Major Falls dined with us.</p>","pageId":937,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1381,"lock":null}
20:13:19.587 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.587 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/1/1435
20:13:19.587 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1435,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A miserable cold morning. Wind NE. rained continuously all day. After breakfast packed up my cloths &amp; spent the remainder of the day till dinner playing at billiards until Colonel Ogilvie, captain Lewis &amp; Harry RM. The former of whom with Major Falls dined with us.</p>","pageId":937,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1381,"lock":null}
20:13:19.587 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/10/1446
20:13:19.587 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1446,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still damp unpleasant weather &amp; appearance of more rain. Wind NW. Called a little earlier upon Lord Beverley who had again gone out. Returned to Nottingham Place. At 2 o'clock walked down to Charring Cross &amp; there got upon a stage &amp; went to the Elephant &amp; castle &amp; thence walked to George Harry Apollo Buildings, Walworth &amp; saw Henry H. who I found laid up, being much bruised &amp; injured by the upsetting of a Blackwell Stage. Returned by stage &amp; dined at &frac12; past 5 o'clock with Richmond. Walked home early in the evening.</p>","pageId":940,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1392,"lock":null}
20:13:19.587 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.588 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/10/1446
20:13:19.588 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1446,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still damp unpleasant weather &amp; appearance of more rain. Wind NW. Called a little earlier upon Lord Beverley who had again gone out. Returned to Nottingham Place. At 2 o'clock walked down to Charring Cross &amp; there got upon a stage &amp; went to the Elephant &amp; castle &amp; thence walked to George Harry Apollo Buildings, Walworth &amp; saw Henry H. who I found laid up, being much bruised &amp; injured by the upsetting of a Blackwell Stage. Returned by stage &amp; dined at &frac12; past 5 o'clock with Richmond. Walked home early in the evening.</p>","pageId":940,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1392,"lock":null}
20:13:19.588 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/11/1447
20:13:19.588 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1447,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of dull cloudy weather, wind NNW &amp; every appearance of more rain. William, Emma &amp; Lee went to church. I did not go being obliged to take some <span class=highlight_yellow>Cuberts</span>. At 3 o'clock walked through the Regents Park to the Zoological Gardens with which &amp; the collection of wild beasts. I was much pleased. Returned home &amp; dressed &amp; went to dine with Mr Leaskill at 7 o'clock, a small party, only Captain Greg &amp; myself there</p>","pageId":941,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1393,"lock":null}
20:13:19.588 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.588 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/11/1447
20:13:19.588 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1447,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of dull cloudy weather, wind NNW &amp; every appearance of more rain. William, Emma &amp; Lee went to church. I did not go being obliged to take some <span class=highlight_yellow>Cuberts</span>. At 3 o'clock walked through the Regents Park to the Zoological Gardens with which &amp; the collection of wild beasts. I was much pleased. Returned home &amp; dressed &amp; went to dine with Mr Leaskill at 7 o'clock, a small party, only Captain Greg &amp; myself there</p>","pageId":941,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1393,"lock":null}
20:13:19.588 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/12/1448
20:13:19.588 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1448,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day but rather cloudy. Wind NW &amp; NNW. After lunch walked down to St James street &amp; saw the nobility etc. go to court. Her Majesty holding a drawing room.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Dined with C <span class=highlight_yellow>Reibarud</span>. J Griffith &amp; WBS there.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Mary Scott <font color=#BFBFBF>(daughter of WBS) </font>went to school</p>","pageId":941,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1394,"lock":null}
20:13:19.588 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.588 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/12/1448
20:13:19.588 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1448,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day but rather cloudy. Wind NW &amp; NNW. After lunch walked down to St James street &amp; saw the nobility etc. go to court. Her Majesty holding a drawing room.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Dined with C <span class=highlight_yellow>Reibarud</span>. J Griffith &amp; WBS there.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Mary Scott <font color=#BFBFBF>(daughter of WBS) </font>went to school</p>","pageId":941,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1394,"lock":null}
20:13:19.588 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/13/1449
20:13:19.588 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1449,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind N by W. Wrote to Robert Snowdon. Lee Scott went to School. Walked down to St James Street. His Majesty holding a Levee went along the Strand &amp; called on Bob Marsh. Returned &amp; saw the company come from the Levee. Walked with WBS in Regent Street at 6 o'clock dined alone at the Blue Ports &amp; afterwards went home.</p>","pageId":941,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1395,"lock":null}
20:13:19.588 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.590 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/13/1449
20:13:19.590 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1449,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind N by W. Wrote to Robert Snowdon. Lee Scott went to School. Walked down to St James Street. His Majesty holding a Levee went along the Strand &amp; called on Bob Marsh. Returned &amp; saw the company come from the Levee. Walked with WBS in Regent Street at 6 o'clock dined alone at the Blue Ports &amp; afterwards went home.</p>","pageId":941,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1395,"lock":null}
20:13:19.590 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/14/1450
20:13:19.590 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1450,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind from the N &amp; E. Wrote a letter to Lord Beverley &amp; afterwards called upon him &amp; found him at home, very graciously received. Entered into a long account &amp; related to him all the inconsistencies respecting any complaint about being <span class=highlight_yellow>regazzetted</span> etc, but he could not interfere at the same. Explained himself as not surprised at my feelings &amp; regret that it should have happened, but that he thought no further change could be made. Took a Paddington stage into the city. Called at the <span class=highlight_yellow>courting</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>homes</span> &amp; thence walked down to Mrs Carr's. Saw Boswell the <span class=highlight_yellow>Decgttonte</span> and dined there. Spent the evening &amp; returned by stage at night.</p>","pageId":942,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1396,"lock":null}
20:13:19.590 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.591 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/14/1450
20:13:19.591 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1450,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind from the N &amp; E. Wrote a letter to Lord Beverley &amp; afterwards called upon him &amp; found him at home, very graciously received. Entered into a long account &amp; related to him all the inconsistencies respecting any complaint about being <span class=highlight_yellow>regazzetted</span> etc, but he could not interfere at the same. Explained himself as not surprised at my feelings &amp; regret that it should have happened, but that he thought no further change could be made. Took a Paddington stage into the city. Called at the <span class=highlight_yellow>courting</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>homes</span> &amp; thence walked down to Mrs Carr's. Saw Boswell the <span class=highlight_yellow>Decgttonte</span> and dined there. Spent the evening &amp; returned by stage at night.</p>","pageId":942,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1396,"lock":null}
20:13:19.591 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/15/1451
20:13:19.591 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1451,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind N by E. Remained in the house till after 1 o'clock expecting Boswell, but he did not come. Walked round the inner circle of the Regents Park &amp; thence to Bob Marsh's  &amp; WBS &amp; I afterwards walked up by Regents Street home to dinner. Found that Boswell had called after I had left home.</p>","pageId":942,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1397,"lock":null}
20:13:19.591 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.591 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/15/1451
20:13:19.591 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1451,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind N by E. Remained in the house till after 1 o'clock expecting Boswell, but he did not come. Walked round the inner circle of the Regents Park &amp; thence to Bob Marsh's  &amp; WBS &amp; I afterwards walked up by Regents Street home to dinner. Found that Boswell had called after I had left home.</p>","pageId":942,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1397,"lock":null}
20:13:19.591 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/16/1452
20:13:19.591 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1452,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind from the north. Wrote to Lord Beverley requesting him to present one to His Majesty at the Levee on Wednesday next &amp; left the letter at his house. Thence walked down Regents Street. St James's Street round the park &amp; there to Richmond's. Walked again up Regents Street &amp; dined with Richmond at &frac12; past 5 o'clock</p>","pageId":943,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1398,"lock":null}
20:13:19.591 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.592 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/16/1452
20:13:19.592 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1452,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind from the north. Wrote to Lord Beverley requesting him to present one to His Majesty at the Levee on Wednesday next &amp; left the letter at his house. Thence walked down Regents Street. St James's Street round the park &amp; there to Richmond's. Walked again up Regents Street &amp; dined with Richmond at &frac12; past 5 o'clock</p>","pageId":943,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1398,"lock":null}
20:13:19.592 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/17/1453
20:13:19.592 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1453,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another delightful autumnal morning. Wind north. Received a note from H Harry to say they called upon me this morning. A little after 1 o'clock, he, Miss G Hurry &amp; Miss Fenwick called &amp; we drove to the Zoological Gardens. Afterwards to the Coliseum with which we were much delighted &amp; astonished &amp; most particularly with the Swiss Cottage &amp; arcade. Thence we drove to Walworth &amp; I dined with them. Walked home in the evening where I found a note from Lord Beverley saying he will have much pleasure in presenting me to His Majesty on Wednesday next.</p>","pageId":943,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1399,"lock":null}
20:13:19.592 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.592 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/17/1453
20:13:19.592 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1453,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another delightful autumnal morning. Wind north. Received a note from H Harry to say they called upon me this morning. A little after 1 o'clock, he, Miss G Hurry &amp; Miss Fenwick called &amp; we drove to the Zoological Gardens. Afterwards to the Coliseum with which we were much delighted &amp; astonished &amp; most particularly with the Swiss Cottage &amp; arcade. Thence we drove to Walworth &amp; I dined with them. Walked home in the evening where I found a note from Lord Beverley saying he will have much pleasure in presenting me to His Majesty on Wednesday next.</p>","pageId":943,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1399,"lock":null}
20:13:19.592 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/18/1454
20:13:19.592 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1454,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Slept in the house all the morning. Richmond called at 3 o'clock &amp; drove me out in his gig. Went round by Highgate &amp; Hampstead &amp; returned by Regent &amp; Hyde Park Home to dinner. Bob marsh also dined with us.</p>","pageId":943,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1400,"lock":null}
20:13:19.592 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.593 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/18/1454
20:13:19.593 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1454,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Slept in the house all the morning. Richmond called at 3 o'clock &amp; drove me out in his gig. Went round by Highgate &amp; Hampstead &amp; returned by Regent &amp; Hyde Park Home to dinner. Bob marsh also dined with us.</p>","pageId":943,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1400,"lock":null}
20:13:19.593 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/19/1455
20:13:19.593 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1455,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine morning. Rather cloudy. Wind SW. Expected Boswell up but he did not come until after I had started for the city. Went ...</p>","pageId":943,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1401,"lock":null}
20:13:19.593 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.593 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/19/1455
20:13:19.593 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1455,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine morning. Rather cloudy. Wind SW. Expected Boswell up but he did not come until after I had started for the city. Went ...</p>","pageId":943,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1401,"lock":null}
20:13:19.593 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/19/1456
20:13:19.593 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1456,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":19,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... to the office. Received a short letter from Bess, very angry for not writing to her. Called at Harman's about the Hope's Wyburn bill which has been lagging at the docks agent for my acceptance. Wrote to Rob<font color=#BFBFBF>er</font><sup>t</sup> S<font color=#BFBFBF>tephenson</font> to send it up. Called at J Chapman. Took a cab &amp; drove direct to St James. Called at the Lord Chamberlains office. Saw Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Master</span> who was very polite &amp; introduced me as to how I am to act at the Levee. Left a card with him. Walked home &amp; wrote to Bess blowing her up for her saucy letter. Dined at home</p>","pageId":944,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1402,"lock":null}
20:13:19.593 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.594 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/19/1456
20:13:19.594 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1456,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":19,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... to the office. Received a short letter from Bess, very angry for not writing to her. Called at Harman's about the Hope's Wyburn bill which has been lagging at the docks agent for my acceptance. Wrote to Rob<font color=#BFBFBF>er</font><sup>t</sup> S<font color=#BFBFBF>tephenson</font> to send it up. Called at J Chapman. Took a cab &amp; drove direct to St James. Called at the Lord Chamberlains office. Saw Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Master</span> who was very polite &amp; introduced me as to how I am to act at the Levee. Left a card with him. Walked home &amp; wrote to Bess blowing her up for her saucy letter. Dined at home</p>","pageId":944,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1402,"lock":null}
20:13:19.594 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/2/1436
20:13:19.594 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1436,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine clear morning. Wind NW but cool. After breakfasting with Mr Lee, got upon the Red Robin coach driven by Pearce at 10 o'clock &amp; started for Town where we arrived at &frac14; before 7 o'clock travelling a new &amp; by far the more beautiful road, over the Hog Back. Here we had a drenching shower of rain &amp; hail, through Guilford to town. Got to Nottingham Place at 7 o'clock. Had a cup of tea &amp; went to bed at 10 o'clock</p>","pageId":937,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1382,"lock":null}
20:13:19.594 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.594 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/2/1436
20:13:19.594 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1436,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine clear morning. Wind NW but cool. After breakfasting with Mr Lee, got upon the Red Robin coach driven by Pearce at 10 o'clock &amp; started for Town where we arrived at &frac14; before 7 o'clock travelling a new &amp; by far the more beautiful road, over the Hog Back. Here we had a drenching shower of rain &amp; hail, through Guilford to town. Got to Nottingham Place at 7 o'clock. Had a cup of tea &amp; went to bed at 10 o'clock</p>","pageId":937,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1382,"lock":null}
20:13:19.594 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/20/1457
20:13:19.594 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1457,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine autumnal morning. Wind WNW. Been a little rain in the night. Took an omnibus  into the city. At the offices. <del>Called upon Messrs Harman's statement they had sent the Hope's Wyburn bill to Shields for above</del>. Walked down to Miss Carr. Boswell gone down to Maldon this morning to the ship, which it appears, arrived there a fortnight ago, but he had not heard of it. Returned to the office &amp; WBS &amp; I walked out of the city together. Called at Bob Marsh's who afterwards joined is in Regents Street &amp; went to Nottingham Place to dinner</p>","pageId":944,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1403,"lock":null}
20:13:19.594 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.595 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/20/1457
20:13:19.595 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1457,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine autumnal morning. Wind WNW. Been a little rain in the night. Took an omnibus  into the city. At the offices. <del>Called upon Messrs Harman's statement they had sent the Hope's Wyburn bill to Shields for above</del>. Walked down to Miss Carr. Boswell gone down to Maldon this morning to the ship, which it appears, arrived there a fortnight ago, but he had not heard of it. Returned to the office &amp; WBS &amp; I walked out of the city together. Called at Bob Marsh's who afterwards joined is in Regents Street &amp; went to Nottingham Place to dinner</p>","pageId":944,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1403,"lock":null}
20:13:19.595 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/21/1458
20:13:19.595 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1458,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A rainy morning. Wind SSW very unfortunate, having to go to the Levee but hope it will clear up. WBS returned from the city at 1 o'clock. When I dressed myself in full fig &amp; drove in a hackney coach to St James Palace &amp; was presented to the King. The Levee was not numerously attended, being nearly all naval &amp; military ...</p>","pageId":944,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1404,"lock":null}
20:13:19.595 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.595 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/21/1458
20:13:19.595 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1458,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A rainy morning. Wind SSW very unfortunate, having to go to the Levee but hope it will clear up. WBS returned from the city at 1 o'clock. When I dressed myself in full fig &amp; drove in a hackney coach to St James Palace &amp; was presented to the King. The Levee was not numerously attended, being nearly all naval &amp; military ...</p>","pageId":944,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1404,"lock":null}
20:13:19.595 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/21/1459
20:13:19.595 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1459,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":21,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... decorated with all their orders, it was a very splendid &amp; magnificent sight. I thought I should have been very nervous, but was not at all so. I was nominally presented by the Earl of Beverley, but in fact by the Lord in waiting who was I believe was Lord ____  <font color=#BFBFBF>Earl of Gosford</font>   I had the honour of kissing the Kings hand. Lord Beverley found me out in the ante room &amp; was particularly polite &amp; attentive. After leaving the Levee, WBS &amp; Bob Marsh were waiting for me &amp; we walked along Pall Mall &amp; I got a coach &amp; drove home where I exchanged my dress &amp; returned to Richmond where I dined</p>","pageId":945,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1405,"lock":null}
20:13:19.595 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.596 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/21/1459
20:13:19.596 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1459,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":21,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... decorated with all their orders, it was a very splendid &amp; magnificent sight. I thought I should have been very nervous, but was not at all so. I was nominally presented by the Earl of Beverley, but in fact by the Lord in waiting who was I believe was Lord ____  <font color=#BFBFBF>Earl of Gosford</font>   I had the honour of kissing the Kings hand. Lord Beverley found me out in the ante room &amp; was particularly polite &amp; attentive. After leaving the Levee, WBS &amp; Bob Marsh were waiting for me &amp; we walked along Pall Mall &amp; I got a coach &amp; drove home where I exchanged my dress &amp; returned to Richmond where I dined</p>","pageId":945,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1405,"lock":null}
