20:13:19.597 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1461,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":22,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<figure>\r\n  <a href=\"https://www.google.co.uk/maps/@51.517132,-0.1352775,3a,75y,209.35h,106.25t/data=!3m6!1e1!3m4!1sCciW8XD9OFT7hqAUlA4XKA!2e0!7i16384!8i8192?hl=en\" >\r\n    <img src=\"images/img2805-blue-posts-pub.jpg\" width=\"600px\" />\r\n    <figcaption>Blue Posts Pub</figcaption>\r\n  </a>\r\n</figure>","pageId":945,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":1407,"lock":null}
20:13:19.597 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/22/1462
20:13:19.597 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1462,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":22,"sequence":3.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW. After breakfast WBS &amp; I went into the city &amp; at 11 o'clock embarked on board the Brocklebank steamer with an immense crowd of people &amp; preceded to Woolwich to see the <font color=#BFBFBF>HMS </font>Thunderer 74 a round ship launched. An immense concourse of people present. The King &amp; Queen arrived about 2 o'clock &amp; soon afterwards the Thunderer slid into the river in most beautiful style, the best launch I ever saw. Afterwards it was a grand &amp; imposing sight. Returned to town &amp; dined at the Blue Ports at 6 o'clock</p>","pageId":945,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1408,"lock":null}
20:13:19.597 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
