20:13:19.603 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1438,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<figure>\r\n  <a href=\"https://www.google.co.uk/maps/@51.5191111,-0.1409154,3a,75y,36.87h,100.58t/data=!3m6!1e1!3m4!1sSt-OkhktadIXO3pMUDzlJw!2e0!7i16384!8i8192?hl=en\" >\r\n    <img src=\"images/img2798-crown-and-septre-london.png\" width=\"600px\" />\r\n    <figcaption>Crown and Septre, London</figcaption>\r\n  </a>\r\n</figure>","pageId":938,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":1384,"lock":null}
20:13:19.603 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/4/1439
20:13:19.603 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1439,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":4,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind WSW. Breakfasted with C Richmond. He drove me in the afternoon around &amp; called upon Mrs Fletcher alias Hoffman then through the park by Pimlico &amp; Westminster to Greenwich. Called &amp; saw Geo<font color=#BFBFBF>rge</font> Watt and his wife, dined off whitebait etc. at the Crown &amp; Sceptre &amp; returned to town at 7 o'clock to tea. Got home in good time</p>","pageId":938,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1385,"lock":null}
20:13:19.603 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.603 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/4/1439
20:13:19.603 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1439,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":4,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind WSW. Breakfasted with C Richmond. He drove me in the afternoon around &amp; called upon Mrs Fletcher alias Hoffman then through the park by Pimlico &amp; Westminster to Greenwich. Called &amp; saw Geo<font color=#BFBFBF>rge</font> Watt and his wife, dined off whitebait etc. at the Crown &amp; Sceptre &amp; returned to town at 7 o'clock to tea. Got home in good time</p>","pageId":938,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1385,"lock":null}
20:13:19.603 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/5/1440
20:13:19.603 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1440,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind SW &amp; warm. Took the Paddington Stage into the city. Went to the office, nothing there, at the Coal Exchange. Saw there Brown &amp; Fenwick. Walked out of the city. Called upon Bob Marsh, strolled round by Pall Mall, St James's Street &amp; Piccadilly to Richmond's to dinner.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Got to Nottingham place at &frac12; past 10 o'clock &amp; found WBS Mary &amp; Lee had arrived.</p>","pageId":938,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1386,"lock":null}
20:13:19.603 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.603 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/5/1440
20:13:19.603 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1440,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind SW &amp; warm. Took the Paddington Stage into the city. Went to the office, nothing there, at the Coal Exchange. Saw there Brown &amp; Fenwick. Walked out of the city. Called upon Bob Marsh, strolled round by Pall Mall, St James's Street &amp; Piccadilly to Richmond's to dinner.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Got to Nottingham place at &frac12; past 10 o'clock &amp; found WBS Mary &amp; Lee had arrived.</p>","pageId":938,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1386,"lock":null}
20:13:19.603 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/6/1441
20:13:19.603 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1441,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Rather close. WBS went out the city. Arrived myself in the West End of the town all the morning. Dined at &frac12; past 5 o'clock with Junior Wright at Blackfriars, a small party <span class=highlight_yellow>there. </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Crg</span> Richmond, G Walters, Mr Gordon, G Kain &amp; two Miss Jobling's of Austlery</p>","pageId":938,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1387,"lock":null}
20:13:19.603 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.604 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/6/1441
20:13:19.604 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1441,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Rather close. WBS went out the city. Arrived myself in the West End of the town all the morning. Dined at &frac12; past 5 o'clock with Junior Wright at Blackfriars, a small party <span class=highlight_yellow>there. </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Crg</span> Richmond, G Walters, Mr Gordon, G Kain &amp; two Miss Jobling's of Austlery</p>","pageId":938,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1387,"lock":null}
20:13:19.604 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/7/1442
20:13:19.604 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1442,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull unpleasant morning. Heavy showers all day. Wind SW. Took a walk &amp; called upon Mr Lenskill &amp; Mr Ward. Met Captain Shepherd in the Burley Tea Arcade who has got appointed to the <font color=#BFBFBF>HMS </font>Melville 74 &amp; going out to the East Indies with <font color=#BFBFBF>admiral </font>Sir J<font color=#BFBFBF>ohn</font> Gore. Dined with Richmond at 6 o'clock to meet Mr &amp; Mrs Hoffman alias Mary Fletcher, his sister &amp; J Wrights</p>","pageId":939,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1388,"lock":null}
20:13:19.604 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.604 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/7/1442
20:13:19.604 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1442,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull unpleasant morning. Heavy showers all day. Wind SW. Took a walk &amp; called upon Mr Lenskill &amp; Mr Ward. Met Captain Shepherd in the Burley Tea Arcade who has got appointed to the <font color=#BFBFBF>HMS </font>Melville 74 &amp; going out to the East Indies with <font color=#BFBFBF>admiral </font>Sir J<font color=#BFBFBF>ohn</font> Gore. Dined with Richmond at 6 o'clock to meet Mr &amp; Mrs Hoffman alias Mary Fletcher, his sister &amp; J Wrights</p>","pageId":939,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1388,"lock":null}
20:13:19.604 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/8/1443
20:13:19.604 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1443,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<figure>\r\n  <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coronation_of_William_IV_and_Adelaide\" >\r\n    <img src=\"images/img2799-coronation-william-4th.jpg\" width=\"600px\" />\r\n    <figcaption>Coronation of William IV</figcaption>\r\n  </a>\r\n</figure>","pageId":939,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":1389,"lock":null}
20:13:19.604 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.605 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/8/1443
20:13:19.605 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1443,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<figure>\r\n  <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coronation_of_William_IV_and_Adelaide\" >\r\n    <img src=\"images/img2799-coronation-william-4th.jpg\" width=\"600px\" />\r\n    <figcaption>Coronation of William IV</figcaption>\r\n  </a>\r\n</figure>","pageId":939,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":1389,"lock":null}
20:13:19.605 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/8/1444
20:13:19.605 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1444,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":8,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind SW. The town all alive &amp; on the move towards Charring Cross, Pall Mall etc. to see Coronation Procession. After breakfast I went out but could not see the procession, so great was the crowd.  It appearing however to be near the United Services Club House after it had passed I saw major Falls who asked me in &amp; upon I had a very fine view of the whole of it on its return. A most splendid &amp; magnificent sight it was. Saw there Majesties very distinctly. Unfortunately there was a great deal of rain which they were in the Abbey which made the streets very dirty &amp; dampt the pleasure of the people no doubt very much. Dined with Bob Marsh &amp; in the evening saw the illuminations which passed good</p>","pageId":939,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1390,"lock":null}
20:13:19.605 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.605 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/8/1444
20:13:19.605 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1444,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":8,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind SW. The town all alive &amp; on the move towards Charring Cross, Pall Mall etc. to see Coronation Procession. After breakfast I went out but could not see the procession, so great was the crowd.  It appearing however to be near the United Services Club House after it had passed I saw major Falls who asked me in &amp; upon I had a very fine view of the whole of it on its return. A most splendid &amp; magnificent sight it was. Saw there Majesties very distinctly. Unfortunately there was a great deal of rain which they were in the Abbey which made the streets very dirty &amp; dampt the pleasure of the people no doubt very much. Dined with Bob Marsh &amp; in the evening saw the illuminations which passed good</p>","pageId":939,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1390,"lock":null}
20:13:19.605 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/9/1445
20:13:19.605 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1445,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very unpleasant day. Rained incessantly. Wind NW. Did not go out until 2 o'clock. Called upon Beverley who was not at home. Left my card. Walked down to Bob Marsh and Richmond's. Got a letter from Stephenson who will not be cleared so soon as expected. Answered it &amp; told him I should not be at Hull &amp; of my intention to leave town on Tuesday by the city of Edinburgh steamer. Called at Hawtry the dentists &amp; got my teeth cleaned. Dined at 6 o'clock at Nottingham Place. Richmond &amp; Bob Marsh dined with us.</p>","pageId":940,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1391,"lock":null}
20:13:19.605 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:19.606 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/9/1445
20:13:19.606 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1445,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very unpleasant day. Rained incessantly. Wind NW. Did not go out until 2 o'clock. Called upon Beverley who was not at home. Left my card. Walked down to Bob Marsh and Richmond's. Got a letter from Stephenson who will not be cleared so soon as expected. Answered it &amp; told him I should not be at Hull &amp; of my intention to leave town on Tuesday by the city of Edinburgh steamer. Called at Hawtry the dentists &amp; got my teeth cleaned. Dined at 6 o'clock at Nottingham Place. Richmond &amp; Bob Marsh dined with us.</p>","pageId":940,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1391,"lock":null}
