20:13:19.913 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":2097,"version":0,"year":1834,"month":6,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind SW. Walked round by the colliery &amp; Barnes. And afterwards to Amble where a Newcastle steam boat had arrived with a party. Commenced raining &amp; continued heavy for the rest of the day</p>","pageId":1082,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2037,"lock":null}
20:13:19.913 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1834/6/19/2098
20:13:19.913 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":2098,"version":0,"year":1834,"month":6,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind SW. Tom Smith drove Robert &amp; me to Felton <font color=#BFBFBF>where </font>we got upon the coach &amp; drove to the Race course. The sport very good. Mr Ord with Tomboy   won the gold cup again, having won it last year. Captain Potts won the Walls<font color=#BFBFBF>en</font>d Harrier Cup. Mr &amp; Mrs Dixon drove me out to Benton where I dined &amp; stayed all night.</p>","pageId":1082,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2038,"lock":null}
