20:13:21.260 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/100
20:13:21.260 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":100,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another very cold day. Wind NNE. Dined with the whist club invited by H Harry. Spent a pleasant day</p>","pageId":693,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":95,"lock":null}
20:13:21.260 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.261 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/100
20:13:21.261 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":100,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another very cold day. Wind NNE. Dined with the whist club invited by H Harry. Spent a pleasant day</p>","pageId":693,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":95,"lock":null}
20:13:21.261 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1000
20:13:21.261 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1000,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":7,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind WNW Captain Webb &amp; I with the boys went on a boat down to the rocks to fish but had no sport. Whilst there a part of the cliff gave way &amp; falling upon a poor girl who happened to be sitting underneath completely buried. She was soon dug out but dreadfully crushed &amp; quite dead. Her sister was close to her &amp; saw the accident. Returned home &amp; had some dinner at 5 o'clock. Spent the latter part of the evening at H Harry's</p>","pageId":833,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":951,"lock":null}
20:13:21.261 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.261 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1000
20:13:21.261 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1000,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":7,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind WNW Captain Webb &amp; I with the boys went on a boat down to the rocks to fish but had no sport. Whilst there a part of the cliff gave way &amp; falling upon a poor girl who happened to be sitting underneath completely buried. She was soon dug out but dreadfully crushed &amp; quite dead. Her sister was close to her &amp; saw the accident. Returned home &amp; had some dinner at 5 o'clock. Spent the latter part of the evening at H Harry's</p>","pageId":833,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":951,"lock":null}
20:13:21.261 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1001
20:13:21.261 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1001,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":7,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning but rather dull. Wind SSW &amp; blowing hard. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home. Again in the evening walked with Mark to Tynemouth. Heard this evening of Leddill having resigned! Consequently there is no possibility of a contest for the county</p>","pageId":833,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":952,"lock":null}
20:13:21.261 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.261 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1001
20:13:21.261 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1001,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":7,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning but rather dull. Wind SSW &amp; blowing hard. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home. Again in the evening walked with Mark to Tynemouth. Heard this evening of Leddill having resigned! Consequently there is no possibility of a contest for the county</p>","pageId":833,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":952,"lock":null}
20:13:21.261 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1002
20:13:21.261 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1002,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":7,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy morning blowing fresh at SW. Walked up to Tynemouth, met Harry Nicholson &amp; Richardson who had been over the bar with the Harvey bound to <span class=highlight_yellow>Ascksaget</span>. Dined at home. Took wine with Richardson &amp; spent a very pleasant afternoon &amp; in the evening again walked to Tynemouth</p>","pageId":833,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":953,"lock":null}
20:13:21.261 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.262 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1002
20:13:21.262 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1002,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":7,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy morning blowing fresh at SW. Walked up to Tynemouth, met Harry Nicholson &amp; Richardson who had been over the bar with the Harvey bound to <span class=highlight_yellow>Ascksaget</span>. Dined at home. Took wine with Richardson &amp; spent a very pleasant afternoon &amp; in the evening again walked to Tynemouth</p>","pageId":833,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":953,"lock":null}
20:13:21.262 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1003
20:13:21.262 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1003,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":7,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning But again blowing hard at WSW It large concussion of people with A professional gentleman with <span class=highlight_yellow>Baudr</span>, flags to went to Chester Whence they met the Bale &amp; brought him through the upper part of town to the George Tavern after which low sat down to an excellent &amp; well arranged discussion nearly 200 freehold all went off well. The latter part of the evening a glorious scene of drunk cuffs and confusion amongst the lower set of freeholders.</p>","pageId":834,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":954,"lock":null}
20:13:21.262 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
