20:13:21.266 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1012,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":7,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful sunny morning. Wind SW. Walked to Tynemouth. Could not go to church, having taken taken Cubebs. Our new vicar. Mr Reed preached today for the first time. Dined at home. A Harry and Allen took wine with me &amp; in the evening we walked to Tynemouth. An immense deal of company there</p>","pageId":836,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":963,"lock":null}
20:13:21.266 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1013
20:13:21.266 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1013,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":7,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most delightful morning. Very slight breeze from SW. Afterwards NW. A Harry &amp; I took a cullier &amp; went round ...</p>","pageId":836,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":964,"lock":null}
20:13:21.266 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.267 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1013
20:13:21.267 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1013,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":7,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most delightful morning. Very slight breeze from SW. Afterwards NW. A Harry &amp; I took a cullier &amp; went round ...</p>","pageId":836,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":964,"lock":null}
20:13:21.267 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1014
20:13:21.267 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1014,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":7,"day":26,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... to Tynemouth haven where I bathed. Walked home to dinner. In the afternoon we took I Richardson's coble &amp; went to sea mackerel fishing. Stood as far as Hartley Bay but caught nothing. Ran to the south &amp; brought up off the Herd where we caught several guraets &amp; got home at 10 o'clock after a very pleasant day</p>","pageId":837,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":965,"lock":null}
20:13:21.267 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
