20:13:21.278 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1036,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":8,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, but during the day heavy showers. Wind very variable, from all quarters of the compass. Having taken a <span class=highlight_yellow>seid</span><span class=highlight_yellow> </span><span class=highlight_yellow>le</span><span class=highlight_yellow>tz</span> could not go to church. Wallked with A Harry to Tynemouth. At church in the afternoon. Dined at 5 o'clock. Walked to Tynemouth in the evening. Turned out very wet. Finished at A Harry's</p>","pageId":842,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":985,"lock":null}
20:13:21.278 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1037
20:13:21.278 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1037,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":8,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy morning &amp; appearance of rain. Wind NW. Received a letter from Stephenson dated Archangel  29<sup>th</sup> June &amp; 3<sup>rd</sup> July. All well. Turned out a very fine day. A Harry &amp; I walked to Tynemouth. J Tinley, C Meleur,AI &amp; K Harry dined with us at 5 o'clock. Finished the evening &amp; stayed all night at the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":842,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":986,"lock":null}
