20:13:21.287 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1053,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":8,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW. William &amp; I took our guns &amp; walked with Mrs Tealey &amp; his wife.  Robersons to Marsden where the committee for the preservation for ship wrecks met &amp; tried several experiments. We afterwards returned by steam to Shields. H Harry dined with us at the Mulstrum at night</p>","pageId":845,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1001,"lock":null}
20:13:21.287 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1054
20:13:21.287 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1054,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW. Dined at home. William &amp; I walked to Preston in the afternoon. At home in the evening</p>","pageId":846,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1002,"lock":null}
20:13:21.287 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.288 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1054
20:13:21.288 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1054,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW. Dined at home. William &amp; I walked to Preston in the afternoon. At home in the evening</p>","pageId":846,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1002,"lock":null}
20:13:21.288 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1055
20:13:21.288 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1055,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Been a great deal of rain in the night &amp; still continuous heavy wind SW. Borrowed &pound;300 of Chapman's upon WBS &amp; I are named executors to pay bills &amp; for Mrs Scott's executors, funeral etc. Dined at home. In the evening there was a total eclipse of the moon</p>","pageId":846,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1003,"lock":null}
20:13:21.288 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.288 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1055
20:13:21.288 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1055,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Been a great deal of rain in the night &amp; still continuous heavy wind SW. Borrowed &pound;300 of Chapman's upon WBS &amp; I are named executors to pay bills &amp; for Mrs Scott's executors, funeral etc. Dined at home. In the evening there was a total eclipse of the moon</p>","pageId":846,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1003,"lock":null}
20:13:21.288 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1056
20:13:21.288 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1056,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very boisterous day with rain &amp; blowing hard from N by W to N &amp; NNE which brought on a heavy sea. HMS Cordelia came in. William &amp; I took the coach to Benton Lane &amp; walked up to Dixons, but they were at Belford.  Walked home to dinner. In the evening at a Quadrille party at J Tenby.</p>","pageId":846,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1004,"lock":null}
20:13:21.288 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.289 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1056
20:13:21.289 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1056,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very boisterous day with rain &amp; blowing hard from N by W to N &amp; NNE which brought on a heavy sea. HMS Cordelia came in. William &amp; I took the coach to Benton Lane &amp; walked up to Dixons, but they were at Belford.  Walked home to dinner. In the evening at a Quadrille party at J Tenby.</p>","pageId":846,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1004,"lock":null}
20:13:21.289 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1057
20:13:21.289 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1057,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; calmer weather. Wind NE. Engaged with WBS preparing for his departure. Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>albraith</font> with us. Dined at home. WBS embarked at 5 o'clock on board the Ahoy of <span class=highlight_yellow>Ed</span><span class=highlight_yellow>inb</span><span class=highlight_yellow>u</span><span class=highlight_yellow>rgh</span> Steamer for London. Wind changed to SSE. At the Duke &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Druries</span> in the evening.</p>","pageId":846,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1005,"lock":null}
20:13:21.289 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.289 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1057
20:13:21.289 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1057,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; calmer weather. Wind NE. Engaged with WBS preparing for his departure. Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>albraith</font> with us. Dined at home. WBS embarked at 5 o'clock on board the Ahoy of <span class=highlight_yellow>Ed</span><span class=highlight_yellow>inb</span><span class=highlight_yellow>u</span><span class=highlight_yellow>rgh</span> Steamer for London. Wind changed to SSE. At the Duke &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Druries</span> in the evening.</p>","pageId":846,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1005,"lock":null}
20:13:21.289 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1058
20:13:21.289 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1058,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind WNW. Walked to Tynemouth. Attended morning service with the military. Dined at home. Drury &amp; Sadler dined with me. H Harry came in afterwards. At the Mulstrum in the evening.</p>","pageId":846,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1006,"lock":null}
20:13:21.289 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
