20:13:21.295 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":107,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An exceedingly fine day &amp; mild wind W by S. Dined at the George Tavern. The dinner given by a party of married men consisting of J Dale president: Mr Clark   vise: A Dale, J Tindley, W C Wright. R Peach, A Metcalf     Bachelors: I Craig, Mr Horner, E Drurg, J Keilyside, A Harry</p>","pageId":694,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":102,"lock":null}
20:13:21.295 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1070
20:13:21.295 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1070,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning Wind WSW. Went down to the Hope. The starboard side as bad as the other. A number of the bolts bad. Walked to Tynemouth. Saw Potts hounds run a trail. Dined on board the Hope. I Dale, Harry French &amp; I took wine at the George &amp; spent a pleasant afternoon at the Mulstrum in the evening</p>","pageId":849,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1018,"lock":null}
20:13:21.295 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
