20:13:21.303 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1085,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":10,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind at SE. Received a letter from B B Galbralth. Dined at home. Spent the evening at Dr Wiltons</p>","pageId":852,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1033,"lock":null}
20:13:21.303 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1086
20:13:21.303 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1086,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":10,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp morning. Wind SW. A great many light ships off the bar. Went to church. Dined at home. Took wine with Mr Allen. Walked to Tynemouth. In the evening. Saw Ann. H Harry spent the evening with me.</p>","pageId":852,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1034,"lock":null}
20:13:21.303 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.303 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1086
20:13:21.303 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1086,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":10,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp morning. Wind SW. A great many light ships off the bar. Went to church. Dined at home. Took wine with Mr Allen. Walked to Tynemouth. In the evening. Saw Ann. H Harry spent the evening with me.</p>","pageId":852,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1034,"lock":null}
20:13:21.303 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1087
20:13:21.303 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1087,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":10,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning Wind NW. Sent &amp; brought Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>albraith</font> home. Mrs Man having died last night. Dined at home. Walked to Tynemouth &amp; saw the 80<sup>th</sup> inspected by General Bouverie Spent the evening with H Harry. Wrote to WBS</p>","pageId":852,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1035,"lock":null}
20:13:21.303 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.304 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1087
20:13:21.304 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1087,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":10,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning Wind NW. Sent &amp; brought Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>albraith</font> home. Mrs Man having died last night. Dined at home. Walked to Tynemouth &amp; saw the 80<sup>th</sup> inspected by General Bouverie Spent the evening with H Harry. Wrote to WBS</p>","pageId":852,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1035,"lock":null}
20:13:21.304 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1088
20:13:21.304 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1088,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":10,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful autumnal morning &amp; wind NW. Walked with H Harry round by the rocks. Tynemouth Cullercoats Sands &amp; fields, home. Dined at home &amp; spent the afternoon at Dr <span class=highlight_yellow>Dr</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span><span class=highlight_yellow>w</span><span class=highlight_yellow>y's</span> garden. In the evening at the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":852,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1036,"lock":null}
20:13:21.304 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.304 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1088
20:13:21.304 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1088,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":10,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful autumnal morning &amp; wind NW. Walked with H Harry round by the rocks. Tynemouth Cullercoats Sands &amp; fields, home. Dined at home &amp; spent the afternoon at Dr <span class=highlight_yellow>Dr</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span><span class=highlight_yellow>w</span><span class=highlight_yellow>y's</span> garden. In the evening at the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":852,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1036,"lock":null}
20:13:21.304 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1089
20:13:21.304 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1089,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":10,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning Wind NNW. Mrs Dixon came down before I was dressed &amp; took Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>albraith</font> to Newcastle with her. Dined at home. Allen fed with me. &amp; we afterwards spend the afternoon on board the Broderick. At the Mulstrum in the evening</p>","pageId":853,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1037,"lock":null}
20:13:21.304 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.305 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1089
20:13:21.305 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1089,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":10,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning Wind NNW. Mrs Dixon came down before I was dressed &amp; took Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>albraith</font> to Newcastle with her. Dined at home. Allen fed with me. &amp; we afterwards spend the afternoon on board the Broderick. At the Mulstrum in the evening</p>","pageId":853,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1037,"lock":null}
20:13:21.305 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/109
20:13:21.305 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":109,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind WSW. Received a most distressing letter from Mr Vernon Rector of Carlow of the poor Bafer being very ill of a typhous fever. I therefore have determined to set off for carlow in the morning from South Shields at 5 o'clock by Pelot Leeds coach</p>","pageId":694,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":104,"lock":null}
20:13:21.305 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
