20:13:21.305 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":109,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind WSW. Received a most distressing letter from Mr Vernon Rector of Carlow of the poor Bafer being very ill of a typhous fever. I therefore have determined to set off for carlow in the morning from South Shields at 5 o'clock by Pelot Leeds coach</p>","pageId":694,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":104,"lock":null}
20:13:21.305 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1090
20:13:21.305 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1090,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":10,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Beautiful weather Wind NW. In the house all the morning having taken medicine. Dined at home. At Allens in the afternoon &amp; in the evening at the whist club</p>","pageId":853,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1038,"lock":null}
