20:13:21.325 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1128,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":11,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Been a great deal of rain in the night. Wind SW. Went to church. Walked to Tynemouth in the afternoon Dined at J Tealays. Captain Deans &amp; two lieutenants of HMS Childers there. Received a parcel from WBS by J H Richardson, deeds <span class=highlight_yellow>for</span> silver spoon</p>","pageId":861,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1076,"lock":null}
20:13:21.325 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1129
20:13:21.325 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1129,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":11,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine cold morning Wind WSW. Received a letter from WBS with Hope's archangel account but not <span class=highlight_yellow>reliance</span> the delivered very little more than <span class=highlight_yellow>good</span> deals Paid Robert &amp; Leadbetter their &frac14; year wages &pound;10.11/- draft on chapmans exor account Dined at home. Called on J Young Paid Mrs Wright for E<font color=#BFBFBF>mma</font> Galbraiths education &pound;13.3.9 at the theatre &amp; Mulstrum in the evening</p>","pageId":861,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1077,"lock":null}
20:13:21.325 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.325 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1129
20:13:21.325 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1129,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":11,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine cold morning Wind WSW. Received a letter from WBS with Hope's archangel account but not <span class=highlight_yellow>reliance</span> the delivered very little more than <span class=highlight_yellow>good</span> deals Paid Robert &amp; Leadbetter their &frac14; year wages &pound;10.11/- draft on chapmans exor account Dined at home. Called on J Young Paid Mrs Wright for E<font color=#BFBFBF>mma</font> Galbraiths education &pound;13.3.9 at the theatre &amp; Mulstrum in the evening</p>","pageId":861,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1077,"lock":null}
20:13:21.325 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/113
20:13:21.325 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":113,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>During the whole of last night we had a heavy sea &amp; foul wind blowing WSW very hard, to contend with but fortunately a fine boat under us. As it was low water when we started, we overtook to steam Office packit at anchor, at the Rock not able to proceed for want of water, having left 2 &frac12;  hours before us so that after all, I lost no time, no thanks to the rascally clerks at the coach office. We kept company all night &amp; after a tedious passage arrived at the custom House quay, Dublin at 3 o'clock PM. Took my luggage to Mackens Hotel, Dawson Street where I stayed all night</p>","pageId":694,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":108,"lock":null}
20:13:21.325 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.325 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/113
20:13:21.325 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":113,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>During the whole of last night we had a heavy sea &amp; foul wind blowing WSW very hard, to contend with but fortunately a fine boat under us. As it was low water when we started, we overtook to steam Office packit at anchor, at the Rock not able to proceed for want of water, having left 2 &frac12;  hours before us so that after all, I lost no time, no thanks to the rascally clerks at the coach office. We kept company all night &amp; after a tedious passage arrived at the custom House quay, Dublin at 3 o'clock PM. Took my luggage to Mackens Hotel, Dawson Street where I stayed all night</p>","pageId":694,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":108,"lock":null}
20:13:21.326 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1130
