20:13:21.327 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1132,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":11,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A showery morning Wind NE. Been a great deal of rain in the night. Sea high. Paid Gibson butcher bill &frac14; of year &pound;4.9/- also executors of Scott <span class=highlight_yellow>painer</span> &pound;3.8- for the home &amp; &pound;12.19/- property. Walked to Tynemouth &amp; called upon two officers of the 15<sup>th</sup> regiment Hind &amp; <font color=#A6A6A6>[         ]</font> afterwards. Walked up &amp; dined at the Point with Sadby. Attended the whist club in the evening &amp; the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":861,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1080,"lock":null}
20:13:21.327 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1133
20:13:21.327 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1133,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":11,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty morning. Wind light at SW. Walked with Cunningham &amp; A Richardson round by the fields to Cullercoats, returning by the <span class=highlight_yellow>jany</span> &amp; Tynemouth home to dinner. In the afternoon at the billiard room &amp; at the Albion in the evening</p>","pageId":861,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1081,"lock":null}
