20:13:21.331 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1141,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":11,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Wintery weather and blowing strong from SE. On board the Hope people engaged with the wind <span class=highlight_yellow>lafe</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>preparing</span> for new barrel &amp; paul bits. On breaking the old barrel off, found the wind <span class=highlight_yellow>lefs</span> sprung &amp; rotten. Obliged to condemn it. Dined at home. In the billiard room afternoon &amp; at the whist club. In the evening  at the Duke.</p>","pageId":862,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1089,"lock":null}
20:13:21.331 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1142
20:13:21.331 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1142,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":11,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of stormy weather.  Still blowing a gale at ESE. Did not go to church. Dined at home. H Harry &amp; Nicholson came in &amp; took wine with me. Spent the evening at the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":863,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1090,"lock":null}
