20:13:21.339 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":116,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":17,"sequence":3.0000,"text":"<figure>\r\n  <img src=\"images/img2842-image-map-carlow.jpg\" width=\"600px\" />\r\n  <figcaption>Map of Carlow</figcaption>\r\n</figure>","pageId":null,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":null,"lock":null}
20:13:21.339 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1160
20:13:21.339 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1160,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very dull thick &amp; raining morning. Wind SW but little of it. Received  a letter from WBS answered it informing him of the sailing of the Hope &amp; Dined at home.</p>\r\n<p>At the Albion in the evening, for the benefit of Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>P</span><span class=highlight_yellow>er</span><span class=highlight_yellow>rs</span>, the <span class=highlight_yellow>vishrak</span> as the bells started of the gents of the commercial newsroom but not more than three or four there. Called at the Mulstrum</p>\r\n<p>HMS Childers came</p>\r\n<p>Answered WBS's letter informing him also that chapman had agreed to service the note of &pound;300 for four months. They carried &pound;50 to my account remitted by WBS</p>","pageId":867,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1108,"lock":null}
20:13:21.339 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.340 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1160
20:13:21.340 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1160,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very dull thick &amp; raining morning. Wind SW but little of it. Received  a letter from WBS answered it informing him of the sailing of the Hope &amp; Dined at home.</p>\r\n<p>At the Albion in the evening, for the benefit of Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>P</span><span class=highlight_yellow>er</span><span class=highlight_yellow>rs</span>, the <span class=highlight_yellow>vishrak</span> as the bells started of the gents of the commercial newsroom but not more than three or four there. Called at the Mulstrum</p>\r\n<p>HMS Childers came</p>\r\n<p>Answered WBS's letter informing him also that chapman had agreed to service the note of &pound;300 for four months. They carried &pound;50 to my account remitted by WBS</p>","pageId":867,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1108,"lock":null}
20:13:21.340 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1161
20:13:21.340 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1161,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind SW Dined at home. HMS <span class=highlight_yellow>Jacasacy</span> came into harbour to lay as a guard ship. At the billiard room &amp; whist club in the evening</p>","pageId":867,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1109,"lock":null}
20:13:21.340 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.340 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1161
20:13:21.340 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1161,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind SW Dined at home. HMS <span class=highlight_yellow>Jacasacy</span> came into harbour to lay as a guard ship. At the billiard room &amp; whist club in the evening</p>","pageId":867,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1109,"lock":null}
20:13:21.340 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1162
20:13:21.340 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1162,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>In the night it began to blow very hard from the NNE. &amp; continued pretty near a gale the whole of the day from that to NE with heavy showers of hail &amp; snow &amp; high sea. Another <span class=highlight_yellow>catic</span> put in making two, live government steamers, a Green Boy, 28 gun frigate in the harbour. Attended a public meeting for the purpose of entering this resolution with regard to the Rail road. Dined at home. At the billiard &amp; news rooms &amp; finished at the Duke of York. Got &pound;5 of chapman</p>","pageId":867,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1110,"lock":null}
20:13:21.340 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.341 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1162
20:13:21.341 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1162,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>In the night it began to blow very hard from the NNE. &amp; continued pretty near a gale the whole of the day from that to NE with heavy showers of hail &amp; snow &amp; high sea. Another <span class=highlight_yellow>catic</span> put in making two, live government steamers, a Green Boy, 28 gun frigate in the harbour. Attended a public meeting for the purpose of entering this resolution with regard to the Rail road. Dined at home. At the billiard &amp; news rooms &amp; finished at the Duke of York. Got &pound;5 of chapman</p>","pageId":867,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1110,"lock":null}
20:13:21.341 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1163
20:13:21.341 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1163,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>it blew very hard last night from the NE with showers of hail &amp; snow, but towards morning relented &amp; at breakfast time wind NW. But at sea still apparently <span class=highlight_yellow>Easta</span> of north. Paid Ed: Keids <span class=highlight_yellow>moshvo</span> &pound;1.13.9 &frac14; years wages. Dined at home. Attended the whist club at Craigs in the evening. Frosty</p>","pageId":868,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1111,"lock":null}
20:13:21.341 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.341 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1163
20:13:21.341 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1163,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>it blew very hard last night from the NE with showers of hail &amp; snow, but towards morning relented &amp; at breakfast time wind NW. But at sea still apparently <span class=highlight_yellow>Easta</span> of north. Paid Ed: Keids <span class=highlight_yellow>moshvo</span> &pound;1.13.9 &frac14; years wages. Dined at home. Attended the whist club at Craigs in the evening. Frosty</p>","pageId":868,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1111,"lock":null}
20:13:21.341 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1164
20:13:21.341 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1164,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>More moderate &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>rainy</span> weather. Wind W by S. A frost during the night. Did not go to church. Read the service at home. In the afternoon it came on to blow a heavy gale of wind at NW. Many ships got to sea.</p>\r\n<p>HMS Chelders running to go to sea but at blowing hard with a heavy fresh in the river, the ships were quite unmanageable. The first officer on board the cutter &amp; threw to the opposite side of the river &amp; letting go her anchor prevented her going to shore. Some <span class=highlight_yellow>coll</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span><span class=highlight_yellow>cse</span> there got foul of her &amp; finally she was prevented going to sea &amp; obliged next tide to move again in her old birth. Dined with J Tenley where the officer was expected but prevented coming.</p>\r\n<p>10 o'clock pm calmer weather again</p>","pageId":868,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1112,"lock":null}
20:13:21.341 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.341 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1164
20:13:21.341 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1164,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>More moderate &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>rainy</span> weather. Wind W by S. A frost during the night. Did not go to church. Read the service at home. In the afternoon it came on to blow a heavy gale of wind at NW. Many ships got to sea.</p>\r\n<p>HMS Chelders running to go to sea but at blowing hard with a heavy fresh in the river, the ships were quite unmanageable. The first officer on board the cutter &amp; threw to the opposite side of the river &amp; letting go her anchor prevented her going to shore. Some <span class=highlight_yellow>coll</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span><span class=highlight_yellow>cse</span> there got foul of her &amp; finally she was prevented going to sea &amp; obliged next tide to move again in her old birth. Dined with J Tenley where the officer was expected but prevented coming.</p>\r\n<p>10 o'clock pm calmer weather again</p>","pageId":868,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1112,"lock":null}
20:13:21.341 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1165
20:13:21.341 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1165,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>During the night the wind veered round to the NE. Blowing half a gale and a heavy sea came on. The <font color=#BFBFBF>HMS </font>Childers moored into Peggy's hole again. Cunningham dined with me. At the billiard room in the afternoon. J Agusley got his discharge today from hews &amp; billiard room having given himself up to drunkenness. At the theatre in the evening. The bespeak of the officers of the garrison.</p>\r\n<p>P J Hutchison &pound;2.16.3 averages</p>","pageId":869,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1113,"lock":null}
20:13:21.341 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.342 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1165
20:13:21.342 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1165,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>During the night the wind veered round to the NE. Blowing half a gale and a heavy sea came on. The <font color=#BFBFBF>HMS </font>Childers moored into Peggy's hole again. Cunningham dined with me. At the billiard room in the afternoon. J Agusley got his discharge today from hews &amp; billiard room having given himself up to drunkenness. At the theatre in the evening. The bespeak of the officers of the garrison.</p>\r\n<p>P J Hutchison &pound;2.16.3 averages</p>","pageId":869,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1113,"lock":null}
20:13:21.342 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1166
20:13:21.342 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1166,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, rather Cold. Wind W by N.  Sea fallen. Walked up to the Point to dine with Sadler. Spent a pleasant day</p>","pageId":869,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1114,"lock":null}
20:13:21.342 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
