20:13:21.356 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1193,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another foggy morning. Wind about west. On board the Hope, finished her loading, but did not go to sea, the weather having such an unsettled appearance &amp; wind so far from the southward. Dined at home. In the evening attended the whist club at Mr Gortlier R A at Tynemouth Place</p>","pageId":877,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1139,"lock":null}
20:13:21.356 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1194
20:13:21.356 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1194,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of foggy weather. Wind SW. Did not go to church as Mr Burdan was to sit in our pew to try how he liked it before he would determine upon taking it. Dined at home. Dr Drury &amp; friends came in &amp; took a glass of wine with me. In the evening at the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":877,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1140,"lock":null}
20:13:21.356 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.356 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1194
20:13:21.356 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1194,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of foggy weather. Wind SW. Did not go to church as Mr Burdan was to sit in our pew to try how he liked it before he would determine upon taking it. Dined at home. Dr Drury &amp; friends came in &amp; took a glass of wine with me. In the evening at the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":877,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1140,"lock":null}
20:13:21.356 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1195
20:13:21.356 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1195,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still very unpleasant foggy weather. Wind SSW. Received a letter from WBS. Sent him a copy of Chapmans book for the last quarter, also gave him authority to apply to the Duke for a commission in the Northumbria Militia. Dined at home. Wind freshened at SE &amp; every appearance of bad weather.</p>","pageId":877,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1141,"lock":null}
20:13:21.356 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.357 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1195
20:13:21.357 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1195,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still very unpleasant foggy weather. Wind SSW. Received a letter from WBS. Sent him a copy of Chapmans book for the last quarter, also gave him authority to apply to the Duke for a commission in the Northumbria Militia. Dined at home. Wind freshened at SE &amp; every appearance of bad weather.</p>","pageId":877,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1141,"lock":null}
20:13:21.357 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1196
20:13:21.357 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1196,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very damp foggy morning. Wind fresh at SE &amp; a good deal of sea. Dined at 5 o'clock with the Gastling RA Tynemouth Place. A very pleasant party. Got home before1 o'clock in the morning. Gave notes to the Premium &amp; Hope clubs of the Hope being loaded. Leadbetter went to Newcastle</p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1142,"lock":null}
20:13:21.357 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.357 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1196
20:13:21.357 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1196,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very damp foggy morning. Wind fresh at SE &amp; a good deal of sea. Dined at 5 o'clock with the Gastling RA Tynemouth Place. A very pleasant party. Got home before1 o'clock in the morning. Gave notes to the Premium &amp; Hope clubs of the Hope being loaded. Leadbetter went to Newcastle</p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1142,"lock":null}
20:13:21.357 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1197
20:13:21.357 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1197,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp &amp; foggy weather. Still continuing with a SE wind. <span class=highlight_yellow>Signed</span> the <span class=highlight_yellow>book</span> for the Hope's <span class=highlight_yellow>cassign</span> of <span class=highlight_yellow>oxd</span>. <span class=highlight_yellow>Redheangh</span> for &pound;153.18.8 date 14<sup>th</sup> Jan at 60 days on WBS. Leadbetter not having returned from Newcastle. Robert &amp; I dined on board the Hope. At the Albion in the evening. Leadbetter got home in the evening.</p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1143,"lock":null}
20:13:21.357 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.358 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1197
20:13:21.358 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1197,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp &amp; foggy weather. Still continuing with a SE wind. <span class=highlight_yellow>Signed</span> the <span class=highlight_yellow>book</span> for the Hope's <span class=highlight_yellow>cassign</span> of <span class=highlight_yellow>oxd</span>. <span class=highlight_yellow>Redheangh</span> for &pound;153.18.8 date 14<sup>th</sup> Jan at 60 days on WBS. Leadbetter not having returned from Newcastle. Robert &amp; I dined on board the Hope. At the Albion in the evening. Leadbetter got home in the evening.</p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1143,"lock":null}
20:13:21.358 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1198
20:13:21.358 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1198,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very rainy &amp; foggy day &amp; blowing strong from SE &amp; high sea. Sent the bill for the Hope's cargo by Dunn the <span class=highlight_yellow>coach</span><span class=highlight_yellow>man</span> to Mr Heindhaigh. Received a letter from Margaret Scott of Crathorn, I having forgot to send her 20/- her quarters allowance. Sent it by return of post. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; the whist club in the evening. Drew upon Chapman for &pound;5</p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1144,"lock":null}
20:13:21.358 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.358 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1198
20:13:21.358 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1198,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very rainy &amp; foggy day &amp; blowing strong from SE &amp; high sea. Sent the bill for the Hope's cargo by Dunn the <span class=highlight_yellow>coach</span><span class=highlight_yellow>man</span> to Mr Heindhaigh. Received a letter from Margaret Scott of Crathorn, I having forgot to send her 20/- her quarters allowance. Sent it by return of post. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; the whist club in the evening. Drew upon Chapman for &pound;5</p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1144,"lock":null}
20:13:21.358 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1199
20:13:21.358 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1199,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning blowing hard &amp; has been all night from the E by S &amp; ESE with a heavy sea. On board the Hope. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; the Albion &amp; Mulstrum in the evening. Gave Bess a turn, <u>first time</u><span class=underline_double> since</span></p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1145,"lock":null}
20:13:21.358 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.358 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1199
20:13:21.358 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1199,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning blowing hard &amp; has been all night from the E by S &amp; ESE with a heavy sea. On board the Hope. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; the Albion &amp; Mulstrum in the evening. Gave Bess a turn, <u>first time</u><span class=underline_double> since</span></p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1145,"lock":null}
20:13:21.358 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/12
20:13:21.358 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":12,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Dined with Mrs Scott &amp; spent the evening at home. Wind &amp; weather the same as yesterday</p>","pageId":687,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":9,"lock":null}
20:13:21.358 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.359 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/12
20:13:21.359 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":12,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Dined with Mrs Scott &amp; spent the evening at home. Wind &amp; weather the same as yesterday</p>","pageId":687,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":9,"lock":null}
20:13:21.359 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/120
20:13:21.359 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":120,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":17,"sequence":7.0000,"text":"<p>... upon reflection, I am resigned and convinced that I have been spared a great deal of painful feeling distress &amp; misery by not having witnessed her suffering &amp; tis a consolation to find that she has had so many kind &amp; attentive friends about her, particularly one Mr Vernon, whose conduct both to my poor sister &amp; myself I shall I trust never forget or be ungrateful for. He insists upon my staying at his house &amp; his great anxiety id to console &amp; make me comfortable. Poor little Emma has fortunately been at Captain Butlins at Broomville &amp; the boys at school. Poor children, they are too young to be sensible of the irreparable loss they have sustained. But I trust that god the father of all will spare &amp; enable me to supply the place of their dear parents they have lost. John J Baker came up to see me in the evening</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":110,"lock":null}
20:13:21.359 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.359 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/120
20:13:21.359 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":120,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":17,"sequence":7.0000,"text":"<p>... upon reflection, I am resigned and convinced that I have been spared a great deal of painful feeling distress &amp; misery by not having witnessed her suffering &amp; tis a consolation to find that she has had so many kind &amp; attentive friends about her, particularly one Mr Vernon, whose conduct both to my poor sister &amp; myself I shall I trust never forget or be ungrateful for. He insists upon my staying at his house &amp; his great anxiety id to console &amp; make me comfortable. Poor little Emma has fortunately been at Captain Butlins at Broomville &amp; the boys at school. Poor children, they are too young to be sensible of the irreparable loss they have sustained. But I trust that god the father of all will spare &amp; enable me to supply the place of their dear parents they have lost. John J Baker came up to see me in the evening</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":110,"lock":null}
20:13:21.359 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1200
20:13:21.359 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1200,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A deluge of rain this morning. Wind about East with a heavy sea. Went by Dunn's coach to Newcastle. Dined &amp; stayed all night at D Dixons. Mentioned to him my having applied to the Duke for a commission in the North<font color=#BFBFBF>umbria</font> militia of which he approved</p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1146,"lock":null}
