20:13:21.372 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1224
20:13:21.372 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1224,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A continuance of mild weather. Wind SSW. At church in the morning. Dined with H Harry. Received a letter from WBS. In the evening at the Mulstrum.</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":887,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1170,"lock":null}
20:13:21.372 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1225
20:13:21.372 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1225,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A beautiful morning. Wind SW. Strolled about the town until dinner at 2 o'clock at home. At the billiard room all the afternoon &amp; at the Albion in the evening</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":887,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1171,"lock":null}
20:13:21.372 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.372 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1225
20:13:21.372 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1225,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A beautiful morning. Wind SW. Strolled about the town until dinner at 2 o'clock at home. At the billiard room all the afternoon &amp; at the Albion in the evening</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":887,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1171,"lock":null}
20:13:21.372 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1226
20:13:21.372 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1226,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild morning. Wind SW. Dined at 1 o'clock with J Ridhard on board the Nautilus &amp; in the evening went to a party at J Cunningham's. Wrote a note yesterday to D Dixon requesting him to ask Colonel Coulston if he could give me any positive information about my commission.</p>","pageId":887,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1172,"lock":null}
20:13:21.372 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.373 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1226
20:13:21.373 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1226,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild morning. Wind SW. Dined at 1 o'clock with J Ridhard on board the Nautilus &amp; in the evening went to a party at J Cunningham's. Wrote a note yesterday to D Dixon requesting him to ask Colonel Coulston if he could give me any positive information about my commission.</p>","pageId":887,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1172,"lock":null}
20:13:21.373 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1227
20:13:21.373 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1227,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A damp morning having been rain in the night. Wind WNW. Received a note from D Dixon, having seen Colonel Coulston who says I shall be in the regiment in a few days for a captaincy. Dined again on board the Nautilus &amp; at the Albion in the evening.</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":887,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1173,"lock":null}
20:13:21.373 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.373 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1227
20:13:21.373 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1227,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A damp morning having been rain in the night. Wind WNW. Received a note from D Dixon, having seen Colonel Coulston who says I shall be in the regiment in a few days for a captaincy. Dined again on board the Nautilus &amp; at the Albion in the evening.</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":887,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1173,"lock":null}
20:13:21.373 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1228
20:13:21.373 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1228,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine morning blowing fresh at WNW. Went by the coach to Newcastle. Called at the club house to see Colonel Coulson who had left town in the morning. At D Dixons, saw Dixon &amp; the ladies. Called on young Bigger who gave me the names of the trader men in London who have the regulation patterns. Walked down from Newcastle. Met Dr Drury &amp; Mr Harrison near Mr Robson who were on their way to dine with Saddler at the Point &amp; prevailed on me to accompany them. At the whist club &amp; Mulstrum in the evening.</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":888,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1174,"lock":null}
20:13:21.373 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.374 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1228
20:13:21.374 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1228,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine morning blowing fresh at WNW. Went by the coach to Newcastle. Called at the club house to see Colonel Coulson who had left town in the morning. At D Dixons, saw Dixon &amp; the ladies. Called on young Bigger who gave me the names of the trader men in London who have the regulation patterns. Walked down from Newcastle. Met Dr Drury &amp; Mr Harrison near Mr Robson who were on their way to dine with Saddler at the Point &amp; prevailed on me to accompany them. At the whist club &amp; Mulstrum in the evening.</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":888,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1174,"lock":null}
20:13:21.374 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1229
20:13:21.374 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1229,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A continuance of fine weather. Wind WNW.</p> <p></p> <p>Received a letter from WBS &amp; after breakfast went on board the Jane at his request to see Mr Brown to desire him not to clear the Harmony or of cleared to order the master to stop below Gravesend until after the 1 March when the coal duties are to be taken off.</p> <p></p> <p>Attended a meeting at the Commercial &amp; entered into resolutions to be followed up by petitions against the proposed <span class=highlight_yellow>carecase</span> of duty upon north American timber.</p> <p></p> <p>Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon. Suppered with H harry</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":888,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1175,"lock":null}
20:13:21.374 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.374 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1229
20:13:21.374 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1229,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A continuance of fine weather. Wind WNW.</p> <p></p> <p>Received a letter from WBS &amp; after breakfast went on board the Jane at his request to see Mr Brown to desire him not to clear the Harmony or of cleared to order the master to stop below Gravesend until after the 1 March when the coal duties are to be taken off.</p> <p></p> <p>Attended a meeting at the Commercial &amp; entered into resolutions to be followed up by petitions against the proposed <span class=highlight_yellow>carecase</span> of duty upon north American timber.</p> <p></p> <p>Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon. Suppered with H harry</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":888,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1175,"lock":null}
20:13:21.374 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/123
20:13:21.374 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":123,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant day. Wind still from the North. Did not go to church. Read the service at home. Received a letter from William remitting a &pound;50 Bank Post bill. Took a long walk with Mr Vernon along the Athy road &amp; returned to dinner at &frac12; past 5 o'clock. The boys again with us. W W Fishbrown called upon me</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":113,"lock":null}
20:13:21.374 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.375 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/123
20:13:21.375 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":123,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant day. Wind still from the North. Did not go to church. Read the service at home. Received a letter from William remitting a &pound;50 Bank Post bill. Took a long walk with Mr Vernon along the Athy road &amp; returned to dinner at &frac12; past 5 o'clock. The boys again with us. W W Fishbrown called upon me</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":113,"lock":null}
20:13:21.375 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1230
20:13:21.375 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1230,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A beautiful morning. Wind NW. Wrote to WBS to order all my clothes etc. for the North<font color=#BFBFBF>humbria</font> Regiment immediately, should I be in the <span class=highlight_yellow>Gagelle</span> which is expected. Took wine at the Albion with W C Wright etc. &amp; attended the club at Dr Drury's in the evening.</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":888,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1176,"lock":null}
20:13:21.375 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.375 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1230
20:13:21.375 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1230,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A beautiful morning. Wind NW. Wrote to WBS to order all my clothes etc. for the North<font color=#BFBFBF>humbria</font> Regiment immediately, should I be in the <span class=highlight_yellow>Gagelle</span> which is expected. Took wine at the Albion with W C Wright etc. &amp; attended the club at Dr Drury's in the evening.</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":888,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1176,"lock":null}
20:13:21.375 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1231
20:13:21.376 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1231,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":19,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p><p>Withdrew the &pound;500 insurance on the Hope from the Great Premium Club &amp; put it into the Eligible making &pound;1000 in that club. Left a written notice with Bulmers clerk to that effect.</p> <p></p> <p>A good deal of rain this evening.</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":889,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1177,"lock":null}
20:13:21.376 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.376 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1231
20:13:21.376 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1231,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":19,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p><p>Withdrew the &pound;500 insurance on the Hope from the Great Premium Club &amp; put it into the Eligible making &pound;1000 in that club. Left a written notice with Bulmers clerk to that effect.</p> <p></p> <p>A good deal of rain this evening.</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":889,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1177,"lock":null}
20:13:21.376 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1232
20:13:21.376 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1232,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine day. Wind NNW. Must have been in the night NNE there being a deal of sea on the bar. Went to church in the morning. Sadler dined with me &amp; H Harry came in &amp; took wine with us. At the Multrum in the evening</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":889,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1178,"lock":null}
20:13:21.376 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.376 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1232
20:13:21.376 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1232,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine day. Wind NNW. Must have been in the night NNE there being a deal of sea on the bar. Went to church in the morning. Sadler dined with me &amp; H Harry came in &amp; took wine with us. At the Multrum in the evening</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":889,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1178,"lock":null}
20:13:21.376 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1233
20:13:21.376 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1233,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A beautiful morning. Wind NW. Much disappointed at not finding my name in the Gazette. Took a long walk with Cunningham round by Preston, Whitley, Cullercoats &amp; Tynemouth. Wrote to WBS with an account of <span class=highlight_yellow>units</span>. Dined at Jebbs at 5 o'clock, a gentleman's party &amp; spent a very pleasant day</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":889,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1179,"lock":null}
20:13:21.376 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.377 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1233
20:13:21.377 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1233,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A beautiful morning. Wind NW. Much disappointed at not finding my name in the Gazette. Took a long walk with Cunningham round by Preston, Whitley, Cullercoats &amp; Tynemouth. Wrote to WBS with an account of <span class=highlight_yellow>units</span>. Dined at Jebbs at 5 o'clock, a gentleman's party &amp; spent a very pleasant day</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":889,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1179,"lock":null}
20:13:21.377 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1234
20:13:21.377 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1234,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>Blowing hard half a gale from NNE &amp; has been rain or snow during the night. Called upon the <span class=highlight_yellow>messrs</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>Hdestorns</span>  at Mr Reeds. Dined at home &amp; in the evening went to the assembly which was a very good one. About 68 there. Got home at 4 o'clock. Paid Brown 16/ my subscription</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":889,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1180,"lock":null}
20:13:21.377 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.377 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1234
20:13:21.377 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1234,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>Blowing hard half a gale from NNE &amp; has been rain or snow during the night. Called upon the <span class=highlight_yellow>messrs</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>Hdestorns</span>  at Mr Reeds. Dined at home &amp; in the evening went to the assembly which was a very good one. About 68 there. Got home at 4 o'clock. Paid Brown 16/ my subscription</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":889,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1180,"lock":null}
20:13:21.377 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1235
20:13:21.377 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1235,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine frosty morning. Wind WNW. Received a letter from WBS. Walked to Tynemouth. Called upon &amp; had lunch with Jibbs. Dined at 5 o'clock with H Dale &amp; spent a very pleasant day</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":889,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1181,"lock":null}
20:13:21.377 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.378 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1235
20:13:21.378 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1235,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine frosty morning. Wind WNW. Received a letter from WBS. Walked to Tynemouth. Called upon &amp; had lunch with Jibbs. Dined at 5 o'clock with H Dale &amp; spent a very pleasant day</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":889,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1181,"lock":null}
20:13:21.378 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1236
20:13:21.378 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1236,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful morning. Wind NW. Received a letter from WBS with his note for &pound;95.10 enclosed. Dined at home. Mr Lockwood to his dinner with me. In the evening at the club. The Samarang frigate got orders to go to <span class=highlight_yellow>Chathace</span> &amp; take all the mariners</p>","pageId":890,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1182,"lock":null}
20:13:21.378 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.378 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1236
20:13:21.378 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1236,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful morning. Wind NW. Received a letter from WBS with his note for &pound;95.10 enclosed. Dined at home. Mr Lockwood to his dinner with me. In the evening at the club. The Samarang frigate got orders to go to <span class=highlight_yellow>Chathace</span> &amp; take all the mariners</p>","pageId":890,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1182,"lock":null}
20:13:21.378 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1237
20:13:21.378 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1237,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Blowing hard at WNW. The Samarang frigate sailed at 1 o'clock. Dined at home. Paid <span class=highlight_yellow>Twigell</span> &pound;2.14. <span class=highlight_yellow>tharp</span> 15/ <span class=highlight_yellow>coates</span> &pound;1.15/ <span class=highlight_yellow>Tygack</span> &pound;1.8. all for the Hope. At the Duke of York &amp; Mulstrum in the evening.</p>","pageId":890,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1183,"lock":null}
20:13:21.378 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.378 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1237
20:13:21.378 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1237,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Blowing hard at WNW. The Samarang frigate sailed at 1 o'clock. Dined at home. Paid <span class=highlight_yellow>Twigell</span> &pound;2.14. <span class=highlight_yellow>tharp</span> 15/ <span class=highlight_yellow>coates</span> &pound;1.15/ <span class=highlight_yellow>Tygack</span> &pound;1.8. all for the Hope. At the Duke of York &amp; Mulstrum in the evening.</p>","pageId":890,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1183,"lock":null}
20:13:21.378 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1238
20:13:21.378 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1238,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A dull rainy morning. Wind NE. Received the Hope's <span class=highlight_yellow>assales</span> from WBS. Took the 11 o'clock steam boat &amp; went to Newcastle. Called to see Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>albraith</font>. Could learn nothing further with regard to our conversation. All as much in the dark &amp; suspense as myself. Saw Dixon &amp; the ladies in Westgate Street where I lunched. Received of the <span class=highlight_yellow>Hind</span><span class=highlight_yellow>h</span><span class=highlight_yellow>augh</span> &pound;36.0.9 being the difference between what the Hope made &amp; 11/- freight applied. Returned by steam by the 4 o'clock boat &amp; came home to dinner. Attended the club at Tibb's in the evening</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":890,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1184,"lock":null}
20:13:21.378 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.379 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1238
20:13:21.379 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1238,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A dull rainy morning. Wind NE. Received the Hope's <span class=highlight_yellow>assales</span> from WBS. Took the 11 o'clock steam boat &amp; went to Newcastle. Called to see Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>albraith</font>. Could learn nothing further with regard to our conversation. All as much in the dark &amp; suspense as myself. Saw Dixon &amp; the ladies in Westgate Street where I lunched. Received of the <span class=highlight_yellow>Hind</span><span class=highlight_yellow>h</span><span class=highlight_yellow>augh</span> &pound;36.0.9 being the difference between what the Hope made &amp; 11/- freight applied. Returned by steam by the 4 o'clock boat &amp; came home to dinner. Attended the club at Tibb's in the evening</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":890,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1184,"lock":null}
20:13:21.379 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1239
20:13:21.379 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1239,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A thick damp morning. Wind SW. Did not go to church. Dined at home. In the evening at the Abbey &amp; Mulstrums</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":890,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1185,"lock":null}
20:13:21.379 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.379 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1239
20:13:21.379 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1239,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A thick damp morning. Wind SW. Did not go to church. Dined at home. In the evening at the Abbey &amp; Mulstrums</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":890,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1185,"lock":null}
20:13:21.379 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/124
20:13:21.379 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":124,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind still from the North. Engaged all the morning in examining Dear Betsy's books &amp; papers. In the afternoon Mr Vernon, the boys &amp; I walked out to Crossleigh to see the Herrings &amp; also called upon F Falkener, went round by Old derrgy &amp; home to dinner</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":114,"lock":null}
20:13:21.379 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.380 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/124
20:13:21.380 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":124,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind still from the North. Engaged all the morning in examining Dear Betsy's books &amp; papers. In the afternoon Mr Vernon, the boys &amp; I walked out to Crossleigh to see the Herrings &amp; also called upon F Falkener, went round by Old derrgy &amp; home to dinner</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":114,"lock":null}
20:13:21.380 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1240
20:13:21.380 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1240,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine but cold morning having been a frost in the night. Wind NW. My name not in the Gazette. Received a letter from WBS stating the season that Lord Melbourn had not made up his mind as to filling up the vacancies. Gave Robert a draft for &pound;5 executor's account for the house. Drew also for &pound;6.9 to pay Mrs Dixon for sundries got for Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>albraith</font>. Paid into Chapman on my own account WBS's note for &pound;95.10 &amp; &pound;36.0.9 received of Hindhaugh = 131.16.9. Called upon Dr Drury &amp; gave him a draft on C&amp;C for his bills &pound;11.4/- afterwards walked up to Craigs &amp; took wine at the Mulstrum in the evening.</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":891,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1186,"lock":null}
20:13:21.380 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.380 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1240
20:13:21.380 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1240,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine but cold morning having been a frost in the night. Wind NW. My name not in the Gazette. Received a letter from WBS stating the season that Lord Melbourn had not made up his mind as to filling up the vacancies. Gave Robert a draft for &pound;5 executor's account for the house. Drew also for &pound;6.9 to pay Mrs Dixon for sundries got for Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>albraith</font>. Paid into Chapman on my own account WBS's note for &pound;95.10 &amp; &pound;36.0.9 received of Hindhaugh = 131.16.9. Called upon Dr Drury &amp; gave him a draft on C&amp;C for his bills &pound;11.4/- afterwards walked up to Craigs &amp; took wine at the Mulstrum in the evening.</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":891,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1186,"lock":null}
20:13:21.380 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1241
20:13:21.380 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1241,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Frosty &amp; wind at NW blowing fresh. Called upon Captain Webb. He &amp; I walked round by the high end of the town, Plett's Yard &amp; Chesterton, home to dinner. In the afternoon at the billiard room &amp; at the Duke of York in the evening.</p>","pageId":891,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1187,"lock":null}
20:13:21.380 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.380 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1241
20:13:21.380 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1241,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Frosty &amp; wind at NW blowing fresh. Called upon Captain Webb. He &amp; I walked round by the high end of the town, Plett's Yard &amp; Chesterton, home to dinner. In the afternoon at the billiard room &amp; at the Duke of York in the evening.</p>","pageId":891,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1187,"lock":null}
20:13:21.381 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1242
20:13:21.381 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1242,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A rainy morning. Wind fresh at W by N. paid Robert &pound;2.4/ Walton the brewer bills 3<sup>rd</sup> &amp; 4<sup>th</sup> coal voyage which will be given credit for as sent, be being in <span class=highlight_yellow>asseasy</span>. Engaged today making up ships books. Dined at home. At the Abbey in the evening. The Hope arrived</p>","pageId":891,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1188,"lock":null}
20:13:21.381 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.381 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1242
20:13:21.381 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1242,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A rainy morning. Wind fresh at W by N. paid Robert &pound;2.4/ Walton the brewer bills 3<sup>rd</sup> &amp; 4<sup>th</sup> coal voyage which will be given credit for as sent, be being in <span class=highlight_yellow>asseasy</span>. Engaged today making up ships books. Dined at home. At the Abbey in the evening. The Hope arrived</p>","pageId":891,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1188,"lock":null}
20:13:21.381 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1243
20:13:21.381 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1243,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A rainy morning &amp; light air at SE. Did not go to church. Dr Drury dined with me &amp; H Harry came in after dinner &amp; took wine. At the Mulstrum in the evening</p>","pageId":892,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1189,"lock":null}
20:13:21.381 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.381 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1243
20:13:21.381 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1243,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A rainy morning &amp; light air at SE. Did not go to church. Dr Drury dined with me &amp; H Harry came in after dinner &amp; took wine. At the Mulstrum in the evening</p>","pageId":892,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1189,"lock":null}
20:13:21.381 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1244
20:13:21.381 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1244,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Quite summer weather. Wind NW. Received a letter from WBS. Not yet gazetted. Bound <span class=highlight_yellow>J</span><font color=#BFBFBF><span class=highlight_yellow>u</span></font><span class=highlight_yellow>n</span><font color=#BFBFBF><span class=highlight_yellow>io</span></font><sup><span class=highlight_yellow>r</span></sup> <span class=highlight_yellow>Hall</span> Beal as apprentice for 6 years at &pound;45. At the ship, carpenters still busy with the stern. Gave orders to build the cabin windows up &amp; to put up bulk heads for a sail cabin where the after lockers were. Dined on board the <span class=highlight_yellow>Crives</span> with A Nicholas. At the Duke of York in the evening. Received a letter from WBS</p>","pageId":892,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1190,"lock":null}
20:13:21.381 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.382 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1244
20:13:21.382 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1244,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Quite summer weather. Wind NW. Received a letter from WBS. Not yet gazetted. Bound <span class=highlight_yellow>J</span><font color=#BFBFBF><span class=highlight_yellow>u</span></font><span class=highlight_yellow>n</span><font color=#BFBFBF><span class=highlight_yellow>io</span></font><sup><span class=highlight_yellow>r</span></sup> <span class=highlight_yellow>Hall</span> Beal as apprentice for 6 years at &pound;45. At the ship, carpenters still busy with the stern. Gave orders to build the cabin windows up &amp; to put up bulk heads for a sail cabin where the after lockers were. Dined on board the <span class=highlight_yellow>Crives</span> with A Nicholas. At the Duke of York in the evening. Received a letter from WBS</p>","pageId":892,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1190,"lock":null}
20:13:21.382 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1245
20:13:21.382 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1245,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind S by W. Received a letter from Captain Crisp adj<font color=#BFBFBF>utant</font> of the regiment stating the Col<font color=#BFBFBF>onel</font> Coul<font color=#BFBFBF>son</font> having received a notification from the Duke of N<font color=#BFBFBF>orthamptonshire</font>  that my commission was preparing  &amp; that I must order my uniform etc &amp; hold myself in readiness to join. Attended a meeting at the North <span class=highlight_yellow>aems</span>, the room full, to petition both houses of parliament to pass the reform bill &amp; setting forth our approval of the measure. Went up to the ship. Dined at home. Wrote to WBS giving him a copy of the above mentioned letter. At the Albion in the evening.</p>","pageId":892,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1191,"lock":null}
20:13:21.382 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.382 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1245
20:13:21.382 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1245,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind S by W. Received a letter from Captain Crisp adj<font color=#BFBFBF>utant</font> of the regiment stating the Col<font color=#BFBFBF>onel</font> Coul<font color=#BFBFBF>son</font> having received a notification from the Duke of N<font color=#BFBFBF>orthamptonshire</font>  that my commission was preparing  &amp; that I must order my uniform etc &amp; hold myself in readiness to join. Attended a meeting at the North <span class=highlight_yellow>aems</span>, the room full, to petition both houses of parliament to pass the reform bill &amp; setting forth our approval of the measure. Went up to the ship. Dined at home. Wrote to WBS giving him a copy of the above mentioned letter. At the Albion in the evening.</p>","pageId":892,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1191,"lock":null}
20:13:21.382 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1246
20:13:21.382 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1246,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind NNW. Walked out to Whitley &amp; called upon Mr J Wright &amp; returned home by Cullercoats &amp; Tynemouth to dinner. Dr Drury, Charlton &amp; I had wine at Sears &amp; finished the evening at the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":892,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1192,"lock":null}
20:13:21.382 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.383 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1246
20:13:21.383 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1246,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind NNW. Walked out to Whitley &amp; called upon Mr J Wright &amp; returned home by Cullercoats &amp; Tynemouth to dinner. Dr Drury, Charlton &amp; I had wine at Sears &amp; finished the evening at the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":892,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1192,"lock":null}
20:13:21.383 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1247
20:13:21.383 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1247,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful day. Wind SW. Went to Newcastle by steam &amp; ordered coals down on Monday. Enrolled <span class=highlight_yellow>H A </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Bealls</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>interviews</span> at the Custom House. Returned home to dinner. Dr Drewry &amp; Chartson dined with me. At the club in the evening.</p>","pageId":893,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1193,"lock":null}
20:13:21.383 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.383 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1247
20:13:21.383 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1247,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful day. Wind SW. Went to Newcastle by steam &amp; ordered coals down on Monday. Enrolled <span class=highlight_yellow>H A </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Bealls</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>interviews</span> at the Custom House. Returned home to dinner. Dr Drewry &amp; Chartson dined with me. At the club in the evening.</p>","pageId":893,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1193,"lock":null}
20:13:21.383 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1248
20:13:21.383 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1248,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet unpleasant day. Wind between SW &amp; WNW. Could not get to the ship. Received a letter from WBS informing me of my name being in the Gazette, which I see in this days papers. Dined at home. H harry, Cunningham &amp; and I took wine at the Albion &amp; in the evening finished at the Duke <font color=#BFBFBF>of York</font><font color=#BFBFBF> </font></p>","pageId":893,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1194,"lock":null}
20:13:21.383 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.384 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1248
20:13:21.384 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1248,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet unpleasant day. Wind between SW &amp; WNW. Could not get to the ship. Received a letter from WBS informing me of my name being in the Gazette, which I see in this days papers. Dined at home. H harry, Cunningham &amp; and I took wine at the Albion &amp; in the evening finished at the Duke <font color=#BFBFBF>of York</font><font color=#BFBFBF> </font></p>","pageId":893,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1194,"lock":null}
20:13:21.384 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1249
20:13:21.384 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1249,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning and wind SW. Received a letter from Alnwick from the adj<font color=#BFBFBF>utant</font> Crisp ordering me to join the Regiment. Walked to Tynemouth with the intention of taking a warm bath, but they are not yet open for the season. Returned &amp; went up to the Hope. <span class=highlight_yellow>Repairs</span> nearly finished. At high water they hauled her off the shore &amp; dropped her down to Custom House Quay. Toward the afternoon it began to blow very hard varying between SSW &amp; SSE &amp; increased to a gale which continued all night. Spent the evening at home writing etc.</p>","pageId":893,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1195,"lock":null}
20:13:21.384 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.384 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1249
20:13:21.384 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1249,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning and wind SW. Received a letter from Alnwick from the adj<font color=#BFBFBF>utant</font> Crisp ordering me to join the Regiment. Walked to Tynemouth with the intention of taking a warm bath, but they are not yet open for the season. Returned &amp; went up to the Hope. <span class=highlight_yellow>Repairs</span> nearly finished. At high water they hauled her off the shore &amp; dropped her down to Custom House Quay. Toward the afternoon it began to blow very hard varying between SSW &amp; SSE &amp; increased to a gale which continued all night. Spent the evening at home writing etc.</p>","pageId":893,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1195,"lock":null}
20:13:21.384 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/125
20:13:21.384 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":125,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of the same sort of weather with the cool wind. Engaged all the morning with Mr Turner in examining &amp; entering rents. In the afternoon Mr Vernon &amp; I took a walk along the Kilkenny Road, returned home to drefs &amp; took a family dinner with Mr W<sup>en</sup> Fishburn who was exceedingly kind, but yet I should have preferred dining quietly at Mr Vernon's. Received a letter from William</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":115,"lock":null}
20:13:21.384 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.384 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/125
20:13:21.384 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":125,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of the same sort of weather with the cool wind. Engaged all the morning with Mr Turner in examining &amp; entering rents. In the afternoon Mr Vernon &amp; I took a walk along the Kilkenny Road, returned home to drefs &amp; took a family dinner with Mr W<sup>en</sup> Fishburn who was exceedingly kind, but yet I should have preferred dining quietly at Mr Vernon's. Received a letter from William</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":115,"lock":null}
20:13:21.384 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1250
20:13:21.384 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1250,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning blowing fresh from WSW. Engaged at home all the morning packing up. Dined at home. Took wine with H Harry. A very rainy afternoon &amp; blowing hard from SSW. At the Abbey &amp; Mulstrum in the evening. Received a letter from WBS</p>","pageId":893,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1196,"lock":null}
20:13:21.384 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
