20:13:21.390 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1260,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine mild weather. Wind West. Attended church parade the whole of the officers &amp; men. Went to church. Paraded at 5 o'clock in the afternoon. Dined at the mess. Captain Biggs finished <span class=highlight_yellow>withing</span> his <span class=highlight_yellow>com</span><font color=#BFBFBF><span class=highlight_yellow>pany</span></font>. Kept it up very late. Did not get to bed till 4 o'clock in the morning. Received a letter from WBS</p>","pageId":894,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1206,"lock":null}
20:13:21.390 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1261
20:13:21.390 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1261,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Weather continues very fine. Parade as usual at 10 o'clock in the pasture &amp; again at 2 o'clock. Dined at mess. A large party, being stranger day. Mr Bussale of Broom, <span class=highlight_yellow>Pard</span> &amp; others there. Took tea with William Forster</p>","pageId":894,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1207,"lock":null}
