20:13:21.399 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/128
20:13:21.399 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":128,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>This day rather cooler. Wind NW with showers of rain. Engaged again all the morning in packing up &amp; separating the books that I take to England from those for sale. Called upon Dr Reed &amp; Dr Home. Dined at Mr Vernon's with the boys Received letter from fanny Smith</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":118,"lock":null}
20:13:21.399 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.400 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/128
20:13:21.400 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":128,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>This day rather cooler. Wind NW with showers of rain. Engaged again all the morning in packing up &amp; separating the books that I take to England from those for sale. Called upon Dr Reed &amp; Dr Home. Dined at Mr Vernon's with the boys Received letter from fanny Smith</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":118,"lock":null}
20:13:21.400 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1280
20:13:21.400 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1280,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":4,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind changed to WNW. Settled Robert's book &amp; paid him &pound;13.-1<sup>d</sup> my private expenses for the year up to this time. Looked into the Duke's court. Went to Tynemouth races. A great many people there. Dined at 4 o'clock at the Northumberland Alms with McBain &amp; the jury. Called in the evening at the Mulstrum. Wind changed to east.</p>","pageId":899,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1226,"lock":null}
20:13:21.400 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.400 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1280
20:13:21.400 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1280,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":4,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind changed to WNW. Settled Robert's book &amp; paid him &pound;13.-1<sup>d</sup> my private expenses for the year up to this time. Looked into the Duke's court. Went to Tynemouth races. A great many people there. Dined at 4 o'clock at the Northumberland Alms with McBain &amp; the jury. Called in the evening at the Mulstrum. Wind changed to east.</p>","pageId":899,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1226,"lock":null}
20:13:21.400 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1281
20:13:21.400 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1281,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind NW. Turned out rather showery. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined with Jibbs &amp; afterwards went to the Sands to see the races. Lockerwood and Charlton gave us wine in the evening &amp; finished off at the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":899,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1227,"lock":null}
20:13:21.400 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
