20:13:21.408 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1296,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<figure>\r\n  <a href=\"https://maps.nls.uk/view/index.cfm?id=102346464\" >\r\n    <img src=\"images/img2762-north-shields-walk.png\" width=\"600px\" />\r\n    <figcaption>img2762-north-shields-walk</figcaption>\r\n  </a>\r\n</figure>","pageId":902,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":1242,"lock":null}
20:13:21.408 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.408 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1296
20:13:21.408 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1296,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<figure>\r\n  <a href=\"https://maps.nls.uk/view/index.cfm?id=102346464\" >\r\n    <img src=\"images/img2762-north-shields-walk.png\" width=\"600px\" />\r\n    <figcaption>img2762-north-shields-walk</figcaption>\r\n  </a>\r\n</figure>","pageId":902,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":1242,"lock":null}
20:13:21.408 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1297
20:13:21.408 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1297,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":19,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather. Wind ESE. Walked up to the ship with H Harry &amp; round by Percy Main the turnpike, home to dinner. Spent the afternoon on board the Tom Shand &amp; the evening at the Mulstrum. Wrote to WBS</p>","pageId":902,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1243,"lock":null}
20:13:21.408 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.408 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1297
20:13:21.408 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1297,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":19,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather. Wind ESE. Walked up to the ship with H Harry &amp; round by Percy Main the turnpike, home to dinner. Spent the afternoon on board the Tom Shand &amp; the evening at the Mulstrum. Wrote to WBS</p>","pageId":902,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1243,"lock":null}
20:13:21.408 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1298
20:13:21.408 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1298,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine but rather damp morning. Wind ESE. The charter for the Hope arrived by the post from Hull. The Merchants Messrs Wade Sons &amp; Forster Wybury &amp; Hull. 70/ for <span class=highlight_yellow>deals</span> &amp; buttons. The latter not to exceed 6/8. Ordered 3 casks or pork of Bradshaws &amp; 5 <span class=highlight_yellow>loaves</span> of bread of Walkerley &amp; a new main topgallantsail. Dined at home &amp; in the afternoon H Harry gave the Doctor &amp; me some wine at the Northumberland Alms. Afterwards at the Abbey &amp; Mulstrum</p>","pageId":903,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1244,"lock":null}
20:13:21.408 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.409 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1298
20:13:21.409 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1298,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine but rather damp morning. Wind ESE. The charter for the Hope arrived by the post from Hull. The Merchants Messrs Wade Sons &amp; Forster Wybury &amp; Hull. 70/ for <span class=highlight_yellow>deals</span> &amp; buttons. The latter not to exceed 6/8. Ordered 3 casks or pork of Bradshaws &amp; 5 <span class=highlight_yellow>loaves</span> of bread of Walkerley &amp; a new main topgallantsail. Dined at home &amp; in the afternoon H Harry gave the Doctor &amp; me some wine at the Northumberland Alms. Afterwards at the Abbey &amp; Mulstrum</p>","pageId":903,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1244,"lock":null}
20:13:21.409 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1299
20:13:21.409 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1299,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cold morning. Wind NE. Paid into Chapmans the <span class=highlight_yellow>hote</span> for &pound;97.9. Gave Stephenson &pound;50. Got the pork, bread etc on board. Had a few friends to dine with me at 5 o'clock. <span class=highlight_yellow>veg</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>Te</span><span class=highlight_yellow>nley's</span> Rudyard 15<sup>th</sup> Regiment Dick artillery J Wright &amp; Boswell.</p>","pageId":903,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1245,"lock":null}
20:13:21.409 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.409 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1299
20:13:21.409 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1299,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cold morning. Wind NE. Paid into Chapmans the <span class=highlight_yellow>hote</span> for &pound;97.9. Gave Stephenson &pound;50. Got the pork, bread etc on board. Had a few friends to dine with me at 5 o'clock. <span class=highlight_yellow>veg</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>Te</span><span class=highlight_yellow>nley's</span> Rudyard 15<sup>th</sup> Regiment Dick artillery J Wright &amp; Boswell.</p>","pageId":903,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1245,"lock":null}
20:13:21.409 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/13
20:13:21.409 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":13,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got captain Hallam to moor the Hope securely by carrying an anchor out astern. Dined with Mrs Scott &amp; spent the evening at Mrs Greenhours, met a large party, a regular squeeze; quadrille &amp; broke up at 12 o'clock. It was cold with snow in the evening</p>","pageId":687,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":10,"lock":null}
20:13:21.409 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.409 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/13
20:13:21.409 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":13,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got captain Hallam to moor the Hope securely by carrying an anchor out astern. Dined with Mrs Scott &amp; spent the evening at Mrs Greenhours, met a large party, a regular squeeze; quadrille &amp; broke up at 12 o'clock. It was cold with snow in the evening</p>","pageId":687,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":10,"lock":null}
20:13:21.410 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/130
20:13:21.410 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":130,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet day. Wind WSW. Captain Butler read the morning service. We afterwards took a drive between showers &amp; returned to dinner</p>","pageId":696,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":120,"lock":null}
20:13:21.410 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.410 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/130
20:13:21.410 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":130,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet day. Wind WSW. Captain Butler read the morning service. We afterwards took a drive between showers &amp; returned to dinner</p>","pageId":696,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":120,"lock":null}
20:13:21.410 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1300
20:13:21.410 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1300,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning but cool with a NE wind. Got a cask of rum on board the Hope. Ordered the men on shore as they refused to sign articles for less than &pound;3 per month. Stephenson at Newcastle clearing.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Ministries in a minority of eight upon Gen<font color=#BFBFBF>era</font>l  Gascoyne's amendment on the reform bill respecting English members. Attended a meeting at the George tavern called in consequence of the minister being in the minority for the purpose of explaining their determination to support them in their proposed <span class=highlight_yellow>grievances</span> &amp; not to give any candidate a vote until he promises to support reform.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Finished at the Albion &amp; Mulstrum.</p>\r\n<p><u> </u></p>","pageId":903,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1246,"lock":null}
20:13:21.410 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.410 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1300
20:13:21.410 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1300,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning but cool with a NE wind. Got a cask of rum on board the Hope. Ordered the men on shore as they refused to sign articles for less than &pound;3 per month. Stephenson at Newcastle clearing.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Ministries in a minority of eight upon Gen<font color=#BFBFBF>era</font>l  Gascoyne's amendment on the reform bill respecting English members. Attended a meeting at the George tavern called in consequence of the minister being in the minority for the purpose of explaining their determination to support them in their proposed <span class=highlight_yellow>grievances</span> &amp; not to give any candidate a vote until he promises to support reform.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Finished at the Albion &amp; Mulstrum.</p>\r\n<p><u> </u></p>","pageId":903,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1246,"lock":null}
20:13:21.410 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1301
20:13:21.410 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1301,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cold day &amp; blowing fresh from NNE &amp; sea coming on. Received a letter from WBS &amp; answered it. Called at Chapmans, Mr Spence declines answering our note, but proposes continuing the <span class=highlight_yellow>loan</span> on my giving a bill upon WBS to have his acceptance, the <span class=highlight_yellow>time</span> to be afterward agreed upon when I secure WBS's answer. Walked up to the ship, all ready for sea, excepting <span class=highlight_yellow>wind</span>. Towed her down to the low end of the town. Dined at home. On board the Mr Shand in the afternoon &amp; at the Mulstrum in the evening.</p>","pageId":904,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1247,"lock":null}
20:13:21.410 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.411 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1301
20:13:21.411 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1301,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cold day &amp; blowing fresh from NNE &amp; sea coming on. Received a letter from WBS &amp; answered it. Called at Chapmans, Mr Spence declines answering our note, but proposes continuing the <span class=highlight_yellow>loan</span> on my giving a bill upon WBS to have his acceptance, the <span class=highlight_yellow>time</span> to be afterward agreed upon when I secure WBS's answer. Walked up to the ship, all ready for sea, excepting <span class=highlight_yellow>wind</span>. Towed her down to the low end of the town. Dined at home. On board the Mr Shand in the afternoon &amp; at the Mulstrum in the evening.</p>","pageId":904,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1247,"lock":null}
20:13:21.411 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1302
20:13:21.411 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1302,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull damp morning. Wind NNE &amp; much sea. A good deal of rain during the day. An account this morning of there being having prorogued parliament in person.  Dined at home. Took wine with the doctor &amp; finished at the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":904,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1248,"lock":null}
20:13:21.411 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.411 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1302
20:13:21.411 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1302,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull damp morning. Wind NNE &amp; much sea. A good deal of rain during the day. An account this morning of there being having prorogued parliament in person.  Dined at home. Took wine with the doctor &amp; finished at the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":904,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1248,"lock":null}
20:13:21.411 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1303
20:13:21.411 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1303,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind NNE. Paid by draft on executors account &frac12; years taxes &pound;14.7.11 &amp; on my own account {premium &pound;8.17, own account &pound;10.15, WBS &pound;5} &pound;24.12. Dined on board the Hope, H Harry &amp; Webb with me. Finished off at the Albion.</p>","pageId":904,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1249,"lock":null}
20:13:21.411 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.412 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1303
20:13:21.412 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1303,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind NNE. Paid by draft on executors account &frac12; years taxes &pound;14.7.11 &amp; on my own account {premium &pound;8.17, own account &pound;10.15, WBS &pound;5} &pound;24.12. Dined on board the Hope, H Harry &amp; Webb with me. Finished off at the Albion.</p>","pageId":904,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1249,"lock":null}
20:13:21.412 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1304
20:13:21.412 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1304,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A foggy rainy day. Wind SE &amp; SSE. Some ships went to sea amongst them the Geronimi. We could not get men &amp; were therefore obliged to lay. Dined at home. On board the Mr Shand. Spent the evening at the Albion &amp; Mulstrum</p>","pageId":904,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1250,"lock":null}
20:13:21.412 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.412 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1304
20:13:21.412 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1304,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A foggy rainy day. Wind SE &amp; SSE. Some ships went to sea amongst them the Geronimi. We could not get men &amp; were therefore obliged to lay. Dined at home. On board the Mr Shand. Spent the evening at the Albion &amp; Mulstrum</p>","pageId":904,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1250,"lock":null}
20:13:21.412 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1305
20:13:21.412 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1305,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another foggy &amp; rainy morning &amp; but little wind at SSW. Got our men this morning for &pound;2.17.6 per month &amp; have the ship out. Dined at home &amp; in the afternoon the Hope sailed with a fresh breeze at SSE. Finished at the Albion. Received a letter from WBS</p>","pageId":905,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1251,"lock":null}
20:13:21.412 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.412 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1305
20:13:21.412 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1305,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another foggy &amp; rainy morning &amp; but little wind at SSW. Got our men this morning for &pound;2.17.6 per month &amp; have the ship out. Dined at home &amp; in the afternoon the Hope sailed with a fresh breeze at SSE. Finished at the Albion. Received a letter from WBS</p>","pageId":905,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1251,"lock":null}
20:13:21.412 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1306
20:13:21.412 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1306,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather but still dull &amp; looks like more rain. Called and saw Mr Spear who agreed to take out joint note payable at <span class=highlight_yellow>neis</span>. Leis for the loan of &pound;300 at 4 or 6 months. Wrote to WBS to that effect. Dined with the Committees of the Eligible &amp; United clubs. In the evening at the Malstrum.</p>","pageId":905,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1252,"lock":null}
20:13:21.412 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.412 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1306
20:13:21.412 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1306,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather but still dull &amp; looks like more rain. Called and saw Mr Spear who agreed to take out joint note payable at <span class=highlight_yellow>neis</span>. Leis for the loan of &pound;300 at 4 or 6 months. Wrote to WBS to that effect. Dined with the Committees of the Eligible &amp; United clubs. In the evening at the Malstrum.</p>","pageId":905,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1252,"lock":null}
20:13:21.412 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1307
20:13:21.412 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1307,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Went with Lockwood by Dunn's coach to Newcastle &amp; put up at the Turf Hotel where we also dined at the Wallsend Hunt dinner &amp; stayed all night.</p>","pageId":905,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1253,"lock":null}
20:13:21.412 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.413 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1307
20:13:21.413 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1307,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Went with Lockwood by Dunn's coach to Newcastle &amp; put up at the Turf Hotel where we also dined at the Wallsend Hunt dinner &amp; stayed all night.</p>","pageId":905,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1253,"lock":null}
20:13:21.413 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1308
20:13:21.413 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1308,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very rainy day. Wind continues from SE. The election for Newcastle took place. I went to the Guild Hall but I could not get near enough to the hustings to hear any part of the speeches. For Mr Ridley &amp; Mr Hodgson returned without opposition. Lucky fellows. Saw them chained. Had a lunch at the Turf &amp; returned to Shields by Dunn. At the Duke of York &amp; Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":905,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1254,"lock":null}
20:13:21.413 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.413 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1308
20:13:21.413 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1308,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very rainy day. Wind continues from SE. The election for Newcastle took place. I went to the Guild Hall but I could not get near enough to the hustings to hear any part of the speeches. For Mr Ridley &amp; Mr Hodgson returned without opposition. Lucky fellows. Saw them chained. Had a lunch at the Turf &amp; returned to Shields by Dunn. At the Duke of York &amp; Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":905,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1254,"lock":null}
20:13:21.413 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1309
20:13:21.413 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1309,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning &amp; all the appearance of more rain. Afterwards turned out a fine warm spring day. Walked to Cullercoats Sands. Ed Charlton dined with me. H Harry &amp; Sadler came in afterwards &amp; took wine. Sadler brought the account from the committee room of the Bell having retired. Finished off at the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":906,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1255,"lock":null}
20:13:21.413 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.413 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1309
20:13:21.413 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1309,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning &amp; all the appearance of more rain. Afterwards turned out a fine warm spring day. Walked to Cullercoats Sands. Ed Charlton dined with me. H Harry &amp; Sadler came in afterwards &amp; took wine. Sadler brought the account from the committee room of the Bell having retired. Finished off at the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":906,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1255,"lock":null}
20:13:21.413 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/131
20:13:21.413 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":131,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull and damp morning. Wind the same. Left Broomville &amp; reached Carlow without rain. Received a letter from William. Dined with Mr Vernon</p>","pageId":696,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":121,"lock":null}
20:13:21.413 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.415 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/131
20:13:21.415 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":131,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull and damp morning. Wind the same. Left Broomville &amp; reached Carlow without rain. Received a letter from William. Dined with Mr Vernon</p>","pageId":696,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":121,"lock":null}
20:13:21.415 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1310
20:13:21.415 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1310,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Weather much the same. Wind about N by E. Tom Smith arrived this morning being his rent day. Walked with him to Tynemouth. Dined at home at 4 o'clock. Received a letter from WBS this morning. Called upon Mrs Robinson but she refused to give me an order on Chapmans for Mr R's debt. At the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":906,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1256,"lock":null}
20:13:21.415 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.415 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1310
20:13:21.415 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1310,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Weather much the same. Wind about N by E. Tom Smith arrived this morning being his rent day. Walked with him to Tynemouth. Dined at home at 4 o'clock. Received a letter from WBS this morning. Called upon Mrs Robinson but she refused to give me an order on Chapmans for Mr R's debt. At the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":906,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1256,"lock":null}
20:13:21.415 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1311
20:13:21.415 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1311,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull orning &amp; damp heavy been a good deal of rain in the night. Wind SE. Lord Howielt &amp; Mr Beaumont came into the town conducted by an immense crowd of people with bands &amp; colours, whom they addressed from a hustings erected in front on the Commercial. Turned out a very rainy afternoon. H Harry dined with us at the Mulstrum. In the evening gave Jonny Smith &pound;28.1.6 <span class=highlight_yellow>Int</span> for his mother.</p>","pageId":906,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1257,"lock":null}
20:13:21.415 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.416 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1311
20:13:21.416 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1311,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull orning &amp; damp heavy been a good deal of rain in the night. Wind SE. Lord Howielt &amp; Mr Beaumont came into the town conducted by an immense crowd of people with bands &amp; colours, whom they addressed from a hustings erected in front on the Commercial. Turned out a very rainy afternoon. H Harry dined with us at the Mulstrum. In the evening gave Jonny Smith &pound;28.1.6 <span class=highlight_yellow>Int</span> for his mother.</p>","pageId":906,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1257,"lock":null}
20:13:21.416 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1312
20:13:21.416 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1312,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine sprint morning. A light breeze at NE. Tom Smith left for Newcastle after breakfast. Took a walk to Cullercoat Sands &amp; dined with Lockwood &amp; in the evening attended the theatre to <span class=highlight_yellow>se</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span><span class=highlight_yellow> beam</span>. At the Mustrum.</p>","pageId":906,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1258,"lock":null}
20:13:21.416 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.416 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1312
20:13:21.416 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1312,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine sprint morning. A light breeze at NE. Tom Smith left for Newcastle after breakfast. Took a walk to Cullercoat Sands &amp; dined with Lockwood &amp; in the evening attended the theatre to <span class=highlight_yellow>se</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span><span class=highlight_yellow> beam</span>. At the Mustrum.</p>","pageId":906,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1258,"lock":null}
20:13:21.416 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1313
20:13:21.416 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1313,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning &amp; at last a change of wind having got from the NW. Walked to Tynemouth &amp; from thence by the sands to Whitley Park and called upon Mr J Weight. Wind changes to NNE with heavy showers of hail &amp; rain in one of which I was caught &amp; got nearly wet through.  Returned home to dinner. Spent the evening at home.</p>","pageId":907,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1259,"lock":null}
20:13:21.416 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.416 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1313
20:13:21.416 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1313,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning &amp; at last a change of wind having got from the NW. Walked to Tynemouth &amp; from thence by the sands to Whitley Park and called upon Mr J Weight. Wind changes to NNE with heavy showers of hail &amp; rain in one of which I was caught &amp; got nearly wet through.  Returned home to dinner. Spent the evening at home.</p>","pageId":907,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1259,"lock":null}
20:13:21.416 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1314
20:13:21.416 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1314,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but cold. Wind NW. heavy changed from NE from which <span class=highlight_yellow>ash</span> it has been blowing fresh all night with a heavy sea. Dined at home. At Dr Drury's in the afternoon &amp; in the evening went to the theatre, but the house was so badly attended that <span class=highlight_yellow>Kean</span> would not perform. Finished at the Albion</p>","pageId":907,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1260,"lock":null}
20:13:21.416 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.417 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1314
20:13:21.417 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1314,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but cold. Wind NW. heavy changed from NE from which <span class=highlight_yellow>ash</span> it has been blowing fresh all night with a heavy sea. Dined at home. At Dr Drury's in the afternoon &amp; in the evening went to the theatre, but the house was so badly attended that <span class=highlight_yellow>Kean</span> would not perform. Finished at the Albion</p>","pageId":907,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1260,"lock":null}
