20:13:21.419 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1318,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most delightful day. Wind NE. Walked to Tynemouth. The mariners under <span class=highlight_yellow>a</span><span class=highlight_yellow>rre</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ars</span> in case they should be wanted at the collieries. Dined at home. Drank punch on board the Douglas in the afternoon &amp; at the Musltrum in the evening.</p>","pageId":908,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1264,"lock":null}
20:13:21.419 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1319
20:13:21.419 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1319,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind ENE. H Harry &amp; I walked by the river side through Howdon to Willington colliery and returned home by the turnpike.  The men at work with detachments of the yeomanry &amp; the 15<sup>th</sup> to protect them. Dined at home &amp; in the afternoon walked up to Billy Mill &amp; took wine with Charlton's. At the Mulstrum in the evening.</p>","pageId":908,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1265,"lock":null}
20:13:21.419 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.419 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1319
20:13:21.419 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1319,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind ENE. H Harry &amp; I walked by the river side through Howdon to Willington colliery and returned home by the turnpike.  The men at work with detachments of the yeomanry &amp; the 15<sup>th</sup> to protect them. Dined at home &amp; in the afternoon walked up to Billy Mill &amp; took wine with Charlton's. At the Mulstrum in the evening.</p>","pageId":908,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1265,"lock":null}
20:13:21.419 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/132
20:13:21.419 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":132,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another dull day with showers of rain. Wind WSW. Engaged in the morning writing and walked out with Mr Vernon, returned to dinner.  Mr Jameson &amp; Reverend O'Connor dined with us. Spent a very pleasant day</p>","pageId":696,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":122,"lock":null}
