20:13:21.437 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1347,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cloudy morning with slight rain &amp; blowing fresh from N by E &amp; good deal of sea on. Received a letter from WBS. Attended a meeting for the relief of the seamen out of employment, whose families are in great distress, subscribed a Guinea. Dined at home. Called at the Doctor's &amp; walked up to his garden &amp; spent the evening playing at quoits. At the Albion</p>","pageId":915,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1293,"lock":null}
20:13:21.437 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1348
20:13:21.437 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1348,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind NW. Afterwards turned out a most delightful day &amp; the wind again from the old quarter NE. Walked up to High Cheston &amp; called upon Mr Robson as bridegroom. Dined at home. At Tynemouth in the evening.. Took coffee with J Tinley.</p>","pageId":915,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1294,"lock":null}
20:13:21.437 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.437 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1348
20:13:21.437 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1348,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind NW. Afterwards turned out a most delightful day &amp; the wind again from the old quarter NE. Walked up to High Cheston &amp; called upon Mr Robson as bridegroom. Dined at home. At Tynemouth in the evening.. Took coffee with J Tinley.</p>","pageId":915,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1294,"lock":null}
20:13:21.437 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1349
20:13:21.437 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1349,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cloudy morning. Wind NW. Glass fallen &amp; more the appearance of rain. Received a letter from Emma Galbraith informing me of the holy days commencing on the 17<sup>th</sup>. <span class=highlight_yellow>But</span> glad to see her so much improved in her writing. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home. At Tynemouth again &amp; Cullercoat Sands in the afternoon &amp; evening. At the Albion.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Towards noon the wind got into the old quarter NE again &amp; turned out a most beautiful day.</p>","pageId":915,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1295,"lock":null}
20:13:21.437 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.438 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1349
20:13:21.438 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1349,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cloudy morning. Wind NW. Glass fallen &amp; more the appearance of rain. Received a letter from Emma Galbraith informing me of the holy days commencing on the 17<sup>th</sup>. <span class=highlight_yellow>But</span> glad to see her so much improved in her writing. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home. At Tynemouth again &amp; Cullercoat Sands in the afternoon &amp; evening. At the Albion.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Towards noon the wind got into the old quarter NE again &amp; turned out a most beautiful day.</p>","pageId":915,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1295,"lock":null}
20:13:21.438 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/135
20:13:21.438 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":135,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":5,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine spring day with a shower of rain in the morning. Wind SW. Mr Vernon &amp; I walked out to_____ &amp; dined with J Fitzmaurice. The house stands about halfway up the mountain &amp; commands a most extensive &amp; beautiful view of the surrounding country for many miles, bounded by the Wiklow &amp; other mountains, taking in Carlow in north 10 miles or more off &amp; other towns. We spent a very pleasant day. Received from &amp; wrote a letter to William</p>","pageId":696,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":125,"lock":null}
20:13:21.438 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.438 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/135
20:13:21.438 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":135,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":5,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine spring day with a shower of rain in the morning. Wind SW. Mr Vernon &amp; I walked out to_____ &amp; dined with J Fitzmaurice. The house stands about halfway up the mountain &amp; commands a most extensive &amp; beautiful view of the surrounding country for many miles, bounded by the Wiklow &amp; other mountains, taking in Carlow in north 10 miles or more off &amp; other towns. We spent a very pleasant day. Received from &amp; wrote a letter to William</p>","pageId":696,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":125,"lock":null}
20:13:21.438 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1350
20:13:21.438 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1350,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather cloudy. Wind W by N. Afterwards NE. H Harry &amp; I walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home. Went again to Tynemouth in the afternoon. Saw Bess became friends again &amp; had a long walk with her. Got to the <span class=highlight_yellow>Mont</span>, <span class=highlight_yellow>trcien</span> about 11 o'clock</p>","pageId":916,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1296,"lock":null}
20:13:21.438 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.439 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1350
20:13:21.439 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1350,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather cloudy. Wind W by N. Afterwards NE. H Harry &amp; I walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home. Went again to Tynemouth in the afternoon. Saw Bess became friends again &amp; had a long walk with her. Got to the <span class=highlight_yellow>Mont</span>, <span class=highlight_yellow>trcien</span> about 11 o'clock</p>","pageId":916,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1296,"lock":null}
20:13:21.439 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1351
20:13:21.439 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1351,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At last a change in the weather, having rain, but wild &amp; wind WSW. A fine <span class=highlight_yellow>growing</span> day. Dined at home. Spent the afternoon with Bess at Mrs Woodham's. H Harry &amp; I walked to Tynemouth in the evening. Called on our return at the Duke of York &amp; afterwards at the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":916,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1297,"lock":null}
20:13:21.439 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.439 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1351
20:13:21.439 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1351,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At last a change in the weather, having rain, but wild &amp; wind WSW. A fine <span class=highlight_yellow>growing</span> day. Dined at home. Spent the afternoon with Bess at Mrs Woodham's. H Harry &amp; I walked to Tynemouth in the evening. Called on our return at the Duke of York &amp; afterwards at the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":916,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1297,"lock":null}
20:13:21.439 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1352
20:13:21.439 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1352,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet morning. The rain will do great good. The country being much in want of it. Wind E by S. Dined at home. Spent the afternoon on board the Telemachus, with Mr Bradshaw. At the Albion &amp; Mulstrum in the evening</p>","pageId":916,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1298,"lock":null}
20:13:21.439 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.440 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1352
20:13:21.440 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1352,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet morning. The rain will do great good. The country being much in want of it. Wind E by S. Dined at home. Spent the afternoon on board the Telemachus, with Mr Bradshaw. At the Albion &amp; Mulstrum in the evening</p>","pageId":916,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1298,"lock":null}
20:13:21.440 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1353
20:13:21.440 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1353,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind WNW but in the middle of the day again changed to SE. Did not go to church. Dined at home. In the afternoon walked to Billy Mill &amp; took wine with Charlton. Walked to Tynemouth in the evening &amp; afterwards at the Commercial &amp; Mulstrum</p>","pageId":916,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1299,"lock":null}
20:13:21.440 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.440 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1353
20:13:21.440 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1353,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind WNW but in the middle of the day again changed to SE. Did not go to church. Dined at home. In the afternoon walked to Billy Mill &amp; took wine with Charlton. Walked to Tynemouth in the evening &amp; afterwards at the Commercial &amp; Mulstrum</p>","pageId":916,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1299,"lock":null}
20:13:21.440 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1354
20:13:21.440 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1354,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind SE. Received a letter yesterday from Stephenson of his arrival at <span class=highlight_yellow>Wyburg</span> on the 13<sup>th</sup> May &amp; his lower-hold being full at the date of his letter, the 20<sup>th</sup>. Went by steamer to Newcastle. I walked out to Benton to dine &amp; stay all night. Mrs Smith &amp; Fanny just arrived from Togston &amp; entered taking Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>albraith</font> back with them on Saturday</p>","pageId":917,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1300,"lock":null}
20:13:21.440 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.440 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1354
20:13:21.440 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1354,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind SE. Received a letter yesterday from Stephenson of his arrival at <span class=highlight_yellow>Wyburg</span> on the 13<sup>th</sup> May &amp; his lower-hold being full at the date of his letter, the 20<sup>th</sup>. Went by steamer to Newcastle. I walked out to Benton to dine &amp; stay all night. Mrs Smith &amp; Fanny just arrived from Togston &amp; entered taking Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>albraith</font> back with them on Saturday</p>","pageId":917,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1300,"lock":null}
20:13:21.440 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1355
20:13:21.440 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1355,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind SW. Very unwell last night &amp; all the day suffered from eating some salmon. Walked into Newcastle with D Dixon. Saw Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>albraith</font> &amp; took the steam boat to Shields. Dined with Doctor &amp; afterwards walked up to his garden. Very unwell this evening. Took some tincture of rhubarb a couple of pills &amp; went early to bed.</p>","pageId":917,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1301,"lock":null}
20:13:21.440 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.441 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1355
20:13:21.441 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1355,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind SW. Very unwell last night &amp; all the day suffered from eating some salmon. Walked into Newcastle with D Dixon. Saw Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>albraith</font> &amp; took the steam boat to Shields. Dined with Doctor &amp; afterwards walked up to his garden. Very unwell this evening. Took some tincture of rhubarb a couple of pills &amp; went early to bed.</p>","pageId":917,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1301,"lock":null}
20:13:21.441 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1356
20:13:21.441 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1356,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning blowing fresh at SW by S. Received a letter from Stephenson of his safe arrival at Hull after a fine passage of sixteen days from Wy<font color=#BFBFBF>n</font>burg <font color=#BFBFBF>(Cape Town)</font>. He has to lay 8 days quarantine.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>P<font color=#BFBFBF>ai</font>d average Hope Club &pound;9.17.6 &amp; Mrs Brown sail-making etc. &pound;5.15.6. Wrote to Stephenson. Dined at home. Went on board W<font color=#BFBFBF>illia</font>m C Wright's ship the Mulgrave Castle with H Harry, bound to Archangel. At the Albion &amp; afterwards at the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":917,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1302,"lock":null}
20:13:21.441 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.441 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1356
20:13:21.441 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1356,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning blowing fresh at SW by S. Received a letter from Stephenson of his safe arrival at Hull after a fine passage of sixteen days from Wy<font color=#BFBFBF>n</font>burg <font color=#BFBFBF>(Cape Town)</font>. He has to lay 8 days quarantine.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>P<font color=#BFBFBF>ai</font>d average Hope Club &pound;9.17.6 &amp; Mrs Brown sail-making etc. &pound;5.15.6. Wrote to Stephenson. Dined at home. Went on board W<font color=#BFBFBF>illia</font>m C Wright's ship the Mulgrave Castle with H Harry, bound to Archangel. At the Albion &amp; afterwards at the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":917,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1302,"lock":null}
20:13:21.441 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1357
20:13:21.441 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1357,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine growing morning. Been a shower &amp; the appearance of more rain. Wind SW.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Received a letter (post paid) from Harenan &amp; Co, London, enclosing Stephenson's WyBurg bills of &pound;50.5/ for acceptance. Accepted at by leave of Chapman's payable at Barketts &amp; Co, dated 29<sup>th</sup> Aug &amp; returned it by post. Lockwood dined with me. Walked round in the afternoon by the Doctor's garden to Tynemouth. At Tynemouth also in the morning. At the Albion &amp; Mulstrum in the evening.</p>","pageId":918,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1303,"lock":null}
20:13:21.441 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.442 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1357
20:13:21.442 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1357,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine growing morning. Been a shower &amp; the appearance of more rain. Wind SW.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Received a letter (post paid) from Harenan &amp; Co, London, enclosing Stephenson's WyBurg bills of &pound;50.5/ for acceptance. Accepted at by leave of Chapman's payable at Barketts &amp; Co, dated 29<sup>th</sup> Aug &amp; returned it by post. Lockwood dined with me. Walked round in the afternoon by the Doctor's garden to Tynemouth. At Tynemouth also in the morning. At the Albion &amp; Mulstrum in the evening.</p>","pageId":918,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1303,"lock":null}
20:13:21.442 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1358
20:13:21.442 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1358,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind about West. Received a letter from WBS from Carlow &amp; clear Stephenson's letter from Wyburg of his being loaded. Wrote to WBS. Dined at home. Walked to Tynemouth in the afternoon with H Harry. At the Duke of York &amp; Mulstrum</p>","pageId":918,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1304,"lock":null}
20:13:21.442 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.442 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1358
20:13:21.442 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1358,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind about West. Received a letter from WBS from Carlow &amp; clear Stephenson's letter from Wyburg of his being loaded. Wrote to WBS. Dined at home. Walked to Tynemouth in the afternoon with H Harry. At the Duke of York &amp; Mulstrum</p>","pageId":918,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1304,"lock":null}
20:13:21.442 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1359
20:13:21.442 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1359,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind SSW. A shower of rain about 1 o'clock. L<font color=#BFBFBF>ieutenan</font><sup>t</sup> Griffin RM took his dinner with me &amp; Webb came along afterwards. Walked to Tynemouth in the evening. P<font color=#BFBFBF>ai</font><sup>d</sup> E Reid's mother &pound;2.6.9 balance of <span class=highlight_yellow>gegarayers</span> wages</p>","pageId":918,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1305,"lock":null}
20:13:21.442 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.443 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1359
20:13:21.443 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1359,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind SSW. A shower of rain about 1 o'clock. L<font color=#BFBFBF>ieutenan</font><sup>t</sup> Griffin RM took his dinner with me &amp; Webb came along afterwards. Walked to Tynemouth in the evening. P<font color=#BFBFBF>ai</font><sup>d</sup> E Reid's mother &pound;2.6.9 balance of <span class=highlight_yellow>gegarayers</span> wages</p>","pageId":918,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1305,"lock":null}
20:13:21.443 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/136
20:13:21.443 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":136,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":5,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine spring day, very warm, with a few gentle showers. Wind SW. Engaged in the morning packing then called upon Mr W Fishbeam. Dined at Mr Vernon. The two Mr Cureys dined with us. Spent a very pleasant evening</p>","pageId":696,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":126,"lock":null}
20:13:21.443 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.443 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/136
20:13:21.443 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":136,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":5,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine spring day, very warm, with a few gentle showers. Wind SW. Engaged in the morning packing then called upon Mr W Fishbeam. Dined at Mr Vernon. The two Mr Cureys dined with us. Spent a very pleasant evening</p>","pageId":696,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":126,"lock":null}
20:13:21.443 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1360
20:13:21.443 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1360,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind SW. Went to church. Walked to Tynemouth. One company of the 60<sup>th</sup> marched for Newcastle. Lockerwood, J Rudyard &amp; Griffin dined with me at Tynemouth again in the evening &amp; afterwards at the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":918,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1306,"lock":null}
20:13:21.443 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.444 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1360
20:13:21.444 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1360,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind SW. Went to church. Walked to Tynemouth. One company of the 60<sup>th</sup> marched for Newcastle. Lockerwood, J Rudyard &amp; Griffin dined with me at Tynemouth again in the evening &amp; afterwards at the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":918,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1306,"lock":null}
20:13:21.444 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1361
20:13:21.444 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1361,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind about West. Gave Roberts a draft for &pound;5 for the house. Got &pound;5 of Chapmans on my own account. H Harry &amp; I took the steamer to Newcastle &amp; walked up to the course. The two last races very well contested. Very little company there <span class=highlight_yellow>ended</span> &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>left</span> from <span class=highlight_yellow>there</span> usual. Dined at the Grand Stand. Walked into Newcastle again &amp; returned to Shields which we did not reach until 11 o'clock having been <span class=highlight_yellow>agreed</span> at St Peter's &amp; 3 &frac12; hours in coming down. At the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":919,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1307,"lock":null}
20:13:21.444 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.445 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1361
20:13:21.445 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1361,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind about West. Gave Roberts a draft for &pound;5 for the house. Got &pound;5 of Chapmans on my own account. H Harry &amp; I took the steamer to Newcastle &amp; walked up to the course. The two last races very well contested. Very little company there <span class=highlight_yellow>ended</span> &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>left</span> from <span class=highlight_yellow>there</span> usual. Dined at the Grand Stand. Walked into Newcastle again &amp; returned to Shields which we did not reach until 11 o'clock having been <span class=highlight_yellow>agreed</span> at St Peter's &amp; 3 &frac12; hours in coming down. At the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":919,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1307,"lock":null}
20:13:21.445 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1362
20:13:21.445 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1362,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy dull morning. Wind SW. Lunched with J Tinley who afterwards drove us up in his phaeton to the races. The <span class=highlight_yellow>racing</span> as good as could be. Returned to Tinley's to dinner at &frac12; past 7 o'clock</p>","pageId":919,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1308,"lock":null}
20:13:21.445 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.445 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1362
20:13:21.445 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1362,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy dull morning. Wind SW. Lunched with J Tinley who afterwards drove us up in his phaeton to the races. The <span class=highlight_yellow>racing</span> as good as could be. Returned to Tinley's to dinner at &frac12; past 7 o'clock</p>","pageId":919,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1308,"lock":null}
20:13:21.445 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1363
20:13:21.445 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1363,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind SE. received a letter from Stephenson informing us of the ship's being released from quarantine on the Monday before she took the ground as she delivered in the old harbour at Mr Eade's warf. Bathed for the first time this season. Dined at home. H Harry, Richardson &amp; I went over the water to Bullocks &amp; had some <span class=highlight_yellow>peanalary</span>. At the Albion in the evening &amp; afterwards at the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":919,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1309,"lock":null}
20:13:21.445 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.445 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1363
20:13:21.445 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1363,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind SE. received a letter from Stephenson informing us of the ship's being released from quarantine on the Monday before she took the ground as she delivered in the old harbour at Mr Eade's warf. Bathed for the first time this season. Dined at home. H Harry, Richardson &amp; I went over the water to Bullocks &amp; had some <span class=highlight_yellow>peanalary</span>. At the Albion in the evening &amp; afterwards at the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":919,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1309,"lock":null}
20:13:21.445 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1364
20:13:21.445 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1364,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind  SE having been west at night. Lunched with J Tinley who afterwards drove me, Major <span class=highlight_yellow>Garthwest</span> etc to the races which were but indifferent but attended by crowds of people. Got home to dinner at 7 o'clock in the evening. At the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":920,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1310,"lock":null}
20:13:21.445 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.446 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1364
20:13:21.446 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1364,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind  SE having been west at night. Lunched with J Tinley who afterwards drove me, Major <span class=highlight_yellow>Garthwest</span> etc to the races which were but indifferent but attended by crowds of people. Got home to dinner at 7 o'clock in the evening. At the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":920,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1310,"lock":null}
20:13:21.446 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1365
20:13:21.446 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1365,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine growing rain &amp; been showers during the night. Wind WNW. Glass fallen.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Paid &pound;14 into C<font color=#BFBFBF>hapman'</font>s on account of ex<font color=#BFBFBF>ecut</font>ors. Dined at home. At the Albion in the afternoon &amp; in the evening walked to Tynemouth. At the Mulstrum at night.</p>","pageId":920,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1311,"lock":null}
20:13:21.446 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.446 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1365
20:13:21.446 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1365,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine growing rain &amp; been showers during the night. Wind WNW. Glass fallen.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Paid &pound;14 into C<font color=#BFBFBF>hapman'</font>s on account of ex<font color=#BFBFBF>ecut</font>ors. Dined at home. At the Albion in the afternoon &amp; in the evening walked to Tynemouth. At the Mulstrum at night.</p>","pageId":920,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1311,"lock":null}
20:13:21.446 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1366
20:13:21.446 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1366,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cloudy day with showers. Wind variable between NNE &amp; NNW. Received a letter from WBS from Dublin of his intention of being here tomorrow or Monday. Went over the water to enquire about the coach to York. Dined at home. Engaged writing etc. in the afternoon &amp; at the Albion in the evening. A very rainy night.</p>","pageId":920,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1312,"lock":null}
20:13:21.446 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.447 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1366
20:13:21.447 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1366,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cloudy day with showers. Wind variable between NNE &amp; NNW. Received a letter from WBS from Dublin of his intention of being here tomorrow or Monday. Went over the water to enquire about the coach to York. Dined at home. Engaged writing etc. in the afternoon &amp; at the Albion in the evening. A very rainy night.</p>","pageId":920,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1312,"lock":null}
20:13:21.447 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1367
20:13:21.447 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1367,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning but fair. Wind fresh at N by E &amp; NNE. Crossed the water &amp; got on the coach for York westside at 8 o'clock where we arrived at 6 o'clock to dinner after a very pleasant drive without rain. Got an <span class=highlight_yellow>inside</span> in the march at &frac12; past 7 o'clock &amp; arrived at Hull at &frac12; past 12 o'clock. A beautiful moonlight night. Drank a glass of whiskey Toddy &amp; went to bed.</p>","pageId":920,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1313,"lock":null}
20:13:21.447 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.447 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1367
20:13:21.447 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1367,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning but fair. Wind fresh at N by E &amp; NNE. Crossed the water &amp; got on the coach for York westside at 8 o'clock where we arrived at 6 o'clock to dinner after a very pleasant drive without rain. Got an <span class=highlight_yellow>inside</span> in the march at &frac12; past 7 o'clock &amp; arrived at Hull at &frac12; past 12 o'clock. A beautiful moonlight night. Drank a glass of whiskey Toddy &amp; went to bed.</p>","pageId":920,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1313,"lock":null}
20:13:21.447 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1368
20:13:21.447 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1368,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind N by E. After breakfast went &amp; Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Garbertts</span>, met Stephenson on the road. Afterwards walked to the ship &amp; saw the merchant but would not freight until the ship is out. Dined on board. A heavy thunder storm in the afternoon &amp; continued to rain all day. Stephenson &amp; I in the evening walked round the docks etc &amp; finished with a glass of toddy at the <span class=highlight_yellow>Ina</span></p>","pageId":921,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1314,"lock":null}
20:13:21.447 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.448 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1368
20:13:21.448 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1368,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind N by E. After breakfast went &amp; Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Garbertts</span>, met Stephenson on the road. Afterwards walked to the ship &amp; saw the merchant but would not freight until the ship is out. Dined on board. A heavy thunder storm in the afternoon &amp; continued to rain all day. Stephenson &amp; I in the evening walked round the docks etc &amp; finished with a glass of toddy at the <span class=highlight_yellow>Ina</span></p>","pageId":921,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1314,"lock":null}
20:13:21.448 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1369
20:13:21.448 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1369,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull &amp; very sultry close morning. Wind N by W &amp; NNW. Called upon Martin Orr at the Garrison. Saw Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Garb</span><span class=highlight_yellow>utt</span> but declined fixing a foreign mail being expected &amp; the chance of freights being better. H French dined with me on board after having a long walk about the town. The ship out &amp; cleared this afternoon. Wrote to Bess B. Martin Orr &amp; his wife called upon me at the ship. Set H French <span class=highlight_yellow>part</span> of the way home &amp; amused myself the remainder of the evening by strolling round the town. Turned out a very rainy day.</p>","pageId":921,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1315,"lock":null}
20:13:21.448 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.448 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1369
20:13:21.448 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1369,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull &amp; very sultry close morning. Wind N by W &amp; NNW. Called upon Martin Orr at the Garrison. Saw Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Garb</span><span class=highlight_yellow>utt</span> but declined fixing a foreign mail being expected &amp; the chance of freights being better. H French dined with me on board after having a long walk about the town. The ship out &amp; cleared this afternoon. Wrote to Bess B. Martin Orr &amp; his wife called upon me at the ship. Set H French <span class=highlight_yellow>part</span> of the way home &amp; amused myself the remainder of the evening by strolling round the town. Turned out a very rainy day.</p>","pageId":921,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1315,"lock":null}
20:13:21.448 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/137
20:13:21.448 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":137,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":5,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day but cold wind NW. Went to church in the morning &amp; heard a very good discourse from Mr Vernon. Wrote a letter to Mrs Scott. Dined at the Mr Careys &amp; spent an extremely pleasant day. Present Mr Vernon, Captain Warren (65<sup>th</sup> regiment), 2 Careys, Ed Butler &amp; Mr Ballerely. Came into wine</p>","pageId":696,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":127,"lock":null}
20:13:21.448 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.448 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/137
20:13:21.448 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":137,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":5,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day but cold wind NW. Went to church in the morning &amp; heard a very good discourse from Mr Vernon. Wrote a letter to Mrs Scott. Dined at the Mr Careys &amp; spent an extremely pleasant day. Present Mr Vernon, Captain Warren (65<sup>th</sup> regiment), 2 Careys, Ed Butler &amp; Mr Ballerely. Came into wine</p>","pageId":696,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":127,"lock":null}
20:13:21.448 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1370
20:13:21.448 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1370,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very rainy morning. Wind NW. Called at <span class=highlight_yellow>Garbu</span><span class=highlight_yellow>tt'</span><span class=highlight_yellow>s</span>. Stephenson busy paying dock dues etc. &amp; getting ships provisions on board. The rain &amp; wind prevented the lighters working &amp; we got no ballast today. Dined at 4 o'clock with J Bell. Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Ward</span> dined with us. In the evening walked to H French's house &amp; spent it with <span class=highlight_yellow>nens</span> &amp; Fanny</p>","pageId":921,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1316,"lock":null}
20:13:21.448 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.449 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1370
20:13:21.449 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1370,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very rainy morning. Wind NW. Called at <span class=highlight_yellow>Garbu</span><span class=highlight_yellow>tt'</span><span class=highlight_yellow>s</span>. Stephenson busy paying dock dues etc. &amp; getting ships provisions on board. The rain &amp; wind prevented the lighters working &amp; we got no ballast today. Dined at 4 o'clock with J Bell. Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Ward</span> dined with us. In the evening walked to H French's house &amp; spent it with <span class=highlight_yellow>nens</span> &amp; Fanny</p>","pageId":921,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1316,"lock":null}
20:13:21.449 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1371
20:13:21.449 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1371,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather. Wind NNW. Breakfasted with Orr &amp; his wife at the Garrison. Saw the armoury containing the arms of all the local militias etc of the district, about 20000. Walked up to the ship, a <span class=highlight_yellow>lighter</span> up with 40 tons of ballast. At Garbutt's, Wade not having got the deal <span class=highlight_yellow>counted</span> are unable to settle the freight. Dined on board. Walked about the town &amp; docks in the afternoon &amp; spent the evening with Orr. Wrote to WBS</p>","pageId":922,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1317,"lock":null}
20:13:21.449 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
