20:13:21.450 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1373,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<figure>\r\n  <a href=\"https://www.google.co.uk/maps/@53.741044,-0.3337215,3a,75y,64.63h,92.28t/data=!3m6!1e1!3m4!1scLHcGbd_2wPlsjJKGXzqHQ!2e0!7i13312!8i6656?hl=en\" >\r\n    <img src=\"images/img2780-cross-keys-hull.jpg\" width=\"600px\" />\r\n    <figcaption>The Cross Keys Hotel, Hull</figcaption>\r\n  </a>\r\n</figure>","pageId":920,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":1319,"lock":null}
20:13:21.450 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1374
20:13:21.450 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1374,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":2,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A most delightful morning. Wind SW. the Hope <span class=highlight_yellow>warped</span> down to Southend pier &amp; at high water sailed for Wyburg. Mr Garbutt settled the freight with the merchant &amp; I settled his account for brokerage etc receiving a bill at 4 months, accepted payment at <span class=highlight_yellow>Glgme</span> &amp; their bills at 2 months for balance of first half freight <span class=highlight_yellow>smith</span> to &pound;50.4 &amp; cash &pound;1-9-9. Mr G<font color=#BFBFBF>arbutt</font>'s account &pound;15.6.6</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Dined with Mr Garbutt &amp; in the evening H French took grog with me at the Cross Keys. Received of Mr Stephenson &pound;8- to give the carpenter's wife &pound;5 &amp; the cook &pound;3. Paid Stephenson &pound;6.0.1 the balance of his Wyburg account due to him.</p>","pageId":922,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1320,"lock":null}
20:13:21.450 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.451 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1374
20:13:21.451 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1374,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":2,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A most delightful morning. Wind SW. the Hope <span class=highlight_yellow>warped</span> down to Southend pier &amp; at high water sailed for Wyburg. Mr Garbutt settled the freight with the merchant &amp; I settled his account for brokerage etc receiving a bill at 4 months, accepted payment at <span class=highlight_yellow>Glgme</span> &amp; their bills at 2 months for balance of first half freight <span class=highlight_yellow>smith</span> to &pound;50.4 &amp; cash &pound;1-9-9. Mr G<font color=#BFBFBF>arbutt</font>'s account &pound;15.6.6</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Dined with Mr Garbutt &amp; in the evening H French took grog with me at the Cross Keys. Received of Mr Stephenson &pound;8- to give the carpenter's wife &pound;5 &amp; the cook &pound;3. Paid Stephenson &pound;6.0.1 the balance of his Wyburg account due to him.</p>","pageId":922,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1320,"lock":null}
