20:13:21.453 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":138,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":5,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day with a cool NW wind. The cattle fair at Carlow, town was crowded. Got the last trunk nearly packed with books, plates etc. Dined at Mr Vernon</p>","pageId":696,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":128,"lock":null}
20:13:21.453 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1380
20:13:21.453 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1380,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most delightful morning. Wind SE. paid Walnsley baker &pound;9.3, Morris butcher &pound;9, Bradshaws Irish pork 3 casks &pound;9. J Tinley dined with us at 5 o'clock. Ben Galbraith &amp; I walked to Tynemouth in the evening.</p>","pageId":924,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1326,"lock":null}
20:13:21.453 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.454 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1380
20:13:21.454 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1380,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most delightful morning. Wind SE. paid Walnsley baker &pound;9.3, Morris butcher &pound;9, Bradshaws Irish pork 3 casks &pound;9. J Tinley dined with us at 5 o'clock. Ben Galbraith &amp; I walked to Tynemouth in the evening.</p>","pageId":924,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1326,"lock":null}
20:13:21.454 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1381
20:13:21.454 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1381,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Beautiful weather. Wind SE. Went with WBS on board the City of Edinburgh to take his birth to London.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Bathed at 1 o'clock. Accompanied a party of officers to Wallsend and dined with <span class=highlight_yellow>Hotts</span> a large party &amp; spent a very pleasant day. He was so kind as to send his carriage for us. At the Mulstrum in the evening.</p>","pageId":924,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1327,"lock":null}
20:13:21.454 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.454 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1381
20:13:21.454 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1381,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Beautiful weather. Wind SE. Went with WBS on board the City of Edinburgh to take his birth to London.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Bathed at 1 o'clock. Accompanied a party of officers to Wallsend and dined with <span class=highlight_yellow>Hotts</span> a large party &amp; spent a very pleasant day. He was so kind as to send his carriage for us. At the Mulstrum in the evening.</p>","pageId":924,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1327,"lock":null}
20:13:21.454 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1382
20:13:21.454 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1382,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind SE. Moor &amp; his brothers with J Tinley with us. Foster Moor signed a document making over to us all his stack &amp; crop etc &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>resigning</span> the farm which we have allowed Mr Moor to take as <span class=highlight_yellow>tinanl</span>. Walked up to Preston. People busy with the potatoes &amp; turnips &amp; clearing the hedges.  Gave in a draft on Chapmans for &pound;20 for WBS. <span class=highlight_yellow>Dined</span> at 2 o'clock. Went on board the City of Edinburgh steamer with WBS &amp; saw him sail for London. Ben &amp; I walked to Tynemouth in the evening. A heavy rain about &frac12; past 10 o'clock</p>","pageId":924,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1328,"lock":null}
20:13:21.454 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.454 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1382
20:13:21.454 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1382,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind SE. Moor &amp; his brothers with J Tinley with us. Foster Moor signed a document making over to us all his stack &amp; crop etc &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>resigning</span> the farm which we have allowed Mr Moor to take as <span class=highlight_yellow>tinanl</span>. Walked up to Preston. People busy with the potatoes &amp; turnips &amp; clearing the hedges.  Gave in a draft on Chapmans for &pound;20 for WBS. <span class=highlight_yellow>Dined</span> at 2 o'clock. Went on board the City of Edinburgh steamer with WBS &amp; saw him sail for London. Ben &amp; I walked to Tynemouth in the evening. A heavy rain about &frac12; past 10 o'clock</p>","pageId":924,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1328,"lock":null}
20:13:21.454 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1383
20:13:21.454 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1383,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning after the rain, having been a good deal in the night 7 the appearance yet of more wind E by N &amp; ENE. At church in the morning. D Dixon called but we were out. Dined at home. Took tea with Messrs Harry, walked to Tynemouth in the evening. Very foggy &amp; damp. Finished at H Harry's with a glass of whiskey</p>","pageId":924,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1329,"lock":null}
20:13:21.454 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.455 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1383
20:13:21.455 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1383,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning after the rain, having been a good deal in the night 7 the appearance yet of more wind E by N &amp; ENE. At church in the morning. D Dixon called but we were out. Dined at home. Took tea with Messrs Harry, walked to Tynemouth in the evening. Very foggy &amp; damp. Finished at H Harry's with a glass of whiskey</p>","pageId":924,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1329,"lock":null}
20:13:21.455 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1384
20:13:21.455 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1384,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind ESE. Very foggy. Ben &amp; I got on board a steamer &amp; went to Newcastle. Saw D Dixon. I walked with him out to Benton, dined &amp; in the evening walked through the country to Shields. Called at the Mustrum</p>","pageId":925,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1330,"lock":null}
20:13:21.455 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.455 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1384
20:13:21.455 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1384,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind ESE. Very foggy. Ben &amp; I got on board a steamer &amp; went to Newcastle. Saw D Dixon. I walked with him out to Benton, dined &amp; in the evening walked through the country to Shields. Called at the Mustrum</p>","pageId":925,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1330,"lock":null}
20:13:21.455 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1385
20:13:21.455 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1385,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of foggy weather. Wind ENE. Paid Gibson butcher. Wyburg &pound;8.6/-. Walked to Tynemouth &amp; afterwards out to Preston &amp; dined with Mr Wright. Walked home again in the evening. Called at the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":925,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1331,"lock":null}
20:13:21.455 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.455 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1385
20:13:21.455 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1385,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of foggy weather. Wind ENE. Paid Gibson butcher. Wyburg &pound;8.6/-. Walked to Tynemouth &amp; afterwards out to Preston &amp; dined with Mr Wright. Walked home again in the evening. Called at the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":925,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1331,"lock":null}
20:13:21.455 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1386
20:13:21.455 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1386,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very unpleasant foggy &amp; damp morning. Wind NE. Cleared away towards noon. I joined Mr Ilderton &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>ofserted</span> in his <span class=highlight_yellow>canses</span> also promised him my vote. Dined with him &amp; party at the George at 5 o'clock</p>","pageId":925,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1332,"lock":null}
20:13:21.455 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.456 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1386
20:13:21.456 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1386,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very unpleasant foggy &amp; damp morning. Wind NE. Cleared away towards noon. I joined Mr Ilderton &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>ofserted</span> in his <span class=highlight_yellow>canses</span> also promised him my vote. Dined with him &amp; party at the George at 5 o'clock</p>","pageId":925,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1332,"lock":null}
20:13:21.456 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1387
20:13:21.456 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1387,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy morning with the appearance of showers having been showers during the night. Wind SE. Ben Galbraith &amp; Robert set off in Dunn's gig to catch the Alnwick coach at Newcastle for Felton where Tom Smith's phaeton will meet them. I could not go having promised to continue my assistance to Mr Ilderton all day &amp; very successful. Sat down to dinner at 5 o'clock. Called at the Albion in the evening.</p>","pageId":925,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1333,"lock":null}
20:13:21.456 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.456 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1387
20:13:21.456 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1387,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy morning with the appearance of showers having been showers during the night. Wind SE. Ben Galbraith &amp; Robert set off in Dunn's gig to catch the Alnwick coach at Newcastle for Felton where Tom Smith's phaeton will meet them. I could not go having promised to continue my assistance to Mr Ilderton all day &amp; very successful. Sat down to dinner at 5 o'clock. Called at the Albion in the evening.</p>","pageId":925,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1333,"lock":null}
20:13:21.456 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1388
20:13:21.456 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1388,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cloudy morning &amp; been some rain. Wind ENE. A very heavy rain for an hour or so which prevented us beginning our canvas until near 11 o'clock commencing at the Wooden bridge &amp; canvassed all the upper part of the town. Milburn Place etc and were very successful. Lunched at Mr Barkers &amp; canvassed Tynemouth in the evening. Dined at 8 o'clock &amp; spent a jolly evening.</p>","pageId":926,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1334,"lock":null}
20:13:21.456 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.456 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1388
20:13:21.456 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1388,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cloudy morning &amp; been some rain. Wind ENE. A very heavy rain for an hour or so which prevented us beginning our canvas until near 11 o'clock commencing at the Wooden bridge &amp; canvassed all the upper part of the town. Milburn Place etc and were very successful. Lunched at Mr Barkers &amp; canvassed Tynemouth in the evening. Dined at 8 o'clock &amp; spent a jolly evening.</p>","pageId":926,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1334,"lock":null}
20:13:21.456 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1389
20:13:21.458 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1389,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Breakfasted early &amp; took the 8 o'clock steamer for Newcastle &amp; at 1 o'clock got upon the coach for Felton where I arrived at a little after 1 o'clock. Had an early dinner &amp; afterwards borrowed a nod of Melrose &amp; had a few hours fishing but little success. Walked down in the cool of the evening to Togston. Got there at &frac12; past 6 o'clock. Found the Clutterbucks dining there.</p>","pageId":926,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1335,"lock":null}
20:13:21.458 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
