20:13:21.460 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1394,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A delightful day &amp; fresh SW breeze. Mr &amp; Mrs Dixon left us for Benton. Walked to the <span class=highlight_yellow>Burches</span> &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Colleerg</span>  with Tom, Lady Smith &amp; family of Tyleys. Called &amp; took lunch. A family party to dinner</p>","pageId":927,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1340,"lock":null}
20:13:21.460 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1395
20:13:21.460 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1395,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind SW. Baker Kop Snowdon &amp; I walked down to <span class=highlight_yellow>w</span><span class=highlight_yellow>aters</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ide</span> to finish, by the time we got there it began to rain heavily, which gave us a soaking. Had but poor sport. Killed about a dozen, not large but fine fish. Returned to dinner at &frac12; past 4 o'clock</p>","pageId":927,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1341,"lock":null}
