20:13:21.462 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1399,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":23,"sequence":3.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful day. Ben Galbraith, Rob Snowdon &amp; I after breakfast, set off to fish at the Hermitage. I however turned off to begin at the Granary but the tide had risen too high. Walked up to the mill streams &amp; fished there all the morning. Fanny &amp; Bell Smith &amp; Emma Galbraith came down &amp; joined us &amp; we all dined together at the Hermitage <font color=#BFBFBF>Inn</font>. Fished up the <span class=highlight_yellow>w</span><span class=highlight_yellow>aterside</span> &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Morick</span> streams in the evening but had very poor sport. Got home to supper after spending a most delightful day.</p>","pageId":928,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1345,"lock":null}
20:13:21.462 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/14
20:13:21.462 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":14,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Dined with Mrs Scott. Spent the evening with the Whist club. Lost 4/-. Wind SE with frost. Wrote to Sir D Smith</p>","pageId":687,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":11,"lock":null}
20:13:21.462 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
