20:13:21.468 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":141,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":5,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine summers day. Amused myself with fly fishing, but had poor sport. Returned to captain Butlers to dinner. Mr &amp; Mrs S George dined with us. Spent a very pleasant day</p>","pageId":696,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":131,"lock":null}
20:13:21.468 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1410
20:13:21.468 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1410,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind SW &amp; ESE. Walked to Tynemouth. Ben G<font color=#BFBFBF>ailbraith</font> went to Newcastle to see Emma. At Tynemouth again in the afternoon. Had a most delightful bath at the end of Cullercoats Sands &amp; dined with L<font color=#BFBFBF>ieutenan</font><sup>t</sup> Mitchel &amp; Lockerwood at the castle. Bess met me on the mound, gave her a long lecture but <span class=highlight_yellow>query</span> it has any good effect. Heavy shower of rain</p>","pageId":930,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1356,"lock":null}
20:13:21.468 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.469 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1410
20:13:21.469 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1410,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind SW &amp; ESE. Walked to Tynemouth. Ben G<font color=#BFBFBF>ailbraith</font> went to Newcastle to see Emma. At Tynemouth again in the afternoon. Had a most delightful bath at the end of Cullercoats Sands &amp; dined with L<font color=#BFBFBF>ieutenan</font><sup>t</sup> Mitchel &amp; Lockerwood at the castle. Bess met me on the mound, gave her a long lecture but <span class=highlight_yellow>query</span> it has any good effect. Heavy shower of rain</p>","pageId":930,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1356,"lock":null}
20:13:21.469 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1411
20:13:21.469 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1411,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind NW. Bathed before breakfast. Engaged at home writing. Dined at home. Called and took a glass of wine with the Doctor. Walked up to Tynemouth. Called &amp; spent the evening at the Castle. At the Mulstrum at night. P<font color=#BFBFBF>ai</font><sup>d</sup> Brown <span class=highlight_yellow>Tarters</span> 17/-</p>","pageId":930,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1357,"lock":null}
20:13:21.469 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.469 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1411
20:13:21.469 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1411,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind NW. Bathed before breakfast. Engaged at home writing. Dined at home. Called and took a glass of wine with the Doctor. Walked up to Tynemouth. Called &amp; spent the evening at the Castle. At the Mulstrum at night. P<font color=#BFBFBF>ai</font><sup>d</sup> Brown <span class=highlight_yellow>Tarters</span> 17/-</p>","pageId":930,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1357,"lock":null}
20:13:21.469 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1412
20:13:21.469 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1412,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NNE. Assisted Roberts in packing up my cloths. Drew on Chapmans &pound;15 on my own account &amp; &pound;20 on ex<font color=#BFBFBF>ecut</font>ors acc<font color=#BFBFBF>oun</font>t  for BB Galgraith's expenses to London etc. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. Wrote to Bess B: &amp; sent &pound;5. Embarked at 5 o'clock on board the City of Edinburgh steamer &amp; sailed a little after 6 o'clock, having on board about 40 passengers. A most beautiful evening's walk a little swell at sea which soon sent some of the <span class=highlight_yellow>crewmen</span> along ...</p>","pageId":930,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1358,"lock":null}
20:13:21.469 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.469 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1412
20:13:21.469 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1412,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NNE. Assisted Roberts in packing up my cloths. Drew on Chapmans &pound;15 on my own account &amp; &pound;20 on ex<font color=#BFBFBF>ecut</font>ors acc<font color=#BFBFBF>oun</font>t  for BB Galgraith's expenses to London etc. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. Wrote to Bess B: &amp; sent &pound;5. Embarked at 5 o'clock on board the City of Edinburgh steamer &amp; sailed a little after 6 o'clock, having on board about 40 passengers. A most beautiful evening's walk a little swell at sea which soon sent some of the <span class=highlight_yellow>crewmen</span> along ...</p>","pageId":930,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1358,"lock":null}
20:13:21.469 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1413
20:13:21.469 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1413,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind from the N &amp; E. Got up at 8 o'clock &amp; breakfasted at 9 o'clock. From the noise &amp; tremulous motion caused by the engine I got very little sleep. The boat off Scarborough at 3 o'clock in the morning &amp; landed Mr J Brandling etc &amp; passed Flamb<font color=#BFBFBF>o</font>ro<font color=#BFBFBF>ugh</font> Head at 5 o'clock &amp; the Dadgeon light about 1 o'clock. Dined at 3 o'clock &amp; at the same time off Cromer. It was after 8 o'clock before we got through the Roads.</p>","pageId":931,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1359,"lock":null}
20:13:21.469 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.470 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1413
20:13:21.470 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1413,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind from the N &amp; E. Got up at 8 o'clock &amp; breakfasted at 9 o'clock. From the noise &amp; tremulous motion caused by the engine I got very little sleep. The boat off Scarborough at 3 o'clock in the morning &amp; landed Mr J Brandling etc &amp; passed Flamb<font color=#BFBFBF>o</font>ro<font color=#BFBFBF>ugh</font> Head at 5 o'clock &amp; the Dadgeon light about 1 o'clock. Dined at 3 o'clock &amp; at the same time off Cromer. It was after 8 o'clock before we got through the Roads.</p>","pageId":931,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1359,"lock":null}
20:13:21.470 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1414
20:13:21.470 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1414,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at &frac12; past 5 o'clock the vessel a little below the Nore light. A fine morning with a fresh breeze from the NW. Having a strong ebb tide against us, we did not reach Blackwell until about 1 o'clock when J Mitchell RM, Ben &amp; I put all our luggage into a boat &amp; rowed up to the tower stairs, took a coach &amp; drove to Philpot Lane &amp; therein to Nottingham place. Ben &amp; I there walked out. Dined at 6 o'clock <font color=#BFBFBF>at </font>Richmond, Mitchell &amp; Bob Marsh dined with us. With the latter I became reconciled and friendly again he having explained his sorrow &amp; shame at his conduct towards me. This reconciliation has contributed much to the pleasure of my visit to London together with a letter received from Col<font color=#BFBFBF>onel </font> Foswell saying that he will pay his son's debt to me, which may be considered a god send; It will however enable me to pay my expenses &amp; so enjoy my visit the more.</p>","pageId":931,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1360,"lock":null}
20:13:21.470 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.470 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1414
20:13:21.470 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1414,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at &frac12; past 5 o'clock the vessel a little below the Nore light. A fine morning with a fresh breeze from the NW. Having a strong ebb tide against us, we did not reach Blackwell until about 1 o'clock when J Mitchell RM, Ben &amp; I put all our luggage into a boat &amp; rowed up to the tower stairs, took a coach &amp; drove to Philpot Lane &amp; therein to Nottingham place. Ben &amp; I there walked out. Dined at 6 o'clock <font color=#BFBFBF>at </font>Richmond, Mitchell &amp; Bob Marsh dined with us. With the latter I became reconciled and friendly again he having explained his sorrow &amp; shame at his conduct towards me. This reconciliation has contributed much to the pleasure of my visit to London together with a letter received from Col<font color=#BFBFBF>onel </font> Foswell saying that he will pay his son's debt to me, which may be considered a god send; It will however enable me to pay my expenses &amp; so enjoy my visit the more.</p>","pageId":931,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1360,"lock":null}
20:13:21.470 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1415
20:13:21.470 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1415,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning with rain. Wind NNE. Did not go out till near 12 o'clock. Called upon MrWard &amp; Richmond. Wrote to Bess. WBS, Ben G<font color=#BFBFBF>albraith</font> &amp; I dined at the Blue Posts &amp; afterwards went to Astleys</p>","pageId":931,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1361,"lock":null}
20:13:21.470 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
