20:13:21.471 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1416,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<figure>\r\n  <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northumberland_House\" >\r\n    <img src=\"images/img2791-northumberland-house-london.jpg\" width=\"600px\" />\r\n    <figcaption>Northumberland House, London</figcaption>\r\n  </a>\r\n</figure>","pageId":931,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":1362,"lock":null}
20:13:21.471 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1417
20:13:21.471 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1417,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":17,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. WBS &amp; <font color=#BFBFBF>I</font> walked down to &amp; called at North<font color=#BFBFBF>umber</font>l<font color=#BFBFBF>an</font>d House. Saw and had a long conversation with Mr Boyle who thought that I had not been well treated. Called &amp; sat with Bob Marsh, went with him to the court of chancery, afterwards had a long wait round by the west end. Towards dinner time we had a tremendous heavy storm of rain, thunder &amp; lightening. Dined with Richardson at 6 o'clock, and in the evening took a boat at Westminster Bridge &amp; went to Vauxhall but did not go in as there were no <span class=highlight_yellow>fine</span> works. Returned &amp; got into the gallery of the House of Commons where we sat until 2 o'clock in the morning. Nothing interesting going on.</p>","pageId":931,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1363,"lock":null}
20:13:21.471 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
