20:13:21.472 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1417,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":17,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. WBS &amp; <font color=#BFBFBF>I</font> walked down to &amp; called at North<font color=#BFBFBF>umber</font>l<font color=#BFBFBF>an</font>d House. Saw and had a long conversation with Mr Boyle who thought that I had not been well treated. Called &amp; sat with Bob Marsh, went with him to the court of chancery, afterwards had a long wait round by the west end. Towards dinner time we had a tremendous heavy storm of rain, thunder &amp; lightening. Dined with Richardson at 6 o'clock, and in the evening took a boat at Westminster Bridge &amp; went to Vauxhall but did not go in as there were no <span class=highlight_yellow>fine</span> works. Returned &amp; got into the gallery of the House of Commons where we sat until 2 o'clock in the morning. Nothing interesting going on.</p>","pageId":931,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1363,"lock":null}
20:13:21.472 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1418
20:13:21.472 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1418,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind about N. After breakfast got upon a Paddington Stage &amp; rode into the city to get my fishing rods. Surprised but could not find <span class=highlight_yellow>Kitchinman</span>. The <span class=highlight_yellow>juaker</span>, <span class=highlight_yellow>droked</span> Lane having been cleaned away for the approach to London Bridge. Walked out of the city to the west end. Called upon &amp; dined with Richmond. W Richmond &amp; Miss Legg dinned with us. Got to Nottingham Place at 12 o'clock</p>","pageId":931,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1364,"lock":null}
