20:13:21.473 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1420,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":19,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<figure>\r\n  <a href=\"https://southamptonlocalhistorycentre.files.wordpress.com/2014/11/lhf-journal-19-spring-2012.pdf\" >\r\n    <img src=\"images/img2792-baths-southampton.jpg\" width=\"600px\" />\r\n    <figcaption>Baths at Southampton</figcaption>\r\n  </a>\r\n</figure>","pageId":932,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":1366,"lock":null}
20:13:21.473 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1421
20:13:21.473 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1421,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":19,"sequence":3.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning having been rain in the night. Wind fresh at WNW. In endeavouring to throw my portmanteau upon my shoulder, it being very heavy, I strained the muscles of my back very severely &amp; I fear I shall not soon recover from it. Pain very acute. Got on the coach at the White Horse <span class=highlight_yellow>ally</span> at 8 o'clock with WBS &amp; BBG &amp; started for Southampton where we arrived at &frac12; past 4 o'clock having had very fine weather &amp; a pleasant journey, the dust being laid by the rain. My back very painful &amp; with some difficulty got down to my lodgings &amp; to bed. We got Mrs Sands lodgings, the same as when at Southampton before.</p>","pageId":932,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1367,"lock":null}
20:13:21.473 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.474 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1421
20:13:21.474 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1421,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":19,"sequence":3.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning having been rain in the night. Wind fresh at WNW. In endeavouring to throw my portmanteau upon my shoulder, it being very heavy, I strained the muscles of my back very severely &amp; I fear I shall not soon recover from it. Pain very acute. Got on the coach at the White Horse <span class=highlight_yellow>ally</span> at 8 o'clock with WBS &amp; BBG &amp; started for Southampton where we arrived at &frac12; past 4 o'clock having had very fine weather &amp; a pleasant journey, the dust being laid by the rain. My back very painful &amp; with some difficulty got down to my lodgings &amp; to bed. We got Mrs Sands lodgings, the same as when at Southampton before.</p>","pageId":932,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1367,"lock":null}
20:13:21.474 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1422
20:13:21.474 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1422,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day &amp; blowing fresh from the WNW. I made an attempt to get out of bed this morning but my back was so bad I was obliged to lay down again. Breakfasted in bed. About 1 o'clock determined to make another attempt to get up &amp; dress myself &amp; with much difficulty &amp; pain &amp; the assistance of Ben I succeeded. After being up &amp; walking a short time, found myself much easier. Walked down to the Pier &amp; baths. Had a warm bath &amp; Mr Lee afterwards drove me home in his gig. The remainder of the afternoon &amp; evening found myself much relieved. About dinner time we had a very heavy squall with rain.</p>","pageId":932,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1368,"lock":null}
20:13:21.474 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.474 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1422
20:13:21.474 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1422,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day &amp; blowing fresh from the WNW. I made an attempt to get out of bed this morning but my back was so bad I was obliged to lay down again. Breakfasted in bed. About 1 o'clock determined to make another attempt to get up &amp; dress myself &amp; with much difficulty &amp; pain &amp; the assistance of Ben I succeeded. After being up &amp; walking a short time, found myself much easier. Walked down to the Pier &amp; baths. Had a warm bath &amp; Mr Lee afterwards drove me home in his gig. The remainder of the afternoon &amp; evening found myself much relieved. About dinner time we had a very heavy squall with rain.</p>","pageId":932,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1368,"lock":null}
20:13:21.474 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1423
20:13:21.474 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1423,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but blowing hard from the N by E. got up &amp; walked to Mr Lee's to breakfast. Walked down to the post office &amp; pier. Mr Lee drove me down to Shirley to call upon the Lewis. Dined at Mr Lees</p>","pageId":933,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1369,"lock":null}
20:13:21.474 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.475 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1423
20:13:21.475 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1423,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but blowing hard from the N by E. got up &amp; walked to Mr Lee's to breakfast. Walked down to the post office &amp; pier. Mr Lee drove me down to Shirley to call upon the Lewis. Dined at Mr Lees</p>","pageId":933,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1369,"lock":null}
20:13:21.475 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1424
20:13:21.475 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1424,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning . Wind fresh from N by E. Played at billiards. The Lewis's came in &amp; dined at Mr Lees. Messrs Horsford &amp; Hawksley came in the evening. My back much better.</p>","pageId":933,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1370,"lock":null}
20:13:21.475 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.475 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1424
20:13:21.475 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1424,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning . Wind fresh from N by E. Played at billiards. The Lewis's came in &amp; dined at Mr Lees. Messrs Horsford &amp; Hawksley came in the evening. My back much better.</p>","pageId":933,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1370,"lock":null}
20:13:21.475 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1425
20:13:21.475 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1425,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An exceedingly fine morning. Wind SW. Wrote to Garbull &amp; son of Hull to inform him when the Hope arrived etc. Dined at 2 o'clock at Mr lee's. The Lewis there &amp; embarked at &frac12; past 5 o'clock on board the Ariadne steam boat at 6 o'clock. Sailed for Guernsey with a good many passengers on board. A most beautiful evening. Moon light &amp; not a cloud to be seen. I walked the deck until we had passed the Needles &amp; went to bed at 12 o'clock. R Marsh with us</p>","pageId":933,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1371,"lock":null}
20:13:21.475 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.475 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1425
20:13:21.475 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1425,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An exceedingly fine morning. Wind SW. Wrote to Garbull &amp; son of Hull to inform him when the Hope arrived etc. Dined at 2 o'clock at Mr lee's. The Lewis there &amp; embarked at &frac12; past 5 o'clock on board the Ariadne steam boat at 6 o'clock. Sailed for Guernsey with a good many passengers on board. A most beautiful evening. Moon light &amp; not a cloud to be seen. I walked the deck until we had passed the Needles &amp; went to bed at 12 o'clock. R Marsh with us</p>","pageId":933,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1371,"lock":null}
20:13:21.475 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1426
20:13:21.475 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1426,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather cloudy. Wind SW. Got up at 6 o'clock at which time we were abreast of the ____ with Alderney, Sark &amp; Guernsey or S<sup>t</sup> Peters <font color=#BFBFBF>Port </font>in sight. Came to an anchor in Guernsey Sands about 8 o'clock &amp; landed after a most delightful passage. The town of St Peter port is beautifully situated above the bay upon a rising hill &amp; consists of a great many very excellent houses. It is of considerable extent but the streets are narrow. It however is rapidly improving and contains a great many beautiful private houses as well as public institutions, the collage the most striking ...</p>","pageId":933,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1372,"lock":null}
20:13:21.475 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.476 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1426
20:13:21.476 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1426,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather cloudy. Wind SW. Got up at 6 o'clock at which time we were abreast of the ____ with Alderney, Sark &amp; Guernsey or S<sup>t</sup> Peters <font color=#BFBFBF>Port </font>in sight. Came to an anchor in Guernsey Sands about 8 o'clock &amp; landed after a most delightful passage. The town of St Peter port is beautifully situated above the bay upon a rising hill &amp; consists of a great many very excellent houses. It is of considerable extent but the streets are narrow. It however is rapidly improving and contains a great many beautiful private houses as well as public institutions, the collage the most striking ...</p>","pageId":933,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1372,"lock":null}
20:13:21.476 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1427
20:13:21.476 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1427,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":24,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>We put up at Mousehole Hotel which is near the harbour &amp; the back bed room window commanded an exceedingly fine view of the sea adjacent islands. This hotel I recommend to all travellers both for the activity &amp; attention of the landlady &amp; her daughter Mrs ____ &amp; their reasonable charges. There is a small harbour formed by piers which is dry at low water. The rise and fall is very considerable being I should think thirty feet.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Having changed our cloths &amp; made ourselves comfortable we had breakfast. Much to our surprise met James Basher in the coffee room who agreed to join our party at dinner. After breakfast strolled out to see the town. Much pleased with the new market. Fish &amp; butchers etc. It is the best &amp; most perfect thing of the kind I ever saw or heard of.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Afterwards called upon Dr Proctor who was not at home. Went over &amp; saw the interior of the collage, a very fine institution &amp; apparently well placed &amp; of it were not for the low heavy square towers in the centre would be a handsome building.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>During the afternoon saw the <span class=highlight_yellow>presence</span> feast of the town &amp; walked up to the garrison which stands very high upon the south point of the bay which <span class=highlight_yellow>with</span> the town, it &amp; fort completely commands. In our rambles we met with old Charlton late of the firm of Scott &amp; Charlton, who came &amp; dined with us at 6 o'clock. He has lived about a year here. Saw Dr Proctor this afternoon. Much pleased with him.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p></p>","pageId":934,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1373,"lock":null}
20:13:21.476 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.476 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1427
20:13:21.476 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1427,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":24,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>We put up at Mousehole Hotel which is near the harbour &amp; the back bed room window commanded an exceedingly fine view of the sea adjacent islands. This hotel I recommend to all travellers both for the activity &amp; attention of the landlady &amp; her daughter Mrs ____ &amp; their reasonable charges. There is a small harbour formed by piers which is dry at low water. The rise and fall is very considerable being I should think thirty feet.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Having changed our cloths &amp; made ourselves comfortable we had breakfast. Much to our surprise met James Basher in the coffee room who agreed to join our party at dinner. After breakfast strolled out to see the town. Much pleased with the new market. Fish &amp; butchers etc. It is the best &amp; most perfect thing of the kind I ever saw or heard of.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Afterwards called upon Dr Proctor who was not at home. Went over &amp; saw the interior of the collage, a very fine institution &amp; apparently well placed &amp; of it were not for the low heavy square towers in the centre would be a handsome building.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>During the afternoon saw the <span class=highlight_yellow>presence</span> feast of the town &amp; walked up to the garrison which stands very high upon the south point of the bay which <span class=highlight_yellow>with</span> the town, it &amp; fort completely commands. In our rambles we met with old Charlton late of the firm of Scott &amp; Charlton, who came &amp; dined with us at 6 o'clock. He has lived about a year here. Saw Dr Proctor this afternoon. Much pleased with him.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p></p>","pageId":934,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1373,"lock":null}
20:13:21.476 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1428
20:13:21.476 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1428,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Most delightful weather. Wind SW. Had a warm bath this morning. At 12 o'clock we all got into a four wheeled vehicle. Drove round the greater part of the island, excepting the north angles, but there is nothing very picturesque or beautiful to be seen. Got home to dinner at 6 o'clock. Ian Basnes dines out</p>","pageId":935,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1374,"lock":null}
20:13:21.476 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.477 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1428
20:13:21.477 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1428,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Most delightful weather. Wind SW. Had a warm bath this morning. At 12 o'clock we all got into a four wheeled vehicle. Drove round the greater part of the island, excepting the north angles, but there is nothing very picturesque or beautiful to be seen. Got home to dinner at 6 o'clock. Ian Basnes dines out</p>","pageId":935,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1374,"lock":null}
20:13:21.477 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1429
20:13:21.477 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1429,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather. Amused ourselves by strolling about the markets etc. William went &amp; saw Dr Proctor again, but I being tired did not go. Having settled our bill, at 2 o'clock we again embarked on board the <font color=#000000>Ariadne</font><font size=3.4pt color=#000000>&nbsp;</font>&amp; sailed about 9 o'clock. The vessel most uncomfortably crowded, being about 155 passengers on board. We could not get berths. Passed close by the Island of Alderney. A fine sight.</p>","pageId":935,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1375,"lock":null}
20:13:21.477 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.477 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1429
20:13:21.477 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1429,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather. Amused ourselves by strolling about the markets etc. William went &amp; saw Dr Proctor again, but I being tired did not go. Having settled our bill, at 2 o'clock we again embarked on board the <font color=#000000>Ariadne</font><font size=3.4pt color=#000000>&nbsp;</font>&amp; sailed about 9 o'clock. The vessel most uncomfortably crowded, being about 155 passengers on board. We could not get berths. Passed close by the Island of Alderney. A fine sight.</p>","pageId":935,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1375,"lock":null}
20:13:21.477 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/143
20:13:21.477 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":143,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":5,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning with fine spring showers. Left Captain Butlers &amp; returned to Carlow. Mr Vernon &amp; I dined at Mr Butlins &amp; met a very pleasant party</p>","pageId":697,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":133,"lock":null}
20:13:21.477 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.477 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/143
20:13:21.477 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":143,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":5,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning with fine spring showers. Left Captain Butlers &amp; returned to Carlow. Mr Vernon &amp; I dined at Mr Butlins &amp; met a very pleasant party</p>","pageId":697,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":133,"lock":null}
20:13:21.477 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1430
20:13:21.477 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1430,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind SW. We arrived at Southampton at &frac12; past 5 o'clock, very much fatigued having been waiting to sleep or lay on deck all night. After waiting two hours &amp; a half at the custom house, we were obliged to go home to breakfast without our luggage. Dined at the Lewises at Shirley. Colonel Ogilvie &amp; Captain Cobb there.</p>","pageId":935,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1376,"lock":null}
20:13:21.477 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.478 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1430
20:13:21.478 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1430,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind SW. We arrived at Southampton at &frac12; past 5 o'clock, very much fatigued having been waiting to sleep or lay on deck all night. After waiting two hours &amp; a half at the custom house, we were obliged to go home to breakfast without our luggage. Dined at the Lewises at Shirley. Colonel Ogilvie &amp; Captain Cobb there.</p>","pageId":935,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1376,"lock":null}
20:13:21.478 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1431
20:13:21.478 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1431,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful day. Wind NW. Did not go to church. After lunch took a walk round by the Pier, the baths to the Itchen &amp; crossed the ferry to see PearTree Green. Returned to dinner</p>","pageId":936,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1377,"lock":null}
20:13:21.478 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.478 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1431
20:13:21.478 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1431,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful day. Wind NW. Did not go to church. After lunch took a walk round by the Pier, the baths to the Itchen &amp; crossed the ferry to see PearTree Green. Returned to dinner</p>","pageId":936,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1377,"lock":null}
20:13:21.478 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1432
20:13:21.478 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1432,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of delightful weather. Wind SW. Passed the morning in walking about, playing at billiards etc. Wrote to the Duke of Northumberland at court requesting him to grant me an interview &amp; complaining of my having been a second time passed for the purpose of Captains Loraiac &amp;  being placed over my head. Dined at Mr Lees</p>","pageId":936,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1378,"lock":null}
20:13:21.478 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.478 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1432
20:13:21.478 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1432,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of delightful weather. Wind SW. Passed the morning in walking about, playing at billiards etc. Wrote to the Duke of Northumberland at court requesting him to grant me an interview &amp; complaining of my having been a second time passed for the purpose of Captains Loraiac &amp;  being placed over my head. Dined at Mr Lees</p>","pageId":936,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1378,"lock":null}
20:13:21.478 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1433
20:13:21.478 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1433,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine day. Wind SW. Again engaged much the same as yesterday. Received a letter from Stephenson as which both Roads dated the 24<sup>th</sup> all well. The Lewis' &amp; Mr Carry dined with us. Major Falls of the 93<sup>rd</sup> &amp; Colonel Ogilvie came in the evening.</p>","pageId":936,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1379,"lock":null}
20:13:21.478 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.479 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1433
20:13:21.479 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1433,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine day. Wind SW. Again engaged much the same as yesterday. Received a letter from Stephenson as which both Roads dated the 24<sup>th</sup> all well. The Lewis' &amp; Mr Carry dined with us. Major Falls of the 93<sup>rd</sup> &amp; Colonel Ogilvie came in the evening.</p>","pageId":936,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1379,"lock":null}
20:13:21.479 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1434
20:13:21.479 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1434,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind SW. Bob Marsh left for London. Received an answer from the Duke referring me to Colonel Coulson. The Duke tied up with the gout &amp; not able to see me. Wrote to Stephenson, Major Falls, Colonel Ogilvie, William &amp; I went to Shirley to dine. Amused ourselves in rifle shooting</p>","pageId":936,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1380,"lock":null}
20:13:21.479 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.480 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1434
20:13:21.480 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1434,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind SW. Bob Marsh left for London. Received an answer from the Duke referring me to Colonel Coulson. The Duke tied up with the gout &amp; not able to see me. Wrote to Stephenson, Major Falls, Colonel Ogilvie, William &amp; I went to Shirley to dine. Amused ourselves in rifle shooting</p>","pageId":936,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1380,"lock":null}
20:13:21.480 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1435
20:13:21.480 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1435,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A miserable cold morning. Wind NE. rained continuously all day. After breakfast packed up my cloths &amp; spent the remainder of the day till dinner playing at billiards until Colonel Ogilvie, captain Lewis &amp; Harry RM. The former of whom with Major Falls dined with us.</p>","pageId":937,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1381,"lock":null}
20:13:21.480 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.480 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1435
20:13:21.480 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1435,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A miserable cold morning. Wind NE. rained continuously all day. After breakfast packed up my cloths &amp; spent the remainder of the day till dinner playing at billiards until Colonel Ogilvie, captain Lewis &amp; Harry RM. The former of whom with Major Falls dined with us.</p>","pageId":937,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1381,"lock":null}
20:13:21.480 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1436
20:13:21.480 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1436,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine clear morning. Wind NW but cool. After breakfasting with Mr Lee, got upon the Red Robin coach driven by Pearce at 10 o'clock &amp; started for Town where we arrived at &frac14; before 7 o'clock travelling a new &amp; by far the more beautiful road, over the Hog Back. Here we had a drenching shower of rain &amp; hail, through Guilford to town. Got to Nottingham Place at 7 o'clock. Had a cup of tea &amp; went to bed at 10 o'clock</p>","pageId":937,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1382,"lock":null}
20:13:21.480 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.481 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1436
20:13:21.481 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1436,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine clear morning. Wind NW but cool. After breakfasting with Mr Lee, got upon the Red Robin coach driven by Pearce at 10 o'clock &amp; started for Town where we arrived at &frac14; before 7 o'clock travelling a new &amp; by far the more beautiful road, over the Hog Back. Here we had a drenching shower of rain &amp; hail, through Guilford to town. Got to Nottingham Place at 7 o'clock. Had a cup of tea &amp; went to bed at 10 o'clock</p>","pageId":937,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1382,"lock":null}
20:13:21.481 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1437
20:13:21.481 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1437,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW. Walked into the city by Regents Street called at Oliphant's &amp; got a new hat. Passed along the Strand &amp; returned from the city &amp; dined with C Richmond at &frac12; past 5 o'clock</p>","pageId":937,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1383,"lock":null}
20:13:21.481 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
