20:13:21.481 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1438,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<figure>\r\n  <a href=\"https://www.google.co.uk/maps/@51.5191111,-0.1409154,3a,75y,36.87h,100.58t/data=!3m6!1e1!3m4!1sSt-OkhktadIXO3pMUDzlJw!2e0!7i16384!8i8192?hl=en\" >\r\n    <img src=\"images/img2798-crown-and-septre-london.png\" width=\"600px\" />\r\n    <figcaption>Crown and Septre, London</figcaption>\r\n  </a>\r\n</figure>","pageId":938,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":1384,"lock":null}
20:13:21.481 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1439
20:13:21.482 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1439,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":4,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind WSW. Breakfasted with C Richmond. He drove me in the afternoon around &amp; called upon Mrs Fletcher alias Hoffman then through the park by Pimlico &amp; Westminster to Greenwich. Called &amp; saw Geo<font color=#BFBFBF>rge</font> Watt and his wife, dined off whitebait etc. at the Crown &amp; Sceptre &amp; returned to town at 7 o'clock to tea. Got home in good time</p>","pageId":938,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1385,"lock":null}
20:13:21.482 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
