20:13:21.489 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1456,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":19,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... to the office. Received a short letter from Bess, very angry for not writing to her. Called at Harman's about the Hope's Wyburn bill which has been lagging at the docks agent for my acceptance. Wrote to Rob<font color=#BFBFBF>er</font><sup>t</sup> S<font color=#BFBFBF>tephenson</font> to send it up. Called at J Chapman. Took a cab &amp; drove direct to St James. Called at the Lord Chamberlains office. Saw Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Master</span> who was very polite &amp; introduced me as to how I am to act at the Levee. Left a card with him. Walked home &amp; wrote to Bess blowing her up for her saucy letter. Dined at home</p>","pageId":944,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1402,"lock":null}
20:13:21.489 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1457
20:13:21.490 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1457,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine autumnal morning. Wind WNW. Been a little rain in the night. Took an omnibus  into the city. At the offices. <del>Called upon Messrs Harman's statement they had sent the Hope's Wyburn bill to Shields for above</del>. Walked down to Miss Carr. Boswell gone down to Maldon this morning to the ship, which it appears, arrived there a fortnight ago, but he had not heard of it. Returned to the office &amp; WBS &amp; I walked out of the city together. Called at Bob Marsh's who afterwards joined is in Regents Street &amp; went to Nottingham Place to dinner</p>","pageId":944,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1403,"lock":null}
20:13:21.490 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.490 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1457
20:13:21.490 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1457,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine autumnal morning. Wind WNW. Been a little rain in the night. Took an omnibus  into the city. At the offices. <del>Called upon Messrs Harman's statement they had sent the Hope's Wyburn bill to Shields for above</del>. Walked down to Miss Carr. Boswell gone down to Maldon this morning to the ship, which it appears, arrived there a fortnight ago, but he had not heard of it. Returned to the office &amp; WBS &amp; I walked out of the city together. Called at Bob Marsh's who afterwards joined is in Regents Street &amp; went to Nottingham Place to dinner</p>","pageId":944,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1403,"lock":null}
20:13:21.490 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1458
20:13:21.490 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1458,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A rainy morning. Wind SSW very unfortunate, having to go to the Levee but hope it will clear up. WBS returned from the city at 1 o'clock. When I dressed myself in full fig &amp; drove in a hackney coach to St James Palace &amp; was presented to the King. The Levee was not numerously attended, being nearly all naval &amp; military ...</p>","pageId":944,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1404,"lock":null}
20:13:21.490 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.491 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1458
20:13:21.491 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1458,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A rainy morning. Wind SSW very unfortunate, having to go to the Levee but hope it will clear up. WBS returned from the city at 1 o'clock. When I dressed myself in full fig &amp; drove in a hackney coach to St James Palace &amp; was presented to the King. The Levee was not numerously attended, being nearly all naval &amp; military ...</p>","pageId":944,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1404,"lock":null}
20:13:21.491 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1459
20:13:21.491 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1459,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":21,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... decorated with all their orders, it was a very splendid &amp; magnificent sight. I thought I should have been very nervous, but was not at all so. I was nominally presented by the Earl of Beverley, but in fact by the Lord in waiting who was I believe was Lord ____  <font color=#BFBFBF>Earl of Gosford</font>   I had the honour of kissing the Kings hand. Lord Beverley found me out in the ante room &amp; was particularly polite &amp; attentive. After leaving the Levee, WBS &amp; Bob Marsh were waiting for me &amp; we walked along Pall Mall &amp; I got a coach &amp; drove home where I exchanged my dress &amp; returned to Richmond where I dined</p>","pageId":945,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1405,"lock":null}
20:13:21.491 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.491 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1459
20:13:21.491 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1459,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":21,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... decorated with all their orders, it was a very splendid &amp; magnificent sight. I thought I should have been very nervous, but was not at all so. I was nominally presented by the Earl of Beverley, but in fact by the Lord in waiting who was I believe was Lord ____  <font color=#BFBFBF>Earl of Gosford</font>   I had the honour of kissing the Kings hand. Lord Beverley found me out in the ante room &amp; was particularly polite &amp; attentive. After leaving the Levee, WBS &amp; Bob Marsh were waiting for me &amp; we walked along Pall Mall &amp; I got a coach &amp; drove home where I exchanged my dress &amp; returned to Richmond where I dined</p>","pageId":945,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1405,"lock":null}
20:13:21.491 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/146
20:13:21.491 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":146,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":5,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful and hot summers day. Received two letters from Mrs &amp; Miss Scott. The sale commenced &amp; good prices said to be obtained. Mr Vernon with his unreal kindness &amp; consideration asked a party to dine with us consisting of the two Careys, E Butler, Fishebourne, O'Connor &amp; Captain Ballesby. Spent a pleasant day.</p>","pageId":697,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":136,"lock":null}
20:13:21.491 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.492 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/146
20:13:21.492 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":146,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":5,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful and hot summers day. Received two letters from Mrs &amp; Miss Scott. The sale commenced &amp; good prices said to be obtained. Mr Vernon with his unreal kindness &amp; consideration asked a party to dine with us consisting of the two Careys, E Butler, Fishebourne, O'Connor &amp; Captain Ballesby. Spent a pleasant day.</p>","pageId":697,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":136,"lock":null}
