20:13:21.493 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1462,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":22,"sequence":3.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW. After breakfast WBS &amp; I went into the city &amp; at 11 o'clock embarked on board the Brocklebank steamer with an immense crowd of people &amp; preceded to Woolwich to see the <font color=#BFBFBF>HMS </font>Thunderer 74 a round ship launched. An immense concourse of people present. The King &amp; Queen arrived about 2 o'clock &amp; soon afterwards the Thunderer slid into the river in most beautiful style, the best launch I ever saw. Afterwards it was a grand &amp; imposing sight. Returned to town &amp; dined at the Blue Ports at 6 o'clock</p>","pageId":945,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1408,"lock":null}
20:13:21.493 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1463
20:13:21.493 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1463,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<style>\r\n#t01_18310923 {\r\n  border-collapse: collapse;\r\n}\r\n#t01_18310923 td:nth-child(3) {\r\n  text-align: right;\r\n}\r\n#t01_18310923 td:nth-child(4) {\r\n  text-align: right;\r\n}\r\n#t01_18310923 td:nth-child(5) {\r\n  text-align: right;\r\n}\r\n#c01_18310923 {\r\n  border-top: 1px solid black; \r\n  border-bottom: 1px solid black;\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n<p>A beautiful morning. Wind about W by S. After breakfast walked into the city. At the office, received a letter from Bess B &amp; one from Rob Stephenson by mistake, instead of Stephenson, Wyburn bill enclosing the merchant's bill and notes for the freight.</p>\r\n<table id=\"t01_18310923\">\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"width:50px\">viz.</br>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td style=\"width:400px\">A country Bank note cash</br>&emsp;&emsp;&emsp;Pbls at Musluman</td>\r\n    <td style=\"width:20px\">&pound;10</br>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td style=\"width:20px\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td style=\"width:15px\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td>Little & Co on Smith Payne etc</td>\r\n    <td>12</td>\r\n    <td>18</td>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td>S J Wright on Wheatley & Riots at due</td>\r\n    <td>21</td>\r\n    <td>13</td>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td>J Kin Ward & Co on Glyman</td>\r\n    <td>35</td>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td>Bill Garbalt to JRS on Wades 2nd half payment</td>\r\n    <td>199</td>\r\n    <td>10</td>\r\n    <td>9</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td id=\"c01_18310923\" >279</td>\r\n    <td id=\"c01_18310923\" >1</td>\r\n    <td id=\"c01_18310923\" >9</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>Paid <span class=highlight_yellow>Kitchenmein</span> for repairing fishing rods &pound;1.0.6.</p>\r\n<p>Met H Harry &amp; walked with him down to the Catherine docks to see Hy Nicholson who we found on board &amp; had a lunch with him. His ship out <span class=highlight_yellow>exupting</span> lathwood. He expects to get away about Wednesday &amp; offered me a passage which I think I shall accept. Saw Messrs Harrison &amp; explained Rolt's mistake in sending the freight bill instead of the Wyburn bill. Wrote to Bess. Walked back to Nottingham Place to dinner. Met WBS &amp; Bob Marsh in Regent Street. The latter dined with us.</p>","pageId":946,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1409,"lock":null}
20:13:21.493 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.493 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1463
20:13:21.493 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1463,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<style>\r\n#t01_18310923 {\r\n  border-collapse: collapse;\r\n}\r\n#t01_18310923 td:nth-child(3) {\r\n  text-align: right;\r\n}\r\n#t01_18310923 td:nth-child(4) {\r\n  text-align: right;\r\n}\r\n#t01_18310923 td:nth-child(5) {\r\n  text-align: right;\r\n}\r\n#c01_18310923 {\r\n  border-top: 1px solid black; \r\n  border-bottom: 1px solid black;\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n<p>A beautiful morning. Wind about W by S. After breakfast walked into the city. At the office, received a letter from Bess B &amp; one from Rob Stephenson by mistake, instead of Stephenson, Wyburn bill enclosing the merchant's bill and notes for the freight.</p>\r\n<table id=\"t01_18310923\">\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"width:50px\">viz.</br>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td style=\"width:400px\">A country Bank note cash</br>&emsp;&emsp;&emsp;Pbls at Musluman</td>\r\n    <td style=\"width:20px\">&pound;10</br>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td style=\"width:20px\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td style=\"width:15px\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td>Little & Co on Smith Payne etc</td>\r\n    <td>12</td>\r\n    <td>18</td>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td>S J Wright on Wheatley & Riots at due</td>\r\n    <td>21</td>\r\n    <td>13</td>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td>J Kin Ward & Co on Glyman</td>\r\n    <td>35</td>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td>Bill Garbalt to JRS on Wades 2nd half payment</td>\r\n    <td>199</td>\r\n    <td>10</td>\r\n    <td>9</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td id=\"c01_18310923\" >279</td>\r\n    <td id=\"c01_18310923\" >1</td>\r\n    <td id=\"c01_18310923\" >9</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>Paid <span class=highlight_yellow>Kitchenmein</span> for repairing fishing rods &pound;1.0.6.</p>\r\n<p>Met H Harry &amp; walked with him down to the Catherine docks to see Hy Nicholson who we found on board &amp; had a lunch with him. His ship out <span class=highlight_yellow>exupting</span> lathwood. He expects to get away about Wednesday &amp; offered me a passage which I think I shall accept. Saw Messrs Harrison &amp; explained Rolt's mistake in sending the freight bill instead of the Wyburn bill. Wrote to Bess. Walked back to Nottingham Place to dinner. Met WBS &amp; Bob Marsh in Regent Street. The latter dined with us.</p>","pageId":946,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1409,"lock":null}
20:13:21.493 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1464
20:13:21.493 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1464,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine morning. Wind WSW. H<sup>y</sup> Harry called upon me about 12 o'clock. After lunch we went to the Baker Street Bazaar to look for a gig for Sadler, but did not purchase. Got into a cab in Oxford Street &amp; drove to the Pantechnicon  in Belgrave square, a very splendid large building lately erected for the sale of Carriages etc. etc. An immense number of vehicles of all sorts. One of which a new dennilt we brought for Sadler for &pound;30, a very cheap bargain all that it will want will be two or three coats of varnish in a few months. Returned to Nottingham Place to dinner. H Harry left us a little after 8 o'clock in an omnibus.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>I took suddenly unwell &amp; at bed time took a couple of camomile pills.</p>","pageId":946,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1410,"lock":null}
20:13:21.493 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.494 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1464
20:13:21.494 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1464,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine morning. Wind WSW. H<sup>y</sup> Harry called upon me about 12 o'clock. After lunch we went to the Baker Street Bazaar to look for a gig for Sadler, but did not purchase. Got into a cab in Oxford Street &amp; drove to the Pantechnicon  in Belgrave square, a very splendid large building lately erected for the sale of Carriages etc. etc. An immense number of vehicles of all sorts. One of which a new dennilt we brought for Sadler for &pound;30, a very cheap bargain all that it will want will be two or three coats of varnish in a few months. Returned to Nottingham Place to dinner. H Harry left us a little after 8 o'clock in an omnibus.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>I took suddenly unwell &amp; at bed time took a couple of camomile pills.</p>","pageId":946,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1410,"lock":null}
20:13:21.494 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1465
20:13:21.494 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1465,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of beautiful weather. Wind SW. Swallowed a black draught before breakfast which, with the pills, have had the desired effect.</p>\r\n<p>Did not move out until near 3 o'clock. Then took a walk to the Zoological Gardens &amp; thence to Hyde Park &amp; home to dinner, where I found Richmond had come to feed with us</p>","pageId":947,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1411,"lock":null}
20:13:21.494 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.494 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1465
20:13:21.494 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1465,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of beautiful weather. Wind SW. Swallowed a black draught before breakfast which, with the pills, have had the desired effect.</p>\r\n<p>Did not move out until near 3 o'clock. Then took a walk to the Zoological Gardens &amp; thence to Hyde Park &amp; home to dinner, where I found Richmond had come to feed with us</p>","pageId":947,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1411,"lock":null}
20:13:21.494 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1466
20:13:21.494 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1466,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning having been a little rain. Wind difficult to make out, appears to have got from the east. Took an omnibus <span class=highlight_yellow>to</span> the city. Called at the office. The Hope sailed from Shields on Friday. Walked down to Whitechapel to Stirling's the chemists for a bottle of the essence of cubebs. Thence to the St Catherine docks &amp; dined with H Nicholson on board the Crises, H<font color=#BFBFBF>enr</font><sup>y</sup><sup> </sup>&amp; Sam Hurry there. Left the docks at 6 o'clock &amp; walked to Nottingham Place.</p>\r\n<p>WBS received  letter from Colonel <span class=highlight_yellow>Farwole</span></p>","pageId":947,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1412,"lock":null}
20:13:21.494 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.494 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1466
20:13:21.495 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1466,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning having been a little rain. Wind difficult to make out, appears to have got from the east. Took an omnibus <span class=highlight_yellow>to</span> the city. Called at the office. The Hope sailed from Shields on Friday. Walked down to Whitechapel to Stirling's the chemists for a bottle of the essence of cubebs. Thence to the St Catherine docks &amp; dined with H Nicholson on board the Crises, H<font color=#BFBFBF>enr</font><sup>y</sup><sup> </sup>&amp; Sam Hurry there. Left the docks at 6 o'clock &amp; walked to Nottingham Place.</p>\r\n<p>WBS received  letter from Colonel <span class=highlight_yellow>Farwole</span></p>","pageId":947,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1412,"lock":null}
20:13:21.495 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1467
20:13:21.495 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1467,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull damp morning. Wind SE. Did not go out till late. Walked down by Regents Street &amp; called at Richmond's, thence to the Temple &amp; left my card at <span class=highlight_yellow>wwards</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>chainpers</span>,. Returned to Regent Street at 6 o'clock with Richmond. G Taylor, Bob Marsh, WBS &amp; self there</p>","pageId":947,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1413,"lock":null}
20:13:21.495 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.495 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1467
20:13:21.495 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1467,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull damp morning. Wind SE. Did not go out till late. Walked down by Regents Street &amp; called at Richmond's, thence to the Temple &amp; left my card at <span class=highlight_yellow>wwards</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>chainpers</span>,. Returned to Regent Street at 6 o'clock with Richmond. G Taylor, Bob Marsh, WBS &amp; self there</p>","pageId":947,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1413,"lock":null}
20:13:21.495 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1468
20:13:21.495 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1468,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Been some rain this morning. Rather dull &amp; excessively close &amp; sultry. Wind for the ESE. Took an omnibus into the city. Called at the office. Accepted Stephenson's Wy<font color=#BFBFBF>n</font>berg bill for &pound;44.5/- due 8 Nov payable with WBS &amp; left it at Messrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Halmgons</span>. Went down to the St Catherine dock &amp; dined on board the Crisis. Tea at <span class=highlight_yellow>Lodlins</span>. A heavy fall of rain with lightning at night.</p>","pageId":947,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1414,"lock":null}
20:13:21.495 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.495 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1468
20:13:21.495 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1468,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Been some rain this morning. Rather dull &amp; excessively close &amp; sultry. Wind for the ESE. Took an omnibus into the city. Called at the office. Accepted Stephenson's Wy<font color=#BFBFBF>n</font>berg bill for &pound;44.5/- due 8 Nov payable with WBS &amp; left it at Messrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Halmgons</span>. Went down to the St Catherine dock &amp; dined on board the Crisis. Tea at <span class=highlight_yellow>Lodlins</span>. A heavy fall of rain with lightning at night.</p>","pageId":947,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1414,"lock":null}
20:13:21.495 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1469
20:13:21.495 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1469,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; cooler weather after heavy rain last night. Wind SE. Sat in the house until after 1 o'clock. Called &amp; had a lunch at Miles Forsters offices in Wimpole Street &amp; sat some time with him. Walked in Regent Street till dinner time. Richmond dined with us</p>","pageId":948,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1415,"lock":null}
20:13:21.495 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.496 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1469
20:13:21.496 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1469,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; cooler weather after heavy rain last night. Wind SE. Sat in the house until after 1 o'clock. Called &amp; had a lunch at Miles Forsters offices in Wimpole Street &amp; sat some time with him. Walked in Regent Street till dinner time. Richmond dined with us</p>","pageId":948,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1415,"lock":null}
20:13:21.496 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/147
20:13:21.496 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":147,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":5,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. The sale still going on. Wrote to Mr I Robert about a chain cable for the Hope. Dined early. John &amp; I took a long walk to fish but had no sport</p>","pageId":697,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":137,"lock":null}
20:13:21.496 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.496 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/147
20:13:21.496 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":147,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":5,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. The sale still going on. Wrote to Mr I Robert about a chain cable for the Hope. Dined early. John &amp; I took a long walk to fish but had no sport</p>","pageId":697,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":137,"lock":null}
20:13:21.496 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1470
20:13:21.496 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1470,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>The early part of the morning dull &amp; thick, afterwards cleared away &amp; turned out a fine day. Wind SSE. Got all my luggage into a Hackney coach &amp; down to Philpot lane (there saw Stephenson, the Hope being at Greenwich <del>got up to stone stairs</del>) down on St Catherine dock &amp; the Crises having got out, I <span class=highlight_yellow>proceeded</span> &amp; left all my luggage at Lodlings. Walked up again to Phillpotts Lane, accompanied WBS to Guildhall and having got a Beef Steak at Jewps on WBS, Lee &amp; I walked down to Mr Carr's &amp; drank tea. Called at Codlings &amp; saw H Nicholson who had got the ship down to Duke Shore &amp; expecting to get away in the morning. I determined to accept Mr Carr's offer of a bed. Set WBS part of the way up the Commercial Road. Returned with Nicholson to Lodlings &amp; got to Mr Carr's a little after 10 o'clock. Rained very heavy with a great deal of lightning. Part of the Hope sold today.</p>","pageId":948,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1416,"lock":null}
20:13:21.496 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.497 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1470
20:13:21.497 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1470,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>The early part of the morning dull &amp; thick, afterwards cleared away &amp; turned out a fine day. Wind SSE. Got all my luggage into a Hackney coach &amp; down to Philpot lane (there saw Stephenson, the Hope being at Greenwich <del>got up to stone stairs</del>) down on St Catherine dock &amp; the Crises having got out, I <span class=highlight_yellow>proceeded</span> &amp; left all my luggage at Lodlings. Walked up again to Phillpotts Lane, accompanied WBS to Guildhall and having got a Beef Steak at Jewps on WBS, Lee &amp; I walked down to Mr Carr's &amp; drank tea. Called at Codlings &amp; saw H Nicholson who had got the ship down to Duke Shore &amp; expecting to get away in the morning. I determined to accept Mr Carr's offer of a bed. Set WBS part of the way up the Commercial Road. Returned with Nicholson to Lodlings &amp; got to Mr Carr's a little after 10 o'clock. Rained very heavy with a great deal of lightning. Part of the Hope sold today.</p>","pageId":948,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1416,"lock":null}
20:13:21.497 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1471
20:13:21.497 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1471,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning after a very heavy fall of rain during the night. Wind SSW. Afterwards changeable between <span class=highlight_yellow>N</span> &amp; S by E. After breakfast went to Codlings, Stephenson met me there &amp; we got all my luggage on board the Crisis &amp; about 12 o'clock having got all her ballast in, she weighed anchor &amp; dropped down to Greenwich where we were enabled to sail down the reach &amp; we got to Woolwich between 2 &amp; 3 o'clock. The tide here low we took the ground &amp; there remained until 10 o'clock at which time I had gone to bed but the ship got under way &amp; beat down to earth &amp; brought up between 1 &amp; 2 o'clock in the morning</p>","pageId":949,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1417,"lock":null}
20:13:21.497 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.497 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1471
20:13:21.497 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1471,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning after a very heavy fall of rain during the night. Wind SSW. Afterwards changeable between <span class=highlight_yellow>N</span> &amp; S by E. After breakfast went to Codlings, Stephenson met me there &amp; we got all my luggage on board the Crisis &amp; about 12 o'clock having got all her ballast in, she weighed anchor &amp; dropped down to Greenwich where we were enabled to sail down the reach &amp; we got to Woolwich between 2 &amp; 3 o'clock. The tide here low we took the ground &amp; there remained until 10 o'clock at which time I had gone to bed but the ship got under way &amp; beat down to earth &amp; brought up between 1 &amp; 2 o'clock in the morning</p>","pageId":949,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1417,"lock":null}
20:13:21.497 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1472
20:13:21.497 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1472,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At anchor off Erith. A cloudy morning with showers. Wind fresh from SSW after washing the decks &amp; trimming ballast, the ship having been by the stern, we got under way at about 11 o'clock &amp; beat down to the <span class=highlight_yellow>home</span> light where we brought up at 6 o'clock. The wind having changed during the day to S by W: S: &amp; S by E blowing fresh. Turned after a glass of grog between 8 &amp; 9 o'clock</p>","pageId":949,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1418,"lock":null}
20:13:21.497 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.498 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1472
20:13:21.498 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1472,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At anchor off Erith. A cloudy morning with showers. Wind fresh from SSW after washing the decks &amp; trimming ballast, the ship having been by the stern, we got under way at about 11 o'clock &amp; beat down to the <span class=highlight_yellow>home</span> light where we brought up at 6 o'clock. The wind having changed during the day to S by W: S: &amp; S by E blowing fresh. Turned after a glass of grog between 8 &amp; 9 o'clock</p>","pageId":949,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1418,"lock":null}
20:13:21.498 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1473
20:13:21.498 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1473,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned the hands up about 5 o'clock being low water &amp; the wind at SSW I got up before 6 o'clock. The people busy getting the anchor &amp; setting sails. Had a fine run during the day down <span class=highlight_yellow>swin</span>, studding sails set but not much wind which varied between <span class=highlight_yellow>SE</span> &amp; S by W. At &frac12; past 8 o'clock at night off Aldeburgh &amp; beautiful clear weather but a strong flood tide against us. Turned in about 9 o'clock</p>","pageId":949,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1419,"lock":null}
20:13:21.498 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.498 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1473
20:13:21.498 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1473,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned the hands up about 5 o'clock being low water &amp; the wind at SSW I got up before 6 o'clock. The people busy getting the anchor &amp; setting sails. Had a fine run during the day down <span class=highlight_yellow>swin</span>, studding sails set but not much wind which varied between <span class=highlight_yellow>SE</span> &amp; S by W. At &frac12; past 8 o'clock at night off Aldeburgh &amp; beautiful clear weather but a strong flood tide against us. Turned in about 9 o'clock</p>","pageId":949,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1419,"lock":null}
20:13:21.498 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1474
20:13:21.498 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1474,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at 12 o'clock am. The ship then running with a fresh breeze at SW for the <span class=highlight_yellow>Newrope</span> light which we passed about 1 o'clock &amp; ran through Hasbrough Gateway. Turned into my crib again before 2 o'clock I awoke or rather disturbed at 5 o'clock by a tremendous squall at SW a little to the south w of Cromer with heavy rise. It took us suddenly &amp; without any warning &amp; therefore with all sails standing that they had great difficulty in taking them in. However they succeeded at last in taking them without losing anything, which considering the violence of the squall was fortunate. When they had double reefed the topsails &amp; made all snug I again went to bed. Got up at 8 o'clock still blowing hard from the WSW. We were then abreast of the Dadgrow floating light. It continued to blow fresh all the morning varying between WSW &amp; W by N. After dinner Nicholson &amp; I turned in &amp; had a good snooze until &frac12; past 4 o'clock where we found Flamborough in sight distant probably about 15 miles. Wind &amp; sea very much fallen, but still a fine light breeze from about WSW. All reefs out, top gallant <del>sails set</del> &amp; fore topmast studding sails set. Passed Flamborough Head at 8 o'clock, a most beautiful night. At 9 o'clock we had a glass of grog &amp; I afterwards walked the deck with Nicholson till 12 o'clock when we turned in.</p>","pageId":950,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1420,"lock":null}
20:13:21.498 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.498 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1474
20:13:21.498 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1474,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at 12 o'clock am. The ship then running with a fresh breeze at SW for the <span class=highlight_yellow>Newrope</span> light which we passed about 1 o'clock &amp; ran through Hasbrough Gateway. Turned into my crib again before 2 o'clock I awoke or rather disturbed at 5 o'clock by a tremendous squall at SW a little to the south w of Cromer with heavy rise. It took us suddenly &amp; without any warning &amp; therefore with all sails standing that they had great difficulty in taking them in. However they succeeded at last in taking them without losing anything, which considering the violence of the squall was fortunate. When they had double reefed the topsails &amp; made all snug I again went to bed. Got up at 8 o'clock still blowing hard from the WSW. We were then abreast of the Dadgrow floating light. It continued to blow fresh all the morning varying between WSW &amp; W by N. After dinner Nicholson &amp; I turned in &amp; had a good snooze until &frac12; past 4 o'clock where we found Flamborough in sight distant probably about 15 miles. Wind &amp; sea very much fallen, but still a fine light breeze from about WSW. All reefs out, top gallant <del>sails set</del> &amp; fore topmast studding sails set. Passed Flamborough Head at 8 o'clock, a most beautiful night. At 9 o'clock we had a glass of grog &amp; I afterwards walked the deck with Nicholson till 12 o'clock when we turned in.</p>","pageId":950,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1420,"lock":null}
20:13:21.498 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1475
20:13:21.498 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1475,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>We were disturbed again this morning at about 3 o'clock by a heavy squall with rain from the SSW which increased. I &amp; Nicholson immediately turned out, the ship being off the Tees by the time we got upon deck, they had got the top sail &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>missen</span> stowed &amp; top sail reefed,  <span class=highlight_yellow>lay</span> the ship too soon afterwards left with the head to the land, between Seaham &amp; Hartlepool, the squall gradually subsided &amp; at day light 5 o'clock fine weather again. Ran the ship in for the land &amp; between 7 &amp; 8 o'clock got a piolet on board. Lay off the harbour until the tide flowed sufficiently for us to run the bar, which we did at 11 o'clock, working up to the narrows &amp; then dropping up to the <span class=highlight_yellow>Lenickeln</span> shore where I landed &amp; came home. Robert got my things on shore.</p>\r\n<p>I dined with J Tinley &amp; in the evening called &amp; saw Bess, got home before 11 o'clock</p>","pageId":951,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1421,"lock":null}
20:13:21.498 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.499 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1475
20:13:21.499 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1475,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>We were disturbed again this morning at about 3 o'clock by a heavy squall with rain from the SSW which increased. I &amp; Nicholson immediately turned out, the ship being off the Tees by the time we got upon deck, they had got the top sail &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>missen</span> stowed &amp; top sail reefed,  <span class=highlight_yellow>lay</span> the ship too soon afterwards left with the head to the land, between Seaham &amp; Hartlepool, the squall gradually subsided &amp; at day light 5 o'clock fine weather again. Ran the ship in for the land &amp; between 7 &amp; 8 o'clock got a piolet on board. Lay off the harbour until the tide flowed sufficiently for us to run the bar, which we did at 11 o'clock, working up to the narrows &amp; then dropping up to the <span class=highlight_yellow>Lenickeln</span> shore where I landed &amp; came home. Robert got my things on shore.</p>\r\n<p>I dined with J Tinley &amp; in the evening called &amp; saw Bess, got home before 11 o'clock</p>","pageId":951,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1421,"lock":null}
20:13:21.499 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1476
20:13:21.499 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1476,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp morning having been a great deal of rain at an early hour, blowing fresh at SSW. Paid Robert. Borrowed of him &pound;3 for child 8 weeks &pound;1.16 &amp; settled his book in passages etc. &pound;3.5.3</p>\r\n<p>Dined at the Northumberland Alms being the Dukes court day, the <span class=highlight_yellow>cooks on recorder</span> of Newcastle <span class=highlight_yellow>proceeded</span> there for the first time. At the <span class=highlight_yellow>nefs</span> room ...</p>","pageId":951,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1422,"lock":null}
20:13:21.499 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.499 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1476
20:13:21.499 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1476,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp morning having been a great deal of rain at an early hour, blowing fresh at SSW. Paid Robert. Borrowed of him &pound;3 for child 8 weeks &pound;1.16 &amp; settled his book in passages etc. &pound;3.5.3</p>\r\n<p>Dined at the Northumberland Alms being the Dukes court day, the <span class=highlight_yellow>cooks on recorder</span> of Newcastle <span class=highlight_yellow>proceeded</span> there for the first time. At the <span class=highlight_yellow>nefs</span> room ...</p>","pageId":951,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1422,"lock":null}
20:13:21.499 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1477
20:13:21.499 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1477,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but still blowing hard from the SSW. Several light ships got down &amp; must have had a good run. Lockwood &amp; I walked round by Tynemouth. H Nicholson &amp; Mark dined with me at 3 o'clock. In the evening attended <span class=highlight_yellow>Aldertons</span> Committee room &amp; afterwards with Bess</p>","pageId":952,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1423,"lock":null}
20:13:21.499 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.499 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1477
20:13:21.499 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1477,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but still blowing hard from the SSW. Several light ships got down &amp; must have had a good run. Lockwood &amp; I walked round by Tynemouth. H Nicholson &amp; Mark dined with me at 3 o'clock. In the evening attended <span class=highlight_yellow>Aldertons</span> Committee room &amp; afterwards with Bess</p>","pageId":952,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1423,"lock":null}
20:13:21.499 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1478
20:13:21.500 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1478,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind SW &amp; still looks like more rain. Walked to Preston to see Moor's brother who had not come down. Dined on board the Crisis with A Nicholson. In the evening we walked to Tynemouth at night with Bess</p>","pageId":952,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1424,"lock":null}
20:13:21.500 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.500 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1478
20:13:21.500 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1478,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind SW &amp; still looks like more rain. Walked to Preston to see Moor's brother who had not come down. Dined on board the Crisis with A Nicholson. In the evening we walked to Tynemouth at night with Bess</p>","pageId":952,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1424,"lock":null}
20:13:21.500 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1479
20:13:21.500 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1479,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather. Wind during the day varying between SE &amp; SE. At church in the morning. Saw Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Spencer</span> yesterday who agreed to renew our bill upon our rubbing off &pound;100 or &pound;150. Wrote to WBS. Dined at home. Walked to Tynemouth in the afternoon. Called at Cunningham's Dr Drury there &amp; had some excellent glenlivet with them. Called afterwards at the castle, sat with the Marines &amp; at night again with Bess</p>","pageId":952,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1425,"lock":null}
20:13:21.500 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.500 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1479
20:13:21.500 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1479,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather. Wind during the day varying between SE &amp; SE. At church in the morning. Saw Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Spencer</span> yesterday who agreed to renew our bill upon our rubbing off &pound;100 or &pound;150. Wrote to WBS. Dined at home. Walked to Tynemouth in the afternoon. Called at Cunningham's Dr Drury there &amp; had some excellent glenlivet with them. Called afterwards at the castle, sat with the Marines &amp; at night again with Bess</p>","pageId":952,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1425,"lock":null}
20:13:21.500 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/148
20:13:21.500 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":148,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":5,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Rather a dull morning. Vernon &amp; I left Carlow by coach. Found it afterwards extremely hot &amp; dusty. Got to Dublin at 5 o'clock &amp; dined with Sir C Vernon. Put up at Mackens Hotel</p>","pageId":697,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":138,"lock":null}
20:13:21.500 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.501 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/148
20:13:21.501 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":148,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":5,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Rather a dull morning. Vernon &amp; I left Carlow by coach. Found it afterwards extremely hot &amp; dusty. Got to Dublin at 5 o'clock &amp; dined with Sir C Vernon. Put up at Mackens Hotel</p>","pageId":697,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":138,"lock":null}
20:13:21.501 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1480
20:13:21.501 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1480,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A letter from WBS</p>\r\n<p>A mild morning. Wind SW. A party of us went to Cullercoat Sands &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>found</span> ourselves at Rifle &amp; Pistol shooting at a target. Lunched at the castle &amp; at 4 o'clock dined with J Redhead &amp; Lockwood at the lodgings. I sent them a pair of soles. At night with Bess</p>\r\n<p>This days papers brought an account of the Reform Bill being thrown out of the Lords by a majority of 41. The debate did not conclude till &frac12; past 6 in the morning. Much excitement in London.</p>\r\n<p>A rainy afternoon &amp; night</p>","pageId":953,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1426,"lock":null}
20:13:21.501 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.501 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1480
20:13:21.501 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1480,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A letter from WBS</p>\r\n<p>A mild morning. Wind SW. A party of us went to Cullercoat Sands &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>found</span> ourselves at Rifle &amp; Pistol shooting at a target. Lunched at the castle &amp; at 4 o'clock dined with J Redhead &amp; Lockwood at the lodgings. I sent them a pair of soles. At night with Bess</p>\r\n<p>This days papers brought an account of the Reform Bill being thrown out of the Lords by a majority of 41. The debate did not conclude till &frac12; past 6 in the morning. Much excitement in London.</p>\r\n<p>A rainy afternoon &amp; night</p>","pageId":953,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1426,"lock":null}
20:13:21.501 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1481
20:13:21.501 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1481,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind W by S. Dined with H Nicholson on board the Crisis. J Wight, J Redhead &amp; Lockwood there. With Bess at night</p>","pageId":953,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1427,"lock":null}
20:13:21.501 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.501 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1481
20:13:21.501 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1481,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind W by S. Dined with H Nicholson on board the Crisis. J Wight, J Redhead &amp; Lockwood there. With Bess at night</p>","pageId":953,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1427,"lock":null}
20:13:21.501 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1482
20:13:21.501 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1482,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather. Wind WSW. Went up in a gig to Newcastle. Called &amp; saw Emma Galbraith who was looking well. Payed Mrs Noakes for Emma G's board and education up to June &pound;39.10/-. Afterwards walked out to Benton where I dined &amp; stayed all night. Dixon Clark there, he slept in Newcastle to take the coach in the morning for Oxford. Tom Smith left them in the morning for Togston</p>","pageId":953,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1428,"lock":null}
20:13:21.501 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.502 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1482
20:13:21.502 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1482,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather. Wind WSW. Went up in a gig to Newcastle. Called &amp; saw Emma Galbraith who was looking well. Payed Mrs Noakes for Emma G's board and education up to June &pound;39.10/-. Afterwards walked out to Benton where I dined &amp; stayed all night. Dixon Clark there, he slept in Newcastle to take the coach in the morning for Oxford. Tom Smith left them in the morning for Togston</p>","pageId":953,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1428,"lock":null}
20:13:21.502 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1483
20:13:21.502 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1483,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Beautiful mild weather. Wind in the morning SW. Changed in the afternoon to SSE. Left Benton directly after breakfast &amp; walked out to Newcastle to meet Stephenson who arrived yesterday, fixed the hope to load Bell &amp; Dixons Walls, but won't get coals for upwards of a fortnight. Took the steamer to Shields.</p>\r\n<p>Found a letter from WBS with the Hopes freight account but no note, brokers commission being changed which WBS thought an error. Paid an average Eligible Club &pound;14.9.3 &amp; gave Stephenson &pound;20 to pay wages. Dined at home at 5 o'clock. At the whist club in the evening &amp; with Bess at night. A rainy &amp; blowing night</p>","pageId":954,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1429,"lock":null}
20:13:21.502 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.503 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1483
20:13:21.503 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1483,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Beautiful mild weather. Wind in the morning SW. Changed in the afternoon to SSE. Left Benton directly after breakfast &amp; walked out to Newcastle to meet Stephenson who arrived yesterday, fixed the hope to load Bell &amp; Dixons Walls, but won't get coals for upwards of a fortnight. Took the steamer to Shields.</p>\r\n<p>Found a letter from WBS with the Hopes freight account but no note, brokers commission being changed which WBS thought an error. Paid an average Eligible Club &pound;14.9.3 &amp; gave Stephenson &pound;20 to pay wages. Dined at home at 5 o'clock. At the whist club in the evening &amp; with Bess at night. A rainy &amp; blowing night</p>","pageId":954,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1429,"lock":null}
20:13:21.503 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1484
20:13:21.503 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1484,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but blowing hard from the SW. Gave Robert a draft on executors account for &frac12; years taxes &pound;9.5.2. Paid &pound;20 in executors account from my own. Money advanced me by WBS. Walked out &amp; called on Mr Robson. High Cheston. Dined at home at 5 o'clock &amp; with Bess at night.</p>","pageId":954,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1430,"lock":null}
20:13:21.503 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.503 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1484
20:13:21.503 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1484,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but blowing hard from the SW. Gave Robert a draft on executors account for &frac12; years taxes &pound;9.5.2. Paid &pound;20 in executors account from my own. Money advanced me by WBS. Walked out &amp; called on Mr Robson. High Cheston. Dined at home at 5 o'clock &amp; with Bess at night.</p>","pageId":954,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1430,"lock":null}
20:13:21.503 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1485
20:13:21.503 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1485,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather. Wind SW. Afterwards WNW. Went to Newcastle by steamer, called at Chapmans about their &pound;300 bill which they had negotiated upwards of a month ago. Returned by steam. Wrote to WBS. Dined with H Nicholson &amp; with Bess at night</p>","pageId":954,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1431,"lock":null}
20:13:21.503 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
