20:13:21.568 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1613,"version":0,"year":1832,"month":2,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Beautiful weather. Rather frosty. Wind NW. Walked up to <span class=highlight_yellow>Jkcuth</span> dock &amp; dined on board the <span class=highlight_yellow>Crides</span> with H Nicholson. At the theatre at night.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Got &pound;43.10/ of Cs &amp; co on executors account to pay E Galbraith's <span class=highlight_yellow>Buaisd</span> &amp; tomorrow</p>","pageId":987,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1557,"lock":null}
20:13:21.568 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1614
20:13:21.568 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1614,"version":0,"year":1832,"month":2,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; sharp frost. Wind WNW. Breakfasted with Tinley. John drove me up to Newcastle &amp; back again to dinner with him at 5 o'clock. Charles Mallory came &amp; attended the whist club at Goslings in the evening. With Bess at night.</p>","pageId":987,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1558,"lock":null}
