20:13:21.596 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1668,"version":0,"year":1832,"month":4,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold morning. Wind NE. Mr Bird breakfasted with me &amp; came back for dinner. I signed a charter for S<sup>t</sup> Andrew &amp; sent it to WBS.</p>\r\n<p>Benton agricultural show. Dined with Charlton at Boggins. Did not go. Received a charter from the tees Co but refused it. At Bess</p>","pageId":995,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1612,"lock":null}
20:13:21.596 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1669
20:13:21.596 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1669,"version":0,"year":1832,"month":4,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another cold day. Wind ENE. Gully called &amp; lunched. Drury &amp; Charlton dined with me on board the Hope. Called at Harrisons. With Bess at night. Received a letter from WBS</p>","pageId":995,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1613,"lock":null}
20:13:21.596 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.596 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1669
20:13:21.596 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1669,"version":0,"year":1832,"month":4,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another cold day. Wind ENE. Gully called &amp; lunched. Drury &amp; Charlton dined with me on board the Hope. Called at Harrisons. With Bess at night. Received a letter from WBS</p>","pageId":995,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1613,"lock":null}
20:13:21.596 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/167
20:13:21.596 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":167,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Left Carlos at &frac12; past 7 o'clock in a car &amp; went to Athy to breakfast in 1 &frac12; hours being 11 &frac12; miles. Saw Captain Pope respecting the property there, but could learn nothing satisfactory. He said it was a divided property. His father having 2/3 one of which he sold &amp; the other 1/3 was the Galbraeths &amp; to prove it was a divided property he said the Galbraiths had granted a lease of their part consisting of an old house now in ruins &amp; a tanyard in the rear. He further said that the original lease had somehow or other got out of his hands, but that I could see it at Mr Warrens, Jarvis Street Dublin. That he would be glad to give me every information &amp; assistance &amp; allow me to see all papers that are in his possession. Returned to Carlow in the afternoon. Dined alone. Mr Vernon having gone to Coopers Hill &amp; went to a pleasant quadrille party at Mrs Whilliam Fishbourn. We kept it up until 3 o'clock</p>","pageId":699,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":157,"lock":null}
20:13:21.596 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.597 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/167
20:13:21.597 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":167,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Left Carlos at &frac12; past 7 o'clock in a car &amp; went to Athy to breakfast in 1 &frac12; hours being 11 &frac12; miles. Saw Captain Pope respecting the property there, but could learn nothing satisfactory. He said it was a divided property. His father having 2/3 one of which he sold &amp; the other 1/3 was the Galbraeths &amp; to prove it was a divided property he said the Galbraiths had granted a lease of their part consisting of an old house now in ruins &amp; a tanyard in the rear. He further said that the original lease had somehow or other got out of his hands, but that I could see it at Mr Warrens, Jarvis Street Dublin. That he would be glad to give me every information &amp; assistance &amp; allow me to see all papers that are in his possession. Returned to Carlow in the afternoon. Dined alone. Mr Vernon having gone to Coopers Hill &amp; went to a pleasant quadrille party at Mrs Whilliam Fishbourn. We kept it up until 3 o'clock</p>","pageId":699,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":157,"lock":null}
20:13:21.597 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1670
20:13:21.597 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1670,"version":0,"year":1832,"month":4,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Not quite <span class=highlight_yellow>cold</span>. Wind E. Wrote to WBS. Dined at home. Spent the afternoon playing at gravitas with Bradshaw, also spent the evening there</p>","pageId":995,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1614,"lock":null}
20:13:21.597 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
