20:13:21.601 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1679,"version":0,"year":1832,"month":4,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Blowing hard from the SW. Went by steam to Newcastle &amp; fixed the Hope to take coals out to <span class=highlight_yellow>Swinemsend</span> at &pound;6.6 per keel. Returned home to dinner &amp; afterwards went to Tynemouth races which were very bad. Turned out a wet day &amp; spoiled the sport.  At Bess at night</p>","pageId":997,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1623,"lock":null}
20:13:21.601 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/168
20:13:21.601 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":168,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet day. Quite a deluge of rain. Confined to the house all the morning by the wet. Engaged in covrtey for wrote a letter to Mr Buther of Athy. Asking to whom he pays rent for the tanyard. Dined at home with Mr Vernon</p>","pageId":699,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":158,"lock":null}
