20:13:21.698 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1878,"version":0,"year":1832,"month":11,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine frosty morning. Wind WSW. Tom Smith left me. Went over the water &amp; got a parcel for the <span class=highlight_yellow>Hg Wright</span> &amp; paid averages Hope Club, Robert &pound;2.7.2 Mr Clay &pound; 7.7.4 = &pound; 14.14.6.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Dined at home. At the Bells and Table. With Bess</p>","pageId":1025,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1821,"lock":null}
20:13:21.698 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1879
20:13:21.698 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1879,"version":0,"year":1832,"month":11,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Bell to Chapman on WBS for &pound;150 club. A fine weather morning. Wind NW. rather frosty &amp; thick. Dined at 2 o'clock. Walked with A Hurry to Tynemouth. At the Whist Club in the evening</p>","pageId":1025,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1822,"lock":null}
20:13:21.698 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.698 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1879
20:13:21.699 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1879,"version":0,"year":1832,"month":11,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Bell to Chapman on WBS for &pound;150 club. A fine weather morning. Wind NW. rather frosty &amp; thick. Dined at 2 o'clock. Walked with A Hurry to Tynemouth. At the Whist Club in the evening</p>","pageId":1025,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1822,"lock":null}
20:13:21.699 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/188
20:13:21.699 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":188,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. This being a holy day at the Court of Chancery, we could do nothing. I therefor went in the steam boat to Kingstown &amp; dined with J Thompson on board the Royal Charlotte. The Mayor of Anglesey came down &amp; took a sail in his yacht the Pearl. Lieutenant M  Paget came on too and the Royal Charlotte to whom I was introduced. No great honor as it is not likely he will know me again.</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":178,"lock":null}
20:13:21.699 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.699 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/188
