20:13:21.760 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":2003,"version":0,"year":1834,"month":3,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A foggy morning. Rather damp. Wind NE. Received a letter from WBS with leave from Lees &amp; Co to sell the Hope. Called upon Mr Watson, not at home. Walked round by Preston &amp; Tynemouth &amp; Home to dinner. Met <span class=highlight_yellow>Jare</span><span class=highlight_yellow> </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Yoary</span> in the evening. At the George</p>","pageId":1072,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1944,"lock":null}
20:13:21.760 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/2004
20:13:21.760 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":2004,"version":0,"year":1834,"month":3,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild morning. Wind SW. Saw Mr Watson. Did not make a bargain. Determined to lay the ship on shore off the taking her ballast out. Lunched with H Hurry. Dined with <span class=highlight_yellow>Hy</span> Metcalfe &amp; went to the <span class=highlight_yellow>play</span> in the evening. A very good one about  80 people there</p>","pageId":1072,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1945,"lock":null}
