20:13:21.812 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":2111,"version":0,"year":1834,"month":7,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NE. Received a letter from WBS which much relieved my mind &amp; made me feel happier than I have done some time, stating the almost certainty of his getting appointed to a situation on the Coal Exchange by the Factors &amp; also giving me leave to <span class=highlight_yellow>dras</span> upon him for the Hope's tradesmen's bills. H Hurry dined with me. At Tynemouth. Met Bess</p>","pageId":1083,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2051,"lock":null}
20:13:21.812 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/2112
20:13:21.812 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":2112,"version":0,"year":1834,"month":7,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Turned out fine. Wind SE. Received threatening letter from J Metcalf &amp; Son about the Hope's bill. Went over the water &amp; saw them. Promised to pay in 4 months. Dined at home. At the Pig. Walked to Tynemouth in the evening</p>","pageId":1083,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2052,"lock":null}
