20:13:21.931 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":260,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":30,"sequence":4.0000,"text":"<figure>\r\n  <img src=\"images/img2855-image-navarino-house-map.png\" width=\"600px\" />\r\n  <figcaption>Map showing Navarino House</figcaption>\r\n</figure>","pageId":null,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":null,"lock":null}
20:13:21.931 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/261
20:13:21.931 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":261,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":30,"sequence":5.0000,"text":"<p>Rather cloudy in the morning. Wind NE but afterwards turned out an exceedingly fine day. Started at &frac12; past 10 o'clock am with the following party in two sociables &amp; a gig upon a tour round the island viz: Mr Rebecca &amp; Laura Lee, Captain &amp; Mrs Lewis, F Barclay, Bob Marsh, WBS, self &amp; two servants. Stopped &amp; saw Shanklin Chine, called &amp; left our luggage at Ventnor. Drove on to &amp; saw Appuldurcombe the seat of Lord Yarborough containing several fine paintings &amp; finely situated. Returned to Ventnor to dinner &amp; slept. A very pleasant &amp; agreeable party</p>","pageId":707,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":245,"lock":null}
20:13:21.931 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.932 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/261
20:13:21.932 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":261,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":30,"sequence":5.0000,"text":"<p>Rather cloudy in the morning. Wind NE but afterwards turned out an exceedingly fine day. Started at &frac12; past 10 o'clock am with the following party in two sociables &amp; a gig upon a tour round the island viz: Mr Rebecca &amp; Laura Lee, Captain &amp; Mrs Lewis, F Barclay, Bob Marsh, WBS, self &amp; two servants. Stopped &amp; saw Shanklin Chine, called &amp; left our luggage at Ventnor. Drove on to &amp; saw Appuldurcombe the seat of Lord Yarborough containing several fine paintings &amp; finely situated. Returned to Ventnor to dinner &amp; slept. A very pleasant &amp; agreeable party</p>","pageId":707,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":245,"lock":null}
20:13:21.932 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/262
20:13:21.932 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":262,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning but rather cloudy. Wind NE. F Barclay &amp; I got up early &amp; bathed. Started after breakfast &amp; travelled along undercliff &amp; saw the difficult gentlemans seats. Most beautiful &amp; romantic well wooded &amp; cliffs very grand. Stopped at Blackgang Chine, immense high cliffs with waterfall, continued our journey through a beautiful &amp; well cultivated country to Freshwater Bay, where we had lunch about 4 o'clock. Captain Lewis &amp; the ladies went by land to see the Needles. F Barclay, Bob Marsh, WBS and self &amp; two servants went by water &amp; got very well to the Needles which with the cave &amp; majestic chalk cliffs, were very grand. But our return was attended with much unpleasantness to say the least, having an ebb tide &amp; strong wind against us &amp; being in a bad and cranky sea boat, we all got most uncomfortably wet by the spray of the sea. With much difficulty got back to Freshwater Bay to an 8 o'clock dinner. This is a very retired &amp; pretty place</p>","pageId":707,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":246,"lock":null}
20:13:21.932 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.932 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/262
20:13:21.932 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":262,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning but rather cloudy. Wind NE. F Barclay &amp; I got up early &amp; bathed. Started after breakfast &amp; travelled along undercliff &amp; saw the difficult gentlemans seats. Most beautiful &amp; romantic well wooded &amp; cliffs very grand. Stopped at Blackgang Chine, immense high cliffs with waterfall, continued our journey through a beautiful &amp; well cultivated country to Freshwater Bay, where we had lunch about 4 o'clock. Captain Lewis &amp; the ladies went by land to see the Needles. F Barclay, Bob Marsh, WBS and self &amp; two servants went by water &amp; got very well to the Needles which with the cave &amp; majestic chalk cliffs, were very grand. But our return was attended with much unpleasantness to say the least, having an ebb tide &amp; strong wind against us &amp; being in a bad and cranky sea boat, we all got most uncomfortably wet by the spray of the sea. With much difficulty got back to Freshwater Bay to an 8 o'clock dinner. This is a very retired &amp; pretty place</p>","pageId":707,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":246,"lock":null}
20:13:21.932 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/263
20:13:21.932 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":263,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind still from the NE. F Barclay, WBS &amp; I bathed &amp; after breakfast started for Newport where after passing through a pretty country, we arrived about 2 o'clock, stopping to see Carisbrooke Castle on the way. After lunch continued our journey to East Cows, where we dined. <del>For</del> Previously crossing the water to see West Cowes &amp; in the evening, after a most delightful tour &amp; favored with most beautiful weather. We all returned safe to Navarino House much pleased &amp; satisfied. Expenses of the tour &pound;3.10.</p>","pageId":707,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":247,"lock":null}
20:13:21.932 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.933 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/263
20:13:21.933 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":263,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind still from the NE. F Barclay, WBS &amp; I bathed &amp; after breakfast started for Newport where after passing through a pretty country, we arrived about 2 o'clock, stopping to see Carisbrooke Castle on the way. After lunch continued our journey to East Cows, where we dined. <del>For</del> Previously crossing the water to see West Cowes &amp; in the evening, after a most delightful tour &amp; favored with most beautiful weather. We all returned safe to Navarino House much pleased &amp; satisfied. Expenses of the tour &pound;3.10.</p>","pageId":707,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":247,"lock":null}
20:13:21.933 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/264
20:13:21.933 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":264,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather. Wind fresh from the NE. After taking an early breakfast F Barclay, Bob Marsh &amp; I embarked in the Geo<font color=#BFBFBF>rge</font> IV steam boat &amp; went to see Southampton, stopping &frac12; home at Cowes on the way, &amp; after spending a very pleasant day returned to Ryde to dinner. William left for Town</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":248,"lock":null}
20:13:21.933 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.933 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/264
20:13:21.933 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":264,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather. Wind fresh from the NE. After taking an early breakfast F Barclay, Bob Marsh &amp; I embarked in the Geo<font color=#BFBFBF>rge</font> IV steam boat &amp; went to see Southampton, stopping &frac12; home at Cowes on the way, &amp; after spending a very pleasant day returned to Ryde to dinner. William left for Town</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":248,"lock":null}
20:13:21.933 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/265
20:13:21.933 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":265,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still delightful weather. Wind variable between NE &amp; NW but returned to the old quarter NE in the afternoon again. Strolled about the town &amp; pier all day. Dined at Navarino</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":249,"lock":null}
20:13:21.933 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.933 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/265
20:13:21.933 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":265,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still delightful weather. Wind variable between NE &amp; NW but returned to the old quarter NE in the afternoon again. Strolled about the town &amp; pier all day. Dined at Navarino</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":249,"lock":null}
20:13:21.933 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/266
20:13:21.933 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":266,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind NE. Changed to NW &amp; N with thunder &amp; lightning &amp; apparently heavy rain in Hampshire, but returned to the old quarter at night. F Barclay left us this morning for London. Sorry to loose him, a pleasant fellow. Mr Lee &amp; Laura in the chaise &amp; the rest walked to Binstead to see the abbey of which there is little remaining, after lunching on the grass with difficulty &amp; getting our feet covered with mud. We returned home by the beach.</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":250,"lock":null}
20:13:21.933 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.934 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/266
20:13:21.934 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":266,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind NE. Changed to NW &amp; N with thunder &amp; lightning &amp; apparently heavy rain in Hampshire, but returned to the old quarter at night. F Barclay left us this morning for London. Sorry to loose him, a pleasant fellow. Mr Lee &amp; Laura in the chaise &amp; the rest walked to Binstead to see the abbey of which there is little remaining, after lunching on the grass with difficulty &amp; getting our feet covered with mud. We returned home by the beach.</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":250,"lock":null}
20:13:21.934 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/267
20:13:21.934 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":267,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Delightful weather. Wind SE. Sea quite calm. Captain &amp; Mrs Lewis, Bob Marsh &amp; I took a boat &amp; amused ourselves four hours fishing. Great success having caught 89 what they call whiting <span class=highlight_yellow>pacets</span>, a small fish. Took a walk on the pier after dressing &amp; dined at Navarino. The two young Wainwrights dined with us</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":251,"lock":null}
20:13:21.934 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.934 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/267
20:13:21.934 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":267,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Delightful weather. Wind SE. Sea quite calm. Captain &amp; Mrs Lewis, Bob Marsh &amp; I took a boat &amp; amused ourselves four hours fishing. Great success having caught 89 what they call whiting <span class=highlight_yellow>pacets</span>, a small fish. Took a walk on the pier after dressing &amp; dined at Navarino. The two young Wainwrights dined with us</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":251,"lock":null}
20:13:21.934 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/268
20:13:21.934 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":268,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still fine weather. Wind variable between SE &amp; N. Spent the morning Lewis Marsh &amp; I in taking a walk to St John's towards St Helens &amp; home in the afternoon. On the pier blowing very fresh. The Samarary frigate sailed &amp; an Indiaman brought up off Ryde</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":252,"lock":null}
20:13:21.934 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.934 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/268
20:13:21.934 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":268,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still fine weather. Wind variable between SE &amp; N. Spent the morning Lewis Marsh &amp; I in taking a walk to St John's towards St Helens &amp; home in the afternoon. On the pier blowing very fresh. The Samarary frigate sailed &amp; an Indiaman brought up off Ryde</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":252,"lock":null}
20:13:21.934 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/269
20:13:21.934 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":269,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather. Wind ESE. Attended divine services in the morning. The afternoon walked on the pier. Never was at such a dull place on a Sunday. Scarcely a soul to be seen.</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":253,"lock":null}
