20:13:21.938 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":276,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very cold day &amp; blowing a gale of wind from ENE. Did not go to church being unwell with the toothache. Walked upon the pier in the afternoon</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":260,"lock":null}
20:13:21.938 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/277
20:13:21.938 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":277,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Air sharp &amp; frosty. Wind ENE. Walked upon the pier. Played a few games of billiards. Still trouble with the toothache</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":261,"lock":null}
20:13:21.938 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.939 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/277
20:13:21.939 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":277,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Air sharp &amp; frosty. Wind ENE. Walked upon the pier. Played a few games of billiards. Still trouble with the toothache</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":261,"lock":null}
20:13:21.939 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/278
20:13:21.939 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":278,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of uncommonly fine weather. Wind SSE. Captain &amp; Mrs Lewis, Laura, B<font color=#BFBFBF>ob</font> Marsh &amp; I took a sail to &amp; up Portsmouth Harbour round all the men-of-war. Went on board the Royal George Yacht and returned to dinner much gratified &amp; delighted with our excursion.</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":262,"lock":null}
20:13:21.939 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.939 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/278
20:13:21.939 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":278,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of uncommonly fine weather. Wind SSE. Captain &amp; Mrs Lewis, Laura, B<font color=#BFBFBF>ob</font> Marsh &amp; I took a sail to &amp; up Portsmouth Harbour round all the men-of-war. Went on board the Royal George Yacht and returned to dinner much gratified &amp; delighted with our excursion.</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":262,"lock":null}
20:13:21.939 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/279
20:13:21.939 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":279,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather. Wind ESE. We amused ourselves in the morning making a large kite for the boys &amp; in the afternoon walked on the pier. Received from William by George Lee two &pound;5 notes with a letter from Stephenson of the arrival of the Hope at Shields after an 8 day passage on for journey</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":263,"lock":null}
20:13:21.939 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.940 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/279
20:13:21.940 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":279,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather. Wind ESE. We amused ourselves in the morning making a large kite for the boys &amp; in the afternoon walked on the pier. Received from William by George Lee two &pound;5 notes with a letter from Stephenson of the arrival of the Hope at Shields after an 8 day passage on for journey</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":263,"lock":null}
20:13:21.940 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/28
20:13:21.940 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":28,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild day with showers in the morning. Wind SW. Walked to Tynemouth in the morning. Called upon the Miss Ildertons at Mr Sibbs, Mrs Dixon, Bell &amp; Hanna Smith came down &amp; lunched. Dined at home. Tea at Mrs Harrys &amp; whist club in the evening. Heard from &amp; wrote to William</p>","pageId":688,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":25,"lock":null}
20:13:21.940 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.940 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/28
20:13:21.940 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":28,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild day with showers in the morning. Wind SW. Walked to Tynemouth in the morning. Called upon the Miss Ildertons at Mr Sibbs, Mrs Dixon, Bell &amp; Hanna Smith came down &amp; lunched. Dined at home. Tea at Mrs Harrys &amp; whist club in the evening. Heard from &amp; wrote to William</p>","pageId":688,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":25,"lock":null}
20:13:21.940 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/280
20:13:21.940 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":280,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Extraordinary fine weather . Wind about east. Finished &amp; set the kite up. Lounged about the town in the afternoon.</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":264,"lock":null}
20:13:21.940 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.940 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/280
20:13:21.940 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":280,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Extraordinary fine weather . Wind about east. Finished &amp; set the kite up. Lounged about the town in the afternoon.</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":264,"lock":null}
20:13:21.940 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/281
20:13:21.940 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":281,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather. Wind about SE. Passed the day much in the usual way.</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":265,"lock":null}
20:13:21.940 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.941 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/281
20:13:21.941 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":281,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather. Wind about SE. Passed the day much in the usual way.</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":265,"lock":null}
20:13:21.941 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/282
20:13:21.941 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":282,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind SE. After breakfast Rebecca, Mrs Lewis, Lee and the girls &amp; I went in the Isis to Portsmouth on board the Melville man-of-war. Captain Hill &amp; much gratified &amp; pleased with the beautiful order she was in &amp; after lunching with Mrs Hill, returned to Ryde, delighted with our sail. The 1<sup>st</sup> Lieutenant got his promotion this day after 21 years hard service.</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":266,"lock":null}
20:13:21.941 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.941 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/282
20:13:21.941 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":282,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind SE. After breakfast Rebecca, Mrs Lewis, Lee and the girls &amp; I went in the Isis to Portsmouth on board the Melville man-of-war. Captain Hill &amp; much gratified &amp; pleased with the beautiful order she was in &amp; after lunching with Mrs Hill, returned to Ryde, delighted with our sail. The 1<sup>st</sup> Lieutenant got his promotion this day after 21 years hard service.</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":266,"lock":null}
20:13:21.941 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/283
20:13:21.941 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":283,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful day. Wind SW. Went to church in the morning &amp; heard a very poor commonplace sermon from a Mr Moors. Walked upon the pier in the afternoon. Mr &amp; Mrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Gve</span> Lee &amp; Miss Jane Lee dined at Navarinos. Wind changed with <span class=highlight_yellow>a</span> some rain at night</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":267,"lock":null}
20:13:21.941 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.942 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/283
20:13:21.942 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":283,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful day. Wind SW. Went to church in the morning &amp; heard a very poor commonplace sermon from a Mr Moors. Walked upon the pier in the afternoon. Mr &amp; Mrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Gve</span> Lee &amp; Miss Jane Lee dined at Navarinos. Wind changed with <span class=highlight_yellow>a</span> some rain at night</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":267,"lock":null}
20:13:21.942 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/284
20:13:21.942 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":284,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine warm day. Wind SW with a few light showers in the morning. Bob Marshes &amp; I had a most delightful bath after breakfast. The Brocklebank steamer arrived from Brighton on an excursion of pleasure loaded with passengers between 2 &amp; 3 rd, principally trades people in appearance. Lots of vulgarity, pipes &amp; &quot;heavy wet&quot;. Played a few games of billiards.</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":268,"lock":null}
20:13:21.942 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.942 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/284
20:13:21.942 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":284,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine warm day. Wind SW with a few light showers in the morning. Bob Marshes &amp; I had a most delightful bath after breakfast. The Brocklebank steamer arrived from Brighton on an excursion of pleasure loaded with passengers between 2 &amp; 3 rd, principally trades people in appearance. Lots of vulgarity, pipes &amp; &quot;heavy wet&quot;. Played a few games of billiards.</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":268,"lock":null}
20:13:21.942 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/285
20:13:21.942 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":285,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Beautiful weather. Wind SW. Remained in the house until after lunch. In the afternoon strolled about the town. Went to a Quadrille party at the library in the evening. Very well attended &amp; good company. Wrote to William</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":269,"lock":null}
20:13:21.942 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.942 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/285
20:13:21.942 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":285,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Beautiful weather. Wind SW. Remained in the house until after lunch. In the afternoon strolled about the town. Went to a Quadrille party at the library in the evening. Very well attended &amp; good company. Wrote to William</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":269,"lock":null}
20:13:21.942 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/286
20:13:21.942 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":286,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of most extraordinary fine weather, with wind SW. Strolled about the pier &amp; town</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":270,"lock":null}
20:13:21.942 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.943 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/286
20:13:21.943 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":286,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of most extraordinary fine weather, with wind SW. Strolled about the pier &amp; town</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":270,"lock":null}
20:13:21.943 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/287
20:13:21.943 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":287,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A glorious day. Not a cloud to be seen. Wind SW. After breakfast Lewis, Fanny, Bob Marsh took a boat &amp; sailed round to Brading Harbour. Much pleased with the views of the country &amp; coast &amp; delighted with our sail. Got back at &frac12; past 3 pm. Received a letter from William of the arrival of the Hope but too late for yesterdays market.</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":271,"lock":null}
20:13:21.943 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.943 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/287
20:13:21.943 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":287,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A glorious day. Not a cloud to be seen. Wind SW. After breakfast Lewis, Fanny, Bob Marsh took a boat &amp; sailed round to Brading Harbour. Much pleased with the views of the country &amp; coast &amp; delighted with our sail. Got back at &frac12; past 3 pm. Received a letter from William of the arrival of the Hope but too late for yesterdays market.</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":271,"lock":null}
20:13:21.943 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/288
20:13:21.943 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":288,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind SW to W. After breakfast walked to Binstead parsonage, about 1 mile, from Naravinos. In my opinion the prettiest &amp; most picturesque place in the island. The grounds laid out with great taste &amp; kept in the highest order. The views from them very fine. Wrote to William of my intention to be in town on Sunday.</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":272,"lock":null}
20:13:21.943 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.944 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/288
20:13:21.944 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":288,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind SW to W. After breakfast walked to Binstead parsonage, about 1 mile, from Naravinos. In my opinion the prettiest &amp; most picturesque place in the island. The grounds laid out with great taste &amp; kept in the highest order. The views from them very fine. Wrote to William of my intention to be in town on Sunday.</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":272,"lock":null}
20:13:21.944 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/289
20:13:21.944 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":289,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A wet morning. Wind NW to SW. Cleared up before 12 o'clock &amp; turned out a pleasant day. Booked outside place by the Rocket coach from tomorrow morning. Received a letter from William of the sale of the Hope at 32/3</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":273,"lock":null}
20:13:21.944 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
