20:13:21.944 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":289,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A wet morning. Wind NW to SW. Cleared up before 12 o'clock &amp; turned out a pleasant day. Booked outside place by the Rocket coach from tomorrow morning. Received a letter from William of the sale of the Hope at 32/3</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":273,"lock":null}
20:13:21.944 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/29
20:13:21.944 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":29,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of mild weather. Wind NW. Opened two accounts at chapmans WBS &amp; JRS Executors &amp; JRS private. Dined at home &amp; drank tea at Mr Deightoughe , not well</p>","pageId":688,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":26,"lock":null}
20:13:21.944 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.944 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/29
20:13:21.944 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":29,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of mild weather. Wind NW. Opened two accounts at chapmans WBS &amp; JRS Executors &amp; JRS private. Dined at home &amp; drank tea at Mr Deightoughe , not well</p>","pageId":688,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":26,"lock":null}
20:13:21.944 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/290
20:13:21.944 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":290,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A good deal of rain in the night. Wind SW. Left Ryde at 9 o'clock am. Steam for Portsmouth. Took an outside place in the Rocket coach &amp; arrived in London at &frac12; past 7 o'clock pm having had a few showers of rain on the road. Got a bed in Nottingham Place. William out of town at his friend <span class=highlight_yellow>Oliphants</span>. Found a note from him that Stephenson had been obliged to leave the Hope &amp; return to the North in consequence of the illness of his uncle. Spent a very pleasant month with my friends, the Lees at Ryde&amp; sorry to leave there.</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":274,"lock":null}
20:13:21.944 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.945 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/290
20:13:21.945 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":290,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A good deal of rain in the night. Wind SW. Left Ryde at 9 o'clock am. Steam for Portsmouth. Took an outside place in the Rocket coach &amp; arrived in London at &frac12; past 7 o'clock pm having had a few showers of rain on the road. Got a bed in Nottingham Place. William out of town at his friend <span class=highlight_yellow>Oliphants</span>. Found a note from him that Stephenson had been obliged to leave the Hope &amp; return to the North in consequence of the illness of his uncle. Spent a very pleasant month with my friends, the Lees at Ryde&amp; sorry to leave there.</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":274,"lock":null}
20:13:21.945 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/291
20:13:21.945 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":291,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind SW. Went into the city by a Paddington Stage. Saw William. Attended the market &amp; afterwards went down the river and dined on board the Hope. Walked home in the evening on our way drinking tea with <span class=highlight_yellow>Oliphant</span> at Cockspur Street.</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":275,"lock":null}
20:13:21.945 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.945 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/291
20:13:21.945 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":291,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind SW. Went into the city by a Paddington Stage. Saw William. Attended the market &amp; afterwards went down the river and dined on board the Hope. Walked home in the evening on our way drinking tea with <span class=highlight_yellow>Oliphant</span> at Cockspur Street.</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":275,"lock":null}
20:13:21.945 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/292
20:13:21.945 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":292,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning during the day showers of rain. Wind SW. Walked into the city. Brought a new hat of <span class=highlight_yellow>Oliphant</span>. Paid &pound;3 for the Hopes ballast &amp; took a Greenwich boat into the pool to her. Gave the mate charge for the passage to Shields. Returned to the city &amp; had a basin of turtle soup at Bleadens. Afterwards took a Paddington Stage &amp; went with William to see the Zoological Society garden in the Regent park. Well worth the walk. In the evening went to the Argyle rooms &amp; was much amused with <span class=highlight_yellow>Fumtas</span> chin</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":276,"lock":null}
20:13:21.945 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.946 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/292
20:13:21.946 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":292,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning during the day showers of rain. Wind SW. Walked into the city. Brought a new hat of <span class=highlight_yellow>Oliphant</span>. Paid &pound;3 for the Hopes ballast &amp; took a Greenwich boat into the pool to her. Gave the mate charge for the passage to Shields. Returned to the city &amp; had a basin of turtle soup at Bleadens. Afterwards took a Paddington Stage &amp; went with William to see the Zoological Society garden in the Regent park. Well worth the walk. In the evening went to the Argyle rooms &amp; was much amused with <span class=highlight_yellow>Fumtas</span> chin</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":276,"lock":null}
20:13:21.946 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/293
20:13:21.946 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":293,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind SW. Walked into the city. The Hope not to be out, the country craft having been sunk. Met <span class=highlight_yellow>Mr</span> Carr who went out of the city with us, dined at the Blue Ports &amp; in the evening went to Covent Garden Theater &amp; saw at &frac12; price the latter part of Hamlet &amp; Peter Welkins</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":277,"lock":null}
20:13:21.946 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.946 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/293
20:13:21.946 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":293,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind SW. Walked into the city. The Hope not to be out, the country craft having been sunk. Met <span class=highlight_yellow>Mr</span> Carr who went out of the city with us, dined at the Blue Ports &amp; in the evening went to Covent Garden Theater &amp; saw at &frac12; price the latter part of Hamlet &amp; Peter Welkins</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":277,"lock":null}
20:13:21.946 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/294
20:13:21.946 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":294,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still fine weather. Wind SW &amp; SSW. Went down to the Hope, only to do 10 &frac12; cha today. Dined on board. Walked up &amp; went to Drury Lane Theatre to the pit at full price &amp; saw &quot;A cure for the heartache&quot; &amp; XYZ. Very much entertained.</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":278,"lock":null}
20:13:21.946 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.946 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/294
20:13:21.946 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":294,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still fine weather. Wind SW &amp; SSW. Went down to the Hope, only to do 10 &frac12; cha today. Dined on board. Walked up &amp; went to Drury Lane Theatre to the pit at full price &amp; saw &quot;A cure for the heartache&quot; &amp; XYZ. Very much entertained.</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":278,"lock":null}
20:13:21.946 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/295
20:13:21.946 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":295,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather. Wind SW. Now &amp; then a shower of rain. Walked into the city. Attended the Coal Exchange. The Hope not to do anything today. Watt called, took a boat to Hungerford. All dined at the Blue Pasts. Lent Watt 20/- Received of WBS &pound;2.16. Balance of Hopes after her 3<sup>rd</sup> coal voyage.</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":279,"lock":null}
20:13:21.946 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.947 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/295
20:13:21.947 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":295,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather. Wind SW. Now &amp; then a shower of rain. Walked into the city. Attended the Coal Exchange. The Hope not to do anything today. Watt called, took a boat to Hungerford. All dined at the Blue Pasts. Lent Watt 20/- Received of WBS &pound;2.16. Balance of Hopes after her 3<sup>rd</sup> coal voyage.</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":279,"lock":null}
20:13:21.947 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/296
20:13:21.947 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":296,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet morning. Wind WSW. Cleared up towards the middle of the day &amp; turned out a fine afternoon. Went down to the ship about 1 o'clock pm. Found her nearly out. Watt came on board. Sailed about 3 o'clock &amp; got below Woolwich &amp; brought up, where Watt left us. A breeze springing up got underway again about 9 o'clock against the flood but obliged again to let go our anchor about 11 o'clock for want of wind! For the night William slept on board. Brought today a life preserver for 18/- Some white &amp; coloured neckcloths for &pound;2</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":280,"lock":null}
20:13:21.947 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.947 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/296
20:13:21.948 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":296,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet morning. Wind WSW. Cleared up towards the middle of the day &amp; turned out a fine afternoon. Went down to the ship about 1 o'clock pm. Found her nearly out. Watt came on board. Sailed about 3 o'clock &amp; got below Woolwich &amp; brought up, where Watt left us. A breeze springing up got underway again about 9 o'clock against the flood but obliged again to let go our anchor about 11 o'clock for want of wind! For the night William slept on board. Brought today a life preserver for 18/- Some white &amp; coloured neckcloths for &pound;2</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":280,"lock":null}
20:13:21.948 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/297
20:13:21.948 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":297,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind South. Got underway from off _____ at 11 o'clock am with a fresh breeze, landed William at Gravesend. At 1 o'clock pm. At 4 o'clock passed through Shoe Hole 8 o'clock abreast of Harwich &amp; 10 o'clock off the Lowestoft Light &amp; turned in for the night. Blowing fresh.</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":281,"lock":null}
20:13:21.948 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.948 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/297
20:13:21.948 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":297,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind South. Got underway from off _____ at 11 o'clock am with a fresh breeze, landed William at Gravesend. At 1 o'clock pm. At 4 o'clock passed through Shoe Hole 8 o'clock abreast of Harwich &amp; 10 o'clock off the Lowestoft Light &amp; turned in for the night. Blowing fresh.</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":281,"lock":null}
20:13:21.948 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/298
20:13:21.948 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":298,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Blowing hard all night with rain towards morning. Got up at 8 o'clock am. Wind just changed to WNW, rather squally. Ship off Cromer. At 11 o'clock abreast of the floating light. Blowing hard from West. Ship under foresail &amp; reefed topsail, mainsail &amp; double reefed main topsail &amp; reefed trysail. At 2 o'clock pm double reefed fore-top-sail. At 3 o'clock made the Spurn <font color=#BFBFBF>[Point]</font><font color=#BFBFBF> </font> being off the floating light. Still blowing strong from the West</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":282,"lock":null}
20:13:21.948 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.948 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/298
20:13:21.948 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":298,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Blowing hard all night with rain towards morning. Got up at 8 o'clock am. Wind just changed to WNW, rather squally. Ship off Cromer. At 11 o'clock abreast of the floating light. Blowing hard from West. Ship under foresail &amp; reefed topsail, mainsail &amp; double reefed main topsail &amp; reefed trysail. At 2 o'clock pm double reefed fore-top-sail. At 3 o'clock made the Spurn <font color=#BFBFBF>[Point]</font><font color=#BFBFBF> </font> being off the floating light. Still blowing strong from the West</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":282,"lock":null}
20:13:21.948 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/299
20:13:21.948 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":299,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":6,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>About 7 o'clock got bound. Flamborough Head at 10 o'clock. Off Robin Hoods bay blowing hard with squalls at 11 o'clock between the bay &amp; Whitby met a fleet of London vessels. Blowing hard. Nearly run down one vessel owing to his own obstinacy or keeping a bad lookout. Stowed trysail &amp; main sail &amp; took in jib. Very dark ahead. At 12 o'clock or little after it, clear weather but continued to blow off Hunt Cliff Foot. Turned in for the night.</p>","pageId":711,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":283,"lock":null}
20:13:21.948 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.949 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/299
20:13:21.949 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":299,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":6,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>About 7 o'clock got bound. Flamborough Head at 10 o'clock. Off Robin Hoods bay blowing hard with squalls at 11 o'clock between the bay &amp; Whitby met a fleet of London vessels. Blowing hard. Nearly run down one vessel owing to his own obstinacy or keeping a bad lookout. Stowed trysail &amp; main sail &amp; took in jib. Very dark ahead. At 12 o'clock or little after it, clear weather but continued to blow off Hunt Cliff Foot. Turned in for the night.</p>","pageId":711,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":283,"lock":null}
