20:13:21.955 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":312,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild morning. Wind WNW. After breakfast, Emma &amp; I walked to see the new colliery sunk by Tom Smith &amp; others &amp; afterwards went down to Amble &amp; the sands &amp; returned about 2 o'clock after a most pleasurable walk. Tom, Fanny, Anna &amp; Bell returned from Alnwick to dinner at 5 o'clock</p>","pageId":712,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":295,"lock":null}
20:13:21.955 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/313
20:13:21.955 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":313,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful autumnal day. Wind WSW. Drove Fanny, Bell &amp; Emma Galbraith down to Warkworth church. Called upon the <span class=highlight_yellow>Miss</span> Watsons. Saw the Chatterbucks etc. In the afternoon took a walk with Tom to the colliery. <span class=highlight_yellow>res</span> Matt Culley came to dinner at 5 o'clock</p>","pageId":712,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":296,"lock":null}
