20:13:21.962 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":327,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful day. Wind NNW. Went to Warkworth Church in the morning. Called upon Mr &amp; Miss Watons. Drove Fanny &amp; Bell Smith &amp; Emma Galbraith in the afternoon. Robert Brown walked down from Brinkburn, dined &amp; stayed all night. Spent a jolly evening.</p>","pageId":713,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":310,"lock":null}
20:13:21.962 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/328
20:13:21.962 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":328,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A delightful day. Wind, but little in the morning at NW, afterwards changed to SE. Robert Brown left us for Brinkburn. Tom Smith drove him beyond Felton. Went out shooting but had no sport. Birds wild &amp; scent bad.</p>","pageId":713,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":311,"lock":null}
20:13:21.962 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
