20:13:21.962 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":328,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A delightful day. Wind, but little in the morning at NW, afterwards changed to SE. Robert Brown left us for Brinkburn. Tom Smith drove him beyond Felton. Went out shooting but had no sport. Birds wild &amp; scent bad.</p>","pageId":713,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":311,"lock":null}
20:13:21.962 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/329
20:13:21.962 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":329,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cool morning &amp; thick weather. Wind SE. Walked twice to the colliery. Miss M Watson came up &amp; dined at Togston. Played at whist in the evening</p>","pageId":713,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":312,"lock":null}
20:13:21.962 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.963 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/329
20:13:21.963 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":329,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cool morning &amp; thick weather. Wind SE. Walked twice to the colliery. Miss M Watson came up &amp; dined at Togston. Played at whist in the evening</p>","pageId":713,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":312,"lock":null}
20:13:21.963 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/33
20:13:21.963 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":33,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An exceedingly fair day, rather cold. Wind SW. Dined at home. At the assembly in the evening. A very pleasant one, but not numerously attended, about 60 there. Got home at 4 o'clock. Wrote to William</p>","pageId":689,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":30,"lock":null}
20:13:21.963 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.963 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/33
20:13:21.963 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":33,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An exceedingly fair day, rather cold. Wind SW. Dined at home. At the assembly in the evening. A very pleasant one, but not numerously attended, about 60 there. Got home at 4 o'clock. Wrote to William</p>","pageId":689,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":30,"lock":null}
20:13:21.963 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/330
20:13:21.963 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":330,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up at &frac12; past 6 o'clock am. A fine morning. Wind at SE. Breakfasted &amp; rode to Morepeth with Tom Smith, market &amp; fair day there. Left Morpeth by the Shields coach &amp; got home at 4 o'clock. To dinner. Mrs Scott very well. The Hope arrived this afternoon &amp; fixed for Wellington to be loaded on Tuesday. Received a letter from William, the sale with balance now for &pound;73.18/-</p>","pageId":713,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":313,"lock":null}
20:13:21.963 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
