20:13:21.987 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":377,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An exceedingly wet day. Wind about W or W by S. Received a letter from William &amp; answered it ordering by W Taylors desire the Morning Journal &amp; Morning Herald newspapers. At 5 guineas for the Newsroom. Dined at home.</p>","pageId":718,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":360,"lock":null}
20:13:21.987 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/378
20:13:21.987 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":378,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Rather a damp day. Wind E &amp; ESE. Dined at J Tinleys. A pleasant day. There Captain Bunbury, Mr Hopkins 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment, Mr Parr &amp; Doctor White. Afterwards went to the ball. Very well attended for the first time. Upwards of 60 there. Danced with a Miss Paine of Faversham, a very fine girl.</p>\r\n<p>Paid apprentices one quarters wages, &pound;1.8.9 Repaid ex<font color=#BFBFBF>ecut</font>ors &pound;50 borrowed of them. Gave Stephenson &pound;25 to pay wages</p>","pageId":718,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":361,"lock":null}
20:13:21.987 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.987 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/378
20:13:21.987 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":378,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Rather a damp day. Wind E &amp; ESE. Dined at J Tinleys. A pleasant day. There Captain Bunbury, Mr Hopkins 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment, Mr Parr &amp; Doctor White. Afterwards went to the ball. Very well attended for the first time. Upwards of 60 there. Danced with a Miss Paine of Faversham, a very fine girl.</p>\r\n<p>Paid apprentices one quarters wages, &pound;1.8.9 Repaid ex<font color=#BFBFBF>ecut</font>ors &pound;50 borrowed of them. Gave Stephenson &pound;25 to pay wages</p>","pageId":718,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":361,"lock":null}
20:13:21.987 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/379
20:13:21.988 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":379,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild day. Rather damp with rain in the evening. Wind SE. The Hope arrived safe in the evening &frac12; past 6 o'clock. Dined at home. Received the Hope's ac<font color=#BFBFBF>count</font>s along with a balance of &pound;51.11/-</p>","pageId":718,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":362,"lock":null}
20:13:21.988 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
