20:13:21.988 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":379,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild day. Rather damp with rain in the evening. Wind SE. The Hope arrived safe in the evening &frac12; past 6 o'clock. Dined at home. Received the Hope's ac<font color=#BFBFBF>count</font>s along with a balance of &pound;51.11/-</p>","pageId":718,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":362,"lock":null}
20:13:21.988 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/38
20:13:21.988 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":38,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":2,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day, Wind WSW. At church in the morning. Walked to Tynemouth in the afternoon with J Tinley &amp; boys. Dined at home</p>","pageId":689,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":35,"lock":null}
20:13:21.988 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.988 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/38
20:13:21.988 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":38,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":2,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day, Wind WSW. At church in the morning. Walked to Tynemouth in the afternoon with J Tinley &amp; boys. Dined at home</p>","pageId":689,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":35,"lock":null}
20:13:21.988 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/380
20:13:21.988 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":380,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Xmas day. A fine day. Wind SSW. Went to church in the morning &amp; afterwards walked up to Benton to dinner &amp; stayed all night. Wrote to William to take the Hope off risk of British Club</p>","pageId":718,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":363,"lock":null}
20:13:21.988 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.989 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/380
20:13:21.989 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":380,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Xmas day. A fine day. Wind SSW. Went to church in the morning &amp; afterwards walked up to Benton to dinner &amp; stayed all night. Wrote to William to take the Hope off risk of British Club</p>","pageId":718,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":363,"lock":null}
20:13:21.989 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/381
20:13:21.989 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":381,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning &amp; sharp frost. Wind SSW. Walked into Newcastle. Took the Hope on for a turn of <span class=highlight_yellow>townley</span> &amp; gave notice to the Hope Club of my intention to lay her up. Received from Carr &amp; Co &pound;21.6/- on account of WBS. Balance of freight acct <span class=highlight_yellow>o/s</span> Hope. Came down to Shields to dinner &amp; in the evening attended the whist club. The Hope got under the crane to take her manure out for Mr J<font color=#BFBFBF>u</font>n<font color=#BFBFBF>i</font><sup>o</sup><font color=#BFBFBF>r</font> Finewick of Preston Villa. Gave Mrs Scott a draft on Chapmans for &pound;75 her annuity.</p>","pageId":718,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":364,"lock":null}
20:13:21.989 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.989 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/381
20:13:21.989 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":381,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning &amp; sharp frost. Wind SSW. Walked into Newcastle. Took the Hope on for a turn of <span class=highlight_yellow>townley</span> &amp; gave notice to the Hope Club of my intention to lay her up. Received from Carr &amp; Co &pound;21.6/- on account of WBS. Balance of freight acct <span class=highlight_yellow>o/s</span> Hope. Came down to Shields to dinner &amp; in the evening attended the whist club. The Hope got under the crane to take her manure out for Mr J<font color=#BFBFBF>u</font>n<font color=#BFBFBF>i</font><sup>o</sup><font color=#BFBFBF>r</font> Finewick of Preston Villa. Gave Mrs Scott a draft on Chapmans for &pound;75 her annuity.</p>","pageId":718,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":364,"lock":null}
20:13:21.989 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/382
20:13:21.989 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":382,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine seasonable day, rather cold &amp; frosty. Wind S by W. On board the Hope all the morning. Along side the crane getting manure out for which I received of Mr Fenwick &pound;2 there being 80 tons. The people engaged unbending sails &amp; taking down running rigging etc preparatory to laying ship up. Dined at home. In the evening at the whist club at Tom Weights</p>","pageId":718,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":365,"lock":null}
20:13:21.989 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.990 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/382
20:13:21.990 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":382,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine seasonable day, rather cold &amp; frosty. Wind S by W. On board the Hope all the morning. Along side the crane getting manure out for which I received of Mr Fenwick &pound;2 there being 80 tons. The people engaged unbending sails &amp; taking down running rigging etc preparatory to laying ship up. Dined at home. In the evening at the whist club at Tom Weights</p>","pageId":718,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":365,"lock":null}
20:13:21.990 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/383
20:13:21.990 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":383,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A foggy morning &amp; a heavy fall of rain during the whole day. Wind W by S. Cleared up in the evening. At church in the morning. Miss <span class=highlight_yellow>Heevson</span> dined with me. Wrote to William informing him of my having received of Mr Shakers &pound;10.11.2 on account of Messrs Lees, which I carry to WBS Cr. Spent the evening at J Tinleys.</p>","pageId":718,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":366,"lock":null}
20:13:21.990 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.990 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/383
20:13:21.990 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":383,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A foggy morning &amp; a heavy fall of rain during the whole day. Wind W by S. Cleared up in the evening. At church in the morning. Miss <span class=highlight_yellow>Heevson</span> dined with me. Wrote to William informing him of my having received of Mr Shakers &pound;10.11.2 on account of Messrs Lees, which I carry to WBS Cr. Spent the evening at J Tinleys.</p>","pageId":718,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":366,"lock":null}
20:13:21.990 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/384
20:13:21.990 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":384,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine weather day. Excessively cold. Wind SW. Engaged in the morning drawing &amp; on board ship. Dined at home. Took wine with Mark Cunningham &amp; Boswick at the Albion</p>","pageId":718,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":367,"lock":null}
20:13:21.990 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
