20:13:21.997 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":397,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":1,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fair weather but cold. Wind SE &amp; ESE. Sea high. Several light ships got down. Dined at home. In the evening at Tibbs whist club. Paid Reed <span class=highlight_yellow>app</span><span class=highlight_yellow>rentice</span> I Weeks board lodgings 7/-</p>","pageId":720,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":379,"lock":null}
20:13:21.997 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/398
20:13:21.997 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":398,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":1,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A thick dull day, but dry. Wind variable. At church in the morning. Received a letter from I &amp; B Galbraith &amp; Mr Vernon. Dined at home. In the evening at the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":720,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":380,"lock":null}
20:13:21.997 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.997 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/398
20:13:21.997 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":398,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":1,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A thick dull day, but dry. Wind variable. At church in the morning. Received a letter from I &amp; B Galbraith &amp; Mr Vernon. Dined at home. In the evening at the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":720,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":380,"lock":null}
20:13:21.997 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/399
20:13:21.997 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":399,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":1,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather. Cold with a little hail. Wind ESE &amp; sea high. Several light ships got in. Dined at home. In the evening called &amp; took wine with Tom Wright upon his marriage. A great many there. Spent a pleasant evening.</p>","pageId":720,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":381,"lock":null}
20:13:21.997 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.997 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/399
20:13:21.997 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":399,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":1,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather. Cold with a little hail. Wind ESE &amp; sea high. Several light ships got in. Dined at home. In the evening called &amp; took wine with Tom Wright upon his marriage. A great many there. Spent a pleasant evening.</p>","pageId":720,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":381,"lock":null}
20:13:21.997 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/4
20:13:21.997 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":4,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Here I find myself once more in my native place after misfortune unlooked for &amp; unmeritted &amp; two years of anxiety and in settling our affairs, the disgraceful conduct of our attorney (Baily) &amp; his clients, proceeding from ignorance &amp; stupidity, I believe caused the delay, but which however has ended by the various amendments &amp; and alterations in the deeds suggested by William &amp; myself, much more to the advantage of ourselves &amp; all parties, than could possibly have been anticipated at the commencement. I now trust this is the beginning of a new life, where in its course will be attended with prosperity &amp; happiness both to my brother &amp; myself &amp; that he may soon have it in his power as I'm sure it is his wish &amp; intention to &quot;render unto every man his due&quot; he may have committed errors but this I know, they have been errors of the head not of the heart. If he had a fault, it was too great a desire to serve others without perhaps prudently asking himself whether he could do so, without committing an act of injustice to himself his family or those who were next to those connected to him by the nearest &amp; dearest ties, however &quot;Expereentia docet&quot;. Here's oblivion to the past &amp; may prosperity attend the future. As for myself, I feel as every ...</p>","pageId":685,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1,"lock":null}
20:13:21.997 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:21.998 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/4
20:13:21.998 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":4,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Here I find myself once more in my native place after misfortune unlooked for &amp; unmeritted &amp; two years of anxiety and in settling our affairs, the disgraceful conduct of our attorney (Baily) &amp; his clients, proceeding from ignorance &amp; stupidity, I believe caused the delay, but which however has ended by the various amendments &amp; and alterations in the deeds suggested by William &amp; myself, much more to the advantage of ourselves &amp; all parties, than could possibly have been anticipated at the commencement. I now trust this is the beginning of a new life, where in its course will be attended with prosperity &amp; happiness both to my brother &amp; myself &amp; that he may soon have it in his power as I'm sure it is his wish &amp; intention to &quot;render unto every man his due&quot; he may have committed errors but this I know, they have been errors of the head not of the heart. If he had a fault, it was too great a desire to serve others without perhaps prudently asking himself whether he could do so, without committing an act of injustice to himself his family or those who were next to those connected to him by the nearest &amp; dearest ties, however &quot;Expereentia docet&quot;. Here's oblivion to the past &amp; may prosperity attend the future. As for myself, I feel as every ...</p>","pageId":685,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1,"lock":null}
20:13:21.998 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/40
