20:13:22.001 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":407,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":1,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of frosty weather with snow showers. Wind NW, changed in the afternoon to east, with thaw. Dined at home. Wrote to William</p>","pageId":721,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":389,"lock":null}
20:13:22.001 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/408
20:13:22.001 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":408,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":1,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day &amp; frosty. Wind E by S &amp; changed in the afternoon to W by S. A great many light ships arrived. Walked to Tynemouth with W Ferguson &amp; called upon Captain Bunbury. Dined at home. In the evening at the theatre &frac12; price. Mrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Grose</span><span class=highlight_yellow>'</span><span class=highlight_yellow>s</span> benefit &pound;17 in the house. Paid <span class=highlight_yellow>average</span> Elizabeth. <span class=highlight_yellow>Choice to</span> Hope Club &pound;28.19.2</p>","pageId":721,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":390,"lock":null}
20:13:22.001 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.002 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/408
20:13:22.002 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":408,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":1,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day &amp; frosty. Wind E by S &amp; changed in the afternoon to W by S. A great many light ships arrived. Walked to Tynemouth with W Ferguson &amp; called upon Captain Bunbury. Dined at home. In the evening at the theatre &frac12; price. Mrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Grose</span><span class=highlight_yellow>'</span><span class=highlight_yellow>s</span> benefit &pound;17 in the house. Paid <span class=highlight_yellow>average</span> Elizabeth. <span class=highlight_yellow>Choice to</span> Hope Club &pound;28.19.2</p>","pageId":721,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":390,"lock":null}
20:13:22.002 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/409
20:13:22.002 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":409,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":1,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Exceedingly cold. Wind SE blowing fresh &amp; sea high. A <span class=highlight_yellow>King</span> ship came in in <span class=highlight_yellow>the</span>. Dined at J Tinley's &amp; went to the <span class=highlight_yellow>apunbly</span> in the evening. A most delightful Ball. Suppered afterwards. The dancing at &frac12; past 2 o'clock &amp; Kept it up till 6 o'clock.</p>","pageId":721,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":391,"lock":null}
20:13:22.002 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.002 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/409
20:13:22.002 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":409,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":1,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Exceedingly cold. Wind SE blowing fresh &amp; sea high. A <span class=highlight_yellow>King</span> ship came in in <span class=highlight_yellow>the</span>. Dined at J Tinley's &amp; went to the <span class=highlight_yellow>apunbly</span> in the evening. A most delightful Ball. Suppered afterwards. The dancing at &frac12; past 2 o'clock &amp; Kept it up till 6 o'clock.</p>","pageId":721,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":391,"lock":null}
20:13:22.002 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/41
20:13:22.002 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":41,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":2,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind SW. Changed towards evening to East. Engaged all morning on board the Hope. Having two men employed in overhauling small ropes running rigging to which we found in a much better state than could be expected. Mr Carr late master must have been very careless to say the least, having left some sails, bread, flour &amp; bags &amp; a cask of provisions with the head knocked in &amp; compass as on board which were all destroyed &amp; rotten</p>","pageId":689,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":38,"lock":null}
20:13:22.002 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.002 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/41
20:13:22.002 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":41,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":2,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind SW. Changed towards evening to East. Engaged all morning on board the Hope. Having two men employed in overhauling small ropes running rigging to which we found in a much better state than could be expected. Mr Carr late master must have been very careless to say the least, having left some sails, bread, flour &amp; bags &amp; a cask of provisions with the head knocked in &amp; compass as on board which were all destroyed &amp; rotten</p>","pageId":689,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":38,"lock":null}
20:13:22.002 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/410
20:13:22.002 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":410,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":1,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold day. A continuance of frost &amp; snow and a gale of wind SE &amp; SSE, sea high. A few loaded ships put back. Dined at home. Spent the evening at J Tinleys. Paid Reed a week's lodging 7/-.</p>","pageId":721,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":392,"lock":null}
20:13:22.002 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.003 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/410
20:13:22.003 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":410,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":1,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold day. A continuance of frost &amp; snow and a gale of wind SE &amp; SSE, sea high. A few loaded ships put back. Dined at home. Spent the evening at J Tinleys. Paid Reed a week's lodging 7/-.</p>","pageId":721,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":392,"lock":null}
20:13:22.003 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/411
20:13:22.003 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":411,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":1,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of frost &amp; snow &amp; a gale of wind from SE to SSE. Went to Newcastle to endeavour to get something for the Hope, but did not succeed. People not willing to do anything until after the meeting of coal owners. Dined with J Tinley, a party, Captain <span class=highlight_yellow>Morins</span> &amp; 2 Lieutenants  of the <span class=highlight_yellow>childers</span>, C <span class=highlight_yellow>Milners</span> &amp; sister Miss <span class=highlight_yellow>Atlen</span> Lieutenants 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment</p>","pageId":721,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":393,"lock":null}
20:13:22.003 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.003 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/411
20:13:22.003 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":411,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":1,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of frost &amp; snow &amp; a gale of wind from SE to SSE. Went to Newcastle to endeavour to get something for the Hope, but did not succeed. People not willing to do anything until after the meeting of coal owners. Dined with J Tinley, a party, Captain <span class=highlight_yellow>Morins</span> &amp; 2 Lieutenants  of the <span class=highlight_yellow>childers</span>, C <span class=highlight_yellow>Milners</span> &amp; sister Miss <span class=highlight_yellow>Atlen</span> Lieutenants 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment</p>","pageId":721,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":393,"lock":null}
20:13:22.003 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/412
20:13:22.003 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":412,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":1,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Hard frost. Wind NW. At church in the morning. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home &amp; took wine with A Metcalf</p>","pageId":722,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":394,"lock":null}
20:13:22.003 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.003 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/412
20:13:22.003 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":412,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":1,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Hard frost. Wind NW. At church in the morning. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home &amp; took wine with A Metcalf</p>","pageId":722,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":394,"lock":null}
20:13:22.003 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/413
20:13:22.003 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":413,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":1,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>This morning a thaw commenced, early at blew  a gale of wind with sleet. Wind blowing E by S &amp; S by E. Excessively wet &amp; sloppy walking. Dined at home. Spent the evening &amp; suppered with  Mr Allen. A very pleasant party. Got home at 1 o'clock. Engaged a new washer woman by the quarter.</p>","pageId":722,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":395,"lock":null}
20:13:22.003 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.004 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/413
20:13:22.004 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":413,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":1,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>This morning a thaw commenced, early at blew  a gale of wind with sleet. Wind blowing E by S &amp; S by E. Excessively wet &amp; sloppy walking. Dined at home. Spent the evening &amp; suppered with  Mr Allen. A very pleasant party. Got home at 1 o'clock. Engaged a new washer woman by the quarter.</p>","pageId":722,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":395,"lock":null}
20:13:22.004 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/414
20:13:22.004 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":414,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":1,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of thaw with heavy rain. Much of the snow disappeared. Wind SSE. Went to Newcastle but no freights or anything offering. The <span class=highlight_yellow>fuller</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>obsheiate</span>.  On my return found Mr Watson of Walkworth here. Dined at home. Spent the evening at J Tinleys. <span class=highlight_yellow>Miss</span> Nicholas, Miss Allen and Captain <span class=highlight_yellow>Moorers</span> there.</p>","pageId":722,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":396,"lock":null}
20:13:22.004 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.004 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/414
20:13:22.004 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":414,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":1,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of thaw with heavy rain. Much of the snow disappeared. Wind SSE. Went to Newcastle but no freights or anything offering. The <span class=highlight_yellow>fuller</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>obsheiate</span>.  On my return found Mr Watson of Walkworth here. Dined at home. Spent the evening at J Tinleys. <span class=highlight_yellow>Miss</span> Nicholas, Miss Allen and Captain <span class=highlight_yellow>Moorers</span> there.</p>","pageId":722,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":396,"lock":null}
20:13:22.004 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/415
20:13:22.004 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":415,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":1,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A unpleasant day. Rainy &amp; very wet &amp; dirty walking. Wind NE in the morning which changed to NW. Dined &amp; spent the evening at home.</p>","pageId":722,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":397,"lock":null}
