20:13:22.036 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":479,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of cold weather with showers of snow &amp; wind NNW. Although a heavy swell upon the bar &amp; occasionally breaking, several ships got to sea. Dined at home. In the evening at the Jarvis's with Bell.</p>","pageId":729,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":461,"lock":null}
20:13:22.036 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/48
20:13:22.036 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":48,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":2,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Exceedingly cold weather &amp; frosty. Wind variable between SE &amp; SSW. Dined at home &amp; at a party at Mrs Recds in evening. Sent to William their promissory notes at 12.18 &amp; 24 months to Messrs Lees for &pound;400, 400 &amp; 450 dated  11 feb 1828</p>","pageId":690,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":45,"lock":null}
20:13:22.036 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.036 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/48
20:13:22.036 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":48,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":2,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Exceedingly cold weather &amp; frosty. Wind variable between SE &amp; SSW. Dined at home &amp; at a party at Mrs Recds in evening. Sent to William their promissory notes at 12.18 &amp; 24 months to Messrs Lees for &pound;400, 400 &amp; 450 dated  11 feb 1828</p>","pageId":690,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":45,"lock":null}
20:13:22.036 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/480
20:13:22.036 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":480,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A clear frosty morning. Wind NW. received a letter from William of the sale of the Hope at 38/6  8/3 for <span class=highlight_yellow>Town by</span> = to <span class=highlight_yellow>7</span> freight <span class=highlight_yellow>eneserable</span> work. Dined at home. Slept all night with Bell Jervis at her sisters.</p>","pageId":729,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":462,"lock":null}
20:13:22.036 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.036 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/480
20:13:22.036 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":480,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A clear frosty morning. Wind NW. received a letter from William of the sale of the Hope at 38/6  8/3 for <span class=highlight_yellow>Town by</span> = to <span class=highlight_yellow>7</span> freight <span class=highlight_yellow>eneserable</span> work. Dined at home. Slept all night with Bell Jervis at her sisters.</p>","pageId":729,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":462,"lock":null}
20:13:22.036 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/481
20:13:22.036 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":481,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful mild morning. Wind WNW. Got home to breakfast after sleeping with Bell Jarvis. The wind in the afternoon changed to SE. Several ships sailed for America &amp; the Baltic. The XYZ <span class=highlight_yellow>Ld</span><span class=highlight_yellow> the soles run</span>.  Dined with J Tinley, Ian Carr married to Sam Barton &amp; got home this morning attended the whist club at H Dales.</p>","pageId":729,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":463,"lock":null}
20:13:22.036 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.037 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/481
20:13:22.037 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":481,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful mild morning. Wind WNW. Got home to breakfast after sleeping with Bell Jarvis. The wind in the afternoon changed to SE. Several ships sailed for America &amp; the Baltic. The XYZ <span class=highlight_yellow>Ld</span><span class=highlight_yellow> the soles run</span>.  Dined with J Tinley, Ian Carr married to Sam Barton &amp; got home this morning attended the whist club at H Dales.</p>","pageId":729,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":463,"lock":null}
20:13:22.037 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/482
20:13:22.037 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":482,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp morning wind SSE. Turned out very wet. Wrote to William. Wind changed in the afternoon to SE. Found myself very queer this morning in consequence of late hours &amp; last night at the Dales. Stayed in the house all day. In the evening at the newsroom &amp; called at the Mulstrum &amp; gave Bennett a <span class=highlight_yellow>turn</span>.</p>","pageId":729,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":464,"lock":null}
20:13:22.037 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.037 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/482
20:13:22.037 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":482,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp morning wind SSE. Turned out very wet. Wrote to William. Wind changed in the afternoon to SE. Found myself very queer this morning in consequence of late hours &amp; last night at the Dales. Stayed in the house all day. In the evening at the newsroom &amp; called at the Mulstrum &amp; gave Bennett a <span class=highlight_yellow>turn</span>.</p>","pageId":729,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":464,"lock":null}
20:13:22.037 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/483
20:13:22.037 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":483,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull wet morning. Wind E. Engaged in the house reading until 12 o'clock. Called upon J Hearn about his bell for the Hope, but he was not at the sail-loft. Dined at home.</p>","pageId":729,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":465,"lock":null}
20:13:22.037 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.038 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/483
20:13:22.038 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":483,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull wet morning. Wind E. Engaged in the house reading until 12 o'clock. Called upon J Hearn about his bell for the Hope, but he was not at the sail-loft. Dined at home.</p>","pageId":729,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":465,"lock":null}
20:13:22.038 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/484
20:13:22.038 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":484,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet morning. Wind East &amp; been much rain during the night. Dined with ben Wright &amp; a party <span class=highlight_yellow>ra</span><span class=highlight_yellow> bard</span>. Then Stephen &amp; spent a very pleasant evening.</p>","pageId":729,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":466,"lock":null}
20:13:22.038 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.038 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/484
20:13:22.038 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":484,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet morning. Wind East &amp; been much rain during the night. Dined with ben Wright &amp; a party <span class=highlight_yellow>ra</span><span class=highlight_yellow> bard</span>. Then Stephen &amp; spent a very pleasant evening.</p>","pageId":729,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":466,"lock":null}
20:13:22.038 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/485
20:13:22.038 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":485,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull thick morning &amp; turned out wet. Wind NW. Heard from Mr Stephenson the Hope was out on Monday &amp; going to take in dung. Dined at home.</p>","pageId":729,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":467,"lock":null}
20:13:22.038 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.039 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/485
20:13:22.039 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":485,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull thick morning &amp; turned out wet. Wind NW. Heard from Mr Stephenson the Hope was out on Monday &amp; going to take in dung. Dined at home.</p>","pageId":729,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":467,"lock":null}
20:13:22.039 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/486
20:13:22.039 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":486,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind S by E &amp; heavy sea upon the bar. Bowies Brittania arrived in the harbour this morning without the Captain Mr W Bowie on board. Supposed to have jumped out of the cabin window when off the bar. Dined at home. Mrs Dixon joined me &amp; returned home in the evening.</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":468,"lock":null}
20:13:22.039 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.040 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/486
20:13:22.040 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":486,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind S by E &amp; heavy sea upon the bar. Bowies Brittania arrived in the harbour this morning without the Captain Mr W Bowie on board. Supposed to have jumped out of the cabin window when off the bar. Dined at home. Mrs Dixon joined me &amp; returned home in the evening.</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":468,"lock":null}
20:13:22.040 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/487
20:13:22.040 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":487,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Weather moderating and fair having been very strong all night. Wind about E by S. Several ships arrived this morning. Among them the Hope having left London on Tuesday. A schooner loaded with grain got upon the hard Sand, the sea higher than has been this winter. Went to Newcastle &amp; fixed the Hope to load <span class=highlight_yellow>Townty</span><span class=highlight_yellow> main</span> again the price <span class=highlight_yellow>20/ chat</span> &amp; to be applied 8/6 freight. Returned by steam to dinner. Wind changed to SW &amp; then to SE.</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":469,"lock":null}
20:13:22.040 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.040 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/487
20:13:22.040 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":487,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Weather moderating and fair having been very strong all night. Wind about E by S. Several ships arrived this morning. Among them the Hope having left London on Tuesday. A schooner loaded with grain got upon the hard Sand, the sea higher than has been this winter. Went to Newcastle &amp; fixed the Hope to load <span class=highlight_yellow>Townty</span><span class=highlight_yellow> main</span> again the price <span class=highlight_yellow>20/ chat</span> &amp; to be applied 8/6 freight. Returned by steam to dinner. Wind changed to SW &amp; then to SE.</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":469,"lock":null}
20:13:22.040 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/488
20:13:22.040 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":488,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fair morning. Wind WNW. About 11 o'clock began to rain. Drew &pound;40 out of Chapmans to pay wages &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>hadesmens</span> bells for the Hope. Mr Mark <span class=highlight_yellow>sit </span>took our dinner on board. Wind got to ESE again. Attended the whist club at R Pearts. Wrote to William.</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":470,"lock":null}
20:13:22.040 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.040 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/488
20:13:22.041 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":488,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fair morning. Wind WNW. About 11 o'clock began to rain. Drew &pound;40 out of Chapmans to pay wages &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>hadesmens</span> bells for the Hope. Mr Mark <span class=highlight_yellow>sit </span>took our dinner on board. Wind got to ESE again. Attended the whist club at R Pearts. Wrote to William.</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":470,"lock":null}
20:13:22.041 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/489
20:13:22.041 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":489,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet morning. Wind SSE. Received a letter from William <span class=highlight_yellow>weth</span> the Hope. Balance note $40.11/- &amp; &pound;50 lent = &pound;90.11. Went to church. Dined with J Tinley. Mr &amp; Mrs Carr &amp; Jane Kelsoe there.</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":471,"lock":null}
20:13:22.041 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.041 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/489
20:13:22.041 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":489,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet morning. Wind SSE. Received a letter from William <span class=highlight_yellow>weth</span> the Hope. Balance note $40.11/- &amp; &pound;50 lent = &pound;90.11. Went to church. Dined with J Tinley. Mr &amp; Mrs Carr &amp; Jane Kelsoe there.</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":471,"lock":null}
20:13:22.041 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/49
20:13:22.041 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":49,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":2,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A tremendously heavy storm &amp; fall of snow all day &amp; wind SE. Mr Smith &amp; Fanny unexpectedly arrived some busy body having sent a &quot;message&quot; to Togston in my name, that Mrs Scott was not expected to live more than two or three days. Dined at home &amp; at whist club in the evening</p>","pageId":690,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":46,"lock":null}
20:13:22.041 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.041 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/49
20:13:22.041 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":49,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":2,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A tremendously heavy storm &amp; fall of snow all day &amp; wind SE. Mr Smith &amp; Fanny unexpectedly arrived some busy body having sent a &quot;message&quot; to Togston in my name, that Mrs Scott was not expected to live more than two or three days. Dined at home &amp; at whist club in the evening</p>","pageId":690,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":46,"lock":null}
20:13:22.041 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/490
20:13:22.041 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":490,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Rather a dull morning. Wind blowing fresh from SW &amp; W. Several ships sailed for America but no loaded vessels got out. A heavy sea being upon the bar. Moved the Hope from the crane to a tees in South Shields. The river on the north side being so crowded Dined at home. Joined a party on board the Harmony. <span class=highlight_yellow>Mr</span> Peark in the evening. With Bell Jarvis. Paid into Chapmans. The bill for &pound;90.10/-</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":472,"lock":null}
20:13:22.041 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.042 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/490
20:13:22.042 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":490,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Rather a dull morning. Wind blowing fresh from SW &amp; W. Several ships sailed for America but no loaded vessels got out. A heavy sea being upon the bar. Moved the Hope from the crane to a tees in South Shields. The river on the north side being so crowded Dined at home. Joined a party on board the Harmony. <span class=highlight_yellow>Mr</span> Peark in the evening. With Bell Jarvis. Paid into Chapmans. The bill for &pound;90.10/-</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":472,"lock":null}
20:13:22.042 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/491
20:13:22.042 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":491,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning &amp; blowing fresh from the SW. On board of ship Mr Allen &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Mary</span> &amp; Bell Jarvis. Danced on board with me. Drew a draft for self for &pound;15 &amp; paid into the account of Exors &pound;20. Paid Mr Lough an <span class=highlight_yellow>average</span> for Hope Club &pound;19.2.1. In the evening the wind changed to SSE blowing hard all night with rain.</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":473,"lock":null}
20:13:22.042 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.042 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/491
20:13:22.042 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":491,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning &amp; blowing fresh from the SW. On board of ship Mr Allen &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Mary</span> &amp; Bell Jarvis. Danced on board with me. Drew a draft for self for &pound;15 &amp; paid into the account of Exors &pound;20. Paid Mr Lough an <span class=highlight_yellow>average</span> for Hope Club &pound;19.2.1. In the evening the wind changed to SSE blowing hard all night with rain.</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":473,"lock":null}
20:13:22.042 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/492
20:13:22.042 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":492,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>This morning dry weather but <span class=highlight_yellow>still</span> blowing hard all night &amp; still continuing from SSE &amp; S by E. The Hope moved down to a tier below the library to load up. Dined at home. Wrote the secretary of the Hope Club to reduce the value of the Hope to &pound;1600.</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":474,"lock":null}
20:13:22.042 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.043 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/492
20:13:22.043 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":492,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>This morning dry weather but <span class=highlight_yellow>still</span> blowing hard all night &amp; still continuing from SSE &amp; S by E. The Hope moved down to a tier below the library to load up. Dined at home. Wrote the secretary of the Hope Club to reduce the value of the Hope to &pound;1600.</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":474,"lock":null}
20:13:22.043 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/493
20:13:22.043 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":493,"version":1,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A&nbsp;very&nbsp;wet&nbsp;morning.&nbsp;Wind&nbsp;SW.&nbsp;On&nbsp;board&nbsp;the&nbsp;Hope.&nbsp;She&nbsp;got&nbsp;two&nbsp;keels&nbsp;down&nbsp;today&nbsp;making&nbsp;15.&nbsp;Dined&nbsp;on&nbsp;board.&nbsp;Dr&nbsp;Drewery&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;W&nbsp;Peart&nbsp;with&nbsp;me.&nbsp;A&nbsp;great&nbsp;many&nbsp;ships&nbsp;got&nbsp;to&nbsp;sea&nbsp;this&nbsp;afternoon.&nbsp;The&nbsp;wind&nbsp;changed&nbsp;to&nbsp;S&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;S&nbsp;by&nbsp;E.&nbsp;Poor&nbsp;R&nbsp;Brown&nbsp;died&nbsp;today.&nbsp;A&nbsp;serious&nbsp;loss&nbsp;to&nbsp;his&nbsp;family.&nbsp;</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":475,"lock":null}
20:13:22.043 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.043 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/493
20:13:22.043 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":493,"version":1,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A&nbsp;very&nbsp;wet&nbsp;morning.&nbsp;Wind&nbsp;SW.&nbsp;On&nbsp;board&nbsp;the&nbsp;Hope.&nbsp;She&nbsp;got&nbsp;two&nbsp;keels&nbsp;down&nbsp;today&nbsp;making&nbsp;15.&nbsp;Dined&nbsp;on&nbsp;board.&nbsp;Dr&nbsp;Drewery&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;W&nbsp;Peart&nbsp;with&nbsp;me.&nbsp;A&nbsp;great&nbsp;many&nbsp;ships&nbsp;got&nbsp;to&nbsp;sea&nbsp;this&nbsp;afternoon.&nbsp;The&nbsp;wind&nbsp;changed&nbsp;to&nbsp;S&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;S&nbsp;by&nbsp;E.&nbsp;Poor&nbsp;R&nbsp;Brown&nbsp;died&nbsp;today.&nbsp;A&nbsp;serious&nbsp;loss&nbsp;to&nbsp;his&nbsp;family.&nbsp;</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":475,"lock":null}
20:13:22.043 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/494
20:13:22.043 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":494,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Good Friday. A most beautiful morning. Wind NW. Did not go to church in consequence of poor Robert Brown's death. On board the Hope. She got the remainder of her coals down &amp; sailed this afternoon. Towed out by a steam boat, the wind being from the SSE. Dined at home &amp; afterwards went with H Harry to Mr Sadlers at Whittle Point to take wine in the evening at <span class=highlight_yellow>Nancy</span> Jervis</p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":476,"lock":null}
20:13:22.043 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.043 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/494
20:13:22.044 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":494,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Good Friday. A most beautiful morning. Wind NW. Did not go to church in consequence of poor Robert Brown's death. On board the Hope. She got the remainder of her coals down &amp; sailed this afternoon. Towed out by a steam boat, the wind being from the SSE. Dined at home &amp; afterwards went with H Harry to Mr Sadlers at Whittle Point to take wine in the evening at <span class=highlight_yellow>Nancy</span> Jervis</p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":476,"lock":null}
20:13:22.044 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/495
20:13:22.044 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":495,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, but has been rain early. Wind WNW. Paid the pilot of the Hope &pound;1.15/. Paid <span class=highlight_yellow>Twi</span><span class=highlight_yellow>g</span><span class=highlight_yellow>el</span><span class=highlight_yellow> </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Bragier</span> for the Hope &pound;12.13/-. Call upon &amp; saw about Richard's funeral. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home. In the evening suppered at the Albion upon some oysters, given by A Cunningham. <span class=highlight_lime>With Ann!!!!!!</span></p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":477,"lock":null}
20:13:22.044 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.044 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/495
20:13:22.044 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":495,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, but has been rain early. Wind WNW. Paid the pilot of the Hope &pound;1.15/. Paid <span class=highlight_yellow>Twi</span><span class=highlight_yellow>g</span><span class=highlight_yellow>el</span><span class=highlight_yellow> </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Bragier</span> for the Hope &pound;12.13/-. Call upon &amp; saw about Richard's funeral. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home. In the evening suppered at the Albion upon some oysters, given by A Cunningham. <span class=highlight_lime>With Ann!!!!!!</span></p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":477,"lock":null}
20:13:22.044 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/496
20:13:22.044 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":496,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A wet morning. Wind NW. Signed the Hope's cargo bill &pound;166.5.1 &amp; returned it to Geo Dunn&amp; Sons. Continued raining heavily until 4 o'clock when it cleared up. Dined at home. With Bell Jervis in the evening. Turned out a very rainy night.</p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":478,"lock":null}
20:13:22.044 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.044 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/496
20:13:22.044 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":496,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A wet morning. Wind NW. Signed the Hope's cargo bill &pound;166.5.1 &amp; returned it to Geo Dunn&amp; Sons. Continued raining heavily until 4 o'clock when it cleared up. Dined at home. With Bell Jervis in the evening. Turned out a very rainy night.</p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":478,"lock":null}
20:13:22.044 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/497
20:13:22.044 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":497,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather. Wind about N by E. Turned out a most beautiful &amp; warm day &amp; favourable for Tynemouth Races. Immense number of people out. Dined at home</p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":479,"lock":null}
20:13:22.044 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.045 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/497
20:13:22.045 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":497,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather. Wind about N by E. Turned out a most beautiful &amp; warm day &amp; favourable for Tynemouth Races. Immense number of people out. Dined at home</p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":479,"lock":null}
20:13:22.045 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/498
20:13:22.045 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":498,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Rather a dull morning. Wind SSE. Dixon &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Befry</span> came down from Beaton &amp; the foreman &amp; I attended the remains of poor Rich Brown to the grave with his three youngest boys. I returned with them to dine &amp; stay all night at Benton.</p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":480,"lock":null}
20:13:22.045 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.045 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/498
20:13:22.045 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":498,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Rather a dull morning. Wind SSE. Dixon &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Befry</span> came down from Beaton &amp; the foreman &amp; I attended the remains of poor Rich Brown to the grave with his three youngest boys. I returned with them to dine &amp; stay all night at Benton.</p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":480,"lock":null}
20:13:22.045 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/499
20:13:22.045 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":499,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold morning with a dry easterly wind. Walked down to Shields. Dined at homer &amp; afterwards went to Tynemouth races, very few people there &amp; not worth going to. Drank tea with Mr Tibbs. With Bell Jarvis in the evening</p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":481,"lock":null}
20:13:22.045 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.045 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/499
20:13:22.045 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":499,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold morning with a dry easterly wind. Walked down to Shields. Dined at homer &amp; afterwards went to Tynemouth races, very few people there &amp; not worth going to. Drank tea with Mr Tibbs. With Bell Jarvis in the evening</p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":481,"lock":null}
20:13:22.046 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/5
20:13:22.046 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":5,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":1,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... as every man must do, who keeps there grand maxim in view &quot;Do onto others as you would they should do unto you&quot;, he who attends to this well , never get far wrong &amp; thank god so far I feel I can apply the quotation &quot;mens conscia recti&quot; to myself indeed . I am made to feel it by the kind &amp; friendly manner in which every person receive me I hope I deserve it, I do not know that I ever did an injury to anyone certain never intentionally.</p>\r\n<p>However there is one person whose conduct has indeed been that of a friend &amp; such a friend as seldom is met with &amp; I cannot omit recording it here &amp; were I ever to forget it should indeed be ungrateful &amp; unworthy of every kind feeling. John Tinley is the man who could feel for the misfortunes of another. He it was who paved the way for our emancipation from all difficulties. Where is the friend that would have acted as he did? I fear not to be found. He came forward not a friend in words but in deeds. He made not promises, nor exacted hopes &amp; expectations, to disappoint &amp; blast them when called upon. He saw our situation, he volunteered his services as security, without which we could have effected nothing &amp; thus has the primary cause of our accomplishing all that has been done. He thought he knew us &amp; I hope has not been deceived. This is what I call friendship, true &amp; sincere, not according to the worldly acceptation &amp; profanation of the word, but friendship in the true spirit &amp; meaning of the word.</p>\r\n<p>I yesterday, the last day of the old year, dined with this my excellent friend &amp; accompanied him Miss Barton A party to the ball &amp; spent a very pleasant evening &amp; thus ended the old &amp; began the new year merrily. I hope it is a good omen. Today I again dined with J Tinley to meet Mr Waldie to a very agreeable party.</p>","pageId":686,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2,"lock":null}
20:13:22.046 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.046 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/5
20:13:22.046 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":5,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":1,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... as every man must do, who keeps there grand maxim in view &quot;Do onto others as you would they should do unto you&quot;, he who attends to this well , never get far wrong &amp; thank god so far I feel I can apply the quotation &quot;mens conscia recti&quot; to myself indeed . I am made to feel it by the kind &amp; friendly manner in which every person receive me I hope I deserve it, I do not know that I ever did an injury to anyone certain never intentionally.</p>\r\n<p>However there is one person whose conduct has indeed been that of a friend &amp; such a friend as seldom is met with &amp; I cannot omit recording it here &amp; were I ever to forget it should indeed be ungrateful &amp; unworthy of every kind feeling. John Tinley is the man who could feel for the misfortunes of another. He it was who paved the way for our emancipation from all difficulties. Where is the friend that would have acted as he did? I fear not to be found. He came forward not a friend in words but in deeds. He made not promises, nor exacted hopes &amp; expectations, to disappoint &amp; blast them when called upon. He saw our situation, he volunteered his services as security, without which we could have effected nothing &amp; thus has the primary cause of our accomplishing all that has been done. He thought he knew us &amp; I hope has not been deceived. This is what I call friendship, true &amp; sincere, not according to the worldly acceptation &amp; profanation of the word, but friendship in the true spirit &amp; meaning of the word.</p>\r\n<p>I yesterday, the last day of the old year, dined with this my excellent friend &amp; accompanied him Miss Barton A party to the ball &amp; spent a very pleasant evening &amp; thus ended the old &amp; began the new year merrily. I hope it is a good omen. Today I again dined with J Tinley to meet Mr Waldie to a very agreeable party.</p>","pageId":686,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2,"lock":null}
20:13:22.046 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/50
20:13:22.046 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":50,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":2,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>The weather changed, a fine mild day &amp; rapid thaw wind W to NW. Dined at Mr Wrights. Several ships sailed</p>","pageId":690,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":47,"lock":null}
20:13:22.046 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.046 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/50
20:13:22.046 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":50,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":2,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>The weather changed, a fine mild day &amp; rapid thaw wind W to NW. Dined at Mr Wrights. Several ships sailed</p>","pageId":690,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":47,"lock":null}
20:13:22.046 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/500
20:13:22.046 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":500,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another cold morning. Wind easterly. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined with J Tinley. In the evening called upon Mr J Young &amp; had a long conversation both with him about taking our dividend without surveying. Also he did not seem so determined in his opposition. He desired me to see H Dale &amp; talk to him.</p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":482,"lock":null}
20:13:22.046 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.047 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/500
20:13:22.047 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":500,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another cold morning. Wind easterly. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined with J Tinley. In the evening called upon Mr J Young &amp; had a long conversation both with him about taking our dividend without surveying. Also he did not seem so determined in his opposition. He desired me to see H Dale &amp; talk to him.</p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":482,"lock":null}
20:13:22.047 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/501
20:13:22.047 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":501,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of cold weather &amp; ENE wind. Dined at home &amp; afterwards went with H Harry &amp; R Peart &amp; drank whisky on board the Ardineaple  steamer Captain Cunningham. On our return when the boat reached the shore, Cunningham stumbled &amp; falling upon me, we both rolled overboard. Got a good dunking. Wrote to Mrs Scott of my determination not to make her an allowance.</p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":483,"lock":null}
20:13:22.047 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.047 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/501
20:13:22.047 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":501,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of cold weather &amp; ENE wind. Dined at home &amp; afterwards went with H Harry &amp; R Peart &amp; drank whisky on board the Ardineaple  steamer Captain Cunningham. On our return when the boat reached the shore, Cunningham stumbled &amp; falling upon me, we both rolled overboard. Got a good dunking. Wrote to Mrs Scott of my determination not to make her an allowance.</p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":483,"lock":null}
20:13:22.047 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/502
20:13:22.047 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":502,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning but still cool &amp; wind NE &amp; ENE. Walked with H Harry to Tynemouth. Dined at home. Received a letter from William of the arrival &amp; sale of the Hope on Wednesday at 27/- = to 6/6 freight. This well I'm <span class=highlight_yellow>upheld</span> 8/6. Answered the letter desiring him to tender the Hope to the Gafs Co. to carry coal at &pound;9 a keel or 21/6 freight Newcastle <span class=highlight_yellow>cha</span>. Attended the whist club at Tibbs. Got &pound;5 of Chapman. <span class=highlight_yellow>Paid</span> steam boat for Hope 30/- <span class=highlight_yellow>aformenbec</span> 20/- washing 31/6</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":484,"lock":null}
20:13:22.047 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.048 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/502
20:13:22.048 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":502,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning but still cool &amp; wind NE &amp; ENE. Walked with H Harry to Tynemouth. Dined at home. Received a letter from William of the arrival &amp; sale of the Hope on Wednesday at 27/- = to 6/6 freight. This well I'm <span class=highlight_yellow>upheld</span> 8/6. Answered the letter desiring him to tender the Hope to the Gafs Co. to carry coal at &pound;9 a keel or 21/6 freight Newcastle <span class=highlight_yellow>cha</span>. Attended the whist club at Tibbs. Got &pound;5 of Chapman. <span class=highlight_yellow>Paid</span> steam boat for Hope 30/- <span class=highlight_yellow>aformenbec</span> 20/- washing 31/6</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":484,"lock":null}
20:13:22.048 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/503
20:13:22.048 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":503,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Quite summer weather. Wind S &amp; changed before 12 o'clock to SE. Attended morning service. Dined at home at 2 o'clock &amp; afterwards walked to Tynemouth with H Harry. On our return had a bottle of port at the George. With Bell Jarvis in the evening.</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":485,"lock":null}
20:13:22.048 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.049 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/503
20:13:22.049 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":503,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Quite summer weather. Wind S &amp; changed before 12 o'clock to SE. Attended morning service. Dined at home at 2 o'clock &amp; afterwards walked to Tynemouth with H Harry. On our return had a bottle of port at the George. With Bell Jarvis in the evening.</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":485,"lock":null}
20:13:22.049 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/504
20:13:22.049 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":504,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A showery morning. Wind N by W. In the house all the morning. Mrs Dixon brought Emma down again. Dined at house. In the evening went up to the castle &amp; played a rubber at Dacres rooms.  With rum I think!!!</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":486,"lock":null}
20:13:22.049 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.049 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/504
20:13:22.049 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":504,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A showery morning. Wind N by W. In the house all the morning. Mrs Dixon brought Emma down again. Dined at house. In the evening went up to the castle &amp; played a rubber at Dacres rooms.  With rum I think!!!</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":486,"lock":null}
20:13:22.049 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/505
20:13:22.049 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":505,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A showery morning &amp; blowing fresh from the N &amp; W by N and increased to a very heavy gale of wind varying between NNW and NNE which brought on a tremendous sea, a small sloop in coming in got upon the Heard Sand. Dined at home.</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":487,"lock":null}
20:13:22.049 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.049 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/505
20:13:22.049 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":505,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A showery morning &amp; blowing fresh from the N &amp; W by N and increased to a very heavy gale of wind varying between NNW and NNE which brought on a tremendous sea, a small sloop in coming in got upon the Heard Sand. Dined at home.</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":487,"lock":null}
20:13:22.049 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/506
20:13:22.049 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":506,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>The gale has continued all night with showers of snow with a tremendous sea. Wind continues the same as yesterday. The gales abated towards evening. Dined at home. In the evening with Bell Jarvis</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":488,"lock":null}
20:13:22.049 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.050 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/506
20:13:22.050 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":506,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>The gale has continued all night with showers of snow with a tremendous sea. Wind continues the same as yesterday. The gales abated towards evening. Dined at home. In the evening with Bell Jarvis</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":488,"lock":null}
20:13:22.050 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/507
20:13:22.050 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":507,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; again calm Weather. Wind NW by N. Went to Newcastle by steamer to dine with Mr R <span class=highlight_yellow>Arsey</span> in Eldon Square. Spent a very pleasant day &amp; returned to Shields. In the evening took Mr Dacres <font color=#BFBFBF>&amp;</font><font color=#BFBFBF> </font><span class=highlight_yellow>RA</span> with me. Tom Smith &amp; his mother arrived at Dockwray Square today.</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":489,"lock":null}
20:13:22.050 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.050 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/507
20:13:22.050 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":507,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; again calm Weather. Wind NW by N. Went to Newcastle by steamer to dine with Mr R <span class=highlight_yellow>Arsey</span> in Eldon Square. Spent a very pleasant day &amp; returned to Shields. In the evening took Mr Dacres <font color=#BFBFBF>&amp;</font><font color=#BFBFBF> </font><span class=highlight_yellow>RA</span> with me. Tom Smith &amp; his mother arrived at Dockwray Square today.</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":489,"lock":null}
20:13:22.050 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/508
20:13:22.050 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":508,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW walked about the town with Tom Smith the principle part of the morning. Dined at home &amp; took a walk to Tynemouth after dinner. Accepted <span class=highlight_yellow>In</span> Hearn's bill for &pound;34.7/- at 3 <span class=highlight_yellow>mo</span><span class=highlight_yellow>nth</span><span class=highlight_yellow>s</span> dated 27 April, due 30 July, for repairing Hope's sails. A most extraordinary bill.</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":490,"lock":null}
20:13:22.050 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.051 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/508
20:13:22.051 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":508,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW walked about the town with Tom Smith the principle part of the morning. Dined at home &amp; took a walk to Tynemouth after dinner. Accepted <span class=highlight_yellow>In</span> Hearn's bill for &pound;34.7/- at 3 <span class=highlight_yellow>mo</span><span class=highlight_yellow>nth</span><span class=highlight_yellow>s</span> dated 27 April, due 30 July, for repairing Hope's sails. A most extraordinary bill.</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":490,"lock":null}
20:13:22.051 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/509
20:13:22.051 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":509,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning blowing rather fresh from NW by W. Walked with Tom Smith down to Low Town &amp; afterwards to Alec Sadlers at Whitle Point. Dined at home &amp; after tea again walked to Whitle Point but the sloop had not come down.</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":491,"lock":null}
20:13:22.051 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.051 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/509
20:13:22.051 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":509,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning blowing rather fresh from NW by W. Walked with Tom Smith down to Low Town &amp; afterwards to Alec Sadlers at Whitle Point. Dined at home &amp; after tea again walked to Whitle Point but the sloop had not come down.</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":491,"lock":null}
20:13:22.051 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/51
20:13:22.051 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":51,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":2,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day &amp; a little frost in the air. Wind WNW. A few ships sailed. Dined at home. A letter from William &amp; answered</p>","pageId":690,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":48,"lock":null}
20:13:22.051 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.051 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/51
20:13:22.051 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":51,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":2,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day &amp; a little frost in the air. Wind WNW. A few ships sailed. Dined at home. A letter from William &amp; answered</p>","pageId":690,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":48,"lock":null}
20:13:22.051 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/510
20:13:22.051 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":510,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild morning after a few showers of rain during the night. Wind W by S. Tom Smith, Emma &amp; I went to church &amp; after <font color=#BFBFBF>[the] </font>service, Tom &amp; I walked up through the country to Benton, dined &amp; stayed all night. A very windy day &amp; unpleasant walking.</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":492,"lock":null}
20:13:22.051 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.052 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/510
20:13:22.052 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":510,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild morning after a few showers of rain during the night. Wind W by S. Tom Smith, Emma &amp; I went to church &amp; after <font color=#BFBFBF>[the] </font>service, Tom &amp; I walked up through the country to Benton, dined &amp; stayed all night. A very windy day &amp; unpleasant walking.</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":492,"lock":null}
20:13:22.052 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/511
20:13:22.052 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":511,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning. But still blowing hard from the NW. Amused ourselves for a short time in the plantations with the beagles. Mrs Dixon took us into Newcastle in the carriage. Tom Smith transacted his business there &amp; we afterwards walked down to St Anthon's to see a sloop he had purchased for his colliery. Returned to Shields by steam to dinner.</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":493,"lock":null}
20:13:22.052 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.052 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/511
20:13:22.052 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":511,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning. But still blowing hard from the NW. Amused ourselves for a short time in the plantations with the beagles. Mrs Dixon took us into Newcastle in the carriage. Tom Smith transacted his business there &amp; we afterwards walked down to St Anthon's to see a sloop he had purchased for his colliery. Returned to Shields by steam to dinner.</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":493,"lock":null}
20:13:22.052 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/512
20:13:22.052 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":512,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine spring morning with showers. Wind SSW. Several light ships arrived. Tom &amp; Mrs Smith left us this morning for Benton. Dined at home. Accepted a bill at 3 <span class=highlight_yellow>months</span> dated 16 April for polices &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Insurance</span> 1 &amp; 2 coal voyages in general Premium Club &pound;13.7.10. With Bell Jervis in the evening</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":494,"lock":null}
20:13:22.052 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.052 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/512
20:13:22.052 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":512,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine spring morning with showers. Wind SSW. Several light ships arrived. Tom &amp; Mrs Smith left us this morning for Benton. Dined at home. Accepted a bill at 3 <span class=highlight_yellow>months</span> dated 16 April for polices &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Insurance</span> 1 &amp; 2 coal voyages in general Premium Club &pound;13.7.10. With Bell Jervis in the evening</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":494,"lock":null}
20:13:22.053 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/513
20:13:22.053 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":513,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind SW. Called upon &amp; spent an hour with Fergusson the artist. Dined at home. Afterwards walked to Tynemouth with Fergusson to sketch the ruins. In the evening at <span class=highlight_yellow>Davies</span> Rooms at the Castle</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":495,"lock":null}
20:13:22.053 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.053 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/513
20:13:22.053 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":513,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind SW. Called upon &amp; spent an hour with Fergusson the artist. Dined at home. Afterwards walked to Tynemouth with Fergusson to sketch the ruins. In the evening at <span class=highlight_yellow>Davies</span> Rooms at the Castle</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":495,"lock":null}
20:13:22.053 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/514
20:13:22.053 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":514,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant spring morning. Wind NNW. Changed during the day to NE &amp; again at night to W. Took a walk round by Cullercoat Fields &amp; Tynemouth. A beautiful summers day. Dined with Jackson 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment at the Castle. H Dale, Dacres, RA. Newton &amp; a Lieutenant Hamilton Brown there. (with 1<sup>st</sup> term)</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":496,"lock":null}
20:13:22.053 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.053 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/514
20:13:22.053 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":514,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant spring morning. Wind NNW. Changed during the day to NE &amp; again at night to W. Took a walk round by Cullercoat Fields &amp; Tynemouth. A beautiful summers day. Dined with Jackson 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment at the Castle. H Dale, Dacres, RA. Newton &amp; a Lieutenant Hamilton Brown there. (with 1<sup>st</sup> term)</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":496,"lock":null}
20:13:22.053 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/515
20:13:22.053 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":515,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A wet morning . A fine mild rain. Wind W by N. Called upon Fergusson Dined at home. The Hope arrived this evening after a fine passage. Left Gravesend on Wednesday morning.</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":497,"lock":null}
20:13:22.053 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.054 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/515
20:13:22.054 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":515,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A wet morning . A fine mild rain. Wind W by N. Called upon Fergusson Dined at home. The Hope arrived this evening after a fine passage. Left Gravesend on Wednesday morning.</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":497,"lock":null}
20:13:22.054 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/516
20:13:22.054 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":516,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine spring morning. Some showers during the night. Warmer growing weather at last. Wind W by N. Mr Fergusson &amp; I went to Newcastle by steam on the quay, but could do nothing for the Hope. Called upon Inspector Hodgson &amp; dined with him at his brothers. Returned to Shields in the evening. With Bell Jarvis, remained with her until 4 o'clock in the morning. Received from Geo Dunn &amp; sons &pound;27 being the difference between the freight made &amp; that upheld <span class=highlight_yellow>=rig</span>: 8/6</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":498,"lock":null}
20:13:22.054 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.054 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/516
20:13:22.054 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":516,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine spring morning. Some showers during the night. Warmer growing weather at last. Wind W by N. Mr Fergusson &amp; I went to Newcastle by steam on the quay, but could do nothing for the Hope. Called upon Inspector Hodgson &amp; dined with him at his brothers. Returned to Shields in the evening. With Bell Jarvis, remained with her until 4 o'clock in the morning. Received from Geo Dunn &amp; sons &pound;27 being the difference between the freight made &amp; that upheld <span class=highlight_yellow>=rig</span>: 8/6</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":498,"lock":null}
20:13:22.054 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/517
20:13:22.054 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":517,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning &amp; summers weather SE. Went with Emma to church. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. Took wine with H Harry. Walked to Tynemouth in the  evening.</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":499,"lock":null}
20:13:22.054 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.055 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/517
20:13:22.055 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":517,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning &amp; summers weather SE. Went with Emma to church. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. Took wine with H Harry. Walked to Tynemouth in the  evening.</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":499,"lock":null}
20:13:22.055 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/518
20:13:22.055 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":518,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind ESE. Turned out a very fine day. Went to Newcastle by steam but did not fix the Hope. Returned home to dinner. Walked to Tynemouth in the evening. Paid the men their wages &amp; gave Stephenson a draft for &pound;45</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":500,"lock":null}
20:13:22.055 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
