20:13:22.057 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":520,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind SE. The Hope gone up to the spout this tide. Walked with Captain Webb up to the Hope &amp; dined on board</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":502,"lock":null}
20:13:22.057 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/521
20:13:22.057 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":521,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine day. Wind W by N. Changed to SW. Went by steam to Newcastle. Gave the fitter the Hope's monthly bill. Called upon J Hodgson &amp; returned to dinner. In the evening a little rain.</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":503,"lock":null}
20:13:22.057 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.058 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/521
20:13:22.058 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":521,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine day. Wind W by N. Changed to SW. Went by steam to Newcastle. Gave the fitter the Hope's monthly bill. Called upon J Hodgson &amp; returned to dinner. In the evening a little rain.</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":503,"lock":null}
20:13:22.058 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/522
20:13:22.058 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":522,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning but fine spring weather. Wind NE. Mr Mark, Mr Sadler &amp; I walked up to Cramlington Spout. Found the Hope hauling off &amp; she shortly after proceeded down the river having only taken in 14 keels. Dined with Mr Sadler. With Bell Jarvis in the evening.</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":504,"lock":null}
20:13:22.058 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.058 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/522
20:13:22.058 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":522,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning but fine spring weather. Wind NE. Mr Mark, Mr Sadler &amp; I walked up to Cramlington Spout. Found the Hope hauling off &amp; she shortly after proceeded down the river having only taken in 14 keels. Dined with Mr Sadler. With Bell Jarvis in the evening.</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":504,"lock":null}
20:13:22.058 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/523
20:13:22.058 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":523,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful summers morning. Wind ENE. Received a letter from William agreeing to offer Younger 10/- in the &pound;. Drew &pound;20 out of Chapman. &pound;15 for Stephenson &amp; &pound;5 for self. Drew &pound;5 more in the afternoon. Stephenson wanting &pound;20. Dined at home. In the evening called upon A Dale to propose to join Younger's 10/- in full. Dale <span class=highlight_yellow>sacfe</span> for Younger, who I afterwards found much to my relief of mind had agreed to our proposal. Spent the evening with Mr Allen. With Bell Jervis.</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":505,"lock":null}
20:13:22.058 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.058 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/523
20:13:22.058 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":523,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful summers morning. Wind ENE. Received a letter from William agreeing to offer Younger 10/- in the &pound;. Drew &pound;20 out of Chapman. &pound;15 for Stephenson &amp; &pound;5 for self. Drew &pound;5 more in the afternoon. Stephenson wanting &pound;20. Dined at home. In the evening called upon A Dale to propose to join Younger's 10/- in full. Dale <span class=highlight_yellow>sacfe</span> for Younger, who I afterwards found much to my relief of mind had agreed to our proposal. Spent the evening with Mr Allen. With Bell Jervis.</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":505,"lock":null}
20:13:22.058 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/524
20:13:22.059 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":524,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind SE. The Hope was loaded on Friday but we could not go to sea in consequence of Young business. Determined not to sail until the morning tide. Walked to Tynemouth with H Harry. Took a warm bath. Dined at home. H Harry &amp; Mr Dadler took wine with me. Wrote to William of my intention to sail ...</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":506,"lock":null}
20:13:22.059 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.059 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/524
20:13:22.059 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":524,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind SE. The Hope was loaded on Friday but we could not go to sea in consequence of Young business. Determined not to sail until the morning tide. Walked to Tynemouth with H Harry. Took a warm bath. Dined at home. H Harry &amp; Mr Dadler took wine with me. Wrote to William of my intention to sail ...</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":506,"lock":null}
20:13:22.059 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/525
20:13:22.059 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":525,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At 3 o'clock am got under way &amp; sailed from Shields with a westerly breeze &amp; fine weather. At 10 o'clock am becalmed off Sunderland, the wind having got round to SE. Between 1 &amp; 2 o'clock the breeze freshened a little but we made little way, being ebb tide. At 10 o'clock <span class=highlight_yellow>we</span> went to bed, the ship being abreast of the Tees</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":507,"lock":null}
20:13:22.059 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.059 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/525
20:13:22.059 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":525,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At 3 o'clock am got under way &amp; sailed from Shields with a westerly breeze &amp; fine weather. At 10 o'clock am becalmed off Sunderland, the wind having got round to SE. Between 1 &amp; 2 o'clock the breeze freshened a little but we made little way, being ebb tide. At 10 o'clock <span class=highlight_yellow>we</span> went to bed, the ship being abreast of the Tees</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":507,"lock":null}
20:13:22.059 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/526
20:13:22.059 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":526,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>has been blowing pretty fresh all night from the SE &amp; SSE. Got up at 8 o'clock am. The ship abreast of <span class=highlight_yellow>Hunt</span><span class=highlight_yellow>c</span><span class=highlight_yellow>li</span><span class=highlight_yellow>f</span><span class=highlight_yellow>f</span> Foot. The wind the same but moderate &amp; fine weather. Anne very unwell, but more frightened not having been at sea before. Towards evening wind very calm again. Turned in at 10 o'clock.  The ship in <span class=highlight_yellow>a very</span> little wind.</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":508,"lock":null}
20:13:22.059 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.060 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/526
20:13:22.060 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":526,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>has been blowing pretty fresh all night from the SE &amp; SSE. Got up at 8 o'clock am. The ship abreast of <span class=highlight_yellow>Hunt</span><span class=highlight_yellow>c</span><span class=highlight_yellow>li</span><span class=highlight_yellow>f</span><span class=highlight_yellow>f</span> Foot. The wind the same but moderate &amp; fine weather. Anne very unwell, but more frightened not having been at sea before. Towards evening wind very calm again. Turned in at 10 o'clock.  The ship in <span class=highlight_yellow>a very</span> little wind.</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":508,"lock":null}
20:13:22.060 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/527
20:13:22.060 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":527,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind NE. Turned out a 8 o'clock am. The ship off Robin Hoods but the ebb tide &amp; heavy SE swell setting against us drove us <span class=highlight_yellow>back</span> to Whitby. In the afternoon with the <span class=highlight_yellow>fload</span> a better breeze spring up &amp; set us ahead again &amp; 10 o'clock pm bed time, we were off Scarborough. A fine moonlit night.</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":509,"lock":null}
20:13:22.060 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.060 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/527
20:13:22.060 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":527,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind NE. Turned out a 8 o'clock am. The ship off Robin Hoods but the ebb tide &amp; heavy SE swell setting against us drove us <span class=highlight_yellow>back</span> to Whitby. In the afternoon with the <span class=highlight_yellow>fload</span> a better breeze spring up &amp; set us ahead again &amp; 10 o'clock pm bed time, we were off Scarborough. A fine moonlit night.</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":509,"lock":null}
20:13:22.060 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/528
20:13:22.060 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":528,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at 8 o'clock am been a fresh breeze all night from NE. Got round the Head at 5 o'clock am. A fine morning but rather dull. Had a good sun. About 9 o'clock Cromer. At 10 o'clock turned in being <span class=highlight_yellow>marhasborough</span>. Ann Stokes 1<sup>st</sup> <span class=highlight_yellow>time</span>.</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":510,"lock":null}
20:13:22.060 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.061 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/528
20:13:22.061 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":528,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at 8 o'clock am been a fresh breeze all night from NE. Got round the Head at 5 o'clock am. A fine morning but rather dull. Had a good sun. About 9 o'clock Cromer. At 10 o'clock turned in being <span class=highlight_yellow>marhasborough</span>. Ann Stokes 1<sup>st</sup> <span class=highlight_yellow>time</span>.</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":510,"lock":null}
20:13:22.061 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/529
20:13:22.061 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":529,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up at 8 o'clock am. Very thick weather, but a fine breeze at NE, then appeared to be off Yarmouth behind the sands. We ran until about 1 o'clock pm when we took in studding sails &amp; stood in for the land, which we made a little to the northward of Aldeburgh. The weather clearer from thence. We took our departure to run down <span class=highlight_yellow>raren</span> . About 4 o'clock it turned out a beautiful clear day. At 6 o'clock pm abreast of Orford. At 10 pm being dark, brought up abreast of the Hook of the middle. At a little after 12 o'clock went to bed. A fine moonlit night. With Ann Stokes again!!</p>","pageId":735,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":511,"lock":null}
20:13:22.061 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.061 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/529
20:13:22.061 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":529,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up at 8 o'clock am. Very thick weather, but a fine breeze at NE, then appeared to be off Yarmouth behind the sands. We ran until about 1 o'clock pm when we took in studding sails &amp; stood in for the land, which we made a little to the northward of Aldeburgh. The weather clearer from thence. We took our departure to run down <span class=highlight_yellow>raren</span> . About 4 o'clock it turned out a beautiful clear day. At 6 o'clock pm abreast of Orford. At 10 pm being dark, brought up abreast of the Hook of the middle. At a little after 12 o'clock went to bed. A fine moonlit night. With Ann Stokes again!!</p>","pageId":735,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":511,"lock":null}
20:13:22.061 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/53
20:13:22.061 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":53,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":2,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day and frosty, Wind WNW. Got the fore rigging over the mast head &amp; the main mast out &amp; found it much decayed both foot and head &amp; fear we shall be obliged to have a new one. Ordered a new bowsprit of Morton &amp; Thompson. Dined at home &amp; spent the evening with N Bird</p>","pageId":690,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":50,"lock":null}
20:13:22.061 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.061 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/53
20:13:22.061 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":53,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":2,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day and frosty, Wind WNW. Got the fore rigging over the mast head &amp; the main mast out &amp; found it much decayed both foot and head &amp; fear we shall be obliged to have a new one. Ordered a new bowsprit of Morton &amp; Thompson. Dined at home &amp; spent the evening with N Bird</p>","pageId":690,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":50,"lock":null}
20:13:22.061 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/530
20:13:22.061 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":530,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At 3 o'clock <font color=#BFBFBF>[in]</font> the morning they got the ship under way, with a light breeze from the NE. At 7 o'clock I got up &amp; went upon deck, past through a large fleet of light ships. At 8 o'clock got the flood with a little more wind. Again passed a great number of light ships. Between 5 &amp; 6 o'clock brought up a little blow Gravesend. The crew went to bed early. Ann &amp; I walked the deck until after 10 o'clock. Sat up until 12 o'clock. Went to bed to Ann</p>","pageId":735,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":512,"lock":null}
20:13:22.061 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.062 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/530
20:13:22.062 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":530,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At 3 o'clock <font color=#BFBFBF>[in]</font> the morning they got the ship under way, with a light breeze from the NE. At 7 o'clock I got up &amp; went upon deck, past through a large fleet of light ships. At 8 o'clock got the flood with a little more wind. Again passed a great number of light ships. Between 5 &amp; 6 o'clock brought up a little blow Gravesend. The crew went to bed early. Ann &amp; I walked the deck until after 10 o'clock. Sat up until 12 o'clock. Went to bed to Ann</p>","pageId":735,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":512,"lock":null}
20:13:22.062 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/531
20:13:22.062 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":531,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up about 7 o'clock. A most delightful morning. Wind unfortunately changed to W so that at the early morning tide, we could not move, There also being very little of it. After breakfast dressed myself &amp; landed at Gravesend about 11 o'clock, waited until <span class=highlight_yellow>about</span> 1 o'clock before I could get a coach. Got to town at 4 o'clock pm. Left the ships papers at the office &amp; got to Nottingham Place at &frac12; past 5 o'clock. Found them all well &amp; glad to see me. Bob Marsh &amp; his father dined with us. Heavy rain in the afternoon.</p>","pageId":735,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":513,"lock":null}
20:13:22.062 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.062 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/531
20:13:22.062 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":531,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up about 7 o'clock. A most delightful morning. Wind unfortunately changed to W so that at the early morning tide, we could not move, There also being very little of it. After breakfast dressed myself &amp; landed at Gravesend about 11 o'clock, waited until <span class=highlight_yellow>about</span> 1 o'clock before I could get a coach. Got to town at 4 o'clock pm. Left the ships papers at the office &amp; got to Nottingham Place at &frac12; past 5 o'clock. Found them all well &amp; glad to see me. Bob Marsh &amp; his father dined with us. Heavy rain in the afternoon.</p>","pageId":735,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":513,"lock":null}
20:13:22.062 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/532
20:13:22.062 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":532,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, but blowing hard from the N by E. William &amp; I walked into the city. Called upon Bob Marsh only a short time at the office, when Stephenson brought Ann up. I walked with her to Grays Inn, showed her St Pants, went round by Oxford &amp; Regents street &amp; Ann feet being very sore we after buying a pair of easy shoes, took a coach &amp; drove to  new inn. Dined with Bob Marsh &amp; afterwards we all went to the pit at Covent garden Theatre. Ann much astonished at the size &amp; splendour of the houses. We saw Romeo &amp; Juliet performed by C Kenneth &amp; Mrs Smithson. Then afterwards the Devils Elixir, not worth seeing. Ann &amp; I slept at the Fountain in Catherine Street</p>","pageId":735,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":514,"lock":null}
20:13:22.062 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.063 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/532
20:13:22.063 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":532,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, but blowing hard from the N by E. William &amp; I walked into the city. Called upon Bob Marsh only a short time at the office, when Stephenson brought Ann up. I walked with her to Grays Inn, showed her St Pants, went round by Oxford &amp; Regents street &amp; Ann feet being very sore we after buying a pair of easy shoes, took a coach &amp; drove to  new inn. Dined with Bob Marsh &amp; afterwards we all went to the pit at Covent garden Theatre. Ann much astonished at the size &amp; splendour of the houses. We saw Romeo &amp; Juliet performed by C Kenneth &amp; Mrs Smithson. Then afterwards the Devils Elixir, not worth seeing. Ann &amp; I slept at the Fountain in Catherine Street</p>","pageId":735,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":514,"lock":null}
20:13:22.063 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/533
20:13:22.063 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":533,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind still fresh from the N by E. We got breakfast at 11 o'clock &amp; afterwards walked into the Green park round by the Kings Place by Pall Mall to Somerset House &amp; saw the exhibition. Ann much pleased with her mornings <span class=highlight_yellow>amusements</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>took</span> &amp;  left in Grays Inn. Walked into the city. Attended <span class=highlight_yellow>Changes</span>, did nothing with the ship &amp; walked to Nottingham Place to dinner. The Hope could not be sold today.</p>","pageId":735,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":515,"lock":null}
20:13:22.063 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.063 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/533
20:13:22.063 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":533,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind still fresh from the N by E. We got breakfast at 11 o'clock &amp; afterwards walked into the Green park round by the Kings Place by Pall Mall to Somerset House &amp; saw the exhibition. Ann much pleased with her mornings <span class=highlight_yellow>amusements</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>took</span> &amp;  left in Grays Inn. Walked into the city. Attended <span class=highlight_yellow>Changes</span>, did nothing with the ship &amp; walked to Nottingham Place to dinner. The Hope could not be sold today.</p>","pageId":735,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":515,"lock":null}
20:13:22.063 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/534
20:13:22.063 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":534,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful morning. Wind blowing fresh at N by E. Called upon Mr ward. Walked into the city. On my way saw Ann. Attended the coal market with much difficulty they sold <span class=highlight_yellow>58/2</span> of the Hope's cargo. Walked out of the city. Saw Ann again. Called upon Richmond found him looking well, though still lame. Returned by Regents <span class=highlight_yellow>He</span> to Mr Lee to dinner. Bob marsh with us.</p>","pageId":735,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":516,"lock":null}
20:13:22.063 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.063 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/534
20:13:22.063 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":534,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful morning. Wind blowing fresh at N by E. Called upon Mr ward. Walked into the city. On my way saw Ann. Attended the coal market with much difficulty they sold <span class=highlight_yellow>58/2</span> of the Hope's cargo. Walked out of the city. Saw Ann again. Called upon Richmond found him looking well, though still lame. Returned by Regents <span class=highlight_yellow>He</span> to Mr Lee to dinner. Bob marsh with us.</p>","pageId":735,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":516,"lock":null}
20:13:22.063 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/535
20:13:22.063 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":535,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather. Wind NE. Wrote to Mr Vernon to send <span class=highlight_yellow>Inspector</span> Galbraith to London. Walked into the city. Attended <span class=highlight_yellow>changers</span>. Did nothing. Dined with Richmond.</p>","pageId":735,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":517,"lock":null}
20:13:22.063 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.064 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/535
20:13:22.064 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":535,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather. Wind NE. Wrote to Mr Vernon to send <span class=highlight_yellow>Inspector</span> Galbraith to London. Walked into the city. Attended <span class=highlight_yellow>changers</span>. Did nothing. Dined with Richmond.</p>","pageId":735,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":517,"lock":null}
20:13:22.064 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/536
20:13:22.064 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":536,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning but fine weather. Wind still NE &amp; ENE. Mr Lee drove me into the city. Attended the local exchange. Sold 63 more of the Hope's coals. Went to the Royal Ex. Could not fix. Walked out of the city. Dined at Mr Lees. Mr &amp; Bob Marsh &amp; F Barclay there.</p>","pageId":736,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":518,"lock":null}
20:13:22.064 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.064 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/536
20:13:22.064 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":536,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning but fine weather. Wind still NE &amp; ENE. Mr Lee drove me into the city. Attended the local exchange. Sold 63 more of the Hope's coals. Went to the Royal Ex. Could not fix. Walked out of the city. Dined at Mr Lees. Mr &amp; Bob Marsh &amp; F Barclay there.</p>","pageId":736,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":518,"lock":null}
20:13:22.064 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/537
20:13:22.064 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":537,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another cloudy morning. Wind NE. Walked into the city. Called upon Bob Marsh. He &amp; his father walked with me down to the Hope. Saw the St Catherine Docks in our way &amp; the most perfect &amp; comfortable perhaps of thing of the sort all the warehouses &amp; upon so good a place. Had lunch on board &amp; I afterwards attended changes but did nothing for the ship. Walked out of the city with Inspector Chapman &amp; dined with him. His brothers the captain, Thomas, Ben, Mr Graham &amp; a Mr Day there.</p>","pageId":736,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":519,"lock":null}
20:13:22.064 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.065 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/537
20:13:22.065 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":537,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another cloudy morning. Wind NE. Walked into the city. Called upon Bob Marsh. He &amp; his father walked with me down to the Hope. Saw the St Catherine Docks in our way &amp; the most perfect &amp; comfortable perhaps of thing of the sort all the warehouses &amp; upon so good a place. Had lunch on board &amp; I afterwards attended changes but did nothing for the ship. Walked out of the city with Inspector Chapman &amp; dined with him. His brothers the captain, Thomas, Ben, Mr Graham &amp; a Mr Day there.</p>","pageId":736,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":519,"lock":null}
20:13:22.065 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/538
20:13:22.065 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":538,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cloudy morning. Wind about N. Went with the Miss Lees to the chapel in Vern Street. Afterwards called upon Mr &amp; Mrs Lumley in Gower Street. Mr Lee very unwell, consumption, going to leave this <span class=highlight_yellow>home</span>. Called upon Mr Linskill. Went to see Mary &amp; Emma in Sloan Street &amp; then to the park. Dined with Mr ward &amp; spent a pleasant day.</p>","pageId":736,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":520,"lock":null}
20:13:22.065 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.065 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/538
20:13:22.065 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":538,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cloudy morning. Wind about N. Went with the Miss Lees to the chapel in Vern Street. Afterwards called upon Mr &amp; Mrs Lumley in Gower Street. Mr Lee very unwell, consumption, going to leave this <span class=highlight_yellow>home</span>. Called upon Mr Linskill. Went to see Mary &amp; Emma in Sloan Street &amp; then to the park. Dined with Mr ward &amp; spent a pleasant day.</p>","pageId":736,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":520,"lock":null}
20:13:22.065 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/539
20:13:22.065 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":539,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very dull morning &amp; light rain. Wind NW. Walked into the city. At the coal exchange the remainder of the Hope sold. Attended the Royal Exchange but could not fix the Hope. Walked to Mr Lees to dinner. Bob Marsh dined with us.</p>","pageId":736,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":521,"lock":null}
20:13:22.065 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
