20:13:22.066 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":539,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very dull morning &amp; light rain. Wind NW. Walked into the city. At the coal exchange the remainder of the Hope sold. Attended the Royal Exchange but could not fix the Hope. Walked to Mr Lees to dinner. Bob Marsh dined with us.</p>","pageId":736,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":521,"lock":null}
20:13:22.066 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/54
20:13:22.066 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":54,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":2,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind WSW but changed to SSW towards the evening. Got the Hope upon the blocks &amp; the flat up to light water mark caulked. Condemned the main mast. Dined at home</p>","pageId":690,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":51,"lock":null}
20:13:22.066 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.066 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/54
20:13:22.066 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":54,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":2,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind WSW but changed to SSW towards the evening. Got the Hope upon the blocks &amp; the flat up to light water mark caulked. Condemned the main mast. Dined at home</p>","pageId":690,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":51,"lock":null}
20:13:22.066 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/540
20:13:22.066 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":540,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind NW. Walked into the city. Saw Ann. Fixed the Hope for Petersburg with Mr Hubbard ar 26/-. <span class=highlight_yellow>&amp; </span><span class=highlight_yellow>iow</span><span class=highlight_yellow> for fellow</span>. Walked to Mr Lees to dinner. Bob Marsh there, he &amp; the guests having been to Kensington gardens</p>","pageId":736,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":522,"lock":null}
20:13:22.066 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.067 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/540
20:13:22.067 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":540,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind NW. Walked into the city. Saw Ann. Fixed the Hope for Petersburg with Mr Hubbard ar 26/-. <span class=highlight_yellow>&amp; </span><span class=highlight_yellow>iow</span><span class=highlight_yellow> for fellow</span>. Walked to Mr Lees to dinner. Bob Marsh there, he &amp; the guests having been to Kensington gardens</p>","pageId":736,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":522,"lock":null}
20:13:22.067 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/541
20:13:22.067 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":541,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; very hot. Wind NW. Rode into the city. Went to the Bull at Alegate &amp; saw Ann Stokes set off for <span class=highlight_yellow>Hford</span>. Went to the ship with William, Bob Marsh &amp; Vincent , dined on board. Returned to Aldgate to meet Ann. Took her to Astleys theatre &amp; afterwards slept at the Fountain</p>","pageId":736,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":523,"lock":null}
20:13:22.067 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.067 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/541
20:13:22.067 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":541,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; very hot. Wind NW. Rode into the city. Went to the Bull at Alegate &amp; saw Ann Stokes set off for <span class=highlight_yellow>Hford</span>. Went to the ship with William, Bob Marsh &amp; Vincent , dined on board. Returned to Aldgate to meet Ann. Took her to Astleys theatre &amp; afterwards slept at the Fountain</p>","pageId":736,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":523,"lock":null}
20:13:22.067 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/542
20:13:22.067 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":542,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":3,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... upon one of which, <span class=highlight_yellow>Yelagin</span>. We landed &amp; walked through the plantations, the walk of which are beautiful, in good order &amp; under the management of an English <span class=highlight_yellow>Lumana</span> &amp; and attached to a very fine palace of the Emperor that stands close to the water. Near it is a bridge which we crossed to the opposite Island of <span class=highlight_yellow>Kam</span><span class=highlight_yellow>enny</span>, at the end is a handsome theatre, placed there to be near this summer retreat of the Emperor's. This is a very fashionable theatre &amp; attended principally by the court, but I believe open to all. Here they perform French, Italian &amp; German operas. These islands are the property of the Emperor &amp; noblemen. The grounds most beautifully laid out &amp; always open to the public. The Russians being much more <span class=highlight_yellow>ce</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ri</span><span class=highlight_yellow>bal</span> in this respect than John Bull. They delight in seeing the people strolling about the grounds &amp; have seats placed in all directions for their accommodation. We then proceeded through these fairy grounds to the island of <span class=highlight_yellow>Kres</span><span class=highlight_yellow>tovsky</span> Island where Mr Dye has a cottage for the summer. Here we took tea with his family &amp; late in the evening returned to Petersburg which we did not reach till after 1 o'clock in the morning exceptionally tired with our walk</p>","pageId":750,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":524,"lock":null}
20:13:22.067 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.068 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/542
20:13:22.068 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":542,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":3,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... upon one of which, <span class=highlight_yellow>Yelagin</span>. We landed &amp; walked through the plantations, the walk of which are beautiful, in good order &amp; under the management of an English <span class=highlight_yellow>Lumana</span> &amp; and attached to a very fine palace of the Emperor that stands close to the water. Near it is a bridge which we crossed to the opposite Island of <span class=highlight_yellow>Kam</span><span class=highlight_yellow>enny</span>, at the end is a handsome theatre, placed there to be near this summer retreat of the Emperor's. This is a very fashionable theatre &amp; attended principally by the court, but I believe open to all. Here they perform French, Italian &amp; German operas. These islands are the property of the Emperor &amp; noblemen. The grounds most beautifully laid out &amp; always open to the public. The Russians being much more <span class=highlight_yellow>ce</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ri</span><span class=highlight_yellow>bal</span> in this respect than John Bull. They delight in seeing the people strolling about the grounds &amp; have seats placed in all directions for their accommodation. We then proceeded through these fairy grounds to the island of <span class=highlight_yellow>Kres</span><span class=highlight_yellow>tovsky</span> Island where Mr Dye has a cottage for the summer. Here we took tea with his family &amp; late in the evening returned to Petersburg which we did not reach till after 1 o'clock in the morning exceptionally tired with our walk</p>","pageId":750,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":524,"lock":null}
20:13:22.068 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/543
20:13:22.068 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":543,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up at 11 o'clock. Breakfasted at the Fountain &amp; saw Ann safe to her aunty. Walked into the city. Called at the country house. William gone. Returned to Nottingham Place with Mr Lee. Went with the Lees to dine with A Patterson at Clapton, a party. A very fine but extremely hot day. Wind WNW &amp; NW. Received a letter from Mr Vernon of J Galbraith setting off for London.</p>","pageId":736,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":525,"lock":null}
