20:13:22.079 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":565,"version":1,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":20,"sequence":5.0000,"text":"<figure>\r\n  <img src=\"images/img2891-image-copenhagen-east.png\" width=\"600px\" />\r\n  <figcaption>Voyage east from Copenhagen</figcaption>\r\n</figure>","pageId":null,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":null,"lock":null}
20:13:22.079 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/566
20:13:22.079 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":566,"version":2,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"input/json\r\n<p>Between 3 &amp; 4 o'clock feeling my <span class=highlight_yellow>coppers</span> very hot &amp; a might great thirst upon me, I got up for a drink of water. I was much surprised to find the ship under way &amp; running with a light breeze and studding ...</p>\r\n\r\ndatabase\r\n\"<p>Between&nbsp;3&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;4&nbsp;o&#39;clock&nbsp;feeling&nbsp;my&nbsp;cough&nbsp;very&nbsp;bad&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;a&nbsp;mighty&nbsp;great&nbsp;thirst&nbsp;upon&nbsp;me,&nbsp;I&nbsp;got&nbsp;up&nbsp;for&nbsp;a&nbsp;drink&nbsp;of&nbsp;water&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;was&nbsp;much&nbsp;surprised&nbsp;to&nbsp;find&nbsp;the&nbsp;ship&nbsp;under&nbsp;way&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;running&nbsp;with&nbsp;a&nbsp;light&nbsp;breeze&nbsp;and&nbsp;slow&nbsp;going.</p>\"","pageId":741,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":543,"lock":null}
20:13:22.079 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.080 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/566
20:13:22.080 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":566,"version":2,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"input/json\r\n<p>Between 3 &amp; 4 o'clock feeling my <span class=highlight_yellow>coppers</span> very hot &amp; a might great thirst upon me, I got up for a drink of water. I was much surprised to find the ship under way &amp; running with a light breeze and studding ...</p>\r\n\r\ndatabase\r\n\"<p>Between&nbsp;3&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;4&nbsp;o&#39;clock&nbsp;feeling&nbsp;my&nbsp;cough&nbsp;very&nbsp;bad&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;a&nbsp;mighty&nbsp;great&nbsp;thirst&nbsp;upon&nbsp;me,&nbsp;I&nbsp;got&nbsp;up&nbsp;for&nbsp;a&nbsp;drink&nbsp;of&nbsp;water&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;was&nbsp;much&nbsp;surprised&nbsp;to&nbsp;find&nbsp;the&nbsp;ship&nbsp;under&nbsp;way&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;running&nbsp;with&nbsp;a&nbsp;light&nbsp;breeze&nbsp;and&nbsp;slow&nbsp;going.</p>\"","pageId":741,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":543,"lock":null}
20:13:22.080 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/567
20:13:22.080 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":567,"version":4,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":20,"sequence":3.0000,"text":"<p>... splendid &amp; magnificent. The houses all large &amp; good &amp; very clean. The streets the same. The dwellings of the higher classes also in fact palaces. The city is very strongly fortified &amp; the barracks numerous &amp; one an immense scale &amp; capable of containing a very strong force. At present there are 9000 men garrisoned in them exclusively of sailors.</p>\r\n<p>Our guide regarded much that we had not visited Copenhagen on a Sunday, when we should have seen more of the inhabitants particularly the middle and better classes who are to be seen promenading &amp; their favourite walk, he informed us, was in the Kings gardens, behind the palace, built by Inego Jones, but not occupied by the Royal Family. They live in one of the Square formed by four Palaces particularly handsome buildings,  but not upon a large scale. The King &amp; Queen having each one &amp; Prince Christian &amp; his brother the other two.</p>\r\n<p>They have just finished a new Palace of an immense size, for the King, the exterior only I should observe is complete. The interior being get in an unfinished state. &lsquo;tis upon a very grand scale has a most magnificent appearance &amp; is well situated having a large space or open part of the town at its point, through which the river or canal run, wide &amp; deep enough to admit small craft, presumably fishing &amp; marked boats here are also placed the theatre and various public offices. The King's library &amp; stables &amp; riding house attached to the Palace are of an immense size, into the latter we were admitted, indeed they appeared open to the public.</p>\r\n<p>But for the stud. I can speak little in praise, the houses of which the stable was full were very small, of an inferior breed, something like Little the <span class=highlight_yellow>Hanoverian</span> of all long tails, in fact I could have almost fancied magical looking at Astley Stud instead of The King of Denmark. Speaking of him, he appeared to be much beloved, acceptable to the poorest ...</p>","pageId":742,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":544,"lock":null}
20:13:22.080 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.080 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/567
20:13:22.080 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":567,"version":4,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":20,"sequence":3.0000,"text":"<p>... splendid &amp; magnificent. The houses all large &amp; good &amp; very clean. The streets the same. The dwellings of the higher classes also in fact palaces. The city is very strongly fortified &amp; the barracks numerous &amp; one an immense scale &amp; capable of containing a very strong force. At present there are 9000 men garrisoned in them exclusively of sailors.</p>\r\n<p>Our guide regarded much that we had not visited Copenhagen on a Sunday, when we should have seen more of the inhabitants particularly the middle and better classes who are to be seen promenading &amp; their favourite walk, he informed us, was in the Kings gardens, behind the palace, built by Inego Jones, but not occupied by the Royal Family. They live in one of the Square formed by four Palaces particularly handsome buildings,  but not upon a large scale. The King &amp; Queen having each one &amp; Prince Christian &amp; his brother the other two.</p>\r\n<p>They have just finished a new Palace of an immense size, for the King, the exterior only I should observe is complete. The interior being get in an unfinished state. &lsquo;tis upon a very grand scale has a most magnificent appearance &amp; is well situated having a large space or open part of the town at its point, through which the river or canal run, wide &amp; deep enough to admit small craft, presumably fishing &amp; marked boats here are also placed the theatre and various public offices. The King's library &amp; stables &amp; riding house attached to the Palace are of an immense size, into the latter we were admitted, indeed they appeared open to the public.</p>\r\n<p>But for the stud. I can speak little in praise, the houses of which the stable was full were very small, of an inferior breed, something like Little the <span class=highlight_yellow>Hanoverian</span> of all long tails, in fact I could have almost fancied magical looking at Astley Stud instead of The King of Denmark. Speaking of him, he appeared to be much beloved, acceptable to the poorest ...</p>","pageId":742,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":544,"lock":null}
20:13:22.080 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/568
20:13:22.080 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":568,"version":3,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":20,"sequence":4.0000,"text":"<p>... devoting four hours on certain days in the week to passing any complaints or receiving petitions, which he does from the parties themselves, not as with our King through a minister which by the bye I think the proper way, the King of Denmark makes himself too common in the respect though he constantly attains his object, the love of his people. He keeps up very little state and presumably the city the same as any private individual without any attendant. We did not see him. He &amp; the family being at their country residence in Jutland.</p>\r\n<p>At &frac12; past 11 o'clock am returned to Mr Ryan's  extremely heated &amp; rather tired with our walk &amp; after refreshing ourselves with a glass of his good medicine &amp; water &amp; thanking him for his attention, we got into our boat &amp; again embarked at about 12 o'clock. Whilst the crew were getting the anchor up, Bob, <span class=highlight_yellow>Inspector</span> G &amp; I undressed, jumped overboard &amp; had a most delightful bath. By the time we had got on board again the ship was under way, with the wind at SE, not very favourable for us. After making two or three boards, blowing by this time, a fresh breeze, we go through the grounds &amp; at 3 o'clock the pilot left us between the islands of Saltholm &amp; Drag&oslash;r, the extreme point of Jutland. Met a fleet of loaded vessels running down to Elslnem at 5 o'clock pm. Passed Falsterbo on the starboard tack, close hauled, wind about ESE. At &frac14; past 8 o'clock tacked Moen Island bearing SW distant about 6 miles. A clear frosty looking sky, wind, current &amp; heavy swell against us &amp; no appearance of a change this night. At 9 o'clock Bob and I took one glass of comfort &amp; went to bed.</p>","pageId":743,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":545,"lock":null}
20:13:22.080 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.081 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/568
20:13:22.081 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":568,"version":3,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":20,"sequence":4.0000,"text":"<p>... devoting four hours on certain days in the week to passing any complaints or receiving petitions, which he does from the parties themselves, not as with our King through a minister which by the bye I think the proper way, the King of Denmark makes himself too common in the respect though he constantly attains his object, the love of his people. He keeps up very little state and presumably the city the same as any private individual without any attendant. We did not see him. He &amp; the family being at their country residence in Jutland.</p>\r\n<p>At &frac12; past 11 o'clock am returned to Mr Ryan's  extremely heated &amp; rather tired with our walk &amp; after refreshing ourselves with a glass of his good medicine &amp; water &amp; thanking him for his attention, we got into our boat &amp; again embarked at about 12 o'clock. Whilst the crew were getting the anchor up, Bob, <span class=highlight_yellow>Inspector</span> G &amp; I undressed, jumped overboard &amp; had a most delightful bath. By the time we had got on board again the ship was under way, with the wind at SE, not very favourable for us. After making two or three boards, blowing by this time, a fresh breeze, we go through the grounds &amp; at 3 o'clock the pilot left us between the islands of Saltholm &amp; Drag&oslash;r, the extreme point of Jutland. Met a fleet of loaded vessels running down to Elslnem at 5 o'clock pm. Passed Falsterbo on the starboard tack, close hauled, wind about ESE. At &frac14; past 8 o'clock tacked Moen Island bearing SW distant about 6 miles. A clear frosty looking sky, wind, current &amp; heavy swell against us &amp; no appearance of a change this night. At 9 o'clock Bob and I took one glass of comfort &amp; went to bed.</p>","pageId":743,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":545,"lock":null}
20:13:22.081 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/569
20:13:22.081 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":569,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at &frac12; 7 o'clock. Found the ship still in sight of Falsterbo, having been working to windward all night &amp; made but little progress, <span class=highlight_yellow>wind</span> fast. After breakfast read the service &amp; lessons of the day. Just before I got upon deck, the XYZ passed us homeward bound, with a fine breeze &amp; studdingsails set. We continued working to westward the whole of the day. At 9 o'clock took our gin &amp; water &amp; went to bed.</p>","pageId":743,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":546,"lock":null}
20:13:22.081 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.081 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/569
20:13:22.081 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":569,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at &frac12; 7 o'clock. Found the ship still in sight of Falsterbo, having been working to windward all night &amp; made but little progress, <span class=highlight_yellow>wind</span> fast. After breakfast read the service &amp; lessons of the day. Just before I got upon deck, the XYZ passed us homeward bound, with a fine breeze &amp; studdingsails set. We continued working to westward the whole of the day. At 9 o'clock took our gin &amp; water &amp; went to bed.</p>","pageId":743,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":546,"lock":null}
20:13:22.081 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/57
20:13:22.081 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":57,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":2,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, but turned dull towards afternoon &amp; damp wind veered from E by S to S by E. Dined at home. A party at Mrs Stephen's at Tynemouth in the evening</p>","pageId":691,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":54,"lock":null}
20:13:22.081 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.081 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/57
20:13:22.081 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":57,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":2,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, but turned dull towards afternoon &amp; damp wind veered from E by S to S by E. Dined at home. A party at Mrs Stephen's at Tynemouth in the evening</p>","pageId":691,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":54,"lock":null}
20:13:22.081 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/570
20:13:22.081 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":570,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather but wind still from the east &amp; rather cool. Towards the afternoon the wind gradually decreased &amp; became much warmer, so that we are in hope it will die away &amp; shall have a change. This working to windward in the Baltic is much more tiresome than anywhere else. The current also being always against you. In the evening became quite calm. At 9 o'clock took our tumbler of whisky toddy &amp; went to bed. The Swedish coast very fine &amp; pretty, well wooded.</p>","pageId":743,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":547,"lock":null}
20:13:22.081 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.082 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/570
20:13:22.082 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":570,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather but wind still from the east &amp; rather cool. Towards the afternoon the wind gradually decreased &amp; became much warmer, so that we are in hope it will die away &amp; shall have a change. This working to windward in the Baltic is much more tiresome than anywhere else. The current also being always against you. In the evening became quite calm. At 9 o'clock took our tumbler of whisky toddy &amp; went to bed. The Swedish coast very fine &amp; pretty, well wooded.</p>","pageId":743,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":547,"lock":null}
20:13:22.082 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/571
20:13:22.082 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":571,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out before  8 o'clock &amp; most beautiful morning &amp; although calm during the night, the sea so smooth, that the ship with the little air there was, has, as the Captain terms it, been sliding through the water. To my surprise, found Bornholm in sight. The north of the island bearing east distant about 10 miles SE by E which is about an hour changed to SSW. Set foretopmast &amp; maintop gallant studding sails.</p>","pageId":743,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":548,"lock":null}
20:13:22.082 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.082 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/571
20:13:22.082 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":571,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out before  8 o'clock &amp; most beautiful morning &amp; although calm during the night, the sea so smooth, that the ship with the little air there was, has, as the Captain terms it, been sliding through the water. To my surprise, found Bornholm in sight. The north of the island bearing east distant about 10 miles SE by E which is about an hour changed to SSW. Set foretopmast &amp; maintop gallant studding sails.</p>","pageId":743,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":548,"lock":null}
20:13:22.082 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/572
20:13:22.082 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":572,"version":2,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":23,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... The slightest air possible during the whole of the day &amp; making such little way that we were enabled to catch a couple of coldlings by our lines going near the bottom. At 6 o'clock pm a slight breeze sprung up from the NNE which run us pretty near against the north end of Bornholm, where at 9 o'clock it suddenly changed to against us, but died away to a dead calm. Had our whisky &amp; water &amp; turned in. Bornholm a very fine island as sun with the glass.</p>","pageId":744,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":549,"lock":null}
20:13:22.082 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.083 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/572
20:13:22.083 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":572,"version":2,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":23,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... The slightest air possible during the whole of the day &amp; making such little way that we were enabled to catch a couple of coldlings by our lines going near the bottom. At 6 o'clock pm a slight breeze sprung up from the NNE which run us pretty near against the north end of Bornholm, where at 9 o'clock it suddenly changed to against us, but died away to a dead calm. Had our whisky &amp; water &amp; turned in. Bornholm a very fine island as sun with the glass.</p>","pageId":744,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":549,"lock":null}
20:13:22.083 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/573
20:13:22.083 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":573,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at 8 o'clock after a sound snooze. After a dead calm, the whole of the night, at 6 o'clock this morning a breeze sprung up from NW &amp; when we got upon deck, found we were gradually loosing slight of the island. Got studding sails set, but not at any time going more than four knots, sometimes not so much.</p>\r\n<p>Most beautiful weather, but the sun not so scorching as yesterday. Accompanied the whole day by thousands of large dragon flies that flew about &amp; alighted upon our rigging which was at times covered with them. At &frac12; past 8 o'clock, went below &amp; had our rum &amp; water &amp; when we went to bed at &frac12; past 9 o'clock, the wind continued favourable &amp; a fine breeze.</p>","pageId":744,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":550,"lock":null}
20:13:22.083 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.083 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/573
20:13:22.083 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":573,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at 8 o'clock after a sound snooze. After a dead calm, the whole of the night, at 6 o'clock this morning a breeze sprung up from NW &amp; when we got upon deck, found we were gradually loosing slight of the island. Got studding sails set, but not at any time going more than four knots, sometimes not so much.</p>\r\n<p>Most beautiful weather, but the sun not so scorching as yesterday. Accompanied the whole day by thousands of large dragon flies that flew about &amp; alighted upon our rigging which was at times covered with them. At &frac12; past 8 o'clock, went below &amp; had our rum &amp; water &amp; when we went to bed at &frac12; past 9 o'clock, the wind continued favourable &amp; a fine breeze.</p>","pageId":744,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":550,"lock":null}
20:13:22.083 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/574
20:13:22.083 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":574,"version":3,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":25,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... knots. At &frac14; past 4 o'clock supposed to two abreast <font color=#BFBFBF>of </font>the south end of the Ireland of Gotland &amp; when we going with a fine NW breeze at the rate of 7 &frac12; knots. Suddenly &amp; in a moment, taken all aback, got lower &amp; topmast studdingsails in, wind in the courses of a few minutes, flying all round the compass in the most extraordinary way. At last <span class=highlight_yellow>sumed</span> to settle at east.</p>\r\n<p>A large ship upon our weather bow. Supposed to be a republican frigate. The captain amused himself today in painting the covering boards &amp; waterways. The men this afternoon employed in washing the beef, the whole of which is unfortunately very much tainted. In the course of the evening the wind got to the WSW so that we laid up ENE going on 3 &amp; 4 knots. At 8 o'clock took our grog &amp; turned in at 11 o'clock. Wind more favourable</p>","pageId":744,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":551,"lock":null}
20:13:22.083 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.083 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/574
20:13:22.083 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":574,"version":3,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":25,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... knots. At &frac14; past 4 o'clock supposed to two abreast <font color=#BFBFBF>of </font>the south end of the Ireland of Gotland &amp; when we going with a fine NW breeze at the rate of 7 &frac12; knots. Suddenly &amp; in a moment, taken all aback, got lower &amp; topmast studdingsails in, wind in the courses of a few minutes, flying all round the compass in the most extraordinary way. At last <span class=highlight_yellow>sumed</span> to settle at east.</p>\r\n<p>A large ship upon our weather bow. Supposed to be a republican frigate. The captain amused himself today in painting the covering boards &amp; waterways. The men this afternoon employed in washing the beef, the whole of which is unfortunately very much tainted. In the course of the evening the wind got to the WSW so that we laid up ENE going on 3 &amp; 4 knots. At 8 o'clock took our grog &amp; turned in at 11 o'clock. Wind more favourable</p>","pageId":744,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":551,"lock":null}
20:13:22.083 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/575
