20:13:22.111 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":628,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":25,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... packet from Mr Dye, a present for Emma Galbraith. Mr L took a glass of grog with us &amp; we afterwards accompanied him on board. The Chase, captain Thompson arrived today in 13 days from Hull, and had supper.</p>","pageId":761,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":592,"lock":null}
20:13:22.111 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/629
20:13:22.111 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":629,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning, but exceptionally hot. The wind having got round to the north &amp; an appearance of changing. We after breakfast hauled out of the mole but being quite calm were obliged to get a boat ahead &amp; toe the ship down to the guard ship. Cleared at the guard ship about 12 o'clock &amp; proceeded with a leading wind, but little of it.</p>","pageId":761,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":593,"lock":null}
20:13:22.111 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.111 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/629
20:13:22.111 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":629,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning, but exceptionally hot. The wind having got round to the north &amp; an appearance of changing. We after breakfast hauled out of the mole but being quite calm were obliged to get a boat ahead &amp; toe the ship down to the guard ship. Cleared at the guard ship about 12 o'clock &amp; proceeded with a leading wind, but little of it.</p>","pageId":761,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":593,"lock":null}
20:13:22.111 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/63
20:13:22.111 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":63,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":2,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine spring day. Wind SW. Dined at home &amp; at the whist club in the evening. Mrs Smith left us for Togston. Brought a trysailmast &amp; gib boom for &pound;4.12.6 &amp; got them on board</p>","pageId":691,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":60,"lock":null}
20:13:22.111 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.112 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/63
20:13:22.112 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":63,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":2,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine spring day. Wind SW. Dined at home &amp; at the whist club in the evening. Mrs Smith left us for Togston. Brought a trysailmast &amp; gib boom for &pound;4.12.6 &amp; got them on board</p>","pageId":691,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":60,"lock":null}
20:13:22.112 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/630
20:13:22.112 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":630,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, rather dull. The ship working windward, the wind having unfortunately changed during the night direct against us being west. Continued <span class=highlight_yellow>binting</span> about all day without making any way. For little to the eastward of Seascar Island. In the evening we again got a leading wind &amp; before bed time, getting more to the northward, we were enabled to set lower fore &amp; topmast &amp; studding sails with a fine fresh breeze</p>","pageId":761,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":594,"lock":null}
20:13:22.112 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.112 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/630
20:13:22.112 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":630,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, rather dull. The ship working windward, the wind having unfortunately changed during the night direct against us being west. Continued <span class=highlight_yellow>binting</span> about all day without making any way. For little to the eastward of Seascar Island. In the evening we again got a leading wind &amp; before bed time, getting more to the northward, we were enabled to set lower fore &amp; topmast &amp; studding sails with a fine fresh breeze</p>","pageId":761,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":594,"lock":null}
20:13:22.112 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/631
20:13:22.112 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":631,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very thick wet disagreeable morning, been raining nearly all night, but thank God, with a fine fresh breeze from the eastward. The ship making good way passed the north end of Hogsland this morning at 6 o'clock. Continued raining all day from 5 &frac12; to 6 &frac12; knots. When we went to bed at a little before 10 o'clock we were abreast of Revel, still blowing fresh from the East. </p>","pageId":761,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":595,"lock":null}
20:13:22.112 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
