20:13:22.114 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":635,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out before 8 o'clock. A fine morning. A light breeze at ENE going about 3 or 3 &frac12; knots. Studding sails set. About dinner time it began to rain &amp; continued very heavy until 3 o'clock. When we passed round Dago Island &amp; entered the Baltic. At &frac12; past 5 o'clock the wind changed to west ...</p>","pageId":761,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":597,"lock":null}
20:13:22.115 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/636
20:13:22.115 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":636,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":30,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>In the evening light winds &amp; inclined to calm. Turned in before 10 o'clock after a glass of grog</p>","pageId":762,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":598,"lock":null}
20:13:22.115 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.115 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/636
20:13:22.115 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":636,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":30,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>In the evening light winds &amp; inclined to calm. Turned in before 10 o'clock after a glass of grog</p>","pageId":762,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":598,"lock":null}
20:13:22.115 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/637
20:13:22.115 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":637,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather and light breezes from WNW. During the whole of the morning mainly calm, barely going 2 knots with rather a strong sea. In the evening about 5 o'clock the wind got to the ENE &amp; increased to a fine breeze. The ship going about 4 &amp; 5 knots &amp; from midnight to 4 o'clock the wind blew so fresh she increased her rate to 6 knots. This fine breeze continued all night.</p>","pageId":762,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":599,"lock":null}
20:13:22.115 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.115 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/637
20:13:22.115 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":637,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather and light breezes from WNW. During the whole of the morning mainly calm, barely going 2 knots with rather a strong sea. In the evening about 5 o'clock the wind got to the ENE &amp; increased to a fine breeze. The ship going about 4 &amp; 5 knots &amp; from midnight to 4 o'clock the wind blew so fresh she increased her rate to 6 knots. This fine breeze continued all night.</p>","pageId":762,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":599,"lock":null}
20:13:22.115 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/638
20:13:22.115 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":638,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up at &frac12; past 7 o'clock. A fine morning. After a few hours rain  &amp; a beautiful breeze the whole of the night. At 8 o'clock am the wind changed to SE obliged us to get in lower studding sails. At 2 o'clock the wind got to S by W strong breezes &amp; hazy weather &amp; rain, very cold, more like November than August. At 6 o'clock close in with Gothland Ostergarmholm light house N &frac12; W distant about 12 miles. Tacked ship blowing fresh with a heavy head sea. Between 9 &amp; 10 o'clock discussed our grog &amp; turned in.</p>\r\n<p>This afternoon the Dido of Hull captain ____ passed astern of us. We hoisted our colours &amp; he answered</p>","pageId":762,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":600,"lock":null}
20:13:22.115 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.116 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/638
20:13:22.116 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":638,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up at &frac12; past 7 o'clock. A fine morning. After a few hours rain  &amp; a beautiful breeze the whole of the night. At 8 o'clock am the wind changed to SE obliged us to get in lower studding sails. At 2 o'clock the wind got to S by W strong breezes &amp; hazy weather &amp; rain, very cold, more like November than August. At 6 o'clock close in with Gothland Ostergarmholm light house N &frac12; W distant about 12 miles. Tacked ship blowing fresh with a heavy head sea. Between 9 &amp; 10 o'clock discussed our grog &amp; turned in.</p>\r\n<p>This afternoon the Dido of Hull captain ____ passed astern of us. We hoisted our colours &amp; he answered</p>","pageId":762,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":600,"lock":null}
20:13:22.116 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/639
20:13:22.116 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":639,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up at our usual hour. Finer weather, wind NE &amp; strong sea, but still cool. At noon by observation lat:57.8N  Wind WNW. The strong sea preventing us making more than 2 or 3 knots. Read service &amp; lessons for the day. In the afternoon wind NW &amp; blowing fresh, only going from 3 to 4 knots. A few ships in company. Amongst them Bowies Malvina. At 4 o'clock took in top gallants sails. Bob &amp; I very tired of this slow work.</p>\r\n<p>Between 9 &amp; 10 o'clock finished a couple of glasses of warm grog &amp; turned in hoping to sleep better than last night. The tallow casks making a most infernal creaking. Obliged to get the state room port light caulked, a pretty considerable quantity of water having come in &amp; wet my bed</p>","pageId":762,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":601,"lock":null}
20:13:22.116 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.116 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/639
20:13:22.116 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":639,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up at our usual hour. Finer weather, wind NE &amp; strong sea, but still cool. At noon by observation lat:57.8N  Wind WNW. The strong sea preventing us making more than 2 or 3 knots. Read service &amp; lessons for the day. In the afternoon wind NW &amp; blowing fresh, only going from 3 to 4 knots. A few ships in company. Amongst them Bowies Malvina. At 4 o'clock took in top gallants sails. Bob &amp; I very tired of this slow work.</p>\r\n<p>Between 9 &amp; 10 o'clock finished a couple of glasses of warm grog &amp; turned in hoping to sleep better than last night. The tallow casks making a most infernal creaking. Obliged to get the state room port light caulked, a pretty considerable quantity of water having come in &amp; wet my bed</p>","pageId":762,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":601,"lock":null}
20:13:22.116 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/64
20:13:22.116 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":64,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":2,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day day. Wind N by E. Finished with the rigging. Dined at home. At Mrs Greenhows in the evening</p>","pageId":691,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":61,"lock":null}
20:13:22.116 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.117 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/64
20:13:22.117 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":64,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":2,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day day. Wind N by E. Finished with the rigging. Dined at home. At Mrs Greenhows in the evening</p>","pageId":691,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":61,"lock":null}
20:13:22.117 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/640
20:13:22.117 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":640,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning &amp; clear weather, still blowing fresh from the NW which has continued the whole day, with a heavy sea which has prevented us making more than 3 knots. Amused myself the whole of the day reading Peregrine Pickle. At 4 o'clock pm wind got to W by N. At 5 o'clock pm tacked ship &amp; stood across towards Gothland again. By observation at 12 o'clock lat:55.52 Reefed topsail at 2 o'clock pm</p>","pageId":762,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":602,"lock":null}
20:13:22.117 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.117 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/640
20:13:22.117 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":640,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning &amp; clear weather, still blowing fresh from the NW which has continued the whole day, with a heavy sea which has prevented us making more than 3 knots. Amused myself the whole of the day reading Peregrine Pickle. At 4 o'clock pm wind got to W by N. At 5 o'clock pm tacked ship &amp; stood across towards Gothland again. By observation at 12 o'clock lat:55.52 Reefed topsail at 2 o'clock pm</p>","pageId":762,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":602,"lock":null}
20:13:22.117 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/641
20:13:22.117 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":641,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A delightful change. Now beautiful weather. Wind NW &amp; W. Light breeze &amp; sea very much fallen, only going about 2 knots. At 12 o'clock by observation at lat:55.47N. Employed myself all the morning in preparing the wood for a dog kennel. At 2 o'clock pm the wind got to the WSW course NW. At 5 pm set studding sails, top masts &amp; main top gallant. Sea quite fallen &amp; a fine fresh breeze at 6 o'clock wind S course W by S going 5 knots at 10 o'clock <span class=highlight_yellow>discharged</span> our grog &amp; turned in for the night, ship going 5 &frac12; knots</p>","pageId":763,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":603,"lock":null}
20:13:22.117 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.117 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/641
20:13:22.117 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":641,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A delightful change. Now beautiful weather. Wind NW &amp; W. Light breeze &amp; sea very much fallen, only going about 2 knots. At 12 o'clock by observation at lat:55.47N. Employed myself all the morning in preparing the wood for a dog kennel. At 2 o'clock pm the wind got to the WSW course NW. At 5 pm set studding sails, top masts &amp; main top gallant. Sea quite fallen &amp; a fine fresh breeze at 6 o'clock wind S course W by S going 5 knots at 10 o'clock <span class=highlight_yellow>discharged</span> our grog &amp; turned in for the night, ship going 5 &frac12; knots</p>","pageId":763,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":603,"lock":null}
20:13:22.117 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/642
20:13:22.117 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":642,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful day. The ship making good way about 4 &frac12; knots with a fine breeze at SSE going free. We can perceive the Islands of <span class=highlight_yellow>E</span><span class=highlight_yellow>r</span><span class=highlight_yellow>tholm</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ene</span> &amp; Bornholm with the glass. The ship much to my annoyance very leaky. Obliged to pump every hour. At 1 o'clock pm passed close to <span class=highlight_yellow>Erth</span><span class=highlight_yellow>o</span><span class=highlight_yellow>lm</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ene</span>. With a fine breeze at S by E. Studding sails set. These are small rocky islands belonging to Denmark about 11 miles from Bornholm. Upon the largest is a lighthouse, a few small batteries &amp; houses. On the south side a very good harbour I understand. The other two islands are mostly rocks &amp; ...</p>","pageId":763,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":604,"lock":null}
