20:13:22.118 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":642,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful day. The ship making good way about 4 &frac12; knots with a fine breeze at SSE going free. We can perceive the Islands of <span class=highlight_yellow>E</span><span class=highlight_yellow>r</span><span class=highlight_yellow>tholm</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ene</span> &amp; Bornholm with the glass. The ship much to my annoyance very leaky. Obliged to pump every hour. At 1 o'clock pm passed close to <span class=highlight_yellow>Erth</span><span class=highlight_yellow>o</span><span class=highlight_yellow>lm</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ene</span>. With a fine breeze at S by E. Studding sails set. These are small rocky islands belonging to Denmark about 11 miles from Bornholm. Upon the largest is a lighthouse, a few small batteries &amp; houses. On the south side a very good harbour I understand. The other two islands are mostly rocks &amp; ...</p>","pageId":763,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":604,"lock":null}
20:13:22.118 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/643
20:13:22.118 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":643,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out this morning at the usual hour. Coppers hot &amp; rather feverish, took a <span class=highlight_yellow>seidletz</span>, very pleasant answering a double purpose. A beautiful morning. Summer returned. A light breeze at SE. At noon by observation in lat 55.10N. Kept our reach the whole of the day. Wind NW. At 8 o'clock tacked ship. <span class=highlight_yellow>Reigen</span> Island bearing S by W distant 10 or 12 miles.</p>","pageId":763,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":605,"lock":null}
20:13:22.118 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.118 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/643
20:13:22.118 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":643,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out this morning at the usual hour. Coppers hot &amp; rather feverish, took a <span class=highlight_yellow>seidletz</span>, very pleasant answering a double purpose. A beautiful morning. Summer returned. A light breeze at SE. At noon by observation in lat 55.10N. Kept our reach the whole of the day. Wind NW. At 8 o'clock tacked ship. <span class=highlight_yellow>Reigen</span> Island bearing S by W distant 10 or 12 miles.</p>","pageId":763,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":605,"lock":null}
20:13:22.118 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/644
20:13:22.118 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":644,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy morning &amp; fresh breeze at NNW &amp; N. Employed myself all the morning in drawing. At noon clear weather but still a fresh breeze. <span class=highlight_yellow>Falsterbo</span> light bearing WNW distant 8 miles. A large fleet of ships passed us upward bound. At 5 o'clock tacked ship a little to the southward of <span class=highlight_yellow>Moea</span> Island after which it became quite calm until 9 o'clock when we got a light air from the NNW. Afterwards most favourable. At 10 o'clock after our grog we turned in, the ship proceeding quickly towards Drags in the island <span class=highlight_yellow>Verf</span><span class=highlight_yellow> </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Amag</span></p>","pageId":764,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":606,"lock":null}
20:13:22.118 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.118 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/644
20:13:22.118 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":644,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy morning &amp; fresh breeze at NNW &amp; N. Employed myself all the morning in drawing. At noon clear weather but still a fresh breeze. <span class=highlight_yellow>Falsterbo</span> light bearing WNW distant 8 miles. A large fleet of ships passed us upward bound. At 5 o'clock tacked ship a little to the southward of <span class=highlight_yellow>Moea</span> Island after which it became quite calm until 9 o'clock when we got a light air from the NNW. Afterwards most favourable. At 10 o'clock after our grog we turned in, the ship proceeding quickly towards Drags in the island <span class=highlight_yellow>Verf</span><span class=highlight_yellow> </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Amag</span></p>","pageId":764,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":606,"lock":null}
20:13:22.118 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/645
20:13:22.119 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":645,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Hearing the master speaking a ship, I turned out before 7 o'clock. It was Hutchenson's Ajax bound to <span class=highlight_yellow>Wybury</span>, several other ships passing us. Hazy weather &amp; light rain, wind WNW. At &frac12; past 7 o'clock got a piolet onboard &amp; at 8 o'clock passed Drago. At 10 o'clock got there through the Grounds when the piolet left us off Copenhagen proceeding with a fine breeze for <span class=highlight_yellow>Elsinore</span>. The weather cleared up &amp; turned out a fine warm day, giving us a beautiful view of the coast. Brought up at <span class=highlight_yellow>Elsinore</span> at 3 o'clock &amp; went on shore. Received a letter from William informing me of Mrs Scott's illness, not expected to live long &amp; his intention of going to Shields on the 11 th August in the steam boat with C Richmond. Took some wine with <span class=highlight_yellow>warm </span><span class=highlight_yellow>chapurars</span> &amp; afterwards walked out to his fathers house who kindly sent to ask us when he heard of our arrival to go &amp; drink a ...</p>","pageId":764,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":607,"lock":null}
20:13:22.119 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
