20:13:22.121 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":648,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Continuance of clear weather &amp; wind still prevailing from the SSW &amp; SW. Could make no way at 1 o'clock pm &amp; just after taking <span class=highlight_yellow>of position</span> into some port in Norway an extremely heavy gale of wind came on from ...</p>","pageId":764,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":610,"lock":null}
20:13:22.121 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/649
20:13:22.121 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":649,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":11,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... the west which soon caused a tremendous sea. Obliged to him too under close reefed topsails until about 4 o'clock when we <span class=highlight_yellow>wone</span> ship &amp; lay too under close reefed main topsail. What with the howling of the wind, the rolling &amp; tossing of the ship &amp; creaking of tallow casks besides being leaky &amp; upon a lee shore, we had spent a most uncomfortable day. Did not attempt to go to bed, indeed mine was so damp I could not, but I lay down upon the captains about midnight all standing </p>","pageId":765,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":611,"lock":null}
20:13:22.121 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.121 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/649
20:13:22.121 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":649,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":11,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... the west which soon caused a tremendous sea. Obliged to him too under close reefed topsails until about 4 o'clock when we <span class=highlight_yellow>wone</span> ship &amp; lay too under close reefed main topsail. What with the howling of the wind, the rolling &amp; tossing of the ship &amp; creaking of tallow casks besides being leaky &amp; upon a lee shore, we had spent a most uncomfortable day. Did not attempt to go to bed, indeed mine was so damp I could not, but I lay down upon the captains about midnight all standing </p>","pageId":765,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":611,"lock":null}
20:13:22.121 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/65
20:13:22.121 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":65,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":3,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind N. Went to Newcastle &amp; signed bond for Register. Dined at J Tindley, a large party. Paid carpenters &pound;9.12/- - Riggers &pound;7. Wrote to William</p>","pageId":691,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":62,"lock":null}
20:13:22.121 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.122 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/65
20:13:22.122 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":65,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":3,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind N. Went to Newcastle &amp; signed bond for Register. Dined at J Tindley, a large party. Paid carpenters &pound;9.12/- - Riggers &pound;7. Wrote to William</p>","pageId":691,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":62,"lock":null}
20:13:22.122 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/650
20:13:22.122 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":650,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Spent a miserable night, having had little or no sleep. Looked  out about 5 o'clock. The gale as heavy as ever &amp; without any appearance of change, although the sky very clear. At 11 o'clock Masskand Castle in sight distant about 4 leagues, when we determined no longer to contend with the winds but bore away for Gottenburg &amp; in the course of half an hour those wise few that did not follow our example at &frac12; past 3 o'clock we reached Wings sound &amp; before 5 o'clock brought up in the harbour of Warga, a small channel between two docks, rejoicing with the prospect of obtaining a good nights rest. </p>","pageId":765,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":612,"lock":null}
20:13:22.122 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.122 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/650
20:13:22.122 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":650,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Spent a miserable night, having had little or no sleep. Looked  out about 5 o'clock. The gale as heavy as ever &amp; without any appearance of change, although the sky very clear. At 11 o'clock Masskand Castle in sight distant about 4 leagues, when we determined no longer to contend with the winds but bore away for Gottenburg &amp; in the course of half an hour those wise few that did not follow our example at &frac12; past 3 o'clock we reached Wings sound &amp; before 5 o'clock brought up in the harbour of Warga, a small channel between two docks, rejoicing with the prospect of obtaining a good nights rest. </p>","pageId":765,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":612,"lock":null}
20:13:22.122 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/651
20:13:22.122 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":651,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine clear day, but still blowing hard from the westward.</p>\r\n<p>After breakfast, Bob the Captain J Galbraith &amp; I landed. One of the fishermen's yawls (large size) fine sea boats &amp; safe &amp; sailed up to Gothenburg where we spent the day in seeing the town, which is much better than I expected &amp; larger, the country around entirely rock, having a novel wild &amp; beautiful appearance altogether being interspersed with valleys &amp; rivers which were the only spots that could be cultivated &amp; were made the most of. They had one of their annual fares which lasts eight days, but did not seem well attended. After having had our dinner at one of their inns, considering the country very comfortable, we again embarked at 4 o'clock&amp; the winds being against us, we had a <span class=highlight_yellow>turning</span> passage of it, &amp; did not reach the ship until near 8 o'clock.</p>\r\n<p>And after having our tea blowing a cloud &amp; discussing a glass of grog, turned in before 10 o'clock</p>","pageId":765,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":613,"lock":null}
20:13:22.122 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.123 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/651
20:13:22.123 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":651,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine clear day, but still blowing hard from the westward.</p>\r\n<p>After breakfast, Bob the Captain J Galbraith &amp; I landed. One of the fishermen's yawls (large size) fine sea boats &amp; safe &amp; sailed up to Gothenburg where we spent the day in seeing the town, which is much better than I expected &amp; larger, the country around entirely rock, having a novel wild &amp; beautiful appearance altogether being interspersed with valleys &amp; rivers which were the only spots that could be cultivated &amp; were made the most of. They had one of their annual fares which lasts eight days, but did not seem well attended. After having had our dinner at one of their inns, considering the country very comfortable, we again embarked at 4 o'clock&amp; the winds being against us, we had a <span class=highlight_yellow>turning</span> passage of it, &amp; did not reach the ship until near 8 o'clock.</p>\r\n<p>And after having our tea blowing a cloud &amp; discussing a glass of grog, turned in before 10 o'clock</p>","pageId":765,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":613,"lock":null}
20:13:22.123 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/652
20:13:22.123 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":652,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at &frac12; past 7 o'clock. In the middle of the night it became quite calm &amp; the wind changing to the eastward enabled us to get underway. Between 8 &amp; 9 o'clock &amp; to leave a place that I never again wish to see under similar circumstances. As the wind changed with the moon, it will carry us safely to England ...</p>","pageId":765,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":614,"lock":null}
20:13:22.123 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.123 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/652
20:13:22.123 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":652,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at &frac12; past 7 o'clock. In the middle of the night it became quite calm &amp; the wind changing to the eastward enabled us to get underway. Between 8 &amp; 9 o'clock &amp; to leave a place that I never again wish to see under similar circumstances. As the wind changed with the moon, it will carry us safely to England ...</p>","pageId":765,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":614,"lock":null}
20:13:22.123 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/653
20:13:22.123 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":653,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":14,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... should it continue. At 6 o'clock passed the Scaw Light with a fresh breeze &amp; every appearance of it increasing, the sea making very much. Turned <font color=#BFBFBF>in </font>at about our usual hour</p>","pageId":766,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":615,"lock":null}
20:13:22.123 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.123 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/653
20:13:22.123 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":653,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":14,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... should it continue. At 6 o'clock passed the Scaw Light with a fresh breeze &amp; every appearance of it increasing, the sea making very much. Turned <font color=#BFBFBF>in </font>at about our usual hour</p>","pageId":766,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":615,"lock":null}
20:13:22.124 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/654
20:13:22.124 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":654,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up this morning at a little before 8 o'clock after a very boisterous night, the wind having increased to more than half a gale with a tremendous sea, right aft so that we made good way, though at the sacrifice of our comfort. Everything above &amp; below being wet &amp; in confusion. At 5 o'clock this morning a tremendous heavy sea pooped us, stove &amp; carried away our jolly boat &amp; alarmed us so much fearing it had stove in the dark lights &amp; if it had so happened we of course should have been waterlogged. Knowing the delicate state of the <span class=highlight_yellow>archboard</span>, where she was making a great deal of water, the fear of another heavy sea striking us kept me in a very uncomfortable state the whole of the day. Towards evening however both wind &amp; sea fell considerably. We have been going today from 6&frac12;  to 7 knots. Ship laboured very much &amp; made a deal of water. We consider we have got this evening considerably to the westward of the Naze of Norway, say 50 miles.</p>\r\n<p>A great deal of water having come into ...</p>","pageId":766,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":616,"lock":null}
20:13:22.124 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.124 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/654
20:13:22.124 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":654,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up this morning at a little before 8 o'clock after a very boisterous night, the wind having increased to more than half a gale with a tremendous sea, right aft so that we made good way, though at the sacrifice of our comfort. Everything above &amp; below being wet &amp; in confusion. At 5 o'clock this morning a tremendous heavy sea pooped us, stove &amp; carried away our jolly boat &amp; alarmed us so much fearing it had stove in the dark lights &amp; if it had so happened we of course should have been waterlogged. Knowing the delicate state of the <span class=highlight_yellow>archboard</span>, where she was making a great deal of water, the fear of another heavy sea striking us kept me in a very uncomfortable state the whole of the day. Towards evening however both wind &amp; sea fell considerably. We have been going today from 6&frac12;  to 7 knots. Ship laboured very much &amp; made a deal of water. We consider we have got this evening considerably to the westward of the Naze of Norway, say 50 miles.</p>\r\n<p>A great deal of water having come into ...</p>","pageId":766,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":616,"lock":null}
20:13:22.124 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/655
20:13:22.124 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":655,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>More moderate weather. Wind NE. A fine breeze. Ship going about 4 knots. Let reefs out of the top sails, set top gallants sails, <span class=highlight_yellow>square mainsail free</span>, <span class=highlight_yellow>topmasts </span><span class=highlight_yellow>liering</span><span class=highlight_yellow> sail</span> &amp; gib.</p>\r\n<p>Read the duty &amp; Lessons of the day.</p>\r\n<p>The mainsail being split, unbent it &amp; got up another. The breeze rather freshened. This afternoon at NNE &amp; B by E. In the evening took a reef in each topsail &amp; stowed topgallant sails.</p>\r\n<p>Between 9 &amp; 10 turned in, being by my calculation about 100 miles from the Land</p>","pageId":766,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":617,"lock":null}
20:13:22.124 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.124 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/655
20:13:22.124 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":655,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>More moderate weather. Wind NE. A fine breeze. Ship going about 4 knots. Let reefs out of the top sails, set top gallants sails, <span class=highlight_yellow>square mainsail free</span>, <span class=highlight_yellow>topmasts </span><span class=highlight_yellow>liering</span><span class=highlight_yellow> sail</span> &amp; gib.</p>\r\n<p>Read the duty &amp; Lessons of the day.</p>\r\n<p>The mainsail being split, unbent it &amp; got up another. The breeze rather freshened. This afternoon at NNE &amp; B by E. In the evening took a reef in each topsail &amp; stowed topgallant sails.</p>\r\n<p>Between 9 &amp; 10 turned in, being by my calculation about 100 miles from the Land</p>","pageId":766,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":617,"lock":null}
20:13:22.124 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/656
20:13:22.124 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":656,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up this morning much disappointed at not finding ourselves within 20 miles of land, which we should have been had the wind continued as it was last night. But unfortunately it has changed in the night to NW &amp; NW by W &amp; we are now only going 3 knots. The weather fine, but cloudy. Hope we shall have a change before night for I'm anxious to land at Shields.</p>","pageId":766,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":618,"lock":null}
20:13:22.124 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.125 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/656
20:13:22.125 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":656,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up this morning much disappointed at not finding ourselves within 20 miles of land, which we should have been had the wind continued as it was last night. But unfortunately it has changed in the night to NW &amp; NW by W &amp; we are now only going 3 knots. The weather fine, but cloudy. Hope we shall have a change before night for I'm anxious to land at Shields.</p>","pageId":766,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":618,"lock":null}
20:13:22.125 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/657
20:13:22.125 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":657,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":17,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>We are now about 80 miles from the land, returning about SW. Continued this course. Ship making a deal of water.</p>","pageId":767,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":619,"lock":null}
20:13:22.125 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.125 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/657
20:13:22.125 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":657,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":17,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>We are now about 80 miles from the land, returning about SW. Continued this course. Ship making a deal of water.</p>","pageId":767,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":619,"lock":null}
20:13:22.125 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/658
20:13:22.125 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":658,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull couldy morning with rain fresh breeze etc W by N going only 3 &frac12;  knots. At &frac12; past 6 o'clock being thick hazy weather we made Huntcliff foot at least we concluded it to be so. This at first we thought it Tynemouth. We lay the ship to with her head off.</p>","pageId":767,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":620,"lock":null}
20:13:22.125 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.125 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/658
20:13:22.125 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":658,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull couldy morning with rain fresh breeze etc W by N going only 3 &frac12;  knots. At &frac12; past 6 o'clock being thick hazy weather we made Huntcliff foot at least we concluded it to be so. This at first we thought it Tynemouth. We lay the ship to with her head off.</p>","pageId":767,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":620,"lock":null}
20:13:22.125 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/659
20:13:22.126 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":659,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>This morning thick weather the land in sight like a fog bank, but clearing away we found it for certain to be Huntcliff foot, bearing west about five miles. During the morning light <span class=highlight_yellow>wind</span> variable &amp; in the afternoon calm with tremendous heavy rain, thunder &amp; lightning. At night the wind being from the NE light breeze &amp; I very unwell with <span class=highlight_yellow>scumalign</span>. The ship short of Stocks as water coals &amp; pump gear out of order &amp; considering she might reach shields, by daylight, we determined to work to windward &amp; turned in for the night.</p>","pageId":767,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":621,"lock":null}
20:13:22.126 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.126 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/659
20:13:22.126 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":659,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>This morning thick weather the land in sight like a fog bank, but clearing away we found it for certain to be Huntcliff foot, bearing west about five miles. During the morning light <span class=highlight_yellow>wind</span> variable &amp; in the afternoon calm with tremendous heavy rain, thunder &amp; lightning. At night the wind being from the NE light breeze &amp; I very unwell with <span class=highlight_yellow>scumalign</span>. The ship short of Stocks as water coals &amp; pump gear out of order &amp; considering she might reach shields, by daylight, we determined to work to windward &amp; turned in for the night.</p>","pageId":767,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":621,"lock":null}
20:13:22.126 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/66
20:13:22.126 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":66,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":3,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine but cold day. Wind N by E. At church in the morning. Walked to Tynmouth in the afternoon. Dined at home</p>","pageId":691,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":63,"lock":null}
20:13:22.126 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.126 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/66
20:13:22.126 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":66,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":3,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine but cold day. Wind N by E. At church in the morning. Walked to Tynmouth in the afternoon. Dined at home</p>","pageId":691,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":63,"lock":null}
20:13:22.126 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/660
20:13:22.126 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":660,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out this morning between 5 &amp; 6 o'clock found the ship turning to windward off Marsden Rock blowing hard from N by E. The wind having increased during the night with a high sea. At about 9 o'clock, the breeze increasing &amp; no chance of us reaching Tynemouth of getting on shore. Even if we had, we bore away for London much to our chagrin &amp; disappointment having had Shields Dockwray Square <span class=highlight_yellow>etc</span> in view &amp; not able to ...</p>","pageId":767,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":622,"lock":null}
20:13:22.126 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
