20:13:22.132 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":672,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":29,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... made ourselves decent &amp; comfortable Bob &amp; I walked up to George in the Red Lion Square where we made &amp; enjoyed a hearty dinner of pigeon &amp; veal pies &amp; cold <span class=highlight_yellow>mullion</span>, discharged a good glass of punch &amp; returned to Chambers. With the <span class=highlight_yellow>appearance</span> of Mrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Furmedye</span>, Bob's <span class=highlight_yellow>laudress</span>, I made myself a good perch for the night with Bob's <span class=highlight_yellow>mallrafs</span> in the corner of his room, turned in &amp; enjoyed an excellent nights rest, although the bed was rather a hard one.</p>\r\n<p>Thus ends our Petersburg voyage which upon the whole we have enjoyed, but we could have dispensed with the tumultuous bad weather we experienced. Thank God we have got back safe &amp; without any accident worth mentioning to the ship.</p>","pageId":771,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":634,"lock":null}
20:13:22.132 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/673
20:13:22.132 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":673,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up much refreshed. More moderate weather. Wind NE rather cloudy. We fully intended to have gone to church, but Bob &amp; I took up so much linin in the washing &amp; cleaning ourselves that it was past the hour before we were aware of it. Turned out a very fine day. We called upon Mr Ward who had gone to Paris will William. Walked through St James park up to Hyde Park where we strolled till 6 o'clock. Very few people or carriages there. Town exceedingly thin from thence came we went to Mr Piazza Covent garden &amp; enjoyed a comfortable dinner &amp; a good bottle of old port. Returned to Chambers between 10 &amp; 11 o'clock &amp; went to bed.</p>","pageId":771,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":635,"lock":null}
20:13:22.132 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.133 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/673
20:13:22.133 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":673,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up much refreshed. More moderate weather. Wind NE rather cloudy. We fully intended to have gone to church, but Bob &amp; I took up so much linin in the washing &amp; cleaning ourselves that it was past the hour before we were aware of it. Turned out a very fine day. We called upon Mr Ward who had gone to Paris will William. Walked through St James park up to Hyde Park where we strolled till 6 o'clock. Very few people or carriages there. Town exceedingly thin from thence came we went to Mr Piazza Covent garden &amp; enjoyed a comfortable dinner &amp; a good bottle of old port. Returned to Chambers between 10 &amp; 11 o'clock &amp; went to bed.</p>","pageId":771,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":635,"lock":null}
20:13:22.133 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/674
20:13:22.133 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":674,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy morning, rather cool. Wind NE. Walked into the city. Called at the office, nothing there. Proceeded after being at Chapmans to St Catherine's docks. The ship got safe in yesterday. Stephenson noted a protest this morning, the ship having been so leaky. Found Mrs Stephenson on board, eat some dinner with them. Attended <span class=highlight_yellow>cha</span><span class=highlight_yellow>mb</span><span class=highlight_yellow>er</span><span class=highlight_yellow>s</span>. Walked westward &amp; called upon Jobling.</p>","pageId":771,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":636,"lock":null}
20:13:22.133 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.133 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/674
20:13:22.133 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":674,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy morning, rather cool. Wind NE. Walked into the city. Called at the office, nothing there. Proceeded after being at Chapmans to St Catherine's docks. The ship got safe in yesterday. Stephenson noted a protest this morning, the ship having been so leaky. Found Mrs Stephenson on board, eat some dinner with them. Attended <span class=highlight_yellow>cha</span><span class=highlight_yellow>mb</span><span class=highlight_yellow>er</span><span class=highlight_yellow>s</span>. Walked westward &amp; called upon Jobling.</p>","pageId":771,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":636,"lock":null}
20:13:22.133 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/675
20:13:22.133 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":675,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull day &amp; showery. Walked into the city &amp; down to the docks. Found them employed in moving the ship to a birth &amp; then began to deliver her cargo before I left. Went to <span class=highlight_yellow>cha</span><span class=highlight_yellow>mbers</span> &amp; afterwards walked westward. Dined with Jobling in the Adelphi, only ourselves. Spent a pleasant day. Got rather too much wine. Slept all night in Villiers Street</p>","pageId":771,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":637,"lock":null}
20:13:22.133 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.134 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/675
20:13:22.134 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":675,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull day &amp; showery. Walked into the city &amp; down to the docks. Found them employed in moving the ship to a birth &amp; then began to deliver her cargo before I left. Went to <span class=highlight_yellow>cha</span><span class=highlight_yellow>mbers</span> &amp; afterwards walked westward. Dined with Jobling in the Adelphi, only ourselves. Spent a pleasant day. Got rather too much wine. Slept all night in Villiers Street</p>","pageId":771,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":637,"lock":null}
20:13:22.134 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/676
20:13:22.134 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":676,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind NW. Called upon Jobling. He drove me down to Woolwich to see the Lumley's. Eat some cold meat with them &amp; returned to the ship at Greenwich to dinner, where Tom Jobling joined us. Left the ship about 7 o'clock &amp; drove to town. Had a glass of brandy &amp; wine with Jobling &amp; got to bed at &frac12; past 10 o'clock</p>","pageId":771,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":638,"lock":null}
20:13:22.134 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.134 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/676
20:13:22.134 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":676,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind NW. Called upon Jobling. He drove me down to Woolwich to see the Lumley's. Eat some cold meat with them &amp; returned to the ship at Greenwich to dinner, where Tom Jobling joined us. Left the ship about 7 o'clock &amp; drove to town. Had a glass of brandy &amp; wine with Jobling &amp; got to bed at &frac12; past 10 o'clock</p>","pageId":771,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":638,"lock":null}
20:13:22.134 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/677
20:13:22.134 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":677,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW. Bob Marsh &amp; I walked into the city &amp; thence on board the Hope where we dined. The people busy getting the tallow out. Returned to Philpot Lane where we stopped until 6 o'clock with Mary Ann first time. Walked out of the city to chambers &amp; remained all evening. Received a letter from William which came yesterday. Did not answer it.</p>","pageId":772,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":639,"lock":null}
20:13:22.134 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.135 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/677
20:13:22.135 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":677,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW. Bob Marsh &amp; I walked into the city &amp; thence on board the Hope where we dined. The people busy getting the tallow out. Returned to Philpot Lane where we stopped until 6 o'clock with Mary Ann first time. Walked out of the city to chambers &amp; remained all evening. Received a letter from William which came yesterday. Did not answer it.</p>","pageId":772,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":639,"lock":null}
20:13:22.135 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/678
20:13:22.135 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":678,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine day. Wind the same. Bob &amp; I again walked into the city &amp; to the Hope where we lunched. Got all the tallow out today &amp; expect to deliver the copper. Returned to Philpot Lane where I met with Mr James Gale from Carlow. With Maryann again. Took a Greenwich boat at the tower Stairs &amp; went down to Watts, where I dined &amp; stayed all night.</p>","pageId":772,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":640,"lock":null}
20:13:22.135 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
