20:13:22.136 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":680,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":5,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<figure>\r\n  <a href=\"https://853.london/2014/03/10/bugsbys-holed-why-a-bit-of-greenwichs-history-is-under-threat/\">\r\n    <img src=\"images/bugsbys_reach.jpg\" width=\"640px\" />\r\n    <figcaption>Bugsby's Hole</figcaption>\r\n  </a>\r\n</figure>","pageId":null,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":null,"lock":null}
20:13:22.136 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/681
20:13:22.136 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":681,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":5,"sequence":3.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cloudy morning, with a slight shower or two of rain. Wind I think about WSW. Watt prevailed upon me to remain till Monday. Amused ourselves during the morning fishing for eels near Bugsby's Hole. Had poor sport, patience exhausted.  A great many large ships passed us from foreign, with some collisions. Dined at 6 o'clock &amp; in the evening played a rubber of whist</p>","pageId":772,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":641,"lock":null}
20:13:22.136 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
