20:13:22.138 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":684,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":7,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<figure>\r\n  <a href=\"https://pubwiki.co.uk/LondonPubs/Holborn/WhiteHorse.shtml\" >\r\n    <img src=\"images/img2920-WhiteHorse1896.jpg\" width=\"600px\" />\r\n    <figcaption>The White Horse, Fetter Lane, London</figcaption>\r\n  </a>\r\n</figure>","pageId":null,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":null,"lock":null}
20:13:22.138 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/685
20:13:22.138 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":685,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":7,"sequence":3.0000,"text":"<p>A showery day, at intervals, at intervals very fine. Wind about SE. Got into a Greenwich boat at &frac12; past 10 o'clock &amp; landed at Catherine dock. Found them busy with the <span class=highlight_yellow>lathwood</span> which was sold on Thursday to Mr Martin at &pound;16.5/- a fathom. Had not been long on board when Bob Marsh came. We had our dinner &amp; afterwards walked up to Philpot lane where I found a letter from William of his intention to be in town by the Highflyer in the evening.</p>\r\n<p>Called at J Chapmans &amp; from the state of the coal trades, the coal owners having again restricted the <span class=highlight_yellow>vends</span>, raised their price 5/- &amp; refusing either to freight or uphold, I almost determined to send the Hope to <span class=highlight_yellow>memel</span> at 21/- &amp; load for timber. Shall settle tomorrow.</p>\r\n<p>Bob &amp; I called upon J Hodgsons &amp; afterwards took a walk up Regent Street. Brought a new Hat at Oliphants &amp; a pair of trousers at Laffins. At &frac12; past 8 o'clock went to the Cock in Fleet Street &amp; eat some oysters &amp; at 10 o'clock met William &amp; Lea at the White Horse in Fetter Lane having just arrived from Shields by the Highflyer. A very wet night</p>","pageId":772,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":643,"lock":null}
20:13:22.138 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.138 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/685
20:13:22.138 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":685,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":7,"sequence":3.0000,"text":"<p>A showery day, at intervals, at intervals very fine. Wind about SE. Got into a Greenwich boat at &frac12; past 10 o'clock &amp; landed at Catherine dock. Found them busy with the <span class=highlight_yellow>lathwood</span> which was sold on Thursday to Mr Martin at &pound;16.5/- a fathom. Had not been long on board when Bob Marsh came. We had our dinner &amp; afterwards walked up to Philpot lane where I found a letter from William of his intention to be in town by the Highflyer in the evening.</p>\r\n<p>Called at J Chapmans &amp; from the state of the coal trades, the coal owners having again restricted the <span class=highlight_yellow>vends</span>, raised their price 5/- &amp; refusing either to freight or uphold, I almost determined to send the Hope to <span class=highlight_yellow>memel</span> at 21/- &amp; load for timber. Shall settle tomorrow.</p>\r\n<p>Bob &amp; I called upon J Hodgsons &amp; afterwards took a walk up Regent Street. Brought a new Hat at Oliphants &amp; a pair of trousers at Laffins. At &frac12; past 8 o'clock went to the Cock in Fleet Street &amp; eat some oysters &amp; at 10 o'clock met William &amp; Lea at the White Horse in Fetter Lane having just arrived from Shields by the Highflyer. A very wet night</p>","pageId":772,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":643,"lock":null}
20:13:22.138 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/686
20:13:22.138 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":686,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Showery. Wind SW. William &amp; Lea called at new Inn &amp; we went into the city together in a coach. Called at Chapmans but did not freight the Hope, thinking to send her to Shields. Walked down to the ship. William took J Galbraith to Nottingham Place with him. I &amp; J Hodgson ...</p>","pageId":772,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":644,"lock":null}
