20:13:22.151 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":711,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind WNW. Received a letter from William &amp; another from Richmond putting off my visit until Thursday next. Went over to South Shields &amp; called upon ____. Received the butcher for William. Returned &amp; took a walk to Cullercoats. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. The children sailed this afternoon. At the whist club in the evening.</p>","pageId":777,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":669,"lock":null}
20:13:22.151 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/712
20:13:22.151 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":712,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind NE. Afterwards turned out pleasant. Captain Webb &amp; I walked to Whitley Park &amp; called upon Mr J Wright. Returned by Cullercoats &amp; the sands through Tynemouth. Dined at 2 o'clock. At the <span class=highlight_yellow>Mallard</span> soon in the afternoon. At &frac12; past 7 o'clock went to meet Ann but she was not at the place of appointment. Drank tea &amp; spent the evening with Miss Tinley. Playing at cards with the boys. Wind changed. Rained in the evening to SE</p>","pageId":777,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":670,"lock":null}
20:13:22.151 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
