20:13:22.165 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":741,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Most delightful weather. Wind NW. Mrs Glover called &amp; I paid her dividend upon G Morrison's estate. Walked to Tynemouth &amp; called upon Mr R Airey. Dined at home. Saw <font color=#00B0F0>Ann Maxwell</font><font color=#00B0F0> </font>in the evening</p>","pageId":780,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":695,"lock":null}
20:13:22.165 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/742
20:13:22.165 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":742,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":27,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>Went to the theatre &amp; saw Madam Vestris again. She &amp; her sister Miss Bartolozzi performed for the benefit. About ___ in the house</p>","pageId":781,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":696,"lock":null}
20:13:22.165 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.165 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/742
20:13:22.165 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":742,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":27,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>Went to the theatre &amp; saw Madam Vestris again. She &amp; her sister Miss Bartolozzi performed for the benefit. About ___ in the house</p>","pageId":781,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":696,"lock":null}
20:13:22.165 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/743
20:13:22.165 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":743,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. After a rainy night &amp; wind NE, changed now to NNW. During the day variable between W by N &amp; NNE and cold. A sea upon the bar. Amused myself drawing all the morning. Dined at home. Received from Robert &pound;7 on WBS account for newspapers sent Commercial Rooms &amp; &pound;1.18.6 on account of Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>albraith</font>'s.</p>\r\n<p>The Grenville Bay &amp; Love arrived from Greenland well <span class=highlight_yellow>fisked</span>. H Harry &amp; I had a bottle of port together at the George. With Ann Stokes in the evening</p>","pageId":781,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":697,"lock":null}
20:13:22.165 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.166 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/743
20:13:22.166 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":743,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. After a rainy night &amp; wind NE, changed now to NNW. During the day variable between W by N &amp; NNE and cold. A sea upon the bar. Amused myself drawing all the morning. Dined at home. Received from Robert &pound;7 on WBS account for newspapers sent Commercial Rooms &amp; &pound;1.18.6 on account of Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>albraith</font>'s.</p>\r\n<p>The Grenville Bay &amp; Love arrived from Greenland well <span class=highlight_yellow>fisked</span>. H Harry &amp; I had a bottle of port together at the George. With Ann Stokes in the evening</p>","pageId":781,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":697,"lock":null}
20:13:22.166 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/744
20:13:22.166 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":744,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; milder weather. Wind WNW. Engaged the principle part of the morning in drawing. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. In the evening eat some oysters at <span class=highlight_yellow>Marks</span> &amp; afterwards attended  the whist club.</p>","pageId":781,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":698,"lock":null}
20:13:22.166 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.166 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/744
20:13:22.166 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":744,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; milder weather. Wind WNW. Engaged the principle part of the morning in drawing. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. In the evening eat some oysters at <span class=highlight_yellow>Marks</span> &amp; afterwards attended  the whist club.</p>","pageId":781,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":698,"lock":null}
20:13:22.166 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/745
20:13:22.166 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":745,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning. Wind WNW. Again engaged the morning in drawing. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. H Harry &amp; I went to the Commercial &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>punished</span> two bottles of port. His treat having heard of the safe arrival of the Choice at Hull from <span class=highlight_yellow>Wybarz</span> making the voyage in two months. In the evening at Mrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Lays</span> at Tynemouth. Drank tea &amp; played a rubber.</p>","pageId":781,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":699,"lock":null}
20:13:22.166 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.166 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/745
20:13:22.166 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":745,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning. Wind WNW. Again engaged the morning in drawing. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. H Harry &amp; I went to the Commercial &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>punished</span> two bottles of port. His treat having heard of the safe arrival of the Choice at Hull from <span class=highlight_yellow>Wybarz</span> making the voyage in two months. In the evening at Mrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Lays</span> at Tynemouth. Drank tea &amp; played a rubber.</p>","pageId":781,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":699,"lock":null}
20:13:22.166 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/746
20:13:22.166 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":746,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather cool. Wind changeable between NNW &amp; NNE. Sea high, having blown very hard early this morning from NE. Emma Galbraith came to spend the day with Mrs Scott. Took a walk with her round by Preston Lane etc. Dined at 5 o'clock with Allen, J Craig, J Wright, W Harrison &amp; Robinson of the 80<sup>th</sup> there. Spent a pleasant day &amp; won of W Harrison &pound;6</p>","pageId":781,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":700,"lock":null}
20:13:22.166 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.167 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/746
20:13:22.167 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":746,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather cool. Wind changeable between NNW &amp; NNE. Sea high, having blown very hard early this morning from NE. Emma Galbraith came to spend the day with Mrs Scott. Took a walk with her round by Preston Lane etc. Dined at 5 o'clock with Allen, J Craig, J Wright, W Harrison &amp; Robinson of the 80<sup>th</sup> there. Spent a pleasant day &amp; won of W Harrison &pound;6</p>","pageId":781,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":700,"lock":null}
20:13:22.167 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/747
20:13:22.167 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":747,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Rather frosty. Wind NNW. The sea still continues heavy upon the bar. Attended morning services.</p>\r\n<p>Received a letter from WBS &amp; another from Captain Stephenson dated <span class=highlight_yellow>aneruel</span> 17<sup>th</sup> Oct &amp; expecting to sail next day. London on the 15<sup>th</sup> drawn upon Chapmans for expenses &pound;93.4/- which I consider heavy.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home at 2 o'clock &amp; afterwards took a walk to Tynemouth with H Harry. Mrs Scott not so well. Indeed the Dr considering her getting considerably worse. The disease having extended to the armpits.</p>\r\n<p>At the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":781,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":701,"lock":null}
20:13:22.167 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.167 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/747
20:13:22.167 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":747,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Rather frosty. Wind NNW. The sea still continues heavy upon the bar. Attended morning services.</p>\r\n<p>Received a letter from WBS &amp; another from Captain Stephenson dated <span class=highlight_yellow>aneruel</span> 17<sup>th</sup> Oct &amp; expecting to sail next day. London on the 15<sup>th</sup> drawn upon Chapmans for expenses &pound;93.4/- which I consider heavy.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home at 2 o'clock &amp; afterwards took a walk to Tynemouth with H Harry. Mrs Scott not so well. Indeed the Dr considering her getting considerably worse. The disease having extended to the armpits.</p>\r\n<p>At the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":781,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":701,"lock":null}
20:13:22.167 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/748
20:13:22.167 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":748,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild morning. Wind SW. Attended the justice room until dinner time. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. Played at billiards with Ben Wright until 10 o'clock. Several ships got down.</p>","pageId":781,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":702,"lock":null}
20:13:22.167 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
