20:13:22.168 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":75,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":3,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day &amp; extremely mild. Wind WNW. Dined at home</p>","pageId":692,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":72,"lock":null}
20:13:22.168 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.168 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/75
20:13:22.168 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":75,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":3,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day &amp; extremely mild. Wind WNW. Dined at home</p>","pageId":692,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":72,"lock":null}
20:13:22.168 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/750
20:13:22.168 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":750,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind NW. Captain Webb &amp; I took a walk round by the sands to Cullercoats &amp; returned by the fields. Dined at the house at 2 o'clock. Mark came in after dinner &amp; took a bottle of port with me. With Bill Jervis. In the evening at the whist club</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":704,"lock":null}
20:13:22.168 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.169 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/750
20:13:22.169 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":750,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind NW. Captain Webb &amp; I took a walk round by the sands to Cullercoats &amp; returned by the fields. Dined at the house at 2 o'clock. Mark came in after dinner &amp; took a bottle of port with me. With Bill Jervis. In the evening at the whist club</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":704,"lock":null}
20:13:22.169 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/751
20:13:22.169 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":751,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild morning with the appearance of rain. Wind WSW. Dined at the George Tavern with William Harrison who had last a <span class=highlight_yellow>diciseen</span> upon the death of Major <span class=highlight_yellow>Wergs</span>. He (WH) saying that the major was killed at Corunna when it was at S<sup>t</sup> Sabastian's. Had an exceedingly pleasant day &amp; excellent dinner &amp; wine. Present J Tinley, Captain French, Mr West &amp; Mr Robinson of the 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment, Mr Allen, William, Tom &amp; Benj Wright, I Craig, Mr Christie of London, Mr Harrison &amp; myself</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":705,"lock":null}
20:13:22.169 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.169 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/751
20:13:22.169 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":751,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild morning with the appearance of rain. Wind WSW. Dined at the George Tavern with William Harrison who had last a <span class=highlight_yellow>diciseen</span> upon the death of Major <span class=highlight_yellow>Wergs</span>. He (WH) saying that the major was killed at Corunna when it was at S<sup>t</sup> Sabastian's. Had an exceedingly pleasant day &amp; excellent dinner &amp; wine. Present J Tinley, Captain French, Mr West &amp; Mr Robinson of the 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment, Mr Allen, William, Tom &amp; Benj Wright, I Craig, Mr Christie of London, Mr Harrison &amp; myself</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":705,"lock":null}
20:13:22.169 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/752
20:13:22.169 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":752,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind NW. The air rather frosty. Intended going to Newcastle with H Harry but prevented by a most disturbing letter from captain Stephenson of the Hope dated <i>Elsinore</i><i> </i>the 24<sup>th</sup> Oct informing me of the loss of poor J Galbraith. He having fallen overboard from the maintop sail yard when reefing pitching upon the top in his fall, poor fellow, his career has been short but &lsquo;tis all for the best. I hope he has left a world of misery &amp; is now I trust happy with his dear parents. Remained in the house all day in consequence of this sad news. Wrote to WBS, Mr Vernon &amp; D Dixon</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":706,"lock":null}
20:13:22.169 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.169 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/752
20:13:22.169 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":752,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind NW. The air rather frosty. Intended going to Newcastle with H Harry but prevented by a most disturbing letter from captain Stephenson of the Hope dated <i>Elsinore</i><i> </i>the 24<sup>th</sup> Oct informing me of the loss of poor J Galbraith. He having fallen overboard from the maintop sail yard when reefing pitching upon the top in his fall, poor fellow, his career has been short but &lsquo;tis all for the best. I hope he has left a world of misery &amp; is now I trust happy with his dear parents. Remained in the house all day in consequence of this sad news. Wrote to WBS, Mr Vernon &amp; D Dixon</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":706,"lock":null}
20:13:22.169 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/753
20:13:22.169 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":753,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather cool. Wind NW. In consequence of the account of J Galbraith's death, did not go to church. Dined at home. In the evening went &amp; drank tea with J Tinley. Turned out a boisterous night.</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":707,"lock":null}
20:13:22.169 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.170 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/753
20:13:22.170 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":753,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather cool. Wind NW. In consequence of the account of J Galbraith's death, did not go to church. Dined at home. In the evening went &amp; drank tea with J Tinley. Turned out a boisterous night.</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":707,"lock":null}
20:13:22.170 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/754
20:13:22.170 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":754,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine autumnal morning. Wind NW by W. Sea high upon the bar. Took a walk with mark &amp; captain Webb round by Cullercoats. Held the annual meeting at newsrooms. Old Crofs discharged in consequence of his continued disgraceful &amp; insolent conduct. Temple,  Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Lins</span><span class=highlight_yellow> </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Rell's</span> late butler appointed in his place. Dined at home at 2 o'clock.</p>\r\n<p>Fanny Smith arrived from Togston for a few days.</p>\r\n<p>Paid <span class=highlight_yellow>Sab</span><sup><span class=highlight_yellow>n</span></sup><sup> </sup>to newsroom 30/.</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":708,"lock":null}
20:13:22.170 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.170 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/754
20:13:22.170 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":754,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine autumnal morning. Wind NW by W. Sea high upon the bar. Took a walk with mark &amp; captain Webb round by Cullercoats. Held the annual meeting at newsrooms. Old Crofs discharged in consequence of his continued disgraceful &amp; insolent conduct. Temple,  Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Lins</span><span class=highlight_yellow> </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Rell's</span> late butler appointed in his place. Dined at home at 2 o'clock.</p>\r\n<p>Fanny Smith arrived from Togston for a few days.</p>\r\n<p>Paid <span class=highlight_yellow>Sab</span><sup><span class=highlight_yellow>n</span></sup><sup> </sup>to newsroom 30/.</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":708,"lock":null}
20:13:22.170 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/755
20:13:22.170 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":755,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp morning. Wind SW &amp; blowing fresh. Walked out. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. Emma came from school for a few days. Spent the evening at home</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":709,"lock":null}
20:13:22.170 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.171 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/755
20:13:22.171 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":755,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp morning. Wind SW &amp; blowing fresh. Walked out. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. Emma came from school for a few days. Spent the evening at home</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":709,"lock":null}
20:13:22.171 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/756
20:13:22.171 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":756,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull thick morning. Wind W by N. Received a letter from WBS. No account yet of the Hope's arrival. At the billiard room all the morning. Dined at home at 4 o'clock &amp; spent the evening in the house. Paid Mrs Stephenson  mom o &pound;4 carpenter &pound;2.5/- &amp; cook &pound;1.10/-</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":710,"lock":null}
20:13:22.171 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.171 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/756
20:13:22.171 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":756,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull thick morning. Wind W by N. Received a letter from WBS. No account yet of the Hope's arrival. At the billiard room all the morning. Dined at home at 4 o'clock &amp; spent the evening in the house. Paid Mrs Stephenson  mom o &pound;4 carpenter &pound;2.5/- &amp; cook &pound;1.10/-</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":710,"lock":null}
20:13:22.171 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/757
20:13:22.171 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":757,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A foggy and wet morning. Wind WSW. At the news room &amp; in the house all the morning. Received a notice from Brown of the George to quit in May. Called &amp; told him I would not accept it. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. In the evening went to the whist club being a wet evening Tom Smith would not go. Wrote to <span class=highlight_aqua>Baker Galbraith</span></p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":711,"lock":null}
20:13:22.171 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.172 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/757
20:13:22.172 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":757,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A foggy and wet morning. Wind WSW. At the news room &amp; in the house all the morning. Received a notice from Brown of the George to quit in May. Called &amp; told him I would not accept it. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. In the evening went to the whist club being a wet evening Tom Smith would not go. Wrote to <span class=highlight_aqua>Baker Galbraith</span></p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":711,"lock":null}
20:13:22.172 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/758
20:13:22.172 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":758,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Blowing hard from the SE. Walked to Shields with Tom Smith. He set off for Togston, being such an unpleasant morning. Fanny remained. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. Took wine with H Harry &amp; J Cunningham at the Commercial.</p>","pageId":783,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":712,"lock":null}
20:13:22.172 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.172 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/758
20:13:22.172 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":758,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Blowing hard from the SE. Walked to Shields with Tom Smith. He set off for Togston, being such an unpleasant morning. Fanny remained. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. Took wine with H Harry &amp; J Cunningham at the Commercial.</p>","pageId":783,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":712,"lock":null}
20:13:22.172 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/759
20:13:22.172 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":759,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A thick &amp; very damp morning, having been a great deal of rain. Wind South. Fanny Smith left for Togston. Dined with Boswell on board the William Shard. Mark, H Harry &amp; Richardson took wine with us. Spent a pleasant day.</p>","pageId":783,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":713,"lock":null}
20:13:22.172 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.173 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/759
20:13:22.173 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":759,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A thick &amp; very damp morning, having been a great deal of rain. Wind South. Fanny Smith left for Togston. Dined with Boswell on board the William Shard. Mark, H Harry &amp; Richardson took wine with us. Spent a pleasant day.</p>","pageId":783,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":713,"lock":null}
20:13:22.173 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/76
20:13:22.173 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":76,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":3,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine weather. Wind WNW. Engaged painting ship. Several ships sailed for the Baltic. Dined at home</p>","pageId":692,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":73,"lock":null}
20:13:22.173 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.173 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/76
20:13:22.173 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":76,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":3,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine weather. Wind WNW. Engaged painting ship. Several ships sailed for the Baltic. Dined at home</p>","pageId":692,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":73,"lock":null}
20:13:22.173 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/760
20:13:22.173 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":760,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet day. Wind N &amp; NE. Went to church in the morning. Dined at home. Boswell &amp; I took wine &amp; tea with H Harry. At the Mulstrum in the evening.</p>","pageId":783,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":714,"lock":null}
20:13:22.173 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.174 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/760
20:13:22.174 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":760,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet day. Wind N &amp; NE. Went to church in the morning. Dined at home. Boswell &amp; I took wine &amp; tea with H Harry. At the Mulstrum in the evening.</p>","pageId":783,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":714,"lock":null}
20:13:22.174 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/761
20:13:22.174 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":761,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A rainy morning. After a stormy night. Wind variable N by W. N &amp; NE &amp; a heavy sea upon the bar. Wrote to WBS &amp; sent him an account of rents. Received a letter from him of the arrival of the Hope at Gravesend. Dined at 5 o'clock at J Tinley's. William &amp; H Metcalf, H Dale, Mr Gosling, R A J. Wright jn &amp; Mr Duncan from Liverpool there. A very pleasant party.</p>","pageId":783,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":715,"lock":null}
20:13:22.174 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.174 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/761
20:13:22.174 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":761,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A rainy morning. After a stormy night. Wind variable N by W. N &amp; NE &amp; a heavy sea upon the bar. Wrote to WBS &amp; sent him an account of rents. Received a letter from him of the arrival of the Hope at Gravesend. Dined at 5 o'clock at J Tinley's. William &amp; H Metcalf, H Dale, Mr Gosling, R A J. Wright jn &amp; Mr Duncan from Liverpool there. A very pleasant party.</p>","pageId":783,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":715,"lock":null}
20:13:22.174 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/762
20:13:22.174 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":762,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp, thick morning. Wind NW &amp; cold. Dined with Bill Wright on board the Stephen. J Wright jr &amp; Mr Hawks, H French, Mr Wright, Mr Watt, Mr Hobroyd, Mr Hall &amp; myself.</p>","pageId":783,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":716,"lock":null}
20:13:22.174 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
