20:13:22.178 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":769,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very stormy morning &amp; a heavy gale of wind at E by N with sleet showers &amp; been so all night. Increased <font color=#BFBFBF>to </font>a perfect hurricane with a most tremendous sea. Dined at home. H Harry, H Nicolson, Boswell &amp; I had some punch at the Commercial.</p>","pageId":784,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":723,"lock":null}
20:13:22.178 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/77
20:13:22.178 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":77,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":3,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful mild weather. Wind WSW. The Grenville bay sailed for Greenland Dined at Mrs Banks</p>","pageId":692,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":74,"lock":null}
20:13:22.178 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.178 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/77
20:13:22.178 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":77,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":3,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful mild weather. Wind WSW. The Grenville bay sailed for Greenland Dined at Mrs Banks</p>","pageId":692,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":74,"lock":null}
20:13:22.178 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/770
20:13:22.178 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":770,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Weather more moderate &amp; sea much fallen. Wind SE. Dined at home. Had some punch on board the Unanimity with H Nicholson. Attended the card club &amp; had some oysters in the evening with H Harry at Jane Moors.</p>","pageId":784,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":724,"lock":null}
20:13:22.178 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.179 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/770
20:13:22.179 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":770,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Weather more moderate &amp; sea much fallen. Wind SE. Dined at home. Had some punch on board the Unanimity with H Nicholson. Attended the card club &amp; had some oysters in the evening with H Harry at Jane Moors.</p>","pageId":784,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":724,"lock":null}
20:13:22.179 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/771
20:13:22.179 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":771,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Thick weather. Wind NW. Drew &pound;5 out of Chapmans. Dined at home. H Harry, Boswell, Nicholson &amp; I took grog together at the Commercial &amp; afterwards went to the theatre</p>","pageId":784,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":725,"lock":null}
20:13:22.179 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.179 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/771
20:13:22.179 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":771,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Thick weather. Wind NW. Drew &pound;5 out of Chapmans. Dined at home. H Harry, Boswell, Nicholson &amp; I took grog together at the Commercial &amp; afterwards went to the theatre</p>","pageId":784,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":725,"lock":null}
20:13:22.179 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/772
20:13:22.179 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":772,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A thick dull morning with a little rain. Wind about north. Allen &amp; I took a walk to Tynemouth. Government having given up the burial ground to the parish again, excepting 40 feet round the sides of the yard. Dined at home.</p>\r\n<p>Spent the evening with Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Lewison</span>, H Harry, and A Nicholson at the Duke of York.</p>","pageId":784,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":726,"lock":null}
20:13:22.179 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.180 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/772
20:13:22.180 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":772,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A thick dull morning with a little rain. Wind about north. Allen &amp; I took a walk to Tynemouth. Government having given up the burial ground to the parish again, excepting 40 feet round the sides of the yard. Dined at home.</p>\r\n<p>Spent the evening with Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Lewison</span>, H Harry, and A Nicholson at the Duke of York.</p>","pageId":784,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":726,"lock":null}
20:13:22.180 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/773
20:13:22.180 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":773,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A foggy and damp morning. Wind SW. Received a letter from Stephenson of the Hope being out on Saturday having delivered 279 loads 49 feet of timber equal to 320 loads with deals of broken stowage.</p>\r\n<p>Took Emma to church with me. Dined at home &amp; afterwards took wine with Boswell. H Harry &amp; Allen there.</p>\r\n<p>In the evening at mother Maxwell's</p>","pageId":784,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":727,"lock":null}
20:13:22.180 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.180 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/773
20:13:22.180 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":773,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A foggy and damp morning. Wind SW. Received a letter from Stephenson of the Hope being out on Saturday having delivered 279 loads 49 feet of timber equal to 320 loads with deals of broken stowage.</p>\r\n<p>Took Emma to church with me. Dined at home &amp; afterwards took wine with Boswell. H Harry &amp; Allen there.</p>\r\n<p>In the evening at mother Maxwell's</p>","pageId":784,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":727,"lock":null}
20:13:22.180 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/774
20:13:22.180 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":774,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather. Wind SW. Received a letter from William. Dined with H Harry on board the Choice. A pleasant party.</p>","pageId":784,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":728,"lock":null}
20:13:22.180 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.181 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/774
20:13:22.181 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":774,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather. Wind SW. Received a letter from William. Dined with H Harry on board the Choice. A pleasant party.</p>","pageId":784,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":728,"lock":null}
20:13:22.181 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/775
20:13:22.181 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":775,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull &amp; damp morning. Wind S. Afterwards got to SE blowing very hard towards night with heavy rain. Mrs Scott so unwell obliged to keep her bed &amp; not able to see any person. Dined at home. Drank tea &amp; spent the evening at J Tinley's</p>","pageId":785,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":729,"lock":null}
20:13:22.181 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.181 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/775
20:13:22.181 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":775,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull &amp; damp morning. Wind S. Afterwards got to SE blowing very hard towards night with heavy rain. Mrs Scott so unwell obliged to keep her bed &amp; not able to see any person. Dined at home. Drank tea &amp; spent the evening at J Tinley's</p>","pageId":785,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":729,"lock":null}
20:13:22.181 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/776
20:13:22.181 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":776,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another damp &amp; unpleasant morning. After a stormy night, a heavy sea upon the bar. Wind SE.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home. At another max with Catherine. In the evening went to South Shields to Mr Bullocks &amp; partook of an oyster supper &amp; milk. Punch with H Harry, Boswell, Allen &amp; J Richardson. The oysters very large &amp; fine, from Wells</p>","pageId":785,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":730,"lock":null}
20:13:22.181 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.182 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/776
20:13:22.182 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":776,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another damp &amp; unpleasant morning. After a stormy night, a heavy sea upon the bar. Wind SE.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home. At another max with Catherine. In the evening went to South Shields to Mr Bullocks &amp; partook of an oyster supper &amp; milk. Punch with H Harry, Boswell, Allen &amp; J Richardson. The oysters very large &amp; fine, from Wells</p>","pageId":785,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":730,"lock":null}
20:13:22.182 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/777
20:13:22.182 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":777,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very unpleasant damp morning. Wind about south with a heavy sea upon the bar. Two ships have got upon the rock in entering the harbour. Dined at home. Mr Allen came &amp; took wine with me. In the evening attended the whist club.</p>","pageId":785,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":731,"lock":null}
20:13:22.182 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.182 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/777
20:13:22.182 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":777,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very unpleasant damp morning. Wind about south with a heavy sea upon the bar. Two ships have got upon the rock in entering the harbour. Dined at home. Mr Allen came &amp; took wine with me. In the evening attended the whist club.</p>","pageId":785,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":731,"lock":null}
20:13:22.182 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/778
20:13:22.182 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":778,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather but still rather foggy &amp; dull. Wind S &amp; S by E. The <span class=highlight_yellow>Qurnoury</span> belonging to <font color=#222222>Messrs</font><font color=#222222> </font>Young son got upon the rocks last night. Allen &amp; I walked round by Tynemouth &amp; the rocks to see them. Dined at home. Boswell treated H Nicholson &amp; me to some punch at the Mulstrum, it being his last night at Shields</p>","pageId":785,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":732,"lock":null}
20:13:22.182 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
