20:13:22.191 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":795,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A thick frost morning. Wind SW by W. Paid the washerwoman for a quarter washing &pound;1.11.6. On board the Hope. The carpenter busy fixing the new hook at the stern. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon. In the evening at home.</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":749,"lock":null}
20:13:22.191 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/796
20:13:22.191 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":796,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A foggy damp and very unpleasant morning. Some snow on the ground, having fallen during the night. Wind, the little there is NNW. Dined at 4 o'clock at Mr Metcalf's in Saville Street. A party there. Spent a pleasant day. Wrote to William. Called at the Bank. Spencer promised to under me what accommodation I <span class=highlight_yellow>may</span> want this Xmas. Paid Linskill &amp; etc &pound;24.11.6 for <span class=highlight_yellow>cordage</span> &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Lane</span> &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Spence</span> &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Foster</span> &pound;8.10/- for canvas</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":750,"lock":null}
20:13:22.191 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.191 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/796
20:13:22.191 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":796,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A foggy damp and very unpleasant morning. Some snow on the ground, having fallen during the night. Wind, the little there is NNW. Dined at 4 o'clock at Mr Metcalf's in Saville Street. A party there. Spent a pleasant day. Wrote to William. Called at the Bank. Spencer promised to under me what accommodation I <span class=highlight_yellow>may</span> want this Xmas. Paid Linskill &amp; etc &pound;24.11.6 for <span class=highlight_yellow>cordage</span> &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Lane</span> &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Spence</span> &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Foster</span> &pound;8.10/- for canvas</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":750,"lock":null}
20:13:22.191 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/797
20:13:22.191 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":797,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A frosty morning. Wind East. H Harry went with me on board the Hope to give me his advice with regard to the repairs. Found they had taken the broken hold beam out &amp; preparing a new one. Ordered several new <span class=highlight_yellow>kne</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span><span class=highlight_yellow>s</span> to be put in. Dined at home &amp; spent the evening</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":751,"lock":null}
20:13:22.191 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.192 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/797
20:13:22.192 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":797,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A frosty morning. Wind East. H Harry went with me on board the Hope to give me his advice with regard to the repairs. Found they had taken the broken hold beam out &amp; preparing a new one. Ordered several new <span class=highlight_yellow>kne</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span><span class=highlight_yellow>s</span> to be put in. Dined at home &amp; spent the evening</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":751,"lock":null}
20:13:22.192 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/798
20:13:22.192 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":798,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold frosty morning. Wind E by N. Been blowing a gale all night. A heavy sea upon the bar. On board the Hope. The master &amp; carpenter absent looking for some knees for the hold beans. Dined at home. H Harry came in &amp; took wine with me. Mrs Dixon down &amp; took Emma to Benton with her. Attended the whist club in the evening. Saw Ann Maxwell</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":752,"lock":null}
20:13:22.192 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.192 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/798
20:13:22.192 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":798,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold frosty morning. Wind E by N. Been blowing a gale all night. A heavy sea upon the bar. On board the Hope. The master &amp; carpenter absent looking for some knees for the hold beans. Dined at home. H Harry came in &amp; took wine with me. Mrs Dixon down &amp; took Emma to Benton with her. Attended the whist club in the evening. Saw Ann Maxwell</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":752,"lock":null}
20:13:22.192 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/799
20:13:22.192 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":799,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Xmas day. Seasonal weather. Very cold with a little snow. Wind East &amp; blowing hard. Walked up to Benton. Dined &amp; remained all night.</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":753,"lock":null}
20:13:22.192 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.192 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/799
20:13:22.192 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":799,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Xmas day. Seasonal weather. Very cold with a little snow. Wind East &amp; blowing hard. Walked up to Benton. Dined &amp; remained all night.</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":753,"lock":null}
20:13:22.192 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/8
20:13:22.192 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":8,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Again at Newcastle. Saw J Smith Senior &amp; Junior: the old gent: very kind, asked me to dine, &quot;no go&quot; entered upon the subject of the Ariel, showed them W S Brewer's accounts, they seemed to be of our opinion &amp; against any arbitration. Dined with Dixon, had a long conversation about his assisting me. He was extremely kind in his expressions, but said it was out of his power, from his heavy advances to others &amp; having heavy payments to make himself to but that he would consider about it. memo: Its what I expected, not much disappointed. A promise ought to be held sacred. Cold day with rain afternoon</p>","pageId":686,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":5,"lock":null}
20:13:22.192 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.193 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/8
20:13:22.193 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":8,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Again at Newcastle. Saw J Smith Senior &amp; Junior: the old gent: very kind, asked me to dine, &quot;no go&quot; entered upon the subject of the Ariel, showed them W S Brewer's accounts, they seemed to be of our opinion &amp; against any arbitration. Dined with Dixon, had a long conversation about his assisting me. He was extremely kind in his expressions, but said it was out of his power, from his heavy advances to others &amp; having heavy payments to make himself to but that he would consider about it. memo: Its what I expected, not much disappointed. A promise ought to be held sacred. Cold day with rain afternoon</p>","pageId":686,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":5,"lock":null}
20:13:22.193 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/80
20:13:22.193 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":80,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":3,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cloudy morning. Wind NNW. At church in the morning with Fanny Smith Walked to Tynemouth in the afternoon with J Tenley. Dined at home</p>","pageId":692,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":77,"lock":null}
20:13:22.193 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.193 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/80
20:13:22.193 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":80,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":3,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cloudy morning. Wind NNW. At church in the morning with Fanny Smith Walked to Tynemouth in the afternoon with J Tenley. Dined at home</p>","pageId":692,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":77,"lock":null}
20:13:22.193 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/800
20:13:22.193 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":800,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty morning. Wind ESE. A slight fall of snow during the day. Walked into Newcastle with Dixon. Nothing doing on the Quay side in the way of freights, at least none to suite me. Returned to Shields in a gig. Dined at home. In the evening attended the whist club at H Dales. Received a letter from Boswell from Rye informing me he had got 90 passengers for New York</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":754,"lock":null}
20:13:22.193 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.194 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/800
20:13:22.194 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":800,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty morning. Wind ESE. A slight fall of snow during the day. Walked into Newcastle with Dixon. Nothing doing on the Quay side in the way of freights, at least none to suite me. Returned to Shields in a gig. Dined at home. In the evening attended the whist club at H Dales. Received a letter from Boswell from Rye informing me he had got 90 passengers for New York</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":754,"lock":null}
20:13:22.194 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/801
20:13:22.194 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":801,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine seasonal morning. Wind NW &amp; snowing heavy. Did not go to church. Made up the Hope's <span class=highlight_yellow>final</span> voyage in the ships <span class=highlight_yellow>log</span>. She clears nothing much to my unsurprised &amp; disappointment. Dined with H Harry. In the evening with Bell Jarvis &amp; Jane Dryden.</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":755,"lock":null}
20:13:22.194 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.194 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/801
20:13:22.194 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":801,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine seasonal morning. Wind NW &amp; snowing heavy. Did not go to church. Made up the Hope's <span class=highlight_yellow>final</span> voyage in the ships <span class=highlight_yellow>log</span>. She clears nothing much to my unsurprised &amp; disappointment. Dined with H Harry. In the evening with Bell Jarvis &amp; Jane Dryden.</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":755,"lock":null}
20:13:22.194 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/802
20:13:22.194 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":802,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of frost, but not yet much snow has fallen. Wind NW. On board the Hope. The carpenter nearly finished. Intend hauling her off the shore at high water. Dined at home.</p>\r\n<p>Mary <span class=highlight_yellow>Carss</span> called upon me.</p>\r\n<p>H Harry, Mark &amp; I had a glass of grog together. Spent the evening at home.</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":756,"lock":null}
20:13:22.194 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.194 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/802
20:13:22.194 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":802,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of frost, but not yet much snow has fallen. Wind NW. On board the Hope. The carpenter nearly finished. Intend hauling her off the shore at high water. Dined at home.</p>\r\n<p>Mary <span class=highlight_yellow>Carss</span> called upon me.</p>\r\n<p>H Harry, Mark &amp; I had a glass of grog together. Spent the evening at home.</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":756,"lock":null}
20:13:22.194 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/803
20:13:22.194 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":803,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull winters morning. Frost gone, having been rain during the night. Wind E by S but still cold.</p>\r\n<p>Attended a meeting at the church to take into consideration the offer of the board of ordinance either to purchase the burial ground at Tynemouth or give a piece of ground in lieu of it. The meeting determined not to do either, but to let the Board apply to Parliament for an act to take it from us, which they had threatened to do. Dined at home. In the evening H Harry, H Nicolson &amp; I had a glass of grog at the George together</p>","pageId":788,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":757,"lock":null}
20:13:22.194 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.195 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/803
20:13:22.195 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":803,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull winters morning. Frost gone, having been rain during the night. Wind E by S but still cold.</p>\r\n<p>Attended a meeting at the church to take into consideration the offer of the board of ordinance either to purchase the burial ground at Tynemouth or give a piece of ground in lieu of it. The meeting determined not to do either, but to let the Board apply to Parliament for an act to take it from us, which they had threatened to do. Dined at home. In the evening H Harry, H Nicolson &amp; I had a glass of grog at the George together</p>","pageId":788,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":757,"lock":null}
20:13:22.195 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/804
20:13:22.195 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":804,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Rather a dull morning. Inclined to freeze. Wind E by S. Drew &pound;5 out of Chapmans. On board the Hope. Carpenter nearly finished laying the half deck. H Harry &amp; Nicolson lunched on board. Dined at home. Received a letter from WBS &amp; answered it In the evening H Nicholson &amp; I called to see jane Mills. With Jane Dryden</p>","pageId":788,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":758,"lock":null}
20:13:22.195 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.195 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/804
20:13:22.195 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":804,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Rather a dull morning. Inclined to freeze. Wind E by S. Drew &pound;5 out of Chapmans. On board the Hope. Carpenter nearly finished laying the half deck. H Harry &amp; Nicolson lunched on board. Dined at home. Received a letter from WBS &amp; answered it In the evening H Nicholson &amp; I called to see jane Mills. With Jane Dryden</p>","pageId":788,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":758,"lock":null}
20:13:22.195 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/805
20:13:22.195 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":805,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>The wind continuing from the SE makes it appear as if there was not much if any frost. Though some snow has fallen during the night.</p>\r\n<p>The last day of the year, which has been to me anything but a prosperous one. I trust I may be more fortunate the next one. I know not what will become of me. It appears to me my destiny is fixed &amp; that I'm never to rise in the world again.</p>\r\n<p>Walked to Cullercoats &amp; saw the fishing boats come in having been successful. The fish very <span class=highlight_yellow>firm</span>, particularly the haddock. There were 16 boats. Dined at home. Attended the whist club &amp; sat the new year in.</p>","pageId":788,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":759,"lock":null}
20:13:22.195 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.196 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/805
20:13:22.196 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":805,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>The wind continuing from the SE makes it appear as if there was not much if any frost. Though some snow has fallen during the night.</p>\r\n<p>The last day of the year, which has been to me anything but a prosperous one. I trust I may be more fortunate the next one. I know not what will become of me. It appears to me my destiny is fixed &amp; that I'm never to rise in the world again.</p>\r\n<p>Walked to Cullercoats &amp; saw the fishing boats come in having been successful. The fish very <span class=highlight_yellow>firm</span>, particularly the haddock. There were 16 boats. Dined at home. Attended the whist club &amp; sat the new year in.</p>","pageId":788,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":759,"lock":null}
20:13:22.196 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/806
20:13:22.196 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":806,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":1,"day":1,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<div class=\"highlights-section\" >\r\n<section>\r\n\r\n\t<h2>Highlights</h2>\r\n\r\n\t<a href=\"/diaries/1830.html#1830-01-24\">\r\n\t<p>1830-01-24 Mrs Scott falls out of bed and breaks her leg</p>\r\n\t</a>\r\n\r\n\t<a href=\"/diaries/1830.html#1830-07-13\">\r\n\t<p>1830-07-13 JSR witnessed an accident which killed a girl sitting under cliffs</p>\r\n\t</a>\r\n\r\n</section>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"page-break-after: always;\">\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n</div>","pageId":null,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":null,"lock":null}
20:13:22.196 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.197 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/806
20:13:22.197 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":806,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":1,"day":1,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<div class=\"highlights-section\" >\r\n<section>\r\n\r\n\t<h2>Highlights</h2>\r\n\r\n\t<a href=\"/diaries/1830.html#1830-01-24\">\r\n\t<p>1830-01-24 Mrs Scott falls out of bed and breaks her leg</p>\r\n\t</a>\r\n\r\n\t<a href=\"/diaries/1830.html#1830-07-13\">\r\n\t<p>1830-07-13 JSR witnessed an accident which killed a girl sitting under cliffs</p>\r\n\t</a>\r\n\r\n</section>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"page-break-after: always;\">\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n</div>","pageId":null,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":null,"lock":null}
20:13:22.197 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/807
20:13:22.197 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":807,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":1,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Seasonal weather but not very severe. Wind WNW. Walked again to Cullercoats &amp; saw them land their fish which were remarkably fine. Dined at home. In the evening Cunningham, Nicolson, &amp; I went to the Duke of York &amp; drank a jug of punch. In the evening at the Mulstrum &amp; with Bell Jervis</p>","pageId":788,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":760,"lock":null}
20:13:22.197 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.197 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/807
20:13:22.197 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":807,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":1,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Seasonal weather but not very severe. Wind WNW. Walked again to Cullercoats &amp; saw them land their fish which were remarkably fine. Dined at home. In the evening Cunningham, Nicolson, &amp; I went to the Duke of York &amp; drank a jug of punch. In the evening at the Mulstrum &amp; with Bell Jervis</p>","pageId":788,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":760,"lock":null}
20:13:22.197 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/808
20:13:22.197 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":808,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":1,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold morning rather inclined to thaw. Wind NW. J Tinley drove me to Newcastle but could do nothing for the Hope. The Colliers being still off work. Returned with J Tinley &amp; dined with him. In the evening attended the whist club at H Harry's</p>","pageId":788,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":761,"lock":null}
20:13:22.197 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.197 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/808
20:13:22.197 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":808,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":1,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold morning rather inclined to thaw. Wind NW. J Tinley drove me to Newcastle but could do nothing for the Hope. The Colliers being still off work. Returned with J Tinley &amp; dined with him. In the evening attended the whist club at H Harry's</p>","pageId":788,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":761,"lock":null}
