20:13:22.219 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":855,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning Rather frosty wind fresh at NW. Got up at 7 o'clock and went on board the Hope. The pilot on board but decided to not venture to take her out, it being in bad tide &amp; threw feet sea upon the bar. Received a letter from WBS &amp; one from Tom Lee. Answered Tom Lees. Dined at home &amp; spent the afternoon at the billiard table. In the evening, heavy rain &amp; wind to NNE. At the Duke of York with H Harry &amp; Nicholson</p>","pageId":799,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":807,"lock":null}
20:13:22.219 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/856
20:13:22.219 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":856,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A frosty morning wind NW. A sea upon the bar which will prevent the Hope getting out. Dined at home In the evening at the Whist Club.</p>","pageId":799,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":808,"lock":null}
20:13:22.219 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
