20:13:22.220 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":856,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A frosty morning wind NW. A sea upon the bar which will prevent the Hope getting out. Dined at home In the evening at the Whist Club.</p>","pageId":799,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":808,"lock":null}
20:13:22.220 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/857
20:13:22.220 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":857,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A course frost. Wind NNW &amp; blowing fresh &amp; although the sea was breaking upon the bar, several small ships ventured out &amp; some were literally smothered in the surf, but all got out safe. Dined with I Readhead on board the Nautalus At the billiard room in the afternoon. Drank tea at home &amp; in the evening With Bode Jerois &amp; afterwards at the Duke Of York</p>","pageId":799,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":809,"lock":null}
20:13:22.220 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.221 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/857
20:13:22.221 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":857,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A course frost. Wind NNW &amp; blowing fresh &amp; although the sea was breaking upon the bar, several small ships ventured out &amp; some were literally smothered in the surf, but all got out safe. Dined with I Readhead on board the Nautalus At the billiard room in the afternoon. Drank tea at home &amp; in the evening With Bode Jerois &amp; afterwards at the Duke Of York</p>","pageId":799,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":809,"lock":null}
20:13:22.221 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/858
20:13:22.221 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":858,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of frost Wind NW. Got up early &amp; went by stream to Newcastle; had a heavy snow storm Returned to dinner at 1 o'clock. Emma G with us. Mrs Dixon came to see Mrs Scott Not water sufficient for the Hope to get to sea. Attended the Whist Club at Allans in the evening</p>\r\n<p>xx</p>","pageId":799,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":810,"lock":null}
20:13:22.221 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.221 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/858
20:13:22.221 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":858,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of frost Wind NW. Got up early &amp; went by stream to Newcastle; had a heavy snow storm Returned to dinner at 1 o'clock. Emma G with us. Mrs Dixon came to see Mrs Scott Not water sufficient for the Hope to get to sea. Attended the Whist Club at Allans in the evening</p>\r\n<p>xx</p>","pageId":799,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":810,"lock":null}
20:13:22.221 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/859
20:13:22.221 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":859,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty morning Been a delightful fall of snow in the night. Blowing fresh at NWW. Attended morning Service; a collection was made for the singers &pound;9.6 received. Dined at home. Being a fine sea tide a great many ships got to sea among them the Hope. Dined at home &amp; went to afternoon service. Afternoon walked to Tynemouth In the evening at the Duke of York</p>","pageId":800,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":811,"lock":null}
20:13:22.221 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.221 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/859
20:13:22.221 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":859,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty morning Been a delightful fall of snow in the night. Blowing fresh at NWW. Attended morning Service; a collection was made for the singers &pound;9.6 received. Dined at home. Being a fine sea tide a great many ships got to sea among them the Hope. Dined at home &amp; went to afternoon service. Afternoon walked to Tynemouth In the evening at the Duke of York</p>","pageId":800,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":811,"lock":null}
20:13:22.222 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/86
20:13:22.222 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":86,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":3,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>D Brown Spouts &amp; heavy ballast &pound;2.12. Fine weather but rather frosty. Wind WNW. Dined at home. Gave captain Stephenson &pound;2. Received from Scott for spars &pound;4.14/- &amp; allowance for ballast 19/2</p>","pageId":692,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":82,"lock":null}
20:13:22.222 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
