20:13:22.227 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":87,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":3,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning, but cold &amp; frosty. Walked to Newcastle everything very dull, little or nothing doing. Returned in the steam boat. Dined at home. Wind NNW</p>","pageId":692,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":83,"lock":null}
20:13:22.227 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/870
20:13:22.227 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":870,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Most extraordinary Fine weather. Wind about South. Took a walk with A Nicholson round by Preston &amp; Tynmouth. Dined with A Harry on board the Choice &amp; in the Evening at the Whist Club</p>","pageId":802,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":822,"lock":null}
20:13:22.227 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.227 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/870
20:13:22.227 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":870,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Most extraordinary Fine weather. Wind about South. Took a walk with A Nicholson round by Preston &amp; Tynmouth. Dined with A Harry on board the Choice &amp; in the Evening at the Whist Club</p>","pageId":802,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":822,"lock":null}
20:13:22.227 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/871
20:13:22.227 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":871,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine morning, rather Frosty. Wind SW. Sent an answer to Mr Anderson's letter. Hope Club stating the Hope being laid up between 20 Dec &amp; 20 Feb Went with H Harry &amp; the H Pemberton of Quebec to Sunderland. Called upon Capt Bunbury of the 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment &amp; returned to dine with H Harry at 5 o'clock A small party to <span class=highlight_yellow>mubt</span> Mrs Pemberton. attended Mrs Heddill's evening party. Received a letter from WBS confirming the of the sale of the Hope's cargo at 29/6 A miserable price, about 6/6 <span class=highlight_yellow>pecght</span> Shall lose I dare say between &pound;30 &amp; &pound;40</p>","pageId":802,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":823,"lock":null}
20:13:22.227 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.227 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/871
20:13:22.227 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":871,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine morning, rather Frosty. Wind SW. Sent an answer to Mr Anderson's letter. Hope Club stating the Hope being laid up between 20 Dec &amp; 20 Feb Went with H Harry &amp; the H Pemberton of Quebec to Sunderland. Called upon Capt Bunbury of the 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment &amp; returned to dine with H Harry at 5 o'clock A small party to <span class=highlight_yellow>mubt</span> Mrs Pemberton. attended Mrs Heddill's evening party. Received a letter from WBS confirming the of the sale of the Hope's cargo at 29/6 A miserable price, about 6/6 <span class=highlight_yellow>pecght</span> Shall lose I dare say between &pound;30 &amp; &pound;40</p>","pageId":802,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":823,"lock":null}
20:13:22.227 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/872
20:13:22.227 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":872,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A duller foggy morning. Wind SW.  <del>Afterwards got to the L&amp;E</del> <del>Cold accompanied</del> Took a walk with Captain Webb to Tynemouth. Dined with Nicholson a party spent a very Pleasant day &amp; in the evening Attended the Whist Club at I Dales</p>","pageId":802,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":824,"lock":null}
20:13:22.227 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.228 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/872
20:13:22.228 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":872,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A duller foggy morning. Wind SW.  <del>Afterwards got to the L&amp;E</del> <del>Cold accompanied</del> Took a walk with Captain Webb to Tynemouth. Dined with Nicholson a party spent a very Pleasant day &amp; in the evening Attended the Whist Club at I Dales</p>","pageId":802,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":824,"lock":null}
20:13:22.228 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/873
20:13:22.228 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":873,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A foggy morning. Wind NE. Afterwards changed to SE &amp; fine clear weather. Went to Church in the morning. Mr Pemberton accompanied me. I was engaged to dine with I Tealey today but on my return from Church. I found that Mrs Scott was so much poorer &amp; her death expected every moment. I sent an apology. She expired precisely at 9 o'clock without a struggle</p>","pageId":802,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":825,"lock":null}
20:13:22.228 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.228 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/873
20:13:22.228 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":873,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A foggy morning. Wind NE. Afterwards changed to SE &amp; fine clear weather. Went to Church in the morning. Mr Pemberton accompanied me. I was engaged to dine with I Tealey today but on my return from Church. I found that Mrs Scott was so much poorer &amp; her death expected every moment. I sent an apology. She expired precisely at 9 o'clock without a struggle</p>","pageId":802,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":825,"lock":null}
20:13:22.228 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/874
20:13:22.228 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":874,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather Frosty. Wind  SSW. Emma G came From school. Mrs Dixon down &amp; Took Emma to N Coatts with her. Wrote to WBS: BBG: &amp; A <span class=highlight_yellow>Deighera</span> of Mrs Scotts death. Kept the house all day.</p>","pageId":803,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":826,"lock":null}
20:13:22.228 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.229 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/874
20:13:22.229 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":874,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather Frosty. Wind  SSW. Emma G came From school. Mrs Dixon down &amp; Took Emma to N Coatts with her. Wrote to WBS: BBG: &amp; A <span class=highlight_yellow>Deighera</span> of Mrs Scotts death. Kept the house all day.</p>","pageId":803,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":826,"lock":null}
20:13:22.229 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/875
20:13:22.229 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":875,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold morning. Rather Frosty. Wind S by W. In the house All day</p>","pageId":803,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":827,"lock":null}
20:13:22.229 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.230 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/875
20:13:22.230 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":875,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold morning. Rather Frosty. Wind S by W. In the house All day</p>","pageId":803,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":827,"lock":null}
20:13:22.230 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/876
20:13:22.230 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":876,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Dull &amp; thick weather &amp; rather cold. Blowing fresh at NSW. Mr &amp; Mrs Dixon &amp; I Smith came down today for the purpose of having Mrs Scott's will read &amp; which not a little surprised all of us, a more extraordinary one perhaps never was: By it I am left the very handsome legacy of &pound;10 !!! the same to my brother, plainly proving &amp; confirming what her feelings towards us throughout life must have been, inveterately bad, &amp; carried to the grave with her. Peace go with her. I forgive her For all the mischief &amp; misery she Has caused in our family. The party left us in the afternoon.</p>","pageId":803,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":828,"lock":null}
20:13:22.230 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.230 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/876
20:13:22.230 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":876,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Dull &amp; thick weather &amp; rather cold. Blowing fresh at NSW. Mr &amp; Mrs Dixon &amp; I Smith came down today for the purpose of having Mrs Scott's will read &amp; which not a little surprised all of us, a more extraordinary one perhaps never was: By it I am left the very handsome legacy of &pound;10 !!! the same to my brother, plainly proving &amp; confirming what her feelings towards us throughout life must have been, inveterately bad, &amp; carried to the grave with her. Peace go with her. I forgive her For all the mischief &amp; misery she Has caused in our family. The party left us in the afternoon.</p>","pageId":803,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":828,"lock":null}
20:13:22.230 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/877
20:13:22.230 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":877,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day but blowing hard from about west. Received at the bank for Salmon's debt &pound;88.9.3 for WBS &amp; deducted from it 20/- for my trouble &amp; &pound;11.6 money lent to Bob Marsh &amp; sec by WBS in London. Dined with I Finley, being less Of the confinement to the house. Received a letter from WBS </p>","pageId":803,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":829,"lock":null}
20:13:22.230 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.230 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/877
20:13:22.230 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":877,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day but blowing hard from about west. Received at the bank for Salmon's debt &pound;88.9.3 for WBS &amp; deducted from it 20/- for my trouble &amp; &pound;11.6 money lent to Bob Marsh &amp; sec by WBS in London. Dined with I Finley, being less Of the confinement to the house. Received a letter from WBS </p>","pageId":803,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":829,"lock":null}
20:13:22.230 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/878
20:13:22.230 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":878,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Beautiful weather, but very windy at West. Received a letter from ABS in reply to their informing him of Mrs Scott's death, saying he cannot leave London before tonight or tomorrow morning Dined at home. Wes &amp; Fanny Smith excessively angry that we should claim the amount of taxes upon the house paid by us in error &amp; which ought to have been paid by Mrs Scott. Fanny inclined to be very violent, her conduct disgusting &amp; very insulting; displaying more regard for the money than for the aunt. Blew a perfect hurricane with heavy rain the afternoon</p>","pageId":804,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":830,"lock":null}
20:13:22.230 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.231 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/878
20:13:22.231 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":878,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Beautiful weather, but very windy at West. Received a letter from ABS in reply to their informing him of Mrs Scott's death, saying he cannot leave London before tonight or tomorrow morning Dined at home. Wes &amp; Fanny Smith excessively angry that we should claim the amount of taxes upon the house paid by us in error &amp; which ought to have been paid by Mrs Scott. Fanny inclined to be very violent, her conduct disgusting &amp; very insulting; displaying more regard for the money than for the aunt. Blew a perfect hurricane with heavy rain the afternoon</p>","pageId":804,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":830,"lock":null}
20:13:22.231 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/879
20:13:22.231 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":879,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, but still Blowing very hard at NW. In the house All day</p>","pageId":804,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":831,"lock":null}
20:13:22.231 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.231 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/879
20:13:22.231 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":879,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, but still Blowing very hard at NW. In the house All day</p>","pageId":804,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":831,"lock":null}
20:13:22.231 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/88
20:13:22.231 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":88,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":3,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine clear frosty morning &amp; cold. Wind NNW. Showers of sleet &amp; rain in the afternoon. Attended morning service. Dined at home.  <span class=highlight_yellow>Carlea</span> Sunday</p>","pageId":692,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":84,"lock":null}
20:13:22.231 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.232 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/88
20:13:22.232 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":88,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":3,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine clear frosty morning &amp; cold. Wind NNW. Showers of sleet &amp; rain in the afternoon. Attended morning service. Dined at home.  <span class=highlight_yellow>Carlea</span> Sunday</p>","pageId":692,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":84,"lock":null}
20:13:22.232 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/880
20:13:22.232 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":880,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cool morning &amp; blown very hard all day at west. Of course in the house. Fanny Smith again exceedingly violent today. More so than before &amp; insulting. Than I was obliged to speak to her in a way that had the effect of making her silent. Wonder ? Be at opposite William BS did not arrive until after 11 o'clock having called &amp; stopped a short time in Westgate Street. Went to bed from after his arrival.</p>","pageId":804,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":832,"lock":null}
20:13:22.232 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.232 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/880
20:13:22.232 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":880,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cool morning &amp; blown very hard all day at west. Of course in the house. Fanny Smith again exceedingly violent today. More so than before &amp; insulting. Than I was obliged to speak to her in a way that had the effect of making her silent. Wonder ? Be at opposite William BS did not arrive until after 11 o'clock having called &amp; stopped a short time in Westgate Street. Went to bed from after his arrival.</p>","pageId":804,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":832,"lock":null}
20:13:22.232 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/881
20:13:22.232 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":881,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet morning, wind SE Afterwards changed to SW &amp; blowing fresh with fine weather. Brought a large fleet down amongst them the Hope. Dixon &amp; his aid Tom Smith Mrs Yellowley &amp; Emma came down to attend the funeral which took place between 12 &amp; 1 o'clock. Captain Caudisson of the 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment kindly allowing the hearse and carriages to enter the castle ...</p>","pageId":804,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":833,"lock":null}
20:13:22.232 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.233 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/881
20:13:22.233 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":881,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet morning, wind SE Afterwards changed to SW &amp; blowing fresh with fine weather. Brought a large fleet down amongst them the Hope. Dixon &amp; his aid Tom Smith Mrs Yellowley &amp; Emma came down to attend the funeral which took place between 12 &amp; 1 o'clock. Captain Caudisson of the 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment kindly allowing the hearse and carriages to enter the castle ...</p>","pageId":804,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":833,"lock":null}
20:13:22.233 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/882
20:13:22.233 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":882,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":15,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... yard. Mrs Scott's remains placed in the vault above my father. Fanny Smith more violent than ever. Her conduct most disgusting &amp; indecent. Dixon Mrs B &amp; Mr Gallowley returned to Newcastle. Tom Smith accompanied</p>","pageId":805,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":834,"lock":null}
20:13:22.233 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.233 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/882
20:13:22.233 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":882,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":15,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... yard. Mrs Scott's remains placed in the vault above my father. Fanny Smith more violent than ever. Her conduct most disgusting &amp; indecent. Dixon Mrs B &amp; Mr Gallowley returned to Newcastle. Tom Smith accompanied</p>","pageId":805,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":834,"lock":null}
20:13:22.233 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/883
20:13:22.233 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":883,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW &amp; rather cold. Tom Smith, his mother &amp; Fanny left us for Foyston &amp; fortunately without any more unpleasantness. After they left us the weather changed &amp; we had a very stormy day, heavy showers of snow Was &amp; I had the servants up &amp; told them of our plans. Robert agreed to remain with me, also Leadbetter. Hutchison of course leaves us, but will stay in the house until she gets a situation or I wish her to leave. Stephenson has been at NCastle  but could obtain nothing for the Hope only 8/6 pecght offering. Ordered Him to unbind the sails. Gave him a draft upon Chapman for &pound;20 to pay wages. At home all the evening</p>","pageId":805,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":835,"lock":null}
20:13:22.233 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.233 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/883
20:13:22.233 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":883,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW &amp; rather cold. Tom Smith, his mother &amp; Fanny left us for Foyston &amp; fortunately without any more unpleasantness. After they left us the weather changed &amp; we had a very stormy day, heavy showers of snow Was &amp; I had the servants up &amp; told them of our plans. Robert agreed to remain with me, also Leadbetter. Hutchison of course leaves us, but will stay in the house until she gets a situation or I wish her to leave. Stephenson has been at NCastle  but could obtain nothing for the Hope only 8/6 pecght offering. Ordered Him to unbind the sails. Gave him a draft upon Chapman for &pound;20 to pay wages. At home all the evening</p>","pageId":805,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":835,"lock":null}
20:13:22.233 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/884
20:13:22.233 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":884,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull showery day. Wind fresh at NW. Engaged at home in the house with ABS. I gave him his note at 40 days for &pound;75.10/- <font color=#FF0000>Accepted &amp; returned </font><font color=#FF0000>Mrs</font><font color=#FF0000> </font><font color=#FF0000>Bulemer</font><font color=#FF0000> a bill</font> <font color=#FF0000>at</font><font color=#FF0000> 3 </font><font color=#FF0000>hou</font><font color=#FF0000>rs. Due 23 p</font><font color=#FF0000>ricing</font><font color=#FF0000> for Policy presumabl</font><font color=#FF0000>y</font> <font color=#FF0000>almost</font><font color=#FF0000> &pound;16.13.8</font> Dined at home. At 5 o'clock the owner &amp; Master of the Commerce with me about the damages received by him in the wold when the Hope came in contact, agreed to leave it to two gentlemen to decide with have to call in a this. At home all the evening </p>","pageId":805,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":836,"lock":null}
