20:13:22.242 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":901,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A stormy morning with heavy showers of snow. A great deal having fallen during the night. Wind ENE. Dined at home. Emma G: came from school to us. In the evening attended the whist club at Mrs Creigs. And asked the club to come to me on Thursday</p>","pageId":809,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":853,"lock":null}
20:13:22.242 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/902
20:13:22.242 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":902,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty morning wind NW. Emma Mary Carfs &amp; went to church. Heard a funeral sermon from Mr Mark who held the service. The Vicars father being dead &amp; also young Mrs Read he died in London of the gout in the head &amp; after two days illness. Dined at home &amp; afternoon walked with H Henry to Tynemouth. In the evening at <span class=highlight_yellow>n</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ews</span><span class=highlight_yellow> r</span><span class=highlight_yellow>oo</span><span class=highlight_yellow>m</span> &amp; H Harry's</p>","pageId":809,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":854,"lock":null}
20:13:22.242 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
