20:13:22.248 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":914,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine spring morning. Wind SSE. Went with Weller &amp; called upon the Vicar Miss Ratcliff &amp; Mr Matthews. Saw Brown of the George and offered him the house at &pound;80 the nominal rent to be &pound;100. Dined at the George Tavern. The whist club dinner a party of <span class=highlight_yellow>sextecan</span> &amp; spent a pleasant evening</p>","pageId":812,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":866,"lock":null}
20:13:22.248 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/915
20:13:22.248 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":915,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful warm morning. Wind W by S. The painters began painting the house. Repairing the doors, windows. &amp; Dined at home at 2 o'clock. Emma with us. WBS left us at &frac12; past 5 % o'clock by steam for Newcastle and thence to take the ship to London</p>","pageId":812,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":867,"lock":null}
20:13:22.248 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
