20:13:22.249 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":915,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful warm morning. Wind W by S. The painters began painting the house. Repairing the doors, windows. &amp; Dined at home at 2 o'clock. Emma with us. WBS left us at &frac12; past 5 % o'clock by steam for Newcastle and thence to take the ship to London</p>","pageId":812,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":867,"lock":null}
20:13:22.249 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/916
20:13:22.249 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":916,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine soft spring morning with showers. Wind blowing fresh at W by S. Dined at home. Took tea with W Allen &amp; attended the whist club at Mr Richmonds in the evening</p>","pageId":813,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":868,"lock":null}
20:13:22.249 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.249 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/916
20:13:22.249 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":916,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine soft spring morning with showers. Wind blowing fresh at W by S. Dined at home. Took tea with W Allen &amp; attended the whist club at Mr Richmonds in the evening</p>","pageId":813,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":868,"lock":null}
20:13:22.249 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/917
20:13:22.249 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":917,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning Wind WNW. Went to church Rev Mark did duty &amp; gave us an excellent sermon I Tenby &amp; I walked to Tynemouth &amp; I afterwards dined with him, Mr Mark with us</p>","pageId":813,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":869,"lock":null}
20:13:22.249 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.249 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/917
20:13:22.249 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":917,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning Wind WNW. Went to church Rev Mark did duty &amp; gave us an excellent sermon I Tenby &amp; I walked to Tynemouth &amp; I afterwards dined with him, Mr Mark with us</p>","pageId":813,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":869,"lock":null}
20:13:22.249 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/918
20:13:22.249 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":918,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning blowing fresh from SW. A letter came for Captain Jameson of the London which I sent by one of the Hopes boys to the ship at Bewick <span class=highlight_yellow>oCrasters</span> spout. Dined at home, H Harry came in &amp; took wine with him &amp; in the evening he Captain Webb &amp; Peash Frantook of a cockle supper with us.</p>","pageId":813,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":870,"lock":null}
