20:13:22.279 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/981
20:13:22.279 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":981,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":23,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but still cold. With a NE wind. Walked round by the high end of Shields to Dr Drings garden. Dined at home. At the Pig &amp; Whistle &amp; in the evening at Tynemouth. Suppered with A Harry</p>","pageId":827,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":932,"lock":null}
20:13:22.279 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.280 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/981
20:13:22.280 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":981,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":23,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but still cold. With a NE wind. Walked round by the high end of Shields to Dr Drings garden. Dined at home. At the Pig &amp; Whistle &amp; in the evening at Tynemouth. Suppered with A Harry</p>","pageId":827,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":932,"lock":null}
20:13:22.280 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/982
20:13:22.280 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":982,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Rather a dull morning with a continuance of SE wind. &amp; cool. Tool Emma G up with me in Dunn's coach to Newcastle where we met Tom Smith who drove he home with him to Royston for the whole day. Went in the afternoon to the races. A good deal of company, the Gold Cup being to be seen for; which was won by Lord Elcho's Gondolence. Dined in the Grand Stand. Got home at 11 o'clock</p>","pageId":828,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":933,"lock":null}
20:13:22.280 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.280 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/982
20:13:22.280 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":982,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Rather a dull morning with a continuance of SE wind. &amp; cool. Tool Emma G up with me in Dunn's coach to Newcastle where we met Tom Smith who drove he home with him to Royston for the whole day. Went in the afternoon to the races. A good deal of company, the Gold Cup being to be seen for; which was won by Lord Elcho's Gondolence. Dined in the Grand Stand. Got home at 11 o'clock</p>","pageId":828,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":933,"lock":null}
20:13:22.280 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/983
20:13:22.280 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":983,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind east blowing fresh. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home. H Harry came in after dinner &amp; took wine with me &amp; he &amp; H French spent the evening supplied with beer with Mr Jervis</p>","pageId":828,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":934,"lock":null}
20:13:22.280 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.281 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/983
20:13:22.281 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":983,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind east blowing fresh. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home. H Harry came in after dinner &amp; took wine with me &amp; he &amp; H French spent the evening supplied with beer with Mr Jervis</p>","pageId":828,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":934,"lock":null}
20:13:22.281 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/984
20:13:22.281 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":984,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A rainy morning and blowing fresh at SE with a heavy sea upon the bar. Took a short walk. Dined at home. A French gave me a bottle of wine at the George. An awfully heavy thunder storm with a deluge of rain which overflowed the streets in two or three minutes &amp; changed the wind to NW</p>","pageId":828,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":935,"lock":null}
20:13:22.281 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.281 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/984
20:13:22.281 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":984,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A rainy morning and blowing fresh at SE with a heavy sea upon the bar. Took a short walk. Dined at home. A French gave me a bottle of wine at the George. An awfully heavy thunder storm with a deluge of rain which overflowed the streets in two or three minutes &amp; changed the wind to NW</p>","pageId":828,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":935,"lock":null}
20:13:22.281 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/985
20:13:22.281 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":985,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but the wind again from the SE. Took Jehy sec &amp; did not go to church. Dined at home. A French came &amp; took wine with me. In the <font color=#D9D9D9>[afternoon]</font> walked to Tynemouth, rather showery</p>","pageId":828,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":936,"lock":null}
20:13:22.281 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.281 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/985
20:13:22.281 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":985,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but the wind again from the SE. Took Jehy sec &amp; did not go to church. Dined at home. A French came &amp; took wine with me. In the <font color=#D9D9D9>[afternoon]</font> walked to Tynemouth, rather showery</p>","pageId":828,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":936,"lock":null}
20:13:22.281 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/986
20:13:22.281 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":986,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cloudy morning with appearance of rain. Wind SE. Received an account of the poor vicar's death at &frac14; past 8 o'clock on Saturday morning to the inexpressible sorrow of the a <span class=highlight_yellow>alecow</span>. All the ships be hoisted their colours half mast high. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home. In the afternoon a heavy thunder storm with showers at intervals. Went to see A Harry in the evening who has got a light attack of gout.</p>","pageId":829,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":937,"lock":null}
20:13:22.281 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.282 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/986
20:13:22.282 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":986,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cloudy morning with appearance of rain. Wind SE. Received an account of the poor vicar's death at &frac14; past 8 o'clock on Saturday morning to the inexpressible sorrow of the a <span class=highlight_yellow>alecow</span>. All the ships be hoisted their colours half mast high. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home. In the afternoon a heavy thunder storm with showers at intervals. Went to see A Harry in the evening who has got a light attack of gout.</p>","pageId":829,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":937,"lock":null}
20:13:22.282 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/987
20:13:22.282 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":987,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy morning &amp; like more rain again blowing fresh at WNW. Received a letter from B B Gallbraith &amp; answered it. Dined at home. Walked to Tynemouth in the evening</p>","pageId":829,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":938,"lock":null}
20:13:22.282 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
20:13:22.282 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/987
20:13:22.282 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":987,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy morning &amp; like more rain again blowing fresh at WNW. Received a letter from B B Gallbraith &amp; answered it. Dined at home. Walked to Tynemouth in the evening</p>","pageId":829,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":938,"lock":null}
20:13:22.282 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/988
20:13:22.282 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":988,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning something like summer weather at last. Wind WNW afterwards the heat brought is round to SE. Walked out to Whitley Park &amp; called upon I Wright &amp; returned by  Cullercoats to dinner.Webb came in &amp; took part of a bottle of port with me. Walked to Tynemouth in the evening. King William the 4th proclaimed at Newcastle today &amp; the guns fired at Tynemouth castle</p>","pageId":829,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":939,"lock":null}
20:13:22.282 [main] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
